{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_21","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9e43dbc8-95ca-467f-a7ad-9e45fa464f86-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md","offset":1660,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9e43dbc8-95ca-467f-a7ad-9e45fa464f86-31","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","offset":70,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6194,"output_tokens":291,"cache_read_input_tokens":150656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"26b6da21-31a5-4c51-b992-fe9b80d4266e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9e43dbc8-95ca-467f-a7ad-9e45fa464f86-30","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1660→\\n## Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engine/modules/songs.js)\\n\\n- `E.Songbook`: the songbook: songs by id, their moods, get(id), find(mood) (see the manual)\\n- `E.Songbook.find(mood)`: the ids of the songs of a mood, in the order listed\\n- `E.Songbook.get(id)`: a song by id (playable: game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get('town'))), or undefined\\n- `E.Songbook.moods`: every mood a song has, in the order of the manual\\n- `E.Songbook.songs`: every song by id ({ title, mood: [...], bpm, steps, tracks, loop }; the core's own songs are E.songs')\\n\\n## Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js)\\n1670→\\n- `new E.Story(game, o = {}) → story`: new E.Story(game, { people, nodes, vars, on, dialog }): the talk of a game (the manual above)\\n- `story.done(id)`: finish a quest (taken now if it wasn't)\\n- `story.draw(r)`: draw the balloons over their targets and the box (anywhere in draw: both go to the overlay)\\n- `story.emote(target, kind = '!', seconds = 1.5)`: a balloon over target (x, y, z; h: its height) for seconds: '!', '?', 'heart', 'dots', 'note'\\n- `story.get(key)`: a flag or value (key may be a dotted path into vars)\\n- `story.quest(id, title = id, text = '')`: take a quest (or change its title and text): it joins the log\\n- `story.restore(s)`: put back what state() gave (a load)\\n- `story.resume()`: after an event with wait: true, go on (to the choice's goto, or the next step)\\n- `story.run(id, o = {})`: start node id (stopping any other); o.onDone(story) when it ends\\n1680→- `story.set(key, value = true)`: set a flag (value true) or a value\\n- `story.state()`: its vars and quests, as JSON (for a save)\\n- `story.stop()`: stop the node running (its box closes; onDone isn't called)\\n- `story.test(c)`: does a condition hold? (the manual's conditions)\\n- `story.update(dt)`: run the talk and the balloons; true while a node runs (play waits)\\n- `story.auto = 0`: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself (0: it waits for the player)\\n- `story.game`: its game\\n- `story.log = []`: what was said and chosen, oldest first ({ who, name, text }, the last 200: a visual novel's backlog)\\n- `story.node = null`: its id\\n- `story.nodes`: the conversations by id (lists of steps)\\n1690→- `story.on`: the game's event handlers by name\\n- `story.people`: who speaks, by id ({ name, portrait, at })\\n- `story.quests = []`: the quest log, in the order taken ({ id, title, text, done })\\n- `story.running = false`: a node runs\\n- `story.skip = false`: pages type at once and turn at once (choices still wait)\\n- `story.talk`: the E.Dialog it speaks through\\n- `story.vars`: every flag and value (a line's {$name} reads them)\\n\\n## Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js)\\n\\n1700→- `new E.Clock(o = {}) → clock` †: new E.Clock({ day: 240 (real seconds of game time a day), hour: 8 (to start at) })\\n- `clock.hour` †: the hour (0..23)\\n- `clock.label()` †: 'DAY 2 14:30'\\n- `clock.light()` †: the light by the hour: { ambient (.12 at night .. 1 at noon), color (the sky's tint: blue night, warm dawn and dusk) }\\n- `clock.minute` †: the minute (0..59)\\n- `clock.night` †: true from 20:00 to 6:00\\n- `clock.update(dt)` †: run it by dt seconds of game time\\n- `clock.day = 1` †: the day (1, 2, ...)\\n- `clock.length` †: seconds a day\\n- `clock.t` †: hours since the first midnight\\n1710→- `new E.Strategy(game, o = {}) → strategy` †: new E.Strategy(game, { map, kinds, sides, player, fog, on }): see the manual above\\n- `strategy.afford(side, cost)` †: can side pay cost ({ gold: 50 })?\\n- `strategy.ai(side, plan)` †: run side by plan ({ build: [[kind, n]], waves: { first, every, min }, script }): see the manual\\n- `strategy.canPlace(kind, cx, cy, by = null)` †: can a building of kind stand on cells cx, cy (its corner)? On the map, walkable, no unit there (but by, its builder), seen by the player (when it is theirs)\\n- `strategy.cancel(b)` †: take back the last in building's queue (refunded)\\n- `strategy.draw(r)` †: after the world: a ring under each selected unit, health bars over the selected and the hurt, the box being drawn\\n- `strategy.ghost(r, kind, cx, cy)` †: the placement ghost: kind's cells at cx, cy, green where it fits, red where it doesn't\\n- `strategy.input(o = {})` †: the player's pointer and keys, each step (see the manual): selection, groups, orders. o.order: the action that orders (Mouse2 by default where it is bound); o.at(sx, sy) -> the world point under a screen point (map.pick's, by default)\\n- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\\n- `strategy.of(side, kind)` †: the side's standing units of a kind (or all of them, without kind)\\n1720→- `strategy.order(units, kind, target, o = {})` †: give units an order: kind 'move' | 'attack' | 'amove' | 'gather' | 'build' | 'patrol' | 'stop', target ({ x, y }, a unit, or { kind, cx, cy } to build), o.queue: after the orders they have\\n- `strategy.remove(u)` †: take u off the map (it died, a mine ran out)\\n- `strategy.side(id)` †: a side by id: { id, res: { gold: 300 }, ... }\\n- `strategy.smart(units, x, y, target, o = {})` †: the right click: attack a foe at the point, gather a resource, else move (o.queue as order's); a building that makes units takes the point as its rally\\n- `strategy.spawn(kind, side, x, y, o = {})` †: make a unit, building or resource of kind for side at world x, y (o.built: false leaves a building to be built)\\n- `strategy.state()` †: what a proof hashes: every unit's kind, side, cell and HP, each side's resources\\n- `strategy.train(b, kind)` †: queue kind at building (paid now): it comes out after its time, toward building.rally. False when it can't\\n- `strategy.update(dt)` †: run the orders, production, fights, the fog and the AIs by dt seconds\\n- `strategy.visible(u)` †: can the player see u? (the fog: any of its cells in sight; theirs always)\\n- `strategy.fog` †: an E.Fog of the player's sight (walls block it, buildings don't), or null with fog: false\\n1730→- `strategy.game` †: the game it runs in\\n- `strategy.groups` †: control groups: groups[1..9], kept with Ctrl and a digit\\n- `strategy.kinds` †: the kinds by id (units, buildings, resources: see the manual)\\n- `strategy.map` †: the TileMap it stands on (a building blocks its cells)\\n- `strategy.on` †: its events: { attack, death, made, built, gathered, ordered }\\n- `strategy.player` †: the side the player commands (its fog, selection, input)\\n- `strategy.selected = []` †: the player's selection\\n- `strategy.time = 0` †: seconds run (rts.update's dt summed)\\n- `strategy.units = []` †: everything spawned (units, buildings, resources) that still stands\\n- `E.choose(agent, options)` †: the option that best meets an agent's needs ({ gives: { hunger: -.6 }, x, y, cost }): each need it lowers, weighted by that need squared (the urgent first), less the walk (a cell's worth per 400 units) and cost against agent.money; null when none helps\",\"content_concise\":\"1660→\\n## Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engine/modules/songs.js)\\n\\n- `E.Songbook`: the songbook: songs by id, their moods, get(id), find(mood) (see the manual)\\n- `E.Songbook.find(mood)`: the ids of the songs of a mood, in the order listed\\n- `E.Songbook.get(id)`: a song by id (playable: game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get('town'))), or undefined\\n- `E.Songbook.moods`: every mood a song has, in the order of the manual\\n- `E.Songbook.songs`: every song by id ({ title, mood: [...], bpm, steps, tracks, loop }; the core's own songs are E.songs')\\n\\n## Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js)\\n1670→\\n- `new E.Story(game, o = {}) → story`: new E.Story(game, { people, nodes, vars, on, dialog }): the talk of a game (the manual above)\\n- `story.done(id)`: finish a quest (taken now if it wasn't)\\n- `story.draw(r)`: draw the balloons over their targets and the box (anywhere in draw: both go to the overlay)\\n- `story.emote(target, kind = '!', seconds = 1.5)`: a balloon over target (x, y, z; h: its height) for seconds: '!', '?', 'heart', 'dots', 'note'\\n- `story.get(key)`: a flag or value (key may be a dotted path into vars)\\n- `story.quest(id, title = id, text = '')`: take a quest (or change its title and text): it joins the log\\n- `story.restore(s)`: put back what state() gave (a load)\\n- `story.resume()`: after an event with wait: true, go on (to the choice's goto, or the next step)\\n- `story.run(id, o = {})`: start node id (stopping any other); o.onDone(story) when it ends\\n1680→- `story.set(key, value = true)`: set a flag (value true) or a value\\n- `story.state()`: its vars and quests, as JSON (for a save)\\n- `story.stop()`: stop the node running (its box closes; onDone isn't called)\\n- `story.test(c)`: does a condition hold? (the manual's conditions)\\n- `story.update(dt)`: run the talk and the balloons; true while a node runs (play waits)\\n- `story.auto = 0`: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself (0: it waits for the player)\\n- `story.game`: its game\\n- `story.log = []`: what was said and chosen, oldest first ({ who, name, text }, the last 200: a visual novel's backlog)\\n- `story.node = null`: its id\\n- `story.nodes`: the conversations by id (lists of steps)\\n1690→- `story.on`: the game's event handlers by name\\n- `story.people`: who speaks, by id ({ name, portrait, at })\\n- `story.quests = []`: the quest log, in the order taken ({ id, title, text, done })\\n- `story.running = false`: a node runs\\n- `story.skip = false`: pages type at once and turn at once (choices still wait)\\n- `story.talk`: the E.Dialog it speaks through\\n- `story.vars`: every flag and value (a line's {$name} reads them)\\n\\n## Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js)\\n\\n1700→- `new E.Clock(o = {}) → clock` †: new E.Clock({ day: 240 (real seconds of game time a day), hour: 8 (to start at) })\\n- `clock.hour` †: the hour (0..23)\\n- `clock.label()` †: 'DAY 2 14:30'\\n- `clock.light()` †: the light by the hour: { ambient (.12 at night .. 1 at noon), color (the sky's tint: blue night, warm dawn and dusk) }\\n- `clock.minute` †: the minute (0..59)\\n- `clock.night` †: true from 20:00 to 6:00\\n- `clock.update(dt)` †: run it by dt seconds of game time\\n- `clock.day = 1` †: the day (1, 2, ...)\\n- `clock.length` †: seconds a day\\n- `clock.t` †: hours since the first midnight\\n1710→- `new E.Strategy(game, o = {}) → strategy` †: new E.Strategy(game, { map, kinds, sides, player, fog, on }): see the manual above\\n- `strategy.afford(side, cost)` †: can side pay cost ({ gold: 50 })?\\n- `strategy.ai(side, plan)` †: run side by plan ({ build: [[kind, n]], waves: { first, every, min }, script }): see the manual\\n- `strategy.canPlace(kind, cx, cy, by = null)` †: can a building of kind stand on cells cx, cy (its corner)? On the map, walkable, no unit there (but by, its builder), seen by the player (when it is theirs)\\n- `strategy.cancel(b)` †: take back the last in building's queue (refunded)\\n- `strategy.draw(r)` †: after the world: a ring under each selected unit, health bars over the selected and the hurt, the box being drawn\\n- `strategy.ghost(r, kind, cx, cy)` †: the placement ghost: kind's cells at cx, cy, green where it fits, red where it doesn't\\n- `strategy.input(o = {})` †: the player's pointer and keys, each step (see the manual): selection, groups, orders. o.order: the action that orders (Mouse2 by default where it is bound); o.at(sx, sy) -> the world point under a screen point (map.pick's, by default)\\n- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\\n- `strategy.of(side, kind)` †: the side's standing units of a kind (or all of them, without kind)\\n1720→- `strategy.order(units, kind, target, o = {})` †: give units an order: kind 'move' | 'attack' | 'amove' | 'gather' | 'build' | 'patrol' | 'stop', target ({ x, y }, a unit, or { kind, cx, cy } to build), o.queue: after the orders they have\\n- `strategy.remove(u)` †: take u off the map (it died, a mine ran out)\\n- `strategy.side(id)` †: a side by id: { id, res: { gold: 300 }, ... }\\n- `strategy.smart(units, x, y, target, o = {})` †: the right click: attack a foe at the point, gather a resource, else move (o.queue as order's); a building that makes units takes the point as its rally\\n- `strategy.spawn(kind, side, x, y, o = {})` †: make a unit, building or resource of kind for side at world x, y (o.built: false leaves a building to be built)\\n- `strategy.state()` †: what a proof hashes: every unit's kind, side, cell and HP, each side's resources\\n- `strategy.train(b, kind)` †: queue kind at building (paid now): it comes out after its time, toward building.rally. False when it can't\\n- `strategy.update(dt)` †: run the orders, production, fights, the fog and the AIs by dt seconds\\n- `strategy.visible(u)` †: can the player see u? (the fog: any of its cells in sight; theirs always)\\n- `strategy.fog` †: an E.Fog of the player's sight (walls block it, buildings don't), or null with fog: false\\n1730→- `strategy.game` †: the game it runs in\\n- `strategy.groups` †: control groups: groups[1..9], kept with Ctrl and a digit\\n- `strategy.kinds` †: the kinds by id (units, buildings, resources: see the manual)\\n- `strategy.map` †: the TileMap it stands on (a building blocks its cells)\\n- `strategy.on` †: its events: { attack, death, made, built, gathered, ordered }\\n- `strategy.player` †: the side the player commands (its fog, selection, input)\\n- `strategy.selected = []` †: the player's selection\\n- `strategy.time = 0` †: seconds run (rts.update's dt summed)\\n- `strategy.units = []` †: everything spawned (units, buildings, resources) that still stands\\n- `E.choose(agent, options)` †: the option that best meets an agent's needs ({ gives: { hunger: -.6 }, x, y, cost }): each need it lowers, weighted by that need squared (the urgent first), less the walk (a cell's worth per 400 units) and cost against agent.money; null when none helps\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md\",\"offset\":1660,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"\\n## Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engine/modules/songs.js)\\n\\n- `E.Songbook`: the songbook: songs by id, their moods, get(id), find(mood) (see the manual)\\n- `E.Songbook.find(mood)`: the ids of the songs of a mood, in the order listed\\n- `E.Songbook.get(id)`: a song by id (playable: game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get('town'))), or undefined\\n- `E.Songbook.moods`: every mood a song has, in the order of the manual\\n- `E.Songbook.songs`: every song by id ({ title, mood: [...], bpm, steps, tracks, loop }; the core's own songs are E.songs')\\n\\n## Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js)\\n\\n- `new E.Story(game, o = {}) → story`: new E.Story(game, { people, nodes, vars, on, dialog }): the talk of a game (the manual above)\\n- `story.done(id)`: finish a quest (ta