cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":10136,\"content\":\"    if ((this._inflight || 0) >= 2) { this.skipped = (this.skipped || 0) + 1; return; }\"},{\"line_number\":13792,\"content\":\"  acts() { return !this.dead && !Object.keys(this.effects).some(e => (this.rpg.status[e] || {}).skip); }\"},{\"line_number\":14187,\"content\":\"  stays before it turns), story.skip (pages type and turn at once; choices wait).\"},{\"line_number\":14233,\"content\":\"    this.auto = 0; this.skip = false;\"},{\"line_number\":14268,\"content\":\"    this.talk.speed = this.skip ? 1e6 : this._speed;\"},{\"line_number\":14269,\"content\":\"    this.talk.say(s.say, { name, portrait: p.portrait, auto: this.skip ? .08 : this.auto || undefined, choices: ch && ch.length ? ch.map(c => c.text) : null, onChoice: i => { this._pick = ch[i]; note({ who: 'choice', name: '', text: ch[i].text }); }, onDone: () => this._after(s) });\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"dbac8a3b-edb4-4495-999e-d882de60c9ec"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_26","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"story.skip sets talk speed to very high and auto to 0.\n\nPages flip every 0.08 seconds when skip is active. A 10-line scene lasts 0.8 seconds. Choices still pause the flow, so the plan is to either omit them from the main path or auto-select the first option while skip is held.\n\nThe plan calls for tone choices now and then. I'll add one optional bark choice that doesn't block the flow, rather than auto-selecting choices while skip is held.\n\nThe test loop will hold skip and tap confirm whenever a choice appears. The ward map stays small: player spawns at (40, 80), door at (80, 80). Hold right for 0.5 seconds then tap interact. People in beds are determined by campaign.saved.\n\nThe test will verify patient names appear after case 1. For the chart scene, confirm starts the operation and lightboxes precede cases 2, 4, and 10. The test will click the anomaly by moving the pad to its known position from the snapshot or by aiming the cursor over the mark.\n\nThe test will use `input.feed` to simulate mouse clicks for the chart lightbox. It will read the target position from `game.debug.snapshot().lightbox`, feed a down event at that coordinate, then feed an up event. The intern role gets a hint cursor on the anomaly; the resident must find it manually.\n\nThe lightbox test will feed a down event at the anomaly's screen pixel coordinates, advance one frame, then feed an up event.\n\nThe hub will follow the skeleton closely but use the Grand Rounds simulation as its world. The harness connects early and calls ready() immediately after connection resolves. It enables card mode and answers ready on Enter or confirm during the card phase, and answers more on the more button. On start it counts down until time reaches zero before playing. The host simulates and sends snapshots at twelve frames per second.\n\nClients send input at fifteen frames per second. When the timer expires, the host calls finish() with standings, scores, winner status, and awards. At round end, audio mutes and input stops. In server mode, no local player exists but simulation continues and snapshots are still sent. If the host leaves, the hub voids the round without crashing; it simply handles the incoming end signal. Both clients and host exchange traffic continuously: clients send cursor data while hosts broadcast state. During the brief play window, the harness waits for the playing phase, then randomly presses keys for about one and a half seconds before triggering time-up.\n\nThe host sends snapshot state at twelve frames per second. Clients send input at fifteen frames per second. The combined rate stays under the twenty-per-second limit. The host does not send to itself. Clients send their input to the host, and the host sends its full state back to them.\n\nThe server acts as host, sending snapshot state and receiving client input. During the card phase, the harness dispatches an Enter keypress to the iframe so the engine registers it as confirm and answers ready.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-76337fb7-8f73-4a16-ae76-bc397a5a78d5-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"__hubViolations|violation|pageerror|dialog","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/hub/harness.html","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":562,"output_tokens":1559,"cache_read_input_tokens":168320,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"42ce095f-e63d-4c13-86b4-61884f5757a5"}
