15,112,114,105,116,101,40,103,44,32,115,112,114,44,32,120,44,32,121,44,32,102,108,105,112,41,96,32,40,111,114,32,96,123,32,102,108,105,112,44,32,114,111,116,44,32,115,99,97,108,101,32,125,96,41,44,32,96,103,108,111,119,40,103,44,32,48,46,46,49,41,96,32,40,71,80,85,32,103,108,111,119,32,102,111,114,32,119,104,97,116,32,102,111,108,108,111,119,115,41,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":4,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":72,\"content\":\"2. Draw only with `E.px.*`, `E.font`, `E.ui`, sprites, props and the `r.*` helpers. Never use `ctx.arc`, `ctx.stroke`, `ctx.fillText` or canvas gradients on the game buffer (they blur pixels). For translucency and glow use `px.blend(g, alpha, 'add' | 'multiply' | 'screen' | 'normal', () => {...})`, `px.polyDither`, `px.ddisc`, `r.glowDisc` and `r.shadow`: they use stepped alpha and blend modes like PS1 / SNES hardware (or dithering with `E.style.trans = 'dither'` for an NES / Genesis look).\"},{\"line_number\":153,\"content\":\"- Floor marks: `r.shadow(x, y, radius, alpha, color, surfaceZ)`, `r.decal(g => r.groundArc(...))`, `r.groundDisc`, `r.groundRing`, `r.groundPts(x, y, rad, n, z)`.\"},{\"line_number\":157,\"content\":\"- Glowing things you draw yourself: `r.queue(x, y, z, fn, { emissive: true })` is drawn again after lighting so darkness never dims it (flames, lasers, magic, neon). It still hides behind whatever stands in front of it: walls and `r.actor` bodies do this on their own, and any other queued draw can join them with `{ solid: true }`. (Canvas lighting builds a depth-ordered mask for this; `game.r.glowMask = false` skips it on slow machines.)\"},{\"line_number\":160,\"content\":\"- `px.rect(g, x, y, w, h, c)`, `dot`, `line(g, x0, y0, x1, y1, c, width)`, `disc(g, x, y, r, c)`, `ell`, `poly(g, pts, c)`, `polyDither(g, pts, c, 0..1, r.ix, r.iy)`, `ddisc`, `sprite(g, spr, x, y, flip)` (or `{ flip, rot, scale }`), `glow(g, 0..1)` (GPU glow for what follows).\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-46420ec9-06f4-4858-a273-137acdc035ca-23","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1090→## Appendix A: tissue painter\\n\\nRan on this computer at 480x270, 3 to 5 ms a frame under software rendering. It also runs headless. One instance per site. Each frame: stamp pools, wounds and so on from `S`, then `shade(fx)`, then draw `F.cv`.\\n\\n- `stampDisc(x, y, r, height, mat)`, `stampLine(points, r, height, mat)`: per-frame height and material. Height alone (no `mat`) makes a ridge, for Legato.\\n- `shade({ beat, breath, slow, lens, light, dim, spot })`: see its comment. `dyn` and `over` clear after each shade.\\n- `slow: true` is Long Breath's palette. `lens` is Sonar's. `dim` and `spot` are the blackout. A moving `light` is the swaying lamp.\\n\\n```js\\n// Bake once per site, stamp from the sim's state each frame, then shade(). Cosmetic only: the sim never reads it. Needs E = My3D2dge in scope.\\n1100→const BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5].map(v => (v + .5) / 16 - .5);\\nconst hex3 = h => [parseInt(h.slice(1, 3), 16), parseInt(h.slice(3, 5), 16), parseInt(h.slice(5, 7), 16)];\\nfunction makeRamp(keys, n, slow) { // dark to light through hand-picked, hue-shifted keys. slow: the same ramp seen through Long Breath\\n  const c = keys.map(hex3), out = new Uint32Array(n);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const t = i / (n - 1) * (c.length - 1), j = Math.min(c.length - 2, t | 0), f = t - j; let r = c[j][0] + (c[j + 1][0] - c[j][0]) * f, g = c[j][1] + (c[j + 1][1] - c[j][1]) * f, b = c[j][2] + (c[j + 1][2] - c[j][2]) * f;\\n    if (slow) { const y = r * .3 + g * .59 + b * .11; r = y * .55 + 8; g = y * .95 + 14; b = y * 1.05 + 22; } out[i] = 0xff000000 | (Math.min(255, b) << 16) | (Math.min(255, g) << 8) | Math.min(255, r); }\\n  return out;\\n}\\nconst MAT_KEYS = { // name: [ramp keys, specular strength]\\n  wall: [['#1c060c', '#4a0f18', '#7d1f26', '#a93a38'], .35], bowel: [['#3a0e1c', '#8a2f3e', '#c75f62', '#eb9486', '#ffc9b0'], 1], liver: [['#1e0610', '#4e1022', '#7c1e30', '#a83a42', '#d0645c'], .55],\\n1110→  fat: [['#5a3a10', '#a8782a', '#dcb34c', '#f4d97e', '#fff2b8'], .7], vessel: [['#14103a', '#2c2a70', '#4a4aa0', '#7c78c8'], .8], artery: [['#3a0408', '#8c0f14', '#cf2a22', '#f4604a'], 1],\\n  skin: [['#6a3a22', '#a8683f', '#d39a68', '#eebf92'], .12], drape: [['#0c2c2a', '#14504a', '#1f7468', '#2f9a88'], 0], steel: [['#28303a', '#5a6a78', '#9aaab8', '#e8f0f8'], 1.6],\\n  blood: [['#180204', '#3c060a', '#680c10', '#8e1414'], 1.4], wound: [['#0c0104', '#2a0408', '#55090e', '#7a1216'], .5], char: [['#08070a', '#1c181a', '#332a28', '#4a3c34'], 0], gel: [['#0c4a38', '#1c8a64', '#54d0a0', '#b0ffe0'], 1.4] };\\nconst MAT_IDS = Object.keys(MAT_KEYS), MATS = MAT_IDS.map(k => ({ ramp: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20), slow: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20, true), spec: MAT_KEYS[k][1] }));\\nconst matId = n => MAT_IDS.indexOf(n);\\nfunction makeNoise(seed) { let a = seed >>> 0; const R = () => { a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0; let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), a | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };\\n  const L = new Float32Array(65536); for (let i = 0; i < L.length; i++) L[i] = R();\\n  const v = (x, y) => { const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), fx = x - xi, fy = y - yi, u = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), w = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy), s = (p, q) => L[(p & 255) | ((q & 255) << 8)]; return (s(xi, yi) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi) * u) * (1 - w) + (s(xi, yi + 1) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi + 1) * u) * w; };\\n  return { R, fbm: (x, y, o = 4) => { let k = .5, f = 1, n = 0; for (let i = 0; i < o; i++) { n += k * v(x * f, y * f); k *= .5; f *= 2.03; } return n; } }; }\\nclass TissueField {\\n1120→  constructor(W, H, seed = 7) { this.W = W; this.H = H; const N = W * H; this.h = new Float32Array(N); this.m = new Uint8Array(N); this.pulse = new Float32Array(N); this.ao = new Float32Array(N).fill(1); this.dyn = new Float32Array(N); this.over = new Uint8Array(N); this.noise = makeNoise(seed);\\n    this.cv = E.mkCanvas(W, H); this.g = this.cv.getContext('2d'); this.img = this.g.createImageData(W, H); this.u = new Uint32Array(this.img.data.buffer); }\\n  blob(x, y, rx, ry, rot, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, pulse, noise } = this, c = Math.cos(rot), s = Math.sin(rot), R = Math.max(rx, ry) + (o.warp || 0) + 2, id = matId(mat), warp = o.warp || 0, base = o.base || 0, add = !!o.add;\\n    for (let py = Math.max(0, y - R | 0); py < Math.min(H, y + R + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(0, x - R | 0); px < Math.min(W, x + R + 1); px++) {\\n      const wx = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, wy = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03 + 40, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, dx = px - x + wx, dy = py - y + wy, u = (dx * c + dy * s) / rx, v = (-dx * s + dy * c) / ry, d = u * u + v * v; if (d >= 1) continue;\\n      const i = py * W + px, top = base + hgt * Math.sqrt(1 - d); if (add) { h[i] += hgt * (1 - d); m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = Math.max(pulse[i], o.pulse * (1 - d)); } else if (top > h[i]) { h[i] = top; m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = o.pulse * (1 - d); } } }\\n  tube(pts, r, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const step = Math.max(1, r * .35); for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / step | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.blob(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, r, 0, hgt, mat, o); } }\\n  finish(detail = 1.1) { const { W, H, h, ao, noise } = this, N = W * H, blur = new Float32Array(N), tmp = new Float32Array(N), R = 7;\\n    for (let i = 0, y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++, i++) h[i] += (noise.fbm(x * .11, y * .11, 3) - .5) * detail;\\n    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { let s = 0; for (let x = -R; x <= R; x++) s += h[y * W + Math.max(0, x)]; for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { tmp[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += h[y * W + Math.min(W - 1, x + R + 1)] - h[y * W + Math.max(0, x - R)]; } }\\n1130→    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { let s = 0; for (let y = -R; y <= R; y++) s += tmp[Math.max(0, y) * W + x]; for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { blur[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += tmp[Math.min(H - 1, y + R + 1) * W + x] - tmp[Math.max(0, y - R) * W + x]; } }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) ao[i] = Math.max(.42, Math.min(1.08, 1 - (blur[i] - h[i]) * .055)); }\\n  // what the sim's objects stamp each frame, before shade(): dynamic height, and an override material\\n  stampDisc(x, y, r, hgt, mat) { const { W, H, dyn, over } = this, id = mat ? matId(mat) + 1 : 0; for (let py = Math.max(1, y - r | 0); py < Math.min(H - 1, y + r + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(1, x - r | 0); px < Math.min(W - 1, x + r + 1); px++) { const d = ((px - x) ** 2 + (py - y) ** 2) / (r * r); if (d < 1) { const i = py * W + px; dyn[i] = hgt < 0 ? Math.min(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)) : Math.max(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)); if (id) over[i] = id; } } }\\n  stampLine(pts, r, hgt, mat) { for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / Math.max(1, r * .5) | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.stampDisc(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, hgt, mat); } }\\n  // fx: { beat 0..1, breath px, slow: Long Breath palette, lens: {x, y, r} shows the cold palette inside (Sonar), light: [lx, ly], dim: 0..1 darkness, spot: {x, y, r} stays lit while dim }\\n  shade(fx = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, ao, pulse, dyn, over, u } = this, beat = fx.beat || 0, off = Math.round(fx.breath || 0) * W, slow = !!fx.slow, lens = fx.lens, lr2 = lens ? lens.r * lens.r : 0, dim = fx.dim || 0, spot = fx.spot, sr2 = spot ? spot.r * spot.r : 0, lx = fx.light ? fx.light[0] : -.42, ly = fx.light ? fx.light[1] : -.52, lz = Math.sqrt(Math.max(.1, 1 - lx * lx - ly * ly)), hl = Math.hypot(lx, ly, lz + 1), hx = lx / hl, hy = ly / hl, hz = (lz + 1) / hl;\\n    for (let y = 1; y < H - 1; y++) for (let x = 1, i = y * W + 1; x < W - 1; x++, i++) {\\n      const j = Math.max(W + 1, Math.min(W * H - W - 2, i + off)), k = 1 + beat * pulse[j], dx = (h[j - 1] - h[j + 1]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - 1] - dyn[i + 1]) * .5, dy = (h[j - W] - h[j + W]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - W] - dyn[i + W]) * .5, nl = 1 / Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + 1), nx = dx * nl, ny = dy * nl, nz = nl;\\n      const diff = Math.max(0, nx * lx + ny * ly + nz * lz), sh = Math.max(0, nx * hx + ny * hy + nz * hz), ov = over[i], M = MATS[ov ? ov - 1 : m[j]], cold = slow || (lens && (x - lens.x) ** 2 + (y - lens.y) ** 2 < lr2), r = cold ? M.slow : M.ramp, n = r.length, s2 = sh * sh, s4 = s2 * s2, s8 = s4 * s4, s16 = s8 * s8, s32 = s16 * s16;\\n1140→      const lit = dim && !(spot && (x - spot.x) ** 2 + (y - spot.y) ** 2 < sr2) ? 1 - dim : 1, lum = (diff * .92 + s8 * .16 * M.spec + beat * pulse[j] * .6) * (ov ? 1 : ao[j]) * lit, c = Math.max(0, Math.min(n - 1, (lum * (n - 1) + BAYER[(x & 3) | ((y & 3) << 2)] * 1.15 + .5) | 0));\\n      u[i] = s32 * s8 * M.spec * lit > .42 ? (cold ? 0xffffffe0 : 0xfff4f0ff) : r[c]; }\\n    this.g.putImageData(this.img, 0, 0); dyn.fill(0); over.fill(0); }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix B: a site recipe\\n\\n`F.stampDisc` coordinates here use screen pixels. To place sim objects, add `OX, OY`.\\n\\n1150→```js\\n// A site recipe: the abdomen. Design space is 426 x 240 about the screen's centre; a bigger screen only shows more drape.\\nfunction bakeAbdomen(W, H, seed = 11) { const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), cx = W / 2, cy = H / 2 - 4, n = F.noise, rx = 171, ry = 91;\\n  for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { const i = y * W + x, d = ((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2, fold = Math.sin(x * .09 + 1.6 * Math.sin(y * .05)) * 1.6 + Math.sin(y * .17 + x * .03) * .8;\\n    if (d < 1) { F.h[i] = -16 + 12 * d * d + Math.sin(x * .05 + y * .03) * 1.4; F.m[i] = matId('wall'); }            // the cavity\\n    else if (d < 1.28) { const e = (d - 1) / .28; F.h[i] = 4 + 7 * Math.sin(e * Math.PI); F.m[i] = matId('skin'); }  // lips of skin\\n    else { F.h[i] = 6 + fold; F.m[i] = matId('drape'); } }                                                            // drapes to any screen's edge\\n  F.blob(cx - rx * .55, cy - ry * .5, rx * .55, ry * .55, -.3, 17, 'liver', { base: -11, warp: 12 });\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) { const a = n.R() * 6.28, r = .55 + n.R() * .32; F.blob(cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * r, cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * r, 9 + n.R() * 14, 7 + n.R() * 9, n.R() * 3, 8, 'fat', { base: -10, warp: 8 }); }\\n  const coil = (x0, y0, len, dir, r) => { const pts = [[x0, y0]]; let a = dir, x = x0, y = y0; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * 1.5 + Math.sin(i * .9) * .5; x += Math.cos(a) * r * 1.3; y += Math.sin(a) * r * 1.3; if (((x - cx) / (rx * .92)) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / (ry * .92)) ** 2 > 1) { a += 2.4; x += Math.cos(a) * r; y += Math.sin(a) * r; } pts.push([x, y]); } return pts; };\\n1160→  F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .05, cy - ry * .25, 34, .2, 9), 11, 14, 'bowel', { base: -8 }); F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .45, cy + ry * .25, 26, 2.6, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -7 }); F.tube(coil(cx - rx * .35, cy + ry * .45, 22, -.3, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -6 });\\n  const veins = (x, y, a, len, r, mat) => { const pts = [[x, y]]; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * .8; x += Math.cos(a) * 7; y += Math.sin(a) * 7; if (((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2 > .96) break; pts.push([x, y]); if (r > 1.2 && n.R() < .22) veins(x, y, a + (n.R() < .5 ? .9 : -.9), len * .5 | 0, r * .7, mat); } F.tube(pts, r, 1.6, mat, { add: true, pulse: mat === 'artery' ? .35 : 0 }); };\\n  veins(cx - rx * .7, cy - ry * .05, -.2, 16, 2.2, 'vessel'); veins(cx + rx * .7, cy - ry * .6, 2.4, 14, 2, 'artery'); veins(cx + rx * .1, cy + ry * .75, -1.5, 12, 1.8, 'vessel');\\n  for (const a of [-.45, .5, 2.7, 3.6]) { const ex = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.02, ey = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.02, ox = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.5, oy = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.5; F.tube([[ex, ey], [ox, oy]], 4, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); F.tube([[ex - Math.sin(a) * 9, ey + Math.cos(a) * 9], [ex + Math.sin(a) * 9, ey - Math.cos(a) * 9]], 3, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); } // retractors\\n  F.finish(1.1); return F; }\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix C: portrait painter\\n\\nBusts for the four leads. The other four follow the same shape: `frontHair`, `backHair` (polygons in face space, x from the center, y down), `glasses`, `moustache`, `scar`, `cap`, `mask` (`maskUp: true` covers the mouth, for theatre), `lines`, `blush`, `jaw`, `wide`. Cache each expression to a canvas with `E.mkCanvas(112, 128)`; call `E.px.reset` on the target after drawing on it with the canvas API.\",\"content_concise\":\"1090→## Appendix A: tissue painter\\n\\nRan on this computer at 480x270, 3 to 5 ms a frame under software rendering. It also runs headless. One instance per site. Each frame: stamp pools, wounds and so on from `S`, then `shade(fx)`, then draw `F.cv`.\\n\\n- `stampDisc(x, y, r, height, mat)`, `stampLine(points, r, height, mat)`: per-frame height and material. Height alone (no `mat`) makes a ridge, for Legato.\\n- `shade({ beat, breath, slow, lens, light, dim, spot })`: see its comment. `dyn` and `over` clear after each shade.\\n- `slow: true` is Long Breath's palette. `lens` is Sonar's. `dim` and `spot` are the blackout. A moving `light` is the swaying lamp.\\n\\n```js\\n// Bake once per site, stamp from the sim's state each frame, then shade(). Cosmetic only: the sim never reads it. Needs E = My3D2dge in scope.\\n1100→const BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5].map(v => (v + .5) / 16 - .5);\\nconst hex3 = h => [parseInt(h.slice(1, 3), 16), parseInt(h.slice(3, 5), 16), parseInt(h.slice(5, 7), 16)];\\nfunction makeRamp(keys, n, slow) { // dark to light through hand-picked, hue-shifted keys. slow: the same ramp seen through Long Breath\\n  const c = keys.map(hex3), out = new Uint32Array(n);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const t = i / (n - 1) * (c.length - 1), j = Math.min(c.length - 2, t | 0), f = t - j; let r = c[j][0] + (c[j + 1][0] - c[j][0]) * f, g = c[j][1] + (c[j + 1][1] - c[j][1]) * f, b = c[j][2] + (c[j + 1][2] - c[j][2]) * f;\\n    if (slow) { const y = r * .3 + g * .59 + b * .11; r = y * .55 + 8; g = y * .95 + 14; b = y * 1.05 + 22; } out[i] = 0xff000000 | (Math.min(255, b) << 16) | (Math.min(255, g) << 8) | Math.min(255, r); }\\n  return out;\\n}\\nconst MAT_KEYS = { // name: [ramp keys, specular strength]\\n  wall: [['#1c060c', '#4a0f18', '#7d1f26', '#a93a38'], .35], bowel: [['#3a0e1c', '#8a2f3e', '#c75f62', '#eb9486', '#ffc9b0'], 1], liver: [['#1e0610', '#4e1022', '#7c1e30', '#a83a42', '#d0645c'], .55],\\n1110→  fat: [['#5a3a10', '#a8782a', '#dcb34c', '#f4d97e', '#fff2b8'], .7], vessel: [['#14103a', '#2c2a70', '#4a4aa0', '#7c78c8'], .8], artery: [['#3a0408', '#8c0f14', '#cf2a22', '#f4604a'], 1],\\n  skin: [['#6a3a22', '#a8683f', '#d39a68', '#eebf92'], .12], drape: [['#0c2c2a', '#14504a', '#1f7468', '#2f9a88'], 0], steel: [['#28303a', '#5a6a78', '#9aaab8', '#e8f0f8'], 1.6],\\n  blood: [['#180204', '#3c060a', '#680c10', '#8e1414'], 1.4], wound: [['#0c0104', '#2a0408', '#55090e', '#7a1216'], .5], char: [['#08070a', '#1c181a', '#332a28', '#4a3c34'], 0], gel: [['#0c4a38', '#1c8a64', '#54d0a0', '#b0ffe0'], 1.4] };\\nconst MAT_IDS = Object.keys(MAT_KEYS), MATS = MAT_IDS.map(k => ({ ramp: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20), slow: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20, true), spec: MAT_KEYS[k][1] }));\\nconst matId = n => MAT_IDS.indexOf(n);\\nfunction makeNoise(seed) { let a = seed >>> 0; const R = () => { a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0; let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), a | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };\\n  const L = new Float32Array(65536); for (let i = 0; i < L.length; i++) L[i] = R();\\n  const v = (x, y) => { const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), fx = x - xi, fy = y - yi, u = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), w = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy), s = (p, q) => L[(p & 255) | ((q & 255) << 8)]; return (s(xi, yi) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi) * u) * (1 - w) + (s(xi, yi + 1) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi + 1) * u) * w; };\\n  return { R, fbm: (x, y, o = 4) => { let k = .5, f = 1, n = 0; for (let i = 0; i < o; i++) { n += k * v(x * f, y * f); k *= .5; f *= 2.03; } return n; } }; }\\nclass TissueField {\\n1120→  constructor(W, H, seed = 7) { this.W = W; this.H = H; const N = W * H; this.h = new Float32Array(N); this.m = new Uint8Array(N); this.pulse = new Float32Array(N); this.ao = new Float32Array(N).fill(1); this.dyn = new Float32Array(N); this.over = new Uint8Array(N); this.noise = makeNoise(seed);\\n    this.cv = E.mkCanvas(W, H); this.g = this.cv.getContext('2d'); this.img = this.g.createImageData(W, H); this.u = new Uint32Array(this.img.data.buffer); }\\n  blob(x, y, rx, ry, rot, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, pulse, noise } = this, c = Math.cos(rot), s = Math.sin(rot), R = Math.max(rx, ry) + (o.warp || 0) + 2, id = matId(mat), warp = o.warp || 0, base = o.base || 0, add = !!o.add;\\n    for (let py = Math.max(0, y - R | 0); py < Math.min(H, y + R + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(0, x - R | 0); px < Math.min(W, x + R + 1); px++) {\\n      const wx = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, wy = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03 + 40, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, dx = px - x + wx, dy = py - y + wy, u = (dx * c + dy * s) / rx, v = (-dx * s + dy * c) / ry, d = u * u + v * v; if (d >= 1) continue;\\n      const i = py * W + px, top = base + hgt * Math.sqrt(1 - d); if (add) { h[i] += hgt * (1 - d); m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = Math.max(pulse[i], o.pulse * (1 - d)); } else if (top > h[i]) { h[i] = top; m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = o.pulse * (1 - d); } } }\\n  tube(pts, r, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const step = Math.max(1, r * .35); for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / step | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.blob(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, r, 0, hgt, mat, o); } }\\n  finish(detail = 1.1) { const { W, H, h, ao, noise } = this, N = W * H, blur = new Float32Array(N), tmp = new Float32Array(N), R = 7;\\n    for (let i = 0, y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++, i++) h[i] += (noise.fbm(x * .11, y * .11, 3) - .5) * detail;\\n    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { let s = 0; for (let x = -R; x <= R; x++) s += h[y * W + Math.max(0, x)]; for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { tmp[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += h[y * W + Math.min(W - 1, x + R + 1)] - h[y * W + Math.max(0, x - R)]; } }\\n1130→    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { let s = 0; for (let y = -R; y <= R; y++) s += tmp[Math.max(0, y) * W + x]; for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { blur[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += tmp[Math.min(H - 1, y + R + 1) * W + x] - tmp[Math.max(0, y - R) * W + x]; } }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) ao[i] = Math.max(.42, Math.min(1.08, 1 - (blur[i] - h[i]) * .055)); }\\n  // what the sim's objects stamp each frame, before shade(): dynamic height, and an override material\\n  stampDisc(x, y, r, hgt, mat) { const { W, H, dyn, over } = this, id = mat ? matId(mat) + 1 : 0; for (let py = Math.max(1, y - r | 0); py < Math.min(H - 1, y + r + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(1, x - r | 0); px < Math.min(W - 1, x + r + 1); px++) { const d = ((px - x) ** 2 + (py - y) ** 2) / (r * r); if (d < 1) { const i = py * W + px; dyn[i] = hgt < 0 ? Math.min(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)) : Math.max(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)); if (id) over[i] = id; } } }\\n  stampLine(pts, r, hgt, mat) { for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / Math.max(1, r * .5) | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.stampDisc(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, hgt, mat); } }\\n  // fx: { beat 0..1, breath px, slow: Long Breath palette, lens: {x, y, r} shows the cold palette inside (Sonar), light: [lx, ly], dim: 0..1 darkness, spot: {x, y, r} stays lit while dim }\\n  shade(fx = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, ao, pulse, dyn, over, u } = this, beat = fx.beat || 0, off = Math.round(fx.breath || 0) * W, slow = !!fx.slow, lens = fx.lens, lr2 = lens ? lens.r * lens.r : 0, dim = fx.dim || 0, spot = fx.spot, sr2 = spot ? spot.r * spot.r : 0, lx = fx.light ? fx.light[0] : -.42, ly = fx.light ? fx.light[1] : -.52, lz = Math.sqrt(Math.max(.1, 1 - lx * lx - ly * ly)), hl = Math.hypot(lx, ly, lz + 1), hx = lx / hl, hy = ly / hl, hz = (lz + 1) / hl;\\n    for (let y = 1; y < H - 1; y++) for (let x = 1, i = y * W + 1; x < W - 1; x++, i++) {\\n      const j = Math.max(W + 1, Math.min(W * H - W - 2, i + off)), k = 1 + beat * pulse[j], dx = (h[j - 1] - h[j + 1]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - 1] - dyn[i + 1]) * .5, dy = (h[j - W] - h[j + W]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - W] - dyn[i + W]) * .5, nl = 1 / Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + 1), nx = dx * nl, ny = dy * nl, nz = nl;\\n      const diff = Math.max(0, nx * lx + ny * ly + nz * lz), sh = Math.max(0, nx * hx + ny * hy + nz * hz), ov = over[i], M = MATS[ov ? ov - 1 : m[j]], cold = slow || (lens && (x - lens.x) ** 2 + (y - lens.y) ** 2 < lr2), r = cold ? M.slow : M.ramp, n = r.length, s2 = sh * sh, s4 = s2 * s2, s8 = s4 * s4, s16 = s8 * s8, s32 = s16 * s16;\\n1140→      const lit = dim && !(spot && (x - spot.x) ** 2 + (y - spot.y) ** 2 < sr2) ? 1 - dim : 1, lum = (diff * .92 + s8 * .16 * M.spec + beat * pulse[j] * .6) * (ov ? 1 : ao[j]) * lit, c = Math.max(0, Math.min(n - 1, (lum * (n - 1) + BAYER[(x & 3) | ((y & 3) << 2)] * 1.15 + .5) | 0));\\n      u[i] = s32 * s8 * M.spec * lit > .42 ? (cold ? 0xffffffe0 : 0xfff4f0ff) : r[c]; }\\n    this.g.putImageData(this.img, 0, 0); dyn.fill(0); over.fill(0); }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix B: a site recipe\\n\\n`F.stampDisc` coordinates here use screen pixels. To place sim objects, add `OX, OY`.\\n\\n1150→```js\\n// A site recipe: the abdomen. Design space is 426 x 240 about the screen's centre; a bigger screen only shows more drape.\\nfunction bakeAbdomen(W, H, seed = 11) { const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), cx = W / 2, cy = H / 2 - 4, n = F.noise, rx = 171, ry = 91;\\n  for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { const i = y * W + x, d = ((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2, fold = Math.sin(x * .09 + 1.6 * Math.sin(y * .05)) * 1.6 + Math.sin(y * .17 + x * .03) * .8;\\n    if (d < 1) { F.h[i] = -16 + 12 * d * d + Math.sin(x * .05 + y * .03) * 1.4; F.m[i] = matId('wall'); }            // the cavity\\n    else if (d < 1.28) { const e = (d - 1) / .28; F.h[i] = 4 + 7 * Math.sin(e * Math.PI); F.m[i] = matId('skin'); }  // lips of skin\\n    else { F.h[i] = 6 + fold; F.m[i] = matId('drape'); } }                                                            // drapes to any screen's edge\\n  F.blob(cx - rx * .55, cy - ry * .5, rx * .55, ry * .55, -.3, 17, 'liver', { base: -11, warp: 12 });\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) { const a = n.R() * 6.28, r = .55 + n.R() * .32; F.blob(cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * r, cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * r, 9 + n.R() * 14, 7 + n.R() * 9, n.R() * 3, 8, 'fat', { base: -10, warp: 8 }); }\\n  const coil = (x0, y0, len, dir, r) => { const pts = [[x0, y0]]; let a = dir, x = x0, y = y0; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * 1.5 + Math.sin(i * .9) * .5; x += Math.cos(a) * r * 1.3; y += Math.sin(a) * r * 1.3; if (((x - cx) / (rx * .92)) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / (ry * .92)) ** 2 > 1) { a += 2.4; x += Math.cos(a) * r; y += Math.sin(a) * r; } pts.push([x, y]); } return pts; };\\n1160→  F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .05, cy - ry * .25, 34, .2, 9), 11, 14, 'bowel', { base: -8 }); F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .45, cy + ry * .25, 26, 2.6, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -7 }); F.tube(coil(cx - rx * .35, cy + ry * .45, 22, -.3, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -6 });\\n  const veins = (x, y, a, len, r, mat) => { const pts = [[x, y]]; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * .8; x += Math.cos(a) * 7; y += Math.sin(a) * 7; if (((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2 > .96) break; pts.push([x, y]); if (r > 1.2 && n.R() < .22) veins(x, y, a + (n.R() < .5 ? .9 : -.9), len * .5 | 0, r * .7, mat); } F.tube(pts, r, 1.6, mat, { add: true, pulse: mat === 'artery' ? .35 : 0 }); };\\n  veins(cx - rx * .7, cy - ry * .05, -.2, 16, 2.2, 'vessel'); veins(cx + rx * .7, cy - ry * .6, 2.4, 14, 2, 'artery'); veins(cx + rx * .1, cy + ry * .75, -1.5, 12, 1.8, 'vessel');\\n  for (const a of [-.45, .5, 2.7, 3.6]) { const ex = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.02, ey = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.02, ox = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.5, oy = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.5; F.tube([[ex, ey], [ox, oy]], 4, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); F.tube([[ex - Math.sin(a) * 9, ey + Math.cos(a) * 9], [ex + Math.sin(a) * 9, ey - Math.cos(a) * 9]], 3, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); } // retractors\\n  F.finish(1.1); return F; }\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix C: portrait painter\\n\\nBusts for the four leads. The other four follow the same shape: `frontHair`, `backHair` (polygons in face space, x from the center, y down), `glasses`, `moustache`, `scar`, `cap`, `mask` (`maskUp: true` covers the mouth, for theatre), `lines`, `blush`, `jaw`, `wide`. Cache each expression to a canvas with `E.mkCanvas(112, 128)`; call `E.px.reset` on the target after drawing on it with the canvas API.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1090,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"## Appendix A: tissue painter\\n\\nRan on this computer at 480x270, 3 to 5 ms a frame under software rendering. It also runs headless. One instance per site. Each frame: stamp pools, wounds and so on from `S`, then `shade(fx)`, then draw `F.cv`.\\n\\n- `stampDisc(x, y, r, height, mat)`, `stampLine(points, r, height, mat)`: per-frame height and material. Height alone (no `mat`) makes a ridge, for Legato.\\n- `shade({ beat, breath, slow, lens, light, dim, spot })`: see its comment. `dyn` and `over` clear after each shade.\\n- `slow: true` is Long Breath's palette. `lens` is Sonar's. `dim` and `spot` are the blackout. A moving `light` is the swaying lamp.\\n\\n```js\\n// Bake once per site, stamp from the sim's state each frame, then shade(). Cosmetic only: the sim never reads it. Needs E = My3D2dge in scope.\\nconst BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5].map(v => (v + .5) / 16 - .5);\\nconst hex3 = h => [parseInt(h.slice(1, 3), 16), parseInt(h.slice(3, 5), 16), parseInt(h.slice(5, 7), 16)];\\nfunction makeRamp(keys, n, slow) { // dark to light through hand-picked, hue-shifted keys. slow: the same ramp seen through Long Breath\\n  const c = keys.map(hex3), out = new Uint32Array(n);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const t = i / (n - 1) * (c.length - 1), j = Math.min(c.length - 2, t | 0), f = t - j; let r = c[j][0] + (c[j + 1][0] - c[j][0]) * f, g = c[j][1] + (c[j + 1][1] - c[j][1]) * f, b = c[j][2] + (c[j + 1][2] - c[j][2]) * f;\\n    if (slow) { const y = r * .3 + g * .59 + b * .11; r = y * .55 + 8; g = y * .95 + 14; b = y * 1.05 + 22; } out[i] = 0xff000000 | (Math.min(255, b) << 16) | (Math.min(255, g) << 8) | Math.min(255, r); }\\n  return out;\\n}\\nconst MAT_KEYS = { // name: [ramp keys, specular strength]\\n  wall: [['#1c060c', '#4a0f18', '#7d1f26', '#a93a38'], .35], bowel: [['#3a0e1c', '#8a2f3e', '#c75f62', '#eb9486', '#ffc9b0'], 1], liver: [['#1e0610', '#4e1022', '#7c1e30', '#a83a42', '#d0645c'], .55],\\n  fat: [['#5a3a10', '#a8782a', '#dcb34c', '#f4d97e', '#fff2b8'], .7], vessel: [['#14103a', '#2c2a70', '#4a4aa0', '#7c78c8'], .8], artery: [['#3a0408', '#8c0f14', '#cf2a22', '#f4604a'], 1],\\n  skin: [['#6a3a22', '#a8683f', '#d39a68', '#eebf92'], .12], drape: [['#0c2c2a', '#14504a', '#1f7468', '#2f9a88'], 0], steel: [['#28303a', '#5a6a78', '#9aaab8', '#e8f0f8'], 1.6],\\n  blood: [['#180204', '#3c060a', '#680c10', '#8e1414'], 1.4], wound: [['#0c0104', '#2a0408', '#55090e', '#7a1216'], .5], char: [['#08070a', '#1c181a', '#332a28', '#4a3c34'], 0], gel: [['#0c4a38', '#1c8a64', '#54d0a0', '#b0ffe0'], 1.4] };\\nconst MAT_IDS = Object.keys(MAT_KEYS), MATS = MAT_IDS.map(k => ({ ramp: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20), slow: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20, true), spec: MAT_KEYS[k][1] }));\\nconst matId = n => MAT_IDS.indexOf(n);\\nfunction makeNoise(seed) { let a = seed >>> 0; const R = () => { a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0; let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), a | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };\\n  const L = new Float32Array(65536); for (let i = 0; i < L.length; i++) L[i] = R();\\n  const v = (x, y) => { const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), fx = x - xi, fy = y - yi, u = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), w = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy), s = (p, q) => L[(p & 255) | ((q & 255) << 8)]; return (s(xi, yi) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi) * u) * (1 - w) + (s(xi, yi + 1) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi + 1) * u) * w; };\\n  return { R, fbm: (x, y, o = 4) => { let k = .5, f = 1, n = 0; for (let i = 0; i < o; i++) { n += k * v(x * f, y * f); k *= .5; f *= 2.03; } return n; } }; }\\nclass TissueField {\\n  constructor(W, H, seed = 7) { this.W = W; this.H = H; const N = W * H; this.h = new Float32Array(N); this.m = new Uint8Array(N); this.pulse = new Float32Array(N); this.ao = new Float32Array(N).fill(1); this.dyn = new Float32Array(N); this.over = new Uint8Array(N); this.noise = makeNoise(seed);\\n    this.cv = E.mkCanvas(W, H); this.g = this.cv.getContext('2d'); this.img = this.g.createImageData(W, H); this.u = new Uint32Array(this.img.data.buffer); }\\n  blob(x, y, rx, ry, rot, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, pulse, noise } = this, c = Math.cos(rot), s = Math.sin(rot), R = Math.max(rx, ry) + (o.warp || 0) + 2, id = matId(mat), warp = o.warp || 0, base = o.base || 0, add = !!o.add;\\n    for (let py = Math.max(0, y - R | 0); py < Math.min(H, y + R + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(0, x - R | 0); px < Math.min(W, x + R + 1); px++) {\\n      const wx = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, wy = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03 + 40, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, dx = px - x + wx, dy = py - y + wy, u = (dx * c + dy * s) / rx, v = (-dx * s + dy * c) / ry, d = u * u + v * v; if (d >= 1) continue;\\n      const i = py * W + px, top = base + hgt * Math.sqrt(1 - d); if (add) { h[i] += hgt * (1 - d); m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = Math.max(pulse[i], o.pulse * (1 - d)); } else if (top > h[i]) { h[i] = top; m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = o.pulse * (1 - d); } } }\\n  tube(pts, r, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const step = Math.max(1, r * .35); for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / step | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.blob(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, r, 0, hgt, mat, o); } }\\n  finish(detail = 1.1) { const { W, H, h, ao, noise } = this, N = W * H, blur = new Float32Array(N), tmp = new Float32Array(N), R = 7;\\n    for (let i = 0, y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++, i++) h[i] += (noise.fbm(x * .11, y * .11, 3) - .5) * detail;\\n    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { let s = 0; for (let x = -R; x <= R; x++) s += h[y * W + Math.max(0, x)]; for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { tmp[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += h[y * W + Math.min(W - 1, x + R + 1)] - h[y * W + Math.max(0, x - R)]; } }\\n    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { let s = 0; for (let y = -R; y <= R; y++) s += tmp[Math.max(0, y) * W + x]; for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { blur[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += tmp[Math.min(H - 1, y + R + 1) * W + x] - tmp[Math.max(0, y - R) * W + x]; } }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) ao[i] = Math.max(.42, Math.min(1.08, 1 - (blur[i] - h[i]) * .055)); }\\n  // what the sim's objects stamp each frame, before shade(): dynamic height, and an override material\\n  stampDisc(x, y, r, hgt, mat) { const { W, H, dyn, over } = this, id = mat ? matId(mat) + 1 : 0; for (let py = Math.max(1, y - r | 0); py < Math.min(H - 1, y + r + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(1, x - r | 0); px < Math.min(W - 1, x + r + 1); px++) { const d = ((px - x) ** 2 + (py - y) ** 2) / (r * r); if (d < 1) { const i = py * W + px; dyn[i] = hgt < 0 ? Math.min(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)) : Math.max(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)); if (id) over[i] = id; } } }\\n  stampLine(pts, r, hgt, mat) { for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / Math.max(1, r * .5) | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.stampDisc(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, hgt, mat); } }\\n  // fx: { beat 0..1, breath px, slow: Long Breath palette, lens: {x, y, r} shows the cold palette inside (Sonar), light: [lx, ly], dim: 0..1 darkness, spot: {x, y, r} stays lit while dim }\\n  shade(fx = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, ao, pulse, dyn, over, u } = this, beat = fx.beat || 0, off = Math.round(fx.breath || 0) * W, slow = !!fx.slow, lens = fx.lens, lr2 = lens ? lens.r * lens.r : 0, dim = fx.dim || 0, spot = fx.spot, sr2 = spot ? spot.r * spot.r : 0, lx = fx.light ? fx.light[0] : -.42, ly = fx.light ? fx.light[1] : -.52, lz = Math.sqrt(Math.max(.1, 1 - lx * lx - ly * ly)), hl = Math.hypot(lx, ly, lz + 1), hx = lx / hl, hy = ly / hl, hz = (lz + 1) / hl;\\n    for (let y = 1; y < H - 1; y++) for (let x = 1, i = y * W + 1; x < W - 1; x++, i++) {\\n      const j = Math.max(W + 1, Math.min(W * H - W - 2, i + off)), k = 1 + beat * pulse[j], dx = (h[j - 1] - h[j + 1]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - 1] - dyn[i + 1]) * .5, dy = (h[j - W] - h[j + W]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - W] - dyn[i + W]) * .5, nl = 1 / Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + 1), nx = dx * nl, ny = dy * nl, nz = nl;\\n      const diff = Math.max(0, nx * lx + ny * ly + nz * lz), sh = Math.max(0, nx * hx + ny * hy + nz * hz), ov = over[i], M = MATS[ov ? ov - 1 : m[j]], cold = slow || (lens && (x - lens.x) ** 2 + (y - lens.y) ** 2 < lr2), r = cold ? M.slow : M.ramp, n = r.length, s2 = sh * sh, s4 = s2 * s2, s8 = s4 * s4, s16 = s8 * s8, s32 = s16 * s16;\\n      const lit = dim && !(spot && (x - spot.x) ** 2 + (y - spot.y) ** 2 < sr2) ? 1 - dim : 1, lum = (diff * .92 + s8 * .16 * M.spec + beat * pulse[j] * .6) * (ov ? 1 : ao[j]) * lit, c = Math.max(0, Math.min(n - 1, (lum * (n - 1) + BAYER[(x & 3) | ((y & 3) << 2)] * 1.15 + .5) | 0));\\n      u[i] = s32 * s8 * M.spec * lit > .42 ? (cold ? 0xffffffe0 : 0xfff4f0ff) : r[c]; }\\n    this.g.putImageData(this.img, 0, 0); dyn.fill(0); over.fill(0); }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix B: a site recipe\\n\\n`F.stampDisc` coordinates here use screen pixels. To place sim objects, add `OX, OY`.\\n\\n```js\\n// A site recipe: the abdomen. Design space is 426 x 240 about the screen's centre; a bigger screen only shows more drape.\\nfunction bakeAbdomen(W, H, seed = 11) { const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), cx = W / 2, cy = H / 2 - 4, n = F.noise, rx = 171, ry = 91;\\n  for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { const i = y * W + x, d = ((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2, fold = Math.sin(x * .09 + 1.6 * Math.sin(y * .05)) * 1.6 + Math.sin(y * .17 + x * .03) * .8;\\n    if (d < 1) { F.h[i] = -16 + 12 * d * d + Math.sin(x * .05 + y * .03) * 1.4; F.m[i] = matId('wall'); }            // the cavity\\n    else if (d < 1.28) { const e = (d - 1) / .28; F.h[i] = 4 + 7 * Math.sin(e * Math.PI); F.m[i] = matId('skin'); }  // lips of skin\\n    else { F.h[i] = 6 + fold; F.m[i] = matId('drape'); } }                                                            // drapes to any screen's edge\\n  F.blob(cx - rx * .55, cy - ry * .5, rx * .55, ry * .55, -.3, 17, 'liver', { base: -11, warp: 12 });\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) { const a = n.R() * 6.28, r = .55 + n.R() * .32; F.blob(cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * r, cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * r, 9 + n.R() * 14, 7 + n.R() * 9, n.R() * 3, 8, 'fat', { base: -10, warp: 8 }); }\\n  const coil = (x0, y0, len, dir, r) => { const pts = [[x0, y0]]; let a = dir, x = x0, y = y0; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * 1.5 + Math.sin(i * .9) * .5; x += Math.cos(a) * r * 1.3; y += Math.sin(a) * r * 1.3; if (((x - cx) / (rx * .92)) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / (ry * .92)) ** 2 > 1) { a += 2.4; x += Math.cos(a) * r; y += Math.sin(a) * r; } pts.push([x, y]); } return pts; };\\n  F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .05, cy - ry * .25, 34, .2, 9), 11, 14, 'bowel', { base: -8 }); F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .45, cy + ry * .25, 26, 2.6, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -7 }); F.tube(coil(cx - rx * .35, cy + ry * .45, 22, -.3, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -6 });\\n  const veins = (x, y, a, len, r, mat) => { const pts = [[x, y]]; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * .8; x += Math.cos(a) * 7; y += Math.sin(a) * 7; if (((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2 > .96) break; pts.push([x, y]); if (r > 1.2 && n.R() < .22) veins(x, y, a + (n.R() < .5 ? .9 : -.9), len * .5 | 0, r * .7, mat); } F.tube(pts, r, 1.6, mat, { add: true, pulse: mat === 'artery' ? .35 : 0 }); };\\n  veins(cx - rx * .7, cy - ry * .05, -.2, 16, 2.2, 'vessel'); veins(cx + rx * .7, cy - ry * .6, 2.4, 14, 2, 'artery'); veins(cx + rx * .1, cy + ry * .75, -1.5, 12, 1.8, 'vessel');\\n  for (const a of [-.45, .5, 2.7, 3.6]) { const ex = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.02, ey = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.02, ox = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.5, oy = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.5; F.tube([[ex, ey], [ox, oy]], 4, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); F.tube([[ex - Math.sin(a) * 9, ey + Math.cos(a) * 9], [ex + Math.sin(a) * 9, ey - Math.cos(a) * 9]], 3, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); } // retractors\\n  F.finish(1.1); return F; }\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix C: portrait painter\\n\\nBusts for the four leads. The other four follow the same shape: `frontHair`, `backHair` (polygons in face space, x from the center, y down), `glasses`, `moustache`, `scar`, `cap`, `mask` (`maskUp: true` covers the mouth, for theatre), `lines`, `blush`, `jaw`, `wide`. Cache each expression to a canvas with `E.mkCanvas(112, 128)`; call `E.px.reset` on the target after drawing on it with the canvas API.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1339}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"70c88d1d-94c8-4c7c-8c14-1478e9b3cf83"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_49","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to figure out how to get the drawing context in a scene.\n\nI'll use `r.overlay` to draw the surgery field and title in screen space. The renderer's width and height are available as `r.W` and `r.H`.\n\nI'll set the resolution to [426, 240] with expand true. The tissue canvas will be drawn onto the game buffer using drawImage.\n\n`drawImage(F.cv, OX, OY)` is permitted in the overlay. Headless mode uses a null canvas so the call does nothing. The shade computation still runs. At 120fps the 426×240 tissue field costs roughly 100k pixels per frame. That should be fine for short test runs.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-43b516c0-bb14-4b36-8be8-ad0469ead081-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md","offset":1188,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-43b516c0-bb14-4b36-8be8-ad0469ead081-25","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"glyphs|music:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API.md","head_limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12383,"output_tokens":927,"cache_read_input_tokens":105856,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"2bcdae93-4faf-4a6c-9053-67eec2ef6e24"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-43b516c0-bb14-4b36-8be8-ad0469ead081-24","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1188→- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\\n- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\\n1190→- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\\n- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\\n- `shell.back()` †: what cancel does: the screen's own back(), or close it (back to the screen under it; closing the pause screen resumes)\\n- `shell.dispose()` †: take its elements away and let go of the game (game.dispose() does it)\\n- `shell.hide()` †: close every screen (and resume, when the menu paused the game)\\n- `shell.hud(st = {})` †: the HUD, from this step's state (call it every step; a piece left out is hidden, and only what changed is redrawn)\\n- `shell.hud({ objective })` †: { step: '01 / 04', title, text, at: { x, y, z }, from: hero } (the distance in meters, and above or below)\\n- `shell.hud({ status, place, tip })` †: status: 'UNSEEN' or { text, color }; place: 'The Old Harbour'; tip: 'text' or { title, text }\\n- `shell.hud({ bars, counts })` †: bars: [{ label, value, max, kind: 'bar' | 'pips', color }] (health, stamina, a meter); counts: [[label, value]]\\n- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\\n1200→- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\\n- `shell.hud({ minimap })` †: { map, at (with facing), markers: [{ x, y, kind: 'dot' | 'diamond' | 'ring' | 'cross', color }], onClick(x, y) (the world point clicked), fog (an E.Fog: unseen cells black, seen ones dim), camera: true (the ground the screen shows) }\\n- `shell.screen` †: the name of the open screen ('pause', 'settings', 'controls', ...), or null while the game plays\\n- `shell.settings` †: the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key)\\n- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act, primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel), rows: ['glyphs', 'invertY', '#A heading'] (settings' rows, changed as on the settings screen) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates (the new spec over the old). 'settings' takes its items\\n- `shell.show('title')` †: { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\\n- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\\n- `shell.show('results')` †: { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\\n- `shell.show('map')` †: { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) }\\n- `shell.toast(title, text = '', seconds = 4)` †: a message that slides in at the top for a few seconds\\n1210→- `shell.tutorial(title, text = '', seconds = 15)` †: a tutorial card (bottom left, dismissable) for some seconds; tutorial(null) takes it away\\n- `shell.root = null` †: game: the game it is over; o: its options; root: its DOM element (null in a headless game)\\n\\n## 22. Gpu lighting (webgpu)\\n\\n- `game.gpu.active(view)` †: true when it lights frames in this view (ready, enabled and a ground view)\\n- `game.gpu.snapshot()` †: offscreen mode only: read the last frame back as a PNG data URL\\n- `game.gpu.status()` †: 'loading' | 'on' | 'off' | 'unavailable'\\n- `game.gpu.adapterInfo` †: the GPU's description from the browser (vendor, architecture), or null\\n- `game.gpu.ambient` †: the unlit color, [r, g, b] 0..1\\n1220→- `game.gpu.bands = 6` †: how many light bands (fewer is more retro)\\n- `game.gpu.enabled = true` †: false switches it off for now (and the canvas lighting with it, unless game.lights.enabled)\\n- `game.gpu.failed = null` †: why it couldn't start, or null\\n- `game.gpu.fallback = true` †: false keeps a frame it can't draw unlit (by default the canvas lighting stands in, game.lights.on)\\n- `game.gpu.glow = .22` †: the strength of px.glow surfaces\\n- `game.gpu.map = null` †: the TileMap it measures walls on\\n- `game.gpu.offscreen = false` †: render into a texture instead of the page (automated tests; read it with snapshot())\\n- `game.gpu.onStatus = null` †: called (gpu) when its status changes\\n- `game.gpu.ready = false` †: true once the GPU is set up\\n- `game.gpu.shadows = true` †: casters block light\\n1230→- `game.gpu.skipped` †: never queue more than two frames: a slow GPU drops frames instead of building up lag\\n- `game.gpu.spill = 1.1` †: how far light spills past its radius\\n- `game.gpu.wrap = .45` †: how far light wraps round wall corners, 0..1\\n\\n## 23. Sessions\\n\\n- `E.session` †: records a play session on any device and replays it exactly (this section's header says how)\\n- `E.session.frame` †: the frames run since the page loaded\",\"content_concise\":\"1188→- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\\n- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\\n1190→- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version sa