{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_80","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bot is attempting to suture at coordinates 205, 108, but the wound is located at 213, 120.\n\nThe bot is at the first stitch point 205, 108. The stitch array exists but stroke is null. The suture logic requires a valid stroke index to begin.\n\nThe edge trigger should fire since trigitude jumps from 0 to 1. The nearest target is the wound pair at the exact stitch point, so distance is not the issue. The suspicion now shifts to whether prevTrig is already 1 when step runs.\n\nThe suture tool is correctly mapped to digit 3. The next step is to log the player's internal trig, trigEdge, and prevTrig fields after each step, since the current logs only show the raw device value.\n\nThe readInputs logic sets trigEdge and updates prevTrig before applyTools runs. The next step is to log the stitch pairs, player position, and whether trigEdge was consumed after each step.\n\nThe debug script will be modified to dump the wound pairs and player position. The needle is already at the stitch point when trigitude hits 0, so the jump from 0 to 1 on frame 1 should trigger an edge, yet stroke remains null. This suggests the edge event may not be registering despite the value change.\n\nCursor.update bypasses readInputs, but the step function still computes position and velocity correctly. The swap cooldown does not block suture. The tool mapping from wheel input to CFG.TOOLS is also correct. The next step is to re-read stepSuture to check for recent edits that might have broken it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9acb79ff-1896-4d1d-95df-36255e5bfd0e-83","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":600,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id"