e 6 u over healthy tissue with no guide is a slip. Crossing a nerve or eloquent line costs vitals -12 and always counts as a slip.\"},{\"line_number\":244,\"content\":\"**Suture.** A wound has N stitches, each a pair of points across it. Press within 9 u of the next near point, carry across, release within 6 u of the far point. A bad release is a loose stitch (vitals -1, redo it). Each stitch set closes 1/N of the wound and cuts its bleeding. Per stitch: .6 s or less is Textbook, 1.2 s or less is Clean. The wound's grade is the mean. The needle arcs across, the thread pulls tight with a pop, and the wound's lips close on the field.\"},{\"line_number\":272,\"content\":\"**Consult (Cases 10 and 11).** □ or C hands over to the other doctor in .4 s. Gauge shared, each doctor's gift and passive apply: Vale has +15% cursor speed and +25% Sonar radius; Sokolova has +.2 assist and +1 u suture tolerance.\"},{\"line_number\":804,\"content\":\"Each tool: a steel instrument drawn by `E.px` from its tip, with the gloved hand behind it. Forceps open and close on the trigger; the scalpel's blade catches light; the needle arcs and trails blue thread; the syringe's barrel fills; the cautery's tip glows hot; the suction wand shakes; the sonar probe ripples. Wheel tiles: 20 x 20, one strong silhouette each.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"1f6a9693-46fd-47e4-a25f-131d44365124"}
