.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/ferm.js\",\"truncated\":true,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Log fermata stage timing and bot actions\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/terminal/call-34efd43f-c2cc-4f73-adb9-0b7760c68d8b-38.log\",\"total_bytes\":52064}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"1e45f881-95cc-49dd-81c3-5df442ff03cb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_105","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A bug was found: the dome timer goes negative and sticks at t=6.\n\nThe root cause is the `!st.eyeOpen` check. Once `eyeOpen` turns slightly negative, the condition fails and the eye stays closed.\n\nThe fix is to replace `!st.eyeOpen` with `st.eyeOpen <= 0`. This lets the eye reopen once the timer expires.\n\nThe fix for the stuck eye timer is confirmed to work correctly.\n\nA gift spam bug was also found. Steady jumps from 13 to 23 in half a second after a hit, suggesting the award function gives too much steady. The bot then repeatedly asks \"why gift\" while steady drops from 25 to 7.\n\nThe gift spam is not caused by the steady thresholds. Neither gift condition triggers at steady 24. The \"gift\" return must come from the consult flag instead.\n\nThe consult flag is permanently true because needLook remains active while activeDoc stays vale. This forces the gift action every frame and prevents normal operation. tryGifts toggles activeDoc on each consult edge.\n\nThe consult flag is set every frame, but only the first frame creates a consult edge. After that, consultPrev stays true and no further edges fire. activeDoc therefore toggles just once to sokolova. The gift spam is not caused by repeated consult edges.\n\nThe consult flag is permanently true because the function returns early every frame. This prevents any consult edge from firing after the first toggle. The bot therefore stays stuck sending consult and never burns.\n\nThe fix is to make consult a one-shot rising edge. The bot should send consult for exactly one frame when the needed doctor is inactive, then clear the flag so normal operation can resume.\n\nThe consult pulse should be conditional. It should only fire when the needed doctor is inactive and the other flag is not active, preventing toggling between both doctors at once.\n\nThe consult pulse should prioritize the newer need. If both flags are active, the bot should switch to Sokolova once and then stop consulting so it can operate normally.\n\nThe consult pulse should be a single-frame edge. It fires only when the needed doctor is inactive and sets a 0.6-second cooldown. Once the bot switches to Sokolova, the flag clears and surgery resumes normally.\n\nThe first eye window was hit without breath because the consult lock blocked it. Later windows failed for the same reason.\n\nA new risk was found. The second Look gift condition fires every 0.5 seconds once steady reaches 45 and needLook stays true. This could loop rewind forever if the bot keeps triggering it. The sim may also rewind state including steady when second Look succeeds.\n\nRewind restores steady to its value six seconds ago. If steady drops below 45 after a rewind, it charges back up and triggers another rewind. This creates an infinite loop.\n\nThe bot should only use Second Look when a recent slip actually requires undoing. The needLook flag is meant as that signal, but the bot currently consumes it once and then keeps reusing it.\n\nThe bot should track consumed requests in memory. It will set `didBreath` and `didLook` only when it actually fires a gift. This prevents repeated use of the same flag and avoids the infinite rewind loop.\n\nFiring Second Look during fermata would rewind eye hits and erase progress. The plan is to use Long Breath to widen the eye window, then consult Sokolova only if a slip actually occurs. The needLook flag at t=6 signals that undoing is now possible, not an immediate command to rewind.\n\nConsult will be a one-frame pulse that does not block the burn. Long Breath fires once when steady reaches 35 and needBreath is active, again without blocking the burn. Second Look will only trigger after a recent slip or a memory flag, not continuously.\n\nThe concrete implementation is now drafted. Consult pulses once per doctor when the flag changes. Long Breath fires once when steady reaches 35 and the gift is unused. Second Look only triggers when a slip actually occurred, comparing current slips to a memory count.\n\nRewind preserves the bot's memory object, so flags like `usedBreath` survive and cannot be accidentally reset. The first eye window may open before steady reaches 35 during fermata, but consult fixes later windows without needing breath. Stage 2 hides the eye at (250, 90) and slivers; the bot must sonar them.\n\nSonar on the hidden eye marks it and opens it. The tool then switches to cautery for burning. Stage 1 needs four hits total, so one more burn completes it.\n\nThe stage 2 eye burn logic is confirmed. The first block clears `eye.done` and increments hits, so the later stage 2 check sees a finished eye. After one more burn, hits reaches four and slivers are ready. Sonar marks them, forceps pulls them, and stage 3 tension is 40 with pull speed 24, which is safe.\n\nThe stage 3 pull takes about 1.2 seconds, which is acceptable. The note will not snap because the bot’s speed is below the tension threshold. The eloquent line is harmless since the forceps pull does not use a scalpel. After the fix, stage 1 windows repeat every 5.7 seconds.\n\nThe dome timing logic is confirmed: the eye stays closed while a dome lasts, then reopens once the dome ends because `eyeOpen <= 0` becomes true. The gift and consult pulses will be restricted to a single frame so they do not repeat.\n\nA new puzzle emerged: steady drops from 25 to 7 while the bot is asking \"why gift,\" yet no breath was fired and the consult action does not affect steady. The cause of that drop is still unknown.\n\nThe steady drop from 25 to 7 is not caused by consult or gift. The log shows steady peaking at 26 before falling to 15, so the drain must come from another source. A new theory is that toggling to Sokolova triggers Second Look, which rewinds state and resets steady.\n\nThe steady drop from 25 to 7 is not caused by consult or gift. The log shows steady peaking at 26 before falling to 15, so the drain must come from another source. A new theory is that toggling to Sokolova triggers Second Look, which rewinds state and resets steady.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-dc28173a-c7d7-4870-8478-38155835306c-39","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function award","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4416,"output_tokens":4136,"cache_read_input_tokens":103552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"7703188c-a18f-4ecc-88a7-0e547c044d20"}
