 181\\nt 79.8 why grip tool forceps trig 1 at 160 140 held 0 st 2 hits 4 eye hidfalse mktrue opfalse dnfalse altrue sl oh,oh note undefined vit 53 clk 180\\nEND false false  phase Fermata hits 4 stage 2\\n(node:4067626) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"node /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/ferm.js\",\"truncated\":true,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Log fermata stage 2 and 3 bot behavior\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/terminal/call-ee55f322-e6b4-433e-bd77-adeaf3f5e7c1-49.log\",\"total_bytes\":29525}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"0aa5325e-69be-4098-9779-8c50bf4a9b09"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_112","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bot is stuck trying to grip the sliver at (160, 140).\n\nSlivers are marked hidden. The bot tries to grip them anyway because canTouch allows touching marked hidden objects. It should use sonar instead.\n\nThe sliver may not actually be marked. If it were, the bot would use sonar instead of forceps. The mark might be expiring because sonar sets markT to 4 and marks fade over time.\n\nThe bot briefly sonars the sliver at t=70.1, but the mark expires after four seconds and grip resumes. The log interval is only half a second, so short sonar pulses may be missed. Grip still fails to set held even when the bot is directly on top of the sliver.\n\nThe grip code requires `trigEdge` to be true and `held` to be false. The bot is at the exact sliver position, so distance is zero and the object should be found. The mark must be active since the bot selects grip instead of sonar.\n\nThe root cause is now clear. The bot's trigger stays continuously high during sonar, so `trigEdge` never fires. When the tool switches to forceps, the trigger remains held and grip never activates. This creates a loop where sonar keeps refreshing the mark while forceps waits for a rising edge that will never come.\n\nThe fix is to release the trigger for one frame before gripping when switching tools. The bot should tap rather than hold. I am reviewing the forceps act() code.\n\nThe fix is to detect when the trigger was already held by a previous tool, such as sonar. If the bot is near the target and the trigger was down, it will release the trigger this frame so the next frame can press it. This breaks the stuck edge loop. The same bug likely affects suture and scalpel.\n\nSuture and scalpel avoid the bug because they release the trigger before reaching their targets. Cautery holds continuously, so it never needs an edge. Screws share the same forceps grip logic, but they likely worked in c9 only because the approach kept the trigger low during travel.\n\nThe fix will be applied to both forceps and screw grips. Cautery and syringe are unaffected because they do not rely on a rising edge. The approach code will release the trigger if it is already held when switching to a tool that requires an edge.\n\nThe fix is now written. Forceps and screw approaches will release the trigger if it was already held by a previous tool, then press it on the next frame to create a clean rising edge. Normal travel frames remain unaffected because the bot is not yet on target.\n\nThe fix preserves normal behavior. Arrival frames still trigger correctly when the previous frame had a low trigger. Failed grips recover in two frames, which is well under the four-second mark lifetime. If the mark expires during the stuck period, sonar refreshes it and forceps can grip within roughly 0.05 seconds.\n\nThe sliver axis is normalized to [0.6, 0.8]. Pull depth is 12 and tension is 120. The second sliver will be dished after the first. The stage 3 note may share the same trigger-edge bug but the tap fix makes it robust. Whether the eye staying alive blocks progress remains to be seen.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e44f6a80-2b94-4a77-8520-2227eb0bcc0c-50","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/bot/bot.js","old_string":"    if (o.type === 'screw') {\n      if (p.held !== o.id) return go('forceps', o.x + 12, o.y, near(o.x + 12, o.y, 3), { why: 'screw' });","new_string":"    if (o.type === 'screw') {\n      if (p.held !== o.id) {\n        const on = near(o.x + 12, o.y, 3);\n        return go('forceps', o.x + 12, o.y, on && p.prevTrig <= 0.3, { why: 'screw' });\n      }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e44f6a80-2b94-4a77-8520-2227eb0bcc0c-51","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/bot/bot.js","old_string":"      if (p.held !== o.id) return go('forceps', o.x, o.y, near(o.x, o.y, 2.5), { fine, why: 'grip' });","new_string":"      if (p.held !== o.id) {\n        const on = near(o.x, o.y, 2.5);\n        return go('forceps', o.x, o.y, on && p.prevTrig <= 0.3, { fine, why: 'grip' });\n      }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4577,"output_tokens":2466,"cache_read_input_tokens":125696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"b9887661-1a60-49c5-8286-832a12a0fa98"}
