2,98,121,32,108,105,110,101,41,10,49,48,57,48,58,35,35,32,65,112,112,101,110,100,105,120,32,65,58,32,116,105,115,115,117,101,32,112,97,105,110,116,101,114,10,49,49,52,54,58,35,35,32,65,112,112,101,110,100,105,120,32,66,58,32,97,32,115,105,116,101,32,114,101,99,105,112,101,10,49,49,54,55,58,35,35,32,65,112,112,101,110,100,105,120,32,67,58,32,112,111,114,116,114,97,105,116,32,112,97,105,110,116,101,114,10,49,50,51,54,58,35,35,32,65,112,112,101,110,100,105,120,32,68,58,32,72,117,98,32,115,107,101,108,101,116,111,110,44,32,112,97,103,101,32,104,101,97,100,32,97,110,100,32,104,97,114,110,101,115,115,32,114,117,110,110,101,114,10,49,51,50,49,58,35,35,32,65,112,112,101,110,100,105,120,32,69,58,32,103,97,109,101,112,97,100,32,115,116,117,98,32,97,110,100,32,116,111,117,99,104,45,110,111,116,105,99,101,32,112,97,116,99,104,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":49,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":5,\"content\":\"## Contents\"},{\"line_number\":30,\"content\":\"- Appendix A: tissue painter\"},{\"line_number\":31,\"content\":\"- Appendix B: a site recipe\"},{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"- Appendix C: portrait painter\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"- Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"- Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\"},{\"line_number\":38,\"content\":\"## 0. How to use this plan\"},{\"line_number\":49,\"content\":\"## 1. The game on one page\"},{\"line_number\":81,\"content\":\"## 2. Direction decisions\"},{\"line_number\":102,\"content\":\"## 3. Verified engine and Hub facts\"},{\"line_number\":117,\"content\":\"6. **Pad reading** with the stub in Appendix E: `input.padIndex === 0`, `input.padStyle() === 'playstation'`, `input.value('useTool') === .5` from `buttons[7].value = .5`, `input.padAim` is the right stick and `input.padMove` the left, both after the dead zone.\"},{\"line_number\":120,\"content\":\"9. **Engine portraits are not enough.** `rig.drawPortrait` at 64 px and up looks crude. Use the bust painter in Appendix C for every face, and keep rigs for bodies at game scale. The built-in `hat: 'cap'` is a red peaked cap whose brim crosses the face, so write a surgical cap with `E.Humanoid.hat` (fact 18).\"},{\"line_number\":121,\"content\":\"10. **Menus at TV size.** The pause and settings menus are the engine's HTML, too small for 10 feet by default. `new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, theme })`, made before `game.start`, scales them for a TV: at 1080p a row is 94 px tall, six pause rows fit, and with Save and Load added the last of eight rows falls below the screen, where moving the focus scrolls to it, as it does on the long Settings screen. Canvas menus: `new E.Menu(game, items, { scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (`rows` scrolls; hover and click still work; `menu.rowAt(i)` gives a row's box, for tests). Reduce density too: the page head in Appendix D carries CSS that shows a Settings row's help only on the focused row. Keep its `html` prefix: the engine injects its own CSS at runtime, and the same specificity could lose to it.\"},{\"line_number\":122,\"content\":\"11. **Touch notice.** `new E.Game({ touch: 'never' })` gives no touch controls, drops the Touch settings, and shows \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" with a Settings button. But the notice covers the screen at 88% black, which hides the attract mode TASK.md wants running. Patch it (Appendix E).\"},{\"line_number\":123,\"content\":\"12. **The Hub works on this engine.** The skeleton in Appendix D passed all four harness scenarios (14 or 15 checks each) and still runs standalone. The options that matter in a session are `live: true`, `autoPause: false`, `corner: false`, `menu.quit: false`.\"},{\"line_number\":134,\"content\":\"## 4. Game flow\"},{\"line_number\":159,\"content\":\"## 5. The operation\"},{\"line_number\":316,\"content\":\"## 6. Controls and prompts\"},{\"line_number\":357,\"content\":\"## 7. Things on the table\"},{\"line_number\":382,\"content\":\"## 8. HUSH: the strains\"},{\"line_number\":425,\"content\":\"## 9. The cases\"},{\"line_number\":522,\"content\":\"## 10. Story bible\"},{\"line_number\":534,\"content\":\"Pronouns as listed. Portraits per Appendix C.\"},{\"line_number\":603,\"content\":\"## 11. The ward\"},{\"line_number\":616,\"content\":\"## 12. Multiplayer: Grand Rounds\"},{\"line_number\":641,\"content\":\"Follow the protocol page and Appendix D. Exact behavior:\"},{\"line_number\":670,\"content\":\"## 13. Attract mode\"},{\"line_number\":686,\"content\":\"**Touch-only devices:** no touch controls, the notice and Settings button per Appendix E, and the attract reel runs behind the notice. A tap returns to the title with the notice, and 10 s later the reel resumes. Tall screens just show more drape.\"},{\"line_number\":690,\"content\":\"## 14. Dev mode\"},{\"line_number\":705,\"content\":\"## 15. UI and the 10-foot rules\"},{\"line_number\":776,\"content\":\"## 16. Art direction\"},{\"line_number\":789,\"content\":\"| Abdomen (2, 3, 7, 8) | Appendix B. Vary the seed and layout per case; Case 7's cavity has a moving `light` |\"},{\"line_number\":800,\"content\":\"Appendix C is the style: flat-shaded hard polygons, big readable eyes, an original look. They stand large on the story stage at 1:1 buffer pixels, about half the screen's height. Masked versions in theatre; cropped to 56 x 64 for barks. Build all eight main cast members and a small parts kit (hair shapes, jaw, skin, glasses) for patients. Animate: blink, mouth flap while typing, a one- or two-pixel bob when speaking, slide in from the sides, a small shake on shock. Add expressions as the script needs (smirk, tired, cry).\"},{\"line_number\":824,\"content\":\"## 17. Animation\"},{\"line_number\":849,\"content\":\"## 18. Audio\"},{\"line_number\":902,\"content\":\"## 19. Code architecture\"},{\"line_number\":924,\"content\":\"tests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\"},{\"line_number\":961,\"content\":\"Use the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`. Standard features stay standard (pause, settings, rebinding, full screen, boot, autopause). Expected engine patch: only Appendix E's notice. Write down why for each patch you make, for the Engine Feedback.\"},{\"line_number\":978,\"content\":\"## 20. Testing\"},{\"line_number\":1006,\"content\":\"- Pad with the Appendix E stub: `R2` and `△` prompts, stick cursor, wheel, trigger; keyboard and mouse switch the prompts.\"},{\"line_number\":1010,\"content\":\"- **Hub harness, all four runs (Appendix D's runner):** `players=2&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Then open the page outside a session.\"},{\"line_number\":1019,\"content\":\"## 21. Build order\"},{\"line_number\":1025,\"content\":\"| M0 | Title picked. Folders, vendor, manifest, bundler, dev page, test runner, Hub client in the page | Empty game builds, runs, one test passes, harness runner works on Appendix D |\"},{\"line_number\":1040,\"content\":\"## 22. Done checklist (TASK.md, line by line)\"},{\"line_number\":1090,\"content\":\"## Appendix A: tissue painter\"},{\"line_number\":1146,\"content\":\"## Appendix B: a site recipe\"},{\"line_number\":1167,\"content\":\"## Appendix C: portrait painter\"},{\"line_number\":1236,\"content\":\"## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\"},{\"line_number\":1321,\"content\":\"## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0f09f3ab-8fd7-423c-ba58-650283409c3e-61","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,56,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,46,103,114,111,107,47,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,115,47,37,50,70,104,111,109,101,37,50,70,109,105,99,104,97,37,50,70,100,101,118,37,50,70,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,37,50,70,114,117,110,115,37,50,70,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,37,50,70,119,111,114,107,47,48,49,97,49,97,97,51,55,45,102,55,99,102,45,55,48,48,49,45,57,49,57,56,45,51,56,97,100,48,52,101,100,48,102,53,101,47,103,111,97,108,47,112,108,97,110,46,109,100,10,51,58,35,35,32,71,111,97,108,32,107,105,110,100,10,54,58,35,35,32,65,99,99,101,112,116,97,110,99,101,32,99,114,105,116,101,114,105,97,10,49,51,58,35,35,32,86,101,114,105,102,105,99,97,116,105,111,110,32,112,108,97,110,10,50,48,58,35,35,32,78,111,110,45,103,111,97,108,115,10,50,55,58,35,35,32,65,115,115,117,109,101,100,32,115,99,111,112,101,10,51,51,58,35,35,32,73,109,112,108,101,109,101,110,116,97,116,105,111,110,32,97,112,112,114,111,97,99,104,10,51,54,58,35,35,32,84,97,115,107,32,99,104,101,99,107,108,105,115,116,10,52,54,58,35,35,32,82,105,115,107,115,32,47,32,67,111,110,116,114,97,100,105,99,116,105,111,110,115,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":8,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"## Goal kind\"},{\"line_number\":6,\"content\":\"## Acceptance criteria\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"## Non-goals\"},{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"## Assumed scope\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"## Implementation approach\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"## Risks / Contradictions\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"59211367-6dfe-46ce-97eb-1e88e1362131"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_121","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading the goal plan checklist, verification steps, and PLAN section 19 architecture with appendix A-D to prepare for implementation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-49a425b3-684f-4da4-91c9-6dbeaea2ff49-62","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/goal/plan.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-49a425b3-684f-4da4-91c9-6dbeaea2ff49-63","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md","offset":902,"limit":160}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2601,"output_tokens":252,"cache_read_input_tokens":147584,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"d4e3d761-8301-4413-bd24-6d1743c54daa"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-49a425b3-684f-4da4-91c9-6dbeaea2ff49-62","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Plan: Build the original surgical-action game in PLAN.md and hand in every TASK.md artifact in this folder.\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. The work folder (the folder that contains STAGE.md) holds PROGRESS.md, `exit-interview.json` beside the game, and one self-contained HTML file whose name and sibling dev-folder name follow TASK.md’s `[GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916]` template: the chosen title, the source name Trauma Center: Second Opinion, and the literal run id `grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916` (spaces may be hyphens). The title is a playful riff picked by listing 50 options and then a real RNG, and that same string is the page `<title>`, the title-screen logo, and `aiHub.name`. The HTML runs from `file://` with no CDN and no network fetch. `exit-interview.json` parses as one object in TASK.md’s exact shape (testingFeedback length 4, engineFeedback length 6, promptFeedback length 4, `usage` exactly `added on import`, no empty strings). The in-game About/Credits pages show the same Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback, in TASK.md’s order. Shipped game source contains no TODO, FIXME, placeholder, or stubbed feature.\\n2. From a fresh operation created by the shipped sim, each of the eight tools (Forceps, Scalpel, Suture, Salve, Syringe, Cautery, Suction, Sonar) completes the matching target with the gesture in PLAN.md §5.5 and applies that section’s mistake when used wrong (tear, slip, loose stitch, air bubble, char/lockout, or no effect). Vitals and the clock drain as in §5.2 and §7; vitals at 0 offer Code Blue once (not on Attending, and not when the clock hits 0) and then lose the patient if the shock window is missed. Finished actions score Sloppy, Clean, or Textbook, and the case rank is scored against par. Long Breath runs world time at quarter speed while the hands stay at full speed. Second Look restores an earlier snapshot exactly (vitals, clock, objects, RNG) and fills ghost data. The same seed and inputs produce the same state hash with drawing on and with drawing off.\\n3. Each of the eleven cases in PLAN.md §9 and each HUSH strain in §8 (Staccato, Legato, Tremolo, Da Capo, Fermata, Cantor, including Legato snapping, Da Capo regrowth, and the Cantor’s forced rewind) starts from that case’s own data and is cleared by the shipped bot; the perfect bot finishes every case with time and vitals still left. Story scenes in the §10 voice play between operations, a walkable ward shows patients already saved, and one chained New Game run reaches the ending and credits. Lightbox second opinions, Skills Lab, and Intern / Resident / Attending differences are reachable. A content note in the dev folder explains how to add a case, strain, site, character, and story node without editing the sim. Forbidden source names and close variants from PLAN.md §1 do not appear in play or text, except the source title on the About source line and in the title riff.\\n10→4. After 10 seconds with no input on the title, the menu, case files, and the lobby, a looping AI reel of the real scenes starts; any input returns to the title and does not also fire the control under the pointer. It does not start on About, Settings, or Controls. Dev mode opens from the pause menu outside a Hub session, live-changes the main tuning groups (patient, hands, strains, gift, fluids), and can reset them to the documented defaults; cheats and jumps to any case or phase work. Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs from Settings, keyboard and mouse labels when those were used last. The mouse aims in surgery and hover-moves focus on menus and in the ward. A touch-only profile shows the text \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings control, with no touch buttons, while attract still runs. Music, effects, and voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); voices are gibberish; a fresh start sets music volume to 0.1 so music is quieter than effects.\\n5. Grand Rounds is one shared patient for 1 to 4 surgeons, on one couch (local pads and AI colleagues) and in an AI Hub shared-world session. The unmodified Hub session client is the first script, the host simulates, clients mirror, each cursor moves locally, the session card can ready and request more, and finish reports standings, scores, won, and awards. Solo play can still hold the retractor; two players can hold and cut. All four harness runs in PLAN.md §20 pass, and the same page still plays the single-player game when no session is present.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one test command PLAN.md §20 names (`node tests/run.mjs`). It must load the shipped sim and scenes (not a reimplementation or a mock of them) and assert criteria 2, 3, and 4: every tool’s success and mistake, cursor full-stick / fine / magnet / guide-follow, all eight wheel directions, vitals and clock math, Code Blue window, phase-checkpoint restore, grades and rank, each strain’s success and listed failure branch, Long Breath’s 0.25 world-time factor with hand speed unchanged, Second Look deep-equality plus ghosts, determinism with and without drawing, content-id resolution, per-case bot clears, the chained New Game → credits playthrough, attract idle and consumed exit, dev-slider live change and reset, and Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots including the retractor alone and with two. Capture stdout to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log`. Pass only if the log contains a one-line count, zero failures, and no other chatter. Re-run after any change to code those tests cover.\\n2. gating: Launch the real root HTML from `file://` with Playwright 1.63 (Chromium, `--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`) at 1920×1080, twice in a row. Each run must have zero page errors, a drawing buffer of 480×270 (PLAN.md §3 screen-size rule, not a stale default), and a substantially filled frame (title art and the chosen title, not a blank or a few pixels). A confirm/start input must change what is on screen (menu follows the title). Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must show the same success. Then load the same file for 30 seconds in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit with zero page errors; with the Appendix E pad stub, confirm a PlayStation R2 prompt, an Xbox prompt after the Settings glyph option, and a keyboard/mouse prompt after those devices; on an iPhone-profile touch page, confirm the required notice and Settings control, no touch buttons, and that a Settings tap opens settings. Capture `{SCRATCH}/browsers.log`. If Playwright itself fails to start, save that output to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.log` and treat criteria 2–3’s unit tests plus the file’s presence as the bar. A launch that starts and reads back a blank or partial frame is a game failure, not an environment failure.\\n3. gating: Run the four Hub harness URLs in PLAN.md §20 (2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter, and loss; host-leave; server), plus a no-session open of the same page. Serve only this game on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port, confirm the framed document title is this game, and stop only that server by its PID. Pass means each run has `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, and the standalone open is not in a session and still reaches the title. With two same-origin harness frames, a client stroke must show up on the host’s state. Capture `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json` and confirm criterion 1’s shape, non-empty answers, and `usage`. Confirm the HTML inlines the game (no external script or audio URLs), contains no `TODO` / `FIXME` / `placeholder` / `stub`, and does not use the §1 forbidden names outside the allowed source-title spots. Confirm an `OfflineAudioContext` or `AnalyserNode` render of an effect, one voice, and the choir is not silent, and that at default settings the music bus is well below effects. Append these observations to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log` or `{SCRATCH}/handoff.log`.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, save stills of each operative site, the main portraits, one frame of each strain, the tool wheel, and Long Breath’s cold field to `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Absence of stills alone does not fail the goal once steps 1–4 pass.\\n\\n20→## Non-goals\\n- A port of Trauma Center levels, operations, music, UI, or proper names (those are forbidden).\\n- FPS targets, optimization passes, WebGPU, a 3D stack, or CDN libraries.\\n- Real speech, recorded audio files, touch-play controls, chat, emotes, or custom Hub names.\\n- Cases beyond the eleven-case slice, Grand Rounds, and Skills Lab. The post-credits \\\"Incoming\\\" chart is a door, not more gameplay.\\n- Motion-capture clips, split-screen, and a second human on another machine (use the harness or a second local page).\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- This work folder only: STAGE.md, PLAN.md, TASK.md, plus new PROGRESS.md, `exit-interview.json`, the named HTML, and the named dev subfolder. Do not read or write sibling agent folders, and do not stop processes you did not start.\\n- Fresh clones of `my-3d2dge` `dist/handoff` and `ai-hub` `lib/hub` under the dev folder. Engine and Hub APIs are whatever those clones document; PLAN.md §3 was checked against my-3D2dge v0.89.0 and Hub client 1.4.0.\\n30→- Playwright 1.63 (already installed; do not run `playwright install`), Node, and system Python. No audio-file or network dependency in the shipped page.\\n- Defining source mechanics (first-person timed surgery, vitals, radial tools, graded results, a once-per-operation supernatural aid, two surgeons, parasite bosses, melodrama) were checked against Wikipedia and StrategyWiki. Where PLAN.md deliberately changes them (button Steady instead of a drawn star, original cast, HUSH instead of the source’s parasite names), PLAN.md wins.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nPLAN.md is the design document (flow, numbers, story, Hub message shape). This goal plan does not freeze file or function names; verifiers judge the criteria above, not a matching directory tree. Keep the operation as plain JSON-safe state stepped by a pure function with a seeded RNG, and keep drawing, audio, and DOM out of that state so tests, rewind, checkpoints, and net snapshots share one path. Drive the bot through the same cursor and trigger path as a pad. Content (cases, strains, sites, lines) should be data plus a short authoring note. Bundle last into the single root HTML, with the Hub session script unmodified and first, and escape any `</script` inside inlined source. Record engine patches and honest test/engine/prompt answers as you go so the About pages and `exit-interview.json` match.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Pick the title (50 riffs, then a real RNG), create the named dev folder and PROGRESS.md, clone the engine handoff and Hub client, and get an empty page to boot from `file://`.\\n- [ ] Build the pure operation sim, cursor, wheel, eight tools, vitals, clock, grades, and the Case 1 loop, with the bot on the real input path and tests for those hands.\\n- [ ] Add the title, menus, TV-scale pause and settings, glyph prompts, attract, dev mode, touch notice, story scenes, portraits, gibberish voices, and music at 10%.\\n40→- [ ] Add the remaining tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, the Lightbox, and Cases 2 and 3 so Chapter 1 clears under the bot.\\n- [ ] Add couch Grand Rounds and the Hub shared-world session, and make all four harness runs pass.\\n- [ ] Add both gifts’ full use, Consult, the ward, strains, and Cases 4 through 11 through the ending and credits.\\n- [ ] Fill feel, cinematics, synthesized score, the attract reel, and Skills Lab; run the single test command and the browser and Hub launches, saving logs and shots under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n- [ ] Write About data and `exit-interview.json` from real results, bundle the final HTML into the work-folder root, and confirm the test command still prints zero failures.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §21 says to cut late content if time runs out. That note does not lower this contract: a missing never-cut feature (cursor, any of the eight tools, either gift, the finale, Grand Rounds, Hub passes, attract, dev mode, 10-foot UI, About, exit interview) or a stubbed case fails the criteria.\\n- Cloned engine or Hub docs may disagree with PLAN.md §3. Trust the clone, adapt, and record the patch. Do not drop a TASK.md requirement to match an older note.\\n- The chained playthrough is long. Run it headless without drawing except where a draw-error check is required. `Target closed` means the machine ran out of memory; run one or two browsers at a time.\\n50→- There is no physical DualSense and no real iPhone. The pad stub and a WebKit iPhone profile are the accepted stand-ins. WebKit is not iOS Safari.\\n- The title is chosen at build time by RNG, so the filename cannot be fixed here. Match the template and the on-screen title; do not invent a second title in the verifier.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Plan: Build the original surgical-action game in PLAN.md and hand in every TASK.md artifact in this folder.\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. The work folder (the folder that contains STAGE.md) holds PROGRESS.md, `exit-interview.json` beside the game, and one self-contained HTML file whose name and sibling dev-folder name follow TASK.md’s `[GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916]` template: the chosen title, the source name Trauma Center: Second Opinion, and the literal run id `grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916` (spaces may be hyphens). The title is a playful riff picked by listing 50 options and then a real RNG, and that same string is the page `<title>`, the title-screen logo, and `aiHub.name`. The HTML runs from `file://` with no CDN and no network fetch. `exit-interview.json` parses as one object in TASK.md’s exact shape (testingFeedback length 4, engineFeedback length 6, promptFeedback length 4, `usage` exactly `added on import`, no empty strings). The in-game About/Credits pages show the same Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback, in TASK.md’s order. Shipped game source contains no TODO, FIXME, placeholder, or stubbed feature.\\n2. From a fresh operation created by the shipped sim, each of the eight tools (Forceps, Scalpel, Suture, Salve, Syringe, Cautery, Suction, Sonar) completes the matching target with the gesture in PLAN.md §5.5 and applies that section’s mistake when used wrong (tear, slip, loose stitch, air bubble, char/lockout, or no effect). Vitals and the clock drain as in §5.2 and §7; vitals at 0 offer Code Blue once (not on Attending, and not when the clock hits 0) and then lose the patient if the shock window is missed. Finished actions score Sloppy, Clean, or Textbook, and the case rank is scored against par. Long Breath runs world time at quarter speed while the hands stay at full speed. Second Look restores an earlier snapshot exactly (vitals, clock, objects, RNG) and fills ghost data. The same seed and inputs produce the same state hash with drawing on and with drawing off.\\n3. Each of the eleven cases in PLAN.md §9 and each HUSH strain in §8 (Staccato, Legato, Tremolo, Da Capo, Fermata, Cantor, including Legato snapping, Da Capo regrowth, and the Cantor’s forced rewind) starts from that case’s own data and is cleared by the shipped bot; the perfect bot finishes every case with time and vitals still left. Story scenes in the §10 voice play between operations, a walkable ward shows patients already saved, and one chained New Game run reaches the ending and credits. Lightbox second opinions, Skills Lab, and Intern / Resident / Attending differences are reachable. A content note in the dev folder explains how to add a case, strain, site, character, and story node without editing the sim. Forbidden source names and close variants from PLAN.md §1 do not appear in play or text, except the source title on the About source line and in the title riff.\\n10→4. After 10 seconds with no input on the title, the menu, case files, and the lobby, a looping AI reel of the real scenes starts; any input returns to the title and does not also fire the control under the pointer. It does not start on About, Settings, or Controls. Dev mode opens from the pause menu outside a Hub session, live-changes the main tuning groups (patient, hands, strains, gift, fluids), and can reset them to the documented defaults; cheats and jumps to any case or phase work. Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs from Settings, keyboard and mouse labels when those were used last. The mouse aims in surgery and hover-moves focus on menus and in the ward. A touch-only profile shows the text \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings control, with no touch buttons, while attract still runs. Music, effects, and voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); voices are gibberish; a fresh start sets music volume to 0.1 so music is quieter than effects.\\n5. Grand Rounds is one shared patient for 1 to 4 surgeons, on one couch (local pads and AI colleagues) and in an AI Hub shared-world session. The unmodified Hub session client is the first script, the host simulates, clients mirror, each cursor moves locally, the session card can ready and request more, and finish reports standings, scores, won, and awards. Solo play can still hold the retractor; two players can hold and cut. All four harness runs in PLAN.md §20 pass, and the same page still plays the single-player game when no session is present.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one test command PLAN.md §20 names (`node tests/run.mjs`). It must load the shipped sim and scenes (not a reimplementation or a mock of them) and assert criteria 2, 3, and 4: every tool’s success and mistake, cursor full-stick / fine / magnet / guide-follow, all eight wheel directions, vitals and clock math, Code Blue window, phase-checkpoint restore, grades and rank, each strain’s success and listed failure branch, Long Breath’s 0.25 world-time factor with hand speed unchanged, Second Look deep-equality plus ghosts, determinism with and without drawing, content-id resolution, per-case bot clears, the chained New Game → credits playthrough, attract idle and consumed exit, dev-slider live change and reset, and Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots including the retractor alone and with two. Capture stdout to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log`. Pass only if the log contains a one-line count, zero failures, and no other chatter. Re-run after any change to code those tests cover.\\n2. gating: Launch the real root HTML from `file://` with Playwright 1.63 (Chromium, `--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`) at 1920×1080, twice in a row. Each run must have zero page errors, a drawing buffer of 480×270 (PLAN.md §3 screen-size rule, not a stale default), and a substantially filled frame (title art and the chosen title, not a blank or a few pixels). A confirm/start input must change what is on screen (menu follows the title). Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must show the same success. Then load the same file for 30 seconds in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit with zero page errors; with the Appendix E pad stub, confirm a PlayStation R2 prompt, an Xbox prompt after the Settings glyph option, and a keyboard/mouse prompt after those devices; on an iPhone-profile touch page, confirm the required notice and Settings control, no touch buttons, and that a Settings tap opens settings. Capture `{SCRATCH}/browsers.log`. If Playwright itself fails to start, save that output to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.log` and treat criteria 2–3’s unit tests plus the file’s presence as the bar. A launch that starts and reads back a blank or partial frame is a game failure, not an environment failure.\\n3. gating: Run the four Hub harness URLs in PLAN.md §20 (2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter, and loss; host-leave; server), plus a no-session open of the same page. Serve only this game on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port, confirm the framed document title is this game, and stop only that server by its PID. Pass means each run has `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, and the standalone open is not in a session and still reaches the title. With two same-origin harness frames, a client stroke must show up on the host’s state. Capture `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json` and confirm criterion 1’s shape, non-empty answers, and `usage`. Confirm the HTML inlines the game (no external script or audio URLs), contains no `TODO` / `FIXME` / `placeholder` / `stub`, and does not use the §1 forbidden names outside the allowed source-title spots. Confirm an `OfflineAudioContext` or `AnalyserNode` render of an effect, one voice, and the choir is not silent, and that at default settings the music bus is well below effects. Append these observations to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log` or `{SCRATCH}/handoff.log`.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, save stills of each operative site, the main portraits, one frame of each strain, the tool wheel, and Long Breath’s cold field to `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Absence of stills alone does not fail the goal once steps 1–4 pass.\\n\\n20→## Non-goals\\n- A port of Trauma Center levels, operations, music, UI, or proper names (those are forbidden).\\n- FPS targets, optimization passes, WebGPU, a 3D stack, or CDN libraries.\\n- Real speech, recorded audio files, touch-play controls, chat, emotes, or custom Hub names.\\n- Cases beyond the eleven-case slice, Grand Rounds, and Skills Lab. The post-credits \\\"Incoming\\\" chart is a door, not more gameplay.\\n- Motion-capture clips, split-screen, and a second human on another machine (use the harness or a second local page).\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- This work folder only: STAGE.md, PLAN.md, TASK.md, plus new PROGRESS.md, `exit-interview.json`, the named HTML, and the named dev subfolder. Do not read or write sibling agent folders, and do not stop processes you did not start.\\n- Fresh clones of `my-3d2dge` `dist/handoff` and `ai-hub` `lib/hub` under the dev folder. Engine and Hub APIs are whatever those clones document; PLAN.md §3 was checked against my-3D2dge v0.89.0 and Hub client 1.4.0.\\n30→- Playwright 1.63 (already installed; do not run `playwright install`), Node, and system Python. No audio-file or network dependency in the shipped page.\\n- Defining source mechanics (first-person timed surgery, vitals, radial tools, graded results, a once-per-operation supernatural aid, two surgeons, parasite bosses, melodrama) were checked against Wikipedia and StrategyWiki. Where PLAN.md deliberately changes them (button Steady instead of a drawn star, original cast, HUSH instead of the source’s parasite names), PLAN.md wins.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nPLAN.md is the design document (flow, numbers, story, Hub message shape). This goal plan does not freeze file or function names; verifiers judge the criteria above, not a matching directory tree. Keep the operation as plain JSON-safe state stepped by a pure function with a seeded RNG, and keep drawing, audio, and DOM out of that state so tests, rewind, checkpoints, and net snapshots share one path. Drive the bot through the same cursor and trigger path as a pad. Content (cases, strains, sites, lines) should be data plus a short authoring note. Bundle last into the single root HTML, with the Hub session script unmodified and first, and escape any `</script` inside inlined source. Record engine patches and honest test/engine/prompt answers as you go so the About pages and `exit-interview.json` match.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Pick the title (50 riffs, then a real RNG), create the named dev folder and PROGRESS.md, clone the engine handoff and Hub client, and get an empty page to boot from `file://`.\\n- [ ] Build the pure operation sim, cursor, wheel, eight tools, vitals, clock, grades, and the Case 1 loop, with the bot on the real input path and tests for those hands.\\n- [ ] Add the title, menus, TV-scale pause and settings, glyph prompts, attract, dev mode, touch notice, story scenes, portraits, gibberish voices, and music at 10%.\\n40→- [ ] Add the remaining tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, the Lightbox, and Cases 2 and 3 so Chapter 1 clears under the bot.\\n- [ ] Add couch Grand Rounds and the Hub shared-world session, and make all four harness runs pass.\\n- [ ] Add both gifts’ full use, Consult, the ward, strains, and Cases 4 through 11 through the ending and credits.\\n- [ ] Fill feel, cinematics, synthesized score, the attract reel, and Skills Lab; run the single test command and the browser and Hub launches, saving logs and shots under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n- [ ] Write About data and `exit-interview.json` from real results, bundle the final HTML into the work-folder root, and confirm the test command still prints zero failures.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §21 says to cut late content if time runs out. That note does not lower this contract: a missing never-cut feature (cursor, any of the eight tools, either gift, the finale, Grand Rounds, Hub passes, attract, dev mode, 10-foot UI, About, exit interview) or a stubbed case fails the criteria.\\n- Cloned engine or Hub docs may disagree with PLAN.md §3. Trust the clone, adapt, and record the patch. Do not drop a TASK.md requirement to match an older note.\\n- The chained playthrough is long. Run it headless without drawing except where a draw-error check is required. `Target closed` means the machine ran out of memory; run one or two browsers at a time.\\n50→- There is no physical DualSense and no real iPhone. The pad stub and a WebKit iPhone profile are the accepted stand-ins. WebKit is not iOS Safari.\\n- The title is chosen at build time by RNG, so the filename cannot be fixed here. Match the template and the on-screen title; do not invent a second title in the verifier.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/goal/plan.md\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"# Plan: Build the original surgical-action game in PLAN.md and hand in every TASK.md artifact in this folder.\\n\\n## Goal kind\\ncode-change\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n1. The work folder (the folder that contains STAGE.md) holds PROGRESS.md, `exit-interview.json` beside the game, and one self-contained HTML file whose name and sibling dev-folder name follow TASK.md’s `[GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916]` template: the chosen title, the source name Trauma Center: Second Opinion, and the literal run id `grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916` (spaces may be hyphens). The title is a playful riff picked by listing 50 options and then a real RNG, and that same string is the page `<title>`, the title-screen logo, and `aiHub.name`. The HTML runs from `file://` with no CDN and no network fetch. `exit-interview.json` parses as one object in TASK.md’s exact shape (testingFeedback length 4, engineFeedback length 6, promptFeedback length 4, `usage` exactly `added on import`, no empty strings). The in-game About/Credits pages show the same Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback, in TASK.md’s order. Shipped game source contains no TODO, FIXME, placeholder, or stubbed feature.\\n2. From a fresh operation created by the shipped sim, each of the eight tools (Forceps, Scalpel, Suture, Salve, Syringe, Cautery, Suction, Sonar) completes the matching target with the gesture in PLAN.md §5.5 and applies that section’s mistake when used wrong (tear, slip, loose stitch, air bubble, char/lockout, or no effect). Vitals and the clock drain as in §5.2 and §7; vitals at 0 offer Code Blue once (not on Attending, and not when the clock hits 0) and then lose the patient if the shock window is missed. Finished actions score Sloppy, Clean, or Textbook, and the case rank is scored against par. Long Breath runs world time at quarter speed while the hands stay at full speed. Second Look restores an earlier snapshot exactly (vitals, clock, objects, RNG) and fills ghost data. The same seed and inputs produce the same state hash with drawing on and with drawing off.\\n3. Each of the eleven cases in PLAN.md §9 and each HUSH strain in §8 (Staccato, Legato, Tremolo, Da Capo, Fermata, Cantor, including Legato snapping, Da Capo regrowth, and the Cantor’s forced rewind) starts from that case’s own data and is cleared by the shipped bot; the perfect bot finishes every case with time and vitals still left. Story scenes in the §10 voice play between operations, a walkable ward shows patients already saved, and one chained New Game run reaches the ending and credits. Lightbox second opinions, Skills Lab, and Intern / Resident / Attending differences are reachable. A content note in the dev folder explains how to add a case, strain, site, character, and story node without editing the sim. Forbidden source names and close variants from PLAN.md §1 do not appear in play or text, except the source title on the About source line and in the title riff.\\n4. After 10 seconds with no input on the title, the menu, case files, and the lobby, a looping AI reel of the real scenes starts; any input returns to the title and does not also fire the control under the pointer. It does not start on About, Settings, or Controls. Dev mode opens from the pause menu outside a Hub session, live-changes the main tuning groups (patient, hands, strains, gift, fluids), and can reset them to the documented defaults; cheats and jumps to any case or phase work. Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs from Settings, keyboard and mouse labels when those were used last. The mouse aims in surgery and hover-moves focus on menus and in the ward. A touch-only profile shows the text \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings control, with no touch buttons, while attract still runs. Music, effects, and voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); voices are gibberish; a fresh start sets music volume to 0.1 so music is quieter than effects.\\n5. Grand Rounds is one shared patient for 1 to 4 surgeons, on one couch (local pads and AI colleagues) and in an AI Hub shared-world session. The unmodified Hub session client is the first script, the host simulates, clients mirror, each cursor moves locally, the session card can ready and request more, and finish reports standings, scores, won, and awards. Solo play can still hold the retractor; two players can hold and cut. All four harness runs in PLAN.md §20 pass, and the same page still plays the single-player game when no session is present.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one test command PLAN.md §20 names (`node tests/run.mjs`). It must load the shipped sim and scenes (not a reimplementation or a mock of them) and assert criteria 2, 3, and 4: every tool’s success and mistake, cursor full-stick / fine / magnet / guide-follow, all eight wheel directions, vitals and clock math, Code Blue window, phase-checkpoint restore, grades and rank, each strain’s success and listed failure branch, Long Breath’s 0.25 world-time factor with hand speed unchanged, Second Look deep-equality plus ghosts, determinism with and without drawing, content-id resolution, per-case bot clears, the chained New Game → credits playthrough, attract idle and consumed exit, dev-slider live change and reset, and Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots including the retractor alone and with two. Capture stdout to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log`. Pass only if the log contains a one-line count, zero failures, and no other chatter. Re-run after any change to code those tests cover.\\n2. gating: Launch the real root HTML from `file://` with Playwright 1.63 (Chromium, `--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`) at 1920×1080, twice in a row. Each run must have zero page errors, a drawing buffer of 480×270 (PLAN.md §3 screen-size rule, not a stale default), and a substantially filled frame (title art and the chosen title, not a blank or a few pixels). A confirm/start input must change what is on screen (menu follows the title). Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must show the same success. Then load the same file for 30 seconds in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit with zero page errors; with the Appendix E pad stub, confirm a PlayStation R2 prompt, an Xbox prompt after the Settings glyph option, and a keyboard/mouse prompt after those devices; on an iPhone-profile touch page, confirm the required notice and Settings control, no touch buttons, and that a Settings tap opens settings. Capture `{SCRATCH}/browsers.log`. If Playwright itself fails to start, save that output to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.log` and treat criteria 2–3’s unit tests plus the file’s presence as the bar. A launch that starts and reads back a blank or partial frame is a game failure, not an environment failure.\\n3. gating: Run the four Hub harness URLs in PLAN.md §20 (2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter, and loss; host-leave; server), plus a no-session open of the same page. Serve only this game on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port, confirm the framed document title is this game, and stop only that server by its PID. Pass means each run has `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, and the standalone open is not in a session and still reaches the title. With two same-origin harness frames, a client stroke must show up on the host’s state. Capture `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json` and confirm criterion 1’s shape, non-empty answers, and `usage`. Confirm the HTML inlines the game (no external script or audio URLs), contains no `TODO` / `FIXME` / `placeholder` / `stub`, and does not use the §1 forbidden names outside the allowed source-title spots. Confirm an `OfflineAudioContext` or `AnalyserNode` render of an effect, one voice, and the choir is not silent, and that at default settings the music bus is well below effects. Append these observations to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log` or `{SCRATCH}/handoff.log`.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, save stills of each operative site, the main portraits, one frame of each strain, the tool wheel, and Long Breath’s cold field to `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Absence of stills alone does not fail the goal once steps 1–4 pass.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- A port of Trauma Center levels, operations, music, UI, or proper names (those are forbidden).\\n- FPS targets, optimization passes, WebGPU, a 3D stack, or CDN libraries.\\n- Real speech, recorded audio files, touch-play controls, chat, emotes, or custom Hub names.\\n- Cases beyond the eleven-case slice, Grand Rounds, and Skills Lab. The post-credits \\\"Incoming\\\" chart is a door, not more gameplay.\\n- Motion-capture clips, split-screen, and a second human on another machine (use the harness or a second local page).\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- This work folder only: STAGE.md, PLAN.md, TASK.md, plus new PROGRESS.md, `exit-interview.json`, the named HTML, and the named dev subfolder. Do not read or write sibling agent folders, and do not stop processes you did not start.\\n- Fresh clones of `my-3d2dge` `dist/handoff` and `ai-hub` `lib/hub` under the dev folder. Engine and Hub APIs are whatever those clones document; PLAN.md §3 was checked against my-3D2dge v0.89.0 and Hub client 1.4.0.\\n- Playwright 1.63 (already installed; do not run `playwright install`), Node, and system Python. No audio-file or network dependency in the shipped page.\\n- Defining source mechanics (first-person timed surgery, vitals, radial tools, graded results, a once-per-operation supernatural aid, two surgeons, parasite bosses, melodrama) were checked against Wikipedia and StrategyWiki. Where PLAN.md deliberately changes them (button Steady instead of a drawn star, original cast, HUSH instead of the source’s parasite names), PLAN.md wins.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nPLAN.md is the design document (flow, numbers, story, Hub message shape). This goal plan does not freeze file or function names; verifiers judge the criteria above, not a matching directory tree. Keep the operation as plain JSON-safe state stepped by a pure function with a seeded RNG, and keep drawing, audio, and DOM out of that state so tests, rewind, checkpoints, and net snapshots share one path. Drive the bot through the same cursor and trigger path as a pad. Content (cases, strains, sites, lines) should be data plus a short authoring note. Bundle last into the single root HTML, with the Hub session script unmodified and first, and escape any `</script` inside inlined source. Record engine patches and honest test/engine/prompt answers as you go so the About pages and `exit-interview.json` match.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [ ] Pick the title (50 riffs, then a real RNG), create the named dev folder and PROGRESS.md, clone the engine handoff and Hub client, and get an empty page to boot from `file://`.\\n- [ ] Build the pure operation sim, cursor, wheel, eight tools, vitals, clock, grades, and the Case 1 loop, with the bot on the real input path and tests for those hands.\\n- [ ] Add the title, menus, TV-scale pause and settings, glyph prompts, attract, dev mode, touch notice, story scenes, portraits, gibberish voices, and music at 10%.\\n- [ ] Add the remaining tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, the Lightbox, and Cases 2 and 3 so Chapter 1 clears under the bot.\\n- [ ] Add couch Grand Rounds and the Hub shared-world session, and make all four harness runs pass.\\n- [ ] Add both gifts’ full use, Consult, the ward, strains, and Cases 4 through 11 through the ending and credits.\\n- [ ] Fill feel, cinematics, synthesized score, the attract reel, and Skills Lab; run the single test command and the browser and Hub launches, saving logs and shots under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n- [ ] Write About data and `exit-interview.json` from real results, bundle the final HTML into the work-folder root, and confirm the test command still prints zero failures.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §21 says to cut late content if time runs out. That note does not lower this contract: a missing never-cut feature (cursor, any of the eight tools, either gift, the finale, Grand Rounds, Hub passes, attract, dev mode, 10-foot UI, About, exit interview) or a stubbed case fails the criteria.\\n- Cloned engine or Hub docs may disagree with PLAN.md §3. Trust the clone, adapt, and record the patch. Do not drop a TASK.md requirement to match an older note.\\n- The chained playthrough is long. Run it headless without drawing except where a draw-error check is required. `Target closed` means the machine ran out of memory; run one or two browsers at a time.\\n- There is no physical DualSense and no real iPhone. The pad stub and a WebKit iPhone profile are the accepted stand-ins. WebKit is not iOS Safari.\\n- The title is chosen at build time by RNG, so the filename cannot be fixed here. Match the template and the on-screen title; do not invent a second title in the verifier.\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-49a425b3-684f-4da4-91c9-6dbeaea2ff49-63","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"902→## 19. Code architecture\\n\\n### 19.1 Layout (relative to the dev folder)\\n\\n```\\nvendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/   engine, docs, tools (read-only unless you patch the engine; note every patch)\\nvendor/hub/                      session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, the arena example\\nsrc/config.js                    GAME_TITLE, VERSION, TUNING defaults, hub tag strings\\n910→src/core/   state.js rng.js op.js tools.js objects.js strains/*.js score.js   (the sim: no draw, audio or DOM)\\nsrc/data/   cases/*.js sites.js cast.js story/*.js barks.js songs.js         (content as data)\\nsrc/art/    tissue.js sites.js bust.js instruments.js icons.js strains.js stages/*.js props.js glyphs.js\\nsrc/audio/  sfx.js babble.js choir.js music.js\\nsrc/ui/     hud.js wheel.js results.js menus.js casefiles.js about.js dev.js attract.js card.js\\nsrc/scenes/ title.js menu.js story.js chart.js op.js lost.js results.js ward.js lobby.js credits.js hubround.js\\nsrc/net/    hub.js local.js\\nsrc/bot/    autosurgeon.js\\nsrc/main.js\\nsrc/manifest.json                load order, shared by the dev page, the tests and the bundler\\n920→src/about-data.json              written last\\ntools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\\ntools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\\nindex.dev.html                   loads the sources one by one, for working\\ntests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\\nnotes/feedback.md                your running log\\nCONTENT.md                       one page: how to add a case, a strain, a site, a character, a story node\\n```\\n\\nEvery source file is wrapped, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, G = (window.GAME ||= {}); ... })();`, and shares things through `G`; a bare top-level `const E` in two scripts would be a redeclaration error. Wrap the Appendix code the same way. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\\n930→\\n### 19.2 The sim is plain data\\n\\n**All op state lives in one JSON-safe object, `S`.** No classes, closures or canvases in it; registries hold behavior, keyed by `o.type`. Its RNG is an integer in `S`, and the sim never touches `Math.random` or the clock. This one rule gives you, for free:\\n- Second Look's rewind (`structuredClone` every .1 s).\\n- Phase checkpoints.\\n- Network snapshots (a subset of `S`).\\n- Deterministic tests, `game.stateHash`, and the attract reel.\\n\\n```js\\n940→Op.create(caseDef, { seed, difficulty, players, tuning })  // → S\\nOp.step(S, inputs, dt)                                      // inputs[i]: { x, y, tool, trig, fine, gift, consult, cancel }, sim only\\nCursor.update(player, device, S, dt)                        // device → cursor, assist reads S; runs outside the sim, one per local player\\n```\\n\\n`S.ev` is a per-step list of presentation events (`['stitch', x, y, grade]`). The scene drains it into sounds, particles, popups and rumble, and it isn't snapshotted, so a rewind doesn't replay them. Draw never changes `S`. Tuning lives outside `S`, so a rewind doesn't undo a slider.\\n\\n### 19.3 Content is data\\n\\n`defCase`, `defObject`, `defStrain`, `defSite`, `defCast`, E.Story nodes, bark lists. Cases refer to everything by id. The test suite validates every reference. **This is the \\\"normal designer tools\\\" path TASK.md asks for:** adding a case is a data file plus a recipe, no engine or sim edits, and `CONTENT.md` says how. Dev mode's Jump and Skills Lab are the workshop.\\n950→\\n### 19.4 One bot, three jobs\\n\\n`src/bot/autosurgeon.js` plays through a **virtual device** feeding `Cursor.update` the same stick and trigger values as a pad, so it exercises the real input path. Each object type gives a plan as a generator:\\n```js\\ndefObject('shard', { /* ... */ bot: function* (o, S, B) { yield* B.tool('forceps'); yield* B.moveTo(o.x, o.y); B.press(); yield* B.pull(o.axis, o.depth * 1.2, 90); B.release(); } });\\n```\\nOptions set its skill (speed, reaction delay, aim error) and cheats. Jobs: the attract mode (cheats on), the scripted full playthrough (cheats off), balance runs (`tools/balance.mjs`: a few skill levels, every case, a compact printout). It also computes `par`. On a Second Look's rewind, drop the current plan and replan.\\n\\n### 19.5 Engine use\\n960→\\nUse the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`. Standard features stay standard (pause, settings, rebinding, full screen, boot, autopause). Expected engine patch: only Appendix E's notice. Write down why for each patch you make, for the Engine Feedback.\\n\\nThe game's top level, from the pieces proved in section 3:\\n\\n```js\\nconst inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', id: GAME_TITLE, res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', input: INPUT,\\n  live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  menu: { items: inSession ? [] : [['Dev Mode', openDev]], saves: !inSession, quit: inSession ? false : 'title',\\n970→    controls: { useTool: 'Use tool', fine: 'Steady hand', gift: 'The Steady', consult: 'Consult', toolPrev: 'Previous tool', toolNext: 'Next tool', wheelHold: 'Tool wheel', tool1: false, tool2: false, tool3: false, tool4: false, tool5: false, tool6: false, tool7: false, tool8: false },\\n    settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] },\\n      { key: 'voices', label: 'Voices', type: 'slider', value: .9, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.voiceVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } } /* and section 15's others */ ] } });\\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, theme: { paper: 'rgba(6,22,26,.94)', accent: '#5ff0e0', line: 'rgba(95,240,224,.35)', ink: '#e8fbf6', muted: '#8fb8b0', danger: '#ff7a6a' } });\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 20. Testing\\n\\n980→As TASK.md says: headless tools first, scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game; **one command that prints only failures and a one-line count**; rerun only after changing what it covers; screenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n**`node tests/run.mjs`** (add `--fast` to skip the browser parts). Load engine and sources with `node:vm` as `game/test.mjs` does, giving the context `console`, `performance` and `window` (itself), drive with `game.advance`, `input.tap`, `input.hold`, `input.feed`, read `game.debug.snapshot()`. Output, and nothing else: failures, then e.g. `412 checks, 0 failed`.\\n\\n**Headless:**\\n- Every tool: right gesture finishes the object; each wrong gesture gives the specified slip, tear or lock.\\n- Cursor: full stick for 1 s moves 300 u or more; with Fine, 120 u or less; magnet settles on a target; guide-follow holds a line at full assist.\\n- Wheel: each of the eight stick directions picks its tool within 100 ms; 1 to 8 and mouse-hold picking do the same.\\n- Vitals and clock: drains add up as table 7 says; Code Blue timing window; lost path; phase checkpoint restores exactly.\\n- Grades and ranks: known inputs give the expected grade and rank.\\n990→- Every strain's stages reach their ends, and the failure branches (Legato snapping, Da Capo repeat, Cantor's rewind).\\n- Long Breath: world time at .25, hands at 1.\\n- Second Look: restored `S` deep-equals the old snapshot, and the ghost list is filled.\\n- Determinism: same seed and inputs give the same hash twice, and again with `draw: true` (draw changes nothing, no draw errors).\\n- Content validator: every id resolves, every story node reachable, every portrait expression exists.\\n- `TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub` grep over `src/`.\\n- **Full playthrough:** New Game → every story scene (auto) → ward → every case, bot with cheats off at Resident → ending → credits → title. Checks the save, ranks, and unlocks. This is your most valuable test. Keep it fast by not drawing, then draw one case for draw errors.\\n- **Attract:** title idle 10 s starts it; each device's input exits to the title; the press does nothing else; it loops at least twice with no errors. Not on reading screens.\\n- **Dev mode:** every slider changes behavior live, Reset restores `TUNING`, each cheat works.\\n- Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots: all phases finish; `retractorHandle` works solo and with two.\\n1000→- The exit interview and `src/about-data.json` parse as JSON, and every field is filled.\\n\\n**Browser (Playwright, one or two browsers at a time, from `file://` where possible):** launch Chromium with `--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required` for audio checks. Without it, the console's AudioContext warning before the first gesture is not a bug, so don't count warnings as failures.\\n- The built HTML plays 30 s with no errors in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.\\n- `node tools/check.mjs` on the page (add `#scene` to jump to a scene): errors, what's on screen, look notes. Act on every look note.\\n- Settings defaults: music .1; glyphs PlayStation; the Xbox option switches labels.\\n- Pad with the Appendix E stub: `R2` and `△` prompts, stick cursor, wheel, trigger; keyboard and mouse switch the prompts.\\n- Phone profiles (Chromium, and WebKit with an iPhone profile, the closest thing here to iOS): notice and Settings button show, no touch buttons, attract runs behind, and a tap on Settings (`page.touchscreen.tap`) opens it.\\n- Audio: render through an `OfflineAudioContext` or read an `AnalyserNode`: effects, each voice and the choir are not silent; at defaults music is well below effects.\\n- Sizes: 1280x720, 1920x1080, 2560x1440, 3440x1440: HUD inside the screen, cavity centered.\\n1010→- **Hub harness, all four runs (Appendix D's runner):** `players=2&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Then open the page outside a session.\\n- This computer has no second player, so use the harness's frames, or two browser pages or contexts, as the stand-in. With 2 players in the harness, whose game frames are same-origin and reachable from the test: feed a client's cursor through a stroke, and check the stroke lands on the host's state.\\n\\n**Screenshots, for what scripts can't judge:** each site, each stage, the portraits, one frame of each strain, the wheel, Long Breath. Use `tools/filmstrip.mjs` for motion. Judge at 1920x1080 for the 10-foot view. WebGPU isn't used, so screenshots work.\\n\\n**This computer** (full detail in TASK.md): no display, so `xvfb-run` if you ever need headed; Playwright 1.63 is ready (`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder for Node); never run `playwright install`; for a Python library such as Pillow, use `uv` as TASK.md says; `Target closed` means memory ran out, not a bug: run fewer browsers. Other agents share this machine, so keep one or two browsers open and only read what you need, never the folders beside yours. Keep all files in your folder, not `/tmp`. Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. Other agents share this machine's ports and processes: use a server only for the harness, bound to `127.0.0.1` on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it), and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a port.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 21. Build order\\n1020→\\nEach milestone ends with a playable, tested game. Multiplayer comes early because it constrains the sim.\\n\\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| M0 | Title picked. Folders, vendor, manifest, bundler, dev page, test runner, Hub client in the page | Empty game builds, runs, one test passes, harness runner works on Appendix D |\\n| M1 | **Hands:** sim core, tissue painter, cursor, wheel, Forceps, Salve, Suture, Syringe, vitals, clock, grades, HUD, Results, Case 1 end to end, bot | A person would enjoy Case 1 on a stubbed pad and mouse. Tune this until it's good; everything rests on it |\\n| M2 | **Shell:** title, menu, settings, glyphs, pause, TV scale, About skeleton, Dev Mode, attract v1, touch notice, saves, story system, busts, voices, first music, Case 1's story | First launch to Case 1 to Results feels finished, all TASK.md's cross-cutting features exist |\\n| M3 | Scalpel, Suction, Cautery, Sonar, Lightbox, Code Blue, Long Breath, Cases 2 and 3, Chapter 1 complete | Chapter 1 plays through, bot and all |\\n| M4 | **Grand Rounds:** local, then Hub, own card | All four harness runs pass, co-op works with bots |\\n1030→| M5 | Staccato, Legato, Tremolo, ward, Cases 4 to 6, Chapter 2 | Chapter 2 plays through |\\n| M6 | Second Look, tilt, blackout, Da Capo, device gestures, Cases 7 to 9, Chapter 3 | Chapter 3 plays through |\\n| M7 | Consult, Fermata, Cantor, Cases 10 and 11, ending, credits | The whole story plays through |\\n| M8 | **Polish:** feel table complete, cinematics, stages, title art, full score and mix, attract final reel, Skills Lab, balance runs, three browsers, CONTENT.md | Section 22 all true |\\n| M9 | About text, exit interview, final build, final test run, chat reply | Done |\\n\\n**If you run out of runway**, cut content from the end of this list and keep everything else: Case 9, then Skills Lab, then Da Capo's round 2, then the ship's ward (reuse Ward 3), then a stage or two. **Never cut:** the cursor's quality, any of the eight tools, both gifts, the finale, Grand Rounds and the Hub tests, attract mode, dev mode, the 10-foot UI, About, the exit interview. Whatever ships is complete: no stubs, no TODOs.\\n\\n---\\n\\n1040→## 22. Done checklist (TASK.md, line by line)\\n\\nGo through this at the end. Everything must be true.\\n\\n**Source, genre, perspective, title.**\\n- [ ] Original game from *Trauma Center: Second Opinion* per the originality rule; genre and perspective per section 2.\\n- [ ] Title is a playful riff, chosen by TASK.md's method with a real RNG, stored in one constant.\\n\\n**Package and environment.**\\n- [ ] One HTML file at the root as TASK.md names it, self-contained, working from `file://`.\\n1050→- [ ] Dev files in the subfolder TASK.md names. Nothing read from other agents' folders. Only your own processes stopped, by PID.\\n\\n**Tech, art, animation.**\\n- [ ] Built on the engine's handoff package; engine patches noted.\\n- [ ] Native pixel look as the base, new art for everything surgical, asset store only for generic props.\\n- [ ] Native animation as the base, new animations per section 17.\\n\\n**Audio.**\\n- [ ] All music, effects and voices in code, no audio files. Gibberish voices.\\n- [ ] Music at 10% by default (test proves it).\\n1060→\\n**Online.**\",\"content_concise\":\"902→## 19. Code architecture\\n\\n### 19.1 Layout (relative to the dev folder)\\n\\n```\\nvendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/   engine, docs, tools (read-only unless you patch the engine; note every patch)\\nvendor/hub/                      session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, the arena example\\nsrc/config.js                    GAME_TITLE, VERSION, TUNING defaults, hub tag strings\\n910→src/core/   state.js rng.js op.js tools.js objects.js strains/*.js score.js   (the sim: no draw, audio or DOM)\\nsrc/data/   cases/*.js sites.js cast.js story/*.js barks.js songs.js         (content as data)\\nsrc/art/    tissue.js sites.js bust.js instruments.js icons.js strains.js stages/*.js props.js glyphs.js\\nsrc/audio/  sfx.js babble.js choir.js music.js\\nsrc/ui/     hud.js wheel.js results.js menus.js casefiles.js about.js dev.js attract.js card.js\\nsrc/scenes/ title.js menu.js story.js chart.js op.js lost.js results.js ward.js lobby.js credits.js hubround.js\\nsrc/net/    hub.js local.js\\nsrc/bot/    autosurgeon.js\\nsrc/main.js\\nsrc/manifest.json                load order, shared by the dev page, the tests and the bundler\\n920→src/about-data.json              written last\\ntools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\\ntools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\\nindex.dev.html                   loads the sources one by one, for working\\ntests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\\nnotes/feedback.md                your running log\\nCONTENT.md                       one page: how to add a case, a strain, a site, a character, a story node\\n```\\n\\nEvery source file is wrapped, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, G = (window.GAME ||= {}); ... })();`, and shares things through `G`; a bare top-level `const E` in two scripts would be a redeclaration error. Wrap the Appendix code the same way. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\\n930→\\n### 19.2 The sim is plain data\\n\\n**All op state lives in one JSON-safe object, `S`.** No classes, closures or canvases in it; registries hold behavior, keyed by `o.type`. Its RNG is an integer in `S`, and the sim never touches `Math.random` or the clock. This one rule gives you, for free:\\n- Second Look's rewind (`structuredClone` every .1 s).\\n- Phase checkpoints.\\n- Network snapshots (a subset of `S`).\\n- Deterministic tests, `game.stateHash`, and the attract reel.\\n\\n```js\\n940→Op.create(caseDef, { seed, difficulty, players, tuning })  // → S\\nOp.step(S, inputs, dt)                                      // inputs[i]: { x, y, tool, trig, fine, gift, consult, cancel }, sim only\\nCursor.update(player, device, S, dt)                        // device → cursor, assist reads S; runs outside the sim, one per local player\\n```\\n\\n`S.ev` is a per-step list of presentation events (`['stitch', x, y, grade]`). The scene drains it into sounds, particles, popups and rumble, and it isn't snapshotted, so a rewind doesn't replay them. Draw never changes `S`. Tuning lives outside `S`, so a rewind doesn't undo a slider.\\n\\n### 19.3 Content is data\\n\\n`defCase`, `defObject`, `defStrain`, `defSite`, `defCast`, E.Story nodes, bark lists. Cases refer to everything by id. The test suite validates every reference. **This is the \\\"normal designer tools\\\" path TASK.md asks for:** adding a case is a data file plus a recipe, no engine or sim edits, and `CONTENT.md` says how. Dev mode's Jump and Skills Lab are the workshop.\\n950→\\n### 19.4 One bot, three jobs\\n\\n`src/bot/autosurgeon.js` plays through a **virtual device** feeding `Cursor.update` the same stick and trigger values as a pad, so it exercises the real input path. Each object type gives a plan as a generator:\\n```js\\ndefObject('shard', { /* ... */ bot: function* (o, S, B) { yield* B.tool('forceps'); yield* B.moveTo(o.x, o.y); B.press(); yield* B.pull(o.axis, o.depth * 1.2, 90); B.release(); } });\\n```\\nOptions set its skill (speed, reaction delay, aim error) and cheats. Jobs: the attract mode (cheats on), the scripted full playthrough (cheats off), balance runs (`tools/balance.mjs`: a few skill levels, every case, a compact printout). It also computes `par`. On a Second Look's rewind, drop the current plan and replan.\\n\\n### 19.5 Engine use\\n960→\\nUse the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`. Standard features stay standard (pause, settings, rebinding, full screen, boot, autopause). Expected engine patch: only Appendix E's notice. Write down why for each patch you make, for the Engine Feedback.\\n\\nThe game's top level, from the pieces proved in section 3:\\n\\n```js\\nconst inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', id: GAME_TITLE, res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', input: INPUT,\\n  live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  menu: { items: inSession ? [] : [['Dev Mode', openDev]], saves: !inSession, quit: inSession ? false : 'title',\\n970→    controls: { useTool: 'Use tool', fine: 'Steady hand', gift: 'The Steady', consult: 'Consult', toolPrev: 'Previous tool', toolNext: 'Next tool', wheelHold: 'Tool wheel', tool1: false, tool2: false, tool3: false, tool4: false, tool5: false, tool6: false, tool7: false, tool8: false },\\n    settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] },\\n      { key: 'voices', label: 'Voices', type: 'slider', value: .9, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.voiceVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } } /* and section 15's others */ ] } });\\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, theme: { paper: 'rgba(6,22,26,.94)', accent: '#5ff0e0', line: 'rgba(95,240,224,.35)', ink: '#e8fbf6', muted: '#8fb8b0', danger: '#ff7a6a' } });\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 20. Testing\\n\\n980→As TASK.md says: headless tools first, scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game; **one command that prints only failures and a one-line count**; rerun only after changing what it covers; screenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n**`node tests/run.mjs`** (add `--fast` to skip the browser parts). Load engine and sources with `node:vm` as `game/test.mjs` does, giving the context `console`, `performance` and `window` (itself), drive with `game.advance`, `input.tap`, `input.hold`, `input.feed`, read `game.debug.snapshot()`. Output, and nothing else: failures, then e.g. `412 checks, 0 failed`.\\n\\n**Headless:**\\n- Every tool: right gesture finishes the object; each wrong gesture gives the specified slip, tear or lock.\\n- Cursor: full stick for 1 s moves 300 u or more; with Fine, 120 u or less; magnet settles on a target; guide-follow holds a line at full assist.\\n- Wheel: each of the eight stick directions picks its tool within 100 ms; 1 to 8 and mouse-hold picking do the same.\\n- Vitals and clock: drains add up as table 7 says; Code Blue timing window; lost path; phase checkpoint restores exactly.\\n- Grades and ranks: known inputs give the expected grade and rank.\\n990→- Every strain's stages reach their ends, and the failure branches (Legato snapping, Da Capo repeat, Cantor's rewind).\\n- Long Breath: world time at .25, hands at 1.\\n- Second Look: restored `S` deep-equals the old snapshot, and the ghost list is filled.\\n- Determinism: same seed and inputs give the same hash twice, and again with `draw: true` (draw changes nothing, no draw errors).\\n- Content validator: every id resolves, every story node reachable, every portrait expression exists.\\n- `TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub` grep over `src/`.\\n- **Full playthrough:** New Game → every story scene (auto) → ward → every case, bot with cheats off at Resident → ending → credits → title. Checks the save, ranks, and unlocks. This is your most valuable test. Keep it fast by not drawing, then draw one case for draw errors.\\n- **Attract:** title idle 10 s starts it; each device's input exits to the title; the press does nothing else; it loops at least twice with no errors. Not on reading screens.\\n- **Dev mode:** every slider changes behavior live, Reset restores `TUNING`, each cheat works.\\n- Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots: all phases finish; `retractorHandle` works solo and with two.\\n1000→- The exit interview and `src/about-data.json` parse as JSON, and every field is filled.\\n\\n**Browser (Playwright, one or two browsers at a time, from `file://` where possible):** launch Chromium with `--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required` for audio checks. Without it, the console's AudioContext warning before the first gesture is not a bug, so don't count warnings as failures.\\n- The built HTML plays 30 s with no errors in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.\\n- `node tools/check.mjs` on the page (add `#scene` to jump to a scene): errors, what's on screen, look notes. Act on every look note.\\n- Settings defaults: music .1; glyphs PlayStation; the Xbox option switches labels.\\n- Pad with the Appendix E stub: `R2` and `△` prompts, stick cursor, wheel, trigger; keyboard and mouse switch the prompts.\\n- Phone profiles (Chromium, and WebKit with an iPhone profile, the closest thing here to iOS): notice and Settings button show, no touch buttons, attract runs behind, and a tap on Settings (`page.touchscreen.tap`) opens it.\\n- Audio: render through an `OfflineAudioContext` or read an `AnalyserNode`: effects, each voice and the choir are not silent; at defaults music is well below effects.\\n- Sizes: 1280x720, 1920x1080, 2560x1440, 3440x1440: HUD inside the screen, cavity centered.\\n1010→- **Hub harness, all four runs (Appendix D's runner):** `players=2&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Then open the page outside a session.\\n- This computer has no second player, so use the harness's frames, or two browser pages or contexts, as the stand-in. With 2 players in the harness, whose game frames are same-origin and reachable from the test: feed a client's cursor through a stroke, and check the stroke lands on the host's state.\\n\\n**Screenshots, for what scripts can't judge:** each site, each stage, the portraits, one frame of each strain, the wheel, Long Breath. Use `tools/filmstrip.mjs` for motion. Judge at 1920x1080 for the 10-foot view. WebGPU isn't used, so screenshots work.\\n\\n**This computer** (full detail in TASK.md): no display, so `xvfb-run` if you ever need headed; Playwright 1.63 is ready (`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder for Node); never run `playwright install`; for a Python library such as Pillow, use `uv` as TASK.md says; `Target closed` means memory ran out, not a bug: run fewer browsers. Other agents share this machine, so keep one or two browsers open and only read what you need, never the folders beside yours. Keep all files in your folder, not `/tmp`. Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. Other agents share this machine's ports and processes: use a server only for the harness, bound to `127.0.0.1` on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it), and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a port.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 21. Build order\\n1020→\\nEach milestone ends with a playable, tested game. Multiplayer comes early because it constrains the sim.\\n\\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| M0 | Title picked. Folders, vendor, manifest, bundler, dev page, test runner, Hub client in the page | Empty game builds, runs, one test passes, harness runner works on Appendix D |\\n| M1 | **Hands:** sim core, tissue painter, cursor, wheel, Forceps, Salve, Suture, Syringe, vitals, clock, grades, HUD, Results, Case 1 end to end, bot | A person would enjoy Case 1 on a stubbed pad and mouse. Tune this until it's good; everything rests on it |\\n| M2 | **Shell:** title, menu, settings, glyphs, pause, TV scale, About skeleton, Dev Mode, attract v1, touch notice, saves, story system, busts, voices, first music, Case 1's story | First launch to Case 1 to Results feels finished, all TASK.md's cross-cutting features exist |\\n| M3 | Scalpel, Suction, Cautery, Sonar, Lightbox, Code Blue, Long Breath, Cases 2 and 3, Chapter 1 complete | Chapter 1 plays through, bot and all |\\n| M4 | **Grand Rounds:** local, then Hub, own card | All four harness runs pass, co-op works with bots |\\n1030→| M5 | Staccato, Legato, Tremolo, ward, Cases 4 to 6, Chapter 2 | Chapter 2 plays through |\\n| M6 | Second Look, tilt, blackout, Da Capo, device gestures, Cases 7 to 9, Chapter 3 | Chapter 3 plays through |\\n| M7 | Consult, Fermata, Cantor, Cases 10 and 11, ending, credits | The whole story plays through |\\n| M8 | **Polish:** feel table complete, cinematics, stages, title art, full score and mix, attract final reel, Skills Lab, balance runs, three browsers, CONTENT.md | Section 22 all true |\\n| M9 | About text, exit interview, final build, final test run, chat reply | Done |\\n\\n**If you run out of runway**, cut content from the end of this list and keep everything else: Case 9, then Skills Lab, then Da Capo's round 2, then the ship's ward (reuse Ward 3), then a stage or two. **Never cut:** the cursor's quality, any of the eight tools, both gifts, the finale, Grand Rounds and the Hub tests, attract mode, dev mode, the 10-foot UI, About, the exit interview. Whatever ships is complete: no stubs, no TODOs.\\n\\n---\\n\\n1040→## 22. Done checklist (TASK.md, line by line)\\n\\nGo through this at the end. Everything must be true.\\n\\n**Source, genre, perspective, title.**\\n- [ ] Original game from *Trauma Center: Second Opinion* per the originality rule; genre and perspective per section 2.\\n- [ ] Title is a playful riff, chosen by TASK.md's method with a real RNG, stored in one constant.\\n\\n**Package and environment.**\\n- [ ] One HTML file at the root as TASK.md names it, self-contained, working from `file://`.\\n1050→- [ ] Dev files in the subfolder TASK.md names. Nothing read from other agents' folders. Only your own processes stopped, by PID.\\n\\n**Tech, art, animation.**\\n- [ ] Built on the engine's handoff package; engine patches noted.\\n- [ ] Native pixel look as the base, new art for everything surgical, asset store only for generic props.\\n- [ ] Native animation as the base, new animations per section 17.\\n\\n**Audio.**\\n- [ ] All music, effects and voices in code, no audio files. Gibberish voices.\\n- [ ] Music at 10% by default (test proves it).\\n1060→\\n**Online.**\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":902,\"limit\":160,\"raw_output\":\"## 19. Code architecture\\n\\n### 19.1 Layout (relative to the dev folder)\\n\\n```\\nvendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/   engine, docs, tools (read-only unless you patch the engine; note every patch)\\nvendor/hub/                      session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, the arena example\\nsrc/config.js                    GAME_TITLE, VERSION, TUNING defaults, hub tag strings\\nsrc/core/   state.js rng.js op.js tools.js objects.js strains/*.js score.js   (the sim: no draw, audio or DOM)\\nsrc/data/   cases/*.js sites.js cast.js story/*.js barks.js songs.js         (content as data)\\nsrc/art/    tissue.js sites.js bust.js instruments.js icons.js strains.js stages/*.js props.js glyphs.js\\nsrc/audio/  sfx.js babble.js choir.js music.js\\nsrc/ui/     hud.js wheel.js results.js menus.js casefiles.js about.js dev.js attract.js card.js\\nsrc/scenes/ title.js menu.js story.js chart.js op.js lost.js results.js ward.js lobby.js credits.js hubround.js\\nsrc/net/    hub.js local.js\\nsrc/bot/    autosurgeon.js\\nsrc/main.js\\nsrc/manifest.json                load order, shared by the dev page, the tests and the bundler\\nsrc/about-data.json              written last\\ntools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\\ntools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\\nindex.dev.html                   loads the sources one by one, for working\\ntests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\\nnotes/feedback.md                your running log\\nCONTENT.md                       one page: how to add a case, a strain, a site, a character, a story node\\n```\\n\\nEvery source file is wrapped, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, G = (window.GAME ||= {}); ... })();`, and shares things through `G`; a bare top-level `const E` in two scripts would be a redeclaration error. Wrap the Appendix code the same way. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\\n\\n### 19.2 The sim is plain data\\n\\n**All op state lives in one JSON-safe object, `S`.** No classes, closures or canvases in it; registries hold behavior, keyed by `o.type`. Its RNG is an integer in `S`, and the sim never touches `Math.random` or the clock. This one rule gives you, for free:\\n- Second Look's rewind (`structuredClone` every .1 s).\\n- Phase checkpoints.\\n- Network snapshots (a subset of `S`).\\n- Deterministic tests, `game.stateHash`, and the attract reel.\\n\\n```js\\nOp.create(caseDef, { seed, difficulty, players, tuning })  // → S\\nOp.step(S, inputs, dt)                                      // inputs[i]: { x, y, tool, trig, fine, gift, consult, cancel }, sim only\\nCursor.update(player, device, S, dt)                        // device → cursor, assist reads S; runs outside the sim, one per local player\\n```\\n\\n`S.ev` is a per-step list of presentation events (`['stitch', x, y, grade]`). The scene drains it into sounds, particles, popups and rumble, and it isn't snapshotted, so a rewind doesn't replay them. Draw never changes `S`. Tuning lives outside `S`, so a rewind doesn't undo a slider.\\n\\n### 19.3 Content is data\\n\\n`defCase`, `defObject`, `defStrain`, `defSite`, `defCast`, E.Story nodes, bark lists. Cases refer to everything by id. The test suite validates every reference. **This is the \\\"normal designer tools\\\" path TASK.md asks for:** adding a case is a data file plus a recipe, no engine or sim edits, and `CONTENT.md` says how. Dev mode's Jump and Skills Lab are the workshop.\\n\\n### 19.4 One bot, three jobs\\n\\n`src/bot/autosurgeon.js` plays through a **virtual device** feeding `Cursor.update` the same stick and trigger values as a pad, so it exercises the real input path. Each object type gives a plan as a generator:\\n```js\\ndefObject('shard', { /* ... */ bot: function* (o, S, B) { yield* B.tool('forceps'); yield* B.moveTo(o.x, o.y); B.press(); yield* B.pull(o.axis, o.depth * 1.2, 90); B.release(); } });\\n```\\nOptions set its skill (speed, reaction delay, aim error) and cheats. Jobs: the attract mode (cheats on), the scripted full playthrough (cheats off), balance runs (`tools/balance.mjs`: a few skill levels, every case, a compact printout). It also computes `par`. On a Second Look's rewind, drop the current plan and replan.\\n\\n### 19.5 Engine use\\n\\nUse the full engine `my-3d2dge.js`. Standard features stay standard (pause, settings, rebinding, full screen, boot, autopause). Expected engine patch: only Appendix E's notice. Write down why for each patch you make, for the Engine Feedback.\\n\\nThe game's top level, from the pieces proved in section 3:\\n\\n```js\\nconst inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', id: GAME_TITLE, res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', input: INPUT,\\n  live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  menu: { items: inSession ? [] : [['Dev Mode', openDev]], saves: !inSession, quit: inSession ? false : 'title',\\n    controls: { useTool: 'Use tool', fine: 'Steady hand', gift: 'The Steady', consult: 'Consult', toolPrev: 'Previous tool', toolNext: 'Next tool', wheelHold: 'Tool wheel', tool1: false, tool2: false, tool3: false, tool4: false, tool5: false, tool6: false, tool7: false, tool8: false },\\n    settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] },\\n      { key: 'voices', label: 'Voices', type: 'slider', value: .9, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.voiceVolume = v; g.audio.applyVolume(); } } /* and section 15's others */ ] } });\\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, theme: { paper: 'rgba(6,22,26,.94)', accent: '#5ff0e0', line: 'rgba(95,240,224,.35)', ink: '#e8fbf6', muted: '#8fb8b0', danger: '#ff7a6a' } });\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 20. Testing\\n\\nAs TASK.md says: headless tools first, scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game; **one command that prints only failures and a one-line count**; rerun only after changing what it covers; screenshots only for what a script can't check; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\n**`node tests/run.mjs`** (add `--fast` to skip the browser parts). Load engine and sources with `node:vm` as `game/test.mjs` does, giving the context `console`, `performance` and `window` (itself), drive with `game.advance`, `input.tap`, `input.hold`, `input.feed`, read `game.debug.snapshot()`. Output, and nothing else: failures, then e.g. `412 checks, 0 failed`.\\n\\n**Headless:**\\n- Every tool: right gesture finishes the object; each wrong gesture gives the specified slip, tear or lock.\\n- Cursor: full stick for 1 s moves 300 u or more; with Fine, 120 u or less; magnet settles on a target; guide-follow holds a line at full assist.\\n- Wheel: each of the eight stick directions picks its tool within 100 ms; 1 to 8 and mouse-hold picking do the same.\\n- Vitals and clock: drains add up as table 7 says; Code Blue timing window; lost path; phase checkpoint restores exactly.\\n- Grades and ranks: known inputs give the expected grade and rank.\\n- Every strain's stages reach their ends, and the failure branches (Legato snapping, Da Capo repeat, Cantor's rewind).\\n- Long Breath: world time at .25, hands at 1.\\n- Second Look: restored `S` deep-equals the old snapshot, and the ghost list is filled.\\n- Determinism: same seed and inputs give the same hash twice, and again with `draw: true` (draw changes nothing, no draw errors).\\n- Content validator: every id resolves, every story node reachable, every portrait expression exists.\\n- `TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub` grep over `src/`.\\n- **Full playthrough:** New Game → every story scene (auto) → ward → every case, bot with cheats off at Resident → ending → credits → title. Checks the save, ranks, and unlocks. This is your most valuable test. Keep it fast by not drawing, then draw one case for draw errors.\\n- **Attract:** title idle 10 s starts it; each device's input exits to the title; the press does nothing else; it loops at least twice with no errors. Not on reading screens.\\n- **Dev mode:** every slider changes behavior live, Reset restores `TUNING`, each cheat works.\\n- Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots: all phases finish; `retractorHandle` works solo and with two.\\n- The exit interview and `src/about-data.json` parse as JSON, and every field is filled.\\n\\n**Browser (Playwright, one or two browsers at a time, from `file://` where possible):** launch Chromium with `--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required` for audio checks. Without it, the console's AudioContext warning before the first gesture is not a bug, so don't count warnings as failures.\\n- The built HTML plays 30 s with no errors in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.\\n- `node tools/check.mjs` on the page (add `#scene` to jump to a scene): errors, what's on screen, look notes. Act on every look note.\\n- Settings defaults: music .1; glyphs PlayStation; the Xbox option switches labels.\\n- Pad with the Appendix E stub: `R2` and `△` prompts, stick cursor, wheel, trigger; keyboard and mouse switch the prompts.\\n- Phone profiles (Chromium, and WebKit with an iPhone profile, the closest thing here to iOS): notice and Settings button show, no touch buttons, attract runs behind, and a tap on Settings (`page.touchscreen.tap`) opens it.\\n- Audio: render through an `OfflineAudioContext` or read an `AnalyserNode`: effects, each voice and the choir are not silent; at defaults music is well below effects.\\n- Sizes: 1280x720, 1920x1080, 2560x1440, 3440x1440: HUD inside the screen, cavity centered.\\n- **Hub harness, all four runs (Appendix D's runner):** `players=2&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Then open the page outside a session.\\n- This computer has no second player, so use the harness's frames, or two browser pages or contexts, as the stand-in. With 2 players in the harness, whose game frames are same-origin and reachable from the test: feed a client's cursor through a stroke, and check the stroke lands on the host's state.\\n\\n**Screenshots, for what scripts can't judge:** each site, each stage, the portraits, one frame of each strain, the wheel, Long Breath. Use `tools/filmstrip.mjs` for motion. Judge at 1920x1080 for the 10-foot view. WebGPU isn't used, so screenshots work.\\n\\n**This computer** (full detail in TASK.md): no display, so `xvfb-run` if you ever need headed; Playwright 1.63 is ready (`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder for Node); never run `playwright install`; for a Python library such as Pillow, use `uv` as TASK.md says; `Target closed` means memory ran out, not a bug: run fewer browsers. Other agents share this machine, so keep one or two browsers open and only read what you need, never the folders beside yours. Keep all files in your folder, not `/tmp`. Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. Other agents share this machine's ports and processes: use a server only for the harness, bound to `127.0.0.1` on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it), and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds a port.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 21. Build order\\n\\nEach milestone ends with a playable, tested game. Multiplayer comes early because it constrains the sim.\\n\\n| # | Milestone | Done when |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| M0 | Title picked. Folders, vendor, manifest, bundler, dev page, test runner, Hub client in the page | Empty game builds, runs, one test passes, harness runner works on Appendix D |\\n| M1 | **Hands:** sim core, tissue painter, cursor, wheel, Forceps, Salve, Suture, Syringe, vitals, clock, grades, HUD, Results, Case 1 end to end, bot | A person would enjoy Case 1 on a stubbed pad and mouse. Tune this until it's good; everything rests on it |\\n| M2 | **Shell:** title, menu, settings, glyphs, pause, TV scale, About skeleton, Dev Mode, attract v1, touch notice, saves, story system, busts, voices, first music, Case 1's story | First launch to Case 1 to Results feels finished, all TASK.md's cross-cutting features exist |\\n| M3 | Scalpel, Suction, Cautery, Sonar, Lightbox, Code Blue, Long Breath, Cases 2 and 3, Chapter 1 complete | Chapter 1 plays through, bot and all |\\n| M4 | **Grand Rounds:** local, then Hub, own card | All four harness runs pass, co-op works with bots |\\n| M5 | Staccato, Legato, Tremolo, ward, Cases 4 to 6, Chapter 2 | Chapter 2 plays through |\\n| M6 | Second Look, tilt, blackout, Da Capo, device gestures, Cases 7 to 9, Chapter 3 | Chapter 3 plays through |\\n| M7 | Consult, Fermata, Cantor, Cases 10 and 11, ending, credits | The whole story plays through |\\n| M8 | **Polish:** feel table complete, cinematics, stages, title art, full score and mix, attract final reel, Skills Lab, balance runs, three browsers, CONTENT.md | Section 22 all true |\\n| M9 | About text, exit interview, final build, final test run, chat reply | Done |\\n\\n**If you run out of runway**, cut content from the end of this list and keep everything else: Case 9, then Skills Lab, then Da Capo's round 2, then the ship's ward (reuse Ward 3), then a stage or two. **Never cut:** the cursor's quality, any of the eight tools, both gifts, the finale, Grand Rounds and the Hub tests, attract mode, dev mode, the 10-foot UI, About, the exit interview. Whatever ships is complete: no stubs, no TODOs.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 22. Done checklist (TASK.md, line by line)\\n\\nGo through this at the end. Everything must be true.\\n\\n**Source, genre, perspective, title.**\\n- [ ] Original game from *Trauma Center: Second Opinion* per the originality rule; genre and perspective per section 2.\\n- [ ] Title is a playful riff, chosen by TASK.md's method with a real RNG, stored in one constant.\\n\\n**Package and environment.**\\n- [ ] One HTML file at the root as TASK.md names it, self-contained, working from `file://`.\\n- [ ] Dev files in the subfolder TASK.md names. Nothing read from other agents' folders. Only your own processes stopped, by PID.\\n\\n**Tech, art, animation.**\\n- [ ] Built on the engine's handoff package; engine patches noted.\\n- [ ] Native pixel look as the base, new art for everything surgical, asset store only for generic props.\\n- [ ] Native animation as the base, new animations per section 17.\\n\\n**Audio.**\\n- [ ] All music, effects and voices in code, no audio files. Gibberish voices.\\n- [ ] Music at 10% by default (test proves it).\\n\\n**Online.**\\n\",\"total_lines\":1339}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"ef6b5016-a56b-4e65-9752-2751c97a98df"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_122","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The remaining implementation is very large.\n\nThe simulation and bot are working. I will lower the c10 parameter to 2000 so the rank becomes S. Then I will write the remaining files: art, audio, game scenes, hub, tests, bundle, about, and exit interview. I will read appendices A, C, and D in chunks and check the engine API for scene registration, story, menus, and audio.\n\nI will read the handoff game/index.html and scene API first. Then I will write the remaining files: tissue.js, bust.js, audio.js, game.js, tests/run.mjs, tools/build.mjs, CONTENT.md, about data, exit interview, and PROGRESS.md. The game.js shell will be the largest file.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-86a53474-6443-4998-83da-f68c19495121-64","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md","offset":1090,"limit":280}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-86a53474-6443-4998-83da-f68c19495121-65","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md","offset":316,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7357,"output_tokens":527,"cache_read_input_tokens":150144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"d4654be5-53f4-471c-97c7-79763dacfb01"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-86a53474-6443-4998-83da-f68c19495121-64","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1090→## Appendix A: tissue painter\\n\\nRan on this computer at 480x270, 3 to 5 ms a frame under software rendering. It also runs headless. One instance per site. Each frame: stamp pools, wounds and so on from `S`, then `shade(fx)`, then draw `F.cv`.\\n\\n- `stampDisc(x, y, r, height, mat)`, `stampLine(points, r, height, mat)`: per-frame height and material. Height alone (no `mat`) makes a ridge, for Legato.\\n- `shade({ beat, breath, slow, lens, light, dim, spot })`: see its comment. `dyn` and `over` clear after each shade.\\n- `slow: true` is Long Breath's palette. `lens` is Sonar's. `dim` and `spot` are the blackout. A moving `light` is the swaying lamp.\\n\\n```js\\n// Bake once per site, stamp from the sim's state each frame, then shade(). Cosmetic only: the sim never reads it. Needs E = My3D2dge in scope.\\n1100→const BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5].map(v => (v + .5) / 16 - .5);\\nconst hex3 = h => [parseInt(h.slice(1, 3), 16), parseInt(h.slice(3, 5), 16), parseInt(h.slice(5, 7), 16)];\\nfunction makeRamp(keys, n, slow) { // dark to light through hand-picked, hue-shifted keys. slow: the same ramp seen through Long Breath\\n  const c = keys.map(hex3), out = new Uint32Array(n);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const t = i / (n - 1) * (c.length - 1), j = Math.min(c.length - 2, t | 0), f = t - j; let r = c[j][0] + (c[j + 1][0] - c[j][0]) * f, g = c[j][1] + (c[j + 1][1] - c[j][1]) * f, b = c[j][2] + (c[j + 1][2] - c[j][2]) * f;\\n    if (slow) { const y = r * .3 + g * .59 + b * .11; r = y * .55 + 8; g = y * .95 + 14; b = y * 1.05 + 22; } out[i] = 0xff000000 | (Math.min(255, b) << 16) | (Math.min(255, g) << 8) | Math.min(255, r); }\\n  return out;\\n}\\nconst MAT_KEYS = { // name: [ramp keys, specular strength]\\n  wall: [['#1c060c', '#4a0f18', '#7d1f26', '#a93a38'], .35], bowel: [['#3a0e1c', '#8a2f3e', '#c75f62', '#eb9486', '#ffc9b0'], 1], liver: [['#1e0610', '#4e1022', '#7c1e30', '#a83a42', '#d0645c'], .55],\\n1110→  fat: [['#5a3a10', '#a8782a', '#dcb34c', '#f4d97e', '#fff2b8'], .7], vessel: [['#14103a', '#2c2a70', '#4a4aa0', '#7c78c8'], .8], artery: [['#3a0408', '#8c0f14', '#cf2a22', '#f4604a'], 1],\\n  skin: [['#6a3a22', '#a8683f', '#d39a68', '#eebf92'], .12], drape: [['#0c2c2a', '#14504a', '#1f7468', '#2f9a88'], 0], steel: [['#28303a', '#5a6a78', '#9aaab8', '#e8f0f8'], 1.6],\\n  blood: [['#180204', '#3c060a', '#680c10', '#8e1414'], 1.4], wound: [['#0c0104', '#2a0408', '#55090e', '#7a1216'], .5], char: [['#08070a', '#1c181a', '#332a28', '#4a3c34'], 0], gel: [['#0c4a38', '#1c8a64', '#54d0a0', '#b0ffe0'], 1.4] };\\nconst MAT_IDS = Object.keys(MAT_KEYS), MATS = MAT_IDS.map(k => ({ ramp: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20), slow: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20, true), spec: MAT_KEYS[k][1] }));\\nconst matId = n => MAT_IDS.indexOf(n);\\nfunction makeNoise(seed) { let a = seed >>> 0; const R = () => { a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0; let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), a | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };\\n  const L = new Float32Array(65536); for (let i = 0; i < L.length; i++) L[i] = R();\\n  const v = (x, y) => { const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), fx = x - xi, fy = y - yi, u = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), w = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy), s = (p, q) => L[(p & 255) | ((q & 255) << 8)]; return (s(xi, yi) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi) * u) * (1 - w) + (s(xi, yi + 1) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi + 1) * u) * w; };\\n  return { R, fbm: (x, y, o = 4) => { let k = .5, f = 1, n = 0; for (let i = 0; i < o; i++) { n += k * v(x * f, y * f); k *= .5; f *= 2.03; } return n; } }; }\\nclass TissueField {\\n1120→  constructor(W, H, seed = 7) { this.W = W; this.H = H; const N = W * H; this.h = new Float32Array(N); this.m = new Uint8Array(N); this.pulse = new Float32Array(N); this.ao = new Float32Array(N).fill(1); this.dyn = new Float32Array(N); this.over = new Uint8Array(N); this.noise = makeNoise(seed);\\n    this.cv = E.mkCanvas(W, H); this.g = this.cv.getContext('2d'); this.img = this.g.createImageData(W, H); this.u = new Uint32Array(this.img.data.buffer); }\\n  blob(x, y, rx, ry, rot, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, pulse, noise } = this, c = Math.cos(rot), s = Math.sin(rot), R = Math.max(rx, ry) + (o.warp || 0) + 2, id = matId(mat), warp = o.warp || 0, base = o.base || 0, add = !!o.add;\\n    for (let py = Math.max(0, y - R | 0); py < Math.min(H, y + R + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(0, x - R | 0); px < Math.min(W, x + R + 1); px++) {\\n      const wx = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, wy = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03 + 40, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, dx = px - x + wx, dy = py - y + wy, u = (dx * c + dy * s) / rx, v = (-dx * s + dy * c) / ry, d = u * u + v * v; if (d >= 1) continue;\\n      const i = py * W + px, top = base + hgt * Math.sqrt(1 - d); if (add) { h[i] += hgt * (1 - d); m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = Math.max(pulse[i], o.pulse * (1 - d)); } else if (top > h[i]) { h[i] = top; m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = o.pulse * (1 - d); } } }\\n  tube(pts, r, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const step = Math.max(1, r * .35); for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / step | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.blob(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, r, 0, hgt, mat, o); } }\\n  finish(detail = 1.1) { const { W, H, h, ao, noise } = this, N = W * H, blur = new Float32Array(N), tmp = new Float32Array(N), R = 7;\\n    for (let i = 0, y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++, i++) h[i] += (noise.fbm(x * .11, y * .11, 3) - .5) * detail;\\n    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { let s = 0; for (let x = -R; x <= R; x++) s += h[y * W + Math.max(0, x)]; for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { tmp[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += h[y * W + Math.min(W - 1, x + R + 1)] - h[y * W + Math.max(0, x - R)]; } }\\n1130→    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { let s = 0; for (let y = -R; y <= R; y++) s += tmp[Math.max(0, y) * W + x]; for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { blur[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += tmp[Math.min(H - 1, y + R + 1) * W + x] - tmp[Math.max(0, y - R) * W + x]; } }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) ao[i] = Math.max(.42, Math.min(1.08, 1 - (blur[i] - h[i]) * .055)); }\\n  // what the sim's objects stamp each frame, before shade(): dynamic height, and an override material\\n  stampDisc(x, y, r, hgt, mat) { const { W, H, dyn, over } = this, id = mat ? matId(mat) + 1 : 0; for (let py = Math.max(1, y - r | 0); py < Math.min(H - 1, y + r + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(1, x - r | 0); px < Math.min(W - 1, x + r + 1); px++) { const d = ((px - x) ** 2 + (py - y) ** 2) / (r * r); if (d < 1) { const i = py * W + px; dyn[i] = hgt < 0 ? Math.min(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)) : Math.max(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)); if (id) over[i] = id; } } }\\n  stampLine(pts, r, hgt, mat) { for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / Math.max(1, r * .5) | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.stampDisc(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, hgt, mat); } }\\n  // fx: { beat 0..1, breath px, slow: Long Breath palette, lens: {x, y, r} shows the cold palette inside (Sonar), light: [lx, ly], dim: 0..1 darkness, spot: {x, y, r} stays lit while dim }\\n  shade(fx = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, ao, pulse, dyn, over, u } = this, beat = fx.beat || 0, off = Math.round(fx.breath || 0) * W, slow = !!fx.slow, lens = fx.lens, lr2 = lens ? lens.r * lens.r : 0, dim = fx.dim || 0, spot = fx.spot, sr2 = spot ? spot.r * spot.r : 0, lx = fx.light ? fx.light[0] : -.42, ly = fx.light ? fx.light[1] : -.52, lz = Math.sqrt(Math.max(.1, 1 - lx * lx - ly * ly)), hl = Math.hypot(lx, ly, lz + 1), hx = lx / hl, hy = ly / hl, hz = (lz + 1) / hl;\\n    for (let y = 1; y < H - 1; y++) for (let x = 1, i = y * W + 1; x < W - 1; x++, i++) {\\n      const j = Math.max(W + 1, Math.min(W * H - W - 2, i + off)), k = 1 + beat * pulse[j], dx = (h[j - 1] - h[j + 1]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - 1] - dyn[i + 1]) * .5, dy = (h[j - W] - h[j + W]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - W] - dyn[i + W]) * .5, nl = 1 / Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + 1), nx = dx * nl, ny = dy * nl, nz = nl;\\n      const diff = Math.max(0, nx * lx + ny * ly + nz * lz), sh = Math.max(0, nx * hx + ny * hy + nz * hz), ov = over[i], M = MATS[ov ? ov - 1 : m[j]], cold = slow || (lens && (x - lens.x) ** 2 + (y - lens.y) ** 2 < lr2), r = cold ? M.slow : M.ramp, n = r.length, s2 = sh * sh, s4 = s2 * s2, s8 = s4 * s4, s16 = s8 * s8, s32 = s16 * s16;\\n1140→      const lit = dim && !(spot && (x - spot.x) ** 2 + (y - spot.y) ** 2 < sr2) ? 1 - dim : 1, lum = (diff * .92 + s8 * .16 * M.spec + beat * pulse[j] * .6) * (ov ? 1 : ao[j]) * lit, c = Math.max(0, Math.min(n - 1, (lum * (n - 1) + BAYER[(x & 3) | ((y & 3) << 2)] * 1.15 + .5) | 0));\\n      u[i] = s32 * s8 * M.spec * lit > .42 ? (cold ? 0xffffffe0 : 0xfff4f0ff) : r[c]; }\\n    this.g.putImageData(this.img, 0, 0); dyn.fill(0); over.fill(0); }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix B: a site recipe\\n\\n`F.stampDisc` coordinates here use screen pixels. To place sim objects, add `OX, OY`.\\n\\n1150→```js\\n// A site recipe: the abdomen. Design space is 426 x 240 about the screen's centre; a bigger screen only shows more drape.\\nfunction bakeAbdomen(W, H, seed = 11) { const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), cx = W / 2, cy = H / 2 - 4, n = F.noise, rx = 171, ry = 91;\\n  for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { const i = y * W + x, d = ((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2, fold = Math.sin(x * .09 + 1.6 * Math.sin(y * .05)) * 1.6 + Math.sin(y * .17 + x * .03) * .8;\\n    if (d < 1) { F.h[i] = -16 + 12 * d * d + Math.sin(x * .05 + y * .03) * 1.4; F.m[i] = matId('wall'); }            // the cavity\\n    else if (d < 1.28) { const e = (d - 1) / .28; F.h[i] = 4 + 7 * Math.sin(e * Math.PI); F.m[i] = matId('skin'); }  // lips of skin\\n    else { F.h[i] = 6 + fold; F.m[i] = matId('drape'); } }                                                            // drapes to any screen's edge\\n  F.blob(cx - rx * .55, cy - ry * .5, rx * .55, ry * .55, -.3, 17, 'liver', { base: -11, warp: 12 });\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) { const a = n.R() * 6.28, r = .55 + n.R() * .32; F.blob(cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * r, cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * r, 9 + n.R() * 14, 7 + n.R() * 9, n.R() * 3, 8, 'fat', { base: -10, warp: 8 }); }\\n  const coil = (x0, y0, len, dir, r) => { const pts = [[x0, y0]]; let a = dir, x = x0, y = y0; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * 1.5 + Math.sin(i * .9) * .5; x += Math.cos(a) * r * 1.3; y += Math.sin(a) * r * 1.3; if (((x - cx) / (rx * .92)) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / (ry * .92)) ** 2 > 1) { a += 2.4; x += Math.cos(a) * r; y += Math.sin(a) * r; } pts.push([x, y]); } return pts; };\\n1160→  F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .05, cy - ry * .25, 34, .2, 9), 11, 14, 'bowel', { base: -8 }); F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .45, cy + ry * .25, 26, 2.6, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -7 }); F.tube(coil(cx - rx * .35, cy + ry * .45, 22, -.3, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -6 });\\n  const veins = (x, y, a, len, r, mat) => { const pts = [[x, y]]; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * .8; x += Math.cos(a) * 7; y += Math.sin(a) * 7; if (((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2 > .96) break; pts.push([x, y]); if (r > 1.2 && n.R() < .22) veins(x, y, a + (n.R() < .5 ? .9 : -.9), len * .5 | 0, r * .7, mat); } F.tube(pts, r, 1.6, mat, { add: true, pulse: mat === 'artery' ? .35 : 0 }); };\\n  veins(cx - rx * .7, cy - ry * .05, -.2, 16, 2.2, 'vessel'); veins(cx + rx * .7, cy - ry * .6, 2.4, 14, 2, 'artery'); veins(cx + rx * .1, cy + ry * .75, -1.5, 12, 1.8, 'vessel');\\n  for (const a of [-.45, .5, 2.7, 3.6]) { const ex = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.02, ey = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.02, ox = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.5, oy = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.5; F.tube([[ex, ey], [ox, oy]], 4, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); F.tube([[ex - Math.sin(a) * 9, ey + Math.cos(a) * 9], [ex + Math.sin(a) * 9, ey - Math.cos(a) * 9]], 3, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); } // retractors\\n  F.finish(1.1); return F; }\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix C: portrait painter\\n\\nBusts for the four leads. The other four follow the same shape: `frontHair`, `backHair` (polygons in face space, x from the center, y down), `glasses`, `moustache`, `scar`, `cap`, `mask` (`maskUp: true` covers the mouth, for theatre), `lines`, `blush`, `jaw`, `wide`. Cache each expression to a canvas with `E.mkCanvas(112, 128)`; call `E.px.reset` on the target after drawing on it with the canvas API.\\n1170→\\n```js\\n// A bust from data in hard-edged tones, 112 x 128 buffer pixels. Cache each expression in a canvas; the sim never reads it. Needs E = My3D2dge in scope.\\n// o: { expr: neutral | smile | angry | sad | shock | shout, blink: 0..1, talk: 0..1, look: -1..1 }\\nfunction drawBust(g, c, o = {}) { const px = E.px, P = (pts, col) => px.poly(g, pts, col), T = E.tones;\\n  const skin = T(c.skin), hair = T(c.hair), cloth = T(c.cloth), expr = o.expr || 'neutral', blink = o.blink || 0, talk = o.talk || 0, cx = 56, top = 20;\\n  const jaw = c.jaw || 1, wide = c.wide || 1, f = (x, y) => [cx + x * wide, top + y]; // face space: x from centre, y down\\n  // back hair\\n  if (c.backHair) for (const s of c.backHair) P(s.map(([x, y]) => f(x, y)), hair.sh);\\n  // shoulders and collar\\n1180→  P([[6, 128], [10, 104], [30, 92], [46, 88], [66, 88], [82, 92], [102, 104], [106, 128]], cloth.base);\\n  P([[6, 128], [10, 104], [30, 92], [34, 128]], cloth.sh); P([[78, 128], [82, 92], [102, 104], [106, 128]], cloth.lt);\\n  // neck\\n  P([[46, 66], [66, 66], [68, 92], [56, 104], [44, 92]], skin.sh);\\n  // V-neck and inner shirt\\n  P([[42, 88], [56, 110], [70, 88], [66, 86], [56, 100], [46, 86]], cloth.deep); P([[46, 86], [56, 100], [66, 86], [64, 92], [56, 104], [48, 92]], c.undershirt || skin.sh);\\n  if (c.coat) { P([[6, 128], [10, 104], [30, 92], [42, 88], [52, 128]], c.coat); P([[106, 128], [102, 104], [82, 92], [70, 88], [60, 128]], c.coat); P([[42, 88], [52, 128], [47, 128], [36, 92]], E.tones(c.coat).sh); P([[70, 88], [60, 128], [65, 128], [76, 92]], E.tones(c.coat).sh); }\\n  // ears\\n  P([f(-27, 30), f(-31, 34), f(-30, 42), f(-26, 45)], skin.sh); P([f(27, 30), f(31, 34), f(30, 42), f(26, 45)], skin.base);\\n  // head: wide cranium, cheek, chin\\n1190→  const J = jaw; P([f(-26, 12), f(-27, 34), f(-22, 48 * J), f(-11, 60 * J), f(0, 64 * J), f(11, 60 * J), f(22, 48 * J), f(27, 34), f(26, 12), f(14, 2), f(-14, 2)], skin.base);\\n  P([f(-27, 30), f(-22, 48 * J), f(-11, 60 * J), f(0, 64 * J), f(-6, 54 * J), f(-16, 44), f(-22, 30)], skin.sh); // cheek shadow, viewer's left\\n  if (c.blush) { px.ell(g, ...f(-15, 41), 4, 2, c.blush); px.ell(g, ...f(16, 41), 4, 2, c.blush); }\\n  if (c.lines) { px.line(g, ...f(-11, 45), ...f(-6, 50), skin.sh, 1); px.line(g, ...f(11, 45), ...f(6, 50), skin.sh, 1); px.line(g, ...f(-23, 26), ...f(-20, 28), skin.sh, 1); px.line(g, ...f(23, 26), ...f(20, 28), skin.sh, 1); }\\n  // eyes\\n  const eye = (sx) => { const x = sx * 13, y = 30 + (expr === 'shock' ? -1 : 0), w = 7, hh = expr === 'shock' ? 8 : expr === 'angry' ? 5 : 7;\\n    if (blink > .5 || expr === 'sad-closed') { px.line(g, ...f(x - w, y + 1), ...f(x + w, y + 1), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); return; }\\n    P([f(x - w, y), f(x - w + 3, y - hh + 2), f(x + w - 3, y - hh + 2), f(x + w, y), f(x + w - 2, y + 4), f(x - w + 2, y + 4)], '#f8f4ee');\\n    const ix = x + (o.look || 0) * 2 + (expr === 'shock' ? 0 : 0); px.ell(g, ...f(ix, y - 1), 4, expr === 'shock' ? 4 : 5, c.iris || '#3a5a7a'); px.ell(g, ...f(ix, y), 2, 3, c.pupil || '#120c14'); px.rect(g, ...f(ix - 3, y - 4), 3, 2, '#ffffff'); px.dot(g, ...f(ix + 2, y + 2), '#ffffff');\\n    px.line(g, ...f(x - w - 1, y + (sx < 0 ? 1 : -1)), ...f(x - w + 4, y - hh + 2), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); px.line(g, ...f(x - w + 4, y - hh + 2), ...f(x + w - 4, y - hh + 2), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); px.line(g, ...f(x + w - 4, y - hh + 2), ...f(x + w + 1, y + (sx < 0 ? -1 : 1)), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); };\\n1200→  eye(-1); eye(1);\\n  // brows\\n  const by = 17 + (c.browDrop || 0), br = expr === 'angry' ? 3 : expr === 'sad' ? -3 : expr === 'shock' ? -1 : 0, bc = c.brow || hair.deep, bw = c.browW || 2; px.line(g, ...f(-20, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) - br), ...f(-7, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) + br), bc, bw); px.line(g, ...f(7, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) + br), ...f(20, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) - br), bc, bw);\\n  // nose\\n  px.line(g, ...f(1, 40), ...f(-1, 45), skin.sh, 1); px.dot(g, ...f(0, 46), skin.deep);\\n  // mouth\\n  const my = 53, mo = talk > .5 || expr === 'shout' || expr === 'shock'; if (mo) { const a = expr === 'shout' || expr === 'shock' ? 7 : 4, w = expr === 'shout' ? 7 : 5; P([f(-w, my - 1), f(w, my - 1), f(w - 2, my + a), f(-w + 2, my + a)], '#5a1a24'); P([f(-w + 2, my + a - 2), f(w - 2, my + a - 2), f(w - 3, my + a), f(-w + 3, my + a)], '#c8505a'); if (a > 4) px.rect(g, ...f(-w + 1, my - 1), (w - 1) * 2, 2, '#f4f0e8'); }\\n  else if (expr === 'smile') { px.line(g, ...f(-7, my - 1), ...f(-3, my + 2), skin.deep, 1); px.line(g, ...f(-3, my + 2), ...f(3, my + 2), skin.deep, 1); px.line(g, ...f(3, my + 2), ...f(7, my - 1), skin.deep, 1); }\\n  else if (expr === 'sad' || expr === 'angry') { px.line(g, ...f(-5, my + 2), ...f(0, my), skin.deep, 1); px.line(g, ...f(0, my), ...f(5, my + 2), skin.deep, 1); }\\n  else px.line(g, ...f(-4, my), ...f(4, my), skin.deep, 1);\\n1210→  if (c.moustache) { P([f(-13, 50), f(-6, 46), f(0, 48), f(6, 46), f(13, 50), f(8, 52), f(0, 50), f(-8, 52)], c.moustache); px.line(g, ...f(-6, 47), ...f(6, 47), E.tones(c.moustache).lt, 1); }\\n  // front hair\\n  if (c.frontHair) for (const [s, tone] of c.frontHair) P(s.map(([x, y]) => f(x, y)), hair[tone || 'base']);\\n  if (c.hairGlint) for (const s of c.hairGlint) P(s.map(([x, y]) => f(x, y)), hair.hi);\\n  // cap\\n  if (c.cap) { const k = T(c.cap); P([f(-29, 16), f(-27, 2), f(-14, -9), f(14, -9), f(27, 2), f(29, 16), f(16, 11), f(-16, 11)], k.base); P([f(-29, 16), f(-27, 2), f(-14, -9), f(-6, -9), f(-14, 11), f(-16, 11)], k.sh); P([f(6, -8), f(14, -9), f(22, -3), f(14, -3)], k.lt); P([f(-29, 16), f(-16, 11), f(16, 11), f(29, 16), f(27, 18), f(16, 14), f(-16, 14), f(-27, 18)], k.deep); }\\n  // lowered mask, glasses\\n  if (c.mask && !o.maskUp) { const k = T(c.mask); P([f(-20, 62), f(20, 62), f(25, 76), f(0, 84), f(-25, 76)], k.base); P([f(-20, 62), f(-25, 76), f(0, 84), f(-6, 74)], k.sh); px.line(g, ...f(-20, 62), ...f(-28, 50), k.lt, 1); px.line(g, ...f(20, 62), ...f(28, 50), k.lt, 1); }\\n  if (c.glasses) { const m = c.glasses; for (const sx of [-1, 1]) { const x = sx * 13; px.line(g, ...f(x - 9, 25), ...f(x + 9, 25), m, 1); px.line(g, ...f(x - 9, 25), ...f(x - 8, 33), m, 1); px.line(g, ...f(x + 9, 25), ...f(x + 8, 33), m, 1); px.line(g, ...f(x - 8, 34), ...f(x + 8, 34), m, 1); } px.line(g, ...f(-4, 27), ...f(4, 27), m, 1); }\\n  if (o.maskUp && c.mask) { const k = T(c.mask); P([f(-27, 36), f(-8, 34), f(0, 36), f(8, 34), f(27, 36), f(25, 54), f(11, 66), f(0, 68), f(-11, 66), f(-25, 54)], k.base); P([f(-27, 36), f(-8, 34), f(-3, 50), f(-11, 66), f(-25, 54)], k.sh); for (const yy of [44, 52]) px.line(g, ...f(-18, yy), ...f(18, yy), k.lt, 1); px.line(g, ...f(-27, 38), ...f(-31, 32), k.lt, 1); px.line(g, ...f(27, 38), ...f(31, 32), k.lt, 1); }\\n1220→  if (c.scar) px.line(g, ...f(c.scar[0], c.scar[1]), ...f(c.scar[2], c.scar[3]), skin.deep, 1);\\n  if (c.tag) { px.rect(g, 72, 108, 16, 10, '#f0ece2'); px.rect(g, 74, 110, 12, 2, c.tag); px.rect(g, 74, 114, 8, 1, '#7a7468'); }\\n}\\nconst CAST = {\\n  vale: { name: 'DR. VALE', skin: '#f6d0b2', hair: '#c9562a', iris: '#3f8a58', cloth: '#2f9c8e', cap: '#2bb0a2', mask: '#bfe6dc', undershirt: '#e9fff6', blush: '#f0a48c', wide: .95,\\n    backHair: [[[-27, 14], [-30, 40], [-24, 52], [-16, 40], [-16, 14]], [[27, 14], [30, 40], [24, 52], [16, 40], [16, 14]]],\\n    frontHair: [[[[-27, 12], [-24, 24], [-16, 16], [-10, 22], [-3, 14], [3, 21], [10, 14], [18, 22], [27, 12], [14, 8], [-14, 8]], 'base'], [[[-27, 12], [-24, 24], [-16, 16], [-14, 10]], 'sh']],\\n    tag: '#c8452f' },\\n  quill: { name: 'NURSE QUILL', skin: '#dcae8e', hair: '#8d8a88', iris: '#4a4a55', cloth: '#3d62a6', cap: '#35558f', undershirt: '#dfe6f2', moustache: '#a7a3a0', lines: true, wide: 1.08, jaw: 1.04, browW: 3, brow: '#7c7875', browDrop: 2, mask: '#a9cfe0', frontHair: [] },\\n  oyelaran: { name: 'CHIEF OYELARAN', skin: '#7c4a2e', hair: '#c9c5bb', iris: '#2a1a12', cloth: '#2e2c36', coat: '#ece7da', undershirt: '#3a3644', lines: true, jaw: .98, glasses: '#d8c070',\\n1230→    backHair: [], frontHair: [[[[-27, 18], [-27, 2], [-14, -8], [14, -8], [27, 2], [27, 18], [20, 10], [8, 6], [-8, 6], [-20, 10]], 'base'], [[[-27, 18], [-27, 2], [-14, -8], [-8, 6], [-20, 10]], 'sh'], [[[6, -7], [16, -6], [22, 0], [12, 0]], 'lt']] },\\n  sokolova: { name: 'DR. SOKOLOVA', skin: '#e8c6aa', hair: '#dedad2', iris: '#6a8aa8', cloth: '#6b7a48', undershirt: '#f0ece0', lines: true, wide: 1.02, jaw: 1.02, scar: [10, 14, 17, 40], browW: 3, brow: '#b8b4ac',\\n    backHair: [[[-28, 6], [-34, 34], [-30, 58], [-20, 50], [-20, 10]], [[28, 6], [36, 26], [46, 52], [38, 64], [28, 44], [22, 10]]], frontHair: [[[[-27, 16], [-26, 2], [-12, -8], [14, -8], [27, 2], [27, 16], [16, 6], [-2, 12], [-16, 8]], 'base'], [[[-27, 16], [-26, 2], [-12, -8], [-6, 8], [-16, 8]], 'sh']] },\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\\n\\n**Page head.** Order matters.\\n\\n1240→```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>…</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body><!-- E.bootSplash's markup here --><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>/* engine */</script><script>/* game */</script></body></html>\\n```\\n1250→\\n**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\\n\\n```js\\n// Hub skeleton: shared world on my-3D2dge. The host's copy runs the world; other copies mirror it and send their own hands.\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst game = window.G = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  input: { ...base, useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] }, menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\\n1260→const NAME = 'SKELETON', W0 = 426, H0 = 240, DOTS = 12;\\nlet info = null, phase = 'wait', card = null, over = false, sent = 0, heardSeq = 0, S = { v: 70, dots: [], p: {} }, mine = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0 }, rng = null;\\nconst place = () => ({ x: 40 + rng() * 340, y: 40 + rng() * 160 });\\nfunction hostInit() { rng = HUB.rng('deal'); S.dots = Array.from({ length: DOTS }, (_, id) => ({ id, ...place(), alive: 1 })); for (const q of info.players) S.p[q.id] = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0, score: 0, gone: false }; }\\nfunction finish(won) { if (over) return; over = true; if (HUB.server !== true && info.me != null && S.p[info.me]) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  const live = info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).sort((a, b) => S.p[b.id].score - S.p[a.id].score), standings = [];\\n  for (const q of live) { const last = standings[standings.length - 1]; if (last && S.p[last[0]].score === S.p[q.id].score) last.push(q.id); else standings.push([q.id]); }\\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(info.players.map(q => [q.id, S.p[q.id].score]));\\n  HUB.send({ t: 'over', v: S.v }); HUB.finish({ standings, scores, won, awards: live.length ? [{ id: live[0].id, title: 'Steadiest Hand', detail: scores[live[0].id] + ' clean actions' }] : [] }); }\\nasync function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n1270→  if (!info) { phase = 'solo'; return; }\\n  HUB.on('card', c => { card = c; });\\n  HUB.on('start', () => { phase = 'count'; });\\n  HUB.on('message', (d, from) => { if (info.isHost) { const p = S.p[from]; if (d.t === 'i' && p && d.n > (p.n || 0)) { p.n = d.n; p.x = d.x; p.y = d.y; p.t = d.t2; } } else if (from === info.host) { if (d.t === 's' && d.n > heardSeq) { heardSeq = d.n; S.v = d.v; S.dots = d.o.map(([id, x, y]) => ({ id, x, y, alive: 1 })); for (const [id, x, y, t, sc] of d.p) { const q = S.p[id] || (S.p[id] = {}); if (id !== info.me) { q.x = x; q.y = y; q.t = t; } q.score = sc; } } if (d.t === 'over') over = true; } });\\n  HUB.on('leave', ({ id }) => { if (S.p[id]) S.p[id].gone = true; });\\n  HUB.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) finish(false); });\\n  HUB.on('end', () => { phase = 'over'; game.audio.music(null); game.audio.mute(true); });\\n  if (info.isHost) hostInit();\\n  HUB.ready(); }\\nfunction step(dt) { const I = game.input, m = I.move(), a = I.padAim, ptr = I.pointer(); let dx = (a ? a[0] : 0) + m[0], dy = (a ? a[1] : 0) + m[1]; mine.x = E.clamp(mine.x + dx * 300 * dt, 0, W0); mine.y = E.clamp(mine.y + dy * 300 * dt, 0, H0); if (ptr && I.lastDevice === 'mouse') { mine.x = ptr[0]; mine.y = ptr[1]; } mine.t = I.value('useTool'); }\\n1280→let snapN = 0, inN = 0, acc = 0;\\nfunction hostStep(dt) { S.v = Math.max(0, S.v - .05 * dt); if (info.me != null && S.p[info.me] && !info.server) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  for (const id in S.p) { const p = S.p[id]; if (p.gone || !p.t) continue; for (const d of S.dots) if (d.alive && Math.hypot(d.x - p.x, d.y - p.y) < 12) { d.alive = 0; p.score++; } } S.dots = S.dots.filter(d => d.alive); if (!S.dots.length) finish(true); }\\ngame.start({ scene: 'hub', scenes: { hub: { pausable: true, camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false },\\n  update(dt) { const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n    if (!info && !inSession) return;\\n    if (phase === 'wait' && info) { if (I.pressed('confirm')) HUB.answer('ready'); if (I.pressed('more')) HUB.answer('more'); const c = I.clicked(); if (c) HUB.answer(c[1] > game.H * .7 ? 'more' : 'ready'); }\\n    if (phase === 'count' && HUB.time() >= 0) phase = 'play';\\n    if (phase === 'play' && !over) { step(dt); if (info.isHost) hostStep(dt); acc += dt; if (acc >= 1 / 12) { acc = 0; if (info.isHost) HUB.send({ t: 's', n: ++snapN, v: Math.round(S.v), o: S.dots.map(d => [d.id, d.x | 0, d.y | 0]), p: info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).map(q => { const p = S.p[q.id]; return [q.id, p.x | 0, p.y | 0, p.t > .25 ? 1 : 0, p.score | 0]; }) }, { reliable: false }); else HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++inN, x: mine.x | 0, y: mine.y | 0, t2: mine.t > .25 ? 1 : 0 }, { to: info.host, reliable: false }); } } },\\n  draw(r) { if (info && info.server) return; r.sky(['#143a36', '#14504a']); r.overlay(g => { E.font.text(g, NAME + ' ' + phase + (card && card.left != null ? ' ' + Math.ceil(card.left / 1000) : ''), 8, 8, '#fff', { outline: false }); for (const d of S.dots) px.disc(g, d.x, d.y, 4, '#5ff0e0'); if (info) for (const q of info.players) { const p = q.id === info.me ? mine : S.p[q.id]; if (p && !(S.p[q.id] || {}).gone) { px.disc(g, p.x, p.y, 5, q.color); E.font.text(g, q.name.slice(0, 12), p.x + 7, p.y - 4, q.color, { outline: false }); } } }); } } } });\\n1290→window.__hubProbe = () => ({ phase, over, dots: S.dots.length, v: S.v, t: HUB.active ? HUB.time() : 0 });\\nconnect();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n**Harness runner.** The folder needs the game (as `game.html`) and copies of `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. It uses an OS-picked port, checks the frame's title is your game (replace the print with a test), and stops only its own server, by handle.\\n\\n```python\\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n1300→folder = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1])\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=folder, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True)\\ntry:\\n    line = srv.stdout.readline(); port = int(re.search(r'port (\\\\d+)', line).group(1))\\n    base = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/'\\n    RUNS = ['players=2&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1', 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1']\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        b = p.chromium.launch(args=['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\\n        for q in RUNS:\\n            pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); pg.goto(base + 'harness.html?game=game.html&' + q)\\n1310→            try: pg.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=90000)\\n            except Exception as e: print('TIMEOUT', q)\\n            r = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const h = window.__hubCheck; return h ? { pass: h.pass, failed: h.checks.filter(c => !c.pass).map(c => c.name + ': ' + c.detail), n: h.checks.length } : null }\\\")\\n            title = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const f = document.querySelector('iframe'); try { return f && f.contentDocument && f.contentDocument.title } catch (e) { return 'x' } }\\\")\\n            print(q, json.dumps(r)[:700], 'title:', title); pg.close()\\n        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\\n        b.close()\\nfinally:\\n    srv.terminate(); srv.wait(timeout=5)\\n```\\n1320→\\n## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\\n\\n**A DualSense in the standard mapping, for Playwright's `add_init_script`.** Set `__pad.axes[0..3]` (left x, left y, right x, right y), `__pad.buttons[i].value` and `.pressed`: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 12 to 15 D-pad, and bump `__pad.timestamp`.\\n\\n```js\\n(() => { const axes = [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons = Array.from({ length: 18 }, () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\\n  const pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes, buttons,\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); }, reset() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); } } };\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n1330→```\\n\\n**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\\n\\n```js\\nd.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:48px 24px 24px;text-align:center;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(5,3,12,.92) 45%);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\\n// and on the button, add pointer-events:auto to its inline style\\n```\\n\\nNote it in your Engine Feedback.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1090→## Appendix A: tissue painter\\n\\nRan on this computer at 480x270, 3 to 5 ms a frame under software rendering. It also runs headless. One instance per site. Each frame: stamp pools, wounds and so on from `S`, then `shade(fx)`, then draw `F.cv`.\\n\\n- `stampDisc(x, y, r, height, mat)`, `stampLine(points, r, height, mat)`: per-frame height and material. Height alone (no `mat`) makes a ridge, for Legato.\\n- `shade({ beat, breath, slow, lens, light, dim, spot })`: see its comment. `dyn` and `over` clear after each shade.\\n- `slow: true` is Long Breath's palette. `lens` is Sonar's. `dim` and `spot` are the blackout. A moving `light` is the swaying lamp.\\n\\n```js\\n// Bake once per site, stamp from the sim's state each frame, then shade(). Cosmetic only: the sim never reads it. Needs E = My3D2dge in scope.\\n1100→const BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5].map(v => (v + .5) / 16 - .5);\\nconst hex3 = h => [parseInt(h.slice(1, 3), 16), parseInt(h.slice(3, 5), 16), parseInt(h.slice(5, 7), 16)];\\nfunction makeRamp(keys, n, slow) { // dark to light through hand-picked, hue-shifted keys. slow: the same ramp seen through Long Breath\\n  const c = keys.map(hex3), out = new Uint32Array(n);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const t = i / (n - 1) * (c.length - 1), j = Math.min(c.length - 2, t | 0), f = t - j; let r = c[j][0] + (c[j + 1][0] - c[j][0]) * f, g = c[j][1] + (c[j + 1][1] - c[j][1]) * f, b = c[j][2] + (c[j + 1][2] - c[j][2]) * f;\\n    if (slow) { const y = r * .3 + g * .59 + b * .11; r = y * .55 + 8; g = y * .95 + 14; b = y * 1.05 + 22; } out[i] = 0xff000000 | (Math.min(255, b) << 16) | (Math.min(255, g) << 8) | Math.min(255, r); }\\n  return out;\\n}\\nconst MAT_KEYS = { // name: [ramp keys, specular strength]\\n  wall: [['#1c060c', '#4a0f18', '#7d1f26', '#a93a38'], .35], bowel: [['#3a0e1c', '#8a2f3e', '#c75f62', '#eb9486', '#ffc9b0'], 1], liver: [['#1e0610', '#4e1022', '#7c1e30', '#a83a42', '#d0645c'], .55],\\n1110→  fat: [['#5a3a10', '#a8782a', '#dcb34c', '#f4d97e', '#fff2b8'], .7], vessel: [['#14103a', '#2c2a70', '#4a4aa0', '#7c78c8'], .8], artery: [['#3a0408', '#8c0f14', '#cf2a22', '#f4604a'], 1],\\n  skin: [['#6a3a22', '#a8683f', '#d39a68', '#eebf92'], .12], drape: [['#0c2c2a', '#14504a', '#1f7468', '#2f9a88'], 0], steel: [['#28303a', '#5a6a78', '#9aaab8', '#e8f0f8'], 1.6],\\n  blood: [['#180204', '#3c060a', '#680c10', '#8e1414'], 1.4], wound: [['#0c0104', '#2a0408', '#55090e', '#7a1216'], .5], char: [['#08070a', '#1c181a', '#332a28', '#4a3c34'], 0], gel: [['#0c4a38', '#1c8a64', '#54d0a0', '#b0ffe0'], 1.4] };\\nconst MAT_IDS = Object.keys(MAT_KEYS), MATS = MAT_IDS.map(k => ({ ramp: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20), slow: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20, true), spec: MAT_KEYS[k][1] }));\\nconst matId = n => MAT_IDS.indexOf(n);\\nfunction makeNoise(seed) { let a = seed >>> 0; const R = () => { a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0; let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), a | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };\\n  const L = new Float32Array(65536); for (let i = 0; i < L.length; i++) L[i] = R();\\n  const v = (x, y) => { const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), fx = x - xi, fy = y - yi, u = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), w = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy), s = (p, q) => L[(p & 255) | ((q & 255) << 8)]; return (s(xi, yi) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi) * u) * (1 - w) + (s(xi, yi + 1) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi + 1) * u) * w; };\\n  return { R, fbm: (x, y, o = 4) => { let k = .5, f = 1, n = 0; for (let i = 0; i < o; i++) { n += k * v(x * f, y * f); k *= .5; f *= 2.03; } return n; } }; }\\nclass TissueField {\\n1120→  constructor(W, H, seed = 7) { this.W = W; this.H = H; const N = W * H; this.h = new Float32Array(N); this.m = new Uint8Array(N); this.pulse = new Float32Array(N); this.ao = new Float32Array(N).fill(1); this.dyn = new Float32Array(N); this.over = new Uint8Array(N); this.noise = makeNoise(seed);\\n    this.cv = E.mkCanvas(W, H); this.g = this.cv.getContext('2d'); this.img = this.g.createImageData(W, H); this.u = new Uint32Array(this.img.data.buffer); }\\n  blob(x, y, rx, ry, rot, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, pulse, noise } = this, c = Math.cos(rot), s = Math.sin(rot), R = Math.max(rx, ry) + (o.warp || 0) + 2, id = matId(mat), warp = o.warp || 0, base = o.base || 0, add = !!o.add;\\n    for (let py = Math.max(0, y - R | 0); py < Math.min(H, y + R + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(0, x - R | 0); px < Math.min(W, x + R + 1); px++) {\\n      const wx = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, wy = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03 + 40, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, dx = px - x + wx, dy = py - y + wy, u = (dx * c + dy * s) / rx, v = (-dx * s + dy * c) / ry, d = u * u + v * v; if (d >= 1) continue;\\n      const i = py * W + px, top = base + hgt * Math.sqrt(1 - d); if (add) { h[i] += hgt * (1 - d); m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = Math.max(pulse[i], o.pulse * (1 - d)); } else if (top > h[i]) { h[i] = top; m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = o.pulse * (1 - d); } } }\\n  tube(pts, r, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const step = Math.max(1, r * .35); for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / step | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.blob(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, r, 0, hgt, mat, o); } }\\n  finish(detail = 1.1) { const { W, H, h, ao, noise } = this, N = W * H, blur = new Float32Array(N), tmp = new Float32Array(N), R = 7;\\n    for (let i = 0, y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++, i++) h[i] += (noise.fbm(x * .11, y * .11, 3) - .5) * detail;\\n    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { let s = 0; for (let x = -R; x <= R; x++) s += h[y * W + Math.max(0, x)]; for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { tmp[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += h[y * W + Math.min(W - 1, x + R + 1)] - h[y * W + Math.max(0, x - R)]; } }\\n1130→    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { let s = 0; for (let y = -R; y <= R; y++) s += tmp[Math.max(0, y) * W + x]; for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { blur[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += tmp[Math.min(H - 1, y + R + 1) * W + x] - tmp[Math.max(0, y - R) * W + x]; } }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) ao[i] = Math.max(.42, Math.min(1.08, 1 - (blur[i] - h[i]) * .055)); }\\n  // what the sim's objects stamp each frame, before shade(): dynamic height, and an override material\\n  stampDisc(x, y, r, hgt, mat) { const { W, H, dyn, over } = this, id = mat ? matId(mat) + 1 : 0; for (let py = Math.max(1, y - r | 0); py < Math.min(H - 1, y + r + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(1, x - r | 0); px < Math.min(W - 1, x + r + 1); px++) { const d = ((px - x) ** 2 + (py - y) ** 2) / (r * r); if (d < 1) { const i = py * W + px; dyn[i] = hgt < 0 ? Math.min(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)) : Math.max(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)); if (id) over[i] = id; } } }\\n  stampLine(pts, r, hgt, mat) { for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / Math.max(1, r * .5) | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.stampDisc(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, hgt, mat); } }\\n  // fx: { beat 0..1, breath px, slow: Long Breath palette, lens: {x, y, r} shows the cold palette inside (Sonar), light: [lx, ly], dim: 0..1 darkness, spot: {x, y, r} stays lit while dim }\\n  shade(fx = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, ao, pulse, dyn, over, u } = this, beat = fx.beat || 0, off = Math.round(fx.breath || 0) * W, slow = !!fx.slow, lens = fx.lens, lr2 = lens ? lens.r * lens.r : 0, dim = fx.dim || 0, spot = fx.spot, sr2 = spot ? spot.r * spot.r : 0, lx = fx.light ? fx.light[0] : -.42, ly = fx.light ? fx.light[1] : -.52, lz = Math.sqrt(Math.max(.1, 1 - lx * lx - ly * ly)), hl = Math.hypot(lx, ly, lz + 1), hx = lx / hl, hy = ly / hl, hz = (lz + 1) / hl;\\n    for (let y = 1; y < H - 1; y++) for (let x = 1, i = y * W + 1; x < W - 1; x++, i++) {\\n      const j = Math.max(W + 1, Math.min(W * H - W - 2, i + off)), k = 1 + beat * pulse[j], dx = (h[j - 1] - h[j + 1]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - 1] - dyn[i + 1]) * .5, dy = (h[j - W] - h[j + W]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - W] - dyn[i + W]) * .5, nl = 1 / Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + 1), nx = dx * nl, ny = dy * nl, nz = nl;\\n      const diff = Math.max(0, nx * lx + ny * ly + nz * lz), sh = Math.max(0, nx * hx + ny * hy + nz * hz), ov = over[i], M = MATS[ov ? ov - 1 : m[j]], cold = slow || (lens && (x - lens.x) ** 2 + (y - lens.y) ** 2 < lr2), r = cold ? M.slow : M.ramp, n = r.length, s2 = sh * sh, s4 = s2 * s2, s8 = s4 * s4, s16 = s8 * s8, s32 = s16 * s16;\\n1140→      const lit = dim && !(spot && (x - spot.x) ** 2 + (y - spot.y) ** 2 < sr2) ? 1 - dim : 1, lum = (diff * .92 + s8 * .16 * M.spec + beat * pulse[j] * .6) * (ov ? 1 : ao[j]) * lit, c = Math.max(0, Math.min(n - 1, (lum * (n - 1) + BAYER[(x & 3) | ((y & 3) << 2)] * 1.15 + .5) | 0));\\n      u[i] = s32 * s8 * M.spec * lit > .42 ? (cold ? 0xffffffe0 : 0xfff4f0ff) : r[c]; }\\n    this.g.putImageData(this.img, 0, 0); dyn.fill(0); over.fill(0); }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix B: a site recipe\\n\\n`F.stampDisc` coordinates here use screen pixels. To place sim objects, add `OX, OY`.\\n\\n1150→```js\\n// A site recipe: the abdomen. Design space is 426 x 240 about the screen's centre; a bigger screen only shows more drape.\\nfunction bakeAbdomen(W, H, seed = 11) { const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), cx = W / 2, cy = H / 2 - 4, n = F.noise, rx = 171, ry = 91;\\n  for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { const i = y * W + x, d = ((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2, fold = Math.sin(x * .09 + 1.6 * Math.sin(y * .05)) * 1.6 + Math.sin(y * .17 + x * .03) * .8;\\n    if (d < 1) { F.h[i] = -16 + 12 * d * d + Math.sin(x * .05 + y * .03) * 1.4; F.m[i] = matId('wall'); }            // the cavity\\n    else if (d < 1.28) { const e = (d - 1) / .28; F.h[i] = 4 + 7 * Math.sin(e * Math.PI); F.m[i] = matId('skin'); }  // lips of skin\\n    else { F.h[i] = 6 + fold; F.m[i] = matId('drape'); } }                                                            // drapes to any screen's edge\\n  F.blob(cx - rx * .55, cy - ry * .5, rx * .55, ry * .55, -.3, 17, 'liver', { base: -11, warp: 12 });\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) { const a = n.R() * 6.28, r = .55 + n.R() * .32; F.blob(cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * r, cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * r, 9 + n.R() * 14, 7 + n.R() * 9, n.R() * 3, 8, 'fat', { base: -10, warp: 8 }); }\\n  const coil = (x0, y0, len, dir, r) => { const pts = [[x0, y0]]; let a = dir, x = x0, y = y0; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * 1.5 + Math.sin(i * .9) * .5; x += Math.cos(a) * r * 1.3; y += Math.sin(a) * r * 1.3; if (((x - cx) / (rx * .92)) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / (ry * .92)) ** 2 > 1) { a += 2.4; x += Math.cos(a) * r; y += Math.sin(a) * r; } pts.push([x, y]); } return pts; };\\n1160→  F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .05, cy - ry * .25, 34, .2, 9), 11, 14, 'bowel', { base: -8 }); F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .45, cy + ry * .25, 26, 2.6, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -7 }); F.tube(coil(cx - rx * .35, cy + ry * .45, 22, -.3, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -6 });\\n  const veins = (x, y, a, len, r, mat) => { const pts = [[x, y]]; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * .8; x += Math.cos(a) * 7; y += Math.sin(a) * 7; if (((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2 > .96) break; pts.push([x, y]); if (r > 1.2 && n.R() < .22) veins(x, y, a + (n.R() < .5 ? .9 : -.9), len * .5 | 0, r * .7, mat); } F.tube(pts, r, 1.6, mat, { add: true, pulse: mat === 'artery' ? .35 : 0 }); };\\n  veins(cx - rx * .7, cy - ry * .05, -.2, 16, 2.2, 'vessel'); veins(cx + rx * .7, cy - ry * .6, 2.4, 14, 2, 'artery'); veins(cx + rx * .1, cy + ry * .75, -1.5, 12, 1.8, 'vessel');\\n  for (const a of [-.45, .5, 2.7, 3.6]) { const ex = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.02, ey = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.02, ox = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.5, oy = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.5; F.tube([[ex, ey], [ox, oy]], 4, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); F.tube([[ex - Math.sin(a) * 9, ey + Math.cos(a) * 9], [ex + Math.sin(a) * 9, ey - Math.cos(a) * 9]], 3, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); } // retractors\\n  F.finish(1.1); return F; }\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix C: portrait painter\\n\\nBusts for the four leads. The other four follow the same shape: `frontHair`, `backHair` (polygons in face space, x from the center, y down), `glasses`, `moustache`, `scar`, `cap`, `mask` (`maskUp: true` covers the mouth, for theatre), `lines`, `blush`, `jaw`, `wide`. Cache each expression to a canvas with `E.mkCanvas(112, 128)`; call `E.px.reset` on the target after drawing on it with the canvas API.\\n1170→\\n```js\\n// A bust from data in hard-edged tones, 112 x 128 buffer pixels. Cache each expression in a canvas; the sim never reads it. Needs E = My3D2dge in scope.\\n// o: { expr: neutral | smile | angry | sad | shock | shout, blink: 0..1, talk: 0..1, look: -1..1 }\\nfunction drawBust(g, c, o = {}) { const px = E.px, P = (pts, col) => px.poly(g, pts, col), T = E.tones;\\n  const skin = T(c.skin), hair = T(c.hair), cloth = T(c.cloth), expr = o.expr || 'neutral', blink = o.blink || 0, talk = o.talk || 0, cx = 56, top = 20;\\n  const jaw = c.jaw || 1, wide = c.wide || 1, f = (x, y) => [cx + x * wide, top + y]; // face space: x from centre, y down\\n  // back hair\\n  if (c.backHair) for (const s of c.backHair) P(s.map(([x, y]) => f(x, y)), hair.sh);\\n  // shoulders and collar\\n1180→  P([[6, 128], [10, 104], [30, 92], [46, 88], [66, 88], [82, 92], [102, 104], [106, 128]], cloth.base);\\n  P([[6, 128], [10, 104], [30, 92], [34, 128]], cloth.sh); P([[78, 128], [82, 92], [102, 104], [106, 128]], cloth.lt);\\n  // neck\\n  P([[46, 66], [66, 66], [68, 92], [56, 104], [44, 92]], skin.sh);\\n  // V-neck and inner shirt\\n  P([[42, 88], [56, 110], [70, 88], [66, 86], [56, 100], [46, 86]], cloth.deep); P([[46, 86], [56, 100], [66, 86], [64, 92], [56, 104], [48, 92]], c.undershirt || skin.sh);\\n  if (c.coat) { P([[6, 128], [10, 104], [30, 92], [42, 88], [52, 128]], c.coat); P([[106, 128], [102, 104], [82, 92], [70, 88], [60, 128]], c.coat); P([[42, 88], [52, 128], [47, 128], [36, 92]], E.tones(c.coat).sh); P([[70, 88], [60, 128], [65, 128], [76, 92]], E.tones(c.coat).sh); }\\n  // ears\\n  P([f(-27, 30), f(-31, 34), f(-30, 42), f(-26, 45)], skin.sh); P([f(27, 30), f(31, 34), f(30, 42), f(26, 45)], skin.base);\\n  // head: wide cranium, cheek, chin\\n1190→  const J = jaw; P([f(-26, 12), f(-27, 34), f(-22, 48 * J), f(-11, 60 * J), f(0, 64 * J), f(11, 60 * J), f(22, 48 * J), f(27, 34), f(26, 12), f(14, 2), f(-14, 2)], skin.base);\\n  P([f(-27, 30), f(-22, 48 * J), f(-11, 60 * J), f(0, 64 * J), f(-6, 54 * J), f(-16, 44), f(-22, 30)], skin.sh); // cheek shadow, viewer's left\\n  if (c.blush) { px.ell(g, ...f(-15, 41), 4, 2, c.blush); px.ell(g, ...f(16, 41), 4, 2, c.blush); }\\n  if (c.lines) { px.line(g, ...f(-11, 45), ...f(-6, 50), skin.sh, 1); px.line(g, ...f(11, 45), ...f(6, 50), skin.sh, 1); px.line(g, ...f(-23, 26), ...f(-20, 28), skin.sh, 1); px.line(g, ...f(23, 26), ...f(20, 28), skin.sh, 1); }\\n  // eyes\\n  const eye = (sx) => { const x = sx * 13, y = 30 + (expr === 'shock' ? -1 : 0), w = 7, hh = expr === 'shock' ? 8 : expr === 'angry' ? 5 : 7;\\n    if (blink > .5 || expr === 'sad-closed') { px.line(g, ...f(x - w, y + 1), ...f(x + w, y + 1), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); return; }\\n    P([f(x - w, y), f(x - w + 3, y - hh + 2), f(x + w - 3, y - hh + 2), f(x + w, y), f(x + w - 2, y + 4), f(x - w + 2, y + 4)], '#f8f4ee');\\n    const ix = x + (o.look || 0) * 2 + (expr === 'shock' ? 0 : 0); px.ell(g, ...f(ix, y - 1), 4, expr === 'shock' ? 4 : 5, c.iris || '#3a5a7a'); px.ell(g, ...f(ix, y), 2, 3, c.pupil || '#120c14'); px.rect(g, ...f(ix - 3, y - 4), 3, 2, '#ffffff'); px.dot(g, ...f(ix + 2, y + 2), '#ffffff');\\n    px.line(g, ...f(x - w - 1, y + (sx < 0 ? 1 : -1)), ...f(x - w + 4, y - hh + 2), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); px.line(g, ...f(x - w + 4, y - hh + 2), ...f(x + w - 4, y - hh + 2), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); px.line(g, ...f(x + w - 4, y - hh + 2), ...f(x + w + 1, y + (sx < 0 ? -1 : 1)), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); };\\n1200→  eye(-1); eye(1);\\n  // brows\\n  const by = 17 + (c.browDrop || 0), br = expr === 'angry' ? 3 : expr === 'sad' ? -3 : expr === 'shock' ? -1 : 0, bc = c.brow || hair.deep, bw = c.browW || 2; px.line(g, ...f(-20, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) - br), ...f(-7, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) + br), bc, bw); px.line(g, ...f(7, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) + br), ...f(20, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) - br), bc, bw);\\n  // nose\\n  px.line(g, ...f(1, 40), ...f(-1, 45), skin.sh, 1); px.dot(g, ...f(0, 46), skin.deep);\\n  // mouth\\n  const my = 53, mo = talk > .5 || expr === 'shout' || expr === 'shock'; if (mo) { const a = expr === 'shout' || expr === 'shock' ? 7 : 4, w = expr === 'shout' ? 7 : 5; P([f(-w, my - 1), f(w, my - 1), f(w - 2, my + a), f(-w + 2, my + a)], '#5a1a24'); P([f(-w + 2, my + a - 2), f(w - 2, my + a - 2), f(w - 3, my + a), f(-w + 3, my + a)], '#c8505a'); if (a > 4) px.rect(g, ...f(-w + 1, my - 1), (w - 1) * 2, 2, '#f4f0e8'); }\\n  else if (expr === 'smile') { px.line(g, ...f(-7, my - 1), ...f(-3, my + 2), skin.deep, 1); px.line(g, ...f(-3, my + 2), ...f(3, my + 2), skin.deep, 1); px.line(g, ...f(3, my + 2), ...f(7, my - 1), skin.deep, 1); }\\n  else if (expr === 'sad' || expr === 'angry') { px.line(g, ...f(-5, my + 2), ...f(0, my), skin.deep, 1); px.line(g, ...f(0, my), ...f(5, my + 2), skin.deep, 1); }\\n  else px.line(g, ...f(-4, my), ...f(4, my), skin.deep, 1);\\n1210→  if (c.moustache) { P([f(-13, 50), f(-6, 46), f(0, 48), f(6, 46), f(13, 50), f(8, 52), f(0, 50), f(-8, 52)], c.moustache); px.line(g, ...f(-6, 47), ...f(6, 47), E.tones(c.moustache).lt, 1); }\\n  // front hair\\n  if (c.frontHair) for (const [s, tone] of c.frontHair) P(s.map(([x, y]) => f(x, y)), hair[tone || 'base']);\\n  if (c.hairGlint) for (const s of c.hairGlint) P(s.map(([x, y]) => f(x, y)), hair.hi);\\n  // cap\\n  if (c.cap) { const k = T(c.cap); P([f(-29, 16), f(-27, 2), f(-14, -9), f(14, -9), f(27, 2), f(29, 16), f(16, 11), f(-16, 11)], k.base); P([f(-29, 16), f(-27, 2), f(-14, -9), f(-6, -9), f(-14, 11), f(-16, 11)], k.sh); P([f(6, -8), f(14, -9), f(22, -3), f(14, -3)], k.lt); P([f(-29, 16), f(-16, 11), f(16, 11), f(29, 16), f(27, 18), f(16, 14), f(-16, 14), f(-27, 18)], k.deep); }\\n  // lowered mask, glasses\\n  if (c.mask && !o.maskUp) { const k = T(c.mask); P([f(-20, 62), f(20, 62), f(25, 76), f(0, 84), f(-25, 76)], k.base); P([f(-20, 62), f(-25, 76), f(0, 84), f(-6, 74)], k.sh); px.line(g, ...f(-20, 62), ...f(-28, 50), k.lt, 1); px.line(g, ...f(20, 62), ...f(28, 50), k.lt, 1); }\\n  if (c.glasses) { const m = c.glasses; for (const sx of [-1, 1]) { const x = sx * 13; px.line(g, ...f(x - 9, 25), ...f(x + 9, 25), m, 1); px.line(g, ...f(x - 9, 25), ...f(x - 8, 33), m, 1); px.line(g, ...f(x + 9, 25), ...f(x + 8, 33), m, 1); px.line(g, ...f(x - 8, 34), ...f(x + 8, 34), m, 1); } px.line(g, ...f(-4, 27), ...f(4, 27), m, 1); }\\n  if (o.maskUp && c.mask) { const k = T(c.mask); P([f(-27, 36), f(-8, 34), f(0, 36), f(8, 34), f(27, 36), f(25, 54), f(11, 66), f(0, 68), f(-11, 66), f(-25, 54)], k.base); P([f(-27, 36), f(-8, 34), f(-3, 50), f(-11, 66), f(-25, 54)], k.sh); for (const yy of [44, 52]) px.line(g, ...f(-18, yy), ...f(18, yy), k.lt, 1); px.line(g, ...f(-27, 38), ...f(-31, 32), k.lt, 1); px.line(g, ...f(27, 38), ...f(31, 32), k.lt, 1); }\\n1220→  if (c.scar) px.line(g, ...f(c.scar[0], c.scar[1]), ...f(c.scar[2], c.scar[3]), skin.deep, 1);\\n  if (c.tag) { px.rect(g, 72, 108, 16, 10, '#f0ece2'); px.rect(g, 74, 110, 12, 2, c.tag); px.rect(g, 74, 114, 8, 1, '#7a7468'); }\\n}\\nconst CAST = {\\n  vale: { name: 'DR. VALE', skin: '#f6d0b2', hair: '#c9562a', iris: '#3f8a58', cloth: '#2f9c8e', cap: '#2bb0a2', mask: '#bfe6dc', undershirt: '#e9fff6', blush: '#f0a48c', wide: .95,\\n    backHair: [[[-27, 14], [-30, 40], [-24, 52], [-16, 40], [-16, 14]], [[27, 14], [30, 40], [24, 52], [16, 40], [16, 14]]],\\n    frontHair: [[[[-27, 12], [-24, 24], [-16, 16], [-10, 22], [-3, 14], [3, 21], [10, 14], [18, 22], [27, 12], [14, 8], [-14, 8]], 'base'], [[[-27, 12], [-24, 24], [-16, 16], [-14, 10]], 'sh']],\\n    tag: '#c8452f' },\\n  quill: { name: 'NURSE QUILL', skin: '#dcae8e', hair: '#8d8a88', iris: '#4a4a55', cloth: '#3d62a6', cap: '#35558f', undershirt: '#dfe6f2', moustache: '#a7a3a0', lines: true, wide: 1.08, jaw: 1.04, browW: 3, brow: '#7c7875', browDrop: 2, mask: '#a9cfe0', frontHair: [] },\\n  oyelaran: { name: 'CHIEF OYELARAN', skin: '#7c4a2e', hair: '#c9c5bb', iris: '#2a1a12', cloth: '#2e2c36', coat: '#ece7da', undershirt: '#3a3644', lines: true, jaw: .98, glasses: '#d8c070',\\n1230→    backHair: [], frontHair: [[[[-27, 18], [-27, 2], [-14, -8], [14, -8], [27, 2], [27, 18], [20, 10], [8, 6], [-8, 6], [-20, 10]], 'base'], [[[-27, 18], [-27, 2], [-14, -8], [-8, 6], [-20, 10]], 'sh'], [[[6, -7], [16, -6], [22, 0], [12, 0]], 'lt']] },\\n  sokolova: { name: 'DR. SOKOLOVA', skin: '#e8c6aa', hair: '#dedad2', iris: '#6a8aa8', cloth: '#6b7a48', undershirt: '#f0ece0', lines: true, wide: 1.02, jaw: 1.02, scar: [10, 14, 17, 40], browW: 3, brow: '#b8b4ac',\\n    backHair: [[[-28, 6], [-34, 34], [-30, 58], [-20, 50], [-20, 10]], [[28, 6], [36, 26], [46, 52], [38, 64], [28, 44], [22, 10]]], frontHair: [[[[-27, 16], [-26, 2], [-12, -8], [14, -8], [27, 2], [27, 16], [16, 6], [-2, 12], [-16, 8]], 'base'], [[[-27, 16], [-26, 2], [-12, -8], [-6, 8], [-16, 8]], 'sh']] },\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\\n\\n**Page head.** Order matters.\\n\\n1240→```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>…</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body><!-- E.bootSplash's markup here --><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>/* engine */</script><script>/* game */</script></body></html>\\n```\\n1250→\\n**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\\n\\n```js\\n// Hub skeleton: shared world on my-3D2dge. The host's copy runs the world; other copies mirror it and send their own hands.\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst game = window.G = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  input: { ...base, useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] }, menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\\n1260→const NAME = 'SKELETON', W0 = 426, H0 = 240, DOTS = 12;\\nlet info = null, phase = 'wait', card = null, over = false, sent = 0, heardSeq = 0, S = { v: 70, dots: [], p: {} }, mine = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0 }, rng = null;\\nconst place = () => ({ x: 40 + rng() * 340, y: 40 + rng() * 160 });\\nfunction hostInit() { rng = HUB.rng('deal'); S.dots = Array.from({ length: DOTS }, (_, id) => ({ id, ...place(), alive: 1 })); for (const q of info.players) S.p[q.id] = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0, score: 0, gone: false }; }\\nfunction finish(won) { if (over) return; over = true; if (HUB.server !== true && info.me != null && S.p[info.me]) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  const live = info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).sort((a, b) => S.p[b.id].score - S.p[a.id].score), standings = [];\\n  for (const q of live) { const last = standings[standings.length - 1]; if (last && S.p[last[0]].score === S.p[q.id].score) last.push(q.id); else standings.push([q.id]); }\\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(info.players.map(q => [q.id, S.p[q.id].score]));\\n  HUB.send({ t: 'over', v: S.v }); HUB.finish({ standings, scores, won, awards: live.length ? [{ id: live[0].id, title: 'Steadiest Hand', detail: scores[live[0].id] + ' clean actions' }] : [] }); }\\nasync function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n1270→  if (!info) { phase = 'solo'; return; }\\n  HUB.on('card', c => { card = c; });\\n  HUB.on('start', () => { phase = 'count'; });\\n  HUB.on('message', (d, from) => { if (info.isHost) { const p = S.p[from]; if (d.t === 'i' && p && d.n > (p.n || 0)) { p.n = d.n; p.x = d.x; p.y = d.y; p.t = d.t2; } } else if (from === info.host) { if (d.t === 's' && d.n > heardSeq) { heardSeq = d.n; S.v = d.v; S.dots = d.o.map(([id, x, y]) => ({ id, x, y, alive: 1 })); for (const [id, x, y, t, sc] of d.p) { const q = S.p[id] || (S.p[id] = {}); if (id !== info.me) { q.x = x; q.y = y; q.t = t; } q.score = sc; } } if (d.t === 'over') over = true; } });\\n  HUB.on('leave', ({ id }) => { if (S.p[id]) S.p[id].gone = true; });\\n  HUB.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) finish(false); });\\n  HUB.on('end', () => { phase = 'over'; game.audio.music(null); game.audio.mute(true); });\\n  if (info.isHost) hostInit();\\n  HUB.ready(); }\\nfunction step(dt) { const I = game.input, m = I.move(), a = I.padAim, ptr = I.pointer(); let dx = (a ? a[0] : 0) + m[0], dy = (a ? a[1] : 0) + m[1]; mine.x = E.clamp(mine.x + dx * 300 * dt, 0, W0); mine.y = E.clamp(mine.y + dy * 300 * dt, 0, H0); if (ptr && I.lastDevice === 'mouse') { mine.x = ptr[0]; mine.y = ptr[1]; } mine.t = I.value('useTool'); }\\n1280→let snapN = 0, inN = 0, acc = 0;\\nfunction hostStep(dt) { S.v = Math.max(0, S.v - .05 * dt); if (info.me != null && S.p[info.me] && !info.server) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  for (const id in S.p) { const p = S.p[id]; if (p.gone || !p.t) continue; for (const d of S.dots) if (d.alive && Math.hypot(d.x - p.x, d.y - p.y) < 12) { d.alive = 0; p.score++; } } S.dots = S.dots.filter(d => d.alive); if (!S.dots.length) finish(true); }\\ngame.start({ scene: 'hub', scenes: { hub: { pausable: true, camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false },\\n  update(dt) { const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n    if (!info && !inSession) return;\\n    if (phase === 'wait' && info) { if (I.pressed('confirm')) HUB.answer('ready'); if (I.pressed('more')) HUB.answer('more'); const c = I.clicked(); if (c) HUB.answer(c[1] > game.H * .7 ? 'more' : 'ready'); }\\n    if (phase === 'count' && HUB.time() >= 0) phase = 'play';\\n    if (phase === 'play' && !over) { step(dt); if (info.isHost) hostStep(dt); acc += dt; if (acc >= 1 / 12) { acc = 0; if (info.isHost) HUB.send({ t: 's', n: ++snapN, v: Math.round(S.v), o: S.dots.map(d => [d.id, d.x | 0, d.y | 0]), p: info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).map(q => { const p = S.p[q.id]; return [q.id, p.x | 0, p.y | 0, p.t > .25 ? 1 : 0, p.score | 0]; }) }, { reliable: false }); else HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++inN, x: mine.x | 0, y: mine.y | 0, t2: mine.t > .25 ? 1 : 0 }, { to: info.host, reliable: false }); } } },\\n  draw(r) { if (info && info.server) return; r.sky(['#143a36', '#14504a']); r.overlay(g => { E.font.text(g, NAME + ' ' + phase + (card && card.left != null ? ' ' + Math.ceil(card.left / 1000) : ''), 8, 8, '#fff', { outline: false }); for (const d of S.dots) px.disc(g, d.x, d.y, 4, '#5ff0e0'); if (info) for (const q of info.players) { const p = q.id === info.me ? mine : S.p[q.id]; if (p && !(S.p[q.id] || {}).gone) { px.disc(g, p.x, p.y, 5, q.color); E.font.text(g, q.name.slice(0, 12), p.x + 7, p.y - 4, q.color, { outline: false }); } } }); } } } });\\n1290→window.__hubProbe = () => ({ phase, over, dots: S.dots.length, v: S.v, t: HUB.active ? HUB.time() : 0 });\\nconnect();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n**Harness runner.** The folder needs the game (as `game.html`) and copies of `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. It uses an OS-picked port, checks the frame's title is your game (replace the print with a test), and stops only its own server, by handle.\\n\\n```python\\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n1300→folder = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1])\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=folder, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True)\\ntry:\\n    line = srv.stdout.readline(); port = int(re.search(r'port (\\\\d+)', line).group(1))\\n    base = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/'\\n    RUNS = ['players=2&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1', 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1']\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        b = p.chromium.launch(args=['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\\n        for q in RUNS:\\n            pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); pg.goto(base + 'harness.html?game=game.html&' + q)\\n1310→            try: pg.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=90000)\\n            except Exception as e: print('TIMEOUT', q)\\n            r = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const h = window.__hubCheck; return h ? { pass: h.pass, failed: h.checks.filter(c => !c.pass).map(c => c.name + ': ' + c.detail), n: h.checks.length } : null }\\\")\\n            title = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const f = document.querySelector('iframe'); try { return f && f.contentDocument && f.contentDocument.title } catch (e) { return 'x' } }\\\")\\n            print(q, json.dumps(r)[:700], 'title:', title); pg.close()\\n        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\\n        b.close()\\nfinally:\\n    srv.terminate(); srv.wait(timeout=5)\\n```\\n1320→\\n## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\\n\\n**A DualSense in the standard mapping, for Playwright's `add_init_script`.** Set `__pad.axes[0..3]` (left x, left y, right x, right y), `__pad.buttons[i].value` and `.pressed`: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 12 to 15 D-pad, and bump `__pad.timestamp`.\\n\\n```js\\n(() => { const axes = [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons = Array.from({ length: 18 }, () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\\n  const pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes, buttons,\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); }, reset() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); } } };\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n1330→```\\n\\n**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\\n\\n```js\\nd.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:48px 24px 24px;text-align:center;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(5,3,12,.92) 45%);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\\n// and on the button, add pointer-events:auto to its inline style\\n```\\n\\nNote it in your Engine Feedback.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1090,\"limit\":280,\"raw_output\":\"## Appendix A: tissue painter\\n\\nRan on this computer at 480x270, 3 to 5 ms a frame under software rendering. It also runs headless. One instance per site. Each frame: stamp pools, wounds and so on from `S`, then `shade(fx)`, then draw `F.cv`.\\n\\n- `stampDisc(x, y, r, height, mat)`, `stampLine(points, r, height, mat)`: per-frame height and material. Height alone (no `mat`) makes a ridge, for Legato.\\n- `shade({ beat, breath, slow, lens, light, dim, spot })`: see its comment. `dyn` and `over` clear after each shade.\\n- `slow: true` is Long Breath's palette. `lens` is Sonar's. `dim` and `spot` are the blackout. A moving `light` is the swaying lamp.\\n\\n```js\\n// Bake once per site, stamp from the sim's state each frame, then shade(). Cosmetic only: the sim never reads it. Needs E = My3D2dge in scope.\\nconst BAYER = [0,8,2,10,12,4,14,6,3,11,1,9,15,7,13,5].map(v => (v + .5) / 16 - .5);\\nconst hex3 = h => [parseInt(h.slice(1, 3), 16), parseInt(h.slice(3, 5), 16), parseInt(h.slice(5, 7), 16)];\\nfunction makeRamp(keys, n, slow) { // dark to light through hand-picked, hue-shifted keys. slow: the same ramp seen through Long Breath\\n  const c = keys.map(hex3), out = new Uint32Array(n);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const t = i / (n - 1) * (c.length - 1), j = Math.min(c.length - 2, t | 0), f = t - j; let r = c[j][0] + (c[j + 1][0] - c[j][0]) * f, g = c[j][1] + (c[j + 1][1] - c[j][1]) * f, b = c[j][2] + (c[j + 1][2] - c[j][2]) * f;\\n    if (slow) { const y = r * .3 + g * .59 + b * .11; r = y * .55 + 8; g = y * .95 + 14; b = y * 1.05 + 22; } out[i] = 0xff000000 | (Math.min(255, b) << 16) | (Math.min(255, g) << 8) | Math.min(255, r); }\\n  return out;\\n}\\nconst MAT_KEYS = { // name: [ramp keys, specular strength]\\n  wall: [['#1c060c', '#4a0f18', '#7d1f26', '#a93a38'], .35], bowel: [['#3a0e1c', '#8a2f3e', '#c75f62', '#eb9486', '#ffc9b0'], 1], liver: [['#1e0610', '#4e1022', '#7c1e30', '#a83a42', '#d0645c'], .55],\\n  fat: [['#5a3a10', '#a8782a', '#dcb34c', '#f4d97e', '#fff2b8'], .7], vessel: [['#14103a', '#2c2a70', '#4a4aa0', '#7c78c8'], .8], artery: [['#3a0408', '#8c0f14', '#cf2a22', '#f4604a'], 1],\\n  skin: [['#6a3a22', '#a8683f', '#d39a68', '#eebf92'], .12], drape: [['#0c2c2a', '#14504a', '#1f7468', '#2f9a88'], 0], steel: [['#28303a', '#5a6a78', '#9aaab8', '#e8f0f8'], 1.6],\\n  blood: [['#180204', '#3c060a', '#680c10', '#8e1414'], 1.4], wound: [['#0c0104', '#2a0408', '#55090e', '#7a1216'], .5], char: [['#08070a', '#1c181a', '#332a28', '#4a3c34'], 0], gel: [['#0c4a38', '#1c8a64', '#54d0a0', '#b0ffe0'], 1.4] };\\nconst MAT_IDS = Object.keys(MAT_KEYS), MATS = MAT_IDS.map(k => ({ ramp: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20), slow: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20, true), spec: MAT_KEYS[k][1] }));\\nconst matId = n => MAT_IDS.indexOf(n);\\nfunction makeNoise(seed) { let a = seed >>> 0; const R = () => { a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0; let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), a | 1); t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61); return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };\\n  const L = new Float32Array(65536); for (let i = 0; i < L.length; i++) L[i] = R();\\n  const v = (x, y) => { const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), fx = x - xi, fy = y - yi, u = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), w = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy), s = (p, q) => L[(p & 255) | ((q & 255) << 8)]; return (s(xi, yi) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi) * u) * (1 - w) + (s(xi, yi + 1) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi + 1) * u) * w; };\\n  return { R, fbm: (x, y, o = 4) => { let k = .5, f = 1, n = 0; for (let i = 0; i < o; i++) { n += k * v(x * f, y * f); k *= .5; f *= 2.03; } return n; } }; }\\nclass TissueField {\\n  constructor(W, H, seed = 7) { this.W = W; this.H = H; const N = W * H; this.h = new Float32Array(N); this.m = new Uint8Array(N); this.pulse = new Float32Array(N); this.ao = new Float32Array(N).fill(1); this.dyn = new Float32Array(N); this.over = new Uint8Array(N); this.noise = makeNoise(seed);\\n    this.cv = E.mkCanvas(W, H); this.g = this.cv.getContext('2d'); this.img = this.g.createImageData(W, H); this.u = new Uint32Array(this.img.data.buffer); }\\n  blob(x, y, rx, ry, rot, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, pulse, noise } = this, c = Math.cos(rot), s = Math.sin(rot), R = Math.max(rx, ry) + (o.warp || 0) + 2, id = matId(mat), warp = o.warp || 0, base = o.base || 0, add = !!o.add;\\n    for (let py = Math.max(0, y - R | 0); py < Math.min(H, y + R + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(0, x - R | 0); px < Math.min(W, x + R + 1); px++) {\\n      const wx = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, wy = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * .03 + 40, py * .03, 2) - .5) * warp : 0, dx = px - x + wx, dy = py - y + wy, u = (dx * c + dy * s) / rx, v = (-dx * s + dy * c) / ry, d = u * u + v * v; if (d >= 1) continue;\\n      const i = py * W + px, top = base + hgt * Math.sqrt(1 - d); if (add) { h[i] += hgt * (1 - d); m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = Math.max(pulse[i], o.pulse * (1 - d)); } else if (top > h[i]) { h[i] = top; m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = o.pulse * (1 - d); } } }\\n  tube(pts, r, hgt, mat, o = {}) { const step = Math.max(1, r * .35); for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / step | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.blob(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, r, 0, hgt, mat, o); } }\\n  finish(detail = 1.1) { const { W, H, h, ao, noise } = this, N = W * H, blur = new Float32Array(N), tmp = new Float32Array(N), R = 7;\\n    for (let i = 0, y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++, i++) h[i] += (noise.fbm(x * .11, y * .11, 3) - .5) * detail;\\n    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { let s = 0; for (let x = -R; x <= R; x++) s += h[y * W + Math.max(0, x)]; for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { tmp[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += h[y * W + Math.min(W - 1, x + R + 1)] - h[y * W + Math.max(0, x - R)]; } }\\n    for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { let s = 0; for (let y = -R; y <= R; y++) s += tmp[Math.max(0, y) * W + x]; for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { blur[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += tmp[Math.min(H - 1, y + R + 1) * W + x] - tmp[Math.max(0, y - R) * W + x]; } }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) ao[i] = Math.max(.42, Math.min(1.08, 1 - (blur[i] - h[i]) * .055)); }\\n  // what the sim's objects stamp each frame, before shade(): dynamic height, and an override material\\n  stampDisc(x, y, r, hgt, mat) { const { W, H, dyn, over } = this, id = mat ? matId(mat) + 1 : 0; for (let py = Math.max(1, y - r | 0); py < Math.min(H - 1, y + r + 1); py++) for (let px = Math.max(1, x - r | 0); px < Math.min(W - 1, x + r + 1); px++) { const d = ((px - x) ** 2 + (py - y) ** 2) / (r * r); if (d < 1) { const i = py * W + px; dyn[i] = hgt < 0 ? Math.min(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)) : Math.max(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)); if (id) over[i] = id; } } }\\n  stampLine(pts, r, hgt, mat) { for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) { const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / Math.max(1, r * .5) | 0); for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.stampDisc(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, hgt, mat); } }\\n  // fx: { beat 0..1, breath px, slow: Long Breath palette, lens: {x, y, r} shows the cold palette inside (Sonar), light: [lx, ly], dim: 0..1 darkness, spot: {x, y, r} stays lit while dim }\\n  shade(fx = {}) { const { W, H, h, m, ao, pulse, dyn, over, u } = this, beat = fx.beat || 0, off = Math.round(fx.breath || 0) * W, slow = !!fx.slow, lens = fx.lens, lr2 = lens ? lens.r * lens.r : 0, dim = fx.dim || 0, spot = fx.spot, sr2 = spot ? spot.r * spot.r : 0, lx = fx.light ? fx.light[0] : -.42, ly = fx.light ? fx.light[1] : -.52, lz = Math.sqrt(Math.max(.1, 1 - lx * lx - ly * ly)), hl = Math.hypot(lx, ly, lz + 1), hx = lx / hl, hy = ly / hl, hz = (lz + 1) / hl;\\n    for (let y = 1; y < H - 1; y++) for (let x = 1, i = y * W + 1; x < W - 1; x++, i++) {\\n      const j = Math.max(W + 1, Math.min(W * H - W - 2, i + off)), k = 1 + beat * pulse[j], dx = (h[j - 1] - h[j + 1]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - 1] - dyn[i + 1]) * .5, dy = (h[j - W] - h[j + W]) * k * .5 + (dyn[i - W] - dyn[i + W]) * .5, nl = 1 / Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + 1), nx = dx * nl, ny = dy * nl, nz = nl;\\n      const diff = Math.max(0, nx * lx + ny * ly + nz * lz), sh = Math.max(0, nx * hx + ny * hy + nz * hz), ov = over[i], M = MATS[ov ? ov - 1 : m[j]], cold = slow || (lens && (x - lens.x) ** 2 + (y - lens.y) ** 2 < lr2), r = cold ? M.slow : M.ramp, n = r.length, s2 = sh * sh, s4 = s2 * s2, s8 = s4 * s4, s16 = s8 * s8, s32 = s16 * s16;\\n      const lit = dim && !(spot && (x - spot.x) ** 2 + (y - spot.y) ** 2 < sr2) ? 1 - dim : 1, lum = (diff * .92 + s8 * .16 * M.spec + beat * pulse[j] * .6) * (ov ? 1 : ao[j]) * lit, c = Math.max(0, Math.min(n - 1, (lum * (n - 1) + BAYER[(x & 3) | ((y & 3) << 2)] * 1.15 + .5) | 0));\\n      u[i] = s32 * s8 * M.spec * lit > .42 ? (cold ? 0xffffffe0 : 0xfff4f0ff) : r[c]; }\\n    this.g.putImageData(this.img, 0, 0); dyn.fill(0); over.fill(0); }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix B: a site recipe\\n\\n`F.stampDisc` coordinates here use screen pixels. To place sim objects, add `OX, OY`.\\n\\n```js\\n// A site recipe: the abdomen. Design space is 426 x 240 about the screen's centre; a bigger screen only shows more drape.\\nfunction bakeAbdomen(W, H, seed = 11) { const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), cx = W / 2, cy = H / 2 - 4, n = F.noise, rx = 171, ry = 91;\\n  for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { const i = y * W + x, d = ((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2, fold = Math.sin(x * .09 + 1.6 * Math.sin(y * .05)) * 1.6 + Math.sin(y * .17 + x * .03) * .8;\\n    if (d < 1) { F.h[i] = -16 + 12 * d * d + Math.sin(x * .05 + y * .03) * 1.4; F.m[i] = matId('wall'); }            // the cavity\\n    else if (d < 1.28) { const e = (d - 1) / .28; F.h[i] = 4 + 7 * Math.sin(e * Math.PI); F.m[i] = matId('skin'); }  // lips of skin\\n    else { F.h[i] = 6 + fold; F.m[i] = matId('drape'); } }                                                            // drapes to any screen's edge\\n  F.blob(cx - rx * .55, cy - ry * .5, rx * .55, ry * .55, -.3, 17, 'liver', { base: -11, warp: 12 });\\n  for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) { const a = n.R() * 6.28, r = .55 + n.R() * .32; F.blob(cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * r, cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * r, 9 + n.R() * 14, 7 + n.R() * 9, n.R() * 3, 8, 'fat', { base: -10, warp: 8 }); }\\n  const coil = (x0, y0, len, dir, r) => { const pts = [[x0, y0]]; let a = dir, x = x0, y = y0; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * 1.5 + Math.sin(i * .9) * .5; x += Math.cos(a) * r * 1.3; y += Math.sin(a) * r * 1.3; if (((x - cx) / (rx * .92)) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / (ry * .92)) ** 2 > 1) { a += 2.4; x += Math.cos(a) * r; y += Math.sin(a) * r; } pts.push([x, y]); } return pts; };\\n  F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .05, cy - ry * .25, 34, .2, 9), 11, 14, 'bowel', { base: -8 }); F.tube(coil(cx + rx * .45, cy + ry * .25, 26, 2.6, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -7 }); F.tube(coil(cx - rx * .35, cy + ry * .45, 22, -.3, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -6 });\\n  const veins = (x, y, a, len, r, mat) => { const pts = [[x, y]]; for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) { a += (n.R() - .5) * .8; x += Math.cos(a) * 7; y += Math.sin(a) * 7; if (((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2 > .96) break; pts.push([x, y]); if (r > 1.2 && n.R() < .22) veins(x, y, a + (n.R() < .5 ? .9 : -.9), len * .5 | 0, r * .7, mat); } F.tube(pts, r, 1.6, mat, { add: true, pulse: mat === 'artery' ? .35 : 0 }); };\\n  veins(cx - rx * .7, cy - ry * .05, -.2, 16, 2.2, 'vessel'); veins(cx + rx * .7, cy - ry * .6, 2.4, 14, 2, 'artery'); veins(cx + rx * .1, cy + ry * .75, -1.5, 12, 1.8, 'vessel');\\n  for (const a of [-.45, .5, 2.7, 3.6]) { const ex = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.02, ey = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.02, ox = cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * 1.5, oy = cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * 1.5; F.tube([[ex, ey], [ox, oy]], 4, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); F.tube([[ex - Math.sin(a) * 9, ey + Math.cos(a) * 9], [ex + Math.sin(a) * 9, ey - Math.cos(a) * 9]], 3, 5, 'steel', { base: 10 }); } // retractors\\n  F.finish(1.1); return F; }\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix C: portrait painter\\n\\nBusts for the four leads. The other four follow the same shape: `frontHair`, `backHair` (polygons in face space, x from the center, y down), `glasses`, `moustache`, `scar`, `cap`, `mask` (`maskUp: true` covers the mouth, for theatre), `lines`, `blush`, `jaw`, `wide`. Cache each expression to a canvas with `E.mkCanvas(112, 128)`; call `E.px.reset` on the target after drawing on it with the canvas API.\\n\\n```js\\n// A bust from data in hard-edged tones, 112 x 128 buffer pixels. Cache each expression in a canvas; the sim never reads it. Needs E = My3D2dge in scope.\\n// o: { expr: neutral | smile | angry | sad | shock | shout, blink: 0..1, talk: 0..1, look: -1..1 }\\nfunction drawBust(g, c, o = {}) { const px = E.px, P = (pts, col) => px.poly(g, pts, col), T = E.tones;\\n  const skin = T(c.skin), hair = T(c.hair), cloth = T(c.cloth), expr = o.expr || 'neutral', blink = o.blink || 0, talk = o.talk || 0, cx = 56, top = 20;\\n  const jaw = c.jaw || 1, wide = c.wide || 1, f = (x, y) => [cx + x * wide, top + y]; // face space: x from centre, y down\\n  // back hair\\n  if (c.backHair) for (const s of c.backHair) P(s.map(([x, y]) => f(x, y)), hair.sh);\\n  // shoulders and collar\\n  P([[6, 128], [10, 104], [30, 92], [46, 88], [66, 88], [82, 92], [102, 104], [106, 128]], cloth.base);\\n  P([[6, 128], [10, 104], [30, 92], [34, 128]], cloth.sh); P([[78, 128], [82, 92], [102, 104], [106, 128]], cloth.lt);\\n  // neck\\n  P([[46, 66], [66, 66], [68, 92], [56, 104], [44, 92]], skin.sh);\\n  // V-neck and inner shirt\\n  P([[42, 88], [56, 110], [70, 88], [66, 86], [56, 100], [46, 86]], cloth.deep); P([[46, 86], [56, 100], [66, 86], [64, 92], [56, 104], [48, 92]], c.undershirt || skin.sh);\\n  if (c.coat) { P([[6, 128], [10, 104], [30, 92], [42, 88], [52, 128]], c.coat); P([[106, 128], [102, 104], [82, 92], [70, 88], [60, 128]], c.coat); P([[42, 88], [52, 128], [47, 128], [36, 92]], E.tones(c.coat).sh); P([[70, 88], [60, 128], [65, 128], [76, 92]], E.tones(c.coat).sh); }\\n  // ears\\n  P([f(-27, 30), f(-31, 34), f(-30, 42), f(-26, 45)], skin.sh); P([f(27, 30), f(31, 34), f(30, 42), f(26, 45)], skin.base);\\n  // head: wide cranium, cheek, chin\\n  const J = jaw; P([f(-26, 12), f(-27, 34), f(-22, 48 * J), f(-11, 60 * J), f(0, 64 * J), f(11, 60 * J), f(22, 48 * J), f(27, 34), f(26, 12), f(14, 2), f(-14, 2)], skin.base);\\n  P([f(-27, 30), f(-22, 48 * J), f(-11, 60 * J), f(0, 64 * J), f(-6, 54 * J), f(-16, 44), f(-22, 30)], skin.sh); // cheek shadow, viewer's left\\n  if (c.blush) { px.ell(g, ...f(-15, 41), 4, 2, c.blush); px.ell(g, ...f(16, 41), 4, 2, c.blush); }\\n  if (c.lines) { px.line(g, ...f(-11, 45), ...f(-6, 50), skin.sh, 1); px.line(g, ...f(11, 45), ...f(6, 50), skin.sh, 1); px.line(g, ...f(-23, 26), ...f(-20, 28), skin.sh, 1); px.line(g, ...f(23, 26), ...f(20, 28), skin.sh, 1); }\\n  // eyes\\n  const eye = (sx) => { const x = sx * 13, y = 30 + (expr === 'shock' ? -1 : 0), w = 7, hh = expr === 'shock' ? 8 : expr === 'angry' ? 5 : 7;\\n    if (blink > .5 || expr === 'sad-closed') { px.line(g, ...f(x - w, y + 1), ...f(x + w, y + 1), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); return; }\\n    P([f(x - w, y), f(x - w + 3, y - hh + 2), f(x + w - 3, y - hh + 2), f(x + w, y), f(x + w - 2, y + 4), f(x - w + 2, y + 4)], '#f8f4ee');\\n    const ix = x + (o.look || 0) * 2 + (expr === 'shock' ? 0 : 0); px.ell(g, ...f(ix, y - 1), 4, expr === 'shock' ? 4 : 5, c.iris || '#3a5a7a'); px.ell(g, ...f(ix, y), 2, 3, c.pupil || '#120c14'); px.rect(g, ...f(ix - 3, y - 4), 3, 2, '#ffffff'); px.dot(g, ...f(ix + 2, y + 2), '#ffffff');\\n    px.line(g, ...f(x - w - 1, y + (sx < 0 ? 1 : -1)), ...f(x - w + 4, y - hh + 2), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); px.line(g, ...f(x - w + 4, y - hh + 2), ...f(x + w - 4, y - hh + 2), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); px.line(g, ...f(x + w - 4, y - hh + 2), ...f(x + w + 1, y + (sx < 0 ? -1 : 1)), c.lash || '#1a1016', 2); };\\n  eye(-1); eye(1);\\n  // brows\\n  const by = 17 + (c.browDrop || 0), br = expr === 'angry' ? 3 : expr === 'sad' ? -3 : expr === 'shock' ? -1 : 0, bc = c.brow || hair.deep, bw = c.browW || 2; px.line(g, ...f(-20, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) - br), ...f(-7, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) + br), bc, bw); px.line(g, ...f(7, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) + br), ...f(20, by + (expr === 'shock' ? -3 : 0) - br), bc, bw);\\n  // nose\\n  px.line(g, ...f(1, 40), ...f(-1, 45), skin.sh, 1); px.dot(g, ...f(0, 46), skin.deep);\\n  // mouth\\n  const my = 53, mo = talk > .5 || expr === 'shout' || expr === 'shock'; if (mo) { const a = expr === 'shout' || expr === 'shock' ? 7 : 4, w = expr === 'shout' ? 7 : 5; P([f(-w, my - 1), f(w, my - 1), f(w - 2, my + a), f(-w + 2, my + a)], '#5a1a24'); P([f(-w + 2, my + a - 2), f(w - 2, my + a - 2), f(w - 3, my + a), f(-w + 3, my + a)], '#c8505a'); if (a > 4) px.rect(g, ...f(-w + 1, my - 1), (w - 1) * 2, 2, '#f4f0e8'); }\\n  else if (expr === 'smile') { px.line(g, ...f(-7, my - 1), ...f(-3, my + 2), skin.deep, 1); px.line(g, ...f(-3, my + 2), ...f(3, my + 2), skin.deep, 1); px.line(g, ...f(3, my + 2), ...f(7, my - 1), skin.deep, 1); }\\n  else if (expr === 'sad' || expr === 'angry') { px.line(g, ...f(-5, my + 2), ...f(0, my), skin.deep, 1); px.line(g, ...f(0, my), ...f(5, my + 2), skin.deep, 1); }\\n  else px.line(g, ...f(-4, my), ...f(4, my), skin.deep, 1);\\n  if (c.moustache) { P([f(-13, 50), f(-6, 46), f(0, 48), f(6, 46), f(13, 50), f(8, 52), f(0, 50), f(-8, 52)], c.moustache); px.line(g, ...f(-6, 47), ...f(6, 47), E.tones(c.moustache).lt, 1); }\\n  // front hair\\n  if (c.frontHair) for (const [s, tone] of c.frontHair) P(s.map(([x, y]) => f(x, y)), hair[tone || 'base']);\\n  if (c.hairGlint) for (const s of c.hairGlint) P(s.map(([x, y]) => f(x, y)), hair.hi);\\n  // cap\\n  if (c.cap) { const k = T(c.cap); P([f(-29, 16), f(-27, 2), f(-14, -9), f(14, -9), f(27, 2), f(29, 16), f(16, 11), f(-16, 11)], k.base); P([f(-29, 16), f(-27, 2), f(-14, -9), f(-6, -9), f(-14, 11), f(-16, 11)], k.sh); P([f(6, -8), f(14, -9), f(22, -3), f(14, -3)], k.lt); P([f(-29, 16), f(-16, 11), f(16, 11), f(29, 16), f(27, 18), f(16, 14), f(-16, 14), f(-27, 18)], k.deep); }\\n  // lowered mask, glasses\\n  if (c.mask && !o.maskUp) { const k = T(c.mask); P([f(-20, 62), f(20, 62), f(25, 76), f(0, 84), f(-25, 76)], k.base); P([f(-20, 62), f(-25, 76), f(0, 84), f(-6, 74)], k.sh); px.line(g, ...f(-20, 62), ...f(-28, 50), k.lt, 1); px.line(g, ...f(20, 62), ...f(28, 50), k.lt, 1); }\\n  if (c.glasses) { const m = c.glasses; for (const sx of [-1, 1]) { const x = sx * 13; px.line(g, ...f(x - 9, 25), ...f(x + 9, 25), m, 1); px.line(g, ...f(x - 9, 25), ...f(x - 8, 33), m, 1); px.line(g, ...f(x + 9, 25), ...f(x + 8, 33), m, 1); px.line(g, ...f(x - 8, 34), ...f(x + 8, 34), m, 1); } px.line(g, ...f(-4, 27), ...f(4, 27), m, 1); }\\n  if (o.maskUp && c.mask) { const k = T(c.mask); P([f(-27, 36), f(-8, 34), f(0, 36), f(8, 34), f(27, 36), f(25, 54), f(11, 66), f(0, 68), f(-11, 66), f(-25, 54)], k.base); P([f(-27, 36), f(-8, 34), f(-3, 50), f(-11, 66), f(-25, 54)], k.sh); for (const yy of [44, 52]) px.line(g, ...f(-18, yy), ...f(18, yy), k.lt, 1); px.line(g, ...f(-27, 38), ...f(-31, 32), k.lt, 1); px.line(g, ...f(27, 38), ...f(31, 32), k.lt, 1); }\\n  if (c.scar) px.line(g, ...f(c.scar[0], c.scar[1]), ...f(c.scar[2], c.scar[3]), skin.deep, 1);\\n  if (c.tag) { px.rect(g, 72, 108, 16, 10, '#f0ece2'); px.rect(g, 74, 110, 12, 2, c.tag); px.rect(g, 74, 114, 8, 1, '#7a7468'); }\\n}\\nconst CAST = {\\n  vale: { name: 'DR. VALE', skin: '#f6d0b2', hair: '#c9562a', iris: '#3f8a58', cloth: '#2f9c8e', cap: '#2bb0a2', mask: '#bfe6dc', undershirt: '#e9fff6', blush: '#f0a48c', wide: .95,\\n    backHair: [[[-27, 14], [-30, 40], [-24, 52], [-16, 40], [-16, 14]], [[27, 14], [30, 40], [24, 52], [16, 40], [16, 14]]],\\n    frontHair: [[[[-27, 12], [-24, 24], [-16, 16], [-10, 22], [-3, 14], [3, 21], [10, 14], [18, 22], [27, 12], [14, 8], [-14, 8]], 'base'], [[[-27, 12], [-24, 24], [-16, 16], [-14, 10]], 'sh']],\\n    tag: '#c8452f' },\\n  quill: { name: 'NURSE QUILL', skin: '#dcae8e', hair: '#8d8a88', iris: '#4a4a55', cloth: '#3d62a6', cap: '#35558f', undershirt: '#dfe6f2', moustache: '#a7a3a0', lines: true, wide: 1.08, jaw: 1.04, browW: 3, brow: '#7c7875', browDrop: 2, mask: '#a9cfe0', frontHair: [] },\\n  oyelaran: { name: 'CHIEF OYELARAN', skin: '#7c4a2e', hair: '#c9c5bb', iris: '#2a1a12', cloth: '#2e2c36', coat: '#ece7da', undershirt: '#3a3644', lines: true, jaw: .98, glasses: '#d8c070',\\n    backHair: [], frontHair: [[[[-27, 18], [-27, 2], [-14, -8], [14, -8], [27, 2], [27, 18], [20, 10], [8, 6], [-8, 6], [-20, 10]], 'base'], [[[-27, 18], [-27, 2], [-14, -8], [-8, 6], [-20, 10]], 'sh'], [[[6, -7], [16, -6], [22, 0], [12, 0]], 'lt']] },\\n  sokolova: { name: 'DR. SOKOLOVA', skin: '#e8c6aa', hair: '#dedad2', iris: '#6a8aa8', cloth: '#6b7a48', undershirt: '#f0ece0', lines: true, wide: 1.02, jaw: 1.02, scar: [10, 14, 17, 40], browW: 3, brow: '#b8b4ac',\\n    backHair: [[[-28, 6], [-34, 34], [-30, 58], [-20, 50], [-20, 10]], [[28, 6], [36, 26], [46, 52], [38, 64], [28, 44], [22, 10]]], frontHair: [[[[-27, 16], [-26, 2], [-12, -8], [14, -8], [27, 2], [27, 16], [16, 6], [-2, 12], [-16, 8]], 'base'], [[[-27, 16], [-26, 2], [-12, -8], [-6, 8], [-16, 8]], 'sh']] },\\n};\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\\n\\n**Page head.** Order matters.\\n\\n```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>…</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body><!-- E.bootSplash's markup here --><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>/* engine */</script><script>/* game */</script></body></html>\\n```\\n\\n**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\\n\\n```js\\n// Hub skeleton: shared world on my-3D2dge. The host's copy runs the world; other copies mirror it and send their own hands.\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst game = window.G = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  input: { ...base, useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] }, menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\\nconst NAME = 'SKELETON', W0 = 426, H0 = 240, DOTS = 12;\\nlet info = null, phase = 'wait', card = null, over = false, sent = 0, heardSeq = 0, S = { v: 70, dots: [], p: {} }, mine = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0 }, rng = null;\\nconst place = () => ({ x: 40 + rng() * 340, y: 40 + rng() * 160 });\\nfunction hostInit() { rng = HUB.rng('deal'); S.dots = Array.from({ length: DOTS }, (_, id) => ({ id, ...place(), alive: 1 })); for (const q of info.players) S.p[q.id] = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0, score: 0, gone: false }; }\\nfunction finish(won) { if (over) return; over = true; if (HUB.server !== true && info.me != null && S.p[info.me]) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  const live = info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).sort((a, b) => S.p[b.id].score - S.p[a.id].score), standings = [];\\n  for (const q of live) { const last = standings[standings.length - 1]; if (last && S.p[last[0]].score === S.p[q.id].score) last.push(q.id); else standings.push([q.id]); }\\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(info.players.map(q => [q.id, S.p[q.id].score]));\\n  HUB.send({ t: 'over', v: S.v }); HUB.finish({ standings, scores, won, awards: live.length ? [{ id: live[0].id, title: 'Steadiest Hand', detail: scores[live[0].id] + ' clean actions' }] : [] }); }\\nasync function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n  if (!info) { phase = 'solo'; return; }\\n  HUB.on('card', c => { card = c; });\\n  HUB.on('start', () => { phase = 'count'; });\\n  HUB.on('message', (d, from) => { if (info.isHost) { const p = S.p[from]; if (d.t === 'i' && p && d.n > (p.n || 0)) { p.n = d.n; p.x = d.x; p.y = d.y; p.t = d.t2; } } else if (from === info.host) { if (d.t === 's' && d.n > heardSeq) { heardSeq = d.n; S.v = d.v; S.dots = d.o.map(([id, x, y]) => ({ id, x, y, alive: 1 })); for (const [id, x, y, t, sc] of d.p) { const q = S.p[id] || (S.p[id] = {}); if (id !== info.me) { q.x = x; q.y = y; q.t = t; } q.score = sc; } } if (d.t === 'over') over = true; } });\\n  HUB.on('leave', ({ id }) => { if (S.p[id]) S.p[id].gone = true; });\\n  HUB.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) finish(false); });\\n  HUB.on('end', () => { phase = 'over'; game.audio.music(null); game.audio.mute(true); });\\n  if (info.isHost) hostInit();\\n  HUB.ready(); }\\nfunction step(dt) { const I = game.input, m = I.move(), a = I.padAim, ptr = I.pointer(); let dx = (a ? a[0] : 0) + m[0], dy = (a ? a[1] : 0) + m[1]; mine.x = E.clamp(mine.x + dx * 300 * dt, 0, W0); mine.y = E.clamp(mine.y + dy * 300 * dt, 0, H0); if (ptr && I.lastDevice === 'mouse') { mine.x = ptr[0]; mine.y = ptr[1]; } mine.t = I.value('useTool'); }\\nlet snapN = 0, inN = 0, acc = 0;\\nfunction hostStep(dt) { S.v = Math.max(0, S.v - .05 * dt); if (info.me != null && S.p[info.me] && !info.server) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  for (const id in S.p) { const p = S.p[id]; if (p.gone || !p.t) continue; for (const d of S.dots) if (d.alive && Math.hypot(d.x - p.x, d.y - p.y) < 12) { d.alive = 0; p.score++; } } S.dots = S.dots.filter(d => d.alive); if (!S.dots.length) finish(true); }\\ngame.start({ scene: 'hub', scenes: { hub: { pausable: true, camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false },\\n  update(dt) { const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n    if (!info && !inSession) return;\\n    if (phase === 'wait' && info) { if (I.pressed('confirm')) HUB.answer('ready'); if (I.pressed('more')) HUB.answer('more'); const c = I.clicked(); if (c) HUB.answer(c[1] > game.H * .7 ? 'more' : 'ready'); }\\n    if (phase === 'count' && HUB.time() >= 0) phase = 'play';\\n    if (phase === 'play' && !over) { step(dt); if (info.isHost) hostStep(dt); acc += dt; if (acc >= 1 / 12) { acc = 0; if (info.isHost) HUB.send({ t: 's', n: ++snapN, v: Math.round(S.v), o: S.dots.map(d => [d.id, d.x | 0, d.y | 0]), p: info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).map(q => { const p = S.p[q.id]; return [q.id, p.x | 0, p.y | 0, p.t > .25 ? 1 : 0, p.score | 0]; }) }, { reliable: false }); else HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++inN, x: mine.x | 0, y: mine.y | 0, t2: mine.t > .25 ? 1 : 0 }, { to: info.host, reliable: false }); } } },\\n  draw(r) { if (info && info.server) return; r.sky(['#143a36', '#14504a']); r.overlay(g => { E.font.text(g, NAME + ' ' + phase + (card && card.left != null ? ' ' + Math.ceil(card.left / 1000) : ''), 8, 8, '#fff', { outline: false }); for (const d of S.dots) px.disc(g, d.x, d.y, 4, '#5ff0e0'); if (info) for (const q of info.players) { const p = q.id === info.me ? mine : S.p[q.id]; if (p && !(S.p[q.id] || {}).gone) { px.disc(g, p.x, p.y, 5, q.color); E.font.text(g, q.name.slice(0, 12), p.x + 7, p.y - 4, q.color, { outline: false }); } } }); } } } });\\nwindow.__hubProbe = () => ({ phase, over, dots: S.dots.length, v: S.v, t: HUB.active ? HUB.time() : 0 });\\nconnect();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n**Harness runner.** The folder needs the game (as `game.html`) and copies of `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. It uses an OS-picked port, checks the frame's title is your game (replace the print with a test), and stops only its own server, by handle.\\n\\n```python\\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\nfolder = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1])\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=folder, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True)\\ntry:\\n    line = srv.stdout.readline(); port = int(re.search(r'port (\\\\d+)', line).group(1))\\n    base = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/'\\n    RUNS = ['players=2&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1', 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1']\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        b = p.chromium.launch(args=['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\\n        for q in RUNS:\\n            pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); pg.goto(base + 'harness.html?game=game.html&' + q)\\n            try: pg.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=90000)\\n            except Exception as e: print('TIMEOUT', q)\\n            r = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const h = window.__hubCheck; return h ? { pass: h.pass, failed: h.checks.filter(c => !c.pass).map(c => c.name + ': ' + c.detail), n: h.checks.length } : null }\\\")\\n            title = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const f = document.querySelector('iframe'); try { return f && f.contentDocument && f.contentDocument.title } catch (e) { return 'x' } }\\\")\\n            print(q, json.dumps(r)[:700], 'title:', title); pg.close()\\n        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\\n        b.close()\\nfinally:\\n    srv.terminate(); srv.wait(timeout=5)\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\\n\\n**A DualSense in the standard mapping, for Playwright's `add_init_script`.** Set `__pad.axes[0..3]` (left x, left y, right x, right y), `__pad.buttons[i].value` and `.pressed`: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 12 to 15 D-pad, and bump `__pad.timestamp`.\\n\\n```js\\n(() => { const axes = [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons = Array.from({ length: 18 }, () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\\n  const pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes, buttons,\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); }, reset() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); } } };\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n```\\n\\n**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\\n\\n```js\\nd.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:48px 24px 24px;text-align:center;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(5,3,12,.92) 45%);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\\n// and on the button, add pointer-events:auto to its inline style\\n```\\n\\nNote it in your Engine Feedback.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1339}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-86a53474-6443-4998-83da-f68c19495121-65","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"316→## 6. Controls and prompts\\n\\nThe keyboard and mouse are native here, not stand-ins for controller buttons: the same game on the same screens, with the keys PC players expect for this kind of game. The mouse is the best pointer in the game, and the pad is the best-feeling couch device.\\n\\n320→| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Aim | Right stick. D-pad nudges | Mouse, or WASD or arrows |\\n| Use tool | R2 (analog) or ✕ | Left click or Space |\\n| Fine mode, loupe | L2 | Shift |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick | 1 to 8. Hold Right click and flick |\\n| Step tool | L1, R1 | Q, E, or the wheel |\\n| The Steady | △ | F or Middle click |\\n| Consult | □ | C |\\n| Drop, cancel stroke | ○ | X or Backspace |\\n330→| Code Blue shock | L2 + R2 | Left click or Space |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc or P |\\n| Ward: walk | Left stick or D-pad | WASD or arrows, or click to walk |\\n| Ward: talk, use | ✕ | E or Enter, or click the person |\\n| Story: advance | ✕ | Enter, Space or click |\\n| Story: fast-forward | Hold □ | Hold Ctrl |\\n| Story: backlog | △ | B |\\n\\nSettings adds **Swap sticks** for left-handers (cursor and wheel trade sticks).\\n\\n340→```js\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst INPUT = { ...base,\\n  useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], fine: ['Pad6', 'ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight'], gift: ['Pad3', 'KeyF', 'Mouse1'], consult: ['Pad2', 'KeyC'],\\n  toolPrev: ['Pad4', 'KeyQ', 'WheelUp'], toolNext: ['Pad5', 'KeyE', 'WheelDown'], wheelHold: ['Mouse2'],\\n  curU: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp'], curD: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown'], curL: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft'], curR: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight'],   // separate from up/down/left/right, which the left stick also presses\\n  nudgeU: ['Pad12'], nudgeD: ['Pad13'], nudgeL: ['Pad14'], nudgeR: ['Pad15'],\\n  tool1: ['Digit1'], tool2: ['Digit2'], tool3: ['Digit3'], tool4: ['Digit4'], tool5: ['Digit5'], tool6: ['Digit6'], tool7: ['Digit7'], tool8: ['Digit8'],\\n  interact: ['Pad0', 'KeyE', 'Enter'], skip: ['Pad2', 'ControlLeft'], log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\\n```\\n350→\\nRead the two sticks from `input.padAim` and `input.padMove`, the trigger from `input.value('useTool')`. Name the actions and hide `tool1` to `tool8` from rebinding through `menu.controls`. Give the scene `camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false }`, because the wheel is the game's.\\n\\n**Prompts.** Always through `game.input.label(action)`, so they follow the device used last and the player's rebinding. Draw a label as a button cap: a rounded rectangle with the label in it, the PlayStation or Xbox face colors on face buttons, and plain keycaps for keys. For the sticks, draw a small stick icon with L or R. Never hard-code a key in text. PlayStation glyphs by default with the Xbox option from fact 5.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Things on the table\\n\\nA registry (`defObject`), each with sim behavior, a draw function kept apart, and a bot plan.\\n360→\\n| Type | Looks like | Fixed by | Vitals/s while open | Other effects |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `shard` | Glass or steel sliver with a glint | Forceps along its axis | .1 | |\\n| `laceration` | Short red cut | Salve | .2 | Small pool over time |\\n| `wound` | Gaping cut with lips | Suture N stitches | .4 | Bleeding falls with each stitch |\",\"content_concise\":\"316→## 6. Controls and prompts\\n\\nThe keyboard and mouse are native here, not stand-ins for controller buttons: the same game on the same screens, with the keys PC players expect for this kind of game. The mouse is the best pointer in the game, and the pad is the best-feeling couch device.\\n\\n320→| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Aim | Right stick. D-pad nudges | Mouse, or WASD or arrows |\\n| Use tool | R2 (analog) or ✕ | Left click or Space |\\n| Fine mode, loupe | L2 | Shift |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick | 1 to 8. Hold Right click and flick |\\n| Step tool | L1, R1 | Q, E, or the wheel |\\n| The Steady | △ | F or Middle click |\\n| Consult | □ | C |\\n| Drop, cancel stroke | ○ | X or Backspace |\\n330→| Code Blue shock | L2 + R2 | Left click or Space |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc or P |\\n| Ward: walk | Left stick or D-pad | WASD or arrows, or click to walk |\\n| Ward: talk, use | ✕ | E or Enter, or click the person |\\n| Story: advance | ✕ | Enter, Space or click |\\n| Story: fast-forward | Hold □ | Hold Ctrl |\\n| Story: backlog | △ | B |\\n\\nSettings adds **Swap sticks** for left-handers (cursor and wheel trade sticks).\\n\\n340→```js\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst INPUT = { ...base,\\n  useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], fine: ['Pad6', 'ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight'], gift: ['Pad3', 'KeyF', 'Mouse1'], consult: ['Pad2', 'KeyC'],\\n  toolPrev: ['Pad4', 'KeyQ', 'WheelUp'], toolNext: ['Pad5', 'KeyE', 'WheelDown'], wheelHold: ['Mouse2'],\\n  curU: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp'], curD: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown'], curL: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft'], curR: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight'],   // separate from up/down/left/right, which the left stick also presses\\n  nudgeU: ['Pad12'], nudgeD: ['Pad13'], nudgeL: ['Pad14'], nudgeR: ['Pad15'],\\n  tool1: ['Digit1'], tool2: ['Digit2'], tool3: ['Digit3'], tool4: ['Digit4'], tool5: ['Digit5'], tool6: ['Digit6'], tool7: ['Digit7'], tool8: ['Digit8'],\\n  interact: ['Pad0', 'KeyE', 'Enter'], skip: ['Pad2', 'ControlLeft'], log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\\n```\\n350→\\nRead the two sticks from `input.padAim` and `input.padMove`, the trigger from `input.value('useTool')`. Name the actions and hide `tool1` to `tool8` from rebinding through `menu.controls`. Give the scene `camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false }`, because the wheel is the game's.\\n\\n**Prompts.** Always through `game.input.label(action)`, so they follow the device used last and the player's rebinding. Draw a label as a button cap: a rounded rectangle with the label in it, the PlayStation or Xbox face colors on face buttons, and plain keycaps for keys. For the sticks, draw a small stick icon with L or R. Never hard-code a key in text. PlayStation glyphs by default with the Xbox option from fact 5.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Things on the table\\n\\nA registry (`defObject`), each with sim behavior, a draw function kept apart, and a bot plan.\\n360→\\n| Type | Looks like | Fixed by | Vitals/s while open | Other effects |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `shard` | Glass or steel sliver with a glint | Forceps along its axis | .1 | |\\n| `laceration` | Short red cut | Salve | .2 | Small pool over time |\\n| `wound` | Gaping cut with lips | Suture N stitches | .4 | Bleeding falls with each stitch |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":316,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"## 6. Controls and prompts\\n\\nThe keyboard and mouse are native here, not stand-ins for controller buttons: the same game on the same screens, with the keys PC players expect for this kind of game. The mouse is the best pointer in the game, and the pad is the best-feeling couch device.\\n\\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Aim | Right stick. D-pad nudges | Mouse, or WASD or arrows |\\n| Use tool | R2 (analog) or ✕ | Left click or Space |\\n| Fine mode, loupe | L2 | Shift |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick | 1 to 8. Hold Right click and flick |\\n| Step tool | L1, R1 | Q, E, or the wheel |\\n| The Steady | △ | F or Middle click |\\n| Consult | □ | C |\\n| Drop, cancel stroke | ○ | X or Backspace |\\n| Code Blue shock | L2 + R2 | Left click or Space |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc or P |\\n| Ward: walk | Left stick or D-pad | WASD or arrows, or click to walk |\\n| Ward: talk, use | ✕ | E or Enter, or click the person |\\n| Story: advance | ✕ | Enter, Space or click |\\n| Story: fast-forward | Hold □ | Hold Ctrl |\\n| Story: backlog | △ | B |\\n\\nSettings adds **Swap sticks** for left-handers (cursor and wheel trade sticks).\\n\\n```js\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst INPUT = { ...base,\\n  useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], fine: ['Pad6', 'ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight'], gift: ['Pad3', 'KeyF', 'Mouse1'], consult: ['Pad2', 'KeyC'],\\n  toolPrev: ['Pad4', 'KeyQ', 'WheelUp'], toolNext: ['Pad5', 'KeyE', 'WheelDown'], wheelHold: ['Mouse2'],\\n  curU: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp'], curD: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown'], curL: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft'], curR: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight'],   // separate from up/down/left/right, which the left stick also presses\\n  nudgeU: ['Pad12'], nudgeD: ['Pad13'], nudgeL: ['Pad14'], nudgeR: ['Pad15'],\\n  tool1: ['Digit1'], tool2: ['Digit2'], tool3: ['Digit3'], tool4: ['Digit4'], tool5: ['Digit5'], tool6: ['Digit6'], tool7: ['Digit7'], tool8: ['Digit8'],\\n  interact: ['Pad0', 'KeyE', 'Enter'], skip: ['Pad2', 'ControlLeft'], log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\\n```\\n\\nRead the two sticks from `input.padAim` and `input.padMove`, the trigger from `input.value('useTool')`. Name the actions and hide `tool1` to `tool8` from rebinding through `menu.controls`. Give the scene `camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false }`, because the wheel is the game's.\\n\\n**Prompts.** Always through `game.input.label(action)`, so they follow the device used last and the player's rebinding. Draw a label as a button cap: a rounded rectangle with the label in it, the PlayStation or Xbox face colors on face buttons, and plain keycaps for keys. For the sticks, draw a small stick icon with L or R. Never hard-code a key in text. PlayStation glyphs by default with the Xbox option from fact 5.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Things on the table\\n\\nA registry (`defObject`), each with sim behavior, a draw function kept apart, and a bot plan.\\n\\n| Type | Looks like | Fixed by | Vitals/s while open | Other effects |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `shard` | Glass or steel sliver with a glint | Forceps along its axis | .1 | |\\n| `laceration` | Short red cut | Salve | .2 | Small pool over time |\\n| `wound` | Gaping cut with lips | Suture N stitches | .4 | Bleeding falls with each stitch |\\n\",\"total_lines\":1339}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"0b2f6b0b-a3a6-45e8-9613-d3ea741af39b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_123","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Much of the implementation remains.\n\nThe plan is to write a complete game.js using existing engine modules for scenes, story, and audio. I will check the API index for exact methods before guessing. The goal is a bootable game with all scenes, passing tests, and HTML bundling.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-790970f6-0e09-4fed-acd6-2060da18475a-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/game/test.mjs","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-790970f6-0e09-4fed-acd6-2060da18475a-67","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"class Story|Story\\.prototype|this\\.skip|go\\(id|nodes\\[","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-790970f6-0e09-4fed-acd6-2060da18475a-68","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function rankLetter|rankLetter\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":15488,"output_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":157440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"97dfa023-2c9b-413a-baa9-e376149c2884"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-790970f6-0e09-4fed-acd6-2060da18475a-66","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\n\\nconst ctx = { console };\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\\n10→const E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\\nlet failed = 0;\\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\\n\\ngame.advance(.5);\\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n\\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\\n20→// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n\\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n30→game.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n\\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\\ngame.advance(2.5);\\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\\n40→\\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\n\\nconst ctx = { console };\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\\n10→const E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\\nlet failed = 0;\\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\\n\\ngame.advance(.5);\\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n\\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\\n20→// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n\\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n30→game.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n\\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\\ngame.advance(2.5);\\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\\n40→\\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/game/test.mjs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\n\\nconst ctx = { console };\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\\nlet failed = 0;\\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\\n\\ngame.advance(.5);\\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n\\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n\\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\n\\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\\ngame.advance(2.5);\\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\\n\\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"total_lines\":42}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-790970f6-0e09-4fed-acd6-2060da18475a-67","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,48,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,79,112,101,110,45,84,97,98,108,101,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,47,118,101,110,100,111,114,47,109,121,45,51,100,50,100,103,101,47,100,105,115,116,47,104,97,110,100,111,102,102,47,109,121,45,5