50,53,41,44,32,115,105,100,101,32,40,48,41,32,97,110,100,32,111,118,101,114,104,101,97,100,32,40,57,48,44,32,115,99,97,108,101,32,49,58,32,119,111,114,108,100,32,120,47,121,32,61,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,32,112,105,120,101,108,115,41,59,32,110,101,119,32,69,46,71,97,109,101,40,123,32,118,105,101,119,58,32,39,105,115,111,39,32,125,41,32,97,110,100,32,103,97,109,101,46,115,101,116,86,105,101,119,40,39,115,105,100,101,39,41,32,116,97,107,101,32,116,104,101,105,114,32,110,97,109,101,115,10,50,50,57,58,45,32,96,118,105,101,119,46,115,101,116,40,121,97,119,44,32,112,105,116,99,104,44,32,115,99,97,108,101,32,61,32,49,44,32,122,66,111,111,115,116,32,61,32,49,41,96,58,32,99,104,97,110,103,101,32,116,104,101,32,97,110,103,108,101,115,32,97,110,100,32,115,99,97,108,101,32,105,110,32,112,108,97,99,101,32,40,103,97,109,101,46,115,101,116,86,105,101,119,32,97,110,100,32,114,111,116,97,116,101,86,105,101,119,32,117,115,101,32,116,104,101,105,114,32,111,119,110,32,99,111,112,105,101,115,41,59,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,115,32,116,104,101,32,118,105,101,119,10,53,48,54,58,45,32,96,103,97,109,101,46,115,101,116,86,105,101,119,40,118,41,96,58,32,115,119,105,116,99,104,32,116,104,101,32,118,105,101,119,58,32,97,110,32,105,100,32,102,114,111,109,32,69,46,86,73,69,87,83,32,40,39,105,115,111,39,44,32,39,115,105,100,101,39,44,32,46,46,46,41,32,111,114,32,97,32,86,105,101,119,59,32,107,101,101,112,115,32,122,111,111,109,32,97,110,100,32,116,117,114,110,10,53,54,53,58,45,32,96,103,97,109,101,46,118,105,101,119,96,58,32,116,104,101,32,118,105,101,119,32,116,104,101,32,103,97,109,101,32,100,114,97,119,115,32,105,110,32,110,111,119,32,40,116,104,101,32,99,104,111,115,101,110,32,111,110,101,44,32,119,105,116,104,32,122,111,111,109,32,97,110,100,32,116,117,114,110,58,32,114,101,97,100,32,105,116,44,32,99,104,97,110,103,101,32,105,116,32,119,105,116,104,32,115,101,116,86,105,101,119,41,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":4,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":222,\"content\":\"- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\"},{\"line_number\":229,\"content\":\"- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\"},{\"line_number\":506,\"content\":\"- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\"},{\"line_number\":565,\"content\":\"- `game.view`: the view the game draws in now (the chosen one, with zoom and turn: read it, change it with setView)\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"7efd3e30-3123-481b-a620-a86c79171ff2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_158","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Planning camera angles for the game views: side for title, overhead for opponent, three-quarter for ward, and front for story.\n\nStory stages will use side view instead of front, since no front camera exists. Rain weather will be set on the title screen and drawn as a flat overlay. A compact test file is being prepared to cover requirements without being overly long.\n\nA compact test structure is being drafted with a lightweight `check` helper. Bot playthroughs are being evaluated for speed: 11 cases at roughly one second each, but a full story plus bot operations inside the game loop could require thousands of steps.\n\nPlaythroughs would take roughly 26 seconds total, which is acceptable. However, enabling draw mode for every test case would force the game to shade every frame across thousands of frames, making it far too slow. The plan is to set draw: true only in the browser and keep it false in headless mode, while still ensuring at least one test case runs with drawing enabled so errors remain visible.\n\nThe draw flag will be set by checking for the browser document object. In headless mode, the game will skip tissue shading but still render the HUD cheaply with pixels. Tests that need to verify shade errors can force them on for a single frame.\n\nA single test will force shade for one frame to verify errors. Headless mode will skip tissue shading and bake blur unless forced. The field() helper will return a cheap no-op stub in headless mode so draw code does not crash.\n\nThe shade function will be a no-op in headless mode unless forced. Player score will increment on trigger edges when an object completes its action, tracked via `p.actions` and sorted into standings. A `hostStep` function is being drafted to aggregate local and remote player inputs for the simulation.\n\nLocal player inputs will omit x and y coordinates so the cursor position is not overwritten. Remote inputs will include x and y from network messages. The server has no local player, so every client sends input to keep traffic flowing bidirectionally. The host will send snapshots to clients.\n\nClients will send inputs before the six-second play window closes. The host will not call finish on leave; the phase remains active and the round may void if time-up never arrives. The shared world does not need progress tracking, so finish alone is sufficient. Cards will call ready() immediately after connect, before any card events arrive.\n\nThe hub will answer 'ready' when the player presses confirm during the wait phase after the card loads. The server copy will skip drawing but still update and send snapshots. It will not index the local player since info.me is absent there.\n\nHub probe and inject helpers are being exposed on the global object for test access. The probe returns phase, hover state, player positions, and active time. The inject helper lets tests place the cursor directly. Host will apply incoming input messages to the correct seat by matching sender IDs against the player list.\n\nClient input will use the injected cursor if present, otherwise the local hand. The host applies remote inputs to `S.players` immediately, so the simulation state updates before the next snapshot is sent.\n\nThe harness controls the round clock, so injecting a client stroke after two players connect is difficult. A separate short page or custom check may be needed to verify that strokes appear on the host state.\n\nA separate playwright script will be added to hub.py after the four harness runs. It will open the harness, wait for the playing phase, inject a client stroke, read the host probe, and write the result to hub.log. This check will not interfere with harness timing or count toward the test suite.\n\nThe stroke injection check will be folded into the existing players=2 harness run instead of running a separate fifth session. After the round reaches the playing phase, the runner will inject a client stroke and poll the host probe to verify it appears on the host state. This avoids extra time and keeps the test within the controlled hub.py script.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d2f1e72c-6987-4d53-b4ce-4da085677bbe-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"iframe|contentWindow","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/hub/harness.html","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1430,"output_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":135552,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"0e4a205a-bc46-4850-9a03-98d4843aa99d"}
