2,114,111,111,109,115,32,101,110,100,32,119,105,116,104,32,103,97,112,115,32,97,116,32,116,104,101,105,114,32,100,111,111,114,115,44,32,115,97,118,101,32,114,111,111,109,115,32,83,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,98,111,115,115,39,115,32,66,44,32,116,104,101,32,104,101,114,111,39,115,32,99,101,108,108,32,98,108,105,110,107,105,110,103,59,32,111,58,32,123,32,97,108,108,44,32,99,111,108,111,114,44,32,119,97,108,108,44,32,115,97,118,101,44,32,98,111,115,115,32,125,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":2,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API-INDEX.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":763,\"content\":\"- `map.drawFloor(r)`: draw the baked floor (first thing in draw, after r.sky); walls come from queueWalls(r)\"},{\"line_number\":1619,\"content\":\"- `world.drawMap(g, x, y, cell = 6, o = {})`: draw the explored map with its top-left cell at x, y, each cell a square of cell pixels: the seen cells (o.all: every room's), walls where rooms end with gaps at their doors, save rooms S and the boss's B, the hero's cell blinking; o: { all, color, wall, save, boss }\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"ea06a5af-6d03-4bb1-85f9-93596856568b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_164","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Ward will use TileMap and Humanoid.\n\nWard's code sets up a three-quarter view, enables lights, and creates a body and humanoid rig. Movement is driven by input scaled to 46 pixels per second. The rig updates using the hero's current state or position. A proximity check detects when the hero nears the door.\n\nThe near check now uses a 48-pixel radius and spawn is 24 pixels away. Patients will be positioned along the hall.\n\nPeople will be pulled from GAME.WARD[chapter]. Hovering over a person highlights them. Clicking triggers interaction. A case files menu is also planned. The game ID is set to GAME_TITLE. Settings include music volume and a glyph style selector.\n\nSettings now include voice volume, difficulty level, and surgical assist. Voice volume is a slider from 0 to 1. Difficulty offers intern, resident, or attending options. Surgical assist is a slider from 0 to 1.4.\n\nCursor speed is a slider from 80 to 500. A toggle swaps the control sticks. Sustained tools can be set to hold or toggle. Hints are enabled by default. Blood color offers red and muted options.\n\nText speed is added as a slider from 0.5 to 3. Player-assisted tuning will not mark the game dirty, so normal saves can still earn ranks; only dev panel changes do. Rank saving requires both dirty and cheat flags to be false. The music setting will be wired directly to the audio engine.\n\nGlyph labels will be generated dynamically from the current setting. Tests will verify that switching between PlayStation and Xbox modes produces different strings for the same input.\n\nBrowser tests will set the last input device to a pad stub so glyph labels are not confused with keyboard keys. Node tests will only verify the default PlayStation setting and the availability of the Xbox option. A `GAME.playHand` helper will be added for the operator and hub modules. Attract segments will avoid fade issues.\n\nAttract fade lasts 0.22 seconds. Idle time is reset while a shell screen is active, preventing the title scene from counting idle time during settings. Input exits attract mode. Title confirm is suppressed when leaving attract to avoid accidental selection.\n\nThe title scene update clears the suppress flag and returns early to block input for one frame. If the scene switch happens immediately, this prevents the title from reacting to the same frame's input. During a fade-out, the old scene may still update briefly, so attract mode will also check the scene name and exit early.\n\nAttract tests will advance the title scene for over ten seconds without input, then verify the attract screen activates and a tap returns to the title. A fresh game state prevents accidental input during that wait.\n\nDev tuning tests will set patient drain via `GAME.Dev.set`, confirm the value updates, and verify reset restores the original value. The cheat lockVitals flag will block vitals from dropping.\n\nThe menu items list will be checked to ensure it contains Dev Mode.\n\nA bot will play each grand rounds case with four players, difficulty set to resident. The test will verify the bot wins and vitals and clock remain stable. The full playthrough is included in tests even though it may be slow. A fast debug mode could skip the game loop for speed.\n\nThe full playthrough will run at normal speed. The operator scene can use a burst mode to play all eleven cases in one update, but the headless test must always execute it. The --fast flag only skips browser tests.\n\nEleven grand rounds cases total roughly 16,800 steps. The bot device is expensive to scan objects. The full run should take about five to fifteen seconds. Dressing scenes add up to four seconds per case. That adds another forty-four seconds of game time across all cases. The extra time is acceptable. The operator scene could force the dressing trigger once to skip that wait.\n\nThe operator scene will force the dressing trigger once during driver mode so the playthrough skips the four-second wait. Lost cases will fail the test instead of hanging.\n\nA `pump` loop will drive the story playthrough. It taps confirm on choice scenes and advances 0.05 seconds per step. Chart scenes get a mark click. Results, ward, and credits scenes also tap confirm with 0.05 or 0.2 second delays.\n\nThe pump loop will advance 0.25 seconds per step until the title scene appears after one second. The maximum game-time budget is set to 4000 seconds, which equals roughly 480,000 steps at 120 Hz. To keep wall time reasonable, the operator scene may run up to ninety simulation steps per frame during driver mode, clearing about 180 seconds of surgery per update.\n\nThe operator scene will substep thirty simulation steps per advance when debug.driver is active. This clears about thirty seconds of surgery per update and removes most scene overhead.\n\nThe operator scene will substep twenty simulation steps per advance when debug.driver is active. This keeps wall time reasonable while still letting the scene run the simulation. The test driver catches up the operation, not a gameplay fast-forward. Attract mode will keep normal step timing so the reel stays watchable.\n\nThe operator scene will substep twenty-four simulation steps per frame during driver mode, advancing roughly six seconds of surgery per advance(0.25). Eleven grand rounds cases need about seventy such advances plus story time, which runs at normal speed.\n\nThe substep math is verified: roughly 198,000 bot calls during the playthrough should take about ten to forty seconds. A hard timeout will force a loss if a case hangs. Files are being written now.\n\nc10 will run in the background to confirm rank while files are written. Input checks for `anyPressed`, `mouse.t`, and `padAim` nulls are being added. The art file will copy the appendix and add muscle, tendon, brain, heart, and hush materials before `MAT_IDS` is built.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Case 10’s par is already lowered. Next I’ll confirm that rank, then add the field art, audio, and the playable shell on top of the sim."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2cca2e08-0d98-4367-9f6c-5a8f71edb0c5-59","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/play.js c10","description":"Replay case 10 to confirm rank S","block_until_ms":60000}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2cca2e08-0d98-4367-9f6c-5a8f71edb0c5-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":1748,"limit":16}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2793,"output_tokens":4059,"cache_read_input_tokens":150016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"d9ed16b1-2120-47b1-910b-8d0f21bb86b1"}
