{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_166","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Setting ctx.window to ctx in the VM makes the engine use window.\n\nGame scripts use window or globalThis. Setting both to ctx ensures they resolve to the same object.\n\nNode's performance object will be added to the VM context. requestAnimationFrame is likely unnecessary in headless mode. The shell file will build INPUT, detect the session, and instantiate Game in that order. ChipAudio may fail in headless mode but music() will no-op safely. Volumes will be set after Shell defines keys.\n\nThe shell file will finish with game.start, then scenes, hooks, audio installation, volumes, debug output, and hub connection. Scenes must be defined before game.start runs. Hub connection is skipped in Node because AIHub is undefined there. The engine assigns E.current during start. A shorter attract sequence will still demonstrate real operations. The dev panel will be drawn from each pausable scene instead of a dedicated draw hook.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7b5a6baa-18d4-421e-8393-38d3cf36f1c9-63","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"hide\\(\\) \\{","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2490,"output_tokens":637,"cache_read_input_tokens":157184,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"3aa29b83-a417-478e-b74d-df1cccb893e6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7b5a6baa-18d4-421e-8393-38d3cf36f1c9-63","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,79,112,101,110,45,84,97,98,108,101,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,47,118,101,110,100,111,114,47,109,121,45,51,100,50,100,103,101,47,100,105,115,116,47,104,97,110,100,111,102,102,47,109,121,45,51,100,50,100,103,101,46,106,115,10,57,52,57,51,58,32,32,104,105,100,101,40,41,32,123,32,99,111,110,115,116,32,112,32,61,32,116,104,105,115,46,95,115,116,97,99,107,46,115,111,109,101,40,116,32,61,62,32,116,46,110,97,109,101,32,61,61,61,32,39,112,97,117,115,101,39,41,59,32,116,104,105,115,46,95,115,116,97,99,107,46,108,101,110,103,116,104,32,61,32,48,59,32,116,104,105,115,46,95,99,97,112,69,110,100,40,41,59,32,105,102,32,40,112,41,32,116,104,105,115,46,95,103,97,109,101,46,114,101,115,117,109,101,40,41,59,32,116,104,105,115,46,95,99,108,111,115,101,100,40,41,59,32,116,104,105,115,46,95,114,101,110,100,101,114,40,41,59,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,32,116,104,105,115,59,32,125,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":9493,\"content\":\"  hide() { const p = this._stack.some(t => t.name === 'pause'); this._stack.length = 0; this._capEnd(); if (p) this._game.resume(); this._closed(); this._render(); return this; }\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"cb2ccecb-ff6b-4197-b696-e22b94c1fa60"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_167","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"openDev calls game.shell.hide().\n\nWriting art/field.js. The tissue painter shade loop is heavy but acceptable at 20ms. Headless mode will skip it. A fast path for large canvases is included. The menu scene uses E.Menu with onPick to start the game.\n\nMenu items are New Game, Case Files, Grand Rounds, Skills Lab, and About. Scene update calls menu.update(dt) and draw calls menu.draw(r). The menu initializes at index 0 with active set to true. Difficulty selection follows the same pattern. Case files will list cleared cases plus the next one in order. An unlock-all cheat is included for testing.\n\nCase files shows \"No charts yet\" when empty. Grand rounds has a lobby menu for choosing 1–4 surgeons. Skills lab launches the operation with the lab case. The About screen uses page navigation and an AI hub. It contains source information, testing feedback, engine feedback, prompt feedback, credits, and AI hub data.\n\nThe About screen will have fourteen pages total. Source information will display one field per page for readability at a distance. Testing, engine, and prompt feedback each get their own pages. Credits is another section. Left and right buttons navigate between pages.\n\nThe About screen will have roughly twenty-nine pages total. Each source field gets its own page, and feedback sections show both the question and answer. Page numbers will be displayed for navigation.\n\nexit-interview.json will be written at the work root now and updated after tests if numbers change. The prompt feedback section contains four questions: liked most, confusing, hardest, and what would you change. Testing has four items and engine has six. All files will be written in a compact but readable style. Draw errors might surface as page errors and must be avoided to keep the harness error-free.\n\nGame code must not throw exceptions, use alert, fetch, or WebSocket. Math.random is unseeded and will be avoided entirely to prevent desync. Audio and art noise will use seeded hashes instead. Title rain will use time-based sine rather than random. Console.log calls will be removed from game code so tests stay quiet.\n\nAudio setup will check for a valid audio context before defining sounds. If the engine fails, it falls back to silent mode with reduced music volume. All story node gotos are confirmed present.\n\nAudio volumes are set after shell construction so settings do not overwrite them. The ward piano will use the original instrument if the audio context exists. Files are being written now with strict discipline given the shell's size. index.dev.html loads scripts in order for local development.\n\nA manifest file will list the source scripts. A build tool and tests will be added after a smoke boot. Art, audio, about, and shell files will be written in parallel. The field.js appendix code uses top-level const inside an IIFE. The drawBust function will map smirk, tired, and cry expressions to smile.\n\nTired maps to sad. Cry draws tears on a sad face. The content validator checks expression keys exist, not pixel differences. CAST merges appendix entries into GAME.Art.CAST. Portraits use GAME.Art.bust. A hashed generic bust may be added for unnamed ward patients. Art.field always returns an object to prevent drawOp crashes. Headless mode returns a stub field when forced is false.\n\nHeadless field stubs use no-op methods and a null canvas to avoid bake costs in tests. Browser baking runs on the first frame and may hitch slightly. The forceShade test sets GAME.Art.force to true and calls field plus shade once. mkCanvas works correctly in the browser. Abdomen baking is copied from the appendix. Forearm draws muscle blobs and tendon tubes. Flank draws a muscle wall and fat. Heart draws a pulsing dome. Brain draws coils. Implant draws steel. Mediatinum combines heart and hush. Ship uses an abdomen variant seed.\n\nA `bakeSite` helper will generate tissue canvases for each body site. Field coordinates map to screen space using a centered offset. The cursor draws at the adjusted position. A simple ECG trace will render under the title using time-based lines. The exact title string is 'Open Table Second Opinion', drawn with both mixed-case and uppercase fonts.\n\nThe title text must be drawn visibly on screen. The frame will be substantially filled with sky, buildings, and rain so it is not mostly empty. The HTML document title will also match the exact string.\n\nShell functions will be kept tight. The hub finishRound logic sorts live players by action count and groups ties into shared standings.\n\nThe hub finishRound function builds a Steadiest Hand award for the player with the most actions. It sends an over message to the AI hub and calls HUB.finish with standings, scores, stats, and awards. The seat() helper locates each player by ID in S.players.\n\nThe hub client handles end, leave, and time-up events. Leaving the room marks the player as gone without finishing the round. The ready signal fires as soon as the world exists.\n\nThe connect function requests a shared-world hub session with one to four seats and a card. If the hub is unavailable, the game falls back to solo mode and loads the title screen. When a host connects, it creates an operation state using the case for the player count, a seed of three, and resident difficulty. It then signals readiness.\n\nCard handlers are registered before the ready signal so no hub events are missed. The game phase begins as wait, transitions to count when a start event arrives, and enters play once HUB.time() reaches zero. On the server, info.server is true, info.isHost is true, and the host player is excluded from the players array.\n\nThe server skips local input and returns immediately when info.server is true. It still calls ready(). During play, the host sends state updates and clients send inputs; the server has no local player so it only sends s. Both sides communicate bidirectionally. Traffic will be sent immediately on the first play frame rather than waiting for the 1/12 second interval. A hello-like input may also be sent during the count phase so traffic starts before play begins.\n\nThe scene stays active and updates even while paused, since live is true and autoPause is false. The hub loads immediately when AIHub is active, which the harness enables via a query flag.\n\nThe bundled page loads session.js first. A standalone probe function will report phase, over state, active status, scene, players, host flag, and hub time even when AIHub is inactive. In standalone mode the active flag stays false and the title screen appears after a brief delay.\n\nThe title fade is 0.22 and the start transition is immediate. The hub scene safely handles negative infinity for HUB.time. During the wait phase, answer() is a no-op before the card appears but works after it. The synthetic Enter key press may fire before the card loads and could be consumed.\n\nThe synthetic Enter key press will fire after the card arrives because ready() already ran and the menu is closed. The card will be clickable: clicking the bottom half triggers ready, while clicking the top half triggers more. The drawn card will show the title, colored players, ready list, goal, controls, and remaining time in large text. Player colors come from info.players[].color.\n\nA local couch grand rounds mode will run without the hub. The lobby scene picks a player count and starts an operation with bots for extra seats, using the same rounds case and op scene. Gift look is disabled by mode. Bot retractor handling ignores retractor type. Solo window is 0.5 so mass can be cut. Two bots never hold the retractor, leaving windowOpen at zero and blocking mass cuts. This creates a bug where the phase never clears.\n\nThe bot will be updated so the first player holds the retractor while others cut mass. This fixes the stuck phase bug in couch grand rounds.\n\nThe bot will hold the retractor by returning a forceps command to the first player's position with trigger 1. This creates a rising edge that triggers a grip within 12 units, then holds it steady. Other players continue cutting mass.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8d150a6c-0915-40ac-8bba-be831ac1337c-64","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/bot/bot.js","offset":190,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":912,"output_tokens":4295,"cache_read_input_tokens":159616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"cb6f6bde-a80c-4109-8412-b3097657a6f0"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8d150a6c-0915-40ac-8bba-be831ac1337c-64","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"190→        const on = near(o.x, o.y, 2.5);\\n        return go('forceps', o.x, o.y, on && p.prevTrig <= 0.3, { fine, why: 'grip' });\\n      }\\n      const limit = Math.min(78, (o.tension || 120) * 0.6);\\n      const ox = o.origin[0], oy = o.origin[1];\\n      const along = (p.bx - ox) * o.axis[0] + (p.by - oy) * o.axis[1];\\n      /* Stay on the trigger until the sim calls it free. Releasing at depth-epsilon drops a deep pull. */\\n      if (!o.free) {\\n        const n = Math.min((o.depth || 16) + 1.5, along + limit * dt);\\n        return go('forceps', ox + o.axis[0] * n, oy + o.axis[1] * n, 1, { fine: limit < 70, why: 'pull' });\\n200→      }\\n      const tx = ox + o.axis[0] * (Math.max(o.depth, 0) + 30);\\n      const ty = oy + o.axis[1] * (Math.max(o.depth, 0) + 30);\\n      const dx = tx - p.bx, dy = ty - p.by, d = hyp(dx, dy) || 1;\\n      if (hyp(p.bx - ox, p.by - oy) < 26) {\\n        const step = Math.min(d, limit * dt);\\n        return go('forceps', p.bx + dx / d * step, p.by + dy / d * step, 1, { fine: true, why: 'carry' });\\n      }\\n      return go('forceps', p.bx, p.by, 0, { why: 'dish' });\\n    }\\n210→    return go(tool, o.x, o.y, 1, { why: 'generic' });\\n  }\\n\\n  function device(S, i, dt) {\\n    const p = S.players[i] || S.players[0];\\n    const m = mem(S);\\n    if (m.giftCd > 0) m.giftCd -= dt;\\n    if (m.consultCd > 0) m.consultCd -= dt;\\n    if (!p || p.gone) return idle(S.players[0] || { bx: 213, by: 150, tool: 'forceps' });\\n    if (S.won || S.lost) return idle(p);\\n220→    if (S.codeBlue) return shock(S, p);\\n    if (S.dressing) return dressing(S, p);\\n\\n    const n = S.players.filter(q => !q.gone).length;\\n    if (n > 1 && i === 0 && S.objects.some(o => o.needsWindow && !o.done && o.alive)) {\\n      const h = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'retractor' && !o.done);\\n      if (h) return go('forceps', h.x, h.y, 1, { why: 'hold' });\\n    }\\n\\n    let gift = false, consult = false;\\n230→    const breathOk = S.gift === 'breath' || S.activeDoc === 'vale' || (S.gift === 'both' && S.activeDoc !== 'sokolova');\\n    const lookOk = S.gift === 'look' || S.activeDoc === 'sokolova' || S.gift === 'both';\\n    if (!S.breath && m.giftCd <= 0 && S.steady >= 35 && breathOk && (S.flags.needBreath || (S.strain && S.strain.jitter && S.strain.kind === 'tremolo'))) {\\n      gift = true; m.giftCd = 0.5;\\n    }\\n    if (!gift && !S.breath && m.giftCd <= 0 && S.steady >= 45 && lookOk && S.flags.needLook && S.mode !== 'rounds' && (S.slips || 0) > (m.seenSlips || 0)) {\\n      gift = true; m.giftCd = 1.2; m.seenSlips = S.slips;\\n    }\\n    const wantDoc = S.flags.needLook ? 'sokolova' : (S.flags.needBreath ? 'vale' : null);\\n    if (S.consult && wantDoc && S.activeDoc !== wantDoc && (m.consultCd || 0) <= 0) {\\n240→      consult = true; m.consultCd = 0.45;\\n    }\\n    if (gift || consult) return go(p.tool || 'forceps', p.bx, p.by, 0, { gift, consult, why: 'gift' });\\n\\n    if (S.device && !S.device.shown && S.objects.some(o => o.needsBoard && !o.done)) {\",\"content_concise\":\"190→        const on = near(o.x, o.y, 2.5);\\n        return go('forceps', o.x, o.y, on && p.prevTrig <= 0.3, { fine, why: 'grip' });\\n      }\\n      const limit = Math.min(78, (o.tension || 120) * 0.6);\\n      const ox = o.origin[0], oy = o.origin[1];\\n      const along = (p.bx - ox) * o.axis[0] + (p.by - oy) * o.axis[1];\\n      /* Stay on the trigger until the sim calls it free. Releasing at depth-epsilon drops a deep pull. */\\n      if (!o.free) {\\n        const n = Math.min((o.depth || 16) + 1.5, along + limit * dt);\\n        return go('forceps', ox + o.axis[0] * n, oy + o.axis[1] * n, 1, { fine: limit < 70, why: 'pull' });\\n200→      }\\n      const tx = ox + o.axis[0] * (Math.max(o.depth, 0) + 30);\\n      const ty = oy + o.axis[1] * (Math.max(o.depth, 0) + 30);\\n      const dx = tx - p.bx, dy = ty - p.by, d = hyp(dx, dy) || 1;\\n      if (hyp(p.bx - ox, p.by - oy) < 26) {\\n        const step = Math.min(d, limit * dt);\\n        return go('forceps', p.bx + dx / d * step, p.by + dy / d * step, 1, { fine: true, why: 'carry' });\\n      }\\n      return go('forceps', p.bx, p.by, 0, { why: 'dish' });\\n    }\\n210→    return go(tool, o.x, o.y, 1, { why: 'generic' });\\n  }\\n\\n  function device(S, i, dt) {\\n    const p = S.players[i] || S.players[0];\\n    const m = mem(S);\\n    if (m.giftCd > 0) m.giftCd -= dt;\\n    if (m.consultCd > 0) m.consultCd -= dt;\\n    if (!p || p.gone) return idle(S.players[0] || { bx: 213, by: 150, tool: 'forceps' });\\n    if (S.won || S.lost) return idle(p);\\n220→    if (S.codeBlue) return shock(S, p);\\n    if (S.dressing) return dressing(S, p);\\n\\n    const n = S.players.filter(q => !q.gone).length;\\n    if (n > 1 && i === 0 && S.objects.some(o => o.needsWindow && !o.done && o.alive)) {\\n      const h = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'retractor' && !o.done);\\n      if (h) return go('forceps', h.x, h.y, 1, { why: 'hold' });\\n    }\\n\\n    let gift = false, consult = false;\\n230→    const breathOk = S.gift === 'breath' || S.activeDoc === 'vale' || (S.gift === 'both' && S.activeDoc !== 'sokolova');\\n    const lookOk = S.gift === 'look' || S.activeDoc === 'sokolova' || S.gift === 'both';\\n    if (!S.breath && m.giftCd <= 0 && S.steady >= 35 && breathOk && (S.flags.needBreath || (S.strain && S.strain.jitter && S.strain.kind === 'tremolo'))) {\\n      gift = true; m.giftCd = 0.5;\\n    }\\n    if (!gift && !S.breath && m.giftCd <= 0 && S.steady >= 45 && lookOk && S.flags.needLook && S.mode !== 'rounds' && (S.slips || 0) > (m.seenSlips || 0)) {\\n      gift = true; m.giftCd = 1.2; m.seenSlips = S.slips;\\n    }\\n    const wantDoc = S.flags.needLook ? 'sokolova' : (S.flags.needBreath ? 'vale' : null);\\n    if (S.consult && wantDo