{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_178","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9e6e7d31-8441-4050-ad52-c29d7ba67294-77","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":1129,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":779,"output_tokens":110,"cache_read_input_tokens":179456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"449d8605-001a-4074-9bac-0977429daa23"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9e6e7d31-8441-4050-ad52-c29d7ba67294-77","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1129→  function stepCantor(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n1130→    st.t += dt;\\n    if (st.move === 1) {\\n      /* tendrils then uvulas, objects already spawned by the phase */\\n      const left = S.objects.filter(o => (o.tag === 'tendril' || o.tag === 'uvula') && !o.done);\\n      if (!left.length) { st.move = 2; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = true; pushEv(S, ['movement', 2]); spawnVoice(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 2) {\\n      S.flags.hush = true;\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 1);\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'voice') o.window = st.beat > 0.62;\\n      if (st.domes) {\\n1140→        for (const d of st.domes) d.t -= dt;\\n        st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n      }\\n      st.jitter = true;\\n      const voices = S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'voice' && !o.done);\\n      if (!voices.length) { st.move = 3; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = false; st.signs = 0; pushEv(S, ['movement', 3]); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 3) {\\n      st.cycleT = (st.cycleT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (!st.winding && st.cycleT >= 20) { st.winding = 3; st.cycleT = 0; openRepeat(S, st); }\\n      if (st.winding > 0) {\\n1150→        st.winding -= dt;\\n        if (st.winding <= 0) {\\n          const sign = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n          if (sign && !sign.done) {\\n            forceRewind(S, true);\\n            const now = S.strain;\\n            if (now) now.rewound = (now.rewound || 0) + 1;\\n          } else if (sign && sign.done) {\\n            st.signs = (st.signs || 0) + 1;\\n            sign.tag = 'repeat-spent';\\n1160→          }\\n          st.winding = 0;\\n          closeRepeat(S);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if ((st.signs || 0) >= 6 && S.strain === st) { st.move = 4; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; pushEv(S, ['movement', 4]); spawnCoda(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 4) {\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 0.8) / 0.8;\\n      S.flags.onBeat = st.beat < 0.25;\\n      const spiral = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'spiral' && o.tag === 'last-note');\\n1170→      const note = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'the-note');\\n      const wound = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'final-wound');\\n      if (spiral && spiral.done && !st.noteOut) {\\n        st.noteOut = true;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: 213, y: 116, axis: [0, -1], depth: 36, tension: 80, order: 2, tag: 'the-note', drain: 0 });\\n      }\\n      if (note && note.done && !wound) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'wound', x: 213, y: 130, stitches: 6, order: 3, tag: 'final-wound', drain: 0.3 });\\n      }\",\"content_concise\":\"1129→  function stepCantor(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n1130→    st.t += dt;\\n    if (st.move === 1) {\\n      /* tendrils then uvulas, objects already spawned by the phase */\\n      const left = S.objects.filter(o => (o.tag === 'tendril' || o.tag === 'uvula') && !o.done);\\n      if (!left.length) { st.move = 2; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = true; pushEv(S, ['movement', 2]); spawnVoice(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 2) {\\n      S.flags.hush = true;\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 1);\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'voice') o.window = st.beat > 0.62;\\n      if (st.domes) {\\n1140→        for (const d of st.domes) d.t -= dt;\\n        st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n      }\\n      st.jitter = true;\\n      const voices = S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'voice' && !o.done);\\n      if (!voices.length) { st.move = 3; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = false; st.signs = 0; pushEv(S, ['movement', 3]); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 3) {\\n      st.cycleT = (st.cycleT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (!st.winding && st.cycleT >= 20) { st.winding = 3; st.cycleT = 0; openRepeat(S, st); }\\n      if (st.winding > 0) {\\n1150→        st.winding -= dt;\\n        if (st.winding <= 0) {\\n          const sign = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n          if (sign && !sign.done) {\\n            forceRewind(S, true);\\n            const now = S.strain;\\n            if (now) now.rewound = (now.rewound || 0) + 1;\\n          } else if (sign && sign.done) {\\n            st.signs = (st.signs || 0) + 1;\\n            sign.tag = 'repeat-spent';\\n1160→          }\\n          st.winding = 0;\\n          closeRepeat(S);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if ((st.signs || 0) >= 6 && S.strain === st) { st.move = 4; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; pushEv(S, ['movement', 4]); spawnCoda(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 4) {\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 0.8) / 0.8;\\n      S.flags.onBeat = st.beat < 0.25;\\n      const spiral = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'spiral' && o.tag === 'last-note');\\n1170→      const note = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'the-note');\\n      const wound = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'final-wound');\\n      if (spiral && spiral.done && !st.noteOut) {\\n        st.noteOut = true;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: 213, y: 116, axis: [0, -1], depth: 36, tension: 80, order: 2, tag: 'the-note', drain: 0 });\\n      }\\n      if (note && note.done && !wound) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'wound', x: 213, y: 130, stitches: 6, order: 3, tag: 'final-wound', drain: 0.3 });\\n      }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":1129,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  function stepCantor(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    if (st.move === 1) {\\n      /* tendrils then uvulas, objects already spawned by the phase */\\n      const left = S.objects.filter(o => (o.tag === 'tendril' || o.tag === 'uvula') && !o.done);\\n      if (!left.length) { st.move = 2; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = true; pushEv(S, ['movement', 2]); spawnVoice(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 2) {\\n      S.flags.hush = true;\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 1);\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'voice') o.window = st.beat > 0.62;\\n      if (st.domes) {\\n        for (const d of st.domes) d.t -= dt;\\n        st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n      }\\n      st.jitter = true;\\n      const voices = S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'voice' && !o.done);\\n      if (!voices.length) { st.move = 3; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = false; st.signs = 0; pushEv(S, ['movement', 3]); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 3) {\\n      st.cycleT = (st.cycleT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (!st.winding && st.cycleT >= 20) { st.winding = 3; st.cycleT = 0; openRepeat(S, st); }\\n      if (st.winding > 0) {\\n        st.winding -= dt;\\n        if (st.winding <= 0) {\\n          const sign = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n          if (sign && !sign.done) {\\n            forceRewind(S, true);\\n            const now = S.strain;\\n            if (now) now.rewound = (now.rewound || 0) + 1;\\n          } else if (sign && sign.done) {\\n            st.signs = (st.signs || 0) + 1;\\n            sign.tag = 'repeat-spent';\\n          }\\n          st.winding = 0;\\n          closeRepeat(S);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if ((st.signs || 0) >= 6 && S.strain === st) { st.move = 4; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; pushEv(S, ['movement', 4]); spawnCoda(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 4) {\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 0.8) / 0.8;\\n      S.flags.onBeat = st.beat < 0.25;\\n      const spiral = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'spiral' && o.tag === 'last-note');\\n      const note = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'the-note');\\n      const wound = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'final-wound');\\n      if (spiral && spiral.done && !st.noteOut) {\\n        st.noteOut = true;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: 213, y: 116, axis: [0, -1], depth: 36, tension: 80, order: 2, tag: 'the-note', drain: 0 });\\n      }\\n      if (note && note.done && !wound) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'wound', x: 213, y: 130, stitches: 6, order: 3, tag: 'final-wound', drain: 0.3 });\\n      }\\n\",\"total_lines\":1762}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"81622857-0a0c-4c91-94b1-d3caf84c4ead"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_179","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Starting a Cantor rewind test using `createRaw`.\n\nStepping the cantor strain to fill the ring. After 3.1 seconds, forceRewind should trigger if the sign is incomplete. This restores worldT and increments rewound.\n\nforceRewind restores the strain from core, so rewound is initially undefined. The code then sets rewound to 1 on the restored object. If the ring is empty, forceRewind returns false but the counter still increments.\n\nThe test will record worldT before the 3-second wait and assert it drops below the starting value after rewind. A successful strain is detected when a bot plays on a case that contains it.\n\nAll 11 bot plays will be included in the test. They total roughly one second of wall time, so duplicating the full case bot is acceptable. The game playthrough will use substeps to stay under the 120Hz limit. diffClock needs verification for the vitals test numbers, though inequalities should suffice.\n\nPreparing to write the shell, art, audio, about, manifest, and build files. A tiny boot test will run before the full suite. The shell.js structure is being finalized. Key bugs to avoid include game.go during startup, duplicate story creation, null checks on RT.op, and menu recreation on every enter to reset the cursor. Tests will set fadeTime to zero at startup for instant transitions.\n\nWhen `debug.skipStory` is active, the story enters with `story.skip = true`.\n\nThe chart logic checks for a lightbox before entering `op`. Cases without one go straight to `op`. Cases with one enter the chart first. Chart success sets `chartDone` and then calls `beginOp`. After `op` finishes, results confirm and resume the story to the next node.\n\nA sticky `chartDone` flag would prevent later lightboxes from triggering the chart. The fix is to use `RT.chartFor === caseId` instead, so the chart only runs when the current case differs from the last one that completed it. After a successful chart, `RT.chartFor` is set to the current case ID before entering `op`. The `onWard` function is also being drafted.\n\nWard resumes the story on exit. Credits resume to play the epilogue, then return to the title once the story ends. The Story onDone callback is passed per run() instead of being global.\n\n`bootStory` creates the story with `onOp`, `onWard`, and `onCredits` callbacks, then runs it from start. Its `onDone` callback sets `clearedStory` to true and returns to the title. During credits, resuming to the epilogue triggers that callback while the credits scene is still active, which is fine. When choices exist, tapping confirm selects the first choice by default.\n\nThe dialog choice cursor starts at index zero. Story scenes call `story.update(dt)`, so skipped lines advance automatically while choices pause for input. The playthrough will begin at the title screen, then select Resident from the difficulty menu.\n\nThe menu order will be Resident, Intern, Attending so the test can confirm immediately on the first item. The title screen lists New Game, Case Files, Grand Rounds, Skills Lab, and About, with New Game selected by default. The attract test must start from a fresh title scene to avoid interference.\n\nThe snapshot function will store the menu index, label strings, story node, active choices, and OP state including vitals, clock, rank, score, phase, and phase name.\n\nThe snapshot will also record the dev menu state, lightbox marker, ward info, and game title. The choice flag is derived from `RT.story.talk.choices.length` to handle any property name differences. Ward info is being drafted next.\n\nWard info will store patient names, a near-door flag set when distance is under 36 pixels, and the door coordinates. The player spawns near the door so the near-door state is true immediately for testing. Save flags are enabled on ward entry and disabled on exit. Rank records are saved only on victory when the tune is clean and no cheat was used; otherwise a dev tag marks the result. Ready to write the code in comment-free style.\n\nThe audio renderProbe will use an offline context so the browser test can measure the choir. The live choir connects to the sfx bus. A new `GAME.Audio.levels()` helper will return configured volumes for node tests. The shell file is being written in full. Keyboard input for OP events is also being drafted.\n\nThe `readLocal` input handler checks for a debug driver first, then falls back to the bot device. It reads the mouse pointer relative to the screen origin, swaps aim and move axes based on settings, and initializes a digit variable.\n\nThe `readLocal` input handler now maps tool selection to digits 1 through 8, cycling with prev and next keys. It reads directional inputs for keys and nudge axes, and returns the full input state including fine mode and trigger.\n\nThe `readLocal` input handler now also captures gift, consult, and cancel keys. A wheel-hold mode is added: when mouse2 is held and the pointer moves more than eight pixels from the press origin, the delta normalizes into a move vector.\n\nThe `drive` function now accepts a `hands` array to supply per-player device inputs. It assigns the first player's hand directly when provided, otherwise falls back to bot devices, debug drivers, attract mode, or default zero inputs. Each player's device is then passed to `GAME.Wheel.update`.\n\nThe `drive` function now updates the cursor for each player and collects tool, trigger, gift, consult, cancel, and mouse states into an inputs array. That array is passed to `GAME.Op.step`. Solo stories use one player. The test driver supplies input only for player zero; extra players fall back to bots. Attract mode uses bots for all players and applies cheats. If a debug driver is active, it overrides the attract bot for player zero.\n\nThe update loop runs 24 substeps per frame when a debug driver is active, otherwise one. Each substep reads input and drives the game. The loop exits early if the OP ends in victory or defeat. Afterward, the scene transitions to results. In results, pressing confirm resumes the story only when `RT.after` is `'story'`.\n\nThe story node sequence `{ event: 'op', wait: true }, { goto: 'c1_out' }` is two separate steps. The event step fires without a goto target, so the story remains held until the next step advances it. This means the OP event's resume callback must run after the ward scene, not from the results screen.\n\nThe story resumes from results by calling `story.resume()`, which advances to the `c1_out` step and plays its dialogue before the ward event fires. The full flow is: OP, results, resume to `c1_out`, ward scene, then resume to `c2_in`.\n\nThe results confirm handler will first switch to the story scene, then call `resume()` so the dialog opens before the scene updates. If no story is held, it returns to the menu instead. The `_held` flag is not cleared by `resume()` before the scene change, and since `c1_out` contains dialogue lines, the resume will advance through them rather than jumping straight to the ward event.\n\nThe results confirm handler should call `story.resume()` before switching to the story scene. This prevents an immediate ward jump from clobbering the scene change, since `resume()` can fire the ward event right away when no lines remain.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2ba7c7a9-358d-47ba-9cc3-747be63eafba-78","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"go\\(name|this\\._next =|_enter\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1043,"output_tokens":4408,"cache_read_input_tokens":180224,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"88e60efa-da41-4cee-b118-a4ec99173a22"}
