{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_181","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"game.go with fadeTime 0 sets _next and enters at the start of the next step rather than immediately.\n\nsceneName only changes on the next advance. Calling go twice in one update overwrites _next. The plan is to check if story.resume() set a redirect flag, and if not, fall back to game.go('story').\n\nThe redirect flag is set inside onWard and checked after resume. The story scene stays idle when not running or held. After resuming, the dialog remains open and story.update handles the next step. For a new game, bootStory runs first, then skip is enabled before story.run so the opening line is fast.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d7d9ba61-144f-421d-9451-bfa21e1f74e5-80","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"get W\\(\\)|this\\.W =","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":10}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2052,"output_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":185984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"ea7d2420-f5b3-474c-b9e8-fdff1e849b66"}
