32,101,108,115,101,32,110,117,108,108,32,42,47,10,49,49,49,52,45,32,32,100,111,117,98,108,101,84,97,112,40,41,32,123,32,114,101,116,117,114,110,32,116,104,105,115,46,95,116,97,112,50,65,116,59,32,125,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1106,\"content\":\"  pointer() { return this._fedAt || (this.mouse.active ? this.screenPoint(this.mouse.cx, this.mouse.cy) : null); }\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"908bfa4a-43ad-4a22-a0c0-50e1e5408b05"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_183","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"screenPoint converts to buffer pixels.\n\nclicked() returns position. I'll use both clicked and feed. Writing all files in one batch now. about.js will include full interview data. exit-interview.json will be written directly at the work root so build can overwrite it from the same source. The test runner's playthrough is too slow. A debug.fast flag should help.\n\nStory updates are paused during operator mode. The test runner will verify that choices populate correctly. Confirm taps will only trigger when a choice is actually visible.\n\nA fallback will tap confirm if the story stalls on a choice for two seconds. Menu and scene input won't conflict. Camera zoom and wheel are disabled in all scenes.\n\nWard and lobby camera angles are set. Operator and ward scenes will use game.focus. The art file will include appendix code, instruments, stage, and tool wheel icons. Tool drawing stays simple with pixel primitives. The wheel renders during operator mode when the move stick or wheel is held. Files will be written now. PROGRESS.md will be updated at the end.\n\nnotes/feedback.md will record nine pre-shell issues caught by tests, seven of them game-breaking. The perfect-bot playthrough was the most helpful input; the Node NO_COLOR warning was the least. C3 vitals are already at 46, so no fix is needed there. I will be careful with nulls while writing files to avoid shell bugs.\n\nHeadless tests will verify draw errors by calling Art.field directly with force enabled. Creating a second Game instance would replace E.current and break the running game, so that approach is avoided. Scene draw errors will instead be caught by a flag set during the playthrough.\n\nThe game will always be constructed with draw: true so draw errors are caught. Headless tests will shade only once per frame, even during substepping, and only when forced or not headless.\n\nA unit test will bake a small 160x90 field and shade it to catch draw errors. The playthrough will shade one operator case with force enabled. Vector draw errors will be checked after the run.\n\nA `beginCase` helper will jump straight to operator mode for quick testing. It creates an operator scene from a case definition and routes back to the menu. Tests will call it with zero fade, force draw enabled, and a brief advance to verify no draw errors occur.\n\n`beginCase` will be exported for quick dev jumps. The title scene will call `GAME.Art.backdrop(g, W, H, time)`. Overlay drawing after `drawImage` requires a canvas reset to clear the internal context buffer. Title rain will use short pixel line segments. Music switching will be made safe so it never throws.\n\nA `play` function will switch songs safely, skipping if audio is missing or already playing. It will catch exceptions so browser errors cannot crash the harness. Notes will be kept simple to avoid invalid syntax. Choir will start during the hush and final songs and stop otherwise, routed through the sfx bus.\n\nThe choir function will use three sawtooth oscillators at 196 Hz with 0.04 gain, routed through the sfx bus and wrapped in a stop method that catches exceptions. A `letter` voice function is also being drafted for individual letter sounds.\n\nThe `letter` voice function generates a triangle-wave oscillator at a frequency derived from the character code, with a 6 ms gain ramp and 0.06 s duration, routed through the voice bus. Formant filters will be added if the browser supports biquad filters.\n\nTwo bandpass filters will be added for vowel sounds, wrapped in a try block so the simple oscillator still plays if the browser lacks biquad support. An offline renderProbe will compute RMS levels for effects, voice, choir, and music to drive audio feedback. Music gain is set to 0.1 while effect gain stays at 0.8, so music RMS should remain below half the effect level. The shell will assign game.settings.music to 0.1 and verify the engine exposes it as either settings.music or audio.musicVolume.\n\nCONTENT.md will be added. build.mjs will escape closing script tags. Harness files and game.html will be copied to the dev folder root so the server can serve them directly. session.js will be pasted verbatim as the first script. A simple body with canvas is enough for the boot splash. The page title, meta hub tags, and appendix CSS will be included.\n\nThe shell will be written as a single file, splitting only if it becomes too large. The dev panel and attract mode will be included in that same file. An attract reel is being drafted with timed segments: six seconds of story, followed by three operator cases (c1, c3, c6) each lasting twelve to fifteen seconds with cheat mode enabled.\n\nThe attract reel will loop and include operator case c11. Story segments will auto-skip. Input during attract returns to title without saving. A DEMO ribbon will render in the draw loop. The test will advance 10.5 seconds to guarantee the idle timer hits ten seconds and triggers attract.\n\nThe idle timer will ignore synthetic mouse input by recording the initial mouse timestamp on the first hook call and only counting subsequent changes. This prevents the engine from falsely registering input during startup. The attract reel will not trigger during the title scene's first frames before the ten-second idle threshold is reached.\n\nOpening the settings screen resets the idle timer. The about scene is intentionally excluded from input watching. Browser tests will use Python's synchronous Playwright API instead of Node, avoiding an npm install in the dev folder. Node will handle unit tests. The fast runner skips browser checks, while the full runner can spawn Python and swallow its output.\n\nBrowser tests will run separately from unit tests, spawned one at a time by the full runner. The verification plan requires running these steps manually, so I will write and execute the scripts directly. For the launch test, the viewport is set to 1920x1080 on file:// with Chromium, using two screenshots and a 480x270 buffer. To read the canvas dimensions in the browser, I will evaluate `My3D2dge.current.W` because the game object is not globally exposed.\n\nThe title string will be written to document.title and possibly the canvas. A snapshot helper will be exposed on window.__ot for tests. The art file will be complete but its shade function copied exactly. Materials are computed at load time, so adding them before MAT_IDS is safe. The bust draw function closes over E = My3D2dge at load time.\n\nThe eight cast members are Vale, Quill, Oyelaran, Sokolova, Percy, Odalys, Hale, and Clementine. A unit test will verify that drawBust does not throw for every expression on each character by using a mock overlay context from mkCanvas, where E.px no-ops safely.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Case 10 now clears at rank S (score 2613, vitals 70, clock 239). I’m adding the field, sound, and the scene shell next."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-74d8f9e8-a069-4c8a-b052-f32ece29f80c-82","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/art/field.js","new_string":"/* Tissue, sites, busts, instruments, and the title stage. Drawing never writes the sim. */\n(() => {\n  const E = My3D2dge;\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\n\n  const BAYER = [0, 8, 2, 10, 12, 4, 14, 6, 3, 11, 1, 9, 15, 7, 13, 5].map(v => (v + 0.5) / 16 - 0.5);\n  const hex3 = h => [parseInt(h.slice(1, 3), 16), parseInt(h.slice(3, 5), 16), parseInt(h.slice(5, 7), 16)];\n  function makeRamp(keys, n, slow) {\n    const c = keys.map(hex3), out = new Uint32Array(n);\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n      const t = i / (n - 1) * (c.length - 1), j = Math.min(c.length - 2, t | 0), f = t - j;\n      let r = c[j][0] + (c[j + 1][0] - c[j][0]) * f, g = c[j][1] + (c[j + 1][1] - c[j][1]) * f, b = c[j][2] + (c[j + 1][2] - c[j][2]) * f;\n      if (slow) { const y = r * 0.3 + g * 0.59 + b * 0.11; r = y * 0.55 + 8; g = y * 0.95 + 14; b = y * 1.05 + 22; }\n      out[i] = 0xff000000 | (Math.min(255, b) << 16) | (Math.min(255, g) << 8) | Math.min(255, r);\n    }\n    return out;\n  }\n  const MAT_KEYS = {\n    wall: [['#1c060c', '#4a0f18', '#7d1f26', '#a93a38'], 0.35],\n    bowel: [['#3a0e1c', '#8a2f3e', '#c75f62', '#eb9486', '#ffc9b0'], 1],\n    liver: [['#1e0610', '#4e1022', '#7c1e30', '#a83a42', '#d0645c'], 0.55],\n    fat: [['#5a3a10', '#a8782a', '#dcb34c', '#f4d97e', '#fff2b8'], 0.7],\n    vessel: [['#14103a', '#2c2a70', '#4a4aa0', '#7c78c8'], 0.8],\n    artery: [['#3a0408', '#8c0f14', '#cf2a22', '#f4604a'], 1],\n    skin: [['#6a3a22', '#a8683f', '#d39a68', '#eebf92'], 0.12],\n    drape: [['#0c2c2a', '#14504a', '#1f7468', '#2f9a88'], 0],\n    steel: [['#28303a', '#5a6a78', '#9aaab8', '#e8f0f8'], 1.6],\n    blood: [['#180204', '#3c060a', '#680c10', '#8e1414'], 1.4],\n    wound: [['#0c0104', '#2a0408', '#55090e', '#7a1216'], 0.5],\n    char: [['#08070a', '#1c181a', '#332a28', '#4a3c34'], 0],\n    gel: [['#0c4a38', '#1c8a64', '#54d0a0', '#b0ffe0'], 1.4],\n    muscle: [['#4a1820', '#8a3038', '#c45a58', '#e88878'], 0.4],\n    tendon: [['#c8b89a', '#e4d2b0', '#f4e6cc', '#fff6e8'], 0.3],\n    brain: [['#c48aa0', '#e0a8b8', '#f0c8d0', '#f8e0e6'], 0.5],\n    heart: [['#6a1020', '#a82030', '#e04548', '#ff8878'], 1],\n    hush: [['#143038', '#1e6870', '#3ec8b0', '#d8fff4'], 1.2],\n    gold: [['#6a4a10', '#c8a040', '#f0d070', '#fff0b0'], 1.3],\n  };\n  const MAT_IDS = Object.keys(MAT_KEYS);\n  const MATS = MAT_IDS.map(k => ({ ramp: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20), slow: makeRamp(MAT_KEYS[k][0], 20, true), spec: MAT_KEYS[k][1] }));\n  const matId = n => MAT_IDS.indexOf(n);\n\n  function makeNoise(seed) {\n    let a = seed >>> 0;\n    const R = () => {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      let t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), a | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n    const L = new Float32Array(65536);\n    for (let i = 0; i < L.length; i++) L[i] = R();\n    const v = (x, y) => {\n      const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), fx = x - xi, fy = y - yi;\n      const u = fx * fx * (3 - 2 * fx), w = fy * fy * (3 - 2 * fy);\n      const s = (p, q) => L[(p & 255) | ((q & 255) << 8)];\n      return (s(xi, yi) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi) * u) * (1 - w) + (s(xi, yi + 1) * (1 - u) + s(xi + 1, yi + 1) * u) * w;\n    };\n    return { R, fbm: (x, y, o = 4) => { let k = 0.5, f = 1, n = 0; for (let i = 0; i < o; i++) { n += k * v(x * f, y * f); k *= 0.5; f *= 2.03; } return n; } };\n  }\n\n  class TissueField {\n    constructor(W, H, seed = 7) {\n      this.W = W; this.H = H;\n      const N = W * H;\n      this.h = new Float32Array(N); this.m = new Uint8Array(N); this.pulse = new Float32Array(N);\n      this.ao = new Float32Array(N).fill(1); this.dyn = new Float32Array(N); this.over = new Uint8Array(N);\n      this.noise = makeNoise(seed);\n      this.cv = E.mkCanvas(W, H); this.g = this.cv.getContext('2d');\n      this.img = this.g.createImageData(W, H); this.u = new Uint32Array(this.img.data.buffer);\n    }\n    blob(x, y, rx, ry, rot, hgt, mat, o = {}) {\n      const { W, H, h, m, pulse, noise } = this, c = Math.cos(rot), s = Math.sin(rot);\n      const R = Math.max(rx, ry) + (o.warp || 0) + 2, id = matId(mat), warp = o.warp || 0, base = o.base || 0, add = !!o.add;\n      for (let py = Math.max(0, y - R | 0); py < Math.min(H, y + R + 1); py++) {\n        for (let px = Math.max(0, x - R | 0); px < Math.min(W, x + R + 1); px++) {\n          const wx = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * 0.03, py * 0.03, 2) - 0.5) * warp : 0;\n          const wy = warp ? (noise.fbm(px * 0.03 + 40, py * 0.03, 2) - 0.5) * warp : 0;\n          const dx = px - x + wx, dy = py - y + wy, u = (dx * c + dy * s) / rx, v = (-dx * s + dy * c) / ry, d = u * u + v * v;\n          if (d >= 1) continue;\n          const i = py * W + px, top = base + hgt * Math.sqrt(1 - d);\n          if (add) { h[i] += hgt * (1 - d); m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = Math.max(pulse[i], o.pulse * (1 - d)); }\n          else if (top > h[i]) { h[i] = top; m[i] = id; if (o.pulse) pulse[i] = o.pulse * (1 - d); }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    tube(pts, r, hgt, mat, o = {}) {\n      const step = Math.max(1, r * 0.35);\n      for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) {\n        const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / step | 0);\n        for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.blob(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, r, 0, hgt, mat, o);\n      }\n    }\n    finish(detail = 1.1) {\n      const { W, H, h, ao, noise } = this, N = W * H, blur = new Float32Array(N), tmp = new Float32Array(N), R = 7;\n      for (let i = 0, y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++, i++) h[i] += (noise.fbm(x * 0.11, y * 0.11, 3) - 0.5) * detail;\n      for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) {\n        let s = 0;\n        for (let x = -R; x <= R; x++) s += h[y * W + Math.max(0, x)];\n        for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) { tmp[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += h[y * W + Math.min(W - 1, x + R + 1)] - h[y * W + Math.max(0, x - R)]; }\n      }\n      for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {\n        let s = 0;\n        for (let y = -R; y <= R; y++) s += tmp[Math.max(0, y) * W + x];\n        for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) { blur[y * W + x] = s / (2 * R + 1); s += tmp[Math.min(H - 1, y + R + 1) * W + x] - tmp[Math.max(0, y - R) * W + x]; }\n      }\n      for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) ao[i] = Math.max(0.42, Math.min(1.08, 1 - (blur[i] - h[i]) * 0.055));\n    }\n    stampDisc(x, y, r, hgt, mat) {\n      const { W, H, dyn, over } = this, id = mat ? matId(mat) + 1 : 0;\n      for (let py = Math.max(1, y - r | 0); py < Math.min(H - 1, y + r + 1); py++) {\n        for (let px = Math.max(1, x - r | 0); px < Math.min(W - 1, x + r + 1); px++) {\n          const d = ((px - x) ** 2 + (py - y) ** 2) / (r * r);\n          if (d < 1) {\n            const i = py * W + px;\n            dyn[i] = hgt < 0 ? Math.min(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d)) : Math.max(dyn[i], hgt * (1 - d));\n            if (id) over[i] = id;\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n    stampLine(pts, r, hgt, mat) {\n      for (let k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) {\n        const [x0, y0] = pts[k], [x1, y1] = pts[k + 1], n = Math.max(1, Math.hypot(x1 - x0, y1 - y0) / Math.max(1, r * 0.5) | 0);\n        for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) this.stampDisc(x0 + (x1 - x0) * i / n, y0 + (y1 - y0) * i / n, r, hgt, mat);\n      }\n    }\n    shade(fx = {}) {\n      const { W, H, h, m, ao, pulse, dyn, over, u } = this;\n      const beat = fx.beat || 0, off = Math.round(fx.breath || 0) * W, slow = !!fx.slow, lens = fx.lens;\n      const lr2 = lens ? lens.r * lens.r : 0, dim = fx.dim || 0, spot = fx.spot, sr2 = spot ? spot.r * spot.r : 0;\n      const lx = fx.light ? fx.light[0] : -0.42, ly = fx.light ? fx.light[1] : -0.52;\n      const lz = Math.sqrt(Math.max(0.1, 1 - lx * lx - ly * ly)), hl = Math.hypot(lx, ly, lz + 1);\n      const hx = lx / hl, hy = ly / hl, hz = (lz + 1) / hl;\n      for (let y = 1; y < H - 1; y++) {\n        for (let x = 1, i = y * W + 1; x < W - 1; x++, i++) {\n          const j = Math.max(W + 1, Math.min(W * H - W - 2, i + off)), k = 1 + beat * pulse[j];\n          const dx = (h[j - 1] - h[j + 1]) * k * 0.5 + (dyn[i - 1] - dyn[i + 1]) * 0.5;\n          const dy = (h[j - W] - h[j + W]) * k * 0.5 + (dyn[i - W] - dyn[i + W]) * 0.5;\n          const nl = 1 / Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy + 1), nx = dx * nl, ny = dy * nl, nz = nl;\n          const diff = Math.max(0, nx * lx + ny * ly + nz * lz), sh = Math.max(0, nx * hx + ny * hy + nz * hz);\n          const ov = over[i], M = MATS[ov ? ov - 1 : m[j]];\n          const cold = slow || (lens && (x - lens.x) ** 2 + (y - lens.y) ** 2 < lr2);\n          const r = cold ? M.slow : M.ramp, n = r.length, s2 = sh * sh, s4 = s2 * s2, s8 = s4 * s4, s16 = s8 * s8, s32 = s16 * s16;\n          const lit = dim && !(spot && (x - spot.x) ** 2 + (y - spot.y) ** 2 < sr2) ? 1 - dim : 1;\n          const lum = (diff * 0.92 + s8 * 0.16 * M.spec + beat * pulse[j] * 0.6) * (ov ? 1 : ao[j]) * lit;\n          const c = Math.max(0, Math.min(n - 1, (lum * (n - 1) + BAYER[(x & 3) | ((y & 3) << 2)] * 1.15 + 0.5) | 0));\n          u[i] = s32 * s8 * M.spec * lit > 0.42 ? (cold ? 0xffffffe0 : 0xfff4f0ff) : r[c];\n        }\n      }\n      this.g.putImageData(this.img, 0, 0); dyn.fill(0); over.fill(0);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function cavity(F, W, H, wall) {\n    const cx = W / 2, cy = H / 2 - 4, rx = 171, ry = 91;\n    for (let y = 0; y < H; y++) for (let x = 0; x < W; x++) {\n      const i = y * W + x, d = ((x - cx) / rx) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / ry) ** 2;\n      const fold = Math.sin(x * 0.09 + 1.6 * Math.sin(y * 0.05)) * 1.6;\n      if (d < 1) { F.h[i] = -16 + 12 * d * d; F.m[i] = matId(wall || 'wall'); }\n      else if (d < 1.28) { const e = (d - 1) / 0.28; F.h[i] = 4 + 7 * Math.sin(e * Math.PI); F.m[i] = matId('skin'); }\n      else { F.h[i] = 6 + fold; F.m[i] = matId('drape'); }\n    }\n    return { cx, cy, rx, ry };\n  }\n\n  function bakeAbdomen(W, H, seed) {\n    const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), n = F.noise, box = cavity(F, W, H, 'wall'), { cx, cy, rx, ry } = box;\n    F.blob(cx - rx * 0.55, cy - ry * 0.5, rx * 0.55, ry * 0.55, -0.3, 17, 'liver', { base: -11, warp: 12 });\n    for (let i = 0; i < 9; i++) {\n      const a = n.R() * 6.28, r = 0.55 + n.R() * 0.32;\n      F.blob(cx + Math.cos(a) * rx * r, cy + Math.sin(a) * ry * r, 9 + n.R() * 14, 7 + n.R() * 9, n.R() * 3, 8, 'fat', { base: -10, warp: 8 });\n    }\n    const coil = (x0, y0, len, dir, r) => {\n      const pts = [[x0, y0]]; let a = dir, x = x0, y = y0;\n      for (let i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n        a += (n.R() - 0.5) * 1.5 + Math.sin(i * 0.9) * 0.5;\n        x += Math.cos(a) * r * 1.3; y += Math.sin(a) * r * 1.3;\n        if (((x - cx) / (rx * 0.92)) ** 2 + ((y - cy) / (ry * 0.92)) ** 2 > 1) { a += 2.4; x += Math.cos(a) * r; y += Math.sin(a) * r; }\n        pts.push([x, y]);\n      }\n      return pts;\n    };\n    F.tube(coil(cx + rx * 0.05, cy - ry * 0.25, 34, 0.2, 9), 11, 14, 'bowel', { base: -8 });\n    F.tube(coil(cx + rx * 0.45, cy + ry * 0.25, 26, 2.6, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -7 });\n    F.tube(coil(cx - rx * 0.35, cy + ry * 0.45, 22, -0.3, 9), 10, 15, 'bowel', { base: -6 });\n    F.finish(1.1);\n    return F;\n  }\n\n  function bakeForearm(W, H, seed) {\n    const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), box = cavity(F, W, H, 'muscle'), { cx, cy, rx, ry } = box;\n    for (let i = -3; i <= 3; i++) F.blob(cx, cy + i * 16, rx * 0.72, 7, 0.15, 9, i % 2 ? 'muscle' : 'tendon', { base: -8, warp: 6 });\n    F.tube([[cx - rx * 0.6, cy], [cx + rx * 0.6, cy - 8]], 3, 4, 'gold', { add: true });\n    F.finish(0.8);\n    return F;\n  }\n\n  function bakeFlank(W, H, seed) {\n    const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), { cx, cy, rx, ry } = cavity(F, W, H, 'muscle');\n    for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) F.blob(cx - rx * 0.3 + i * 22, cy + 10, 16, 10, 0.2, 8, 'fat', { base: -8 });\n    F.tube([[cx - rx * 0.7, cy + ry * 0.2], [cx + rx * 0.7, cy - ry * 0.15]], 4, 3, 'wound', { add: true });\n    F.finish(0.9);\n    return F;\n  }\n\n  function bakeHeart(W, H, seed) {\n    const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), { cx, cy, rx, ry } = cavity(F, W, H, 'wall');\n    F.blob(cx, cy, rx * 0.42, ry * 0.55, 0.2, 22, 'heart', { base: -6, pulse: 0.8, warp: 6 });\n    F.tube([[cx - 20, cy - 10], [cx + 30, cy + 16], [cx + 10, cy + 28]], 3, 3, 'artery', { add: true, pulse: 0.5 });\n    F.finish(0.7);\n    return F;\n  }\n\n  function bakeBrain(W, H, seed) {\n    const F = new TissueField(W, H, seed), n = F.noise, { cx, cy, rx, ry } = cavity(F, W, H, 'brain');\n    for (let i = 0; i < 14; i++) {\n      const a = n.R() * 6.28;\n      F.blob(cx + Math.cos(