ne_number\":768,\"content\":\"    /** clickAt: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y], for the one step after it (clicked()) */\"},{\"line_number\":854,\"content\":\"      const d = this._down; this._down = null;   // a click or tap: lifted within a few pixels of where it landed (a drag, the stick's, is none): clicked() for a step,\"},{\"line_number\":1097,\"content\":\"   *  it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(input.clicked())) ... */\"},{\"line_number\":1098,\"content\":\"  clicked() { return this._clickAt; }\"},{\"line_number\":1121,\"content\":\"  /** a pointer event in screen pixels, as the browser's would give: feed('down' | 'move' | 'up', x, y, { touch: false,\"},{\"line_number\":1124,\"content\":\"   *  feed('zoom', x, y, { k: 1.1 }): a wheel's notch or a pinch about that point */\"},{\"line_number\":1125,\"content\":\"  feed(type, x, y, o = {}) {\"},{\"line_number\":1782,\"content\":\"  /** what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to\"},{\"line_number\":5521,\"content\":\"   * line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(),\"},{\"line_number\":9204,\"content\":\"    const c = inp.clicked(), d = (c || asking) && this._dims(), tapped = !!c && c[0] >= d.x && c[0] < d.x + d.w && c[1] >= d.y && c[1] < d.y + d.h;   // a tap on the box, as confirm\"},{\"line_number\":9297,\"content\":\"  /** entry i's box on the screen, [x, y, w, h] in screen pixels: where a click or tap picks it (a test's feed('down') and\"},{\"line_number\":9298,\"content\":\"   *  feed('up') there); null while it is scrolled out of view */\"},{\"line_number\":9310,\"content\":\"    const tap = row(inp.clicked());   // a click or tap on an entry picks it\"},{\"line_number\":10648,\"content\":\"const clicked = I => I.clicked ? I.clicked() : null;   // (a tap: the full engine's; the agent edition has none)\"},{\"line_number\":10725,\"content\":\"    if (P.some(q => q.anyPressed()) || joined || clicked(I)) { this._idle = 0; this.phase = 'title'; return 'title'; }   // (any player's input, or one joining)\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7841a53d-eb68-4443-b1c8-c3575ebf4f98-44","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"400→  }\\n\\n  function titleBackdrop(g, W, H, t) {\\n    const px = E.px;\\n    px.rect(g, 0, 0, W, H, '#071018');\\n    px.rect(g, 0, H * 0.62 | 0, W, H, '#0c1c28');\\n    px.rect(g, 0, (H * 0.72) | 0, W, 8, '#16324a');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\\n      const x = 18 + i * ((W - 30) / 8), h = 40 + ((i * 17) % 28);\\n      px.rect(g, x, (H * 0.62) - h, 16, h, i % 2 ? '#102838' : '#173448');\\n410→      for (let wy = 6; wy < h - 4; wy += 7) if ((i + wy) % 3 === 0) px.rect(g, x + 3, (H * 0.62) - h + wy, 3, 2, '#f0d78a');\\n    }\\n    px.rect(g, W * 0.55, 28, 4, (H * 0.62) - 20, '#1a3044');\\n    px.rect(g, W * 0.72, 18, 3, (H * 0.62) - 10, '#1a3044');\\n    const sweep = (t * 40) % (W + 40) - 20;\\n    px.rect(g, sweep, (H * 0.78) | 0, 18, 6, '#c84848');\\n    px.rect(g, sweep + 22, (H * 0.78) | 0, 10, 6, '#d8d2c4');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 28; i++) {\\n      const x = (i * 47 + t * 30) % W, y = (i * 29 + t * 70) % H;\\n      px.line(g, x, y, x + 1, y + 4, '#8fb8c8', 1);\\n420→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stage(g, name, W, H, t) {\\n    const px = E.px;\\n    const sky = name === 'harbor' ? '#071018' : name === 'chapel' ? '#140e18' : '#07141c';\\n    px.rect(g, 0, 0, W, H, sky);\\n    px.rect(g, 0, 150, W, H - 150, '#102028');\\n    if (name === 'theatre') {\\n      px.rect(g, 20, 20, W - 40, 90, '#0c2428');\\n430→      for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) px.rect(g, 36 + i * 36, 36, 18, 10, '#1a4a44');\\n      px.rect(g, W / 2 - 30, 18, 60, 8, '#f2f0e6');\\n    } else if (name === 'office') {\\n      px.rect(g, 30, 40, 80, 50, '#1a2830');\\n      px.rect(g, 40, 70, 28, 16, '#c8a45a');\\n    } else if (name === 'harbor' || name === 'ship') {\\n      titleBackdrop(g, W, H, t);\\n    } else if (name === 'chapel') {\\n      px.rect(g, W / 2 - 8, 24, 16, 70, '#2a2030');\\n      px.rect(g, W / 2 - 20, 40, 40, 6, '#3a3040');\\n440→    } else {\\n      px.rect(g, 16, 30, W - 32, 70, '#102830');\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) px.rect(g, 28 + i * 40, 44, 22, 14, '#d8e4dc');\\n    }\\n    const lamp = 80 + Math.sin(t) * 10;\\n    px.rect(g, lamp, 8, 18, 4, '#f0e2b0');\\n  }\\n\\n  GAME.Art = { TissueField, fieldFor, bust, drawBust, CAST, toolIcon, drawHand, titleBackdrop, stage, matId };\\n})();\",\"content_concise\":\"400→  }\\n\\n  function titleBackdrop(g, W, H, t) {\\n    const px = E.px;\\n    px.rect(g, 0, 0, W, H, '#071018');\\n    px.rect(g, 0, H * 0.62 | 0, W, H, '#0c1c28');\\n    px.rect(g, 0, (H * 0.72) | 0, W, 8, '#16324a');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\\n      const x = 18 + i * ((W - 30) / 8), h = 40 + ((i * 17) % 28);\\n      px.rect(g, x, (H * 0.62) - h, 16, h, i % 2 ? '#102838' : '#173448');\\n410→      for (let wy = 6; wy < h - 4; wy += 7) if ((i + wy) % 3 === 0) px.rect(g, x + 3, (H * 0.62) - h + wy, 3, 2, '#f0d78a');\\n    }\\n    px.rect(g, W * 0.55, 28, 4, (H * 0.62) - 20, '#1a3044');\\n    px.rect(g, W * 0.72, 18, 3, (H * 0.62) - 10, '#1a3044');\\n    const sweep = (t * 40) % (W + 40) - 20;\\n    px.rect(g, sweep, (H * 0.78) | 0, 18, 6, '#c84848');\\n    px.rect(g, sweep + 22, (H * 0.78) | 0, 10, 6, '#d8d2c4');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 28; i++) {\\n      const x = (i * 47 + t * 30) % W, y = (i * 29 + t * 70) % H;\\n      px.line(g, x, y, x + 1, y + 4, '#8fb8c8', 1);\\n420→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stage(g, name, W, H, t) {\\n    const px = E.px;\\n    const sky = name === 'harbor' ? '#071018' : name === 'chapel' ? '#140e18' : '#07141c';\\n    px.rect(g, 0, 0, W, H, sky);\\n    px.rect(g, 0, 150, W, H - 150, '#102028');\\n    if (name === 'theatre') {\\n      px.rect(g, 20, 20, W - 40, 90, '#0c2428');\\n430→      for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) px.rect(g, 36 + i * 36, 36, 18, 10, '#1a4a44');\\n      px.rect(g, W / 2 - 30, 18, 60, 8, '#f2f0e6');\\n    } else if (name === 'office') {\\n      px.rect(g, 30, 40, 80, 50, '#1a2830');\\n      px.rect(g, 40, 70, 28, 16, '#c8a45a');\\n    } else if (name === 'harbor' || name === 'ship') {\\n      titleBackdrop(g, W, H, t);\\n    } else if (name === 'chapel') {\\n      px.rect(g, W / 2 - 8, 24, 16, 70, '#2a2030');\\n      px.rect(g, W / 2 - 20, 40, 40, 6, '#3a3040');\\n440→    } else {\\n      px.rect(g, 16, 30, W - 32, 70, '#102830');\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) px.rect(g, 28 + i * 40, 44, 22, 14, '#d8e4dc');\\n    }\\n    const lamp = 80 + Math.sin(t) * 10;\\n    px.rect(g, lamp, 8, 18, 4, '#f0e2b0');\\n  }\\n\\n  GAME.Art = { TissueField, fieldFor, bust, drawBust, CAST, toolIcon, drawHand, titleBackdrop, stage, matId };\\n})();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/art/field.js\",\"offset\":400,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  }\\n\\n  function titleBackdrop(g, W, H, t) {\\n    const px = E.px;\\n    px.rect(g, 0, 0, W, H, '#071018');\\n    px.rect(g, 0, H * 0.62 | 0, W, H, '#0c1c28');\\n    px.rect(g, 0, (H * 0.72) | 0, W, 8, '#16324a');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\\n      const x = 18 + i * ((W - 30) / 8), h = 40 + ((i * 17) % 28);\\n      px.rect(g, x, (H * 0.62) - h, 16, h, i % 2 ? '#102838' : '#173448');\\n      for (let wy = 6; wy < h - 4; wy += 7) if ((i + wy) % 3 === 0) px.rect(g, x + 3, (H * 0.62) - h + wy, 3, 2, '#f0d78a');\\n    }\\n    px.rect(g, W * 0.55, 28, 4, (H * 0.62) - 20, '#1a3044');\\n    px.rect(g, W * 0.72, 18, 3, (H * 0.62) - 10, '#1a3044');\\n    const sweep = (t * 40) % (W + 40) - 20;\\n    px.rect(g, sweep, (H * 0.78) | 0, 18, 6, '#c84848');\\n    px.rect(g, sweep + 22, (H * 0.78) | 0, 10, 6, '#d8d2c4');\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 28; i++) {\\n      const x = (i * 47 + t * 30) % W, y = (i * 29 + t * 70) % H;\\n      px.line(g, x, y, x + 1, y + 4, '#8fb8c8', 1);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stage(g, name, W, H, t) {\\n    const px = E.px;\\n    const sky = name === 'harbor' ? '#071018' : name === 'chapel' ? '#140e18' : '#07141c';\\n    px.rect(g, 0, 0, W, H, sky);\\n    px.rect(g, 0, 150, W, H - 150, '#102028');\\n    if (name === 'theatre') {\\n      px.rect(g, 20, 20, W - 40, 90, '#0c2428');\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 6; i++) px.rect(g, 36 + i * 36, 36, 18, 10, '#1a4a44');\\n      px.rect(g, W / 2 - 30, 18, 60, 8, '#f2f0e6');\\n    } else if (name === 'office') {\\n      px.rect(g, 30, 40, 80, 50, '#1a2830');\\n      px.rect(g, 40, 70, 28, 16, '#c8a45a');\\n    } else if (name === 'harbor' || name === 'ship') {\\n      titleBackdrop(g, W, H, t);\\n    } else if (name === 'chapel') {\\n      px.rect(g, W / 2 - 8, 24, 16, 70, '#2a2030');\\n      px.rect(g, W / 2 - 20, 40, 40, 6, '#3a3040');\\n    } else {\\n      px.rect(g, 16, 30, W - 32, 70, '#102830');\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) px.rect(g, 28 + i * 40, 44, 22, 14, '#d8e4dc');\\n    }\\n    const lamp = 80 + Math.sin(t) * 10;\\n    px.rect(g, lamp, 8, 18, 4, '#f0e2b0');\\n  }\\n\\n  GAME.Art = { TissueField, fieldFor, bust, drawBust, CAST, toolIcon, drawHand, titleBackdrop, stage, matId };\\n})();\\n\",\"total_lines\":449}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"a3b619b3-bcaf-4ee4-855d-585c326855a8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_197","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I understand the requirements and am ready to write the files.\n\nAudio design is set: songs as objects, SFX via define, voice via Web Audio biquad formants, choir via detuned saws. Headless mode will be no-op. About data and shell scripts are next. Ward gets a simple tile map with the player near the door.\n\nWard patients are humanoids. Interact via confirm or E near doors and people. Doors spawn 1–2 tiles from the player. Chapter data comes from GAME.WARD[chapter]. After an operation, the story resumes to a ward event that loads saved patients.\n\nAfter an operation, the completed case's patient is added to the saved ward list. Exiting the ward triggers story.resume(), which processes the goto c2_in step and runs the c2_in dialogue immediately inside the story scene.\n\nWard exit needs RT.redirect cleared and game.go('story') called after resume. After an operation, results resume triggers the cN_out dialogue and story resumes into it. Credits events inside c11_out appear after several lines.\n\nCredits resume to the epilogue, which ends and returns to title. The Incoming chart will appear as a door on the credits screen after the epilogue, not as gameplay.\n\nThe credits scene will display pages of text, with the final page showing Incoming chart details; confirming returns to title after the story ends. The hub implementation follows the skeleton but uses a real simulation, connecting as a shared-world host and deriving the round case from the player count.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0763fc78-dda9-4605-8f1e-0794a04fe13b-45","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"S\\.hold|hold:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4539,"output_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":104064,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"8e6429f2-e7f2-49ad-b9bc-da0fddb19fa4"}
