{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_200","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I understand the requirements.\n\nBeginning to write the core files: audio.js, about.js, about-data.json, shell.js, tests, build, content, and feedback. Checking E.Input.DEFAULT keys and Settings slider format for correct implementation.\n\nAdding difficulty options, assist slider, cursor speed, stick swaps, sustained hold, hints, blood color, and text speed to the settings. The pause menu will include Dev Mode and Restart Phase items. Save and load are engine-provided automatically when enabled. Save capability is restricted to the ward scene.\n\nDrafting the attract idle logic. It hooks into input to detect user activity via pressed keys, held buttons, mouse movement, and analog stick or movement input.\n\nThe attract idle logic now transitions to the title scene when input is detected, and returns to attract after ten seconds of inactivity. Idle detection is limited to title, menu, casefiles, and lobby scenes while the shell is closed and the game is not paused. A timing issue was noted: the hook runs before scene updates.\n\nConfirmed that consuming all input inside the hook prevents the title scene from registering the same press on the next frame. The suppress flag is extra safety for held keys.\n\nThe attract reel will cycle through Op, Story, and Bot segments using demo mode with cheats. It will lock vitals, freeze the clock, enable one-hit mode, and drive the bot device. A DEMO ribbon will label it and the loop will repeat indefinitely.\n\nA `driveOp` function is being drafted to simulate player inputs for the demo loop.\n\nThe `driveOp` function now routes player inputs through the debug driver, bot device, local hands, or default bot based on runtime flags. It updates each player's wheel and cursor using the generated device data.\n\nThe `driveOp` function now assembles input arrays for each player and passes them to `GAME.Op.step`. A `readLocal` helper is being drafted to read local controller inputs, respecting the stick-swap setting by swapping aim and movement axes, and scanning for tool digit presses.\n\nThe `readLocal` helper is being completed with aim, move, fine, trig, gift, consult, cancel, and digit fields. WASD keys are being mapped to a separate keys array. The held input Set uses raw key codes such as KeyW and KeyA.\n\nWASD keys are mapped to a separate cursor vector, distinct from menu direction controls. D-pad inputs serve as menu navigation in menus and as nudge actions in the OP scene when a gamepad is detected. Mouse coordinates are calculated relative to the screen center when a pointer exists and the last input device was a mouse or pointer feed. The wheel hold action maps to Mouse2.\n\nWheel hold now uses mouse pan delta as movement when the delta exceeds eight pixels. Tool selection cycles to the next digit on press. A headless-safe paintField helper is being drafted.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-624f3fe1-173d-4e96-be20-ee0df867bcd0-51","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"shade\\(|stampDisc|this\\.cv|finish\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/art/field.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4845,"output_tokens":2183,"cache_read_input_tokens":112128,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"15c82c71-8693-433b-8ca6-c3d534ed3ebe"}
