ave failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\\n    if (!this.saved) warn('settings:save', 'the settings could not be saved (storage is blocked or full): they last for this visit');\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"f43788d0-a458-4e55-b217-b6281828e95e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_206","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that the music value of 0.1 applies via standard apply.\n\nAbout screen will be a menu item and a button at the end of credits. Credits scene is separate from About but reachable from it. The story epilogue ends before credits. Event credits fires before epilogue. c11_out lines will trigger the credits scene.\n\nCredits pages advance on confirm. The final page resumes the story and triggers the epilogue. After the epilogue ends, the scene returns to the title.\n\nIncoming will appear as the final credits page text, showing a chart on a door. After resuming from credits, the scene returns to story if the story is still running; otherwise it goes to title. The credits event sets a redirect flag before entering the credits scene.\n\nThe redirect flag stays null, so resuming from results returns to the story scene. The ward event fires after the out dialogue and does not interfere with the op resume flow. The credits event triggers during the c11_out dialog onDone, while the story scene is still updating.\n\nThe story scene update defers the go('credits') call to the next frame so the current frame can finish drawing before leaving. The story scene will exit to title only when the story is not running and not held. The chart lightbox opens from the op event when the chartFor ID differs from the current one.\n\nThe `on.op` handler sets the pending operation and checks whether a chart lightbox should open. If so, it redirects to the chart scene; otherwise it begins the operation. Chart success updates the chart state and bonus values before entering the operation scene. The bonus application was mistakenly placed after character creation, but the character object does not exist yet at that point.\n\nChart penalties apply to the created state: ten seconds subtracted per wrong answer and twenty added per correct one. After three misses, the chart still proceeds with those penalties rather than failing the case. Mark positions on the screen are calculated from screen pixels, and clicks must land within fourteen pixels of a mark. The keyboard will use a film cursor that confirms when it is near a mark. The ward scene enters in three-quarter view, enables saving, and sets the chapter from the current case ID.\n\nThe ward scene spawns the hero near the door and marks them as near it. Movement uses the stick or WASD. Mouse hover shifts focus toward the pointer. Confirming while near the door disables saving, resumes the story, and returns to the story scene unless a redirect is set. The exit routine also disables saving.\n\nThe test confirms once to leave the ward. Patients will be visible in the snapshot. Rank saves will write to RT.ranks when a case is won without tuning or cheating. Snapshot exposes ranks and savedPatients. Unlocks will track finished cases in snapshot.unlocked.\n\nThe difficulty menu lists Intern, Resident, and Attending. Case files appear in order; locked ones remain hidden until the previous case is beaten. A fresh game leaves all files locked except perhaps the first. The lobby scene holds one to four surgeons, and confirming starts a local grand rounds session with bots for the remaining seats. The hub scene replaces the title when the player is already inside an active session. The `GAME.beginCase` function is being drafted.\n\n`GAME.beginCase` seeds the operation state with difficulty set to resident and then enters the operation scene. A debug snapshot helper will be exposed as `window.__ot`. The attract test advances ten and a half seconds on the title screen without input to trigger the attract scene, then verifies that tapping returns to the title and suppresses the menu.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0d6b590d-572b-44b7-b3b7-3dba6d1f2141-59","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"windowOpen","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1696,"output_tokens":1944,"cache_read_input_tokens":129024,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"225c09cb-4b70-41b3-a04b-8b68db51aa5b"}
