{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-32b06109-c79b-4f8e-b39e-77bf4f373e2d-60","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1325→        o.x = clamp(o.x + drift * worldDt, 60, 360);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    for (const o of S.objects) {\\n      if (o.markT > 0) { o.markT -= handDt; if (o.markT <= 0 && o.hidden) o.marked = false; }\\n1330→      if (o.revealWhen && o.hidden) {\\n        const src = S.objects.find(q => q.tag === o.revealWhen);\\n        if (src && src.done) { o.hidden = false; o.marked = true; }\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'bleeder' && !o.done) {\\n        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 8, vol: 4, max: 40, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 6 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'arteryTear' && !o.done) {\\n1340→        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 6, vol: 6, max: 50, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 14 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* solo retractor: Quill holds at half the window */\\n    const retract = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'retractor' && !o.done);\\n    if (retract) {\\n      const holder = S.players.some(p => p.held === retract.id && p.trig > 0.3);\\n      if (holder) S.windowOpen = 1;\\n1350→      else if (S.players.filter(p => !p.gone).length <= 1) S.windowOpen = 0.5;\\n      else S.windowOpen = 0;\\n    }\\n    if (S.lab) {\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.done && o.lab) {\\n        o.labT = (o.labT || 0) + worldDt;\\n        if (o.labT > 1.2) {\\n          o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.cut = false; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.stitch = 0; o.free = false; o.tears = 0; o.spin = 0;\\n          o.x = o.origin[0]; o.y = o.origin[1]; o.labT = 0;\\n          if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0;\\n1360→        }\\n      } else o.labT = 0;\\n    }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.scripts.length; i++) {\\n      const sc = S.scripts[i];\",\"content_concise\":\"1325→        o.x = clamp(o.x + drift * worldDt, 60, 360);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    for (const o of S.objects) {\\n      if (o.markT > 0) { o.markT -= handDt; if (o.markT <= 0 && o.hidden) o.marked = false; }\\n1330→      if (o.revealWhen && o.hidden) {\\n        const src = S.objects.find(q => q.tag === o.revealWhen);\\n        if (src && src.done) { o.hidden = false; o.marked = true; }\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'bleeder' && !o.done) {\\n        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 8, vol: 4, max: 40, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 6 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'arteryTear' && !o.done) {\\n1340→        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 6, vol: 6, max: 50, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 14 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* solo retractor: Quill holds at half the window */\\n    const retract = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'retractor' && !o.done);\\n    if (retract) {\\n      const holder = S.players.some(p => p.held === retract.id && p.trig > 0.3);\\n      if (holder) S.windowOpen = 1;\\n1350→      else if (S.players.filter(p => !p.gone).length <= 1) S.windowOpen = 0.5;\\n      else S.windowOpen = 0;\\n    }\\n    if (S.lab) {\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.done && o.lab) {\\n        o.labT = (o.labT || 0) + worldDt;\\n        if (o.labT > 1.2) {\\n          o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.cut = false; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.stitch = 0; o.free = false; o.tears = 0; o.spin = 0;\\n          o.x = o.origin[0]; o.y = o.origin[1]; o.labT = 0;\\n          if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0;\\n1360→        }\\n      } else o.labT = 0;\\n    }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.scripts.length; i++) {\\n      const sc = S.scripts[i];\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":1325,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"        o.x = clamp(o.x + drift * worldDt, 60, 360);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    for (const o of S.objects) {\\n      if (o.markT > 0) { o.markT -= handDt; if (o.markT <= 0 && o.hidden) o.marked = false; }\\n      if (o.revealWhen && o.hidden) {\\n        const src = S.objects.find(q => q.tag === o.revealWhen);\\n        if (src && src.done) { o.hidden = false; o.marked = true; }\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'bleeder' && !o.done) {\\n        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 8, vol: 4, max: 40, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 6 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'arteryTear' && !o.done) {\\n        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 6, vol: 6, max: 50, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 14 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* solo retractor: Quill holds at half the window */\\n    const retract = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'retractor' && !o.done);\\n    if (retract) {\\n      const holder = S.players.some(p => p.held === retract.id && p.trig > 0.3);\\n      if (holder) S.windowOpen = 1;\\n      else if (S.players.filter(p => !p.gone).length <= 1) S.windowOpen = 0.5;\\n      else S.windowOpen = 0;\\n    }\\n    if (S.lab) {\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.done && o.lab) {\\n        o.labT = (o.labT || 0) + worldDt;\\n        if (o.labT > 1.2) {\\n          o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.cut = false; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.stitch = 0; o.free = false; o.tears = 0; o.spin = 0;\\n          o.x = o.origin[0]; o.y = o.origin[1]; o.labT = 0;\\n          if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0;\\n        }\\n      } else o.labT = 0;\\n    }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.scripts.length; i++) {\\n      const sc = S.scripts[i];\\n\",\"total_lines\":1762}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"f15a7eb7-e856-4f07-a39d-47348157b5cf"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_208","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Bot seat 0 holds the retractor, so windowOpen becomes 1.\n\nA solo test will spawn a raw state with a retractor and mass, step once, and verify windowOpen is 0.5. A two-player test will create players, make them, and step with the bot device or manual hold.\n\nBot.play roundsCase will run the full Grand Rounds test. The ferry clear is skipped if time is tight but included and fixed if it fails. A legato snap test will use spawnStrain. Tests will use real functions and be corrected after running. The bust bug will also be fixed.\n\nA self-contained `renderProbe` helper will use `OfflineAudioContext` to render audio without the game's AudioContext. It returns a Promise so browser tests can await the result.\n\n`renderProbe` will compute RMS amplitude by rendering a short buffer via `startRendering()`, then averaging the squared samples in the channel data.\n\nBrowser tests will verify effect, voice, and choir amplitudes are above 0.001 while music stays below half the effects level. Node tests will assert settings.music equals 0.1. The live game routes choir to the sfx bus. A SONGS constant is being defined with a night track at 84 BPM using triangle and square waves.\n\nA `play` function will load songs from the SONGS constant and trigger them through the game audio system with a 0.4-second fade and looping. A `blip` helper is being added to generate sawtooth oscillator tones on the voice bus, keyed by character code.\n\nThe `blip` helper now uses a bandpass filter and exponential gain ramps to create short, percussive tones on the voice bus. A `choir` function is being added to stop any active choir and start a new one routed to the sfx bus. SFX definitions are also being drafted.\n\nSFX definitions are being added for events like 'snip'. The test runner will use an OT_INNER environment flag to prevent nested spawns. Shell.js is being written next at roughly 1500 lines. Content files, manifest, index.dev.html, build.mjs, and tests are also planned.\n\nThe test runner strips FORCE_COLOR and NO_COLOR from the inner spawn environment. It captures stdout and stderr, then filters to keep only lines starting with FAIL or the final check count. Warnings on stderr are discarded unless they begin with FAIL.\n\nThe outer Node process may still emit a color warning to stderr before the filter strips it. That would violate the requirement for clean output.\n\nThe color warning is emitted by Node before user code runs, so it bypasses the outer filter. A shell script entry point is needed to suppress it.\n\nThe color warning is emitted by Node's util/colors module when both FORCE_COLOR and NO_COLOR are present. Setting NODE_NO_WARNINGS=1 cannot suppress it because the parent process has already started. A quick test script will verify exactly when the warning fires.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a044196d-8515-4e4a-8850-092228f20fce-61","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"FORCE_COLOR=1 NO_COLOR=1 node -e \"console.log('stdout-hi')\" 2>/tmp/ot-warn.txt; echo EXIT:$?; echo '---stderr---'; cat /tmp/ot-warn.txt; echo '---'","description":"See when Node prints the color warning"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1022,"output_tokens":2271,"cache_read_input_tokens":132864,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"efc4f361-9717-4406-9c23-5e38ba0f1ac8"}
