{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_224","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The engine sets debug to null in its constructor.\n\nAssigning `game.debug` after the game constructor is safe. I'll add a snapshot method and `window.__ot`. Files will be written in parallel batches. I need to fix `field.js`, update audio, about JSON/JS, and shell. Shell is large so I'll write it carefully. I also need to verify `E.font.title` and `px.disc` signatures.\n\nHeadless overlay context works with draw:true. Scene draw methods receive the renderer. I'll set camera zoom and wheel to false on scenes that shouldn't zoom, and pausable to true on op, ward, lab, and hub. A chapterOf helper will look up case chapters, and ward people will be drawn from GAME.WARD[chapter].\n\nI mapped each case to a patient key. The ward lists already contain the correct people by chapter, so no extra tracking is needed. I'll add a door near spawn and set snapshot flags for patients and interact text. Humanoids will be drawn if feasible, though missing fields might cause errors.\n\nI'll use E.Humanoid for ward characters with a coat outfit and green cloth color. The rig.draw signature matches the template. I'll initialize RT.map as an E.TileMap with drawFloor and queueWalls, though headless failures there would break playthrough.\n\nThe template runs headless successfully. I'll use E.Body for the hero with a radius of 6, setting velocity before each update. The hero will spawn 20 pixels south of the door on a floor tile, staying still to avoid collisions. map.find('door') will locate the door cell.\n\nI'll write the map and fix any test failures that arise. I'll keep new file lines under a reasonable length. I'm checking stepLegato to ensure the snap test matches the API, then I'll create a legato Op with vitals at 80 and clock at 200, spawn its head tag, and yank it with high inst.\n\nI'll write a compact shell and add test helpers for press and move. A forceps success test will simulate a shard at 180, 110 with axis [1, 0], depth 14, and order 1, then move the mouse onto it and grip by updating the player device through Wheel.update.\n\nI'll drive the simulation with Cursor.update and Op.step inside a frames loop. The forceps must grip within 12 units of the shard, pull along its axis until freed, then dish. I'll validate correct gestures by running Bot.play on a minimal createRaw shard simulation, and test mistakes manually.\n\nI confirmed the tear condition for the mistake test: inst must exceed tension or perp must exceed 8 while the object is not free. I will trigger a tear by placing the player far away and stepping. The shell file will be split into logical sections within one file. I also drafted manifest.json with the exact script load order.\n\nbuild.mjs will concatenate scripts from the manifest, escape closing tags, wrap them in a page head, and write the root HTML plus dev/game.html. It will also copy harness, bridge, and round.js. I will write exit-interview.json directly now so it is present immediately; the build script can regenerate it later if needed. An index.dev.html will load engine and scripts separately for debugging, while the hand-in deliverable remains the bundled HTML.\n\nThe page title will be exactly \"Open Table Second Opinion\". The boot splash markup will be a static div with id `e3-boot` and role `status`, since the engine looks for that element. CSS will come from appendix D.\n\nThe engine bundle and session.js will be placed under vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/ and vendor/hub/session.js. Every script must have its closing </script> tags escaped, and the HTML must contain no external audio URLs or CDN references. The shell will not reference any external resources.\n\naudio.js will avoid Math.random and instead use oscillators for choir and voice. renderProbe returns a Promise, but it falls back to null if OfflineAudioContext is unavailable. Node tests expect null and settings.music at 0.1, while browser tests await the probe result. I need to verify whether Node 24 includes OfflineAudioContext.\n\nNode 24 likely lacks OfflineAudioContext, so the audio probe will safely return null. The shell file will be written in full in one pass and validated with node --check for syntax errors. The playthrough test sets skipStory to true at startup so story choices are bypassed; the engine enters story mode and immediately skips if that flag is set.\n\nThe story `enter()` method will only call `run('start')` when the story is not already running. This prevents duplicate starts after an operation and ensures returning from results resumes the held conversation instead of restarting it. The credits scene will not interrupt the story.\n\nThe epilogue test will loop until the title screen appears. When the epilogue ends, story running becomes false and the update loop returns to the title. If the credits scene is still active, the resume path first enters story mode, auto-skips the final line, and then exits to the title.\n\nThe credits scene will display a chart pinned to the door and end with the shift over. The skills lab will be a real case with practice operations, a cancel control to return to the menu, and lab cheats already built into its operation. The lobby menu will let the player select one of four rounds, start that case with bots on seats greater than zero and the local seat at zero, and confirm to begin.\n\nGrand Rounds bot.play will run independently of the scene. The case menu will unlock cases in order, starting with c1 and allowing replay of cleared cases afterward. Confirming a case begins its operation directly via beginCase, bypassing story for players but keeping the chart lightbox path. Difficulty is stored in RT.diff. A new game resets the cleared flags for the current run while preserving the overall record.\n\nI will reset RT.cleared on new game to clear the run, but preserve RT.best and snapshot.ranks as the overall record. The test reads final ranks after the playthrough, so clearing only progress flags is sufficient.\n\nThe newGame function resets difficulty, ranks, cleared flags, and case state, then stops any running story before entering the story scene. The test harness will set game.fadeTime to zero immediately after load to prevent frame delays.\n\nThe menu scene correctly consumes input on pick, so the scene update does not also handle confirm. The difficulty scene is a standalone scene with its own menu; the title screen routes to it, and the test selects New Game by tapping down and confirming. The tap helper sets a single press for one frame, which Menu processes via pressed or repeat.\n\nThe menu scene will recreate its E.Menu instance inside enter() so the list is fresh each time. The title screen routes to the menu scene, and the menu itself lists New Game, Case Files, Grand Rounds, Skills Lab, and About.\n\nThe menu scene routes each selection to its target: Case Files, Lobby, Skills Lab, or About. The update method checks for cancel input to return to the title. The lab case is started directly from the menu via beginCase. Quill barks will be drawn occasionally during operations using a deterministic index from GAME.BARKS instead of Math.random.\n\nQuill barks will use a deterministic index `(S.t / 8 | 0) % BARKS.length` instead of random selection. The dev panel pages will be added simply.\n\nFor testing live dev changes, the test will use `Op.createRaw` with explicit vitals, drain, and no tutorial freeze. This avoids the tutorial phase where drain is frozen.\n\nThe live-dev test will verify that a vitals drop of exactly 3 occurs after raising the patient drain to 3, then confirm the value returns to normal once the dev tune resets. A `lockVitals` cheat will be tested by locking vitals and stepping; the value must remain unchanged. The full-stick cursor-speed test will use the default stick sensitivity of 330 and reset any modified dev settings afterward.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cb860213-8b51-4f03-a6d8-9c8aef9e9e46-81","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":70,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2233,"output_tokens":4014,"cache_read_input_tokens":158464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"693a5250-cd3a-4bb4-9c09-ae6a0a963b33"}
