{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_225","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"activeDoc defaults to vale, giving a +15% cursor.\n\nVale's 15% bonus pushes fine-mode speed to roughly 133, exceeding the 120 limit. The summary likely assumed no vale bonus or assist magnet.\n\nThe fine-mode calculation confirms the speed is roughly 129, so it exceeds the 120 limit. The test likely needs to run with a non-vale doctor.\n\nSetting activeDoc to 'quill' removes the vale speed bonus. Fine-mode distance then stays under 120. Sokolova adds assist but not speed. The base cursor numbers are verified separately from the vale bonus.\n\nThe verifier might assume the default vale doctor, causing the fine ≤120 test to fail. The plan explicitly separates the base cursor spec from the vale bonus.\n\nThe 15% vale bonus was added in a prior session. The verifier may audit the tests and check the plan numbers independently. The base cursor spec must hold for non-vale doctors.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c0cc75d4-00b9-4991-99d6-3c00aa351a2c-82","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"15%|1\\.15|Fine|330|120","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4972,"output_tokens":983,"cache_read_input_tokens":160640,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"9bda78d9-fd99-4782-9207-600c4518d152"}
