the source.\\n\\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\\n\\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\\n\\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\\n\\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\\n\\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\\n\\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\\n\\n## This computer\\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\\n\\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\\n  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \\\"Target closed\\\", \\\"page crashed\\\" or \\\"browser has been closed\\\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\\n\\n### What this computer doesn't have\\n\\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\\n\\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\\n\\n### Sharing this computer\\n\\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\\n\\n## Goal\\n\\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\\n\\nScope\\n\\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\\n\\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\\n\\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\\n\\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\\n\\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\\n\\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\\n\\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\\n\\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\\n\\n## Done\\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"4f72ea08-7f9a-430e-a7d2-74f6e53953fd"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_227","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Headless scripts will play the game and check its state, including a full playthrough.\n\nOne command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots are used only where scripts cannot look directly. Playwright 1.63 runs on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. A scripted pad, phone profiles, and two browser frames stand in for the missing hardware.\n\nThe research phase requires reading PLAN.md, the my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.\n\nThe tech stack is plain JavaScript and Web Audio. Engine patches move touch-notice CSS to the bottom and add pointer-events to the Settings button so attract mode stays visible. A comment is updated from \"forbidden token\" to \"stand-in token\" to keep shipped-source clean.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0dfa66a7-ccbf-43ab-bed8-eff5ae93c53a-84","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":1448,"limit":35}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3852,"output_tokens":577,"cache_read_input_tokens":167808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"e5d27b31-c00f-4e4d-b73f-9fd5e36613d5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0dfa66a7-ccbf-43ab-bed8-eff5ae93c53a-84","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1448→      p.mouse = !!inp.mouse;\\n      const trig = inp.trig || 0;\\n1450→      p.trigEdge = trig > 0.3 && p.prevTrig <= 0.3;\\n      p.trigRelease = trig <= 0.3 && p.prevTrig > 0.3;\\n      p.prevTrig = trig;\\n      p.trig = trig;\\n      const gift = !!inp.gift;\\n      p.giftEdge = gift && !p.giftPrev;\\n      p.giftPrev = gift;\\n      const consult = !!inp.consult;\\n      p.consultEdge = consult && !p.consultPrev;\\n      p.consultPrev = consult;\\n1460→      p.cancelEdge = !!inp.cancel;\\n      if (p.cancelEdge) { p.held = 0; p.stroke = null; }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function tryGifts(S, tune) {\\n    for (const p of S.players) {\\n      if (!p.giftEdge) continue;\\n      if (S.breath) { S.breath = false; S.worldScale = 1; pushEv(S, ['breath', 0]); continue; }\\n      const doc = S.activeDoc;\\n1470→      const wantLook = doc === 'sokolova' || (S.gift === 'look' && doc !== 'vale');\\n      const wantBreath = doc === 'vale' || S.gift === 'breath' || (S.gift === 'both' && doc === 'vale');\\n      if (S.gift === 'both') {\\n        if (doc === 'sokolova') { if (secondLook(S, tune)) return; }\\n        else if (S.steady >= 35) { S.breath = true; pushEv(S, ['breath', 1]); return; }\\n      } else if (S.gift === 'look' || wantLook && S.gift !== 'breath') {\\n        secondLook(S, tune);\\n      } else if (wantBreath && S.steady >= 35) {\\n        S.breath = true;\\n        pushEv(S, ['breath', 1]);\\n1480→      }\\n    }\\n    for (const p of S.players) {\",\"content_concise\":\"1448→      p.mouse = !!inp.mouse;\\n      const trig = inp.trig || 0;\\n1450→      p.trigEdge = trig > 0.3 && p.prevTrig <= 0.3;\\n      p.trigRelease = trig <= 0.3 && p.prevTrig > 0.3;\\n      p.prevTrig = trig;\\n      p.trig = trig;\\n      const gift = !!inp.gift;\\n      p.giftEdge = gift && !p.giftPrev;\\n      p.giftPrev = gift;\\n      const consult = !!inp.consult;\\n      p.consultEdge = consult && !p.consultPrev;\\n      p.consultPrev = consult;\\n1460→      p.cancelEdge = !!inp.cancel;\\n      if (p.cancelEdge) { p.held = 0; p.stroke = null; }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function tryGifts(S, tune) {\\n    for (const p of S.players) {\\n      if (!p.giftEdge) continue;\\n      if (S.breath) { S.breath = false; S.worldScale = 1; pushEv(S, ['breath', 0]); continue; }\\n      const doc = S.activeDoc;\\n1470→      const wantLook = doc === 'sokolova' || (S.gift === 'look' && doc !== 'vale');\\n      const wantBreath = doc === 'vale' || S.gift === 'breath' || (S.gift === 'both' && doc === 'vale');\\n      if (S.gift === 'both') {\\n        if (doc === 'sokolova') { if (secondLook(S, tune)) return; }\\n        else if (S.steady >= 35) { S.breath = true; pushEv(S, ['breath', 1]); return; }\\n      } else if (S.gift === 'look' || wantLook && S.gift !== 'breath') {\\n        secondLook(S, tune);\\n      } else if (wantBreath && S.steady >= 35) {\\n        S.breath = true;\\n        pushEv(S, ['breath', 1]);\\n1480→      }\\n    }\\n    for (const p of S.players) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":1448,\"limit\":35,\"raw_output\":\"      p.mouse = !!inp.mouse;\\n      const trig = inp.trig || 0;\\n      p.trigEdge = trig > 0.3 && p.prevTrig <= 0.3;\\n      p.trigRelease = trig <= 0.3 && p.prevTrig > 0.3;\\n      p.prevTrig = trig;\\n      p.trig = trig;\\n      const gift = !!inp.gift;\\n      p.giftEdge = gift && !p.giftPrev;\\n      p.giftPrev = gift;\\n      const consult = !!inp.consult;\\n      p.consultEdge = consult && !p.consultPrev;\\n      p.consultPrev = consult;\\n      p.cancelEdge = !!inp.cancel;\\n      if (p.cancelEdge) { p.held = 0; p.stroke = null; }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function tryGifts(S, tune) {\\n    for (const p of S.players) {\\n      if (!p.giftEdge) continue;\\n      if (S.breath) { S.breath = false; S.worldScale = 1; pushEv(S, ['breath', 0]); continue; }\\n      const doc = S.activeDoc;\\n      const wantLook = doc === 'sokolova' || (S.gift === 'look' && doc !== 'vale');\\n      const wantBreath = doc === 'vale' || S.gift === 'breath' || (S.gift === 'both' && doc === 'vale');\\n      if (S.gift === 'both') {\\n        if (doc === 'sokolova') { if (secondLook(S, tune)) return; }\\n        else if (S.steady >= 35) { S.breath = true; pushEv(S, ['breath', 1]); return; }\\n      } else if (S.gift === 'look' || wantLook && S.gift !== 'breath') {\\n        secondLook(S, tune);\\n      } else if (wantBreath && S.steady >= 35) {\\n        S.breath = true;\\n        pushEv(S, ['breath', 1]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    for (const p of S.players) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":1762}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"6dd65c41-79ad-45c7-9e3a-9a3d3a2b1a63"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_228","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Setting steady 40, gift breath, gift edge, step, and worldScale 0.\n\nWriting a test to verify cursor delta stays unchanged during breaths because cursor updates sit outside step. Also drafting a code-blue test that forces vitals to zero and checks if maybeDie triggers at the end of step.\n\nCode blue triggers at the start of step, not the end. The first step sets the flag and returns early after maybeDie. Later steps run stepCodeBlue and return immediately.\n\nTo hit peaks at 0.9, 1.8, 2.7, and 3.6 seconds, I will step with small dts until near a peak, then press trigger for one frame and release.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6916db09-020c-40df-a315-5c9043c3a136-85","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":1000,"limit":180}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1075,"output_tokens":661,"cache_read_input_tokens":171648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"42c054ef-a2b4-4c5a-9ce2-5446a8ed7b9a"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6916db09-020c-40df-a315-5c9043c3a136-85","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1000→      if (st.wake <= 0) {\\n        st.wake = 6;\\n        /* a reed returns */\\n        if (S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length < 2) {\\n          addObj(S, { type: 'reed', x: st.x - 20 + rnd(S) * 40, y: st.y - 10, order: 1, tag: 'reed', drain: 0, window: false });\\n        }\\n      }\\n      const mass = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'tremass');\\n      if (mass && mass.done && st.stage === 2) {\\n        st.stage = 3;\\n1010→        addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: st.x, y: st.y, axis: [1, 0], depth: 40, order: 4, tag: 'tremolo-pull', tension: 90, drain: 0.2 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (st.stage === 3) {\\n      const pull = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'tremolo-pull');\\n      if (pull && pull.done) {\\n        st.done = true;\\n        for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'reed' && !o.done) { o.done = true; o.alive = false; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n1020→    /* amp falls when a reed is dosed */\\n    const deadReeds = st.reed0 - S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length;\\n    st.amp = clamp(1 - deadReeds * 0.2, 0.15, 1);\\n    if (st.stage >= 2) st.amp = Math.min(st.amp, 0.2);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepDacapo(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt * sp;\\n    let anyDead = false;\\n    for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n1030→      if (L.dead) { anyDead = true; continue; }\\n      const period = L.period / (st.round === 2 ? 2 : 1);\\n      const openFor = L.openFor / (st.round === 2 ? 2 : 1);\\n      const u = st.t % period;\\n      L.open = u < openFor;\\n      const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n      if (o) { o.open = L.open && !L.dead; o.x = L.x; o.y = L.y; if (o.done && !L.dead) { L.dead = true; anyDead = true; if (st.count < 0) st.count = 10; } }\\n    }\\n    if (st.count >= 0) {\\n      st.count -= dt;\\n1040→      if (st.count <= 0 && st.lobes.some(L => L.dead) && st.lobes.some(L => !L.dead)) {\\n        /* from the top */\\n        for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n          L.dead = false;\\n          const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n          if (o) { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.open = false; if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0; }\\n        }\\n        S.vitals -= 8;\\n        st.count = -1;\\n        st.repeated = (st.repeated || 0) + 1;\\n1050→        if (st.round === 1) { st.round = 2; st.t = 0; spawnBeadsN(S, st, 4); }\\n        pushEv(S, ['dacapo', st.repeated]);\\n      } else if (st.count <= 0) st.count = -1;\\n    }\\n    if (st.lobes.every(L => L.dead) && st.count < 0) {\\n      if (st.round === 1) {\\n        st.round = 2; st.t = 0; st.count = -1;\\n        for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n          L.dead = false;\\n          const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n1060→          if (o) { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0; }\\n        }\\n        spawnBeadsN(S, st, 4);\\n        pushEv(S, ['round2', 1]);\\n      } else if (S.objects.every(o => o.type !== 'bead' || o.done)) st.done = true;\\n    }\\n    if (st.round === 2 && st.lobes.every(L => L.dead) && S.objects.every(o => o.type !== 'bead' || o.done || o.tag !== 'dacapo-bead')) st.done = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function spawnBeadsN(S, st, n) {\\n1070→    st.beads = st.beads || [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n      const b = { x: 180 + i * 16, y: 100, tx: 190 + i * 14, ty: 130, x0: 180 + i * 16, y0: 100, landIn: 0.8, flight: 0.8, dead: false, landed: false, hopped: false };\\n      st.beads.push(b);\\n      const o = addObj(S, { type: 'bead', x: b.x, y: b.y, need: 0.12, order: 6, tag: 'dacapo-bead', drain: 0 });\\n      b.oid = o.id;\\n    }\\n    if (!st.kindBead) st.kindBead = true;\\n  }\\n\\n1080→  function stepFermata(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    for (const d of st.domes) if (d.t > 0) d.t -= dt;\\n    st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n    if (st.stage === 1 && st.domes.length === 0 && !(st.eyeOpen > 0)) {\\n      st.eyeOpen = S.breath ? 2.8 : 0.7;\\n      st.eye.open = true;\\n      const o = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n      if (o) o.open = true;\\n    }\\n1090→    if (st.eyeOpen > 0) {\\n      st.eyeOpen -= dt;\\n      if (st.eyeOpen <= 0) {\\n        st.eye.open = false;\\n        const o = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n        if (o && !o.done) o.open = false;\\n        if (st.hits < 3 && st.stage === 1) {\\n          /* raise another dome */\\n          if (st.domes.length < 3) st.domes.push({ x: st.eye.x, y: st.eye.y, r: 34, t: 5 });\\n        }\\n1100→      }\\n    }\\n    const eye = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n    if (eye && eye.done) { st.hits += 1; eye.done = false; eye.alive = true; eye.burn = 0; eye.prog = 0; eye.open = false; st.eye.open = false; }\\n    if (st.hits >= 3 && st.stage === 1) {\\n      st.stage = 2;\\n      st.eye.x = 250; st.eye.y = 90; st.eye.hidden = true;\\n      if (eye) { eye.x = 250; eye.y = 90; eye.hidden = true; eye.marked = false; eye.done = false; eye.alive = true; }\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: 160, y: 140, axis: [1, 0], depth: 12, order: 3, tag: 'sliver-a', drain: 0.1, hidden: true });\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: 180, y: 150, axis: [0.6, 0.8], depth: 12, order: 3, tag: 'sliver-b', drain: 0.1, hidden: true });\\n1110→    }\\n    if (st.stage === 2 && eye && eye.marked && st.hits < 4) { eye.hidden = false; eye.open = true; }\\n    if (st.stage >= 2 && eye && st.hits >= 4) { eye.open = false; eye.drain = 0; }\\n    if (st.stage === 2) {\\n      const slivers = S.objects.filter(o => o.tag === 'sliver-a' || o.tag === 'sliver-b');\\n      if (st.hits >= 4 && slivers.length && slivers.every(o => o.done)) {\\n        st.stage = 3;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: st.eye.x, y: st.eye.y, axis: [0, -1], depth: 28, tension: 40, order: 5, tag: 'fermata-pull', drain: 0.15 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n1120→    if (st.stage === 3) {\\n      const pull = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'fermata-pull');\\n      if (pull && pull.done) {\\n        st.done = true;\\n        if (eye) { eye.done = true; eye.alive = false; eye.open = false; eye.drain = 0; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepCantor(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n1130→    st.t += dt;\\n    if (st.move === 1) {\\n      /* tendrils then uvulas, objects already spawned by the phase */\\n      const left = S.objects.filter(o => (o.tag === 'tendril' || o.tag === 'uvula') && !o.done);\\n      if (!left.length) { st.move = 2; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = true; pushEv(S, ['movement', 2]); spawnVoice(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 2) {\\n      S.flags.hush = true;\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 1);\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'voice') o.window = st.beat > 0.62;\\n      if (st.domes) {\\n1140→        for (const d of st.domes) d.t -= dt;\\n        st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n      }\\n      st.jitter = true;\\n      const voices = S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'voice' && !o.done);\\n      if (!voices.length) { st.move = 3; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = false; st.signs = 0; pushEv(S, ['movement', 3]); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 3) {\\n      st.cycleT = (st.cycleT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (!st.winding && st.cycleT >= 20) { st.winding = 3; st.cycleT = 0; openRepeat(S, st); }\\n      if (st.winding > 0) {\\n1150→        st.winding -= dt;\\n        if (st.winding <= 0) {\\n          const sign = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n          if (sign && !sign.done) {\\n            forceRewind(S, true);\\n            const now = S.strain;\\n            if (now) now.rewound = (now.rewound || 0) + 1;\\n          } else if (sign && sign.done) {\\n            st.signs = (st.signs || 0) + 1;\\n            sign.tag = 'repeat-spent';\\n1160→          }\\n          st.winding = 0;\\n          closeRepeat(S);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if ((st.signs || 0) >= 6 && S.strain === st) { st.move = 4; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; pushEv(S, ['movement', 4]); spawnCoda(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 4) {\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 0.8) / 0.8;\\n      S.flags.onBeat = st.beat < 0.25;\\n      const spiral = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'spiral' && o.tag === 'last-note');\\n1170→      const note = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'the-note');\\n      const wound = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'final-wound');\\n      if (spiral && spiral.done && !st.noteOut) {\\n        st.noteOut = true;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: 213, y: 116, axis: [0, -1], depth: 36, tension: 80, order: 2, tag: 'the-note', drain: 0 });\\n      }\\n      if (note && note.done && !wound) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'wound', x: 213, y: 130, stitches: 6, order: 3, tag: 'final-wound', drain: 0.3 });\\n      }\\n      if (wound && wound.done) st.done = true;\",\"content_concise\":\"1000→      if (st.wake <= 0) {\\n        st.wake = 6;\\n        /* a reed returns */\\n        if (S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length < 2) {\\n          addObj(S, { type: 'reed', x: st.x - 20 + rnd(S) * 40, y: st.y - 10, order: 1, tag: 'reed', drain: 0, window: false });\\n        }\\n      }\\n      const mass = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'tremass');\\n      if (mass && mass.done && st.stage === 2) {\\n        st.stage = 3;\\n1010→        addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: st.x, y: st.y, axis: [1, 0], depth: 40, order: 4, tag: 'tremolo-pull', tension: 90, drain: 0.2 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (st.stage === 3) {\\n      const pull = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'tremolo-pull');\\n      if (pull && pull.done) {\\n        st.done = true;\\n        for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'reed' && !o.done) { o.done = true; o.alive = false; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n1020→    /* amp falls when a reed is dosed */\\n    const deadReeds = st.reed0 - S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length;\\n    st.amp = clamp(1