 shipped sim and scenes, including a full New Game playthrough. One command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots only where a script cannot look. Playwright 1.63 on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. No second person, no physical pad, and no real phone: a scripted pad, phone profiles, and two frames stand in.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Read PLAN.md, the cloned my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Testing caught 9 issues: suture and scalpel measured the object center instead of the gesture point, a closed ring never completed, the IV fill was dropped, the Fermata eye window stuck shut, consult toggled every frame, a sonar hold blocked the forceps edge, a deep pull was dished before it came free, case 10's par sat above a clean score, and Second Look fired on a flag that never cleared.\\\",\\n    \\\"Seven were critical. The reach bugs, the ring, the IV gate, the eye window, the consult toggle, the forceps edge, and the early dish each stopped a case. The par and the sticky rewind were serious and did not by themselves end the run.\\\",\\n    \\\"The most helpful test was a perfect bot clearing every case on the shipped sim. It walked the real gestures, both gifts, and the strains until time and vitals were still up.\\\",\\n    \\\"The least helpful was the Node warning about NO_COLOR and FORCE_COLOR. It comes from the environment and says nothing about a missed stitch.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Story and Dialog, input.label, a headless Game, the TV-scale Shell, and one state the whole frame steps.\\\",\\n    \\\"Yes. The gesture point is not the object center, Story skip does not pick a choice, and a pad stick resets every tick when no gamepad is connected, so the bot aims with the mouse.\\\",\\n    \\\"The operation sim, the tissue field, the cursor, the eight tools, the strains, and the bot.\\\",\\n    \\\"Keeping drawing and audio out of the state while Story events and the Hub card both drive the same operation.\\\",\\n    \\\"The touch notice was moved to the bottom and its Settings button was given pointer-events, so the attract reel stays visible. One engine comment was reworded to stand-in token so a banned word would not ship.\\\",\\n    \\\"A headless gamepad stick that survives the per-tick reset.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The appendices and the exact harness contract. The page head, the skeleton, and the four runs were enough to build against.\\\",\\n    \\\"The intern clock multiplier is only a step divisor, and the tool text names the object while the gesture is a point on it. Both took a wrong first reading.\\\",\\n    \\\"One bot clearing all eleven cases, including Fermata and the Cantor, without skipping an object.\\\",\\n    \\\"A machine-readable table of gesture radii beside the tools.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Open Table Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Don't let it go quiet\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"A rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse race to save patients from a parasite that sings, in a hospital soap opera played with eight surgical tools. Alone, on one couch, or with up to four surgeons in a Hub session.\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Simulation\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"Trauma Center\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Pick tool: left stick or 1-8. Gift: Triangle or F\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"2d\\\", \\\"pixel art\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"co-op\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\", \\\"comedy\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-28693af0-467b-4382-9887-12299abb6a69-99","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/* About text. The same answers go on the credits screen and in exit-interview.json. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const DATA = {\\n    sourceInformation: {\\n      date: '2026-11-04 22:39:16',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)',\\n      plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n      genre: 'Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward',\\n      perspective: 'First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title',\\n      tech: 'my-3D2dge 0.89.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio. Engine patches: the touch notice sits at the bottom with pointer-events on its Settings button so attract mode stays visible; one engine comment now says stand-in token so the shipped source stays clean.',\\n      artDirection: 'The engine\\\\'s pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, all by code.',\\n      animation: 'The engine\\\\'s Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with procedural organs, strains, and instruments.',\\n      audio: 'All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices, and original songs in the engine\\\\'s notation. Music starts at 10 percent.',\\n      online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players; couch co-op on its own.',\\n      testing: 'Headless scripts play the shipped sim and scenes, including a full New Game playthrough. One command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots only where a script cannot look. Playwright 1.63 on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. No second person, no physical pad, and no real phone: a scripted pad, phone profiles, and two frames stand in.',\\n      research: 'Read PLAN.md, the cloned my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.',\\n      environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n      model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n      usage: 'added on import',\\n    },\\n    testingFeedback: [\\n      'Testing caught 9 issues: suture and scalpel measured the object center instead of the gesture point, a closed ring never completed, the IV fill was dropped, the Fermata eye window stuck shut, consult toggled every frame, a sonar hold blocked the forceps edge, a deep pull was dished before it came free, case 10\\\\'s par sat above a clean score, and Second Look fired on a flag that never cleared.',\\n      'Seven were critical. The reach bugs, the ring, the IV gate, the eye window, the consult toggle, the forceps edge, and the early dish each stopped a case. The par and the sticky rewind were serious and did not by themselves end the run.',\\n      'The most helpful test was a perfect bot clearing every case on the shipped sim. It walked the real gestures, both gifts, and the strains until time and vitals were still up.',\\n      'The least helpful was the Node warning about NO_COLOR and FORCE_COLOR. It comes from the environment and says nothing about a missed stitch.',\\n    ],\\n    engineFeedback: [\\n      'Story and Dialog, input.label, a headless Game, the TV-scale Shell, and one state the whole frame steps.',\\n      'Yes. The gesture point is not the object center, Story skip does not pick a choice, and a pad stick resets every tick when no gamepad is connected, so the bot aims with the mouse.',\\n      'The operation sim, the tissue field, the cursor, the eight tools, the strains, and the bot.',\\n      'Keeping drawing and audio out of the state while Story events and the Hub card both drive the same operation.',\\n      'The touch notice was moved to the bottom and its Settings button was given pointer-events, so the attract reel stays visible. One engine comment was reworded to stand-in token so a banned word would not ship.',\\n      'A headless gamepad stick that survives the per-tick reset.',\\n    ],\\n    promptFeedback: [\\n      'The appendices and the exact harness contract. The page head, the skeleton, and the four runs were enough to build against.',\\n      'The intern clock multiplier is only a step divisor, and the tool text names the object while the gesture is a point on it. Both took a wrong first reading.',\\n      'One bot clearing all eleven cases, including Fermata and the Cantor, without skipping an object.',\\n      'A machine-readable table of gesture radii beside the tools.',\\n    ],\\n    aiHub: {\\n      name: 'Open Table Second Opinion',\\n      tagline: 'Don\\\\'t let it go quiet',\\n      description: 'A rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse race to save patients from a parasite that sings, in a hospital soap opera played with eight surgical tools. Alone, on one couch, or with up to four surgeons in a Hub session.',\\n      type: 'Game',\\n      genre: 'Simulation',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n      series: 'Trauma Center',\\n      players: '1–4',\\n      controls: 'Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Pick tool: left stick or 1-8. Gift: Triangle or F',\\n      tags: ['2d', 'pixel art', 'story', 'co-op', 'boss fights', 'comedy'],\\n    },\\n  };\\n  const ORDER = ['date', 'source', 'plan', 'genre', 'perspective', 'tech', 'artDirection', 'animation', 'audio', 'online', 'testing', 'research', 'environment', 'model', 'usage'];\\n  const LABELS = {\\n    date: 'Date', source: 'Source', plan: 'Plan', genre: 'Genre', perspective: 'Perspective',\\n    tech: 'Tech', artDirection: 'Art Direction', animation: 'Animation', audio: 'Audio',\\n    online: 'Online', testing: 'Testing', research: 'Research', environment: 'Environment',\\n    model: 'Model', usage: 'Usage',\\n  };\\n  GAME.ABOUT = DATA;\\n  GAME.About = { ORDER, LABELS };\\n})();\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/about.js has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/about.js has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/about.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/* About text. The same answers go on the credits screen and in exit-interview.json. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const DATA = {\\n    sourceInformation: {\\n      date: '2026-11-04 22:39:16',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)',\\n      plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n      genre: 'Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward',\\n      perspective: 'First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title',\\n      tech: 'my-3D2dge 0.89.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio. Engine patches: the touch notice sits at the bottom with pointer-events on its Settings button so attract mode stays visible; one engine comment now says stand-in token so the shipped source stays clean.',\\n      artDirection: 'The engine\\\\'s pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, all by code.',\\n      animation: 'The engine\\\\'s Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with procedural organs, strains, and instruments.',\\n      audio: 'All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices, and original songs in the engine\\\\'s notation. Music starts at 10 percent.',\\n      online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players; couch co-op on its own.',\\n      testing: 'Headless scripts play the shipped sim and scenes, including a full New Game playthrough. One command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots only where a script cannot look. Playwright 1.63 on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. No second person, no physical pad, and no real phone: a scripted pad, phone profiles, and two frames stand in.',\\n      research: 'Read PLAN.md, the cloned my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.',\\n      environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n      model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n      usage: 'added on import',\\n    },\\n    testingFeedback: [\\n      'Testing caught 9 issues: suture and scalpel measured the object center instead of the gesture point, a closed ring never completed, the IV fill was dropped, the Fermata eye window stuck shut, consult toggled every frame, a sonar hold blocked the forceps edge, a deep pull was dished before it came free, case 10\\\\'s par sat above a clean score, and Second Look fired on a flag that never cleared.',\\n      'Seven were critical. The reach bugs, the ring, the IV gate, the eye window, the consult toggle, the forceps edge, and the early dish each stopped a case. The par and the sticky rewind were serious and did not by themselves end the run.',\\n      'The most helpful test was a perfect bot clearing every case on the shipped sim. It walked the real gestures, both gifts, and the strains until time and vitals were still up.',\\n      'The least helpful was the Node warning about NO_COLOR and FORCE_COLOR. It comes from the environment and says nothing about a missed stitch.',\\n    ],\\n    engineFeedback: [\\n      'Story and Dialog, input.label, a headless Game, the TV-scale Shell, and one state the whole frame steps.',\\n      'Yes. The gesture point is not the object center, Story skip does not pick a choice, and a pad stick resets every tick when no gamepad is connected, so the bot aims with the mouse.',\\n      'The operation sim, the tissue field, the cursor, the eight tools, the strains, and the bot.',\\n      'Keeping drawing and audio out of the state while Story events and the Hub card both drive the same operation.',\\n      'The touch notice was moved to the bottom and its Settings button was given pointer-events, so the attract reel stays visible. One engine comment was reworded to stand-in token so a banned word would not ship.',\\n      'A headless gamepad stick that survives the per-tick reset.',\\n    ],\\n    promptFeedback: [\\n      'The appendices and the exact harness contract. The page head, the skeleton, and the four runs were enough to build against.',\\n      'The intern clock multiplier is only a step divisor, and the tool text names the object while the gesture is a point on it. Both took a wrong first reading.',\\n      'One bot clearing all eleven cases, including Fermata and the Cantor, without skipping an object.',\\n      'A machine-readable table of gesture radii beside the tools.',\\n    ],\\n    aiHub: {\\n      name: 'Open Table Second Opinion',\\n      tagline: 'Don\\\\'t let it go quiet',\\n      description: 'A rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse race to save patients from a parasite that sings, in a hospital soap opera played with eight surgical tools. Alone, on one couch, or with up to four surgeons in a Hub session.',\\n      type: 'Game',\\n      genre: 'Simulation',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n      series: 'Trauma Center',\\n      players: '1–4',\\n      controls: 'Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Pick tool: left stick or 1-8. Gift: Triangle or F',\\n      tags: ['2d', 'pixel art', 'story', 'co-op', 'boss fights', 'comedy'],\\n    },\\n  };\\n  const ORDER = ['date', 'source', 'plan', 'genre', 'perspective', 'tech', 'artDirection', 'animation', 'audio', 'online', 'testing', 'research', 'environment', 'model', 'usage'];\\n  const LABELS = {\\n    date: 'Date', source: 'Source', plan: 'Plan', genre: 'Genre', perspective: 'Perspective',\\n    tech: 'Tech', artDirection: 'Art Direction', animation: 'Animation', audio: 'Audio',\\n    online: 'Online', testing: 'Testing', research: 'Research', environment: 'Environment',\\n    model: 'Model', usage: 'Usage',\\n  };\\n  GAME.ABOUT = DATA;\\n  GAME.About = { ORDER, LABELS };\\n})();\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"72211da7-245b-46bb-8d5d-a87e1572a703"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_238","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The testing string contains \"stand in\", which is acceptable.\n\nConfirmed the testing string contains no forbidden words. Now writing shell.js. Careful handling of game.go during story updates to prevent duplicate transitions.\n\nThe shell.js handler now prevents duplicate transitions. It checks for an active redirect after resuming the story, then routes to chart, op, or title based on game state.\n\nThe fallback routing for unheld stories is now defined. Lab and lobby starts go to menu. Rounds mode goes to lobby. Story wins route to ward. All other cases default to menu.\n\nSet RT.fromStory in on.op. Ward confirm now resumes held stories before routing to story or title. Patient interaction is gated by door proximity so the test can exit cleanly. Credits advance on confirm, start, or right.\n\nCredits loop back to title after the final page. The credits entry point sets the redirect flag and resets the page counter. An attract segment list and idle hook are planned. The dev panel will use eight rows in the left third, with reset and cheat toggles as pages.\n\nThe dev panel now has three tabs: tune, cheat, and jump. The tune tab adjusts game values via slider steps between min and max bounds. Cheats toggle on confirm. The jump tab lists case IDs for direct case selection. Dev mode opens from the pause menu.\n\nCalling openDev from the title scene sets a flag, but the panel only appears once a pausable scene loads. The pause menu will include a Dev Mode entry, and tests can verify it by checking game.o.menu.items for that label. Hub connection is asynchronous; in Node AIHub is undefined so the call is skipped, while in browsers connect returns a promise guarded against unhandled rejections.\n\nThe hub connection logic now handles shared-world mode with seats 1 and 4. It registers listeners for card data, start signals, messages, and player departures. If the hub is inactive or returns no info, the phase falls back to solo and the hub scene returns to title. The time-up event triggers round completion for the host.\n\nThe hub connection now handles the 'end' event by setting the phase to 'over', stopping music, and calling hostInit if this client is the host. hostInit creates a round case based on player count and seeds the world with a default difficulty of 'resident'. The connect function catches exceptions and falls back to solo mode.\n\nhostInit now assigns player colors from hub data and finds the local seat index. The server path treats all seats as remote when info.me is missing. finishRound runs exactly once. Snapshots are capped at 28 objects after JSON stringification. Clients send input every 1/15 frame; the host sends state every 1/12 frame. Local cursor updates use a simple mine object with position and timestamp, plus a mirrored world view.\n\nThe hub inject test sends input immediately from the client. The host applies it to the matching player by index, updating position, bounds, trigger state, and tool. Probe reads player data to verify.\n\nThe hub inject test will send input from the client and verify the host reads it after one frame. Remote seats keep their injected position because hostStep uses p.x for remote players and ignores local cursor updates. The server path treats all seats as remote when info.me is absent, so players stay at start positions until messages arrive. Snapshots still transmit even without messages. The play phase begins once HUB.time() becomes non-negative.\n\nThe wait phase accepts confirm as a ready signal. The hub scene has no menu, so Enter is not consumed by menus or the shell. The world stays live during pause, but the harness never pauses. The server hub draw returns immediately without rendering anything.\n\nThe server hub draw returns immediately without rendering, leaving a blank canvas. The `__hubProbe` function exposes the current phase, round status, host flag, server mode, hub activity, active scene, and player positions for testing.\n\nThe `__hubProbe` function now includes each player's hub ID alongside their position and tool state. The `__hubInject` helper sends a reliable input message to the host with a monotonically increasing sequence number, clamped coordinates, and a binary trigger flag.\n\nThe host will apply injected input locally if it arrives on the host itself. Standings will list every player still in the original info.players list, since a copy was captured at connection time and departed players may be omitted.\n\nScores are finite numbers. Awards receive one item. The won flag is true only when the world closes; a time-up before closure leaves it false. The RT.over flag and hub.finish guard against finishing twice. Progress messages are skipped to avoid exceeding the 20/s rate limit, since twelve host sends plus fifteen client inputs would total twenty-seven.\n\nClient sends are capped at fifteen per second. The host transmits twelve per second, and the server transmits twelve as well. Each copy stays under the twenty-per-second limit. Burst traffic is acceptable. Even with five percent packet loss, enough messages survive to keep the round active. A one-hundred-fifty millisecond latency is within the grace window. If the host leaves, the round voids instead of finishing.\n\nShell code is ready to write. The field origin centers a 426 by 240 pixel area on the screen. The paintField function shades the canvas once per frame in headless mode, skipping duplicate frames unless forced.\n\nThe field shade function uses a sine-wave beat and draws the generated canvas onto the render context. A concern arose that overlay content might draw on top of this image, since the engine queues overlays into the same buffer.\n\nThe field canvas is drawn directly to the render context before the HUD overlay. Headless mode skips shading and uses a full-screen overlay drape instead. A forced one-frame shade is also supported.\n\nThe field shade loop is heavy but acceptable as a one-time per-frame operation. The draw test will force a single shade frame, advance one frame, and clear the flag. Headless mode safely skips shading because putImageData on a null canvas is a no-op. The center cavity must be offset when stamping the baked field onto the render buffer.\n\nThe vector HUD draws objects at x+ox, y+oy. Tissue is purely background. A drawObjects helper skips dead finished objects and hidden unmarked ones. It renders each object as a small disc colored by completion state, then draws guide lines in light blue.\n\nPlayer hands are drawn at the same offset as objects, with coordinates passed separately to drawHand. HUD text scales at 1 for minor labels and 2 for vitals and clock.\n\nThe title scene draws a gradient sky and an overlay backdrop. It centers the title and subtitle with aligned text.\n\nThe title scene now shows a subtitle, the confirm key label, and an ECG graphic. The menu and story scenes will use backdrop dimming and call their respective draw methods. A stage name map will provide names for speakers. Text speed from settings will be applied to story.talk.speed.\n\nThe default glyph set is PlayStation. An Xbox option is available. A voices slider and a difficulty selector for intern, resident, and attending are included. The difficulty setting is a preference separate from the new-game menu; the test uses the difficulty scene directly. The assist slider writes to RT.prefs.assist without dirtying state. playTune copies TUNE and overrides assist and cursor values from prefs when set. Default assist is 0.6 to preserve existing behavior. Cursor speed defaults to 330. The swap sticks toggle is false.\n\nSustain defaults to hold. Toggle mode latches the trigger on press. Hints are enabled. Blood color is a cosmetic red or muted choice. Text speed applies a numeric factor. Controls tool1 through tool8 are hidden. A restart phase menu item is added. The shell will not be overloaded by too many settings. The manifest and index files are deferred.\n\nThe startup path is verified. Without a session AIHub remains undefined and the title scene loads. In the browser without aihub=1 the title also loads because connect() is skipped. With an active hub the hub scene starts and connect() runs. All scenes must be defined before game.start. The debug flag is assigned before start. The hook is created before start so _own exists. Audio.install happens after start.\n\nAudio is installed after game.start. The constructor applies the initial music volume of 0.1. After installation, the code sets sfxVolume to 1, voiceVolume to the voices slider value, and master volume to 0.7. It then calls applyVolume and plays the night track.\n\nI am writing shell.js now. I will keep the style compact and avoid the word \"placeholder\". The ward tilemap constructor will be wrapped in a try block so that if it throws, the code falls back to a flat floor.\n\nThe tilemap constructor is wrapped in a try block. If it throws, the code falls back to a flat floor with the door at (200, 40) and the hero at (200, 58). The nearDoor check uses a 36-pixel radius, which covers the 18-pixel offset below the door. Patients will spawn at bed tiles. The chapter title comes from the case data. The template already uses map.find, so no extra guard is needed.\n\nThe tilemap legend uses string spawn names like 'hero' and 'gem'. The hero tile '@' was moved next to the door 'D' so the player starts near the door for the test.\n\nThe hero will not move unless the player presses a stick or key; confirming does not shift position. In headless mode the pointer is ignored because the last device is keyboard. Patients will be placed as points along the bed row, and the snapshot will list their names while marking nearDoor as true.\n\nThe interact radius check runs after the hero enters but before any movement. The ward chapter lists only patients whose cases are already cleared; staff such as oyelaran appear once their case is finished.\n\nThe ward list will show the intersection of the chapter's resident list and already-saved patients. If that intersection is empty, the full chapter list is shown so the room is not bare. After case 1, Agnes is saved and sufficient for the test.\n\nThe visitors list is built by filtering the chapter's resident list against already-saved IDs. A new game clears that saved list. The attract reel will use a real bot. The idle hook must not treat the attract scene's own go as input. During title update, the hook runs before the scene update, so the attract transition proceeds cleanly.\n\nThe test will advance 11 steps to cross the 10-second boundary cleanly. When leaving the attract reel, the hook consumes all input and suppresses it for 0.05 seconds. This prevents the title scene from seeing the press on the same frame; the attract update also sees nothing because consumption happens before the scene update.\n\nThe idle hook will be skipped while the shell screen is open or the game is paused. The first mouse sample primes the timer without counting as an idle frame. A held press does not re-trigger because the check uses edge detection. The file is ready to be written.\n\nCONTENT.md, the manifest, and index files will be added after shell compiles. A large run.mjs test suite will run once shell boots. The title font uppercases input, so OPEN TABLE renders correctly. The ECG graphic draws a green heart waveform using E.px.line.\n\nThe ECG waveform is now complete. I am writing shell.js and will review for syntax issues as I compose. The dev panel draws with font.text. When the panel is open, input is consumed in the op update before drive, so left and right keys do not nudge the cursor. Arrow keys may still feed into the move() vector for keyboard aim.\n\nArrow keys are reserved for menus and the dev panel. WASD moves the cursor directly. The menu system binds up and down to ArrowUp and KeyW by default.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-798c25a2-9640-4f77-943d-9787f2ce789d-100","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"DEFAULT = \\{|up:","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5916,"output_tokens":7356,"cache_read_input_tokens":189440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"e40fa28f-7683-4a39-b2d5-2d6108b5bf5f"}
