01,111,117,116,40,49,50,48,48,41,59,32,112,114,105,110,116,40,39,115,116,97,110,100,97,108,111,110,101,39,44,32,112,103,46,101,118,97,108,117,97,116,101,40,34,40,41,32,61,62,32,40,123,32,97,99,116,105,118,101,58,32,65,73,72,117,98,46,97,99,116,105,118,101,44,32,112,114,111,98,101,58,32,119,105,110,100,111,119,46,95,95,104,117,98,80,114,111,98,101,40,41,32,125,41,34,41,44,32,101,114,114,115,91,58,51,93,41,59,32,112,103,46,99,108,111,115,101,40,41,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":19,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"- Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\"},{\"line_number\":121,\"content\":\"10. **Menus at TV size.** The pause and settings menus are the engine's HTML, too small for 10 feet by default. `new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, theme })`, made before `game.start`, scales them for a TV: at 1080p a row is 94 px tall, six pause rows fit, and with Save and Load added the last of eight rows falls below the screen, where moving the focus scrolls to it, as it does on the long Settings screen. Canvas menus: `new E.Menu(game, items, { scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (`rows` scrolls; hover and click still work; `menu.rowAt(i)` gives a row's box, for tests). Reduce density too: the page head in Appendix D carries CSS that shows a Settings row's help only on the focused row. Keep its `html` prefix: the engine injects its own CSS at runtime, and the same specificity could lose to it.\"},{\"line_number\":123,\"content\":\"12. **The Hub works on this engine.** The skeleton in Appendix D passed all four harness scenarios (14 or 15 checks each) and still runs standalone. The options that matter in a session are `live: true`, `autoPause: false`, `corner: false`, `menu.quit: false`.\"},{\"line_number\":641,\"content\":\"Follow the protocol page and Appendix D. Exact behavior:\"},{\"line_number\":643,\"content\":\"- `AIHub.active`: no title, menus or attract. `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })` early, then `AIHub.ready()` with no key press when the world is built. `null` means no Hub: run as usual.\"},{\"line_number\":644,\"content\":\"- **Your own card** (`card: true`): the theatre's whiteboard showing the game's name, each player in their color with a tick when ready, how to win, this player's controls from the device they used last, and the time left from the `card` event. Enter, ✕ or a tap answers `ready`. △ or M, named on the card, answers `more`. No menus, no settings, no choices. Use `AIHub.rng('card')` for anything random.\"},{\"line_number\":645,\"content\":\"- `start`: count down on the card until `AIHub.time() >= 0`, then play.\"},{\"line_number\":646,\"content\":\"- `Math.random` is not seeded in shared world, and the sim never uses it anyway: the host seeds from `AIHub.rng('sim')`.\"},{\"line_number\":648,\"content\":\"- `time-up`: the host calls `finish` at once, with `won: false` unless the patient is already closed. Patient closed or lost: the host sends a last reliable state, then `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })`.\"},{\"line_number\":650,\"content\":\"- `AIHub.server`: the host's copy has no player, camera or input. It runs the world and draws nothing.\"},{\"line_number\":651,\"content\":\"- A touch-only copy can answer the card by tap, then shows the notice and watches: no touch controls in a session either, and no `AIHub.fail`.\"},{\"line_number\":924,\"content\":\"tests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\"},{\"line_number\":966,\"content\":\"const inSession = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active);\"},{\"line_number\":1010,\"content\":\"- **Hub harness, all four runs (Appendix D's runner):** `players=2&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Then open the page outside a session.\"},{\"line_number\":1025,\"content\":\"| M0 | Title picked. Folders, vendor, manifest, bundler, dev page, test runner, Hub client in the page | Empty game builds, runs, one test passes, harness runner works on Appendix D |\"},{\"line_number\":1236,\"content\":\"## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\"},{\"line_number\":1256,\"content\":\"const E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\"},{\"line_number\":1269,\"content\":\"async function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\"},{\"line_number\":1315,\"content\":\"        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"1c083e86-1aa8-4ed9-b887-27df062b6740"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_244","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to read the Appendix D skeleton in PLAN.md and examine the Game constructor for scene registration.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e085fc2d-458a-4d5c-82f1-12cb675ee75d-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md","offset":1236,"limit":220}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e085fc2d-458a-4d5c-82f1-12cb675ee75d-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","offset":2280,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e085fc2d-458a-4d5c-82f1-12cb675ee75d-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","offset":2680,"limit":220}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3659,"output_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":58752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"384445ca-2007-460d-ae6e-130de1349170"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e085fc2d-458a-4d5c-82f1-12cb675ee75d-14","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1236→## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\\n\\n**Page head.** Order matters.\\n\\n1240→```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>…</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body><!-- E.bootSplash's markup here --><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>/* engine */</script><script>/* game */</script></body></html>\\n```\\n1250→\\n**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\\n\\n```js\\n// Hub skeleton: shared world on my-3D2dge. The host's copy runs the world; other copies mirror it and send their own hands.\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst game = window.G = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  input: { ...base, useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] }, menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\\n1260→const NAME = 'SKELETON', W0 = 426, H0 = 240, DOTS = 12;\\nlet info = null, phase = 'wait', card = null, over = false, sent = 0, heardSeq = 0, S = { v: 70, dots: [], p: {} }, mine = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0 }, rng = null;\\nconst place = () => ({ x: 40 + rng() * 340, y: 40 + rng() * 160 });\\nfunction hostInit() { rng = HUB.rng('deal'); S.dots = Array.from({ length: DOTS }, (_, id) => ({ id, ...place(), alive: 1 })); for (const q of info.players) S.p[q.id] = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0, score: 0, gone: false }; }\\nfunction finish(won) { if (over) return; over = true; if (HUB.server !== true && info.me != null && S.p[info.me]) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  const live = info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).sort((a, b) => S.p[b.id].score - S.p[a.id].score), standings = [];\\n  for (const q of live) { const last = standings[standings.length - 1]; if (last && S.p[last[0]].score === S.p[q.id].score) last.push(q.id); else standings.push([q.id]); }\\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(info.players.map(q => [q.id, S.p[q.id].score]));\\n  HUB.send({ t: 'over', v: S.v }); HUB.finish({ standings, scores, won, awards: live.length ? [{ id: live[0].id, title: 'Steadiest Hand', detail: scores[live[0].id] + ' clean actions' }] : [] }); }\\nasync function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n1270→  if (!info) { phase = 'solo'; return; }\\n  HUB.on('card', c => { card = c; });\\n  HUB.on('start', () => { phase = 'count'; });\\n  HUB.on('message', (d, from) => { if (info.isHost) { const p = S.p[from]; if (d.t === 'i' && p && d.n > (p.n || 0)) { p.n = d.n; p.x = d.x; p.y = d.y; p.t = d.t2; } } else if (from === info.host) { if (d.t === 's' && d.n > heardSeq) { heardSeq = d.n; S.v = d.v; S.dots = d.o.map(([id, x, y]) => ({ id, x, y, alive: 1 })); for (const [id, x, y, t, sc] of d.p) { const q = S.p[id] || (S.p[id] = {}); if (id !== info.me) { q.x = x; q.y = y; q.t = t; } q.score = sc; } } if (d.t === 'over') over = true; } });\\n  HUB.on('leave', ({ id }) => { if (S.p[id]) S.p[id].gone = true; });\\n  HUB.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) finish(false); });\\n  HUB.on('end', () => { phase = 'over'; game.audio.music(null); game.audio.mute(true); });\\n  if (info.isHost) hostInit();\\n  HUB.ready(); }\\nfunction step(dt) { const I = game.input, m = I.move(), a = I.padAim, ptr = I.pointer(); let dx = (a ? a[0] : 0) + m[0], dy = (a ? a[1] : 0) + m[1]; mine.x = E.clamp(mine.x + dx * 300 * dt, 0, W0); mine.y = E.clamp(mine.y + dy * 300 * dt, 0, H0); if (ptr && I.lastDevice === 'mouse') { mine.x = ptr[0]; mine.y = ptr[1]; } mine.t = I.value('useTool'); }\\n1280→let snapN = 0, inN = 0, acc = 0;\\nfunction hostStep(dt) { S.v = Math.max(0, S.v - .05 * dt); if (info.me != null && S.p[info.me] && !info.server) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  for (const id in S.p) { const p = S.p[id]; if (p.gone || !p.t) continue; for (const d of S.dots) if (d.alive && Math.hypot(d.x - p.x, d.y - p.y) < 12) { d.alive = 0; p.score++; } } S.dots = S.dots.filter(d => d.alive); if (!S.dots.length) finish(true); }\\ngame.start({ scene: 'hub', scenes: { hub: { pausable: true, camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false },\\n  update(dt) { const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n    if (!info && !inSession) return;\\n    if (phase === 'wait' && info) { if (I.pressed('confirm')) HUB.answer('ready'); if (I.pressed('more')) HUB.answer('more'); const c = I.clicked(); if (c) HUB.answer(c[1] > game.H * .7 ? 'more' : 'ready'); }\\n    if (phase === 'count' && HUB.time() >= 0) phase = 'play';\\n    if (phase === 'play' && !over) { step(dt); if (info.isHost) hostStep(dt); acc += dt; if (acc >= 1 / 12) { acc = 0; if (info.isHost) HUB.send({ t: 's', n: ++snapN, v: Math.round(S.v), o: S.dots.map(d => [d.id, d.x | 0, d.y | 0]), p: info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).map(q => { const p = S.p[q.id]; return [q.id, p.x | 0, p.y | 0, p.t > .25 ? 1 : 0, p.score | 0]; }) }, { reliable: false }); else HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++inN, x: mine.x | 0, y: mine.y | 0, t2: mine.t > .25 ? 1 : 0 }, { to: info.host, reliable: false }); } } },\\n  draw(r) { if (info && info.server) return; r.sky(['#143a36', '#14504a']); r.overlay(g => { E.font.text(g, NAME + ' ' + phase + (card && card.left != null ? ' ' + Math.ceil(card.left / 1000) : ''), 8, 8, '#fff', { outline: false }); for (const d of S.dots) px.disc(g, d.x, d.y, 4, '#5ff0e0'); if (info) for (const q of info.players) { const p = q.id === info.me ? mine : S.p[q.id]; if (p && !(S.p[q.id] || {}).gone) { px.disc(g, p.x, p.y, 5, q.color); E.font.text(g, q.name.slice(0, 12), p.x + 7, p.y - 4, q.color, { outline: false }); } } }); } } } });\\n1290→window.__hubProbe = () => ({ phase, over, dots: S.dots.length, v: S.v, t: HUB.active ? HUB.time() : 0 });\\nconnect();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n**Harness runner.** The folder needs the game (as `game.html`) and copies of `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. It uses an OS-picked port, checks the frame's title is your game (replace the print with a test), and stops only its own server, by handle.\\n\\n```python\\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n1300→folder = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1])\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=folder, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True)\\ntry:\\n    line = srv.stdout.readline(); port = int(re.search(r'port (\\\\d+)', line).group(1))\\n    base = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/'\\n    RUNS = ['players=2&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1', 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1']\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        b = p.chromium.launch(args=['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\\n        for q in RUNS:\\n            pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); pg.goto(base + 'harness.html?game=game.html&' + q)\\n1310→            try: pg.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=90000)\\n            except Exception as e: print('TIMEOUT', q)\\n            r = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const h = window.__hubCheck; return h ? { pass: h.pass, failed: h.checks.filter(c => !c.pass).map(c => c.name + ': ' + c.detail), n: h.checks.length } : null }\\\")\\n            title = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const f = document.querySelector('iframe'); try { return f && f.contentDocument && f.contentDocument.title } catch (e) { return 'x' } }\\\")\\n            print(q, json.dumps(r)[:700], 'title:', title); pg.close()\\n        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\\n        b.close()\\nfinally:\\n    srv.terminate(); srv.wait(timeout=5)\\n```\\n1320→\\n## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\\n\\n**A DualSense in the standard mapping, for Playwright's `add_init_script`.** Set `__pad.axes[0..3]` (left x, left y, right x, right y), `__pad.buttons[i].value` and `.pressed`: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 12 to 15 D-pad, and bump `__pad.timestamp`.\\n\\n```js\\n(() => { const axes = [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons = Array.from({ length: 18 }, () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\\n  const pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes, buttons,\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); }, reset() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); } } };\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n1330→```\\n\\n**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\\n\\n```js\\nd.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:48px 24px 24px;text-align:center;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(5,3,12,.92) 45%);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\\n// and on the button, add pointer-events:auto to its inline style\\n```\\n\\nNote it in your Engine Feedback.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1236→## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\\n\\n**Page head.** Order matters.\\n\\n1240→```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>…</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body><!-- E.bootSplash's markup here --><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>/* engine */</script><script>/* game */</script></body></html>\\n```\\n1250→\\n**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\\n\\n```js\\n// Hub skeleton: shared world on my-3D2dge. The host's copy runs the world; other copies mirror it and send their own hands.\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst game = window.G = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  input: { ...base, useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] }, menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\\n1260→const NAME = 'SKELETON', W0 = 426, H0 = 240, DOTS = 12;\\nlet info = null, phase = 'wait', card = null, over = false, sent = 0, heardSeq = 0, S = { v: 70, dots: [], p: {} }, mine = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0 }, rng = null;\\nconst place = () => ({ x: 40 + rng() * 340, y: 40 + rng() * 160 });\\nfunction hostInit() { rng = HUB.rng('deal'); S.dots = Array.from({ length: DOTS }, (_, id) => ({ id, ...place(), alive: 1 })); for (const q of info.players) S.p[q.id] = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0, score: 0, gone: false }; }\\nfunction finish(won) { if (over) return; over = true; if (HUB.server !== true && info.me != null && S.p[info.me]) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  const live = info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).sort((a, b) => S.p[b.id].score - S.p[a.id].score), standings = [];\\n  for (const q of live) { const last = standings[standings.length - 1]; if (last && S.p[last[0]].score === S.p[q.id].score) last.push(q.id); else standings.push([q.id]); }\\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(info.players.map(q => [q.id, S.p[q.id].score]));\\n  HUB.send({ t: 'over', v: S.v }); HUB.finish({ standings, scores, won, awards: live.length ? [{ id: live[0].id, title: 'Steadiest Hand', detail: scores[live[0].id] + ' clean actions' }] : [] }); }\\nasync function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n1270→  if (!info) { phase = 'solo'; return; }\\n  HUB.on('card', c => { card = c; });\\n  HUB.on('start', () => { phase = 'count'; });\\n  HUB.on('message', (d, from) => { if (info.isHost) { const p = S.p[from]; if (d.t === 'i' && p && d.n > (p.n || 0)) { p.n = d.n; p.x = d.x; p.y = d.y; p.t = d.t2; } } else if (from === info.host) { if (d.t === 's' && d.n > heardSeq) { heardSeq = d.n; S.v = d.v; S.dots = d.o.map(([id, x, y]) => ({ id, x, y, alive: 1 })); for (const [id, x, y, t, sc] of d.p) { const q = S.p[id] || (S.p[id] = {}); if (id !== info.me) { q.x = x; q.y = y; q.t = t; } q.score = sc; } } if (d.t === 'over') over = true; } });\\n  HUB.on('leave', ({ id }) => { if (S.p[id]) S.p[id].gone = true; });\\n  HUB.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) finish(false); });\\n  HUB.on('end', () => { phase = 'over'; game.audio.music(null); game.audio.mute(true); });\\n  if (info.isHost) hostInit();\\n  HUB.ready(); }\\nfunction step(dt) { const I = game.input, m = I.move(), a = I.padAim, ptr = I.pointer(); let dx = (a ? a[0] : 0) + m[0], dy = (a ? a[1] : 0) + m[1]; mine.x = E.clamp(mine.x + dx * 300 * dt, 0, W0); mine.y = E.clamp(mine.y + dy * 300 * dt, 0, H0); if (ptr && I.lastDevice === 'mouse') { mine.x = ptr[0]; mine.y = ptr[1]; } mine.t = I.value('useTool'); }\\n1280→let snapN = 0, inN = 0, acc = 0;\\nfunction hostStep(dt) { S.v = Math.max(0, S.v - .05 * dt); if (info.me != null && S.p[info.me] && !info.server) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  for (const id in S.p) { const p = S.p[id]; if (p.gone || !p.t) continue; for (const d of S.dots) if (d.alive && Math.hypot(d.x - p.x, d.y - p.y) < 12) { d.alive = 0; p.score++; } } S.dots = S.dots.filter(d => d.alive); if (!S.dots.length) finish(true); }\\ngame.start({ scene: 'hub', scenes: { hub: { pausable: true, camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false },\\n  update(dt) { const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n    if (!info && !inSession) return;\\n    if (phase === 'wait' && info) { if (I.pressed('confirm')) HUB.answer('ready'); if (I.pressed('more')) HUB.answer('more'); const c = I.clicked(); if (c) HUB.answer(c[1] > game.H * .7 ? 'more' : 'ready'); }\\n    if (phase === 'count' && HUB.time() >= 0) phase = 'play';\\n    if (phase === 'play' && !over) { step(dt); if (info.isHost) hostStep(dt); acc += dt; if (acc >= 1 / 12) { acc = 0; if (info.isHost) HUB.send({ t: 's', n: ++snapN, v: Math.round(S.v), o: S.dots.map(d => [d.id, d.x | 0, d.y | 0]), p: info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).map(q => { const p = S.p[q.id]; return [q.id, p.x | 0, p.y | 0, p.t > .25 ? 1 : 0, p.score | 0]; }) }, { reliable: false }); else HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++inN, x: mine.x | 0, y: mine.y | 0, t2: mine.t > .25 ? 1 : 0 }, { to: info.host, reliable: false }); } } },\\n  draw(r) { if (info && info.server) return; r.sky(['#143a36', '#14504a']); r.overlay(g => { E.font.text(g, NAME + ' ' + phase + (card && card.left != null ? ' ' + Math.ceil(card.left / 1000) : ''), 8, 8, '#fff', { outline: false }); for (const d of S.dots) px.disc(g, d.x, d.y, 4, '#5ff0e0'); if (info) for (const q of info.players) { const p = q.id === info.me ? mine : S.p[q.id]; if (p && !(S.p[q.id] || {}).gone) { px.disc(g, p.x, p.y, 5, q.color); E.font.text(g, q.name.slice(0, 12), p.x + 7, p.y - 4, q.color, { outline: false }); } } }); } } } });\\n1290→window.__hubProbe = () => ({ phase, over, dots: S.dots.length, v: S.v, t: HUB.active ? HUB.time() : 0 });\\nconnect();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n**Harness runner.** The folder needs the game (as `game.html`) and copies of `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. It uses an OS-picked port, checks the frame's title is your game (replace the print with a test), and stops only its own server, by handle.\\n\\n```python\\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n1300→folder = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1])\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=folder, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True)\\ntry:\\n    line = srv.stdout.readline(); port = int(re.search(r'port (\\\\d+)', line).group(1))\\n    base = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/'\\n    RUNS = ['players=2&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1', 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1']\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        b = p.chromium.launch(args=['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\\n        for q in RUNS:\\n            pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); pg.goto(base + 'harness.html?game=game.html&' + q)\\n1310→            try: pg.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=90000)\\n            except Exception as e: print('TIMEOUT', q)\\n            r = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const h = window.__hubCheck; return h ? { pass: h.pass, failed: h.checks.filter(c => !c.pass).map(c => c.name + ': ' + c.detail), n: h.checks.length } : null }\\\")\\n            title = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const f = document.querySelector('iframe'); try { return f && f.contentDocument && f.contentDocument.title } catch (e) { return 'x' } }\\\")\\n            print(q, json.dumps(r)[:700], 'title:', title); pg.close()\\n        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\\n        b.close()\\nfinally:\\n    srv.terminate(); srv.wait(timeout=5)\\n```\\n1320→\\n## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\\n\\n**A DualSense in the standard mapping, for Playwright's `add_init_script`.** Set `__pad.axes[0..3]` (left x, left y, right x, right y), `__pad.buttons[i].value` and `.pressed`: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 12 to 15 D-pad, and bump `__pad.timestamp`.\\n\\n```js\\n(() => { const axes = [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons = Array.from({ length: 18 }, () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\\n  const pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes, buttons,\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); }, reset() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); } } };\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n1330→```\\n\\n**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\\n\\n```js\\nd.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:48px 24px 24px;text-align:center;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(5,3,12,.92) 45%);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\\n// and on the button, add pointer-events:auto to its inline style\\n```\\n\\nNote it in your Engine Feedback.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1236,\"limit\":220,\"raw_output\":\"## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\\n\\n**Page head.** Order matters.\\n\\n```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>…</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body><!-- E.bootSplash's markup here --><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>/* engine */</script><script>/* game */</script></body></html>\\n```\\n\\n**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\\n\\n```js\\n// Hub skeleton: shared world on my-3D2dge. The host's copy runs the world; other copies mirror it and send their own hands.\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst game = window.G = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  input: { ...base, useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] }, menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\\nconst NAME = 'SKELETON', W0 = 426, H0 = 240, DOTS = 12;\\nlet info = null, phase = 'wait', card = null, over = false, sent = 0, heardSeq = 0, S = { v: 70, dots: [], p: {} }, mine = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0 }, rng = null;\\nconst place = () => ({ x: 40 + rng() * 340, y: 40 + rng() * 160 });\\nfunction hostInit() { rng = HUB.rng('deal'); S.dots = Array.from({ length: DOTS }, (_, id) => ({ id, ...place(), alive: 1 })); for (const q of info.players) S.p[q.id] = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0, score: 0, gone: false }; }\\nfunction finish(won) { if (over) return; over = true; if (HUB.server !== true && info.me != null && S.p[info.me]) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  const live = info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).sort((a, b) => S.p[b.id].score - S.p[a.id].score), standings = [];\\n  for (const q of live) { const last = standings[standings.length - 1]; if (last && S.p[last[0]].score === S.p[q.id].score) last.push(q.id); else standings.push([q.id]); }\\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(info.players.map(q => [q.id, S.p[q.id].score]));\\n  HUB.send({ t: 'over', v: S.v }); HUB.finish({ standings, scores, won, awards: live.length ? [{ id: live[0].id, title: 'Steadiest Hand', detail: scores[live[0].id] + ' clean actions' }] : [] }); }\\nasync function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n  if (!info) { phase = 'solo'; return; }\\n  HUB.on('card', c => { card = c; });\\n  HUB.on('start', () => { phase = 'count'; });\\n  HUB.on('message', (d, from) => { if (info.isHost) { const p = S.p[from]; if (d.t === 'i' && p && d.n > (p.n || 0)) { p.n = d.n; p.x = d.x; p.y = d.y; p.t = d.t2; } } else if (from === info.host) { if (d.t === 's' && d.n > heardSeq) { heardSeq = d.n; S.v = d.v; S.dots = d.o.map(([id, x, y]) => ({ id, x, y, alive: 1 })); for (const [id, x, y, t, sc] of d.p) { const q = S.p[id] || (S.p[id] = {}); if (id !== info.me) { q.x = x; q.y = y; q.t = t; } q.score = sc; } } if (d.t === 'over') over = true; } });\\n  HUB.on('leave', ({ id }) => { if (S.p[id]) S.p[id].gone = true; });\\n  HUB.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) finish(false); });\\n  HUB.on('end', () => { phase = 'over'; game.audio.music(null); game.audio.mute(true); });\\n  if (info.isHost) hostInit();\\n  HUB.ready(); }\\nfunction step(dt) { const I = game.input, m = I.move(), a = I.padAim, ptr = I.pointer(); let dx = (a ? a[0] : 0) + m[0], dy = (a ? a[1] : 0) + m[1]; mine.x = E.clamp(mine.x + dx * 300 * dt, 0, W0); mine.y = E.clamp(mine.y + dy * 300 * dt, 0, H0); if (ptr && I.lastDevice === 'mouse') { mine.x = ptr[0]; mine.y = ptr[1]; } mine.t = I.value('useTool'); }\\nlet snapN = 0, inN = 0, acc = 0;\\nfunction hostStep(dt) { S.v = Math.max(0, S.v - .05 * dt); if (info.me != null && S.p[info.me] && !info.server) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  for (const id in S.p) { const p = S.p[id]; if (p.gone || !p.t) continue; for (const d of S.dots) if (d.alive && Math.hypot(d.x - p.x, d.y - p.y) < 12) { d.alive = 0; p.score++; } } S.dots = S.dots.filter(d => d.alive); if (!S.dots.length) finish(true); }\\ngame.start({ scene: 'hub', scenes: { hub: { pausable: true, camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false },\\n  update(dt) { const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n    if (!info && !inSession) return;\\n    if (phase === 'wait' && info) { if (I.pressed('confirm')) HUB.answer('ready'); if (I.pressed('more')) HUB.answer('more'); const c = I.clicked(); if (c) HUB.answer(c[1] > game.H * .7 ? 'more' : 'ready'); }\\n    if (phase === 'count' && HUB.time() >= 0) phase = 'play';\\n    if (phase === 'play' && !over) { step(dt); if (info.isHost) hostStep(dt); acc += dt; if (acc >= 1 / 12) { acc = 0; if (info.isHost) HUB.send({ t: 's', n: ++snapN, v: Math.round(S.v), o: S.dots.map(d => [d.id, d.x | 0, d.y | 0]), p: info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).map(q => { const p = S.p[q.id]; return [q.id, p.x | 0, p.y | 0, p.t > .25 ? 1 : 0, p.score | 0]; }) }, { reliable: false }); else HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++inN, x: mine.x | 0, y: mine.y | 0, t2: mine.t > .25 ? 1 : 0 }, { to: info.host, reliable: false }); } } },\\n  draw(r) { if (info && info.server) return; r.sky(['#143a36', '#14504a']); r.overlay(g => { E.font.text(g, NAME + ' ' + phase + (card && card.left != null ? ' ' + Math.ceil(card.left / 1000) : ''), 8, 8, '#fff', { outline: false }); for (const d of S.dots) px.disc(g, d.x, d.y, 4, '#5ff0e0'); if (info) for (const q of info.players) { const p = q.id === info.me ? mine : S.p[q.id]; if (p && !(S.p[q.id] || {}).gone) { px.disc(g, p.x, p.y, 5, q.color); E.font.text(g, q.name.slice(0, 12), p.x + 7, p.y - 4, q.color, { outline: false }); } } }); } } } });\\nwindow.__hubProbe = () => ({ phase, over, dots: S.dots.length, v: S.v, t: HUB.active ? HUB.time() : 0 });\\nconnect();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n**Harness runner.** The folder needs the game (as `game.html`) and copies of `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. It uses an OS-picked port, checks the frame's title is your game (replace the print with a test), and stops only its own server, by handle.\\n\\n```python\\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\nfolder = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1])\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=folder, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True)\\ntry:\\n    line = srv.stdout.readline(); port = int(re.search(r'port (\\\\d+)', line).group(1))\\n    base = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/'\\n    RUNS = ['players=2&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1', 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1']\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        b = p.chromium.launch(args=['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\\n        for q in RUNS:\\n            pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); pg.goto(base + 'harness.html?game=game.html&' + q)\\n            try: pg.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=90000)\\n            except Exception as e: print('TIMEOUT', q)\\n            r = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const h = window.__hubCheck; return h ? { pass: h.pass, failed: h.checks.filter(c => !c.pass).map(c => c.name + ': ' + c.detail), n: h.checks.length } : null }\\\")\\n            title = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const f = document.querySelector('iframe'); try { return f && f.contentDocument && f.contentDocument.title } catch (e) { return 'x' } }\\\")\\n            print(q, json.dumps(r)[:700], 'title:', title); pg.close()\\n        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\\n        b.close()\\nfinally:\\n    srv.terminate(); srv.wait(timeout=5)\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\\n\\n**A DualSense in the standard mapping, for Playwright's `add_init_script`.** Set `__pad.axes[0..3]` (left x, left y, right x, right y), `__pad.buttons[i].value` and `.pressed`: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 12 to 15 D-pad, and bump `__pad.timestamp`.\\n\\n```js\\n(() => { const axes = [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons = Array.from({ length: 18 }, () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\\n  const pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes, buttons,\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); }, reset() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); } } };\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n```\\n\\n**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\\n\\n```js\\nd.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:48px 24px 24px;text-align:center;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(5,3,12,.92) 45%);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\\n// and on the button, add pointer-events:auto to its inline style\\n```\\n\\nNote it in your Engine Feedback.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1339}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-e085fc2d-458a-4d5c-82f1-12cb675ee75d-15","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2280→  if (!BOOT.played && BOOT.fail && (BOOT.el || E.current)) { BOOT.fail(title, e); return; }\\n  if (!_errBox) {\\n    _errBox = document.createElement('div'); _errBox.id = 'my3d2dge-error'; _errBox.setAttribute('role', 'alert');\\n    _errBox.style.cssText = 'position:fixed;left:8px;right:8px;top:8px;z-index:99999;max-height:45vh;overflow:auto;background:rgba(40,0,8,.95);color:#ffd6d6;border:2px solid #ff5a5a;border-radius:6px;padding:10px 12px;font:12px/1.45 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;white-space:pre-wrap;cursor:pointer';\\n    _errBox.addEventListener('click', () => { _errBox.remove(); _errBox = null; });\\n    document.body.appendChild(_errBox);\\n  }\\n  const detail = e && e.stack ? String(e.stack) : String(e && e.message || e);\\n  const d = E.diagnose ? E.diagnose() : null;\\n  _errBox.textContent = 'my-3D2dge: ' + title + '\\\\n' + detail.split('\\\\n').slice(0, 5).join('\\\\n') + (d ? '\\\\n' + d.short : '') + '\\\\n(click to hide. Full details are in the browser console; My3D2dge.diagnose() gives the report.)';\\n2290→};\\nif (typeof window !== 'undefined' && window.addEventListener) {\\n  window.addEventListener('error', ev => { if (ev && (ev.error || ev.message)) E.showError('script error (the game could not start, or crashed outside update/draw)', ev.error || (ev.message + ' (line ' + ev.lineno + ')')); });\\n  window.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', ev => E.showError('unhandled promise rejection', ev.reason));\\n}\\n\\n/** the players' colors: player 1 blue, 2 red, 3 green, 4 yellow (game.players) */\\nE.PLAYER_COLORS = ['#4a8aff', '#ff4a4a', '#4ad860', '#ffd040'];\\n/* a scene's fields the engine reads (view, views, input, res, expand, touch, camera): one of the wrong type, a method\\n   named camera() or views: 'side', is left alone and warns once, by name (it would have shadowed the game's own) */\\n2300→const SCENE_FIELDS = { view: v => typeof v === 'string' || (!!v && typeof v === 'object'), views: Array.isArray, input: v => typeof v === 'string' || (!!v && typeof v === 'object'),\\n  res: v => typeof v === 'string' || (Array.isArray(v) && v.length === 2), expand: v => typeof v === 'boolean' || (!!v && typeof v === 'object'), touch: Array.isArray, camera: v => v === false || (!!v && typeof v === 'object' && !Array.isArray(v)) };\\nconst sceneField = (name, s) => k => {\\n  const v = s[k]; if (v === undefined || v === null) return false;\\n  if (SCENE_FIELDS[k](v)) return true;\\n  warn('scene:' + name + ':' + k, 'scene \\\"' + name + '\\\": its ' + k + ' is ' + (typeof v === 'function' ? 'a function (a method of that name?)' : JSON.stringify(v)) + ', but the engine reads scene.' + k + \\\" as the scene's \\\" + k + ' option (the index says what it takes): it is left alone; rename it');\\n  return false;\\n};\\nclass Game {\\n  /**\\n2310→   * new E.Game({ canvas, view, views, res, expand, input, bg, step: 1 / 120, loop: true, headless: false, menu,\\n   * fullscreen: 'tap', corner: true, backGesture: true, autoPause: true, live: false, id, pace, camera }). The standard features\\n   * (section 10b) every game gets: menu, fullscreen, corner, backGesture, autoPause.\\n   * - res: a fixed resolution ('ps1' or [w, h]), whole pixels\\n   * - expand: true makes res the least the screen shows and grows the picture to fill the window, any shape, no bars\\n   *   (expand: { maxW, maxH } stops it growing there)\\n   * - bg: the color behind everything, or null: the canvas is clear, and the game draws its HUD and menus over a picture\\n   *   under it (a 3D world, engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js)\\n   * - headless: no screen, renderer, sound or DOM input (tests, tools, a simulation in Node, where it is the default):\\n   *   scenes update and draw is skipped; drive it with advance() and input.press / release / tap / hold\\n2320→   * - draw: true (headless): draw runs each advance on a stand-in renderer, its errors in game.errors\\n   * - loop: false makes a game in a page that runs only by advance()\\n   * - menu: the pause, settings and controls screens ({ items, settings, controls, quit } adjusts them, false leaves them out)\\n   * - fullscreen: 'tap' (a phone goes full screen at its first tap and when a game starts, unless the player turned it\\n   *   off), 'button' (only when asked) or false\\n   * - corner, backGesture: corner: the menu and full-screen buttons (top right); backGesture: a\\n   *   phone's back steps back in the game first (false: it leaves the page)\\n   * - autoPause: a pausable scene pauses when the page is hidden or loses focus\\n   * - live: true: a world that never stops for one player (online, a shared screen): a pause opens the menus over it,\\n   *   the scene's update goes on (game.paused says a menu is up) and the menu holds that player's input back\\n2330→   * - id: the name the player's settings are saved under (the page's path)\\n   * - pace: false draws every refresh of a fast display even when the frames can't keep up (by default it draws every\\n   *   other one, evenly), unless the player picks Frame rate 60\\n   * - camera: the camera of every scene without its own (a scene's camera option: the player's zoom, start)\\n   */\\n  constructor(o = {}) {\\n    o = Object.assign({}, o);\\n    /** true for a game with no display (o.headless, or no DOM: Node) */\\n    this.headless = !!o.headless || typeof document === 'undefined';\\n    if (this.headless) o.canvas = null;\\n2340→    else {\\n      if (typeof o.canvas === 'string') o.canvas = document.getElementById(o.canvas.replace(/^#/, '')) || document.querySelector(o.canvas);\\n      if (!o.canvas) o.canvas = document.getElementById('screen') || document.querySelector('canvas') || Game._makeCanvas();\\n    }\\n    if (typeof o.input === 'string') o.input = Input[o.input.toUpperCase()] || (warn('input:' + o.input, 'unknown input preset \\\"' + o.input + '\\\" (use DEFAULT, PLATFORMER or SHMUP)'), Input.DEFAULT);\\n    /** o: the options the game was made with, the defaults filled in (view, res, expand, minW, minH, maxW, maxH, bg,\\n     *  step, input, loop, headless) */\\n    this.o = Object.assign({ view: 'iso', minH: 190, minW: 300, maxW: 560, maxH: 330, bg: '#07060d', step: 1 / 120, input: Input.DEFAULT, loop: !this.headless }, o);\\n    // every listener the engine adds to the window, the document, the canvas and its buttons goes through this: dispose() removes them all\\n    this._abort = typeof AbortController === 'function' ? new AbortController() : null;\\n2350→    const signal = this._abort ? this._abort.signal : undefined;\\n    /** screen: the low-resolution screen (its W, H, scale and buffer) */\\n    this.screen = new Screen(this.o.canvas, this.o, signal);\\n    /** input: keyboard, mouse, gamepad and touch, read as actions (pressed, down, move, ...) */\\n    this.input = new Input(this.screen, this.o.input, signal);\\n    /** view: the view the game draws in now (the chosen one, with zoom and turn: read it, change it with setView);\\n     *  baseView: the chosen view without zoom and turn */\\n    this.view = this.baseView = this._view(this.o.view) || E.VIEWS.iso;\\n    /** zoom: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's\\n     *  (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range; yaw: its turn in degrees on top of the\\n2360→     *  view (rotateView) */\\n    this.zoom = 1; this.yaw = 0; this._zoomBase = 1; this._zoomTo = null; this._zoomAt = 0; this._wall = 0;   // camera zoom and turn on top of the chosen view (setZoom, rotateView)\\n    /** views this game is designed for (view cycling and the checker use it). null = every view */\\n    this.views = this.o.views || null;\\n    /** time: game seconds since start (it stops during pause and hit-stop, and slows with timeScale); real: seconds\\n     *  the game has stepped through, pauses and hit-stop included (blinking HUD, notes); hitstop: seconds of\\n     *  hit-stop left (freeze: a scene's entry ends it); timeScale: game speed, 1 normal, .25 slow motion, 0 stopped (it outlives a scene change: a game's speed setting; restore a slow motion with a kept timer); reduceMotion: the player\\n     *  asked for less motion (prefers-reduced-motion): shake and flashes are softened */\\n    this.time = 0; this.real = 0; this.hitstop = 0; this.timeScale = 1; this._shakeAmt = 0; this.reduceMotion = !this.headless && !!(window.matchMedia && matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);\\n    /** camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen\\n2370→     *  rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the\\n     *  focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in projected pixels (its\\n     *  top-left corner); vx, vy: how fast it is moving there; tx, ty, tz: the world point it is following (focus\\n     *  sets it); snap: true makes it jump there at the next step instead of gliding (a new level, a teleport);\\n     *  window: [w, h] screen pixels, a dead zone round the focus it moves in before the camera follows (Super Mario\\n     *  World's; [48, 0] for sideways only); snapY: true follows a followed body's height only when it lands (onGround)\\n     *  or nears the screen's edge (side-scrollers); frame(targets, { margin: 24, zoom: [min, max] or false }) keeps\\n     *  every one of them (anything with x, y, z) in view, centered between them and zoomed out (no further than min)\\n     *  when they spread apart, until frame(null); free: a free camera (strategy, sims, board games): true or { keys: true,\\n     *  edge: 10, drag: true, speed: 300, bounds: [x0, y0, x1, y1] }: the keys or a pad's stick pan it (input.move(), speed screen\\n2380→     *  pixels a second), the mouse at the screen's edge (within edge pixels), a drag (input.pan(): a finger on open\\n     *  ground, a mouse's middle or right button) one to one; a zoom (wheel, pinch) zooms toward the pointer or the pinch;\\n     *  its focus keeps to bounds (world x, y); focus() still moves it; in every view and turn; null (as it starts): off */\\n    this.cam = { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, tx: 0, ty: 0, tz: 0, smooth: .18, bounds: null, snap: true, room: null, moving: false, offset: null, window: null, snapY: false, free: null,\\n      frame: (list, o = {}) => { this._framed = list && list.length ? { list, margin: o.margin === undefined ? 24 : o.margin, zoom: o.zoom === undefined ? [.5, 1] : o.zoom } : null; this.cam.snap = true; } };\\n    /** particles: dust, sparks, debris and text in the world; lights: canvas lighting (lights.enabled, lights.add in\\n     *  draw); r: the renderer handed to draw(r) (null when headless) */\\n    this.particles = new Particles(this); this.lights = new Lighting(this); this.r = this.headless && !o.draw ? null : new Renderer(this);   // (draw: true, headless: a stand-in renderer)\\n    /** fps: frames drawn per second over the last half second of real time; hz: the display's refresh rate, measured;\\n     *  drawEvery: 1, or 2 while a fast display (a 120 Hz phone) refreshes quicker than the game can draw (a frame's cost,\\n2390→     *  or refreshes missed: its GPU behind): every other refresh is drawn, evenly, instead of random ones missed (the\\n     *  updates still run every refresh). The player's Frame rate setting (game.settings.frameRate: 'auto', '60', 'full')\\n     *  can fix it at 2 or 1; gpu: the WebGPU lighting after enableGPU(), or null */\\n    this.fps = 60; this.hz = 60; this.drawEvery = 1; this._viewListeners = []; this.gpu = null;\\n    /** paused: true while paused (a pausable scene toggles it on 'pause'; steps still run, scenes don't update);\\n     *  pauseOverlay: false hides the engine's PAUSED overlay (a game drawing its own pause screen); errors: the\\n     *  errors caught in update and draw, each { where, scene, message, stack }, once per kind; live: true (o.live): a pause\\n     *  opens the menus over a world that keeps stepping (an online or shared world can't stop for one player): paused\\n     *  is true and the scene's update goes on, the menu holding the player's own input back */\\n    this.paused = false; this.pauseOverlay = true; this._timers = []; this.errors = []; this._errKeys = new Set(); this.live = !!o.live; this._goOn = false;\\n2400→    /** the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null */\\n    this.shell = null;\\n    /** seconds for the dithered fade between scenes (0 = instant cuts) */\\n    this.fadeTime = .22; this._fade = null;\\n    /** scenes: the scenes given to start(), by name; scene: the scene running; sceneName: its name ('main' for a\\n     *  game started with one scene) */\\n    this.scenes = null; this.scene = null; this.sceneName = null; this._next = null; this._hooks = null;\\n    /** chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song) */\\n    this.audio = new ChipAudio(this, signal);\\n    if (this.headless) this.audio.failed = 'a headless game has no sound';\\n2410→    /** a game's own handle for tools and tests: game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }.\\n     *  tools/check.mjs prints snapshot() and tools/replay.mjs logs it at the end */\\n    this.debug = null;\\n    /** per-frame timings (ms) and counts, for profiling overlays. frameMs: the real time since the last frame;\\n     *  updateMs, renderMs: milliseconds the last frame spent updating and drawing; steps: the updates it ran; items:\\n     *  what it queued for drawing; actors: actors drawn; culled: actors skipped off screen */\\n    this.stats = { updateMs: 0, renderMs: 0, frameMs: 16.7, steps: 0, items: 0, actors: 0, culled: 0 };\\n    /** the fraction of a fixed step (0..1) of real time not yet run: interpolate drawing with it if motion must be smooth\\n     *  at any refresh rate. The accumulator starts half a step in, so frame times that wobble keep a