{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_246","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Reading PLAN section 6 INPUT and related settings, pause menu, and story API.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6179f2d-8899-47f0-8711-a00a57484a76-21","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md","offset":316,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6179f2d-8899-47f0-8711-a00a57484a76-22","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":180,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6179f2d-8899-47f0-8711-a00a57484a76-23","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","offset":14190,"limit":180}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d6179f2d-8899-47f0-8711-a00a57484a76-24","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/hub/session.js","offset":310,"limit":160}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8770,"output_tokens":484,"cache_read_input_tokens":76672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"48086484-8143-48ee-9380-431d8d466cca"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d6179f2d-8899-47f0-8711-a00a57484a76-21","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"316→## 6. Controls and prompts\\n\\nThe keyboard and mouse are native here, not stand-ins for controller buttons: the same game on the same screens, with the keys PC players expect for this kind of game. The mouse is the best pointer in the game, and the pad is the best-feeling couch device.\\n\\n320→| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Aim | Right stick. D-pad nudges | Mouse, or WASD or arrows |\\n| Use tool | R2 (analog) or ✕ | Left click or Space |\\n| Fine mode, loupe | L2 | Shift |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick | 1 to 8. Hold Right click and flick |\\n| Step tool | L1, R1 | Q, E, or the wheel |\\n| The Steady | △ | F or Middle click |\\n| Consult | □ | C |\\n| Drop, cancel stroke | ○ | X or Backspace |\\n330→| Code Blue shock | L2 + R2 | Left click or Space |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc or P |\\n| Ward: walk | Left stick or D-pad | WASD or arrows, or click to walk |\\n| Ward: talk, use | ✕ | E or Enter, or click the person |\\n| Story: advance | ✕ | Enter, Space or click |\\n| Story: fast-forward | Hold □ | Hold Ctrl |\\n| Story: backlog | △ | B |\\n\\nSettings adds **Swap sticks** for left-handers (cursor and wheel trade sticks).\\n\\n340→```js\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst INPUT = { ...base,\\n  useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], fine: ['Pad6', 'ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight'], gift: ['Pad3', 'KeyF', 'Mouse1'], consult: ['Pad2', 'KeyC'],\\n  toolPrev: ['Pad4', 'KeyQ', 'WheelUp'], toolNext: ['Pad5', 'KeyE', 'WheelDown'], wheelHold: ['Mouse2'],\\n  curU: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp'], curD: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown'], curL: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft'], curR: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight'],   // separate from up/down/left/right, which the left stick also presses\\n  nudgeU: ['Pad12'], nudgeD: ['Pad13'], nudgeL: ['Pad14'], nudgeR: ['Pad15'],\\n  tool1: ['Digit1'], tool2: ['Digit2'], tool3: ['Digit3'], tool4: ['Digit4'], tool5: ['Digit5'], tool6: ['Digit6'], tool7: ['Digit7'], tool8: ['Digit8'],\\n  interact: ['Pad0', 'KeyE', 'Enter'], skip: ['Pad2', 'ControlLeft'], log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\\n```\\n350→\\nRead the two sticks from `input.padAim` and `input.padMove`, the trigger from `input.value('useTool')`. Name the actions and hide `tool1` to `tool8` from rebinding through `menu.controls`. Give the scene `camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false }`, because the wheel is the game's.\\n\\n**Prompts.** Always through `game.input.label(action)`, so they follow the device used last and the player's rebinding. Draw a label as a button cap: a rounded rectangle with the label in it, the PlayStation or Xbox face colors on face buttons, and plain keycaps for keys. For the sticks, draw a small stick icon with L or R. Never hard-code a key in text. PlayStation glyphs by default with the Xbox option from fact 5.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Things on the table\\n\\nA registry (`defObject`), each with sim behavior, a draw function kept apart, and a bot plan.\\n360→\\n| Type | Looks like | Fixed by | Vitals/s while open | Other effects |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `shard` | Glass or steel sliver with a glint | Forceps along its axis | .1 | |\\n| `laceration` | Short red cut | Salve | .2 | Small pool over time |\\n| `wound` | Gaping cut with lips | Suture N stitches | .4 | Bleeding falls with each stitch |\\n| `bleeder` | Pinhole spurting on the beat | Cautery | .5 | Feeds a pool, 6 volume/s |\\n| `arteryTear` | Pulsing spurts | Suture 3 | 1 | Feeds a pool, 14 volume/s |\\n| `pool` | Dark wet metaball, specular | Suction | none | Hides what's under it, drifts on a tilt |\\n| `polyp` | Pink nub | Cautery | .1 | |\\n370→| `mass` | Large lump | Scalpel ring, Forceps lift, leaves a `wound` | .2 | |\\n| `hook` | Barbed steel | Scalpel relief cuts at each barb, then Forceps | .3 | Tears if pulled with barbs set |\\n| `clot` | Dark lump in a vessel | Targeted Syringe, then Forceps | .3 | |\\n| `patch` | Inflamed red hatch | Salve | .1 | |\\n| `nerve`, `eloquent` | Gold line (no-touch) | Avoid | | Touching with Scalpel or Cautery: -12 and a slip |\\n| `retractorHandle` | Steel handle (Grand Rounds) | Forceps hold | | Opens a window on a target while held |\\n| device parts | Screws, wires, leads (Case 9) | Per Case 9 | | |\\n\\nObjects can be **hidden** (need Sonar), **under a pool**, or **tied** to a phase script. Phase scripts are data: `at: [{ t: 25, do: 'lurch' }]`, `when: 'clear'`.\\n\\n380→---\\n\\n## 8. HUSH: the strains\\n\\n**HUSH** stands for *Hyperplastic Undifferentiated Synaptic Hive*: an engineered parasite colony that feeds on pain signals and leaves its host blissful, numb and dying. Strains are named after musical markings, because they sing. Chief Oyelaran: \\\"They sing, Doctor. So we name them like songs.\\\"\\n\\n**Common look and sound.** Teal bioluminescence (`#5ff0e0`) with a dark core (`#0b2a30`), additive halo, lavender on bosses. Teal always means HUSH. They stay bright in Long Breath's cold palette. Every strain has its own figure in the choir voice (18), on the **effects** bus: music defaults to 10%, so no gameplay information may depend on music.\\n\\n### Staccato (Case 4 on)\\nSwarm of beads hopping in bursts on a fixed beat, from hidden **nests**. A closing dotted ring shows each landing spot .5 s ahead. A landing bite leaves a `laceration`. Cautery kills a bead in .12 s. Find nests with Sonar; slash, then Forceps. When the last nest goes, the remaining beads die within 3 s. Sound: \\\"tk-tk-tk\\\" on the beat, so the rhythm is playable by ear.\\n390→\\n### Legato (Case 5 on)\\nA long worm under the tissue, seen as a moving ridge (the painter's `stampLine` with positive height). Its head shows on Sonar.\\n1. Three slur marks lie on its route. Cut the short guide as the ridge nears one; it surfaces.\\n2. Forceps grips the head. Pull slowly: a tension gauge shows the safe rate. Too fast snaps it: the rest regrows a head and flees.\\n3. Every 4th segment has a barb. Release in the hold zone so Quill clamps, burn the barb, regrip. Pull, clamp, burn, regrip is the rhythm of the fight.\",\"content_concise\":\"316→## 6. Controls and prompts\\n\\nThe keyboard and mouse are native here, not stand-ins for controller buttons: the same game on the same screens, with the keys PC players expect for this kind of game. The mouse is the best pointer in the game, and the pad is the best-feeling couch device.\\n\\n320→| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Aim | Right stick. D-pad nudges | Mouse, or WASD or arrows |\\n| Use tool | R2 (analog) or ✕ | Left click or Space |\\n| Fine mode, loupe | L2 | Shift |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick | 1 to 8. Hold Right click and flick |\\n| Step tool | L1, R1 | Q, E, or the wheel |\\n| The Steady | △ | F or Middle click |\\n| Consult | □ | C |\\n| Drop, cancel stroke | ○ | X or Backspace |\\n330→| Code Blue shock | L2 + R2 | Left click or Space |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc or P |\\n| Ward: walk | Left stick or D-pad | WASD or arrows, or click to walk |\\n| Ward: talk, use | ✕ | E or Enter, or click the person |\\n| Story: advance | ✕ | Enter, Space or click |\\n| Story: fast-forward | Hold □ | Hold Ctrl |\\n| Story: backlog | △ | B |\\n\\nSettings adds **Swap sticks** for left-handers (cursor and wheel trade sticks).\\n\\n340→```js\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst INPUT = { ...base,\\n  useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], fine: ['Pad6', 'ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight'], gift: ['Pad3', 'KeyF', 'Mouse1'], consult: ['Pad2', 'KeyC'],\\n  toolPrev: ['Pad4', 'KeyQ', 'WheelUp'], toolNext: ['Pad5', 'KeyE', 'WheelDown'], wheelHold: ['Mouse2'],\\n  curU: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp'], curD: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown'], curL: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft'], curR: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight'],   // separate from up/down/left/right, which the left stick also presses\\n  nudgeU: ['Pad12'], nudgeD: ['Pad13'], nudgeL: ['Pad14'], nudgeR: ['Pad15'],\\n  tool1: ['Digit1'], tool2: ['Digit2'], tool3: ['Digit3'], tool4: ['Digit4'], tool5: ['Digit5'], tool6: ['Digit6'], tool7: ['Digit7'], tool8: ['Digit8'],\\n  interact: ['Pad0', 'KeyE', 'Enter'], skip: ['Pad2', 'ControlLeft'], log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\\n```\\n350→\\nRead the two sticks from `input.padAim` and `input.padMove`, the trigger from `input.value('useTool')`. Name the actions and hide `tool1` to `tool8` from rebinding through `menu.controls`. Give the scene `camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false }`, because the wheel is the game's.\\n\\n**Prompts.** Always through `game.input.label(action)`, so they follow the device used last and the player's rebinding. Draw a label as a button cap: a rounded rectangle with the label in it, the PlayStation or Xbox face colors on face buttons, and plain keycaps for keys. For the sticks, draw a small stick icon with L or R. Never hard-code a key in text. PlayStation glyphs by default with the Xbox option from fact 5.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Things on the table\\n\\nA registry (`defObject`), each with sim behavior, a draw function kept apart, and a bot plan.\\n360→\\n| Type | Looks like | Fixed by | Vitals/s while open | Other effects |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `shard` | Glass or steel sliver with a glint | Forceps along its axis | .1 | |\\n| `laceration` | Short red cut | Salve | .2 | Small pool over time |\\n| `wound` | Gaping cut with lips | Suture N stitches | .4 | Bleeding falls with each stitch |\\n| `bleeder` | Pinhole spurting on the beat | Cautery | .5 | Feeds a pool, 6 volume/s |\\n| `arteryTear` | Pulsing spurts | Suture 3 | 1 | Feeds a pool, 14 volume/s |\\n| `pool` | Dark wet metaball, specular | Suction | none | Hides what's under it, drifts on a tilt |\\n| `polyp` | Pink nub | Cautery | .1 | |\\n370→| `mass` | Large lump | Scalpel ring, Forceps lift, leaves a `wound` | .2 | |\\n| `hook` | Barbed steel | Scalpel relief cuts at each barb, then Forceps | .3 | Tears if pulled with barbs set |\\n| `clot` | Dark lump in a vessel | Targeted Syringe, then Forceps | .3 | |\\n| `patch` | Inflamed red hatch | Salve | .1 | |\\n| `nerve`, `eloquent` | Gold line (no-touch) | Avoid | | Touching with Scalpel or Cautery: -12 and a slip |\\n| `retractorHandle` | Steel handle (Grand Rounds) | Forceps hold | | Opens a window on a target while held |\\n| device parts | Screws, wires, leads (Case 9) | Per Case 9 | | |\\n\\nObjects can be **hidden** (need Sonar), **under a pool**, or **tied** to a phase script. Phase scripts are data: `at: [{ t: 25, do: 'lurch' }]`, `when: 'clear'`.\\n\\n380→---\\n\\n## 8. HUSH: the strains\\n\\n**HUSH** stands for *Hyperplastic Undifferentiated Synaptic Hive*: an engineered parasite colony that feeds on pain signals and leaves its host blissful, numb and dying. Strains are named after musical markings, because they sing. Chief Oyelaran: \\\"They sing, Doctor. So we name them like songs.\\\"\\n\\n**Common look and sound.** Teal bioluminescence (`#5ff0e0`) with a dark core (`#0b2a30`), additive halo, lavender on bosses. Teal always means HUSH. They stay bright in Long Breath's cold palette. Every strain has its own figure in the choir voice (18), on the **effects** bus: music defaults to 10%, so no gameplay information may depend on music.\\n\\n### Staccato (Case 4 on)\\nSwarm of beads hopping in bursts on a fixed beat, from hidden **nests**. A closing dotted ring shows each landing spot .5 s ahead. A landing bite leaves a `laceration`. Cautery kills a bead in .12 s. Find nests with Sonar; slash, then Forceps. When the last nest goes, the remaining beads die within 3 s. Sound: \\\"tk-tk-tk\\\" on the beat, so the rhythm is playable by ear.\\n390→\\n### Legato (Case 5 on)\\nA long worm under the tissue, seen as a moving ridge (the painter's `stampLine` with positive height). Its head shows on Sonar.\\n1. Three slur marks lie on its route. Cut the short guide as the ridge nears one; it surfaces.\\n2. Forceps grips the head. Pull slowly: a tension gauge shows the safe rate. Too fast snaps it: the rest regrows a head and flees.\\n3. Every 4th segment has a barb. Release in the hold zone so Quill clamps, burn the barb, regrip. Pull, clamp, burn, regrip is the rhythm of the fight.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":316,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"## 6. Controls and prompts\\n\\nThe keyboard and mouse are native here, not stand-ins for controller buttons: the same game on the same screens, with the keys PC players expect for this kind of game. The mouse is the best pointer in the game, and the pad is the best-feeling couch device.\\n\\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard and mouse |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Aim | Right stick. D-pad nudges | Mouse, or WASD or arrows |\\n| Use tool | R2 (analog) or ✕ | Left click or Space |\\n| Fine mode, loupe | L2 | Shift |\\n| Pick tool | Left stick flick | 1 to 8. Hold Right click and flick |\\n| Step tool | L1, R1 | Q, E, or the wheel |\\n| The Steady | △ | F or Middle click |\\n| Consult | □ | C |\\n| Drop, cancel stroke | ○ | X or Backspace |\\n| Code Blue shock | L2 + R2 | Left click or Space |\\n| Pause | Options | Esc or P |\\n| Ward: walk | Left stick or D-pad | WASD or arrows, or click to walk |\\n| Ward: talk, use | ✕ | E or Enter, or click the person |\\n| Story: advance | ✕ | Enter, Space or click |\\n| Story: fast-forward | Hold □ | Hold Ctrl |\\n| Story: backlog | △ | B |\\n\\nSettings adds **Swap sticks** for left-handers (cursor and wheel trade sticks).\\n\\n```js\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst INPUT = { ...base,\\n  useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], fine: ['Pad6', 'ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight'], gift: ['Pad3', 'KeyF', 'Mouse1'], consult: ['Pad2', 'KeyC'],\\n  toolPrev: ['Pad4', 'KeyQ', 'WheelUp'], toolNext: ['Pad5', 'KeyE', 'WheelDown'], wheelHold: ['Mouse2'],\\n  curU: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp'], curD: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown'], curL: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft'], curR: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight'],   // separate from up/down/left/right, which the left stick also presses\\n  nudgeU: ['Pad12'], nudgeD: ['Pad13'], nudgeL: ['Pad14'], nudgeR: ['Pad15'],\\n  tool1: ['Digit1'], tool2: ['Digit2'], tool3: ['Digit3'], tool4: ['Digit4'], tool5: ['Digit5'], tool6: ['Digit6'], tool7: ['Digit7'], tool8: ['Digit8'],\\n  interact: ['Pad0', 'KeyE', 'Enter'], skip: ['Pad2', 'ControlLeft'], log: ['Pad3', 'KeyB'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] };\\n```\\n\\nRead the two sticks from `input.padAim` and `input.padMove`, the trigger from `input.value('useTool')`. Name the actions and hide `tool1` to `tool8` from rebinding through `menu.controls`. Give the scene `camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false }`, because the wheel is the game's.\\n\\n**Prompts.** Always through `game.input.label(action)`, so they follow the device used last and the player's rebinding. Draw a label as a button cap: a rounded rectangle with the label in it, the PlayStation or Xbox face colors on face buttons, and plain keycaps for keys. For the sticks, draw a small stick icon with L or R. Never hard-code a key in text. PlayStation glyphs by default with the Xbox option from fact 5.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Things on the table\\n\\nA registry (`defObject`), each with sim behavior, a draw function kept apart, and a bot plan.\\n\\n| Type | Looks like | Fixed by | Vitals/s while open | Other effects |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| `shard` | Glass or steel sliver with a glint | Forceps along its axis | .1 | |\\n| `laceration` | Short red cut | Salve | .2 | Small pool over time |\\n| `wound` | Gaping cut with lips | Suture N stitches | .4 | Bleeding falls with each stitch |\\n| `bleeder` | Pinhole spurting on the beat | Cautery | .5 | Feeds a pool, 6 volume/s |\\n| `arteryTear` | Pulsing spurts | Suture 3 | 1 | Feeds a pool, 14 volume/s |\\n| `pool` | Dark wet metaball, specular | Suction | none | Hides what's under it, drifts on a tilt |\\n| `polyp` | Pink nub | Cautery | .1 | |\\n| `mass` | Large lump | Scalpel ring, Forceps lift, leaves a `wound` | .2 | |\\n| `hook` | Barbed steel | Scalpel relief cuts at each barb, then Forceps | .3 | Tears if pulled with barbs set |\\n| `clot` | Dark lump in a vessel | Targeted Syringe, then Forceps | .3 | |\\n| `patch` | Inflamed red hatch | Salve | .1 | |\\n| `nerve`, `eloquent` | Gold line (no-touch) | Avoid | | Touching with Scalpel or Cautery: -12 and a slip |\\n| `retractorHandle` | Steel handle (Grand Rounds) | Forceps hold | | Opens a window on a target while held |\\n| device parts | Screws, wires, leads (Case 9) | Per Case 9 | | |\\n\\nObjects can be **hidden** (need Sonar), **under a pool**, or **tied** to a phase script. Phase scripts are data: `at: [{ t: 25, do: 'lurch' }]`, `when: 'clear'`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. HUSH: the strains\\n\\n**HUSH** stands for *Hyperplastic Undifferentiated Synaptic Hive*: an engineered parasite colony that feeds on pain signals and leaves its host blissful, numb and dying. Strains are named after musical markings, because they sing. Chief Oyelaran: \\\"They sing, Doctor. So we name them like songs.\\\"\\n\\n**Common look and sound.** Teal bioluminescence (`#5ff0e0`) with a dark core (`#0b2a30`), additive halo, lavender on bosses. Teal always means HUSH. They stay bright in Long Breath's cold palette. Every strain has its own figure in the choir voice (18), on the **effects** bus: music defaults to 10%, so no gameplay information may depend on music.\\n\\n### Staccato (Case 4 on)\\nSwarm of beads hopping in bursts on a fixed beat, from hidden **nests**. A closing dotted ring shows each landing spot .5 s ahead. A landing bite leaves a `laceration`. Cautery kills a bead in .12 s. Find nests with Sonar; slash, then Forceps. When the last nest goes, the remaining beads die within 3 s. Sound: \\\"tk-tk-tk\\\" on the beat, so the rhythm is playable by ear.\\n\\n### Legato (Case 5 on)\\nA long worm under the tissue, seen as a moving ridge (the painter's `stampLine` with positive height). Its head shows on Sonar.\\n1. Three slur marks lie on its route. Cut the short guide as the ridge nears one; it surfaces.\\n2. Forceps grips the head. Pull slowly: a tension gauge shows the safe rate. Too fast snaps it: the rest regrows a head and flees.\\n3. Every 4th segment has a barb. Release in the hold zone so Quill clamps, burn the barb, regrip. Pull, clamp, burn, regrip is the rhythm of the fight.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1339}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d6179f2d-8899-47f0-8711-a00a57484a76-22","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"180→      const d = st.domes[i];\\n      if (d.t > 0 && hypot(x - d.x, y - d.y) <= d.r) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function covered(S, o) {\\n    if (!o.under) return false;\\n    const p = objById(S, o.under);\\n    return !!(p && !p.done && p.vol > 1);\\n190→  }\\n\\n  function canTouch(S, o) {\\n    if (!o || o.done || !o.alive) return false;\\n    if (covered(S, o)) return false;\\n    if (o.hidden && !o.marked) return false;\\n    if (o.needsWindow && S.windowOpen <= 0) return false;\\n    if (o.needsBoard && S.device && !S.device.shown) return false;\\n    if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return !!o.window;\\n    if (o.type === 'lobe') return !!o.open;\\n200→    if (o.type === 'eye') return !!o.open;\\n    if (o.type === 'repeat') return !!o.open;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nearest(S, p, rad, pred) {\\n    let best = null, bd = rad;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!pred(o)) continue;\\n210→      const d = hypot(o.x - p.x, o.y - p.y);\\n      if (d <= bd) { bd = d; best = o; }\\n    }\\n    return best;\\n  }\\n\\n  function lose(S, why) {\\n    if (S.lost || S.won) return;\\n    S.lost = true;\\n    S.reason = why;\\n220→    S.breath = false;\\n    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['lost', why]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function finishCase(S) {\\n    if (S.won || S.lost) return;\\n    S.won = true;\\n    S.closed = true;\\n    S.breath = false;\\n230→    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    const end = Math.max(0, S.clock) * 2 + Math.max(0, S.vitals) * 3;\\n    S.score += end;\\n    S.endBonus = end;\\n    S.rank = rankLetter(S.score, S.par, S.diff, S.slips, S.rankCap);\\n    pushEv(S, ['closed', S.rank, Math.round(S.score)]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function rankLetter(score, par, diff, slips, cap) {\\n    const r = par > 0 ? score / par : 0;\\n240→    let L = r >= 0.95 ? 'S' : r >= 0.8 ? 'A' : r >= 0.6 ? 'B' : r >= 0.4 ? 'C' : 'D';\\n    const order = 'DCBAS';\\n    if (cap === 'B' && order.indexOf(L) > order.indexOf('B')) L = 'B';\\n    if (diff === 'attending' && L === 'S' && !slips) return 'S+';\\n    return L;\\n  }\\n\\n  function takeCore(S) {\\n    return {\\n      rng: S.rng, clock: S.clock, vitals: S.vitals, score: S.score, slips: S.slips,\\n250→      phase: S.phase, steady: S.steady, flow: S.flow, streak: S.streak,\\n      phaseT: S.phaseT, worldT: S.worldT, flags: clone(S.flags),\\n      objects: clone(S.objects), strain: S.strain ? clone(S.strain) : null,\\n      device: S.device ? clone(S.device) : null,\\n      techGood: S.techGood, techAll: S.techAll, bestFlow: S.bestFlow,\\n      codeBlueUsed: S.codeBlueUsed, tutDone: S.tutDone, tutorial: S.tutorial,\\n      windowOpen: S.windowOpen, tiltAmp: S.tiltAmp, dim: S.dim,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n260→  function applyCore(S, core) {\\n    S.rng = core.rng; S.clock = core.clock; S.vitals = core.vitals; S.score = core.score;\\n    S.slips = core.slips; S.phase = core.phase; S.steady = core.steady; S.flow = core.flow;\\n    S.streak = core.streak; S.phaseT = core.phaseT; S.worldT = core.worldT;\\n    S.flags = clone(core.flags); S.objects = clone(core.objects);\\n    S.strain = core.strain ? clone(core.strain) : null;\\n    S.device = core.device ? clone(core.device) : null;\\n    S.techGood = core.techGood; S.techAll = core.techAll; S.bestFlow = core.bestFlow;\\n    S.codeBlueUsed = core.codeBlueUsed; S.tutDone = core.tutDone; S.tutorial = core.tutorial;\\n    S.windowOpen = core.windowOpen; S.tiltAmp = core.tiltAmp; S.dim = core.dim;\",\"content_concise\":\"180→      const d = st.domes[i];\\n      if (d.t > 0 && hypot(x - d.x, y - d.y) <= d.r) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function covered(S, o) {\\n    if (!o.under) return false;\\n    const p = objById(S, o.under);\\n    return !!(p && !p.done && p.vol > 1);\\n190→  }\\n\\n  function canTouch(S, o) {\\n    if (!o || o.done || !o.alive) return false;\\n    if (covered(S, o)) return false;\\n    if (o.hidden && !o.marked) return false;\\n    if (o.needsWindow && S.windowOpen <= 0) return false;\\n    if (o.needsBoard && S.device && !S.device.shown) return false;\\n    if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return !!o.window;\\n    if (o.type === 'lobe') return !!o.open;\\n200→    if (o.type === 'eye') return !!o.open;\\n    if (o.type === 'repeat') return !!o.open;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nearest(S, p, rad, pred) {\\n    let best = null, bd = rad;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!pred(o)) continue;\\n210→      const d = hypot(o.x - p.x, o.y - p.y);\\n      if (d <= bd) { bd = d; best = o; }\\n    }\\n    return best;\\n  }\\n\\n  function lose(S, why) {\\n    if (S.lost || S.won) return;\\n    S.lost = true;\\n    S.reason = why;\\n220→    S.breath = false;\\n    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['lost', why]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function finishCase(S) {\\n    if (S.won || S.lost) return;\\n    S.won = true;\\n    S.closed = true;\\n    S.breath = false;\\n230→    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    const end = Math.max(0, S.clock) * 2 + Math.max(0, S.vitals) * 3;\\n    S.score += end;\\n    S.endBonus = end;\\n    S.rank = rankLetter(S.score, S.par, S.diff, S.slips, S.rankCap);\\n    pushEv(S, ['closed', S.rank, Math.round(S.score)]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function rankLetter(score, par, diff, slips, cap) {\\n    const r = par > 0 ? score / par : 0;\\n240→    let L = r >= 0.95 ? 'S' : r >= 0.8 ? 'A' : r >= 0.6 ? 'B' : r >= 0.4 ? 'C' : 'D';\\n    const order = 'DCBAS';\\n    if (cap === 'B' && order.indexOf(L) > order.indexOf('B')) L = 'B';\\n    if (diff === 'attending' && L === 'S' && !slips) return 'S+';\\n    return L;\\n  }\\n\\n  function takeCore(S) {\\n    return {\\n      rng: S.rng, clock: S.clock, vitals: S.vitals, score: S.score, slips: S.slips,\\n250→      phase: S.phase, steady: S.steady, flow: S.flow, streak: S.streak,\\n      phaseT: S.phaseT, worldT: S.worldT, flags: clone(S.flags),\\n      objects: clone(S.objects), strain: S.strain ? clone(S.strain) : null,\\n      device: S.device ? clone(S.device) : null,\\n      techGood: S.techGood, techAll: S.techAll, bestFlow: S.bestFlow,\\n      codeBlueUsed: S.codeBlueUsed, tutDone: S.tutDone, tutorial: S.tutorial,\\n      windowOpen: S.windowOpen, tiltAmp: S.tiltAmp, dim: S.dim,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n260→  function applyCore(S, core) {\\n    S.rng = core.rng; S.clock = core.clock; S.vitals = core.vitals; S.score = core.score;\\n    S.slips = core.slips; S.phase = core.phase; S.steady = core.steady; S.flow = core.flow;\\n    S.streak = core.streak; S.phaseT = core.phaseT; S.worldT = core.worldT;\\n    S.flags = clone(core.flags); S.objects = clone(core.objects);\\n    S.strain = core.strain ? clone(core.strain) : null;\\n    S.device = core.device ? clone(core.device) : null;\\n    S.techGood = core.techGood; S.techAll = core.techAll; S.bestFlow = core.bestFlow;\\n    S.codeBlueUsed = core.codeBlueUsed; S.tutDone = core.tutDone; S.tutorial = core.tutorial;\\n    S.windowOpen = core.windowOpen; S.tiltAmp = core.tiltAmp; S.dim = core.dim;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":180,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"      const d = st.domes[i];\\n      if (d.t > 0 && hypot(x - d.x, y - d.y) <= d.r) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function covered(S, o) {\\n    if (!o.under) return false;\\n    const p = objById(S, o.under);\\n    return !!(p && !p.done && p.vol > 1);\\n  }\\n\\n  function canTouch(S, o) {\\n    if (!o || o.done || !o.alive) return false;\\n    if (covered(S, o)) return false;\\n    if (o.hidden && !o.marked) return false;\\n    if (o.needsWindow && S.windowOpen <= 0) return false;\\n    if (o.needsBoard && S.device && !S.device.shown) return false;\\n    if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return !!o.window;\\n    if (o.type === 'lobe') return !!o.open;\\n    if (o.type === 'eye') return !!o.open;\\n    if (o.type === 'repeat') return !!o.open;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nearest(S, p, rad, pred) {\\n    let best = null, bd = rad;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!pred(o)) continue;\\n      const d = hypot(o.x - p.x, o.y - p.y);\\n      if (d <= bd) { bd = d; best = o; }\\n    }\\n    return best;\\n  }\\n\\n  function lose(S, why) {\\n    if (S.lost || S.won) return;\\n    S.lost = true;\\n    S.reason = why;\\n    S.breath = false;\\n    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['lost', why]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function finishCase(S) {\\n    if (S.won || S.lost) return;\\n    S.won = true;\\n    S.closed = true;\\n    S.breath = false;\\n    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    const end = Math.max(0, S.clock) * 2 + Math.max(0, S.vitals) * 3;\\n    S.score += end;\\n    S.endBonus = end;\\n    S.rank = rankLetter(S.score, S.par, S.diff, S.slips, S.rankCap);\\n    pushEv(S, ['closed', S.rank, Math.round(S.score)]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function rankLetter(score, par, diff, slips, cap) {\\n    const r = par > 0 ? score / par : 0;\\n    let L = r >= 0.95 ? 'S' : r >= 0.8 ? 'A' : r >= 0.6 ? 'B' : r >= 0.4 ? 'C' : 'D';\\n    const order = 'DCBAS';\\n    if (cap === 'B' && order.indexOf(L) > order.indexOf('B')) L = 'B';\\n    if (diff === 'attending' && L === 'S' && !slips) return 'S+';\\n    return L;\\n  }\\n\\n  function takeCore(S) {\\n    return {\\n      rng: S.rng, clock: S.clock, vitals: S.vitals, score: S.score, slips: S.slips,\\n      phase: S.phase, steady: S.steady, flow: S.flow, streak: S.streak,\\n      phaseT: S.phaseT, worldT: S.worldT, flags: clone(S.flags),\\n      objects: clone(S.objects), strain: S.strain ? clone(S.strain) : null,\\n      device: S.device ? clone(S.device) : null,\\n      techGood: S.techGood, techAll: S.techAll, bestFlow: S.bestFlow,\\n      codeBlueUsed: S.codeBlueUsed, tutDone: S.tutDone, tutorial: S.tutorial,\\n      windowOpen: S.windowOpen, tiltAmp: S.tiltAmp, dim: S.dim,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  function applyCore(S, core) {\\n    S.rng = core.rng; S.clock = core.clock; S.vitals = core.vitals; S.score = core.score;\\n    S.slips = core.slips; S.phase = core.phase; S.steady = core.steady; S.flow = core.flow;\\n    S.streak = core.streak; S.phaseT = core.phaseT; S.worldT = core.worldT;\\n    S.flags = clone(core.flags); S.objects = clone(core.objects);\\n    S.strain = core.strain ? clone(core.strain) : null;\\n    S.device = core.device ? clone(core.device) : null;\\n    S.techGood = core.techGood; S.techAll = core.techAll; S.bestFlow = core.bestFlow;\\n    S.codeBlueUsed = core.codeBlueUsed; S.tutDone = core.tutDone; S.tutorial = core.tutorial;\\n    S.windowOpen = core.windowOpen; S.tiltAmp = core.tiltAmp; S.dim = core.dim;\\n\",\"total_lines\":1762}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d6179f2d-8899-47f0-8711-a00a57484a76-23","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"14190→```js story\\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true });\\nconst story = new E.Story(game, { vars: { gold: 30, hero: 'ROWAN' }, nodes: {\\n  elder: [{ if: 'helping', goto: 'thanks' }, { who: 'elder', say: 'Will you help us, {$hero}?', choices: [\\n    { text: 'Yes', set: 'helping', quest: ['cave', 'The cave', 'Clear the cave north of town'] }, { text: 'No', goto: 'bye' }] },\\n    { add: { gold: 20 } }],\\n  thanks: [{ say: 'Thank you!' }, { if: 'gold >= 50', done: 'cave' }],\\n  bye: [{ say: 'Farewell.' }] } });\\ngame.start({ update(dt) { story.update(dt); }, draw(r) { story.draw(r); } });\\nconst press = n => { for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { game.input.tap('confirm'); game.advance(.5); } };\\n14200→story.run('elder'); press(2);   // the line types out, then the first choice: Yes\\nif (!story.get('helping') || story.get('gold') !== 50 || story.quests[0].id !== 'cave' || story.running) throw new Error('the quest taken');\\nstory.run('elder'); press(2);\\nif (!story.quests[0].done || !story.test('done:cave')) throw new Error('the quest done');\\n```\\nRules: keep the nodes as data (a game's script is an event); put story.state() in the game's save and restore it on a\\nload; one story per game, its talk the only box on screen.\\n*/\\n(function (E) {\\n'use strict';\\n14210→if (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module STORY: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\\n\\n/* =============================================================================\\n * STORY  conversations as data run through a Dialog, flags and values, quests, emote balloons\\n * ========================================================================== */\\nconst { px } = E;\\nconst HEART = E.sprite(['.R.R.', 'RRRRR', 'RRRRR', '.RRR.', '..R..'], { R: '#e8384a' });\\nclass Story {\\n  /** new E.Story(game, { people, nodes, vars, on, dialog }): the talk of a game (the manual above) */\\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\\n14220→    /** game: its game; people: who speaks, by id ({ name, portrait, at }); nodes: the conversations by id (lists of\\n     *  steps); on: the game's event handlers by name */\\n    this.game = game; this.people = o.people || {}; this.nodes = o.nodes || {}; this.on = Object.assign({}, o.on);\\n    /** vars: every flag and value (a line's {$name} reads them) */\\n    this.vars = Object.assign({}, o.vars);\\n    /** talk: the E.Dialog it speaks through */\\n    this.talk = o.dialog || new E.Dialog(game); this.talk.vars = this.vars;\\n    /** quests: the quest log, in the order taken ({ id, title, text, done }) */\\n    this.quests = [];\\n    /** log: what was said and chosen, oldest first ({ who, name, text }, the last 200: a visual novel's backlog) */\\n14230→    this.log = [];\\n    /** auto: seconds a page shows before it turns by itself (0: it waits for the player); skip: pages type at once and\\n     *  turn at once (choices still wait) */\\n    this.auto = 0; this.skip = false;\\n    /** running: a node runs; node: its id */\\n    this.running = false; this.node = null;\\n    this._steps = null; this._i = 0; this._wait = 0; this._held = false; this._then = null; this._pick = null; this._done = null; this._balloons = [];\\n  }\\n  /** start node id (stopping any other); o.onDone(story) when it ends */\\n  run(id, o = {}) {\\n14240→    if (!this.nodes[id]) { E.warn('story:' + id, 'E.Story: no node \\\"' + id + '\\\"'); return this; }\\n    if (this.talk.open) this.talk.close();\\n    this.running = true; this.node = id; this._steps = this.nodes[id]; this._i = 0; this._wait = 0; this._held = false; this._then = null; this._pick = null; this._done = o.onDone || null;\\n    this._next(); return this;\\n  }\\n  /** stop the node running (its box closes; onDone isn't called) */\\n  stop() { this.running = false; this.node = null; this._done = null; if (this.talk.open) this.talk.close(); }\\n  /** after an event with wait: true, go on (to the choice's goto, or the next step) */\\n  resume() { if (!this._held) return; this._held = false; const g = this._then; this._then = null; if (g && !this._jump(g)) return; this._next(); }\\n  // the steps until one waits (a line, a pause, a held event) or the node ends\\n14250→  _next() {\\n    while (this.running) {\\n      const s = this._steps[this._i++];\\n      if (!s) return this._end();\\n      if (s.if !== undefined && !this.test(s.if)) continue;\\n      if (s.say !== undefined) return this._say(s);   // (its event, goto and a choice's run when the box closes)\\n      this._act(s); if (!this.running) return;\\n      if (this._fire(s, s.goto)) return;\\n      if (s.goto && !this._jump(s.goto)) return;\\n      if (!s.event && s.wait > 0) { this._wait = s.wait; return; }\\n14260→    }\\n  }\\n  _say(s) {\\n    const p = this.people[s.who] || {}, ch = s.choices && s.choices.filter(c => c.if === undefined || this.test(c.if));\\n    this._act(s); if (!this.running) return;\\n    const name = s.name || p.name || '', note = e => { this.log.push(e); if (this.log.length > 200) this.log.shift(); };\\n    for (const t of [].concat(s.say)) note({ who: s.who || null, name, text: t });\\n    if (this._speed === undefined) this._speed = this.talk.speed;\\n    this.talk.speed = this.skip ? 1e6 : this._speed;\\n    this.talk.say(s.say, { name, portrait: p.portrait, auto: this.skip ? .08 : this.auto || undefined, choices: ch && ch.length ? ch.map(c => c.text) : null, onChoice: i => { this._pick = ch[i]; note({ who: 'choice', name: '', text: ch[i].text }); }, onDone: () => this._after(s) });\\n14270→  }\\n  _after(s) {\\n    const c = this._pick; this._pick = null;\\n    if (c) { this._act(c); if (!this.running || this._fire(c, c.goto)) return; if (c.goto) { if (this._jump(c.goto)) this._next(); return; } }\\n    if (this._fire(s, s.goto)) return;\\n    if (s.goto && !this._jump(s.goto)) return;\\n    this._next();\\n  }\\n  // a step's or a choice's event: true when the story stops here (it ended, or holds till resume(), then goes to then)\\n  _fire(s, then) {\\n14280→    if (!s.event) return false;\\n    const f = this.on[s.event];\\n    if (f) try { f(this, s); } catch (e) { this.game.fail('story event \\\"' + s.event + '\\\"', e); }\\n    else E.warn('story:on:' + s.event, 'E.Story: no handler for event \\\"' + s.event + '\\\" (on: { ' + s.event + '(story, step) {...} })');\\n    if (!this.running) return true;\\n    if (s.wait) { this._held = true; this._then = then || null; return true; }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n  _jump(id) {\\n    if (!this.nodes[id]) { E.warn('story:' + id, 'E.Story: no node \\\"' + id + '\\\" (a goto)'); this._end(); return false; }\\n14290→    this.node = id; this._steps = this.nodes[id]; this._i = 0; return true;\\n  }\\n  // a step's or a choice's actions: set, add, quest, done, emote, end (its event: _fire)\\n  _act(s) {\\n    if (s.set !== undefined) { if (typeof s.set === 'string') this.vars[s.set] = true; else Object.assign(this.vars, s.set); }\\n    if (s.add) for (const k in s.add) this.vars[k] = (+this.vars[k] || 0) + s.add[k];\\n    if (s.quest) this.quest(...s.quest);\\n    if (s.done) this.done(s.done);\\n    if (s.emote) { const at = (this.people[s.who] || {}).at; if (at) this.emote(at, s.emote); }\\n    if (s.end) this._end();\\n14300→  }\\n  _end() { const f = this._done; this.running = false; this.node = null; this._done = null; if (f) f(this); }\\n  /** run the talk and the balloons; true while a node runs (play waits) */\\n  update(dt) {\\n    for (const b of this._balloons) b.t += dt;\\n    E.prune(this._balloons, b => b.t >= b.dur);\\n    if (!this.running) return false;\\n    if (this._wait > 0) { this._wait -= dt; if (this._wait <= 0) { this._wait = 0; this._next(); } return this.running; }\\n    if (!this._held) this.talk.update(dt);\\n    return this.running;\\n14310→  }\\n  /** a flag or value (key may be a dotted path into vars) */\\n  get(key) { let v = this.vars; for (const k of String(key).split('.')) v = v == null ? undefined : v[k]; return v; }\\n  /** set a flag (value true) or a value */\\n  set(key, value = true) { this.vars[key] = value; return value; }\\n  /** does a condition hold? (the manual's conditions) */\\n  test(c) {\\n    if (c === undefined || c === null) return true;\\n    if (typeof c === 'function') return !!c(this);\\n    if (Array.isArray(c)) return c.every(x => this.test(x));\\n14320→    c = String(c).trim();\\n    if (c[0] === '!') return !this.test(c.slice(1));\\n    let m = /^(quest|done):(.+)$/.exec(c);\\n    if (m) { const q = this.quests.find(q => q.id === m[2]); return !!q && (m[1] === 'quest' || q.done); }\\n    m = /^([\\\\w.$]+)\\\\s*(==|!=|>=|<=|>|<)\\\\s*(.+)$/.exec(c);\\n    if (m) {\\n      const a = this.get(m[1]), w = m[3].trim(), b = w !== '' && !isNaN(+w) ? +w : w.replace(/^['\\\"]|['\\\"]$/g, '');\\n      return m[2] === '==' ? a == b : m[2] === '!=' ? a != b : m[2] === '>=' ? a >= b : m[2] === '<=' ? a <= b : m[2] === '>' ? a > b : a < b;   // (a word compares as text)\\n    }\\n    return !!this.get(c);\\n14330→  }\\n  /** take a quest (or change its title and text): it joins the log */\\n  quest(id, title = id, text = '') {\\n    const q = this.quests.find(q => q.id === id);\\n    if (q) Object.assign(q, { title, text }); else this.quests.push({ id, title, text, done: false });\\n    return this;\\n  }\\n  /** finish a quest (taken now if it wasn't) */\\n  done(id) { if (!this.quests.some(q => q.id === id)) this.quest(id); this.quests.find(q => q.id === id).done = true; return this; }\\n  /** a balloon over target (x, y, z; h: its height) for seconds: '!', '?', 'heart', 'dots', 'note' */\\n14340→  emote(target, kind = '!', seconds = 1.5) { this._balloons.push({ at: target, kind, t: 0, dur: seconds }); return this; }\\n  /** draw the balloons over their targets and the box (anywhere in draw: both go to the overlay) */\\n  draw(r) {\\n    if (this._balloons.length) r.overlay(g => {\\n      for (const b of this._balloons) {\\n        const a = b.at, [sx, sy] = r.w(a.x, a.y, (a.z || 0) + (a.h || 28) + 4), x = Math.round(sx) - 6, y = Math.round(sy) - 14 - Math.round(Math.min(1, b.t * 8) * 3);\\n        px.rect(g, x, y + 1, 13, 9, '#1a1030'); px.rect(g, x + 1, y, 11, 11, '#1a1030'); px.rect(g, x + 1, y + 1, 11, 9, '#ffffff');   // a round-cornered white box,\\n        px.rect(g, x + 4, y + 10, 4, 1, '#ffffff'); px.rect(g, x + 5, y + 11, 2, 1, '#ffffff'); px.dot(g, x + 3, y + 10, '#1a1030'); px.dot(g, x + 8, y + 10, '#1a1030'); px.dot(g, x + 4, y + 11, '#1a1030'); px.dot(g, x + 7, y + 11, '#1a1030'); px.dot(g, x + 5, y + 12, '#1a1030'); px.dot(g, x + 6, y + 12, '#1a1030');   // its tail\\n        if (b.kind === '!') { px.rect(g, x + 6, y + 2, 2, 5, '#e8384a'); px.rect(g, x + 6, y + 8, 2, 1, '#e8384a'); }\\n        else if (b.kind === 'heart') px.sprite(g, HEART, x + 4, y + 3);\\n14350→        else if (b.kind === 'dots') for (let k = 0; k < Math.min(3, Math.floor(b.t * 3) + 1); k++) px.rect(g, x + 3 + k * 3, y + 6, 2, 2, '#1a1030');   // one, two, three\\n        else E.font.text(g, b.kind === 'note' ? '♪' : b.kind, x + 7, y + 2, '#1a1030', { outline: false, align: 'center' });\\n      }\\n    });\\n    this.talk.draw(r);\\n  }\\n  /** its vars and quests, as JSON (for a save) */\\n  state() { return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify({ vars: this.vars, quests: this.quests })); }\\n  /** put back what state() gave (a load) */\\n  restore(s) {\\n14360→    if (!s) return this;\\n    for (const k in this.vars) delete this.vars[k];   // (the same object: the box reads it)\\n    Object.assign(this.vars, JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(s.vars || {}))); this.quests = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(s.quests || [])); return this;\\n  }\\n}\\nE.Story = Story;\\n})(typeof My3D2dge !== 'undefined' ? My3D2dge : undefined);\\n\\n/*!\\nmy-3D2dge module STRATEGY v0.89.1: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays\",\"content_concise\":\"14190→```js story\\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true });\\nconst story = new E.Story(game, { vars: { gold: 30, hero: 'ROWAN' }, nodes: {\\n  elder: [{ if: 'helping', goto: 'thanks'