{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_255","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`game.shell.screen` returns the open shell screen name or null.\n\nShell constructor returns early in headless mode. The screen getter still returns null. Pause overlay defaults to true for the default shell. Dev Mode will be added to the pause menu outside Hub sessions. The `openDev` function is being implemented.\n\n`openDev` hides the shell and resumes the scene. The dev panel overlays the current view. It intercepts confirm, cancel, and directional input while open. Cancel closes it. During active scenes the simulation continues running behind the overlay.\n\nInput keys will be suppressed while the dev panel is open. Left-stick wheel flicks remain functional.\n\nTool selection now supports prev and next buttons. The current tool index cycles through the eight available tools.\n\nTool selection buttons would repeat 16 times during substeps because `pressed` stays true across them. The fix is to apply digit and gift edges only once per engine frame, or consume the input immediately. The operation scene update now runs 16 substeps per frame for the driver seat.\n\nThe 16 substeps per engine step are reserved for bot playthroughs. Human play advances the simulation by a single step per frame. Bot simulation runs at roughly 42 seconds of simulated time per real second.\n\nEleven test cases should finish in roughly fifteen real seconds of advance time. Story skip will use talk.speed 1e6 and auto 0.\n\nStory skip takes about eight seconds of engine time. The bot driver does not need input between substeps. Audio events fire each substep but are harmless in headless mode. Winning or losing advances to the results screen once. Attract mode handles its own timer and skips results unless a segment requires it. Rank is recorded when entering results. The difficulty menu offers Intern, Resident, and Attending.\n\nThe default difficulty selection is Intern. The player must press down once to select Resident before confirming to start the story.\n\nNew Game now routes through the difficulty scene instead of launching directly into the story.\n\nThe main menu will list New Game, Case Files, Grand Rounds, Skills Lab, and About.\n\nCase Files will let players replay cleared cases. Cases may unlock upon completion or as the next available entry. Whether they run with or without the story skip is still undecided.\n\nCase Files will run a case with no story skip. The player selects a case and difficulty, then begins the operation directly.\n\nGrand Rounds uses a couch lobby scene. Players choose one to four surgeons. Solo play starts immediately. Extra seats fill with bots when no additional gamepads are connected. The lobby menu offers 1 through 4 surgeons. Confirming starts the round with that many players, mode rounds, seat zero human, and the rest as bots.\n\nSkills Lab runs the lab case and goes straight to the operation.\n\nThe About scene displays four ordered sections: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback. It scrolls with up or down and returns to the menu on cancel.\n\nCredits pages advance on confirm or right. The final page resumes the held story into the epilogue.\n\nBoth About and Credits include the four feedback sections plus the incoming chart door.\n\nThe credits scene will have six pages: cast, source information, testing feedback, engine feedback, prompt feedback, and an incoming chart door. Confirming advances through each page, with the final one resuming the story into the epilogue. The test pump will confirm through these pages quickly. A full playthrough pump will be written in tests later.\n\nThe ward scene places the hero near the door. A test can confirm immediately to leave, since nearDoor is true by default. After results resume the story, the pump must skip c1_out and wait for the ward event before confirming.\n\nThe full test flow is now mapped. Title confirm opens the menu. New Game selects Intern, then down once to Resident and confirm to start the story. Story skip runs until the choice prompt. The c1_in event triggers the operation without a lightbox. Bot driver clears the case, results appear, and confirming resumes the story into c1_out and the ward event. Confirming at the door advances to c2_in. The c2 operation event shows a chart lightbox for marking and clicking.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0213a3b0-6ba2-407d-bc80-7bf9528e2148-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/audio/audio.js","offset":80,"limit":140}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2602,"output_tokens":2229,"cache_read_input_tokens":132096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"24c2f5ef-ad43-4243-bee4-384f9ceb6467"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0213a3b0-6ba2-407d-bc80-7bf9528e2148-46","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"80→  }\\n\\n  function play(name) {\\n    if (!game || !game.audio || !game.audio.music) return;\\n    const song = SONGS[name] || SONGS.night;\\n    game.audio.music(song, { fade: 0.35, loop: true });\\n  }\\n\\n  function sfx(name) {\\n    if (!game || !game.audio || !game.audio.sfx) return;\\n90→    const voice = PRESETS[name] || PRESETS.ping;\\n    game.audio.sfx(voice, { vol: 0.8, vary: 0 });\\n  }\\n\\n  function blip(ch) {\\n    const b = bus('voice');\\n    const ctx = game && game.audio && game.audio.ctx;\\n    if (!b || !ctx) return;\\n    const code = ch && ch.charCodeAt ? ch.charCodeAt(0) : 64;\\n    const t = ctx.currentTime;\\n100→    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n    o.frequency.value = 160 + (code % 19) * 16;\\n    const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n    f.type = 'bandpass';\\n    f.frequency.value = 640 + (code % 11) * 90;\\n    f.Q.value = 7;\\n    const gn = ctx.createGain();\\n    gn.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n    gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.22, t + 0.012);\\n110→    gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.07);\\n    o.connect(f); f.connect(gn); gn.connect(b);\\n    o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.08);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stopChoir() {\\n    if (!choirNodes) return;\\n    const ctx = game && game.audio && game.audio.ctx;\\n    const t = ctx ? ctx.currentTime : 0;\\n    for (const n of choirNodes) {\\n120→      try { n.gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.05); n.osc.stop(t + 0.06); } catch (e) { /* already quiet */ }\\n    }\\n    choirNodes = null;\\n  }\\n\\n  function choir(on) {\\n    if (!on) { stopChoir(); return; }\\n    if (choirNodes) return;\\n    const b = bus('sfx');\\n    const ctx = game && game.audio && game.audio.ctx;\\n130→    if (!b || !ctx) return;\\n    const t = ctx.currentTime;\\n    choirNodes = [];\\n    const freqs = [196, 201, 247];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < freqs.length; i++) {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = freqs[i];\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'lowpass';\\n140→      f.frequency.value = 900;\\n      const gn = ctx.createGain();\\n      gn.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n      gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.06, t + 0.4);\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(gn); gn.connect(b);\\n      o.start(t);\\n      choirNodes.push({ osc: o, gain: gn });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n150→  function tone(ctx, freq, type, dur, gain) {\\n    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = type;\\n    o.frequency.value = freq;\\n    const g = ctx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, 0);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, dur);\\n    o.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n    o.start(0); o.stop(dur);\\n  }\\n160→\\n  function rmsOf(buf) {\\n    const d = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n    let s = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i++) s += d[i] * d[i];\\n    return Math.sqrt(s / d.length);\\n  }\\n\\n  async function renderProbe() {\\n    const AC = G.OfflineAudioContext || (typeof OfflineAudioContext !== 'undefined' ? OfflineAudioContext : null);\\n170→    if (!AC) return null;\\n    async function render(build) {\\n      const ctx = new AC(1, 12000, 22050);\\n      build(ctx);\\n      const buf = await ctx.startRendering();\\n      return rmsOf(buf);\\n    }\\n    const effect = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 440, 'square', 0.2, 0.4));\\n    const voice = await render((ctx) => {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n180→      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = 280;\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'bandpass';\\n      f.frequency.value = 1100;\\n      f.Q.value = 6;\\n      const g = ctx.createGain();\\n      g.gain.value = 0.35;\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n      o.start(0); o.stop(0.2);\\n190→    });\\n    const choirR = await render((ctx) => {\\n      for (const freq of [196, 201, 247]) tone(ctx, freq, 'sawtooth', 0.3, 0.12);\\n    });\\n    const music = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'triangle', 0.25, 0.1));\\n    const effects = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'square', 0.25, 1));\\n    return { effect, voice, choir: choirR, music, effects };\\n  }\\n\\n  function onEv(ev) {\\n200→    if (!ev || !ev.length) return;\\n    const k = ev[0];\\n    if (k === 'grip' || k === 'free') sfx('grip');\\n    else if (k === 'grade' || k === 'stitch') sfx('stitch');\\n    else if (k === 'tear' || k === 'snap' || k === 'miss') sfx('bad');\\n    else if (k === 'shock' || k === 'codeblue') sfx('shock');\\n    else if (k === 'stamp' || k === 'closed') sfx('stamp');\\n    else if (k === 'breath') choir(ev[1] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n210→  GAME.Audio = { SONGS, install, play, sfx, blip, choir, stopChoir, renderProbe, onEv };\\n})();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"80→  }\\n\\n  function play(name) {\\n    if (!game || !game.audio || !game.audio.music) return;\\n    const song = SONGS[name] || SONGS.night;\\n    game.audio.music(song, { fade: 0.35, loop: true });\\n  }\\n\\n  function sfx(name) {\\n    if (!game || !game.audio || !game.audio.sfx) return;\\n90→    const voice = PRESETS[name] || PRESETS.ping;\\n    game.audio.sfx(voice, { vol: 0.8, vary: 0 });\\n  }\\n\\n  function blip(ch) {\\n    const b = bus('voice');\\n    const ctx = game && game.audio && game.audio.ctx;\\n    if (!b || !ctx) return;\\n    const code = ch && ch.charCodeAt ? ch.charCodeAt(0) : 64;\\n    const t = ctx.currentTime;\\n100→    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n    o.frequency.value = 160 + (code % 19) * 16;\\n    const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n    f.type = 'bandpass';\\n    f.frequency.value = 640 + (code % 11) * 90;\\n    f.Q.value = 7;\\n    const gn = ctx.createGain();\\n    gn.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n    gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.22, t + 0.012);\\n110→    gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.07);\\n    o.connect(f); f.connect(gn); gn.connect(b);\\n    o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.08);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stopChoir() {\\n    if (!choirNodes) return;\\n    const ctx = game && game.audio && game.audio.ctx;\\n    const t = ctx ? ctx.currentTime : 0;\\n    for (const n of choirNodes) {\\n120→      try { n.gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.05); n.osc.stop(t + 0.06); } catch (e) { /* already quiet */ }\\n    }\\n    choirNodes = null;\\n  }\\n\\n  function choir(on) {\\n    if (!on) { stopChoir(); return; }\\n    if (choirNodes) return;\\n    const b = bus('sfx');\\n    const ctx = game && game.audio && game.audio.ctx;\\n130→    if (!b || !ctx) return;\\n    const t = ctx.currentTime;\\n    choirNodes = [];\\n    const freqs = [196, 201, 247];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < freqs.length; i++) {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = freqs[i];\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'lowpass';\\n140→      f.frequency.value = 900;\\n      const gn = ctx.createGain();\\n      gn.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n      gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.06, t + 0.4);\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(gn); gn.connect(b);\\n      o.start(t);\\n      choirNodes.push({ osc: o, gain: gn });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n150→  function tone(ctx, freq, type, dur, gain) {\\n    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = type;\\n    o.frequency.value = freq;\\n    const g = ctx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, 0);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, dur);\\n    o.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n    o.start(0); o.stop(dur);\\n  }\\n160→\\n  function rmsOf(buf) {\\n    const d = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n    let s = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i++) s += d[i] * d[i];\\n    return Math.sqrt(s / d.length);\\n  }\\n\\n  async function renderProbe() {\\n    const AC = G.OfflineAudioContext || (typeof OfflineAudioContext !== 'undefined' ? OfflineAudioContext : null);\\n170→    if (!AC) return null;\\n    async function render(build) {\\n      const ctx = new AC(1, 12000, 22050);\\n      build(ctx);\\n      const buf = await ctx.startRendering();\\n      return rmsOf(buf);\\n    }\\n    const effect = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 440, 'square', 0.2, 0.4));\\n    const voice = await render((ctx) => {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n180→      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = 280;\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'bandpass';\\n      f.frequency.value = 1100;\\n      f.Q.value = 6;\\n      const g = ctx.createGain();\\n      g.gain.value = 0.35;\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n      o.start(0); o.stop(0.2);\\n190→    });\\n    const choirR = await render((ctx) => {\\n      for (const freq of [196, 201, 247]) tone(ctx, freq, 'sawtooth', 0.3, 0.12);\\n    });\\n    const music = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'triangle', 0.25, 0.1));\\n    const effects = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'square', 0.25, 1));\\n    return { effect, voice, choir: choirR, music, effects };\\n  }\\n\\n  function onEv(ev) {\\n200→    if (!ev || !ev.length) return;\\n    const k = ev[0];\\n    if (k === 'grip' || k === 'free') sfx('grip');\\n    else if (k === 'grade' || k === 'stitch') sfx('stitch');\\n    else if (k === 'tear' || k === 'snap' || k === 'miss') sfx('bad');\\n    else if (k === 'shock' || k === 'codeblue') sfx('shock');\\n    else if (k === 'stamp' || k === 'closed') sfx('stamp');\\n    else if (k === 'breath') choir(ev[1] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n210→  GAME.Audio = { SONGS, install, play, sfx, blip, choir, stopChoir, renderProbe, onEv };\\n})();\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/audio/audio.js\",\"offset\":80,\"limit\":140,\"raw_output\":\"  }\\n\\n  function play(name) {\\n    if (!game || !game.audio || !game.audio.music) return;\\n    const song = SONGS[name] || SONGS.night;\\n    game.audio.music(song, { fade: 0.35, loop: true });\\n  }\\n\\n  function sfx(name) {\\n    if (!game || !game.audio || !game.audio.sfx) return;\\n    const voice = PRESETS[name] || PRESETS.ping;\\n    game.audio.sfx(voice, { vol: 0.8, vary: 0 });\\n  }\\n\\n  function blip(ch) {\\n    const b = bus('voice');\\n    const ctx = game && game.audio && game.audio.ctx;\\n    if (!b || !ctx) return;\\n    const code = ch && ch.charCodeAt ? ch.charCodeAt(0) : 64;\\n    const t = ctx.currentTime;\\n    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n    o.frequency.value = 160 + (code % 19) * 16;\\n    const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n    f.type = 'bandpass';\\n    f.frequency.value = 640 + (code % 11) * 90;\\n    f.Q.value = 7;\\n    const gn = ctx.createGain();\\n    gn.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n    gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.22, t + 0.012);\\n    gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.07);\\n    o.connect(f); f.connect(gn); gn.connect(b);\\n    o.start(t); o.stop(t + 0.08);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stopChoir() {\\n    if (!choirNodes) return;\\n    const ctx = game && game.audio && game.audio.ctx;\\n    const t = ctx ? ctx.currentTime : 0;\\n    for (const n of choirNodes) {\\n      try { n.gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, t + 0.05); n.osc.stop(t + 0.06); } catch (e) { /* already quiet */ }\\n    }\\n    choirNodes = null;\\n  }\\n\\n  function choir(on) {\\n    if (!on) { stopChoir(); return; }\\n    if (choirNodes) return;\\n    const b = bus('sfx');\\n    const ctx = game && game.audio && game.audio.ctx;\\n    if (!b || !ctx) return;\\n    const t = ctx.currentTime;\\n    choirNodes = [];\\n    const freqs = [196, 201, 247];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < freqs.length; i++) {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = freqs[i];\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'lowpass';\\n      f.frequency.value = 900;\\n      const gn = ctx.createGain();\\n      gn.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n      gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.06, t + 0.4);\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(gn); gn.connect(b);\\n      o.start(t);\\n      choirNodes.push({ osc: o, gain: gn });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function tone(ctx, freq, type, dur, gain) {\\n    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = type;\\n    o.frequency.value = freq;\\n    const g = ctx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, 0);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, dur);\\n    o.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n    o.start(0); o.stop(dur);\\n  }\\n\\n  function rmsOf(buf) {\\n    const d = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n    let s = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i++) s += d[i] * d[i];\\n    return Math.sqrt(s / d.length);\\n  }\\n\\n  async function renderProbe() {\\n    const AC = G.OfflineAudioContext || (typeof OfflineAudioContext !== 'undefined' ? OfflineAudioContext : null);\\n    if (!AC) return null;\\n    async function render(build) {\\n      const ctx = new AC(1, 12000, 22050);\\n      build(ctx);\\n      const buf = await ctx.startRendering();\\n      return rmsOf(buf);\\n    }\\n    const effect = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 440, 'square', 0.2, 0.4));\\n    const voice = await render((ctx) => {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = 280;\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'bandpass';\\n      f.frequency.value = 1100;\\n      f.Q.value = 6;\\n      const g = ctx.createGain();\\n      g.gain.value = 0.35;\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n      o.start(0); o.stop(0.2);\\n    });\\n    const choirR = await render((ctx) => {\\n      for (const freq of [196, 201, 247]) tone(ctx, freq, 'sawtooth', 0.3, 0.12);\\n    });\\n    const music = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'triangle', 0.25, 0.1));\\n    const effects = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'square', 0.25, 1));\\n    return { effect, voice, choir: choirR, music, effects };\\n  }\\n\\n  function onEv(ev) {\\n    if (!ev || !ev.length) return;\\n    const k = ev[0];\\n    if (k === 'grip' || k === 'free') sfx('grip');\\n    else if (k === 'grade' || k === 'stitch') sfx('stitch');\\n    else if (k === 'tear' || k === 'snap' || k === 'miss') sfx('bad');\\n    else if (k === 'shock' || k === 'codeblue') sfx('shock');\\n    else if (k === 'stamp' || k === 'closed') sfx('stamp');\\n    else if (k === 'breath') choir(ev[1] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n  GAME.Audio = { SONGS, install, play, sfx, blip, choir, stopChoir, renderProbe, onEv };\\n})();\\n\",\"total_lines\":211}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"01443c09-e230-42f6-8f7c-ee370831a089"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_256","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Evaluating whether to use a voice object or a name for audio.sfx.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b16f5393-c1dc-452b-a353-58c4388613d8-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","offset":7860,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3834,"output_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":134656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"a0471161-2933-4ad2-9932-31c0d2c9cc9b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b16f5393-c1dc-452b-a353-58c4388613d8-47","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"7860→  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\\n  /**\\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\\n7870→   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\\n   */\\n  music(song, o = {}) {\\n    if (typeof song === 'string') { const s = E.songs[song]; if (!s) { warn('song:' + song, 'unknown song \\\"' + song + '\\\". Built in: ' + Object.keys(E.songs).join(', ')); return; } song = s; }\\n    if (!song) { this.stopMusic(o.fade); return; }\\n    const old = this.song; if (old && old.src === song && !old.ended && !o.restart) return;\\n7880→    const C = this._clock(song, !!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync), o.loop !== undefined ? o.loop : song.loop !== false, this._now(!!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync)));\\n    if (!C) { warn('music:empty', 'music(song) needs song.tracks with notes'); return; }\\n    this.song = C; this._ats = [];\\n    this._stopSound(old, o.fade); this._sound(C, o.fade);\\n  }\\n  /** stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default) */\\n  stopMusic(fade) { const S = this.song; this.song = null; this._ats = []; this._stopSound(S, fade); }\\n  // a song's clock: its tracks' tokens, its steps' length, where it started (t0, at step s0: a tempo change moves them)\\n  _clock(song, sync, loop, t) {\\n    const tracks = (song.tracks || []).map((tr, k) => Object.assign({}, tr, { k, tokens: String(tr.notes || '').replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/).filter(Boolean) })).filter(tr => tr.tokens.length);\\n7890→    if (!tracks.length) return null;\\n    tracks.forEach((tr, i) => { tr.i = i; });\\n    const steps = song.steps || 4, bpm = song.bpm || 120;\\n    return { src: song, tracks, steps, bpm, spb: 60 / bpm / steps, len: song.len || Math.max(...tracks.map(tr => tr.tokens.length)), loop, sync, start: t, t0: t, s0: 0, done: -1, next: 0, ended: false, vols: tracks.map(tr => tr.on === false ? 0 : 1), bus: null, anchor: null, drift: 0, big: false };\\n  }\\n  // the clock a song runs on: game.time when synced (it pauses with the game), else game.real\\n  _now(sync) { const g = this._game; return g ? (sync ? g.time : g.real) : 0; }\\n  _stepAt(C, t) { return C.s0 + (t - C.t0) / C.spb; }\\n  _timeOf(C, k) { return C.t0 + (k - C.s0) * C.spb; }\\n  // the clock now between the game's steps: what it read at the last frame and the real time since (to schedule the\\n7900→  // sound and to place a tap's event time)\\n  _clockNow(C, perf) {\\n    const g = this._game, base = this._now(C.sync), F = this._fr;\\n    if (!F || !g || typeof performance === 'undefined') return base;\\n    const rate = C.sync && (g.paused || g.hitstop > 0) ? 0 : g.timeScale;\\n    return base + (F.acc + Math.min(.1, ((perf === undefined ? performance.now() : perf) - F.perf) / 1000)) * rate;\\n  }\\n  /** where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on\\n   *  as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's\\n   *  volume), playing } */\",\"content_concise\":\"7860→  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\\n  /**\\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\\n7870→   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\\n   */\\n  music(song, o = {}) {\\n    if (typeof song === 'string') { const s = E.songs[song]; if (!s) { warn('song:' + song, 'unknown song \\\"' + song + '\\\". Built in: ' + Object.keys(E.songs).join(', ')); return; } song = s; }\\n    if (!song) { this.stopMusic(o.fade); return; }\\n    const old = this.song; if (old && old.src === song && !old.ended && !o.restart) return;\\n7880→    const C = this._clock(song, !!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync), o.loop !== undefined ? o.loop : song.loop !== false, this._now(!!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync)));\\n    if (!C) { warn('music:empty', 'music(song) needs song.tracks with notes'); return; }\\n    this.song = C; this._ats = [];\\n    this._stopSound(old, o.fade); this._sound(C, o.fade);\\n  }\\n  /** stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default) */\\n  stopMusic(fade) { const S = this.song; this.song = null; this._ats = []; this._stopSound(S, fade); }\\n  // a song's clock: its tracks' tokens, its steps' length, where it started (t0, at step s0: a tempo change moves them)\\n  _clock(song, sync, loop, t) {\\n    const tracks = (song.tracks || []).map((tr, k) => Object.assign({}, tr, { k, tokens: String(tr.notes || '').replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/).filter(Boolean) })).filter(tr => tr.tokens.length);\\n7890→    if (!tracks.length) return null;\\n    tracks.forEach((tr, i) => { tr.i = i; });\\n    const steps = song.steps || 4, bpm = song.bpm || 120;\\n    return { src: song, tracks, steps, bpm, spb: 60 / bpm / steps, len: song.len || Math.max(...tracks.map(tr => tr.tokens.length)), loop, sync, start: t, t0: t, s0: 0, done: -1, next: 0, ended: false, vols: tracks.map(tr => tr.on === false ? 0 : 1), bus: null, anchor: null, drift: 0, big: false };\\n  }\\n  // the clock a song runs on: game.time when synced (it pauses with the game), else game.real\\n  _now(sync) { const g = this._game; return g ? (sync ? g.time : g.real) : 0; }\\n  _stepAt(C, t) { return C.s0 + (t - C.t0) / C.spb; }\\n  _timeOf(C, k) { return C.t0 + (k - C.s0) * C.spb; }\\n  // the clock now between the game's steps: what it read at the last frame and the real time since (to schedule the\\n7900→  // sound and to place a tap's event time)\\n  _clockNow(C, perf) {\\n    const g = this._game, base = this._now(C.sync), F = this._fr;\\n    if (!F || !g || typeof performance === 'undefined') return base;\\n    const rate = C.sync && (g.paused || g.hitstop > 0) ? 0 : g.timeScale;\\n    return base + (F.acc + Math.min(.1, ((perf === undefined ? performance.now() : perf) - F.perf) / 1000)) * rate;\\n  }\\n  /** where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on\\n   *  as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's\\n   *  volume), playing } */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":7860,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  /** add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 }) */\\n  define(name, voice) { this.presets[name] = voice; }\\n  /**\\n   * Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [\\n   *   { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' },   one token per step\\n   *   { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' },\\n   *   { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] }\\n   * tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines).\\n   * steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else\\n   * its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in).\\n   * THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same\\n   * steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on\\n   * game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing),\\n   * restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }.\\n   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\\n   */\\n  music(song, o = {}) {\\n    if (typeof song === 'string') { const s = E.songs[song]; if (!s) { warn('song:' + song, 'unknown song \\\"' + song + '\\\". Built in: ' + Object.keys(E.songs).join(', ')); return; } song = s; }\\n    if (!song) { this.stopMusic(o.fade); return; }\\n    const old = this.song; if (old && old.src === song && !old.ended && !o.restart) return;\\n    const C = this._clock(song, !!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync), o.loop !== undefined ? o.loop : song.loop !== false, this._now(!!(o.sync !== undefined ? o.sync : song.sync)));\\n    if (!C) { warn('music:empty', 'music(song) needs song.tracks with notes'); return; }\\n    this.song = C; this._ats = [];\\n    this._stopSound(old, o.fade); this._sound(C, o.fade);\\n  }\\n  /** stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default) */\\n  stopMusic(fade) { const S = this.song; this.song = null; this._ats = []; this._stopSound(S, fade); }\\n  // a song's clock: its tracks' tokens, its steps' length, where it started (t0, at step s0: a tempo change moves them)\\n  _clock(song, sync, loop, t) {\\n    const tracks = (song.tracks || []).map((tr, k) => Object.assign({}, tr, { k, tokens: String(tr.notes || '').replace(/\\\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\\\s+/).filter(Boolean) })).filter(tr => tr.tokens.length);\\n    if (!tracks.length) return null;\\n    tracks.forEach((tr, i) => { tr.i = i; });\\n    const steps = song.steps || 4, bpm = song.bpm || 120;\\n    return { src: song, tracks, steps, bpm, spb: 60 / bpm / steps, len: song.len || Math.max(...tracks.map(tr => tr.tokens.length)), loop, sync, start: t, t0: t, s0: 0, done: -1, next: 0, ended: false, vols: tracks.map(tr => tr.on === false ? 0 : 1), bus: null, anchor: null, drift: 0, big: false };\\n  }\\n  // the clock a song runs on: game.time when synced (it pauses with the game), else game.real\\n  _now(sync) { const g = this._game; return g ? (sync ? g.time : g.real) : 0; }\\n  _stepAt(C, t) { return C.s0 + (t - C.t0) / C.spb; }\\n  _timeOf(C, k) { return C.t0 + (k - C.s0) * C.spb; }\\n  // the clock now between the game's steps: what it read at the last frame and the real time since (to schedule the\\n  // sound and to place a tap's event time)\\n  _clockNow(C, perf) {\\n    const g = this._game, base = this._now(C.sync), F = this._fr;\\n    if (!F || !g || typeof performance === 'undefined') return base;\\n    const rate = C.sync && (g.paused || g.hitstop > 0) ? 0 : g.timeScale;\\n    return base + (F.acc + Math.min(.1, ((perf === undefined ? performance.now() : perf) - F.perf) / 1000)) * rate;\\n  }\\n  /** where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on\\n   *  as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's\\n   *  volume), playing } */\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"cf4b5503-09f6-47c3-976f-6880ee026164"}
