{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_263","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The shell buffers input while a screen is open.\n\nEscape pauses the scene on the frame it is pressed. Cancel does not fire that frame. KeyX cancels without pausing. The idle hook runs before shell._step when settings are open.\n\nThe idle hook will check shell.screen to avoid counting frames while settings are open. Attract mode should not run during fade transitions. shell.js will be written in parts, structured into sections for core logic, helpers, story data, and the main draw loop.\n\nThe shell.js structure now includes scenes, attract mode, hub, and hooks. Menus will be built with a reusable E.Menu factory using custom colors. The title screen uses a simple confirm prompt instead of a menu. Case file lists will scroll across six rows. The dev panel is drawn manually with three tabs for tune, cheat, and jump.\n\nTuning keys will be adjusted in steps of one-twentieth of the range. A reset row will be added to the dev panel. A cheat list is being drafted with reveal and infinite steady options.\n\nThe cheat list now includes lock vitals, freeze clock, one hit, autosurgeon, slow motion, clear phase, force lost, and vitals to zero. Slow motion cycles timeScale between 0.25, 0.5, 1, and 2. Any cheat sets RT.cheatUsed to true, which blocks rank. Results checks for dirty tuning, RT.cheatUsed, or active S.cheat flags.\n\nAttract mode will not set RT.cheatUsed or TUNE.dirty, so it cannot poison the campaign rank. The dev panel draws at font scale 1 on the right and closes with cancel when open. Confirming a tune row only resets the selection. Dev input will be handled at the start of the op, ward, and hub update loops.\n\nA shared `devInput()` helper will handle dev panel input across pausable scenes. It consumes cancel to close the panel and handles tab switching with toolPrev, toolNext, or Shift+arrow keys. When the dev panel is open, arrow keys move the panel instead of the hero, while WASD still controls movement.\n\nThe dev panel will always return true to swallow input, which would freeze the ward scene. The op scene should still simulate underneath. Confirm during op is not useTool, but Pad0 might also map to useTool.\n\nThe dev panel will only consume input when it actually handles a dev action. While the panel is open, confirm is ignored so the ward scene can still exit doors. Op still uses useTool normally. Pad0 is both confirm and useTool, but the dev panel avoids binding confirm to any dev action, keeping tool use separate.\n\nGAME.snapshot will be exposed for tests. The attract reel is being defined as a data-driven array of segments, each specifying a scene type, duration, and optional cheat flags.\n\nThe attract reel now includes a rounds segment and a card segment. The story segment will render a bust image and run a minimal story update to keep the narrative state alive.\n\nThe story segment will use the c3_out[2] line node and run a beat update each frame. When a reel segment changes, the story state is reset.\n\nOp segments begin a case with optional cheat flags and drive with real dt instead of the fast demo driver. A 15-second case demo will not finish naturally, so it carries a DEMO ribbon and ranks are not recorded.\n\nAfter the title segment ends, the reel loops back to the start with an incremented loop counter.\n\nAttract draw logic branches by segment type: title draws the title screen, card draws a results-style card, op draws the op scene, and story draws the story state. The camera uses overhead view for op segments and side view for title.\n\nThe attract update will call game.setView once per segment. DEMO text will render at scale 2. beginCase for attract mode will not set fromStory. Chart bonuses now apply when opening an op: right-click adds 20 to clock and steady, while left-click subtracts 10 times the miss count. The chart screen will detect clicks via I.clicked() and screenMark().\n\nChart clicks within 14 pixels of the mark open the op with a bonus. Misses accumulate and trigger a fallback after three. The mark renders as a crosshair. Keyboard confirm does not guess; tests feed clicks directly. screenMark uses current window dimensions, and feed click stores coordinates in screen pixels. The results menu shows Retry and Give up when the player lost, or Continue otherwise.\n\nThe results menu retry path calls `retryPhase` and returns to the op scene. Lab loss sends the player back to the menu, while a lab win continues to the lab and then the menu. Rounds win returns to the lobby. Story wins resume from the held state if the player is holding. `fromStory` is set only on op events, so continuing from results resumes the story.\n\nThe `leaveResults` function now routes to the story scene when `fromStory` is true and a story hold exists. It returns to the menu for lab losses, to the lobby for rounds wins, and to the ward for story-won cases.\n\nResuming a held story from results lands on the c1_out dialogue node, not the ward event. The third branch in leaveResults is only a fallback for stories that have already advanced past the held point. A double-go bug was considered but ruled out because resume() returns immediately when the next step is dialogue.\n\nWard entry enables saving and sets the hero position and visitors. Ward exit disables saving. Confirm near a door resumes a held story if present, otherwise returns to the menu. Story resume from the ward advances to the next cN_in dialogue node.\n\nThe credits scene will advance through pages lazily, using the four ABOUT sections plus an incoming page as the final entry. Confirming on the last page resumes the story epilogue. The about scene from the menu will not resume a held story; cancel returns to the menu. A controls hint using input labels will be added to the title screen.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e0f16310-0ca9-47e7-9641-fb3d16fed17