{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_278","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The game flow works correctly from title through menu, difficulty, resident selection, story choice, and c1 operation.\n\nThe NO_COLOR warning appeared because both color environment variables were set. The test runner must respawn itself without them. I will write tests/run.mjs to handle this, load shipped code, run all checks, print only FAIL lines and a count, and support --fast to skip browser and hub tests.\n\nAll scripts will be loaded once in a fresh process. Pure simulation tests will run first, since they do not touch the game scene. Scene navigation tests will follow.\n\nA reset function will return the game to title between UI tests. It stops the story, clears runtime flags, and advances one step. The attract test will advance ten and a half seconds without input.\n\nThe attract test requires 1260 steps to accumulate ten and a half seconds of idle time. Title scene updates do not reset idle without input. Mouse and keyboard states are clean, so the attract screen should trigger after ten seconds. Playthrough tests will be fast with the 16x speed multiplier.\n\nThe browser tests will use Playwright from the dev folder. I need to verify whether it is installed globally or requires a local install. The Python hub runner can be spawned directly inside run.mjs. Any output from those subprocesses should be swallowed.\n\nI will verify that Playwright is importable before proceeding. The test suite will be written first and run with --fast to validate simulation and scene checks without needing the browser HTML. Then I will create build.mjs, bundle the project, and run the full suite including browser and hub tests.\n\nThe respawn logic filters out NO_COLOR warnings, trace warnings, and node stack traces from the child process output. Only FAIL lines and the final check count are written to stdout.\n\nA `check` helper will track test names, failures, and print FAIL lines. The test body must stay silent because the runner filters output; only the respawn wrapper handles warnings. Scripts will be loaded via vm to avoid polluting globals.\n\nThe game scripts are IIFEs, so vm is the correct loader. Playwright will run in the parent process while tests execute inside a separate vm context. The cursor test must verify that createRaw sets activeDoc from the doctor option, and blank() copies opts.doctor into activeDoc.\n\nThe cursor test will verify that a full-stick aim moves the player at least 300 pixels, while a fine aim caps movement near 120 pixels. With the Vale doctor active, fine aim should yield roughly 132 pixels, exceeding Sokolova's fine aim.\n\nEmpty-field cursor tests verify that a full-stick aim moves the player 310 pixels and a fine aim 120 pixels, both staying within the 418-pixel right edge. The forceps wheel test checks that moving northeast for 100 milliseconds changes the tool to scalpel, since the sector needs only 80 milliseconds to stabilize. A digit test is also being drafted.\n\nThe digit test will verify that wheel input 3 selects the suture tool. Tool tests will drive gestures and call step directly. The suite will be written quickly and refined iteratively. Determinism is guaranteed because the simulation state hash excludes drawing.\n\nA concrete test will step identical states twice and compare hashes. It will also toggle Art.force shade on and off during the same two-second Bot.play run, confirming that drawing does not affect the simulation state hash.\n\nA code-blue test will use createRaw with vitals set to 1, zero drain, and no objects. Stepping the simulation to zero vitals should trigger the code-blue state. A peaks test will step near 0.9 seconds and press.\n\nA test will set clock and vitals to zero before stepping, confirming the simulation loses on time without triggering code blue. Another test will verify that during a long breath, world scale drops to 0.25 while the cursor still moves at real time.\n\nA gift test will set steady to 40 and gift to 'breath' with the Vale doctor active, then step once while gift is true and once while false, verifying the breath state and world scale of 0.25. A second look test will fill the look ring by stepping for one second, then compare the core values after a secondLook.\n\nThe second look test will deep-equal the look ring entry's core objects, clock, and vitals against the pre-step state. It will not compare post-restore steady values because secondLook reduces steady.\n\nA lightbox screen test will verify that the chart snapshot mark equals origin plus mark. Headless coordinates are OX=0 and OY=0 at 427x240. The c2 mark is [248,96].\n\nA difficulty test will compare intern and resident cases. Intern should last longer because its clock divisor is smaller. The test must step past the tutorial freeze, so c2 or a raw state with drain is needed. I also need to verify that createRaw passes the difficulty option through to blank.\n\nThe test suite will also cover legato snap, da capo partial kill, cantor rewind, retractor solo, all eleven bot cases, playthrough, attract, dev, about text, audio volumes, and grand rounds bots. A pump script using the bot device at 45 fps is being sketched to drive the playthrough.\n\nThe pump script will drive the playthrough by tapping confirm through the title, difficulty, and story menus. It will advance the story while no choice is present. When a choice appears it will tap confirm. On the chart screen it will tap the lightbox mark. Inside the operation scene it will advance at half speed. At results it will tap confirm again. Finally it will check that the player is near the door in the ward.\n\nThe pump script will also tap confirm on the credits screen and return to title. Chart clicks require feeding input and then advancing so the scene update reads the click in the same step; feeding after the tick would be too late.\n\nThe tap() helper advances the simulation once after pressing a button. The scene update processes the press during that step, but the actual transition to the next scene happens on the following advance. This means the smoke test must step again to reach the new scene.\n\nThe smoke test confirms that `tap()` only queues a scene transition; the actual switch happens on the next advance. The pump script will therefore need two steps after each tap to reliably enter the new scene.\n\nadvance(1/30) runs multiple _steps, so the scene transition can fire immediately within that same call. The smoke test used a single step() after tap(), which is why an extra step() was needed to reach the new scene.\n\nA `press` helper will queue an input and advance twice to reliably enter the next scene. Chart clicks will feed a move, down, and up gesture before advancing twice. I will verify chart behavior in a small script before writing the full suite.\n\nThe attract test will advance 11 seconds from the title screen. Idle time accumulates each step, so the scene should trigger after about ten seconds and enter on a later step. The pump script will need an extra step to reliably reach the attract screen.\n\nThe attract scene consumes all input, so a confirm press during that scene is discarded and never reaches the title screen. The test must avoid pressing confirm while attract is active.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0c60aea5-b372-4ba8-8ab2-d95d521c02b0-73","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node << 'EOF'\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nconst root = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916';\nconst files = ['src/config.js','src/core/sim.js','src/data/content.js','src/art/field.js','src/audio/audio.js','src/about.js','src/bot/bot.js','src/scenes/shell.js'];\nconst context = { console, performance, Math, Date, setTimeout, clearTimeout, setInterval, clearInterval, navigator: { getGamepads: () => [] }, queueMicrotask };\ncontext.window = context; context.globalThis = context;\nvm.createContext(context);\nvm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(root + '/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js','utf8'), context, { filename: 'engine.js' });\nfor (const f of files) vm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(root+'/'+f,'utf8'), context, { filename: f });\nconst game = context.My3D2dge.current;\ngame.fadeTime = 0;\nconst t0 = Date.now();\ngame.advance(10.2);\nconsole.log('after idle', game.sceneName, 'ms', Date.now()-t0, 'loops', game.debug.snapshot().reel);\ngame.input.tap('confirm');\ngame.advance(0.05);\nconsole.log('after input', game.sceneName, game.debug.snapshot().menu);\nEOF","description":"Check attract idle and that input returns to the title"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1189,"output_tokens":5387,"cache_read_input_tokens":194432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"1414cdd6-9ccc-4514-93bf-05a666a0883e"}
