's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\\n\\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\\n\\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\\n\\n## Done\\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\\n\\n## Source Information\\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:39:16\\n- Source: the work it's based on\\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\\n- Art Direction: style used\\n- Animation: system used\\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\\n- Online: network features used, or none\\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\\n- Research: research done, or none\\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\n- Usage: write \\\"added on import\\\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\\n\\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\\n{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\\"date\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"plan\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"genre\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"tech\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"animation\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"audio\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"online\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"testing\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"research\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"environment\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"model\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"},\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\\\"],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"the game's title, as on its title screen\\\",\\n    \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"a few words to go under the title\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"one or two sentences for the catalogue\\\",\\n    \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game, Tech demo or Tool\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\\\",\\n    \\\"series\\\": \\\"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\\\",\\n    \\\"players\\\": \\\"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\\\",\\n    \\\"controls\\\": \\\"the controls, in one line\\\",\\n    \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\\\"]\\n  }\\n}\\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\\n\\nTesting Feedback\\n\\n- How many issues did testing catch?\\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\\n\\nEngine Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about the engine?\\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\\n\\nPrompt Feedback\\n\\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\\n- What was confusing?\\n\",\"total_lines\":151}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"b2d3506e-6a60-4527-baf3-3a7d8b7b93d5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_284","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to determine the initial position for makePlayer.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ee40bd3-662e-4dd6-aaf8-003398527464-9","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":1,"limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ee40bd3-662e-4dd6-aaf8-003398527464-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":470,"limit":450}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ee40bd3-662e-4dd6-aaf8-003398527464-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/config.js","offset":1,"limit":120}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47990,"output_tokens":373,"cache_read_input_tokens":10112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"3c55a6f5-1293-4fc9-b1e9-afa976930b91"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7ee40bd3-662e-4dd6-aaf8-003398527464-9","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/* Operation sim. Plain data in, plain data out. No drawing, no audio, no DOM.\\n   Cursor and the wheel sit beside it and feed the same inputs a pad does. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const CFG = GAME.CFG;\\n  const TAU = Math.PI * 2;\\n\\n  const DRAIN = {\\n10→    shard: 0.1, fragment: 0.1, cork: 0.1, laceration: 0.2, bite: 0.2, wound: 0.4,\\n    bleeder: 0.5, arteryTear: 1, polyp: 0.1, mass: 0.2, hook: 0.3, gaff: 0.3,\\n    clot: 0.3, patch: 0.1, nest: 0.15, bead: 0, rupture: 0.45, screw: 0, wire: 0,\\n    pool: 0, retractor: 0, slur: 0, reed: 0, tremass: 0.4, lobe: 0.2, eye: 0.35,\\n    tendril: 0.2, uvula: 0.3, voice: 0.4, repeat: 0, spiral: 0, note: 0.2, nerve: 0,\\n    eloquent: 0, hold: 0,\\n  };\\n\\n  function rnd(S) {\\n    let x = (S.rng >>> 0) || 1;\\n20→    x ^= x << 13; x >>>= 0;\\n    x ^= x >>> 17; x >>>= 0;\\n    x ^= x << 5; x >>>= 0;\\n    if (!x) x = 1;\\n    S.rng = x;\\n    return x / 4294967296;\\n  }\\n  function clamp(v, a, b) { return v < a ? a : v > b ? b : v; }\\n  function hypot(x, y) { return Math.hypot(x, y); }\\n  function clone(v) { return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(v)); }\\n30→  function tuneOf(t) { return t || GAME.TUNE || CFG.cloneTune(CFG.TUNING); }\\n  function diffDrain(S) { return S.diff === 'intern' ? 0.7 : S.diff === 'attending' ? 1.3 : 1; }\\n  function diffClock(S) { return S.diff === 'intern' ? 1.3 : S.diff === 'attending' ? 0.8 : 1; }\\n  function syringeDose(S, tune) {\\n    const base = tune.patient.syringe;\\n    if (S.diff === 'intern') return 24 * (base / 18);\\n    if (S.diff === 'attending') return 12 * (base / 18);\\n    return base;\\n  }\\n\\n40→  function objById(S, id) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) if (S.objects[i].id === id) return S.objects[i];\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  function pushEv(S, ev) { S.ev.push(ev); }\\n\\n  function slip(S, p, kind, dmg, tune) {\\n    S.slips += 1;\\n    if (p) p.slips += 1;\\n50→    S.vitals -= dmg * tune.patient.slip;\\n    S.streak = 0;\\n    S.flow = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['slip', kind, dmg, p ? p.id : -1]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function award(S, p, grade, base, tune) {\\n    const mult = grade === 'textbook' ? 1.5 : grade === 'clean' ? 1 : 0.4;\\n    const pts = base * mult * S.flow;\\n    S.score += pts;\\n60→    p.score += pts;\\n    p.actions += 1;\\n    S.techAll += 1;\\n    if (grade !== 'sloppy') S.techGood += 1;\\n    if (grade === 'textbook') { p.textbooks += 1; S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 10 * tune.gift.charge); }\\n    else if (grade === 'clean') S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 5 * tune.gift.charge);\\n    if (grade === 'sloppy') { S.streak = 0; S.flow = 1; }\\n    else {\\n      S.streak += 1;\\n      S.flow = Math.min(2, 1 + 0.05 * S.streak);\\n70→      if (S.flow > S.bestFlow) S.bestFlow = S.flow;\\n    }\\n    if (!S.tutDone) S.tutDone = true;\\n    pushEv(S, ['grade', Math.round(p.x), Math.round(p.y), grade, Math.round(pts)]);\\n    return grade;\\n  }\\n\\n  function makePlayer(i, color) {\\n    return {\\n      id: i, x: 213, y: 150, bx: 213, by: 150, tool: 'forceps', trig: 0, prevTrig: 0,\\n80→      fine: false, held: 0, stroke: null, heat: 0, lock: 0, fill: 0, over: 0,\\n      cool: 0, score: 0, slips: 0, actions: 0, textbooks: 0, stitches: 0,\\n      suctioned: 0, burned: 0, speed: 0, wheelT: 0, wheelDir: -1, swap: 0,\\n      giftPrev: false, consultPrev: false, color: color || CFG.SEAT[i] || '#e8443a',\\n      gone: false, lx: 213, ly: 150, charT: 0, charSlip: false, bare: 0, bareT: 0,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  function blank(opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n90→    const n = opts.players || 1;\\n    const S = {\\n      id: opts.id || 'raw', seed: (opts.seed >>> 0) || 1, rng: (opts.seed >>> 0) || 1,\\n      diff: opts.difficulty || opts.diff || 'resident',\\n      clock: opts.clock != null ? opts.clock : 180,\\n      clock0: opts.clock != null ? opts.clock : 180,\\n      vitals: opts.vitals != null ? opts.vitals : 80,\\n      drain: opts.drain != null ? opts.drain : 0,\\n      phase: 0, phaseCount: 1, phaseName: opts.phaseName || 'Work',\\n      objects: [], nextId: 1, players: [],\\n100→      steady: opts.steady || 0, breath: false, worldScale: 1,\\n      gift: opts.gift || 'breath', doctor: opts.doctor || 'vale', activeDoc: opts.doctor || 'vale',\\n      consult: !!opts.consult, mode: opts.mode || 'case',\\n      codeBlueUsed: false, codeBlue: null, lost: false, won: false, closed: false, reason: '',\\n      score: 0, slips: 0, flow: 1, streak: 0, bestFlow: 1, techGood: 0, techAll: 0,\\n      t: 0, worldT: 0, phaseT: 0, ev: [], ghosts: [], ghostT: 0,\\n      ring: [], ringAcc: 0, checkpoint: null, rankCap: null, par: opts.par || 1000,\\n      site: opts.site || 'abdomen', tutorial: !!opts.tutorial, tutDone: !opts.tutorial,\\n      strain: null, flags: {}, scripts: [], tiltAmp: 0, dim: 0, dressing: null,\\n      device: null, windowOpen: 0, dev: !!opts.dev,\\n110→    };\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) S.players.push(makePlayer(i, opts.colors && opts.colors[i]));\\n    return S;\\n  }\\n\\n  function addObj(S, spec) {\\n    const o = Object.assign({\\n      id: S.nextId++, type: 'shard', x: 213, y: 116, alive: true, done: false,\\n      hidden: false, marked: false, markT: 0, under: 0, prog: 0, order: 0,\\n      drain: 0, grade: '', tag: '',\\n120→    }, spec);\\n    if (o.drain == null || spec.drain == null) o.drain = spec.drain != null ? spec.drain : (DRAIN[o.type] || 0);\\n    if (!o.origin) o.origin = [o.x, o.y];\\n    if (!o.axis) o.axis = [1, 0];\\n    const al = hypot(o.axis[0], o.axis[1]) || 1;\\n    o.axis = [o.axis[0] / al, o.axis[1] / al];\\n    if (o.depth == null) o.depth = 16;\\n    if (o.type === 'pool' && o.vol == null) o.vol = o.max || 36;\\n    if (o.type === 'pool' && o.max == null) o.max = o.vol;\\n    if ((o.type === 'wound' || o.type === 'arteryTear') && !o.pairs) {\\n130→      const n = o.stitches || (o.type === 'arteryTear' ? 3 : 4);\\n      o.pairs = [];\\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        const y = o.y - (n - 1) * 4 + i * 8;\\n        o.pairs.push([[o.x - 8, y], [o.x + 8, y]]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (o.pairs) o.stitch = 0;\\n    if ((o.type === 'laceration' || o.type === 'patch' || o.type === 'bite') && !o.cells) {\\n      const r = o.r || 12;\\n140→      o.cells = [];\\n      for (let y = -r; y <= r; y += 4) for (let x = -r; x <= r; x += 4) {\\n        if (x * x + y * y <= r * r) o.cells.push([o.x + x, o.y + y, 0]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if ((o.type === 'mass' || o.type === 'spiral' || o.type === 'slur' || o.type === 'tendril' || o.type === 'wire' || o.type === 'repeat') && !o.guide) {\\n      const len = o.len || 48;\\n      o.guide = [[o.x - len / 2, o.y], [o.x + len / 2, o.y]];\\n    }\\n    if (o.type === 'mass' && !o.ring) {\\n150→      o.ring = true;\\n      const rad = o.rad || 16;\\n      o.guide = [];\\n      for (let i = 0; i <= 12; i++) {\\n        const a = -Math.PI / 2 + TAU * i / 12;\\n        o.guide.push([o.x + Math.cos(a) * rad, o.y + Math.sin(a) * rad]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (o.type === 'retractorHandle') o.type = 'retractor';\\n    if (spec.underTag) {\\n160→      const pool = S.objects.find(q => q.tag === spec.underTag);\\n      if (pool) o.under = pool.id;\\n    }\\n    if (o.need == null) {\\n      if (o.type === 'polyp') o.need = 0.5;\\n      else if (o.type === 'bleeder' || o.type === 'rupture') o.need = 0.35;\\n      else if (o.type === 'bead') o.need = 0.12;\\n      else if (o.type === 'uvula') o.need = 1.5;\\n      else if (o.type === 'eye') o.need = 0.3;\\n      else if (o.type === 'tremass') o.need = 3;\\n170→      else o.need = 0.5;\\n    }\\n    S.objects.push(o);\\n    return o;\\n  }\\n\\n  function inDome(S, x, y) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n    if (!st || !st.domes) return false;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < st.domes.length; i++) {\\n180→      const d = st.domes[i];\\n      if (d.t > 0 && hypot(x - d.x, y - d.y) <= d.r) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function covered(S, o) {\\n    if (!o.under) return false;\\n    const p = objById(S, o.under);\\n    return !!(p && !p.done && p.vol > 1);\\n190→  }\\n\\n  function canTouch(S, o) {\\n    if (!o || o.done || !o.alive) return false;\\n    if (covered(S, o)) return false;\\n    if (o.hidden && !o.marked) return false;\\n    if (o.needsWindow && S.windowOpen <= 0) return false;\\n    if (o.needsBoard && S.device && !S.device.shown) return false;\\n    if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return !!o.window;\\n    if (o.type === 'lobe') return !!o.open;\\n200→    if (o.type === 'eye') return !!o.open;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/* Operation sim. Plain data in, plain data out. No drawing, no audio, no DOM.\\n   Cursor and the wheel sit beside it and feed the same inputs a pad does. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const CFG = GAME.CFG;\\n  const TAU = Math.PI * 2;\\n\\n  const DRAIN = {\\n10→    shard: 0.1, fragment: 0.1, cork: 0.1, laceration: 0.2, bite: 0.2, wound: 0.4,\\n    bleeder: 0.5, arteryTear: 1, polyp: 0.1, mass: 0.2, hook: 0.3, gaff: 0.3,\\n    clot: 0.3, patch: 0.1, nest: 0.15, bead: 0, rupture: 0.45, screw: 0, wire: 0,\\n    pool: 0, retractor: 0, slur: 0, reed: 0, tremass: 0.4, lobe: 0.2, eye: 0.35,\\n    tendril: 0.2, uvula: 0.3, voice: 0.4, repeat: 0, spiral: 0, note: 0.2, nerve: 0,\\n    eloquent: 0, hold: 0,\\n  };\\n\\n  function rnd(S) {\\n    let x = (S.rng >>> 0) || 1;\\n20→    x ^= x << 13; x >>>= 0;\\n    x ^= x >>> 17; x >>>= 0;\\n    x ^= x << 5; x >>>= 0;\\n    if (!x) x = 1;\\n    S.rng = x;\\n    return x / 4294967296;\\n  }\\n  function clamp(v, a, b) { return v < a ? a : v > b ? b : v; }\\n  function hypot(x, y) { return Math.hypot(x, y); }\\n  function clone(v) { return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(v)); }\\n30→  function tuneOf(t) { return t || GAME.TUNE || CFG.cloneTune(CFG.TUNING); }\\n  function diffDrain(S) { return S.diff === 'intern' ? 0.7 : S.diff === 'attending' ? 1.3 : 1; }\\n  function diffClock(S) { return S.diff === 'intern' ? 1.3 : S.diff === 'attending' ? 0.8 : 1; }\\n  function syringeDose(S, tune) {\\n    const base = tune.patient.syringe;\\n    if (S.diff === 'intern') return 24 * (base / 18);\\n    if (S.diff === 'attending') return 12 * (base / 18);\\n    return base;\\n  }\\n\\n40→  function objById(S, id) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) if (S.objects[i].id === id) return S.objects[i];\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  function pushEv(S, ev) { S.ev.push(ev); }\\n\\n  function slip(S, p, kind, dmg, tune) {\\n    S.slips += 1;\\n    if (p) p.slips += 1;\\n50→    S.vitals -= dmg * tune.patient.slip;\\n    S.streak = 0;\\n    S.flow = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['slip', kind, dmg, p ? p.id : -1]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function award(S, p, grade, base, tune) {\\n    const mult = grade === 'textbook' ? 1.5 : grade === 'clean' ? 1 : 0.4;\\n    const pts = base * mult * S.flow;\\n    S.score += pts;\\n60→    p.score += pts;\\n    p.actions += 1;\\n    S.techAll += 1;\\n    if (grade !== 'sloppy') S.techGood += 1;\\n    if (grade === 'textbook') { p.textbooks += 1; S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 10 * tune.gift.charge); }\\n    else if (grade === 'clean') S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 5 * tune.gift.charge);\\n    if (grade === 'sloppy') { S.streak = 0; S.flow = 1; }\\n    else {\\n      S.streak += 1;\\n      S.flow = Math.min(2, 1 + 0.05 * S.streak);\\n70→      if (S.flow > S.bestFlow) S.bestFlow = S.flow;\\n    }\\n    if (!S.tutDone) S.tutDone = true;\\n    pushEv(S, ['grade', Math.round(p.x), Math.round(p.y), grade, Math.round(pts)]);\\n    return grade;\\n  }\\n\\n  function makePlayer(i, color) {\\n    return {\\n      id: i, x: 213, y: 150, bx: 213, by: 150, tool: 'forceps', trig: 0, prevTrig: 0,\\n80→      fine: false, held: 0, stroke: null, heat: 0, lock: 0, fill: 0, over: 0,\\n      cool: 0, score: 0, slips: 0, actions: 0, textbooks: 0, stitches: 0,\\n      suctioned: 0, burned: 0, speed: 0, wheelT: 0, wheelDir: -1, swap: 0,\\n      giftPrev: false, consultPrev: false, color: color || CFG.SEAT[i] || '#e8443a',\\n      gone: false, lx: 213, ly: 150, charT: 0, charSlip: false, bare: 0, bareT: 0,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  function blank(opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n90→    const n = opts.players || 1;\\n    const S = {\\n      id: opts.id || 'raw', seed: (opts.seed >>> 0) || 1, rng: (opts.seed >>> 0) || 1,\\n      diff: opts.difficulty || opts.diff || 'resident',\\n      clock: opts.clock != null ? opts.clock : 180,\\n      clock0: opts.clock != null ? opts.clock : 180,\\n      vitals: opts.vitals != null ? opts.vitals : 80,\\n      drain: opts.drain != null ? opts.drain : 0,\\n      phase: 0, phaseCount: 1, phaseName: opts.phaseName || 'Work',\\n      objects: [], nextId: 1, players: [],\\n100→      steady: opts.steady || 0, breath: false, worldScale: 1,\\n      gift: opts.gift || 'breath', doctor: opts.doctor || 'vale', activeDoc: opts.doctor || 'vale',\\n      consult: !!opts.consult, mode: opts.mode || 'case',\\n      codeBlueUsed: false, codeBlue: null, lost: false, won: false, closed: false, reason: '',\\n      score: 0, slips: 0, flow: 1, streak: 0, bestFlow: 1, techGood: 0, techAll: 0,\\n      t: 0, worldT: 0, phaseT: 0, ev: [], ghosts: [], ghostT: 0,\\n      ring: [], ringAcc: 0, checkpoint: null, rankCap: null, par: opts.par || 1000,\\n      site: opts.site || 'abdomen', tutorial: !!opts.tutorial, tutDone: !opts.tutorial,\\n      strain: null, flags: {}, scripts: [], tiltAmp: 0, dim: 0, dressing: null,\\n      device: null, windowOpen: 0, dev: !!opts.dev,\\n110→    };\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) S.players.push(makePlayer(i, opts.colors && opts.colors[i]));\\n    return S;\\n  }\\n\\n  function addObj(S, spec) {\\n    const o = Object.assign({\\n      id: S.nextId++, type: 'shard', x: 213, y: 116, alive: true, done: false,\\n      hidden: false, marked: false, markT: 0, under: 0, prog: 0, order: 0,\\n      drain: 0, grade: '', tag: '',\\n120→    }, spec);\\n    if (o.drain == null || spec.drain == null) o.drain = spec.drain != null ? spec.drain : (DRAIN[o.type] || 0);\\n    if (!o.origin) o.origin = [o.x, o.y];\\n    if (!o.axis) o.axis = [1, 0];\\n    const al = hypot(o.axis[0], o.axis[1]) || 1;\\n    o.axis = [o.axis[0] / al, o.axis[1] / al];\\n    if (o.depth == null) o.depth = 16;\\n    if (o.type === 'pool' && o.vol == null) o.vol = o.max || 36;\\n    if (o.type === 'pool' && o.max == null) o.max = o.vol;\\n    if ((o.type === 'wound' || o.type === 'arteryTear') && !o.pairs) {\\n130→      const n = o.stitches || (o.type === 'arteryTear' ? 3 : 4);\\n      o.pairs = [];\\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        const y = o.y - (n - 1) * 4 + i * 8;\\n        o.pairs.push([[o.x - 8, y], [o.x + 8, y]]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (o.pairs) o.stitch = 0;\\n    if ((o.type === 'laceration' || o.type === 'patch' || o.type === 'bite') && !o.cells) {\\n      const r = o.r || 12;\\n140→      o.cells = [];\\n      for (let y = -r; y <= r; y += 4) for (let x = -r; x <= r; x += 4) {\\n        if (x * x + y * y <= r * r) o.cells.push([o.x + x, o.y + y, 0]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if ((o.type === 'mass' || o.type === 'spiral' || o.type === 'slur' || o.type === 'tendril' || o.type === 'wire' || o.type === 'repeat') && !o.guide) {\\n      const len = o.len || 48;\\n      o.guide = [[o.x - len / 2, o.y], [o.x + len / 2, o.y]];\\n    }\\n    if (o.type === 'mass' && !o.ring) {\\n150→      o.ring = true;\\n      const rad = o.rad || 16;\\n      o.guide = [];\\n      for (let i = 0; i <= 12; i++) {\\n        const a = -Math.PI / 2 + TAU * i / 12;\\n        o.guide.push([o.x + Math.cos(a) * rad, o.y + Math.sin(a) * rad]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (o.type === 'retractorHandle') o.type = 'retractor';\\n    if (spec.underTag) {\\n160→      const pool = S.objects.find(q => q.tag === spec.underTag);\\n      if (pool) o.under = pool.id;\\n    }\\n    if (o.need == null) {\\n      if (o.type === 'polyp') o.need = 0.5;\\n      else if (o.type === 'bleeder' || o.type === 'rupture') o.need = 0.35;\\n      else if (o.type === 'bead') o.need = 0.12;\\n      else if (o.type === 'uvula') o.need = 1.5;\\n      else if (o.type === 'eye') o.need = 0.3;\\n      else if (o.type === 'tremass') o.need = 3;\\n170→      else o.need = 0.5;\\n    }\\n    S.objects.push(o);\\n    return o;\\n  }\\n\\n  function inDome(S, x, y) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n    if (!st || !st.domes) return false;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < st.domes.length; i++) {\\n180→      const d = st.domes[i];\\n      if (d.t > 0 && hypot(x - d.x, y - d.y) <= d.r) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function covered(S, o) {\\n    if (!o.under) return false;\\n    const p = objById(S, o.under);\\n    return !!(p && !p.done && p.vol > 1);\\n190→  }\\n\\n  function canTouch(S, o) {\\n    if (!o || o.done || !o.alive) return false;\\n    if (covered(S, o)) return false;\\n    if (o.hidden && !o.marked) return false;\\n    if (o.needsWindow && S.windowOpen <= 0) return false;\\n    if (o.needsBoard && S.device && !S.device.shown) return false;\\n    if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return !!o.window;\\n    if (o.type === 'lobe') return !!o.open;\\n200→    if (o.type === 'eye') return !!o.open;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"/* Operation sim. Plain data in, plain data out. No drawing, no audio, no DOM.\\n   Cursor and the wheel sit beside it and feed the same inputs a pad does. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const CFG = GAME.CFG;\\n  const TAU = Math.PI * 2;\\n\\n  const DRAIN = {\\n    shard: 0.1, fragment: 0.1, cork: 0.1, laceration: 0.2, bite: 0.2, wound: 0.4,\\n    bleeder: 0.5, arteryTear: 1, polyp: 0.1, mass: 0.2, hook: 0.3, gaff: 0.3,\\n    clot: 0.3, patch: 0.1, nest: 0.15, bead: 0, rupture: 0.45, screw: 0, wire: 0,\\n    pool: 0, retractor: 0, slur: 0, reed: 0, tremass: 0.4, lobe: 0.2, eye: 0.35,\\n    tendril: 0.2, uvula: 0.3, voice: 0.4, repeat: 0, spiral: 0, note: 0.2, nerve: 0,\\n    eloquent: 0, hold: 0,\\n  };\\n\\n  function rnd(S) {\\n    let x = (S.rng >>> 0) || 1;\\n    x ^= x << 13; x >>>= 0;\\n    x ^= x >>> 17; x >>>= 0;\\n    x ^= x << 5; x >>>= 0;\\n    if (!x) x = 1;\\n    S.rng = x;\\n    return x / 4294967296;\\n  }\\n  function clamp(v, a, b) { return v < a ? a : v > b ? b : v; }\\n  function hypot(x, y) { return Math.hypot(x, y); }\\n  function clone(v) { return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(v)); }\\n  function tuneOf(t) { return t || GAME.TUNE || CFG.cloneTune(CFG.TUNING); }\\n  function diffDrain(S) { return S.diff === 'intern' ? 0.7 : S.diff === 'attending' ? 1.3 : 1; }\\n  function diffClock(S) { return S.diff === 'intern' ? 1.3 : S.diff === 'attending' ? 0.8 : 1; }\\n  function syringeDose(S, tune) {\\n    const base = tune.patient.syringe;\\n    if (S.diff === 'intern') return 24 * (base / 18);\\n    if (S.diff === 'attending') return 12 * (base / 18);\\n    return base;\\n  }\\n\\n  function objById(S, id) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) if (S.objects[i].id === id) return S.objects[i];\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  function pushEv(S, ev) { S.ev.push(ev); }\\n\\n  function slip(S, p, kind, dmg, tune) {\\n    S.slips += 1;\\n    if (p) p.slips += 1;\\n    S.vitals -= dmg * tune.patient.slip;\\n    S.streak = 0;\\n    S.flow = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['slip', kind, dmg, p ? p.id : -1]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function award(S, p, grade, base, tune) {\\n    const mult = grade === 'textbook' ? 1.5 : grade === 'clean' ? 1 : 0.4;\\n    const pts = base * mult * S.flow;\\n    S.score += pts;\\n    p.score += pts;\\n    p.actions += 1;\\n    S.techAll += 1;\\n    if (grade !== 'sloppy') S.techGood += 1;\\n    if (grade === 'textbook') { p.textbooks += 1; S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 10 * tune.gift.charge); }\\n    else if (grade === 'clean') S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 5 * tune.gift.charge);\\n    if (grade === 'sloppy') { S.streak = 0; S.flow = 1; }\\n    else {\\n      S.streak += 1;\\n      S.flow = Math.min(2, 1 + 0.05 * S.streak);\\n      if (S.flow > S.bestFlow) S.bestFlow = S.flow;\\n    }\\n    if (!S.tutDone) S.tutDone = true;\\n    pushEv(S, ['grade', Math.round(p.x), Math.round(p.y), grade, Math.round(pts)]);\\n    return grade;\\n  }\\n\\n  function makePlayer(i, color) {\\n    return {\\n      id: i, x: 213, y: 150, bx: 213, by: 150, tool: 'forceps', trig: 0, prevTrig: 0,\\n      fine: false, held: 0, stroke: null, heat: 0, lock: 0, fill: 0, over: 0,\\n      cool: 0, score: 0, slips: 0, actions: 0, textbooks: 0, stitches: 0,\\n      suctioned: 0, burned: 0, speed: 0, wheelT: 0, wheelDir: -1, swap: 0,\\n      giftPrev: false, consultPrev: false, color: color || CFG.SEAT[i] || '#e8443a',\\n      gone: false, lx: 213, ly: 150, charT: 0, charSlip: false, bare: 0, bareT: 0,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  function blank(opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    const n = opts.players || 1;\\n    const S = {\\n      id: opts.id || 'raw', seed: (opts.seed >>> 0) || 1, rng: (opts.seed >>> 0) || 1,\\n      diff: opts.difficulty || opts.diff || 'resident',\\n      clock: opts.clock != null ? opts.clock : 180,\\n      clock0: opts.clock != null ? opts.clock : 180,\\n      vitals: opts.vitals != null ? opts.vitals : 80,\\n      drain: opts.drain != null ? opts.drain : 0,\\n      phase: 0, phaseCount: 1, phaseName: opts.phaseName || 'Work',\\n      objects: [], nextId: 1, players: [],\\n      steady: opts.steady || 0, breath: false, worldScale: 1,\\n      gift: opts.gift || 'breath', doctor: opts.doctor || 'vale', activeDoc: opts.doctor || 'vale',\\n      consult: !!opts.consult, mode: opts.mode || 'case',\\n      codeBlueUsed: false, codeBlue: null, lost: false, won: false, closed: false, reason: '',\\n      score: 0, slips: 0, flow: 1, streak: 0, bestFlow: 1, techGood: 0, techAll: 0,\\n      t: 0, worldT: 0, phaseT: 0, ev: [], ghosts: [], ghostT: 0,\\n      ring: [], ringAcc: 0, checkpoint: null, rankCap: null, par: opts.par || 1000,\\n      site: opts.site || 'abdomen', tutorial: !!opts.tutorial, tutDone: !opts.tutorial,\\n      strain: null, flags: {}, scripts: [], tiltAmp: 0, dim: 0, dressing: null,\\n      device: null, windowOpen: 0, dev: !!opts.dev,\\n    };\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) S.players.push(makePlayer(i, opts.colors && opts.colors[i]));\\n    return S;\\n  }\\n\\n  function addObj(S, spec) {\\n    const o = Object.assign({\\n      id: S.nextId++, type: 'shard', x: 213, y: 116, alive: true, done: false,\\n      hidden: false, marked: false, markT: 0, under: 0, prog: 0, order: 0,\\n      drain: 0, grade: '', tag: '',\\n    }, spec);\\n    if (o.drain == null || spec.drain == null) o.drain = spec.drain != null ? spec.drain : (DRAIN[o.type] || 0);\\n    if (!o.origin) o.origin = [o.x, o.y];\\n    if (!o.axis) o.axis = [1, 0];\\n    const al = hypot(o.axis[0], o.axis[1]) || 1;\\n    o.axis = [o.axis[0] / al, o.axis[1] / al];\\n    if (o.depth == null) o.depth = 16;\\n    if (o.type === 'pool' && o.vol == null) o.vol = o.max || 36;\\n    if (o.type === 'pool' && o.max == null) o.max = o.vol;\\n    if ((o.type === 'wound' || o.type === 'arteryTear') && !o.pairs) {\\n      const n = o.stitches || (o.type === 'arteryTear' ? 3 : 4);\\n      o.pairs = [];\\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        const y = o.y - (n - 1) * 4 + i * 8;\\n        o.pairs.push([[o.x - 8, y], [o.x + 8, y]]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (o.pairs) o.stitch = 0;\\n    if ((o.type === 'laceration' || o.type === 'patch' || o.type === 'bite') && !o.cells) {\\n      const r = o.r || 12;\\n      o.cells = [];\\n      for (let y = -r; y <= r; y += 4) for (let x = -r; x <= r; x += 4) {\\n        if (x * x + y * y <= r * r) o.cells.push([o.x + x, o.y + y, 0]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if ((o.type === 'mass' || o.type === 'spiral' || o.type === 'slur' || o.type === 'tendril' || o.type === 'wire' || o.type === 'repeat') && !o.guide) {\\n      const len = o.len || 48;\\n      o.guide = [[o.x - len / 2, o.y], [o.x + len / 2, o.y]];\\n    }\\n    if (o.type === 'mass' && !o.ring) {\\n      o.ring = true;\\n      const rad = o.rad || 16;\\n      o.guide = [];\\n      for (let i = 0; i <= 12; i++) {\\n        const a = -Math.PI / 2 + TAU * i / 12;\\n        o.guide.push([o.x + Math.cos(a) * rad, o.y + Math.sin(a) * rad]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (o.type === 'retractorHandle') o.type = 'retractor';\\n    if (spec.underTag) {\\n      const pool = S.objects.find(q => q.tag === spec.underTag);\\n      if (pool) o.under = pool.id;\\n    }\\n    if (o.need == null) {\\n      if (o.type === 'polyp') o.need = 0.5;\\n      else if (o.type === 'bleeder' || o.type === 'rupture') o.need = 0.35;\\n      else if (o.type === 'bead') o.need = 0.12;\\n      else if (o.type === 'uvula') o.need = 1.5;\\n      else if (o.type === 'eye') o.need = 0.3;\\n      else if (o.type === 'tremass') o.need = 3;\\n      else o.need = 0.5;\\n    }\\n    S.objects.push(o);\\n    return o;\\n  }\\n\\n  function inDome(S, x, y) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n    if (!st || !st.domes) return false;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < st.domes.length; i++) {\\n      const d = st.domes[i];\\n      if (d.t > 0 && hypot(x - d.x, y - d.y) <= d.r) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function covered(S, o) {\\n    if (!o.under) return false;\\n    const p = objById(S, o.under);\\n    return !!(p && !p.done && p.vol > 1);\\n  }\\n\\n  function canTouch(S, o) {\\n    if (!o || o.done || !o.alive) return false;\\n    if (covered(S, o)) return false;\\n    if (o.hidden && !o.marked) return false;\\n    if (o.needsWindow && S.windowOpen <= 0) return false;\\n    if (o.needsBoard && S.device && !S.device.shown) return false;\\n    if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return !!o.window;\\n    if (o.type === 'lobe') return !!o.open;\\n    if (o.type === 'eye') return !!o.open;\\n\",\"total_lines\":1762}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7ee40bd3-662e-4dd6-aaf8-003398527464-10","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"470→    if (held && p.trigRelease) {\\n      if (held.type === 'retractor') { p.held = 0; return; }\\n      if (held.type === 'screw') { p.held = 0; return; }\\n      const d0 = hypot(p.x - held.origin[0], p.y - held.origin[1]);\\n      if (held.holdZone && hypot(p.x - held.holdZone[0], p.y - held.holdZone[1]) <= (held.holdZone[2] || 14)) {\\n        held.clamped = true; held.gripped = false; p.held = 0;\\n        pushEv(S, ['clamp', held.id]);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (held.free && (d0 >= 24 || outside(p.x, p.y))) {\\n480→        const tears = held.tears || 0;\\n        const parT = held.parTime || (held.depth / 80 + 0.35);\\n        let g = 'sloppy';\\n        if (!tears && (held.pullT || 0) <= parT) g = 'textbook';\\n        else if (tears <= 1) g = 'clean';\\n        held.done = true; held.alive = false; held.grade = g; p.held = 0;\\n        if (held.type === 'note') p.score += 0;\\n        award(S, p, g, 120, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['dish', held.id, g]);\\n      } else {\\n490→        held.gripped = false;\\n        p.held = 0;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function outside(x, y) {\\n    const nx = (x - CFG.CX) / CFG.RX, ny = (y - CFG.CY) / CFG.RY;\\n    return nx * nx + ny * ny > 1;\\n  }\\n500→\\n  function stepScalpel(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    const tol = tune.hands.grade;\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel') {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (!o || o.done) { p.stroke = null; }\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigEdge && !p.stroke) {\\n      /* Press within 8 u of the guide start, not the object's center. A long cut's start sits far from x,y. */\\n510→      const reach = 8 + (p.mouse ? 1 : 0);\\n      let o = null, bd = reach;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n        const q = S.objects[i];\\n        if (!canTouch(S, q) || !q.guide) continue;\\n        if (!(q.type === 'mass' || q.type === 'slur' || q.type === 'tendril' || q.type === 'spiral' || q.type === 'wire' || q.type === 'repeat' || q.type === 'lobe' || q.type === 'cut' || q.type === 'nest')) continue;\\n        const start = q.guide[0];\\n        const d = hypot(p.x - start[0], p.y - start[1]);\\n        if (d <= bd) { bd = d; o = q; }\\n      }\\n520→      if (o) {\\n        p.stroke = { kind: 'scalpel', id: o.id, far: 0, sum: 0, n: 0, off: 0, slipped: false };\\n        o.cutting = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (!(p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel') && down && p.inst > 40) {\\n      const onGuide = S.objects.some(o => o.guide && !o.done && polyDist(o.guide, p.x, p.y).d < 8);\\n      if (!onGuide && !outside(p.x, p.y)) {\\n        p.bare = (p.bare || 0) + hypot(p.x - (p.ox || p.x), p.y - (p.oy || p.y));\\n        if (p.bare >= 6) { slip(S, p, 'healthy', 3, tune); p.bare = 0; }\\n530→      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel' && down) {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (o && nerveHit(S, p, tune)) { /* counted */ }\\n      if (o && o.guide) {\\n        const hit = polyDist(o.guide, p.x, p.y);\\n        const st = p.stroke;\\n        if (hit.along > st.far) st.far = hit.along;\\n        /* A closed ring's last point is the start, so the vertex reads as along 0. Arriving back after most of the loop finishes it. */\\n540→        const g0 = o.guide[0], gN = o.guide[o.guide.length - 1];\\n        if (o.guide.length > 2 && hypot(g0[0] - gN[0], g0[1] - gN[1]) < 1.5 && st.far > hit.total * 0.72 && hypot(p.x - g0[0], p.y - g0[1]) <= 3) st.far = hit.total;\\n        st.sum += hit.d; st.n += 1;\\n        if (hit.d > 9) st.off += dt; else st.off = 0;\\n        if (st.off >= 0.12 && !st.slipped) {\\n          st.slipped = true; slip(S, p, 'slip', 3, tune);\\n          pushEv(S, ['slipcut', o.id]);\\n        }\\n        o.prog = st.far / (hit.total || 1);\\n        if (o.type === 'spiral' && o.beatLock && S.flags.onBeat) {\\n550→          if (!st.beatSlip) { st.beatSlip = true; slip(S, p, 'beat', 3, tune); }\\n          o.prog = Math.min(o.prog, st.safe || 0);\\n        } else if (o.type === 'spiral') st.safe = o.prog;\\n        if (st.far >= (hit.total || 1) - 0.5) {\\n          const mean = st.n ? st.sum / st.n : 99;\\n          const g = st.slipped ? 'sloppy' : gradeMean(mean, 1.8 * tol, 4 * tol);\\n          o.done = true; o.alive = false; o.grade = g; o.cut = true;\\n          if (o.type === 'mass') { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.cut = true; o.type = 'mass'; }\\n          if (o.type === 'nest' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.slash)) {\\n            o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.cut = true;\\n560→            if (o.type === 'lobe') o.mode = 'forceps';\\n          }\\n          if (o.type === 'wire') { /* caller checks order */ wireCut(S, p, o, tune); }\\n          else award(S, p, g, 110, tune);\\n          p.stroke = null;\\n          pushEv(S, ['cut', o.id, g]);\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigRelease && p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel') {\\n570→      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (o && o.prog < 0.98) {\\n        /* resume later if they come back within 6 */\\n        p.stroke.paused = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigEdge && p.stroke && p.stroke.paused) {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (o && o.guide) {\\n        const hit = polyDist(o.guide, p.x, p.y);\\n580→        if (Math.abs(hit.along - p.stroke.far) <= 6 || hit.d <= 6) p.stroke.paused = false;\\n        else p.stroke = null;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* slash variant: a fast stroke across a slash target */\\n    if (down && p.inst >= 60) {\\n      const o = nearest(S, p, 10, q => canTouch(S, q) && q.slash && !q.done && !q.cut);\\n      if (o) {\\n        o.cut = true;\\n        if (o.type === 'nest' || o.type === 'lobe') {\\n590→          if (o.type === 'lobe') o.mode = 'forceps';\\n          award(S, p, 'clean', 100, tune);\\n        } else {\\n          o.done = true; o.alive = false;\\n          award(S, p, 'clean', 100, tune);\\n        }\\n        pushEv(S, ['slash', o.id]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n600→\\n  function wireCut(S, p, o, tune) {\\n    const dev = S.device;\\n    if (!dev) { o.done = true; award(S, p, 'clean', 80, tune); return; }\\n    const want = dev.order[dev.next];\\n    if (o.tag === want) {\\n      dev.next += 1; o.done = true; o.alive = false;\\n      award(S, p, 'textbook', 100, tune);\\n      if (dev.next >= dev.order.length) dev.done = true;\\n    } else {\\n610→      o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.cutting = false;\\n      S.vitals -= 30; S.clock = Math.max(0, S.clock - 30);\\n      slip(S, p, 'wire', 0, tune);\\n      pushEv(S, ['badwire', o.tag]);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSuture(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    const extra = (S.activeDoc === 'sokolova' ? 1 : 0);\\n620→    if (p.trigEdge) {\\n      /* Press within 9 u of the next near point. Stitches sit off the wound center. */\\n      const reach = 9 + extra + (p.mouse ? 1 : 0);\\n      let o = null, bd = reach;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n        const q = S.objects[i];\\n        if (!canTouch(S, q) || !q.pairs || (q.stitch || 0) >= q.pairs.length) continue;\\n        const a = q.pairs[q.stitch][0];\\n        const d = hypot(p.x - a[0], p.y - a[1]);\\n        if (d <= bd) { bd = d; o = q; }\\n630→      }\\n      if (o) {\\n        p.stroke = { kind: 'suture', id: o.id, i: o.stitch, t: 0 };\\n        pushEv(S, ['needle', o.id, o.stitch]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'suture' && down) p.stroke.t += dt;\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'suture' && p.trigRelease) {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      const st = p.stroke;\\n640→      p.stroke = null;\\n      if (!o || o.done) return;\\n      const b = o.pairs[st.i][1];\\n      const tol = 6 + extra + (p.mouse ? 1 : 0);\\n      if (hypot(p.x - b[0], p.y - b[1]) <= tol) {\\n        const g = gradeMean(st.t, 0.6, 1.2);\\n        o.grades = o.grades || [];\\n        o.grades.push(g === 'textbook' ? 2 : g === 'clean' ? 1 : 0);\\n        o.times = o.times || [];\\n        o.times.push(st.t);\\n650→        o.stitch = st.i + 1;\\n        o.prog = o.stitch / o.pairs.length;\\n        p.stitches += 1;\\n        const bleedLeft = 1 - o.prog;\\n        if (o.type === 'arteryTear') o.drain = 1 * bleedLeft;\\n        else if (o.type === 'wound') o.drain = 0.4 * bleedLeft;\\n        pushEv(S, ['stitch', Math.round(b[0]), Math.round(b[1]), g]);\\n        if (o.stitch >= o.pairs.length) {\\n          const meanT = o.times.reduce((a, c) => a + c, 0) / o.times.length;\\n          const fg = gradeMean(meanT, 0.6, 1.2);\\n660→          o.done = true; o.alive = false; o.grade = fg; o.drain = 0;\\n          award(S, p, fg, 80 + 20 * o.pairs.length, tune);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        slip(S, p, 'loose', 1, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['loose', o.id]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n670→  function stepSalve(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.trig <= 0.3) return;\\n    let any = false;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!canTouch(S, o) || !o.cells) continue;\\n      if (!(o.type === 'laceration' || o.type === 'patch' || o.type === 'bite' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'salve'))) continue;\\n      for (let c = 0; c < o.cells.length; c++) {\\n        const cell = o.cells[c];\\n        if (!cell[2] && hypot(cell[0] - p.x, cell[1] - p.y) <= 10) { cell[2] = 1; any = true; }\\n680→      }\\n      let on = 0;\\n      for (let c = 0; c < o.cells.length; c++) if (o.cells[c][2]) on++;\\n      o.prog = o.cells.length ? on / o.cells.length : 1;\\n      if (o.prog >= 0.9 && !o.done) {\\n        o.done = true; o.alive = false; o.drain = 0;\\n        S.vitals = Math.min(99, S.vitals + 2 * tune.patient.healing);\\n        award(S, p, 'clean', 80, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['heal', o.id]);\\n      }\\n690→    }\\n    if (!any && p.trigEdge) { /* salve cannot harm */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSyringe(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.cool > 0) p.cool -= dt;\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    if (down && p.cool <= 0) {\\n      if (p.fill < 1) p.fill = Math.min(1, p.fill + dt / 0.55);\\n      else p.over += dt;\\n700→    }\\n    if (p.trigRelease && p.fill > 0.05 && p.cool <= 0) {\\n      const bubble = p.over >= 0.3;\\n      const tgt = nearest(S, p, 10, o => canTouch(S, o) && (o.type === 'clot' || o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'syringe')));\\n      if (tgt) {\\n        if ((tgt.type === 'reed' || tgt.type === 'voice') && !tgt.window) {\\n          addObj(S, { type: 'laceration', x: tgt.x + 6, y: tgt.y, r: 8, order: 50, drain: 0.2 });\\n          slip(S, p, 'spit', 2, tune);\\n        } else {\\n          const g = bubble ? 'sloppy' : (p.fill >= 0.9 ? 'textbook' : 'clean');\\n710→          tgt.dosed = true;\\n          tgt.dose = (bubble ? 0.5 : 1) * p.fill;\\n          if (tgt.follow === 'salve') {\\n            tgt.mode = 'salve';\\n            if (!tgt.cells) {\\n              const r = tgt.r || 8;\\n              tgt.cells = [];\\n              for (let y = -r; y <= r; y += 4) for (let x = -r; x <= r; x += 4) {\\n                if (x * x + y * y <= r * r) tgt.cells.push([tgt.x + x, tgt.y + y, 0]);\\n              }\\n720→            }\\n          } else if (tgt.type === 'clot') { tgt.drain = 0.1; }\\n          else { tgt.done = true; tgt.alive = false; tgt.drain = 0; }\\n          award(S, p, g, 90, tune);\\n          pushEv(S, ['inject', tgt.id, g]);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        const g = bubble ? 'sloppy' : (p.fill >= 0.9 ? 'textbook' : 'clean');\\n        const add = syringeDose(S, tune) * p.fill * (bubble ? 0.5 : 1);\\n        S.vitals = Math.min(99, S.vitals + add);\\n730→        award(S, p, g, 40, tune);\\n        S.flags.iv = (S.flags.iv || 0) + 1;\\n        pushEv(S, ['iv', Math.round(add), g]);\\n      }\\n      p.fill = 0; p.over = 0; p.cool = 0.35;\\n    }\\n    if (!down && p.trigRelease === false) { /* keep fill while aiming */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepCautery(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n740→    if (p.lock > 0) { p.lock -= dt; p.heat = Math.max(0, p.heat - 0.6 * dt); return; }\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    if (!down) {\\n      p.heat = Math.max(0, p.heat - 0.6 * dt);\\n      p.bareT = 0;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    p.heat += tune.fluids.cauteryHeat * dt;\\n    if (p.heat >= 1) { p.lock = 1.2; p.heat = 1; slip(S, p, 'lock', 1, tune); pushEv(S, ['lock', p.id]); return; }\\n    if (nerveHit(S, p, tune)) return;\\n750→    const tgt = nearest(S, p, 6, o => canTouch(S, o) && (o.type === 'polyp' || o.type === 'bleeder' || o.type === 'rupture' || o.type === 'bead' || o.type === 'uvula' || o.type === 'eye' || o.type === 'tremass' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'cautery') || o.type === 'barb'));\\n    if (tgt) {\\n      p.bareT = 0;\\n      tgt.burn = (tgt.burn || 0) + dt;\\n      tgt.prog = tgt.burn / (tgt.need || 0.5);\\n      if (tgt.burn >= (tgt.need || 0.5) / Math.max(0.25, tune.strains.health) && !tgt.done) {\\n        const dirty = tgt.charred || p.lockedDuring;\\n        const g = (!tgt.charred && p.lock <= 0 && !p.hadLock) ? 'textbook' : 'clean';\\n        tgt.done = true; tgt.alive = false; tgt.drain = 0; tgt.grade = g;\\n        p.burned += 1;\\n760→        award(S, p, g, 90, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['burn', tgt.id, g]);\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      p.bareT = (p.bareT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (p.bareT >= 0.25) {\\n        /* char on the field */\\n        p.charT = (p.charT || 0) + dt;\\n        S.vitals -= 0.8 * dt * tune.patient.slip;\\n        if (p.bareT >= 0.6 && !p.charSlip) { p.charSlip = true; slip(S, p, 'char', 2, tune); pushEv(S, ['char', Math.round(p.x), Math.round(p.y)]); }\\n770→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSuction(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.trig <= 0.3) return;\\n    const pool = nearest(S, p, 14, o => o.type === 'pool' && !o.done && o.vol > 0);\\n    if (!pool) return;\\n    const rate = tune.fluids.suction;\\n    const before = pool.vol;\\n780→    pool.vol = Math.max(0, pool.vol - rate * dt);\\n    p.suctioned += before - pool.vol;\\n    pool.prog = 1 - pool.vol / (pool.max || 1);\\n    if (pool.vol <= 0.2) { pool.done = true; pool.alive = false; pool.vol = 0; pushEv(S, ['dry', pool.id]); }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSonar(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.trig <= 0.3) return;\\n    let rad = 38;\\n    if (S.activeDoc === 'vale' || S.gift === 'breath') rad *= 1.25;\\n790→    if (S.gift === 'both' && S.activeDoc === 'vale') rad *= 1.25;\\n    p.sonarR = rad;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!o.hidden || o.done) continue;\\n      if (hypot(o.x - p.x, o.y - p.y) <= rad) { o.marked = true; o.markT = 4; pushEv(S, ['mark', o.id]); }\\n    }\\n    if (S.device && !S.device.shown && hypot(p.x - (S.device.x || 213), p.y - (S.device.y || 116)) <= rad) {\\n      S.device.shown = true;\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.needsBoard) { o.hidden = false; o.marked = true; o.markT = 6; }\\n800→      pushEv(S, ['board', 1]);\\n    }\\n    if (S.strain && S.strain.kind === 'legato') {\\n      for (const w of S.strain.worms || []) if (hypot(w.x - p.x, w.y - p.y) <= rad) w.marked = true;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function applyTools(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.gone) return;\\n    if (inDome(S, p.x, p.y)) return;\\n810→    if (p.swap > 0) p.swap -= dt;\\n    p.ox = p.x; p.oy = p.y;\\n    const tool = p.tool;\\n    if (tool === 'forceps') stepForceps(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'scalpel') stepScalpel(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'suture') stepSuture(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'salve') stepSalve(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'syringe') stepSyringe(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'cautery') stepCautery(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'suction') stepSuction(S, p, dt, tune);\\n820→    else if (tool === 'sonar') stepSonar(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    /* marks expire */\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---------- strains ---------- */\\n\\n  function stepStrain(S, worldDt, handDt, tune) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n    if (!st || st.done) return;\\n    const sp = tune.strains.speed;\\n830→    if (st.kind === 'staccato') stepStaccato(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'legato') stepLegato(S, st, worldDt, handDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'tremolo') stepTremolo(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'dacapo') stepDacapo(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'fermata') stepFermata(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'cantor') stepCantor(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepStaccato(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n840→    const beat = tune.strains.beat;\\n    for (const b of st.beads) {\\n      if (b.dead) continue;\\n      b.landIn -= dt * sp;\\n      if (!b.hopped && b.landIn < 0.5) b.hopped = true;\\n      if (b.landIn <= 0 && !b.landed) {\\n        b.landed = true; b.x = b.tx; b.y = b.ty;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'laceration', x: b.x, y: b.y, r: 8, order: 40, drain: 0.2, tag: 'bite' });\\n        pushEv(S, ['bite', Math.round(b.x), Math.round(b.y)]);\\n      }\\n850→      if (!b.landed) {\\n        const u = clamp(1 - b.landIn / b.flight, 0, 1);\\n        b.x = b.x0 + (b.tx - b.x0) * u;\\n        b.y = b.y0 + (b.ty - b.y0) * u;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* cautery kills beads: mirrored onto objects of type bead */\\n    let nests = 0;\\n    for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'nest' && !o.done && o.tag === st.tag) nests++;\\n    if (!nests && !st.collapse) { st.collapse = 3; }\\n860→    if (st.collapse > 0) {\\n      st.collapse -= dt;\\n      if (st.collapse <= 0) {\\n        for (const b of st.beads) b.dead = true;\\n        for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'bead' && o.tag === st.tag) { o.done = true; o.alive = false; }\\n        st.done = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    syncBeads(S, st);\\n    if (st.beads.length && st.beads.every(b => b.dead) && nests === 0) st.done = true;\\n870→  }\\n\\n  function syncBeads(S, st) {\\n    for (const b of st.beads) {\\n      if (b.dead) continue;\\n      let o = b.oid ? objById(S, b.oid) : null;\\n      if (!o) {\\n        o = addObj(S, { type: 'bead', x: b.x, y: b.y, need: 0.12, order: 5, tag: st.tag, drain: 0 });\\n        b.oid = o.id;\\n      } else {\\n880→        o.x = b.x; o.y = b.y;\\n        if (o.done) b.dead = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepLegato(S, st, dt, handDt, tune, sp) {\\n    for (const w of st.worms) {\\n      if (w.done) continue;\\n      w.t += dt * sp;\\n890→      /* head crawls along its path until surfaced */\\n      if (!w.surfaced && !w.out) {\\n        w.along = Math.min(w.pathLen, w.along + 18 * dt * sp);\\n        const p = pointAlong(w.path, w.along);\\n        w.x = p[0]; w.y = p[1];\\n        /* open a slur guide when the head nears it */\\n        for (const g of w.slurs) {\\n          if (g.opened || g.done) continue;\\n          if (hypot(w.x - g.x, w.y - g.y) < 28) {\\n            g.opened = true;\\n900→            const o = addObj(S, { type: 'slur', x: g.x, y: g.y, len: 18, order: 1, tag: 'slur-' + w.id + '-' + g.i, drain: 0, guide: [[g.x - 9, g.y], [g.x + 9, g.y]] });\\n            g.oid = o.id;\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n      for (const g of w.slurs) {\\n        if (!g.oid || g.done) continue;\\n        const o = objById(S, g.oid);\\n        if (o && o.done) g.done = true;\\n      }\\n910→      const slursLeft = w.slurs.filter(g => !g.done).length;\\n      if (!slursLeft && !w.surfaced) {\\n        w.surfaced = true; w.marked = true;\\n        const head = addObj(S, {\\n          type: 'shard', x: w.x, y: w.y, axis: w.axis || [1, 0], depth: 18, order: 2,\\n          tag: 'legato-head', worm: w.id, tension: 70, drain: 0.15, hidden: false,\\n          holdZone: w.hold || null, barbs: w.barbAt || 0,\\n        });\\n        w.head = head.id;\\n      }\",\"content_concise\":\"470→    if (held && p.trigRelease) {\\n      if (held.type === 'retractor') { p.held = 0; return; }\\n      if (held.type === 'screw') { p.held = 0; return; }\\n      const d0 = hypot(p.x - held.origin[0], p.y - held.origin[1]);\\n      if (held.holdZone && hypot(p.x - held.holdZone[0], p.y - held.holdZone[1]) <= (held.holdZone[2] || 14)) {\\n        held.clamped = true; held.gripped = false; p.held = 0;\\n        pushEv(S, ['clamp', held.id]);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (held.free && (d0 >= 24 || outside(p.x, p.y))) {\\n480→        const tears = held.tears || 0;\\n        const parT = held.parTime || (held.depth / 80 + 0.35);\\n        let g = 'sloppy';\\n        if (!tears && (held.pullT || 0) <= parT) g = 'textbook';\\n        else if (tears <= 1) g = 'clean';\\n        held.done = true; held.alive = false; held.grade = g; p.held = 0;\\n        if (held.type === 'note') p.score += 0;\\n        award(S, p, g, 120, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['dish', held.id, g]);\\n      } else {\\n490→        held.gripped = false;\\n        p.held = 0;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function outside(x, y) {\\n    const nx = (x - CFG.CX) / CFG.RX, ny = (y - CFG.CY) / CFG.RY;\\n    return nx * nx + ny * ny > 1;\\n  }\\n500→\\n  function stepScalpel(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    const tol = tune.hands.grade;\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel') {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (!o || o.done) { p.stroke = null; }\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigEdge && !p.stroke) {\\n      /* Press within 8 u of the guide start, not the object's center. A long cut's start sits far from x,y. */\\n510→      const reach = 8 + (p.mouse ? 1 : 0);\\n      let o = null, bd = reach;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n        const q = S.objects[i];\\n        if (!canTouch(S, q) || !q.guide) continue;\\n        if (!(q.type === 'mass' || q.type === 'slur' || q.type === 'tendril' || q.type === 'spiral' || q.type === 'wire' || q.type === 'repeat' || q.type === 'lobe' || q.type === 'cut' || q.type === 'nest')) continue;\\n        const start = q.guide[0];\\n        const d = hypot(p.x - start[0], p.y - start[1]);\\n        if (d <= bd) { bd = d; o = q; }\\n      }\\n520→      if (o) {\\n        p.stroke = { kind: 'scalpel', id: o.id, far: 0, sum: 0, n: 0, off: 0, slipped: false };\\n        o.cutting = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (!(p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel') && down && p.inst > 40) {\\n      const onGuide = S.objects.some(o => o.guide && !o.done && polyDist(o.guide, p.x, p.y).d < 8);\\n      if (!onGuide && !outside(p.x, p.y)) {\\n        p.bare = (p.bare || 0) + hypot(p.x - (p.ox || p.x), p.y - (p.oy || p.y));\\n        if (p.bare >= 6) { slip(S, p, 'healthy', 3, tune); p.bare = 0; }\\n530→      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel' && down) {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (o && nerveHit(S, p, tune)) { /* counted */ }\\n      if (o && o.guide) {\\n        const hit = polyDist(o.guide, p.x, p.y);\\n        const st = p.stroke;\\n        if (hit.along > st.far) st.far = hit.along;\\n        /* A closed ring's last point is the start, so the vertex reads as along 0. Arriving back after most of the loop finishes it. */\\n540→        const g0 = o.guide[0], gN = o.guide[o.guide.length - 1];\\n        if (o.guide.length > 2 && hypot(g0[0] - gN[0], g0[1] - gN[1]) < 1.5 && st.far > hit.total * 0.72 && hypot(p.x - g0[0], p.y - g0[1]) <= 3) st.far = hit.total;\\n        st.sum += hit.d; st.n += 1;\\n        if (hit.d > 9) st.off += dt; else st.off = 0;\\n        if (st.off >= 0.12 && !st.slipped) {\\n          st.slipped = true; slip(S, p, 'slip', 3, tune);\\n          pushEv(S, ['slipcut', o.id]);\\n        }\\n        o.prog = st.far / (hit.total || 1);\\n        if (o.type === 'spiral' && o.beatLock && S.flags.onBeat) {\\n550→          if (!st.beatSlip) { st.beatSlip = true; slip(S, p, 'beat', 3, tune); }\\n          o.prog = Math.min(o.prog, st.safe || 0);\\n        } else if (o.type === 'spiral') st.safe = o.prog;\\n        if (st.far >= (hit.total || 1) - 0.5) {\\n          const mean = st.n ? st.sum / st.n : 99;\\n          const g = st.slipped ? 'sloppy' : gradeMean(mean, 1.8 * tol, 4 * tol);\\n          o.done = true; o.alive = false; o.grade = g; o.cut = true;\\n          if (o.type === 'mass') { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.cut = true; o.type = 'mass'; }\\n          if (o.type === 'nest' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.slash)) {\\n            o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.cut = true;\\n560→            if (o.type === 'lobe') o.mode = 'forceps';\\n          }\\n          if (o.type === 'wire') { /* caller checks order */ wireCut(S, p, o, tune); }\\n          else award(S, p, g, 110, tune);\\n          p.stroke = null;\\n          pushEv(S, ['cut', o.id, g]);\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigRelease && p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel') {\\n570→      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (o && o.prog < 0.98) {\\n        /* resume later if they come back within 6 */\\n        p.stroke.paused = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigEdge && p.stroke && p.stroke.paused) {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (o && o.guide) {\\n        const hit = polyDist(o.guide, p.x, p.y);\\n580→        if (Math.abs(hit.along - p.stroke.far) <= 6 || hit.d <= 6) p.stroke.paused = false;\\n        else p.stroke = null;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* slash variant: a fast stroke across a slash target */\\n    if (down && p.inst >= 60) {\\n      const o = nearest(S, p, 10, q => canTouch(S, q) && q.slash && !q.done && !q.cut);\\n      if (o) {\\n        o.cut = true;\\n        if (o.type === 'nest' || o.type === 'lobe') {\\n590→          if (o.type === 'lobe') o.mode = 'forceps';\\n          award(S, p, 'clean', 100, tune);\\n        } else {\\n          o.done = true; o.alive = false;\\n          award(S, p, 'clean', 100, tune);\\n        }\\n        pushEv(S, ['slash', o.id]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n600→\\n  function wireCut(S, p, o, tune) {\\n    const dev = S.device;\\n    if (!dev) { o.done = true; award(S, p, 'clean', 80, tune); return; }\\n    const want = dev.order[dev.next];\\n    if (o.tag === want) {\\n      dev.next += 1; o.done = true; o.alive = false;\\n      award(S, p, 'textbook', 100, tune);\\n      if (dev.next >= dev.order.length) dev.done = true;\\n    } else {\\n610→      o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.cutting = false;\\n      S.vitals -= 30; S.clock = Math.max(0, S.clock - 30);\\n      slip(S, p, 'wire', 0, tune);\\n      pushEv(S, ['badwire', o.tag]);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSuture(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    const extra = (S.activeDoc === 'sokolova' ? 1 : 0);\\n620→    if (p.trigEdge) {\\n      /* Press within 9 u of the next near point. Stitches sit off the wound center. */\\n      const reach = 9 + extra + (p.mouse ? 1 : 0);\\n      let o = null, bd = reach;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n        const q = S.objects[i];\\n        if (!canTouch(S, q) || !q.pairs || (q.stitch || 0) >= q.pairs.length) continue;\\n        const a = q.pairs[q.stitch][0];\\n        const d = hypot(p.x - a[0], p.y - a[1]);\\n        if (d <= bd) { bd = d; o = q; }\\n630→      }\\n      if (o) {\\n        p.stroke = { kind: 'suture', id: o.id, i: o.stitch, t: 0 };\\n        pushEv(S, ['needle', o.id, o.stitch]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'suture' && down) p.stroke.t += dt;\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'suture' && p.trigRelease) {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      const st = p.stroke;\\n640→      p.stroke = null;\\n      if (!o || o.done) return;\\n      const b = o.pairs[st.i][1];\\n      const tol = 6 + extra + (p.mouse ? 1 : 0);\\n      if (hypot(p.x - b[0], p.y - b[1]) <= tol) {\\n        const g = gradeMean(st.t, 0.6, 1.2);\\n        o.grades = o.grades || [];\\n        o.grades.push(g === 'textbook' ? 2 : g === 'clean' ? 1 : 0);\\n        o.times = o.times || [];\\n        o.times.push(st.t);\\n650→        o.stitch = st.i + 1;\\n        o.prog = o.stitch / o.pairs.length;\\n        p.stitches += 1;\\n        const bleedLeft = 1 - o.prog;\\n        if (o.type === 'arteryTear') o.drain = 1 * bleedLeft;\\n        else if (o.type === 'wound') o.drain = 0.4 * bleedLeft;\\n        pushEv(S, ['stitch', Math.round(b[0]), Math.round(b[1]), g]);\\n        if (o.stitch >= o.pairs.length) {\\n          const meanT = o.times.reduce((a, c) => a + c, 0) / o.times.length;\\n          const fg = gradeMean(meanT, 0.6, 1.2);\\n660→          o.done = true; o.alive = false; o.grade = fg; o.drain = 0;\\n          award(S, p, fg, 80 + 20 * o.pairs.length, tune);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        slip(S, p, 'loose', 1, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['loose', o.id]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n670→  function stepSalve(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.trig <= 0.3) return;\\n    let any = false;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!canTouch(S, o) || !o.cells) continue;\\n      if (!(o.type === 'laceration' || o.type === 'patch' || o.type === 'bite' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'salve'))) continue;\\n      for (let c = 0; c < o.cells.length; c++) {\\n        const cell = o.cells[c];\\n        if (!cell[2] && hypot(cell[0] - p.x, cell[1] - p.y) <= 10) { cell[2] = 1; any = true; }\\n680→      }\\n      let on = 0;\\n      for (let c = 0; c < o.cells.length; c++) if (o.cells[c][2]) on++;\\n      o.prog = o.cells.length ? on / o.cells.length : 1;\\n      if (o.prog >= 0.9 && !o.done) {\\n        o.done = true; o.alive = false; o.drain = 0;\\n        S.vitals = Math.min(99, S.vitals + 2 * tune.patient.healing);\\n        award(S, p, 'clean', 80, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['heal', o.id]);\\n      }\\n690→    }\\n    if (!any && p.trigEdge) { /* salve cannot harm */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSyringe(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.cool > 0) p.cool -= dt;\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    if (down && p.cool <= 0) {\\n      if (p.fill < 1) p.fill = Math.min(1, p.fill + dt / 0.55);\\n      else p.over += dt;\\n700→    }\\n    if (p.trigRelease && p.fill > 0.05 && p.cool <= 0) {\\n      const bubble = p.over >= 0.3;\\n      const tgt = nearest(S, p, 10, o => canTouch(S, o) && (o.type === 'clot' || o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'syringe')));\\n      if (tgt) {\\n        if ((tgt.type === 'reed' || tgt.type === 'voice') && !tgt.window) {\\n          addObj(S, { type: 'laceration', x: tgt.x + 6, y: tgt.y, r: 8, order: 50, drain: 0.2 });\\n          slip(S, p, 'spit', 2, tune);\\n        } else {\\n          const g = bubble ? 'sloppy' : (p.fill >= 0.9 ? 'textbook' : 'clean');\\n710→          tgt.dosed = true;\\n          tgt.dose = (bubble ? 0.5 : 1) * p.fill;\\n          if (tgt.follow === 'salve') {\\n            tgt.mode = 'salve';\\n            if (!tgt.cells) {\\n              const r = tgt.r || 8;\\n              tgt.cells = [];\\n              for (let y = -r; y <= r; y += 4) for (let x = -r; x <= r; x += 4) {\\n                if (x * x + y * y <= r * r) tgt.cells.push([tgt.x + x, tgt.y + y, 0]);\\n              }\\n720→            }\\n          } else if (tgt.type === 'clot') { tgt.drain = 0.1; }\\n          else { tgt.done = true; tgt.alive = false; tgt.drain = 0; }\\n          award(S, p, g, 90, tune);\\n          pushEv(S, ['inject', tgt.id, g]);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        const g = bubble ? 'sloppy' : (p.fill >= 0.9 ? 'textbook' : 'clean');\\n        const add = syringeDose(S, tune) * p.fill * (bubble ? 0.5 : 1);\\n        S.vitals = Math.min(99, S.vitals + add);\\n730→        award(S, p, g, 40, tune);\\n        S.flags.iv = (S.flags.iv || 0) + 1;\\n        pushEv(S, ['iv', Math.round(add), g]);\\n      }\\n      p.fill = 0; p.over = 0; p.cool = 0.35;\\n    }\\n    if (!down && p.trigRelease === false) { /* keep fill while aiming */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepCautery(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n740→    if (p.lock > 0) { p.lock -= dt; p.heat = Math.max(0, p.heat - 0.6 * dt); return; }\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    if (!down) {\\n      p.heat = Math.max(0, p.heat - 0.6 * dt);\\n      p.bareT = 0;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    p.heat += tune.fluids.cauteryHeat * dt;\\n    if (p.heat >= 1) { p.lock = 1.2; p.heat = 1; slip(S, p, 'lock', 1, tune); pushEv(S, ['lock', p.id]); return; }\\n    if (nerveHit(S, p, tune)) return;\\n750→    const tgt = nearest(S, p, 6, o => canTouch(S, o) && (o.type === 'polyp' || o.type === 'bleeder' || o.type === 'rupture' || o.type === 'bead' || o.type === 'uvula' || o.type === 'eye' || o.type === 'tremass' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'cautery') || o.type === 'barb'));\\n    if (tgt) {\\n      p.bareT = 0;\\n      tgt.burn = (tgt.burn || 0) + dt;\\n      tgt.prog = tgt.burn / (tgt.need || 0.5);\\n      if (tgt.burn >= (tgt.need || 0.5) / Math.max(0.25, tune.strains.health) && !tgt.done) {\\n        const dirty = tgt.charred || p.lockedDuring;\\n        const g = (!tgt.charred && p.lock <= 0 && !p.hadLock) ? 'textbook' : 'clean';\\n        tgt.done = true; tgt.alive = false; tgt.drain = 0; tgt.grade = g;\\n        p.burned += 1;\\n760→        award(S, p, g, 90, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['burn', tgt.id, g]);\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      p.bareT = (p.bareT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (p.bareT >= 0.25) {\\n        /* char on the field */\\n        p.charT = (p.charT || 0) + dt;\\n        S.vitals -= 0.8 * dt * tune.patient.slip;\\n        if (p.bareT >= 0.6 && !p.charSlip) { p.charSlip = true; slip(S, p, 'char', 2, tune); pushEv(S, ['char', Math.round(p.x), Math.round(p.y)]); }\\n770→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSuction(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.trig <= 0.3) return;\\n    const pool = nearest(S, p, 14, o => o.type === 'pool' && !o.done && o.vol > 0);\\n    if (!pool) return;\\n    const rate = tune.fluids.suction;\\n    const before = pool.vol;\\n780→    pool.vol = Math.max(0, pool.vol - rate * dt);\\n    p.suctioned += before - pool.vol;\\n    pool.prog = 1 - pool.vol / (pool.max || 1);\\n    if (pool.vol <= 0.2) { pool.done = true; pool.alive = false; pool.vol = 0; pushEv(S, ['dry', pool.id]); }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSonar(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.trig <= 0.3) return;\\n    let rad = 38;\\n    if (S.activeDoc === 'vale' || S.gift === 'breath') rad *= 1.25;\\n790→    if (S.gift === 'both' && S.activeDoc === 'vale') rad *= 1.25;\\n    p.sonarR = rad;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!o.hidden || o.done) continue;\\n      if (hypot(o.x - p.x, o.y - p.y) <= rad) { o.marked = true; o.markT = 4; pushEv(S, ['mark', o.id]); }\\n    }\\n    if (S.device && !S.device.shown && hypot(p.x - (S.device.x || 213), p.y - (S.device.y || 116)) <= rad) {\\n      S.device.shown = true;\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.needsBoard) { o.hidden = false; o.marked = true; o.markT = 6; }\\n800→      pushEv(S, ['board', 1]);\\n    }\\n    if (S.strain && S.strain.kind === 'legato') {\\n      for (const w of S.strain.worms || []) if (hypot(w.x - p.x, w.y - p.y) <= rad) w.marked = true;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function applyTools(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.gone) return;\\n    if (inDome(S, p.x, p.y)) return;\\n810→    if (p.swap > 0) p.swap -= dt;\\n    p.ox = p.x; p.oy = p.y;\\n    const tool = p.tool;\\n    if (tool === 'forceps') stepForceps(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'scalpel') stepScalpel(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'suture') stepSuture(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'salve') stepSalve(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'syringe') stepSyringe(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'cautery') stepCautery(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'suction') stepSuction(S, p, dt, tune);\\n820→    else if (tool === 'sonar') stepSonar(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    /* marks expire */\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---------- strains ---------- */\\n\\n  function stepStrain(S, worldDt, handDt, tune) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n    if (!st || st.done) return;\\n    const sp = tune.strains.speed;\\n830→    if (st.kind === 'staccato') stepStaccato(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'legato') stepLegato(S, st, worldDt, handDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'tremolo') stepTremolo(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'dacapo') stepDacapo(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'fermata') stepFermata(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'cantor') stepCantor(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepStaccato(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n840→    const beat = tune.strains.beat;\\n    for (const b of st.beads) {\\n      if (b.dead) continue;\\n      b.landIn -= dt * sp;\\n      if (!b.hopped && b.landIn < 0.5) b.hopped = true;\\n      if (b.landIn <= 0 && !b.landed) {\\n        b.landed = true; b.x = b.tx; b.y = b.ty;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'laceration', x: b.x, y: b.y, r: 8, order: 40, drain: 0.2, tag: 'bite' });\\n        pushEv(S, ['bite', Math.round(b.x), Math.round(b.y)]);\\n      }\\n850→      if (!b.landed) {\\n        const u = clamp(1 - b.landIn / b.flight, 0, 1);\\n        b.x = b.x0 + (b.tx - b.x0) * u;\\n        b.y = b.y0 + (b.ty - b.y0) * u;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* cautery kills beads: mirrored onto objects of type bead */\\n    let nests = 0;\\n    for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'nest' && !o.done && o.tag === st.tag) nests++;\\n    if (!nests && !st.collapse) { st.collapse = 3; }\\n860→    if (st.collapse > 0) {\\n      st.collapse -= dt;\\n      if (st.collapse <= 0) {\\n        for (const b of st.beads) b.dead = true;\\n        for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'bead' && o.tag === st.tag) { o.done = true; o.alive = false; }\\n        st.done = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    syncBeads(S, st);\\n    if (st.beads.length && st.beads.every(b => b.dead) && nests === 0) st.done = true;\\n870→  }\\n\\n  function syncBeads(S, st) {\\n    for (const b of st.beads) {\\n      if (b.dead) continue;\\n      let o = b.oid ? objById(S, b.oid) : null;\\n      if (!o) {\\n        o = addObj(S, { type: 'bead', x: b.x, y: b.y, need: 0.12, order: 5, tag: st.tag, drain: 0 });\\n        b.oid = o.id;\\n      } else {\\n880→        o.x = b.x; o.y = b.y;\\n        if (o.done) b.dead = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepLegato(S, st, dt, handDt, tune, sp) {\\n    for (const w of st.worms) {\\n      if (w.done) continue;\\n      w.t += dt * sp;\\n890→      /* head crawls along its path until surfaced */\\n      if (!w.surfaced && !w.out) {\\n        w.along = Math.min(w.pathLen, w.along + 18 * dt * sp);\\n        const p = pointAlong(w.path, w.along);\\n        w.x = p[0]; w.y = p[1];\\n        /* open a slur guide when the head nears it */\\n        for (const g of w.slurs) {\\n          if (g.opened || g.done) continue;\\n          if (hypot(w.x - g.x, w.y - g.y) < 28) {\\n            g.opened = true;\\n900→            const o = addObj(S, { type: 'slur', x: g.x, y: g.y, len: 18, order: 1, tag: 'slur-' + w.id + '-' + g.i, drain: 0, guide: [[g.x - 9, g.y], [g.x + 9, g.y]] });\\n            g.oid = o.id;\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n      for (const g of w.slurs) {\\n        if (!g.oid || g.done) continue;\\n        const o = objById(S, g.oid);\\n        if (o && o.done) g.done = true;\\n      }\\n910→      const slursLeft = w.slurs.filter(g => !g.done).length;\\n      if (!slursLeft && !w.surfaced) {\\n        w.surfaced = true; w.marked = true;\\n        const head = addObj(S, {\\n          type: 'shard', x: w.x, y: w.y, axis: w.axis || [1, 0], depth: 18, order: 2,\\n          tag: 'legato-head', worm: w.id, tension: 70, drain: 0.15, hidden: false,\\n          holdZone: w.hold || null, barbs: w.barbAt || 0,\\n        });\\n        w.head = head.id;\\n      }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":470,\"limit\":450,\"raw_output\":\"    if (held && p.trigRelease) {\\n      if (held.type === 'retractor') { p.held = 0; return; }\\n      if (held.type === 'screw') { p.held = 0; return; }\\n      const d0 = hypot(p.x - held.origin[0], p.y - held.origin[1]);\\n      if (held.holdZone && hypot(p.x - held.holdZone[0], p.y - held.holdZone[1]) <= (held.holdZone[2] || 14)) {\\n        held.clamped = true; held.gripped = false; p.held = 0;\\n        pushEv(S, ['clamp', held.id]);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      if (held.free && (d0 >= 24 || outside(p.x, p.y))) {\\n        const tears = held.tears || 0;\\n        const parT = held.parTime || (held.depth / 80 + 0.35);\\n        let g = 'sloppy';\\n        if (!tears && (held.pullT || 0) <= parT) g = 'textbook';\\n        else if (tears <= 1) g = 'clean';\\n        held.done = true; held.alive = false; held.grade = g; p.held = 0;\\n        if (held.type === 'note') p.score += 0;\\n        award(S, p, g, 120, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['dish', held.id, g]);\\n      } else {\\n        held.gripped = false;\\n        p.held = 0;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function outside(x, y) {\\n    const nx = (x - CFG.CX) / CFG.RX, ny = (y - CFG.CY) / CFG.RY;\\n    return nx * nx + ny * ny > 1;\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepScalpel(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    const tol = tune.hands.grade;\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel') {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (!o || o.done) { p.stroke = null; }\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigEdge && !p.stroke) {\\n      /* Press within 8 u of the guide start, not the object's center. A long cut's start sits far from x,y. */\\n      const reach = 8 + (p.mouse ? 1 : 0);\\n      let o = null, bd = reach;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n        const q = S.objects[i];\\n        if (!canTouch(S, q) || !q.guide) continue;\\n        if (!(q.type === 'mass' || q.type === 'slur' || q.type === 'tendril' || q.type === 'spiral' || q.type === 'wire' || q.type === 'repeat' || q.type === 'lobe' || q.type === 'cut' || q.type === 'nest')) continue;\\n        const start = q.guide[0];\\n        const d = hypot(p.x - start[0], p.y - start[1]);\\n        if (d <= bd) { bd = d; o = q; }\\n      }\\n      if (o) {\\n        p.stroke = { kind: 'scalpel', id: o.id, far: 0, sum: 0, n: 0, off: 0, slipped: false };\\n        o.cutting = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (!(p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel') && down && p.inst > 40) {\\n      const onGuide = S.objects.some(o => o.guide && !o.done && polyDist(o.guide, p.x, p.y).d < 8);\\n      if (!onGuide && !outside(p.x, p.y)) {\\n        p.bare = (p.bare || 0) + hypot(p.x - (p.ox || p.x), p.y - (p.oy || p.y));\\n        if (p.bare >= 6) { slip(S, p, 'healthy', 3, tune); p.bare = 0; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel' && down) {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (o && nerveHit(S, p, tune)) { /* counted */ }\\n      if (o && o.guide) {\\n        const hit = polyDist(o.guide, p.x, p.y);\\n        const st = p.stroke;\\n        if (hit.along > st.far) st.far = hit.along;\\n        /* A closed ring's last point is the start, so the vertex reads as along 0. Arriving back after most of the loop finishes it. */\\n        const g0 = o.guide[0], gN = o.guide[o.guide.length - 1];\\n        if (o.guide.length > 2 && hypot(g0[0] - gN[0], g0[1] - gN[1]) < 1.5 && st.far > hit.total * 0.72 && hypot(p.x - g0[0], p.y - g0[1]) <= 3) st.far = hit.total;\\n        st.sum += hit.d; st.n += 1;\\n        if (hit.d > 9) st.off += dt; else st.off = 0;\\n        if (st.off >= 0.12 && !st.slipped) {\\n          st.slipped = true; slip(S, p, 'slip', 3, tune);\\n          pushEv(S, ['slipcut', o.id]);\\n        }\\n        o.prog = st.far / (hit.total || 1);\\n        if (o.type === 'spiral' && o.beatLock && S.flags.onBeat) {\\n          if (!st.beatSlip) { st.beatSlip = true; slip(S, p, 'beat', 3, tune); }\\n          o.prog = Math.min(o.prog, st.safe || 0);\\n        } else if (o.type === 'spiral') st.safe = o.prog;\\n        if (st.far >= (hit.total || 1) - 0.5) {\\n          const mean = st.n ? st.sum / st.n : 99;\\n          const g = st.slipped ? 'sloppy' : gradeMean(mean, 1.8 * tol, 4 * tol);\\n          o.done = true; o.alive = false; o.grade = g; o.cut = true;\\n          if (o.type === 'mass') { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.cut = true; o.type = 'mass'; }\\n          if (o.type === 'nest' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.slash)) {\\n            o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.cut = true;\\n            if (o.type === 'lobe') o.mode = 'forceps';\\n          }\\n          if (o.type === 'wire') { /* caller checks order */ wireCut(S, p, o, tune); }\\n          else award(S, p, g, 110, tune);\\n          p.stroke = null;\\n          pushEv(S, ['cut', o.id, g]);\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigRelease && p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'scalpel') {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (o && o.prog < 0.98) {\\n        /* resume later if they come back within 6 */\\n        p.stroke.paused = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigEdge && p.stroke && p.stroke.paused) {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      if (o && o.guide) {\\n        const hit = polyDist(o.guide, p.x, p.y);\\n        if (Math.abs(hit.along - p.stroke.far) <= 6 || hit.d <= 6) p.stroke.paused = false;\\n        else p.stroke = null;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* slash variant: a fast stroke across a slash target */\\n    if (down && p.inst >= 60) {\\n      const o = nearest(S, p, 10, q => canTouch(S, q) && q.slash && !q.done && !q.cut);\\n      if (o) {\\n        o.cut = true;\\n        if (o.type === 'nest' || o.type === 'lobe') {\\n          if (o.type === 'lobe') o.mode = 'forceps';\\n          award(S, p, 'clean', 100, tune);\\n        } else {\\n          o.done = true; o.alive = false;\\n          award(S, p, 'clean', 100, tune);\\n        }\\n        pushEv(S, ['slash', o.id]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function wireCut(S, p, o, tune) {\\n    const dev = S.device;\\n    if (!dev) { o.done = true; award(S, p, 'clean', 80, tune); return; }\\n    const want = dev.order[dev.next];\\n    if (o.tag === want) {\\n      dev.next += 1; o.done = true; o.alive = false;\\n      award(S, p, 'textbook', 100, tune);\\n      if (dev.next >= dev.order.length) dev.done = true;\\n    } else {\\n      o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.cutting = false;\\n      S.vitals -= 30; S.clock = Math.max(0, S.clock - 30);\\n      slip(S, p, 'wire', 0, tune);\\n      pushEv(S, ['badwire', o.tag]);\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSuture(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    const extra = (S.activeDoc === 'sokolova' ? 1 : 0);\\n    if (p.trigEdge) {\\n      /* Press within 9 u of the next near point. Stitches sit off the wound center. */\\n      const reach = 9 + extra + (p.mouse ? 1 : 0);\\n      let o = null, bd = reach;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n        const q = S.objects[i];\\n        if (!canTouch(S, q) || !q.pairs || (q.stitch || 0) >= q.pairs.length) continue;\\n        const a = q.pairs[q.stitch][0];\\n        const d = hypot(p.x - a[0], p.y - a[1]);\\n        if (d <= bd) { bd = d; o = q; }\\n      }\\n      if (o) {\\n        p.stroke = { kind: 'suture', id: o.id, i: o.stitch, t: 0 };\\n        pushEv(S, ['needle', o.id, o.stitch]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'suture' && down) p.stroke.t += dt;\\n    if (p.stroke && p.stroke.kind === 'suture' && p.trigRelease) {\\n      const o = objById(S, p.stroke.id);\\n      const st = p.stroke;\\n      p.stroke = null;\\n      if (!o || o.done) return;\\n      const b = o.pairs[st.i][1];\\n      const tol = 6 + extra + (p.mouse ? 1 : 0);\\n      if (hypot(p.x - b[0], p.y - b[1]) <= tol) {\\n        const g = gradeMean(st.t, 0.6, 1.2);\\n        o.grades = o.grades || [];\\n        o.grades.push(g === 'textbook' ? 2 : g === 'clean' ? 1 : 0);\\n        o.times = o.times || [];\\n        o.times.push(st.t);\\n        o.stitch = st.i + 1;\\n        o.prog = o.stitch / o.pairs.length;\\n        p.stitches += 1;\\n        const bleedLeft = 1 - o.prog;\\n        if (o.type === 'arteryTear') o.drain = 1 * bleedLeft;\\n        else if (o.type === 'wound') o.drain = 0.4 * bleedLeft;\\n        pushEv(S, ['stitch', Math.round(b[0]), Math.round(b[1]), g]);\\n        if (o.stitch >= o.pairs.length) {\\n          const meanT = o.times.reduce((a, c) => a + c, 0) / o.times.length;\\n          const fg = gradeMean(meanT, 0.6, 1.2);\\n          o.done = true; o.alive = false; o.grade = fg; o.drain = 0;\\n          award(S, p, fg, 80 + 20 * o.pairs.length, tune);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        slip(S, p, 'loose', 1, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['loose', o.id]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSalve(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.trig <= 0.3) return;\\n    let any = false;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!canTouch(S, o) || !o.cells) continue;\\n      if (!(o.type === 'laceration' || o.type === 'patch' || o.type === 'bite' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'salve'))) continue;\\n      for (let c = 0; c < o.cells.length; c++) {\\n        const cell = o.cells[c];\\n        if (!cell[2] && hypot(cell[0] - p.x, cell[1] - p.y) <= 10) { cell[2] = 1; any = true; }\\n      }\\n      let on = 0;\\n      for (let c = 0; c < o.cells.length; c++) if (o.cells[c][2]) on++;\\n      o.prog = o.cells.length ? on / o.cells.length : 1;\\n      if (o.prog >= 0.9 && !o.done) {\\n        o.done = true; o.alive = false; o.drain = 0;\\n        S.vitals = Math.min(99, S.vitals + 2 * tune.patient.healing);\\n        award(S, p, 'clean', 80, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['heal', o.id]);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (!any && p.trigEdge) { /* salve cannot harm */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSyringe(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.cool > 0) p.cool -= dt;\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    if (down && p.cool <= 0) {\\n      if (p.fill < 1) p.fill = Math.min(1, p.fill + dt / 0.55);\\n      else p.over += dt;\\n    }\\n    if (p.trigRelease && p.fill > 0.05 && p.cool <= 0) {\\n      const bubble = p.over >= 0.3;\\n      const tgt = nearest(S, p, 10, o => canTouch(S, o) && (o.type === 'clot' || o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'syringe')));\\n      if (tgt) {\\n        if ((tgt.type === 'reed' || tgt.type === 'voice') && !tgt.window) {\\n          addObj(S, { type: 'laceration', x: tgt.x + 6, y: tgt.y, r: 8, order: 50, drain: 0.2 });\\n          slip(S, p, 'spit', 2, tune);\\n        } else {\\n          const g = bubble ? 'sloppy' : (p.fill >= 0.9 ? 'textbook' : 'clean');\\n          tgt.dosed = true;\\n          tgt.dose = (bubble ? 0.5 : 1) * p.fill;\\n          if (tgt.follow === 'salve') {\\n            tgt.mode = 'salve';\\n            if (!tgt.cells) {\\n              const r = tgt.r || 8;\\n              tgt.cells = [];\\n              for (let y = -r; y <= r; y += 4) for (let x = -r; x <= r; x += 4) {\\n                if (x * x + y * y <= r * r) tgt.cells.push([tgt.x + x, tgt.y + y, 0]);\\n              }\\n            }\\n          } else if (tgt.type === 'clot') { tgt.drain = 0.1; }\\n          else { tgt.done = true; tgt.alive = false; tgt.drain = 0; }\\n          award(S, p, g, 90, tune);\\n          pushEv(S, ['inject', tgt.id, g]);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        const g = bubble ? 'sloppy' : (p.fill >= 0.9 ? 'textbook' : 'clean');\\n        const add = syringeDose(S, tune) * p.fill * (bubble ? 0.5 : 1);\\n        S.vitals = Math.min(99, S.vitals + add);\\n        award(S, p, g, 40, tune);\\n        S.flags.iv = (S.flags.iv || 0) + 1;\\n        pushEv(S, ['iv', Math.round(add), g]);\\n      }\\n      p.fill = 0; p.over = 0; p.cool = 0.35;\\n    }\\n    if (!down && p.trigRelease === false) { /* keep fill while aiming */ }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepCautery(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.lock > 0) { p.lock -= dt; p.heat = Math.max(0, p.heat - 0.6 * dt); return; }\\n    const down = p.trig > 0.3;\\n    if (!down) {\\n      p.heat = Math.max(0, p.heat - 0.6 * dt);\\n      p.bareT = 0;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    p.heat += tune.fluids.cauteryHeat * dt;\\n    if (p.heat >= 1) { p.lock = 1.2; p.heat = 1; slip(S, p, 'lock', 1, tune); pushEv(S, ['lock', p.id]); return; }\\n    if (nerveHit(S, p, tune)) return;\\n    const tgt = nearest(S, p, 6, o => canTouch(S, o) && (o.type === 'polyp' || o.type === 'bleeder' || o.type === 'rupture' || o.type === 'bead' || o.type === 'uvula' || o.type === 'eye' || o.type === 'tremass' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'cautery') || o.type === 'barb'));\\n    if (tgt) {\\n      p.bareT = 0;\\n      tgt.burn = (tgt.burn || 0) + dt;\\n      tgt.prog = tgt.burn / (tgt.need || 0.5);\\n      if (tgt.burn >= (tgt.need || 0.5) / Math.max(0.25, tune.strains.health) && !tgt.done) {\\n        const dirty = tgt.charred || p.lockedDuring;\\n        const g = (!tgt.charred && p.lock <= 0 && !p.hadLock) ? 'textbook' : 'clean';\\n        tgt.done = true; tgt.alive = false; tgt.drain = 0; tgt.grade = g;\\n        p.burned += 1;\\n        award(S, p, g, 90, tune);\\n        pushEv(S, ['burn', tgt.id, g]);\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      p.bareT = (p.bareT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (p.bareT >= 0.25) {\\n        /* char on the field */\\n        p.charT = (p.charT || 0) + dt;\\n        S.vitals -= 0.8 * dt * tune.patient.slip;\\n        if (p.bareT >= 0.6 && !p.charSlip) { p.charSlip = true; slip(S, p, 'char', 2, tune); pushEv(S, ['char', Math.round(p.x), Math.round(p.y)]); }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSuction(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.trig <= 0.3) return;\\n    const pool = nearest(S, p, 14, o => o.type === 'pool' && !o.done && o.vol > 0);\\n    if (!pool) return;\\n    const rate = tune.fluids.suction;\\n    const before = pool.vol;\\n    pool.vol = Math.max(0, pool.vol - rate * dt);\\n    p.suctioned += before - pool.vol;\\n    pool.prog = 1 - pool.vol / (pool.max || 1);\\n    if (pool.vol <= 0.2) { pool.done = true; pool.alive = false; pool.vol = 0; pushEv(S, ['dry', pool.id]); }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepSonar(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.trig <= 0.3) return;\\n    let rad = 38;\\n    if (S.activeDoc === 'vale' || S.gift === 'breath') rad *= 1.25;\\n    if (S.gift === 'both' && S.activeDoc === 'vale') rad *= 1.25;\\n    p.sonarR = rad;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!o.hidden || o.done) continue;\\n      if (hypot(o.x - p.x, o.y - p.y) <= rad) { o.marked = true; o.markT = 4; pushEv(S, ['mark', o.id]); }\\n    }\\n    if (S.device && !S.device.shown && hypot(p.x - (S.device.x || 213), p.y - (S.device.y || 116)) <= rad) {\\n      S.device.shown = true;\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.needsBoard) { o.hidden = false; o.marked = true; o.markT = 6; }\\n      pushEv(S, ['board', 1]);\\n    }\\n    if (S.strain && S.strain.kind === 'legato') {\\n      for (const w of S.strain.worms || []) if (hypot(w.x - p.x, w.y - p.y) <= rad) w.marked = true;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function applyTools(S, p, dt, tune) {\\n    if (p.gone) return;\\n    if (inDome(S, p.x, p.y)) return;\\n    if (p.swap > 0) p.swap -= dt;\\n    p.ox = p.x; p.oy = p.y;\\n    const tool = p.tool;\\n    if (tool === 'forceps') stepForceps(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'scalpel') stepScalpel(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'suture') stepSuture(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'salve') stepSalve(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'syringe') stepSyringe(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'cautery') stepCautery(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'suction') stepSuction(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    else if (tool === 'sonar') stepSonar(S, p, dt, tune);\\n    /* marks expire */\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---------- strains ---------- */\\n\\n  function stepStrain(S, worldDt, handDt, tune) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n    if (!st || st.done) return;\\n    const sp = tune.strains.speed;\\n    if (st.kind === 'staccato') stepStaccato(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'legato') stepLegato(S, st, worldDt, handDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'tremolo') stepTremolo(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'dacapo') stepDacapo(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'fermata') stepFermata(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n    else if (st.kind === 'cantor') stepCantor(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepStaccato(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    const beat = tune.strains.beat;\\n    for (const b of st.beads) {\\n      if (b.dead) continue;\\n      b.landIn -= dt * sp;\\n      if (!b.hopped && b.landIn < 0.5) b.hopped = true;\\n      if (b.landIn <= 0 && !b.landed) {\\n        b.landed = true; b.x = b.tx; b.y = b.ty;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'laceration', x: b.x, y: b.y, r: 8, order: 40, drain: 0.2, tag: 'bite' });\\n        pushEv(S, ['bite', Math.round(b.x), Math.round(b.y)]);\\n      }\\n      if (!b.landed) {\\n        const u = clamp(1 - b.landIn / b.flight, 0, 1);\\n        b.x = b.x0 + (b.tx - b.x0) * u;\\n        b.y = b.y0 + (b.ty - b.y0) * u;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* cautery kills beads: mirrored onto objects of type bead */\\n    let nests = 0;\\n    for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'nest' && !o.done && o.tag === st.tag) nests++;\\n    if (!nests && !st.collapse) { st.collapse = 3; }\\n    if (st.collapse > 0) {\\n      st.collapse -= dt;\\n      if (st.collapse <= 0) {\\n        for (const b of st.beads) b.dead = true;\\n        for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'bead' && o.tag === st.tag) { o.done = true; o.alive = false; }\\n        st.done = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n    syncBeads(S, st);\\n    if (st.beads.length && st.beads.every(b => b.dead) && nests === 0) st.done = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function syncBeads(S, st) {\\n    for (const b of st.beads) {\\n      if (b.dead) continue;\\n      let o = b.oid ? objById(S, b.oid) : null;\\n      if (!o) {\\n        o = addObj(S, { type: 'bead', x: b.x, y: b.y, need: 0.12, order: 5, tag: st.tag, drain: 0 });\\n        b.oid = o.id;\\n      } else {\\n        o.x = b.x; o.y = b.y;\\n        if (o.done) b.dead = true;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepLegato(S, st, dt, handDt, tune, sp) {\\n    for (const w of st.worms) {\\n      if (w.done) continue;\\n      w.t += dt * sp;\\n      /* head crawls along its path until surfaced */\\n      if (!w.surfaced && !w.out) {\\n        w.along = Math.min(w.pathLen, w.along + 18 * dt * sp);\\n        const p = pointAlong(w.path, w.along);\\n        w.x = p[0]; w.y = p[1];\\n        /* open a slur guide when the head nears it */\\n        for (const g of w.slurs) {\\n          if (g.opened || g.done) continue;\\n          if (hypot(w.x - g.x, w.y - g.y) < 28) {\\n            g.opened = true;\\n            const o = addObj(S, { type: 'slur', x: g.x, y: g.y, len: 18, order: 1, tag: 'slur-' + w.id + '-' + g.i, drain: 0, guide: [[g.x - 9, g.y], [g.x + 9, g.y]] });\\n            g.oid = o.id;\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n      for (const g of w.slurs) {\\n        if (!g.oid || g.done) continue;\\n        const o = objById(S, g.oid);\\n        if (o && o.done) g.done = true;\\n      }\\n      const slursLeft = w.slurs.filter(g => !g.done).length;\\n      if (!slursLeft && !w.surfaced) {\\n        w.surfaced = true; w.marked = true;\\n        const head = addObj(S, {\\n          type: 'shard', x: w.x, y: w.y, axis: w.axis || [1, 0], depth: 18, order: 2,\\n          tag: 'legato-head', worm: w.id, tension: 70, drain: 0.15, hidden: false,\\n          holdZone: w.hold || null, barbs: w.barbAt || 0,\\n        });\\n        w.head = head.id;\\n      }\\n\",\"total_lines\":1762}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7ee40bd3-662e-4dd6-aaf8-003398527464-11","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/* Open Table Second Opinion — title, tuning, and the strings the page and the Hub share. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const GAME_TITLE = 'Open Table Second Opinion';\\n  const RUN = 'grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916';\\n  const SOURCE = 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion';\\n\\n  const TUNING = {\\n10→    patient: { drain: 1, slip: 1, healing: 1, syringe: 18, clock: 1 },\\n    hands: { cursor: 330, fine: 0.35, curve: 1.7, assist: 0.6, magnet: 22, grade: 1 },\\n    strains: { speed: 1, health: 1, spawn: 1, damage: 1, beat: 0.5 },\\n    gift: { charge: 1, breathDrain: 16, breathFactor: 0.25, lookSeconds: 6 },\\n    fluids: { bleed: 1, suction: 60, cauteryHeat: 0.5 },\\n  };\\n\\n  const TOOLS = ['forceps', 'scalpel', 'suture', 'salve', 'syringe', 'cautery', 'suction', 'sonar'];\\n  /* Stick y is negative toward the top of the field. Clockwise from north. */\\n  const WHEEL = [\\n20→    { tool: 'forceps', x: 0, y: -1 },\\n    { tool: 'scalpel', x: 1, y: -1 },\\n    { tool: 'suture', x: 1, y: 0 },\\n    { tool: 'salve', x: 1, y: 1 },\\n    { tool: 'syringe', x: 0, y: 1 },\\n    { tool: 'cautery', x: -1, y: 1 },\\n    { tool: 'suction', x: -1, y: 0 },\\n    { tool: 'sonar', x: -1, y: -1 },\\n  ];\\n\\n30→  function cloneTune(t) {\\n    return {\\n      patient: Object.assign({}, t.patient),\\n      hands: Object.assign({}, t.hands),\\n      strains: Object.assign({}, t.strains),\\n      gift: Object.assign({}, t.gift),\\n      fluids: Object.assign({}, t.fluids),\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n40→  GAME.CFG = {\\n    GAME_TITLE, RUN, SOURCE,\\n    FILE: 'Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-' + RUN,\\n    TUNING, TOOLS, WHEEL, cloneTune,\\n    FIELD_W: 426, FIELD_H: 240, CX: 213, CY: 116, RX: 171, RY: 91,\\n    SEAT: ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'],\\n  };\\n  GAME.TUNE = cloneTune(TUNING);\\n  const DEV_KEYS = [\\n    ['patient.drain', 0, 3], ['patient.slip', 0, 3], ['patient.healing', 0, 3], ['patient.syringe', 0, 40], ['patient.clock', 0.2, 2],\\n50→    ['hands.cursor', 80, 500], ['hands.fine', 0.15, 1], ['hands.curve', 1, 3], ['hands.assist', 0, 1.4], ['hands.magnet', 0, 48], ['hands.grade', 0.5, 2],\\n    ['strains.speed', 0.2, 2], ['strains.health', 0.25, 2], ['strains.spawn', 0.2, 2], ['strains.damage', 0.2, 2], ['strains.beat', 0.2, 1.2],\\n    ['gift.charge', 0.2, 2], ['gift.breathDrain', 4, 40], ['gift.breathFactor', 0.1, 1], ['gift.lookSeconds', 1, 8],\\n    ['fluids.bleed', 0.2, 2], ['fluids.suction', 10, 120], ['fluids.cauteryHeat', 0.15, 1.2],\\n  ];\\n  function devSet(path, value) {\\n    const [g, k] = path.split('.');\\n    if (!GAME.TUNE[g] || !(k in GAME.TUNE[g])) return false;\\n    GAME.TUNE[g][k] = value;\\n    GAME.TUNE.dirty = true;\\n60→    return true;\\n  }\\n  function devReset() {\\n    const next = cloneTune(TUNING);\\n    for (const g of Object.keys(next)) Object.assign(GAME.TUNE[g], next[g]);\\n    GAME.TUNE.dirty = false;\\n  }\\n  function devCheat(S, key, on) {\\n    S.cheat = S.cheat || {};\\n    S.cheat[key] = !!on;\\n70→    return S.cheat;\\n  }\\n  GAME.Dev = { KEYS: DEV_KEYS, set: devSet, reset: devReset, cheat: devCheat, defaults: TUNING };\\n})();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/* Open Table Second Opinion — title, tuning, and the strings the page and the Hub share. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const GAME_TITLE = 'Open Table Second Opinion';\\n  const RUN = 'grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916';\\n  const SOURCE = 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion';\\n\\n  const TUNING = {\\n10→    patient: { drain: 1, slip: 1, healing: 1, syringe: 18, clock: 1 },\\n    hands: { cursor: 330, fine: 0.35, curve: 1.7, assist: 0.6, magnet: 22, grade: 1 },\\n    strains: { speed: 1, health: 1, spawn: 1, damage: 1, beat: 0.5 },\\n    gift: { charge: 1, breathDrain: 16, breathFactor: 0.25, lookSeconds: 6 },\\n    fluids: { bleed: 1, suction: 60, cauteryHeat: 0.5 },\\n  };\\n\\n  const TOOLS = ['forceps', 'scalpel', 'suture', 'salve', 'syringe', 'cautery', 'suction', 'sonar'];\\n  /* Stick y is negative toward the top of the field. Clockwise from north. */\\n  const WHEEL = [\\n20→    { tool: 'forceps', x: 0, y: -1 },\\n    { tool: 'scalpel', x: 1, y: -1 },\\n    { tool: 'suture', x: 1, y: 0 },\\n    { tool: 'salve', x: 1, y: 1 },\\n    { tool: 'syringe', x: 0, y: 1 },\\n    { tool: 'cautery', x: -1, y: 1 },\\n    { tool: 'suction', x: -1, y: 0 },\\n    { tool: 'sonar', x: -1, y: -1 },\\n  ];\\n\\n30→  function cloneTune(t) {\\n    return {\\n      patient: Object.assign({}, t.patient),\\n      hands: Object.assign({}, t.hands),\\n      strains: Object.assign({}, t.strains),\\n      gift: Object.assign({}, t.gift),\\n      fluids: Object.assign({}, t.fluids),\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n40→  GAME.CFG = {\\n    GAME_TITLE, RUN, SOURCE,\\n    FILE: 'Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-' + RUN,\\n    TUNING, TOOLS, WHEEL, cloneTune,\\n    FIELD_W: 426, FIELD_H: 240, CX: 213, CY: 116, RX: 171, RY: 91,\\n    SEAT: ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'],\\n  };\\n  GAME.TUNE = cloneTune(TUNING);\\n  const DEV_KEYS = [\\n    ['patient.drain', 0, 3], ['patient.slip', 0, 3], ['patient.healing', 0, 3], ['patient.syringe', 0, 40], ['patient.clock', 0.2, 2],\\n50→    ['hands.cursor', 80, 500], ['hands.fine', 0.15, 1], ['hands.curve', 1, 3], ['hands.assist', 0, 1.4], ['hands.magnet', 0, 48], ['hands.grade', 0.5, 2],\\n    ['strains.speed', 0.2, 2], ['strains.health', 0.25, 2], ['strains.spawn', 0.2, 2], ['strains.damage', 0.2, 2], ['strains.beat', 0.2, 1.2],\\n    ['gift.charge', 0.2, 2], ['gift.breathDrain', 4, 40], ['gift.breathFactor', 0.1, 1], ['gift.lookSeconds', 1, 8],\\n    ['fluids.bleed', 0.2, 2], ['fluids.suction', 10, 120], ['fluids.cauteryHeat', 0.15, 1.2],\\n  ];\\n  function devSet(path, value) {\\n    const [g, k] = path.split('.');\\n    if (!GAME.TUNE[g] || !(k in GAME.TUNE[g])) return false;\\n    GAME.TUNE[g][k] = value;\\n    GAME.TUNE.dirty = true;\\n60→    return true;\\n  }\\n  function devReset() {\\n    const next = cloneTune(TUNING);\\n    for (const g of Object.keys(next)) Object.assign(GAME.TUNE[g], next[g]);\\n    GAME.TUNE.dirty = false;\\n  }\\n  function devCheat(S, key, on) {\\n    S.cheat = S.cheat || {};\\n    S.cheat[key] = !!on;\\n70→    return S.cheat;\\n  }\\n  GAME.Dev = { KEYS: DEV_KEYS, set: devSet, reset: devReset, cheat: devCheat, defaults: TUNING };\\n})();\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/config.js\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"/* Open Table Second Opinion — title, tuning, and the strings the page and the Hub share. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const GAME_TITLE = 'Open Table Second Opinion';\\n  const RUN = 'grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916';\\n  const SOURCE = 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion';\\n\\n  const TUNING = {\\n    patient: { drain: 1, slip: 1, healing: 1, syringe: 18, clock: 1 },\\n    hands: { cursor: 330, fine: 0.35, curve: 1.7, assist: 0.6, magnet: 22, grade: 1 },\\n    strains: { speed: 1, health: 1, spawn: 1, damage: 1, beat: 0.5 },\\n    gift: { charge: 1, breathDrain: 16, breathFactor: 0.25, lookSeconds: 6 },\\n    fluids: { bleed: 1, suction: 60, cauteryHeat: 0.5 },\\n  };\\n\\n  const TOOLS = ['forceps', 'scalpel', 'suture', 'salve', 'syringe', 'cautery', 'suction', 'sonar'];\\n  /* Stick y is negative toward the top of the field. Clockwise from north. */\\n  const WHEEL = [\\n    { tool: 'forceps', x: 0, y: -1 },\\n    { tool: 'scalpel', x: 1, y: -1 },\\n    { tool: 'suture', x: 1, y: 0 },\\n    { tool: 'salve', x: 1, y: 1 },\\n    { tool: 'syringe', x: 0, y: 1 },\\n    { tool: 'cautery', x: -1, y: 1 },\\n    { tool: 'suction', x: -1, y: 0 },\\n    { tool: 'sonar', x: -1, y: -1 },\\n  ];\\n\\n  function cloneTune(t) {\\n    return {\\n      patient: Object.assign({}, t.patient),\\n      hands: Object.assign({}, t.hands),\\n      strains: Object.assign({}, t.strains),\\n      gift: Object.assign({}, t.gift),\\n      fluids: Object.assign({}, t.fluids),\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  GAME.CFG = {\\n    GAME_TITLE, RUN, SOURCE,\\n    FILE: 'Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-' + RUN,\\n    TUNING, TOOLS, WHEEL, cloneTune,\\n    FIELD_W: 426, FIELD_H: 240, CX: 213, CY: 116, RX: 171, RY: 91,\\n    SEAT: ['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700'],\\n  };\\n  GAME.TUNE = cloneTune(TUNING);\\n  const DEV_KEYS = [\\n    ['patient.drain', 0, 3], ['patient.slip', 0, 3], ['patient.healing', 0, 3], ['patient.syringe', 0, 40], ['patient.clock', 0.2, 2],\\n    ['hands.cursor', 80, 500], ['hands.fine', 0.15, 1], ['hands.curve', 1, 3], ['hands.assist', 0, 1.4], ['hands.magnet', 0, 48], ['hands.grade', 0.5, 2],\\n    ['strains.speed', 0.2, 2], ['strains.health', 0.25, 2], ['strains.spawn', 0.2, 2], ['strains.damage', 0.2, 2], ['strains.beat', 0.2, 1.2],\\n    ['gift.charge', 0.2, 2], ['gift.breathDrain', 4, 40], ['gift.breathFactor', 0.1, 1], ['gift.lookSeconds', 1, 8],\\n    ['fluids.bleed', 0.2, 2], ['fluids.suction', 10, 120], ['fluids.cauteryHeat', 0.15, 1.2],\\n  ];\\n  function devSet(path, value) {\\n    const [g, k] = path.split('.');\\n    if (!GAME.TUNE[g] || !(k in GAME.TUNE[g])) return false;\\n    GAME.TUNE[g][k] = value;\\n    GAME.TUNE.dirty = true;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n  function devReset() {\\n    const next = cloneTune(TUNING);\\n    for (const g of Object.keys(next)) Object.assign(GAME.TUNE[g], next[g]);\\n    GAME.TUNE.dirty = false;\\n  }\\n  function devCheat(S, key, on) {\\n    S.cheat = S.cheat || {};\\n    S.cheat[key] = !!on;\\n    return S.cheat;\\n  }\\n  GAME.Dev = { KEYS: DEV_KEYS, set: devSet, reset: devReset, cheat: devCheat, defaults: TUNING };\\n})();\\n\",\"total_lines\":73}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"d9c9d31d-c284-4a35-a6b0-00706f152f33"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_285","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will check stepCantor, stepDacapo, and stepFermata. I will also review windowOpen logic, content ORDER, and about.js structure to align the test and exit interview.\n\nI am drafting run.mjs. I need to get --fast green first. The sokolova cursor test requires a 300-unit travel distance, but the field clamp limits rightward movement to 205 units. This creates a conflict.\n\nStarting at (20, 120) with a rightward full stick should yield roughly 330 units of travel in one second. The fine threshold is about 116, which fits within the 120 limit. Vale's fine threshold would be roughly 133, exceeding that cap.\n\nI will set up the vale test with a blank sokolova document, hold true to block phase advancement, and no objects. I must ensure the phase does not clear automatically. The step still runs tools and drains the clock.\n\nI will set the clock to 9999 and drain to 0. The player starts at (20, 120) with zero speed. I will clone the tune and disable assist so no magnet pulls occur. Cursor.update can run without stepping the simulation.\n\nThe one-second full-stick test yields roughly 310 units of travel, satisfying the 300-unit minimum. Fine aim lands near 108, safely under the 120 cap. Vale full-stick reaches about 356 units, confirming its roughly 15% speed advantage. The wheel test begins with forceps at index zero.\n\nThe scalpel sits at wheel index 1. A stable stick there needs 0.08 seconds before the tool changes, so the test must finish within 100 milliseconds.\n\nDigit 3 triggers suture immediately.\n\nFor the forceps tear test, a shard spawns at the player position with depth 40, axis [1,0], and tension 120. The grip is on the trig edge. The player then moves perpendicular while holding.\n\nThe forceps tear sequence requires two steps. The first step grasps the shard at its origin. The second step moves the player 20 units perpendicular while holding, which tears the shard once that distance exceeds 8. The dish test pulls along the shard axis past its depth and releases far from the origin; tearing triggers when the instantaneous tension exceeds 120.\n\nThe dish test must move only three units per step to keep instantaneous tension below 120 and avoid tearing before the release. The legato snap test uses a 'legato-head' tag and requires a perpendicular jump greater than eight, but it does not add a laceration. The scalpel slip test starts a cut along a horizontal guide line and then moves off that line by more than nine units for 0.12 seconds.\n\nThe closed ring test uses a mass at 213, 116 with radius 16. The ring guide starts at angle -PI/2, placing the initial point at (213, 100). The cursor will trace this guide and return to the start.\n\nFor suture, a wound is placed at 200, 120 to generate pairs. The test presses at pairs[0][0], holds briefly, and releases at pairs[0][1].\n\nSalve requires painting ninety percent of laceration cells. This can be done by stepping with trigger while visiting each cell.\n\nThe syringe air test holds for more than 0.85 seconds and then releases off target.\n\nSloppy grades still trigger IV. An off-window reed injection causes a laceration. Cautery locks at heat 1 after two seconds, though bare tissue chars and slips; holding 2.1 seconds confirms the lock. Suction empties a 36-unit pool in about 0.7 seconds. Sonar marks a hidden shard within 38 units. RankLetter maps 1400 to S, 0.94×par to A, and zero slips to S+. retry caps rank at B. Code blue drains vitals to zero via step, then peaks.\n\nA zero clock before vitals should be set to tiny values and stepped; the failure reason must be time, not code. Long breath uses a 40-second gift edge with worldScale 0.25. Cursor.update ignores worldScale, so the clock drains slower during the breath while the cursor still uses real dt. Second look fills a ring guide over 0.7 seconds, records the core, changes something, then calls secondLook; the field must match the earlier core rather than the reduced steady state. Determinism requires identical bot play hashes for two creates of the same case, and Art.force must not affect the hash if drawing does not.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-54c099c8-cc18-4882-a81f-850a3ef396d7-12","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":1000,"limit":280}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-54c099c8-cc18-4882-a81f-850a3ef396d7-13","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/about.js","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-54c099c8-cc18-4882-a81f-850a3ef396d7-14","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function (stepCantor|stepDacapo|stepFermata|stepWorld|spawnStrain)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12050,"output_tokens":2455,"cache_read_input_tokens":57984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"eb55fb94-ca5c-47ec-869f-d2deebbcf2f7"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-54c099c8-cc18-4882-a81f-850a3ef396d7-12","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1000→      if (st.wake <= 0) {\\n        st.wake = 6;\\n        /* a reed returns */\\n        if (S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length < 2) {\\n          addObj(S, { type: 'reed', x: st.x - 20 + rnd(S) * 40, y: st.y - 10, order: 1, tag: 'reed', drain: 0, window: false });\\n        }\\n      }\\n      const mass = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'tremass');\\n      if (mass && mass.done && st.stage === 2) {\\n        st.stage = 3;\\n1010→        addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: st.x, y: st.y, axis: [1, 0], depth: 40, order: 4, tag: 'tremolo-pull', tension: 90, drain: 0.2 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (st.stage === 3) {\\n      const pull = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'tremolo-pull');\\n      if (pull && pull.done) {\\n        st.done = true;\\n        for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'reed' && !o.done) { o.done = true; o.alive = false; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n1020→    /* amp falls when a reed is dosed */\\n    const deadReeds = st.reed0 - S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length;\\n    st.amp = clamp(1 - deadReeds * 0.2, 0.15, 1);\\n    if (st.stage >= 2) st.amp = Math.min(st.amp, 0.2);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepDacapo(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt * sp;\\n    let anyDead = false;\\n    for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n1030→      if (L.dead) { anyDead = true; continue; }\\n      const period = L.period / (st.round === 2 ? 2 : 1);\\n      const openFor = L.openFor / (st.round === 2 ? 2 : 1);\\n      const u = st.t % period;\\n      L.open = u < openFor;\\n      const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n      if (o) { o.open = L.open && !L.dead; o.x = L.x; o.y = L.y; if (o.done && !L.dead) { L.dead = true; anyDead = true; if (st.count < 0) st.count = 10; } }\\n    }\\n    if (st.count >= 0) {\\n      st.count -= dt;\\n1040→      if (st.count <= 0 && st.lobes.some(L => L.dead) && st.lobes.some(L => !L.dead)) {\\n        /* from the top */\\n        for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n          L.dead = false;\\n          const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n          if (o) { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.open = false; if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0; }\\n        }\\n        S.vitals -= 8;\\n        st.count = -1;\\n        st.repeated = (st.repeated || 0) + 1;\\n1050→        if (st.round === 1) { st.round = 2; st.t = 0; spawnBeadsN(S, st, 4); }\\n        pushEv(S, ['dacapo', st.repeated]);\\n      } else if (st.count <= 0) st.count = -1;\\n    }\\n    if (st.lobes.every(L => L.dead) && st.count < 0) {\\n      if (st.round === 1) {\\n        st.round = 2; st.t = 0; st.count = -1;\\n        for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n          L.dead = false;\\n          const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n1060→          if (o) { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0; }\\n        }\\n        spawnBeadsN(S, st, 4);\\n        pushEv(S, ['round2', 1]);\\n      } else if (S.objects.every(o => o.type !== 'bead' || o.done)) st.done = true;\\n    }\\n    if (st.round === 2 && st.lobes.every(L => L.dead) && S.objects.every(o => o.type !== 'bead' || o.done || o.tag !== 'dacapo-bead')) st.done = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function spawnBeadsN(S, st, n) {\\n1070→    st.beads = st.beads || [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n      const b = { x: 180 + i * 16, y: 100, tx: 190 + i * 14, ty: 130, x0: 180 + i * 16, y0: 100, landIn: 0.8, flight: 0.8, dead: false, landed: false, hopped: false };\\n      st.beads.push(b);\\n      const o = addObj(S, { type: 'bead', x: b.x, y: b.y, need: 0.12, order: 6, tag: 'dacapo-bead', drain: 0 });\\n      b.oid = o.id;\\n    }\\n    if (!st.kindBead) st.kindBead = true;\\n  }\\n\\n1080→  function stepFermata(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    for (const d of st.domes) if (d.t > 0) d.t -= dt;\\n    st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n    if (st.stage === 1 && st.domes.length === 0 && !(st.eyeOpen > 0)) {\\n      st.eyeOpen = S.breath ? 2.8 : 0.7;\\n      st.eye.open = true;\\n      const o = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n      if (o) o.open = true;\\n    }\\n1090→    if (st.eyeOpen > 0) {\\n      st.eyeOpen -= dt;\\n      if (st.eyeOpen <= 0) {\\n        st.eye.open = false;\\n        const o = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n        if (o && !o.done) o.open = false;\\n        if (st.hits < 3 && st.stage === 1) {\\n          /* raise another dome */\\n          if (st.domes.length < 3) st.domes.push({ x: st.eye.x, y: st.eye.y, r: 34, t: 5 });\\n        }\\n1100→      }\\n    }\\n    const eye = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n    if (eye && eye.done) { st.hits += 1; eye.done = false; eye.alive = true; eye.burn = 0; eye.prog = 0; eye.open = false; st.eye.open = false; }\\n    if (st.hits >= 3 && st.stage === 1) {\\n      st.stage = 2;\\n      st.eye.x = 250; st.eye.y = 90; st.eye.hidden = true;\\n      if (eye) { eye.x = 250; eye.y = 90; eye.hidden = true; eye.marked = false; eye.done = false; eye.alive = true; }\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: 160, y: 140, axis: [1, 0], depth: 12, order: 3, tag: 'sliver-a', drain: 0.1, hidden: true });\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: 180, y: 150, axis: [0.6, 0.8], depth: 12, order: 3, tag: 'sliver-b', drain: 0.1, hidden: true });\\n1110→    }\\n    if (st.stage === 2 && eye && eye.marked && st.hits < 4) { eye.hidden = false; eye.open = true; }\\n    if (st.stage >= 2 && eye && st.hits >= 4) { eye.open = false; eye.drain = 0; }\\n    if (st.stage === 2) {\\n      const slivers = S.objects.filter(o => o.tag === 'sliver-a' || o.tag === 'sliver-b');\\n      if (st.hits >= 4 && slivers.length && slivers.every(o => o.done)) {\\n        st.stage = 3;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: st.eye.x, y: st.eye.y, axis: [0, -1], depth: 28, tension: 40, order: 5, tag: 'fermata-pull', drain: 0.15 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n1120→    if (st.stage === 3) {\\n      const pull = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'fermata-pull');\\n      if (pull && pull.done) {\\n        st.done = true;\\n        if (eye) { eye.done = true; eye.alive = false; eye.open = false; eye.drain = 0; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepCantor(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n1130→    st.t += dt;\\n    if (st.move === 1) {\\n      /* tendrils then uvulas, objects already spawned by the phase */\\n      const left = S.objects.filter(o => (o.tag === 'tendril' || o.tag === 'uvula') && !o.done);\\n      if (!left.length) { st.move = 2; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = true; pushEv(S, ['movement', 2]); spawnVoice(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 2) {\\n      S.flags.hush = true;\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 1);\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'voice') o.window = st.beat > 0.62;\\n      if (st.domes) {\\n1140→        for (const d of st.domes) d.t -= dt;\\n        st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n      }\\n      st.jitter = true;\\n      const voices = S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'voice' && !o.done);\\n      if (!voices.length) { st.move = 3; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = false; st.signs = 0; pushEv(S, ['movement', 3]); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 3) {\\n      st.cycleT = (st.cycleT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (!st.winding && st.cycleT >= 20) { st.winding = 3; st.cycleT = 0; openRepeat(S, st); }\\n      if (st.winding > 0) {\\n1150→        st.winding -= dt;\\n        if (st.winding <= 0) {\\n          const sign = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n          if (sign && !sign.done) {\\n            forceRewind(S, true);\\n            const now = S.strain;\\n            if (now) now.rewound = (now.rewound || 0) + 1;\\n          } else if (sign && sign.done) {\\n            st.signs = (st.signs || 0) + 1;\\n            sign.tag = 'repeat-spent';\\n1160→          }\\n          st.winding = 0;\\n          closeRepeat(S);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if ((st.signs || 0) >= 6 && S.strain === st) { st.move = 4; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; pushEv(S, ['movement', 4]); spawnCoda(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 4) {\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 0.8) / 0.8;\\n      S.flags.onBeat = st.beat < 0.25;\\n      const spiral = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'spiral' && o.tag === 'last-note');\\n1170→      const note = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'the-note');\\n      const wound = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'final-wound');\\n      if (spiral && spiral.done && !st.noteOut) {\\n        st.noteOut = true;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: 213, y: 116, axis: [0, -1], depth: 36, tension: 80, order: 2, tag: 'the-note', drain: 0 });\\n      }\\n      if (note && note.done && !wound) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'wound', x: 213, y: 130, stitches: 6, order: 3, tag: 'final-wound', drain: 0.3 });\\n      }\\n      if (wound && wound.done) st.done = true;\\n1180→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function openRepeat(S, st) {\\n    const existing = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n    if (existing) { existing.done = false; existing.alive = true; existing.open = true; existing.prog = 0; return existing; }\\n    return addObj(S, { type: 'repeat', x: 213, y: 100, len: 36, order: 1, tag: 'repeat', open: true, drain: 0, guide: [[190, 100], [236, 100]] });\\n  }\\n  function closeRepeat(S) {\\n    for (const o of S.objects) if (o.tag === 'repeat' && !o.done) { o.open = false; }\\n1190→  }\\n  function spawnVoice(S, st) {\\n    st.domes = [{ x: 90, y: 70, r: 28, t: 4 }, { x: 330, y: 70, r: 28, t: 5 }];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) addObj(S, { type: 'voice', x: 170 + i * 36, y: 150, hidden: true, order: 1, tag: 'voice', drain: 0.15, window: false });\\n    st.jitter = true; st.amp = 0.45;\\n  }\\n  function spawnCoda(S, st) {\\n    const guide = [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i <= 16; i++) {\\n      const a = i / 16 * Math.PI * 1.6;\\n1200→      guide.push([213 + Math.cos(a) * (20 + i * 3), 116 + Math.sin(a) * (12 + i * 2)]);\\n    }\\n    addObj(S, { type: 'spiral', x: 213, y: 116, guide, order: 1, tag: 'last-note', beatLock: true, drain: 0, ring: false });\\n  }\\n\\n  function spawnStrain(S, kind, opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    if (kind === 'staccato') {\\n      const st = { kind, tag: opts.tag || 'stacc', t: 0, beads: [], done: false, collapse: 0 };\\n      const n = opts.nests || 2;\\n1210→      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'nest', x: opts.x || (180 + i * 40), y: opts.y || 120, hidden: true, order: 2, tag: st.tag, slash: true, drain: 0.15, r: 8 });\\n      }\\n      const beads = opts.beads || 4;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < beads; i++) {\\n        st.beads.push({ x: 160 + i * 12, y: 90, x0: 160 + i * 12, y0: 90, tx: 170 + (i % 3) * 18, ty: 140, landIn: (opts.landIn || 1.1) + i * 0.2, flight: 0.7, dead: false, landed: false, hopped: false });\\n      }\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n1220→    if (kind === 'legato') {\\n      const seg = opts.segments || 8;\\n      const w = makeWorm(S, opts.x || 150, opts.y || 120, seg, 1);\\n      w.marked = false;\\n      const st = { kind, worms: [w], done: false, snapped: false };\\n      /* head starts hidden: a sonar target */\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'hold', x: w.x, y: w.y, hidden: true, order: 0, tag: 'legato-hide', drain: 0 });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n1230→    if (kind === 'tremolo') {\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, amp: 1, stage: 1, x: opts.x || 213, y: opts.y || 116, wake: 6, reed0: 5, done: false, jitter: true, beat: 0, flare: false };\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\\n        const a = -Math.PI / 2 + i * TAU / 5;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'reed', x: st.x + Math.cos(a) * 28, y: st.y + Math.sin(a) * 18, order: 1, tag: 'reed', drain: 0, window: false });\\n      }\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'tremass', x: st.x, y: st.y, need: 3, order: 3, tag: 'tremass', drain: 0.3 });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n1240→    if (kind === 'dacapo') {\\n      const lobes = [\\n        { id: 'A', mode: 'cautery', period: 6, openFor: 2.5, x: 180, y: 110 },\\n        { id: 'B', mode: 'slash', period: 7, openFor: 2.5, x: 213, y: 130 },\\n        { id: 'C', mode: 'syringe', period: 9, openFor: 3, x: 246, y: 112 },\\n      ];\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, round: 1, count: -1, lobes, done: false, repeated: 0 };\\n      for (const L of lobes) {\\n        const spec = { type: 'lobe', x: L.x, y: L.y, mode: L.mode === 'slash' ? 'scalpel' : L.mode, order: 1, tag: 'lobe-' + L.id, open: false, drain: 0.15, need: L.mode === 'cautery' ? 1 : 0.5 };\\n        if (L.mode === 'slash') { spec.guide = [[L.x - 10, L.y], [L.x + 10, L.y]]; spec.mode = 'scalpel'; spec.slash = true; }\\n1250→        if (L.mode === 'syringe') { spec.mode = 'syringe'; spec.follow = 'salve'; }\\n        const o = addObj(S, spec);\\n        L.oid = o.id; L.dead = false; L.open = false;\\n      }\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    if (kind === 'fermata') {\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, stage: 1, hits: 0, eyeOpen: 0, done: false, jitter: false, amp: 0,\\n        domes: [{ x: 200, y: 116, r: 34, t: 5 }],\\n1260→        eye: { x: 200, y: 116, open: false, hidden: false } };\\n      const o = addObj(S, { type: 'eye', x: 200, y: 116, need: 0.3, order: 1, tag: 'eye', open: false, drain: 0.2 });\\n      st.eye.oid = o.id;\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'eloquent', x: 150, y: 100, guide: [[140, 90], [180, 110]], order: 0, drain: 0, tag: 'eloq' });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    if (kind === 'cantor') {\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, move: 1, done: false, signs: 0, jitter: false, amp: 0.4, domes: [] };\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) addObj(S, { type: 'tendril', x: 170 + i * 30, y: 100, len: 28, order: 1, tag: 'tendril', drain: 0.15, guide: [[160 + i * 30, 100], [190 + i * 30, 108]] });\\n1270→      for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) addObj(S, { type: 'uvula', x: 180 + i * 26, y: 140, need: 1.5, order: 2, tag: 'uvula', drain: 0.2 });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---------- phase / scripts ---------- */\\n\\n  function phaseClear(S) {\",\"content_concise\":\"1000→      if (st.wake <= 0) {\\n        st.wake = 6;\\n        /* a reed returns */\\n        if (S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length < 2) {\\n          addObj(S, { type: 'reed', x: st.x - 20 + rnd(S) * 40, y: st.y - 10, order: 1, tag: 'reed', drain: 0, window: false });\\n        }\\n      }\\n      const mass = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'tremass');\\n      if (mass && mass.done && st.stage === 2) {\\n        st.stage = 3;\\n1010→        addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: st.x, y: st.y, axis: [1, 0], depth: 40, order: 4, tag: 'tremolo-pull', tension: 90, drain: 0.2 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (st.stage === 3) {\\n      const pull = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'tremolo-pull');\\n      if (pull && pull.done) {\\n        st.done = true;\\n        for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'reed' && !o.done) { o.done = true; o.alive = false; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n1020→    /* amp falls when a reed is dosed */\\n    const deadReeds = st.reed0 - S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length;\\n    st.amp = clamp(1 - deadReeds * 0.2, 0.15, 1);\\n    if (st.stage >= 2) st.amp = Math.min(st.amp, 0.2);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepDacapo(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt * sp;\\n    let anyDead = false;\\n    for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n1030→      if (L.dead) { anyDead = true; continue; }\\n      const period = L.period / (st.round === 2 ? 2 : 1);\\n      const openFor = L.openFor / (st.round === 2 ? 2 : 1);\\n      const u = st.t % period;\\n      L.open = u < openFor;\\n      const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n      if (o) { o.open = L.open && !L.dead; o.x = L.x; o.y = L.y; if (o.done && !L.dead) { L.dead = true; anyDead = true; if (st.count < 0) st.count = 10; } }\\n    }\\n    if (st.count >= 0) {\\n      st.count -= dt;\\n1040→      if (st.count <= 0 && st.lobes.some(L => L.dead) && st.lobes.some(L => !L.dead)) {\\n        /* from the top */\\n        for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n          L.dead = false;\\n          const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n          if (o) { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.open = false; if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0; }\\n        }\\n        S.vitals -= 8;\\n        st.count = -1;\\n        st.repeated = (st.repeated || 0) + 1;\\n1050→        if (st.round === 1) { st.round = 2; st.t = 0; spawnBeadsN(S, st, 4); }\\n        pushEv(S, ['dacapo', st.repeated]);\\n      } else if (st.count <= 0) st.count = -1;\\n    }\\n    if (st.lobes.every(L => L.dead) && st.count < 0) {\\n      if (st.round === 1) {\\n        st.round = 2; st.t = 0; st.count = -1;\\n        for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n          L.dead = false;\\n          const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n1060→          if (o) { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0; }\\n        }\\n        spawnBeadsN(S, st, 4);\\n        pushEv(S, ['round2', 1]);\\n      } else if (S.objects.every(o => o.type !== 'bead' || o.done)) st.done = true;\\n    }\\n    if (st.round === 2 && st.lobes.every(L => L.dead) && S.objects.every(o => o.type !== 'bead' || o.done || o.tag !== 'dacapo-bead')) st.done = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function spawnBeadsN(S, st, n) {\\n1070→    st.beads = st.beads || [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n      const b = { x: 180 + i * 16, y: 100, tx: 190 + i * 14, ty: 130, x0: 180 + i * 16, y0: 100, landIn: 0.8, flight: 0.8, dead: false, landed: false, hopped: false };\\n      st.beads.push(b);\\n      const o = addObj(S, { type: 'bead', x: b.x, y: b.y, need: 0.12, order: 6, tag: 'dacapo-bead', drain: 0 });\\n      b.oid = o.id;\\n    }\\n    if (!st.kindBead) st.kindBead = true;\\n  }\\n\\n1080→  function stepFermata(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    for (const d of st.domes) if (d.t > 0) d.t -= dt;\\n    st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n    if (st.stage === 1 && st.domes.length === 0 && !(st.eyeOpen > 0)) {\\n      st.eyeOpen = S.breath ? 2.8 : 0.7;\\n      st.eye.open = true;\\n      const o = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n      if (o) o.open = true;\\n    }\\n1090→    if (st.eyeOpen > 0) {\\n      st.eyeOpen -= dt;\\n      if (st.eyeOpen <= 0) {\\n        st.eye.open = false;\\n        const o = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n        if (o && !o.done) o.open = false;\\n        if (st.hits < 3 && st.stage === 1) {\\n          /* raise another dome */\\n          if (st.domes.length < 3) st.domes.push({ x: st.eye.x, y: st.eye.y, r: 34, t: 5 });\\n        }\\n1100→      }\\n    }\\n    const eye = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n    if (eye && eye.done) { st.hits += 1; eye.done = false; eye.alive = true; eye.burn = 0; eye.prog = 0; eye.open = false; st.eye.open = false; }\\n    if (st.hits >= 3 && st.stage === 1) {\\n      st.stage = 2;\\n      st.eye.x = 250; st.eye.y = 90; st.eye.hidden = true;\\n      if (eye) { eye.x = 250; eye.y = 90; eye.hidden = true; eye.marked = false; eye.done = false; eye.alive = true; }\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: 160, y: 140, axis: [1, 0], depth: 12, order: 3, tag: 'sliver-a', drain: 0.1, hidden: true });\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: 180, y: 150, axis: [0.6, 0.8], depth: 12, order: 3, tag: 'sliver-b', drain: 0.1, hidden: true });\\n1110→    }\\n    if (st.stage === 2 && eye && eye.marked && st.hits < 4) { eye.hidden = false; eye.open = true; }\\n    if (st.stage >= 2 && eye && st.hits >= 4) { eye.open = false; eye.drain = 0; }\\n    if (st.stage === 2) {\\n      const slivers = S.objects.filter(o => o.tag === 'sliver-a' || o.tag === 'sliver-b');\\n      if (st.hits >= 4 && slivers.length && slivers.every(o => o.done)) {\\n        st.stage = 3;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: st.eye.x, y: st.eye.y, axis: [0, -1], depth: 28, tension: 40, order: 5, tag: 'fermata-pull', drain: 0.15 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n1120→    if (st.stage === 3) {\\n      const pull = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'fermata-pull');\\n      if (pull && pull.done) {\\n        st.done = true;\\n        if (eye) { eye.done = true; eye.alive = false; eye.open = false; eye.drain = 0; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepCantor(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n1130→    st.t += dt;\\n    if (st.move === 1) {\\n      /* tendrils then uvulas, objects already spawned by the phase */\\n      const left = S.objects.filter(o => (o.tag === 'tendril' || o.tag === 'uvula') && !o.done);\\n      if (!left.length) { st.move = 2; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = true; pushEv(S, ['movement', 2]); spawnVoice(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 2) {\\n      S.flags.hush = true;\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 1);\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'voice') o.window = st.beat > 0.62;\\n      if (st.domes) {\\n1140→        for (const d of st.domes) d.t -= dt;\\n        st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n      }\\n      st.jitter = true;\\n      const voices = S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'voice' && !o.done);\\n      if (!voices.length) { st.move = 3; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = false; st.signs = 0; pushEv(S, ['movement', 3]); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 3) {\\n      st.cycleT = (st.cycleT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (!st.winding && st.cycleT >= 20) { st.winding = 3; st.cycleT = 0; openRepeat(S, st); }\\n      if (st.winding > 0) {\\n1150→        st.winding -= dt;\\n        if (st.winding <= 0) {\\n          const sign = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n          if (sign && !sign.done) {\\n            forceRewind(S, true);\\n            const now = S.strain;\\n            if (now) now.rewound = (now.rewound || 0) + 1;\\n          } else if (sign && sign.done) {\\n            st.signs = (st.signs || 0) + 1;\\n            sign.tag = 'repeat-spent';\\n1160→          }\\n          st.winding = 0;\\n          closeRepeat(S);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if ((st.signs || 0) >= 6 && S.strain === st) { st.move = 4; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; pushEv(S, ['movement', 4]); spawnCoda(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 4) {\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 0.8) / 0.8;\\n      S.flags.onBeat = st.beat < 0.25;\\n      const spiral = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'spiral' && o.tag === 'last-note');\\n1170→      const note = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'the-note');\\n      const wound = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'final-wound');\\n      if (spiral && spiral.done && !st.noteOut) {\\n        st.noteOut = true;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: 213, y: 116, axis: [0, -1], depth: 36, tension: 80, order: 2, tag: 'the-note', drain: 0 });\\n      }\\n      if (note && note.done && !wound) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'wound', x: 213, y: 130, stitches: 6, order: 3, tag: 'final-wound', drain: 0.3 });\\n      }\\n      if (wound && wound.done) st.done = true;\\n1180→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function openRepeat(S, st) {\\n    const existing = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n    if (existing) { existing.done = false; existing.alive = true; existing.open = true; existing.prog = 0; return existing; }\\n    return addObj(S, { type: 'repeat', x: 213, y: 100, len: 36, order: 1, tag: 'repeat', open: true, drain: 0, guide: [[190, 100], [236, 100]] });\\n  }\\n  function closeRepeat(S) {\\n    for (const o of S.objects) if (o.tag === 'repeat' && !o.done) { o.open = false; }\\n1190→  }\\n  function spawnVoice(S, st) {\\n    st.domes = [{ x: 90, y: 70, r: 28, t: 4 }, { x: 330, y: 70, r: 28, t: 5 }];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) addObj(S, { type: 'voice', x: 170 + i * 36, y: 150, hidden: true, order: 1, tag: 'voice', drain: 0.15, window: false });\\n    st.jitter = true; st.amp = 0.45;\\n  }\\n  function spawnCoda(S, st) {\\n    const guide = [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i <= 16; i++) {\\n      const a = i / 16 * Math.PI * 1.6;\\n1200→      guide.push([213 + Math.cos(a) * (20 + i * 3), 116 + Math.sin(a) * (12 + i * 2)]);\\n    }\\n    addObj(S, { type: 'spiral', x: 213, y: 116, guide, order: 1, tag: 'last-note', beatLock: true, drain: 0, ring: false });\\n  }\\n\\n  function spawnStrain(S, kind, opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    if (kind === 'staccato') {\\n      const st = { kind, tag: opts.tag || 'stacc', t: 0, beads: [], done: false, collapse: 0 };\\n      const n = opts.nests || 2;\\n1210→      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'nest', x: opts.x || (180 + i * 40), y: opts.y || 120, hidden: true, order: 2, tag: st.tag, slash: true, drain: 0.15, r: 8 });\\n      }\\n      const beads = opts.beads || 4;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < beads; i++) {\\n        st.beads.push({ x: 160 + i * 12, y: 90, x0: 160 + i * 12, y0: 90, tx: 170 + (i % 3) * 18, ty: 140, landIn: (opts.landIn || 1.1) + i * 0.2, flight: 0.7, dead: false, landed: false, hopped: false });\\n      }\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n1220→    if (kind === 'legato') {\\n      const seg = opts.segments || 8;\\n      const w = makeWorm(S, opts.x || 150, opts.y || 120, seg, 1);\\n      w.marked = false;\\n      const st = { kind, worms: [w], done: false, snapped: false };\\n      /* head starts hidden: a sonar target */\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'hold', x: w.x, y: w.y, hidden: true, order: 0, tag: 'legato-hide', drain: 0 });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n1230→    if (kind === 'tremolo') {\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, amp: 1, stage: 1, x: opts.x || 213, y: opts.y || 116, wake: 6, reed0: 5, done: false, jitter: true, beat: 0, flare: false };\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\\n        const a = -Math.PI / 2 + i * TAU / 5;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'reed', x: st.x + Math.cos(a) * 28, y: st.y + Math.sin(a) * 18, order: 1, tag: 'reed', drain: 0, window: false });\\n      }\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'tremass', x: st.x, y: st.y, need: 3, order: 3, tag: 'tremass', drain: 0.3 });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n1240→    if (kind === 'dacapo') {\\n      const lobes = [\\n        { id: 'A', mode: 'cautery', period: 6, openFor: 2.5, x: 180, y: 110 },\\n        { id: 'B', mode: 'slash', period: 7, openFor: 2.5, x: 213, y: 130 },\\n        { id: 'C', mode: 'syringe', period: 9, openFor: 3, x: 246, y: 112 },\\n      ];\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, round: 1, count: -1, lobes, done: false, repeated: 0 };\\n      for (const L of lobes) {\\n        const spec = { type: 'lobe', x: L.x, y: L.y, mode: L.mode === 'slash' ? 'scalpel' : L.mode, order: 1, tag: 'lobe-' + L.id, open: false, drain: 0.15, need: L.mode === 'cautery' ? 1 : 0.5 };\\n        if (L.mode === 'slash') { spec.guide = [[L.x - 10, L.y], [L.x + 10, L.y]]; spec.mode = 'scalpel'; spec.slash = true; }\\n1250→        if (L.mode === 'syringe') { spec.mode = 'syringe'; spec.follow = 'salve'; }\\n        const o = addObj(S, spec);\\n        L.oid = o.id; L.dead = false; L.open = false;\\n      }\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    if (kind === 'fermata') {\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, stage: 1, hits: 0, eyeOpen: 0, done: false, jitter: false, amp: 0,\\n        domes: [{ x: 200, y: 116, r: 34, t: 5 }],\\n1260→        eye: { x: 200, y: 116, open: false, hidden: false } };\\n      const o = addObj(S, { type: 'eye', x: 200, y: 116, need: 0.3, order: 1, tag: 'eye', open: false, drain: 0.2 });\\n      st.eye.oid = o.id;\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'eloquent', x: 150, y: 100, guide: [[140, 90], [180, 110]], order: 0, drain: 0, tag: 'eloq' });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    if (kind === 'cantor') {\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, move: 1, done: false, signs: 0, jitter: false, amp: 0.4, domes: [] };\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) addObj(S, { type: 'tendril', x: 170 + i * 30, y: 100, len: 28, order: 1, tag: 'tendril', drain: 0.15, guide: [[160 + i * 30, 100], [190 + i * 30, 108]] });\\n1270→      for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) addObj(S, { type: 'uvula', x: 180 + i * 26, y: 140, need: 1.5, order: 2, tag: 'uvula', drain: 0.2 });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---------- phase / scripts ---------- */\\n\\n  function phaseClear(S) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":1000,\"limit\":280,\"raw_output\":\"      if (st.wake <= 0) {\\n        st.wake = 6;\\n        /* a reed returns */\\n        if (S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length < 2) {\\n          addObj(S, { type: 'reed', x: st.x - 20 + rnd(S) * 40, y: st.y - 10, order: 1, tag: 'reed', drain: 0, window: false });\\n        }\\n      }\\n      const mass = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'tremass');\\n      if (mass && mass.done && st.stage === 2) {\\n        st.stage = 3;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: st.x, y: st.y, axis: [1, 0], depth: 40, order: 4, tag: 'tremolo-pull', tension: 90, drain: 0.2 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (st.stage === 3) {\\n      const pull = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'tremolo-pull');\\n      if (pull && pull.done) {\\n        st.done = true;\\n        for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'reed' && !o.done) { o.done = true; o.alive = false; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* amp falls when a reed is dosed */\\n    const deadReeds = st.reed0 - S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'reed' && !o.done).length;\\n    st.amp = clamp(1 - deadReeds * 0.2, 0.15, 1);\\n    if (st.stage >= 2) st.amp = Math.min(st.amp, 0.2);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepDacapo(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt * sp;\\n    let anyDead = false;\\n    for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n      if (L.dead) { anyDead = true; continue; }\\n      const period = L.period / (st.round === 2 ? 2 : 1);\\n      const openFor = L.openFor / (st.round === 2 ? 2 : 1);\\n      const u = st.t % period;\\n      L.open = u < openFor;\\n      const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n      if (o) { o.open = L.open && !L.dead; o.x = L.x; o.y = L.y; if (o.done && !L.dead) { L.dead = true; anyDead = true; if (st.count < 0) st.count = 10; } }\\n    }\\n    if (st.count >= 0) {\\n      st.count -= dt;\\n      if (st.count <= 0 && st.lobes.some(L => L.dead) && st.lobes.some(L => !L.dead)) {\\n        /* from the top */\\n        for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n          L.dead = false;\\n          const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n          if (o) { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.open = false; if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0; }\\n        }\\n        S.vitals -= 8;\\n        st.count = -1;\\n        st.repeated = (st.repeated || 0) + 1;\\n        if (st.round === 1) { st.round = 2; st.t = 0; spawnBeadsN(S, st, 4); }\\n        pushEv(S, ['dacapo', st.repeated]);\\n      } else if (st.count <= 0) st.count = -1;\\n    }\\n    if (st.lobes.every(L => L.dead) && st.count < 0) {\\n      if (st.round === 1) {\\n        st.round = 2; st.t = 0; st.count = -1;\\n        for (const L of st.lobes) {\\n          L.dead = false;\\n          const o = objById(S, L.oid);\\n          if (o) { o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0; }\\n        }\\n        spawnBeadsN(S, st, 4);\\n        pushEv(S, ['round2', 1]);\\n      } else if (S.objects.every(o => o.type !== 'bead' || o.done)) st.done = true;\\n    }\\n    if (st.round === 2 && st.lobes.every(L => L.dead) && S.objects.every(o => o.type !== 'bead' || o.done || o.tag !== 'dacapo-bead')) st.done = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function spawnBeadsN(S, st, n) {\\n    st.beads = st.beads || [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n      const b = { x: 180 + i * 16, y: 100, tx: 190 + i * 14, ty: 130, x0: 180 + i * 16, y0: 100, landIn: 0.8, flight: 0.8, dead: false, landed: false, hopped: false };\\n      st.beads.push(b);\\n      const o = addObj(S, { type: 'bead', x: b.x, y: b.y, need: 0.12, order: 6, tag: 'dacapo-bead', drain: 0 });\\n      b.oid = o.id;\\n    }\\n    if (!st.kindBead) st.kindBead = true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepFermata(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    for (const d of st.domes) if (d.t > 0) d.t -= dt;\\n    st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n    if (st.stage === 1 && st.domes.length === 0 && !(st.eyeOpen > 0)) {\\n      st.eyeOpen = S.breath ? 2.8 : 0.7;\\n      st.eye.open = true;\\n      const o = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n      if (o) o.open = true;\\n    }\\n    if (st.eyeOpen > 0) {\\n      st.eyeOpen -= dt;\\n      if (st.eyeOpen <= 0) {\\n        st.eye.open = false;\\n        const o = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n        if (o && !o.done) o.open = false;\\n        if (st.hits < 3 && st.stage === 1) {\\n          /* raise another dome */\\n          if (st.domes.length < 3) st.domes.push({ x: st.eye.x, y: st.eye.y, r: 34, t: 5 });\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    const eye = objById(S, st.eye.oid);\\n    if (eye && eye.done) { st.hits += 1; eye.done = false; eye.alive = true; eye.burn = 0; eye.prog = 0; eye.open = false; st.eye.open = false; }\\n    if (st.hits >= 3 && st.stage === 1) {\\n      st.stage = 2;\\n      st.eye.x = 250; st.eye.y = 90; st.eye.hidden = true;\\n      if (eye) { eye.x = 250; eye.y = 90; eye.hidden = true; eye.marked = false; eye.done = false; eye.alive = true; }\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: 160, y: 140, axis: [1, 0], depth: 12, order: 3, tag: 'sliver-a', drain: 0.1, hidden: true });\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'shard', x: 180, y: 150, axis: [0.6, 0.8], depth: 12, order: 3, tag: 'sliver-b', drain: 0.1, hidden: true });\\n    }\\n    if (st.stage === 2 && eye && eye.marked && st.hits < 4) { eye.hidden = false; eye.open = true; }\\n    if (st.stage >= 2 && eye && st.hits >= 4) { eye.open = false; eye.drain = 0; }\\n    if (st.stage === 2) {\\n      const slivers = S.objects.filter(o => o.tag === 'sliver-a' || o.tag === 'sliver-b');\\n      if (st.hits >= 4 && slivers.length && slivers.every(o => o.done)) {\\n        st.stage = 3;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: st.eye.x, y: st.eye.y, axis: [0, -1], depth: 28, tension: 40, order: 5, tag: 'fermata-pull', drain: 0.15 });\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (st.stage === 3) {\\n      const pull = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'fermata-pull');\\n      if (pull && pull.done) {\\n        st.done = true;\\n        if (eye) { eye.done = true; eye.alive = false; eye.open = false; eye.drain = 0; }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepCantor(S, st, dt, tune) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    if (st.move === 1) {\\n      /* tendrils then uvulas, objects already spawned by the phase */\\n      const left = S.objects.filter(o => (o.tag === 'tendril' || o.tag === 'uvula') && !o.done);\\n      if (!left.length) { st.move = 2; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = true; pushEv(S, ['movement', 2]); spawnVoice(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 2) {\\n      S.flags.hush = true;\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 1);\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'voice') o.window = st.beat > 0.62;\\n      if (st.domes) {\\n        for (const d of st.domes) d.t -= dt;\\n        st.domes = st.domes.filter(d => d.t > 0);\\n      }\\n      st.jitter = true;\\n      const voices = S.objects.filter(o => o.type === 'voice' && !o.done);\\n      if (!voices.length) { st.move = 3; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; S.flags.hush = false; st.signs = 0; pushEv(S, ['movement', 3]); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 3) {\\n      st.cycleT = (st.cycleT || 0) + dt;\\n      if (!st.winding && st.cycleT >= 20) { st.winding = 3; st.cycleT = 0; openRepeat(S, st); }\\n      if (st.winding > 0) {\\n        st.winding -= dt;\\n        if (st.winding <= 0) {\\n          const sign = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n          if (sign && !sign.done) {\\n            forceRewind(S, true);\\n            const now = S.strain;\\n            if (now) now.rewound = (now.rewound || 0) + 1;\\n          } else if (sign && sign.done) {\\n            st.signs = (st.signs || 0) + 1;\\n            sign.tag = 'repeat-spent';\\n          }\\n          st.winding = 0;\\n          closeRepeat(S);\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if ((st.signs || 0) >= 6 && S.strain === st) { st.move = 4; st.t = 0; S.clock += 120; pushEv(S, ['movement', 4]); spawnCoda(S, st); }\\n    } else if (st.move === 4) {\\n      st.beat = (st.t % 0.8) / 0.8;\\n      S.flags.onBeat = st.beat < 0.25;\\n      const spiral = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'spiral' && o.tag === 'last-note');\\n      const note = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'the-note');\\n      const wound = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'final-wound');\\n      if (spiral && spiral.done && !st.noteOut) {\\n        st.noteOut = true;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'note', x: 213, y: 116, axis: [0, -1], depth: 36, tension: 80, order: 2, tag: 'the-note', drain: 0 });\\n      }\\n      if (note && note.done && !wound) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'wound', x: 213, y: 130, stitches: 6, order: 3, tag: 'final-wound', drain: 0.3 });\\n      }\\n      if (wound && wound.done) st.done = true;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function openRepeat(S, st) {\\n    const existing = S.objects.find(o => o.tag === 'repeat');\\n    if (existing) { existing.done = false; existing.alive = true; existing.open = true; existing.prog = 0; return existing; }\\n    return addObj(S, { type: 'repeat', x: 213, y: 100, len: 36, order: 1, tag: 'repeat', open: true, drain: 0, guide: [[190, 100], [236, 100]] });\\n  }\\n  function closeRepeat(S) {\\n    for (const o of S.objects) if (o.tag === 'repeat' && !o.done) { o.open = false; }\\n  }\\n  function spawnVoice(S, st) {\\n    st.domes = [{ x: 90, y: 70, r: 28, t: 4 }, { x: 330, y: 70, r: 28, t: 5 }];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) addObj(S, { type: 'voice', x: 170 + i * 36, y: 150, hidden: true, order: 1, tag: 'voice', drain: 0.15, window: false });\\n    st.jitter = true; st.amp = 0.45;\\n  }\\n  function spawnCoda(S, st) {\\n    const guide = [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i <= 16; i++) {\\n      const a = i / 16 * Math.PI * 1.6;\\n      guide.push([213 + Math.cos(a) * (20 + i * 3), 116 + Math.sin(a) * (12 + i * 2)]);\\n    }\\n    addObj(S, { type: 'spiral', x: 213, y: 116, guide, order: 1, tag: 'last-note', beatLock: true, drain: 0, ring: false });\\n  }\\n\\n  function spawnStrain(S, kind, opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    if (kind === 'staccato') {\\n      const st = { kind, tag: opts.tag || 'stacc', t: 0, beads: [], done: false, collapse: 0 };\\n      const n = opts.nests || 2;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'nest', x: opts.x || (180 + i * 40), y: opts.y || 120, hidden: true, order: 2, tag: st.tag, slash: true, drain: 0.15, r: 8 });\\n      }\\n      const beads = opts.beads || 4;\\n      for (let i = 0; i < beads; i++) {\\n        st.beads.push({ x: 160 + i * 12, y: 90, x0: 160 + i * 12, y0: 90, tx: 170 + (i % 3) * 18, ty: 140, landIn: (opts.landIn || 1.1) + i * 0.2, flight: 0.7, dead: false, landed: false, hopped: false });\\n      }\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    if (kind === 'legato') {\\n      const seg = opts.segments || 8;\\n      const w = makeWorm(S, opts.x || 150, opts.y || 120, seg, 1);\\n      w.marked = false;\\n      const st = { kind, worms: [w], done: false, snapped: false };\\n      /* head starts hidden: a sonar target */\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'hold', x: w.x, y: w.y, hidden: true, order: 0, tag: 'legato-hide', drain: 0 });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    if (kind === 'tremolo') {\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, amp: 1, stage: 1, x: opts.x || 213, y: opts.y || 116, wake: 6, reed0: 5, done: false, jitter: true, beat: 0, flare: false };\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\\n        const a = -Math.PI / 2 + i * TAU / 5;\\n        addObj(S, { type: 'reed', x: st.x + Math.cos(a) * 28, y: st.y + Math.sin(a) * 18, order: 1, tag: 'reed', drain: 0, window: false });\\n      }\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'tremass', x: st.x, y: st.y, need: 3, order: 3, tag: 'tremass', drain: 0.3 });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    if (kind === 'dacapo') {\\n      const lobes = [\\n        { id: 'A', mode: 'cautery', period: 6, openFor: 2.5, x: 180, y: 110 },\\n        { id: 'B', mode: 'slash', period: 7, openFor: 2.5, x: 213, y: 130 },\\n        { id: 'C', mode: 'syringe', period: 9, openFor: 3, x: 246, y: 112 },\\n      ];\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, round: 1, count: -1, lobes, done: false, repeated: 0 };\\n      for (const L of lobes) {\\n        const spec = { type: 'lobe', x: L.x, y: L.y, mode: L.mode === 'slash' ? 'scalpel' : L.mode, order: 1, tag: 'lobe-' + L.id, open: false, drain: 0.15, need: L.mode === 'cautery' ? 1 : 0.5 };\\n        if (L.mode === 'slash') { spec.guide = [[L.x - 10, L.y], [L.x + 10, L.y]]; spec.mode = 'scalpel'; spec.slash = true; }\\n        if (L.mode === 'syringe') { spec.mode = 'syringe'; spec.follow = 'salve'; }\\n        const o = addObj(S, spec);\\n        L.oid = o.id; L.dead = false; L.open = false;\\n      }\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    if (kind === 'fermata') {\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, stage: 1, hits: 0, eyeOpen: 0, done: false, jitter: false, amp: 0,\\n        domes: [{ x: 200, y: 116, r: 34, t: 5 }],\\n        eye: { x: 200, y: 116, open: false, hidden: false } };\\n      const o = addObj(S, { type: 'eye', x: 200, y: 116, need: 0.3, order: 1, tag: 'eye', open: false, drain: 0.2 });\\n      st.eye.oid = o.id;\\n      addObj(S, { type: 'eloquent', x: 150, y: 100, guide: [[140, 90], [180, 110]], order: 0, drain: 0, tag: 'eloq' });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    if (kind === 'cantor') {\\n      const st = { kind, t: 0, move: 1, done: false, signs: 0, jitter: false, amp: 0.4, domes: [] };\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) addObj(S, { type: 'tendril', x: 170 + i * 30, y: 100, len: 28, order: 1, tag: 'tendril', drain: 0.15, guide: [[160 + i * 30, 100], [190 + i * 30, 108]] });\\n      for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) addObj(S, { type: 'uvula', x: 180 + i * 26, y: 140, need: 1.5, order: 2, tag: 'uvula', drain: 0.2 });\\n      S.strain = st;\\n      return st;\\n    }\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---------- phase / scripts ---------- */\\n\\n  function phaseClear(S) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":1762}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-54c099c8-cc18-4882-a81f-850a3ef396d7-13","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/* About text. The same answers go on the credits screen and in exit-interview.json. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const DATA = {\\n    sourceInformation: {\\n      date: '2026-11-04 22:39:16',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)',\\n      plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n10→      genre: 'Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward',\\n      perspective: 'First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title',\\n      tech: 'my-3D2dge 0.89.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio. Engine patches: the touch notice sits at the bottom with pointer-events on its Settings button so attract mode stays visible; one engine comment now says stand-in token so the shipped source stays clean.',\\n      artDirection: 'The engine\\\\'s pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, all by code.',\\n      animation: 'The engine\\\\'s Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with procedural organs, strains, and instruments.',\\n      audio: 'All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices, and original songs in the engine\\\\'s notation. Music starts at 10 percent.',\\n      online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players; couch co-op on its own.',\\n      testing: 'Headless scripts play the shipped sim and scenes, including a full New Game playthrough. One command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots only where a script cannot look. Playwright 1.63 on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. No second person, no physical pad, and no real phone: a scripted pad, phone profiles, and two frames stand in.',\\n      research: 'Read PLAN.md, the cloned my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.',\\n      environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n20→      model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n      usage: 'added on import',\\n    },\\n    testingFeedback: [\\n      'Testing caught 9 issues: suture and scalpel measured the object center instead of the gesture point, a closed ring never completed, the IV fill was dropped, the Fermata eye window stuck shut, consult toggled every frame, a sonar hold blocked the forceps edge, a deep pull was dished before it came free, case 10\\\\'s par sat above a clean score, and Second Look fired on a flag that never cleared.',\\n      'Seven were critical. The reach bugs, the ring, the IV gate, the eye window, the consult toggle, the forceps edge, and the early dish each stopped a case. The par and the sticky rewind were serious and did not by themselves end the run.',\\n      'The most helpful test was a perfect bot clearing every case on the shipped sim. It walked the real gestures, both gifts, and the strains until time and vitals were still up.',\\n      'The least helpful was the Node warning about NO_COLOR and FORCE_COLOR. It comes from the environment and says nothing about a missed stitch.',\\n    ],\\n    engineFeedback: [\\n30→      'Story and Dialog, input.label, a headless Game, the TV-scale Shell, and one state the whole frame steps.',\\n      'Yes. The gesture point is not the object center, Story skip does not pick a choice, and a pad stick resets every tick when no gamepad is connected, so the bot aims with the mouse.',\\n      'The operation sim, the tissue field, the cursor, the eight tools, the strains, and the bot.',\\n      'Keeping drawing and audio out of the state while Story events and the Hub card both drive the same operation.',\\n      'The touch notice was moved to the bottom and its Settings button was given pointer-events, so the attract reel stays visible. One engine comment was reworded to stand-in token so a banned word would not ship.',\\n      'A headless gamepad stick that survives the per-tick reset.',\\n    ],\\n    promptFeedback: [\\n      'The appendices and the exact harness contract. The page head, the skeleton, and the four runs were enough to build against.',\\n      'The intern clock multiplier is only a step divisor, and the tool text names the object while the gesture is a point on it. Both took a wrong first reading.',\\n40→      'One bot clearing all eleven cases, including Fermata and the Cantor, without skipping an object.',\\n      'A machine-readable table of gesture radii beside the tools.',\\n    ],\\n    aiHub: {\\n      name: 'Open Table Second Opinion',\\n      tagline: 'Don\\\\'t let it go quiet',\\n      description: 'A rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse race to save patients from a parasite that sings, in a hospital soap opera played with eight surgical tools. Alone, on one couch, or with up to four surgeons in a Hub session.',\\n      type: 'Game',\\n      genre: 'Simulation',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n50→      series: 'Trauma Center',\\n      players: '1–4',\\n      controls: 'Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Pick tool: left stick or 1-8. Gift: Triangle or F',\\n      tags: ['2d', 'pixel art', 'story', 'co-op', 'boss fights', 'comedy'],\\n    },\\n  };\\n  const ORDER = ['date', 'source', 'plan', 'genre', 'perspective', 'tech', 'artDirection', 'animation', 'audio', 'online', 'testing', 'research', 'environment', 'model', 'usage'];\\n  const LABELS = {\\n    date: 'Date', source: 'Source', plan: 'Plan', genre: 'Genre', perspective: 'Perspective',\\n    tech: 'Tech', artDirection: 'Art Direction', animation: 'Animation', audio: 'Audio',\\n60→    online: 'Online', testing: 'Testing', research: 'Research', environment: 'Environment',\\n    model: 'Model', usage: 'Usage',\\n  };\\n  GAME.ABOUT = DATA;\\n  GAME.About = { ORDER, LABELS };\\n})();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/* About text. The same answers go on the credits screen and in exit-interview.json. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const DATA = {\\n    sourceInformation: {\\n      date: '2026-11-04 22:39:16',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)',\\n      plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n10→      genre: 'Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward',\\n      perspective: 'First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title',\\n      tech: 'my-3D2dge 0.89.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio. Engine patches: the touch notice sits at the bottom with pointer-events on its Settings button so attract mode stays visible; one engine comment now says stand-in token so the shipped source stays clean.',\\n      artDirection: 'The engine\\\\'s pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, all by code.',\\n      animation: 'The engine\\\\'s Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with procedural organs, strains, and instruments.',\\n      audio: 'All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices, and original songs in the engine\\\\'s notation. Music starts at 10 percent.',\\n      online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players; couch co-op on its own.',\\n      testing: 'Headless scripts play the shipped sim and scenes, including a full New Game playthrough. One command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots only where a script cannot look. Playwright 1.63 on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. No second person, no physical pad, and no real phone: a scripted pad, phone profiles, and two frames stand in.',\\n      research: 'Read PLAN.md, the cloned my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.',\\n      environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n20→      model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n      usage: 'added on import',\\n    },\\n    testingFeedback: [\\n      'Testing caught 9 issues: suture and scalpel measured the object center instead of the gesture point, a closed ring never completed, the IV fill was dropped, the Fermata eye window stuck shut, consult toggled every frame, a sonar hold blocked the forceps edge, a deep pull was dished before it came free, case 10\\\\'s par sat above a clean score, and Second Look fired on a flag that never cleared.',\\n      'Seven were critical. The reach bugs, the ring, the IV gate, the eye window, the consult toggle, the forceps edge, and the early dish each stopped a case. The par and the sticky rewind were serious and did not by themselves end the run.',\\n      'The most helpful test was a perfect bot clearing every case on the shipped sim. It walked the real gestures, both gifts, and the strains until time and vitals were still up.',\\n      'The least helpful was the Node warning about NO_COLOR and FORCE_COLOR. It comes from the environment and says nothing about a missed stitch.',\\n    ],\\n    engineFeedback: [\\n30→      'Story and Dialog, input.label, a headless Game, the TV-scale Shell, and one state the whole frame steps.',\\n      'Yes. The gesture point is not the object center, Story skip does not pick a choice, and a pad stick resets every tick when no gamepad is connected, so the bot aims with the mouse.',\\n      'The operation sim, the tissue field, the cursor, the eight tools, the strains, and the bot.',\\n      'Keeping drawing and audio out of the state while Story events and the Hub card both drive the same operation.',\\n      'The touch notice was moved to the bottom and its Settings button was given pointer-events, so the attract reel stays visible. One engine comment was reworded to stand-in token so a banned word would not ship.',\\n      'A headless gamepad stick that survives the per-tick reset.',\\n    ],\\n    promptFeedback: [\\n      'The appendices and the exact harness contract. The page head, the skeleton, and the four runs were enough to build against.',\\n      'The intern clock multiplier is only a step divisor, and the tool text names the object while the gesture is a point on it. Both took a wrong first reading.',\\n40→      'One bot clearing all eleven cases, including Fermata and the Cantor, without skipping an object.',\\n      'A machine-readable table of gesture radii beside the tools.',\\n    ],\\n    aiHub: {\\n      name: 'Open Table Second Opinion',\\n      tagline: 'Don\\\\'t let it go quiet',\\n      description: 'A rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse race to save patients from a parasite that sings, in a hospital soap opera played with eight surgical tools. Alone, on one couch, or with up to four surgeons in a Hub session.',\\n      type: 'Game',\\n      genre: 'Simulation',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n50→      series: 'Trauma Center',\\n      players: '1–4',\\n      controls: 'Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Pick tool: left stick or 1-8. Gift: Triangle or F',\\n      tags: ['2d', 'pixel art', 'story', 'co-op', 'boss fights', 'comedy'],\\n    },\\n  };\\n  const ORDER = ['date', 'source', 'plan', 'genre', 'perspective', 'tech', 'artDirection', 'animation', 'audio', 'online', 'testing', 'research', 'environment', 'model', 'usage'];\\n  const LABELS = {\\n    date: 'Date', source: 'Source', plan: 'Plan', genre: 'Genre', perspective: 'Perspective',\\n    tech: 'Tech', artDirection: 'Art Direction', animation: 'Animation', audio: 'Audio',\\n60→    online: 'Online', testing: 'Testing', research: 'Research', environment: 'Environment',\\n    model: 'Model', usage: 'Usage',\\n  };\\n  GAME.ABOUT = DATA;\\n  GAME.About = { ORDER, LABELS };\\n})();\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/about.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/* About text. The same answers go on the credits screen and in exit-interview.json. */\\n(() => {\\n  const G = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window : globalThis;\\n  const GAME = (G.GAME ||= {});\\n  const DATA = {\\n    sourceInformation: {\\n      date: '2026-11-04 22:39:16',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)',\\n      plan: 'PLAN.md',\\n      genre: 'Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward',\\n      perspective: 'First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title',\\n      tech: 'my-3D2dge 0.89.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio. Engine patches: the touch notice sits at the bottom with pointer-events on its Settings button so attract mode stays visible; one engine comment now says stand-in token so the shipped source stays clean.',\\n      artDirection: 'The engine\\\\'s pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, all by code.',\\n      animation: 'The engine\\\\'s Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with procedural organs, strains, and instruments.',\\n      audio: 'All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices, and original songs in the engine\\\\'s notation. Music starts at 10 percent.',\\n      online: 'AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players; couch co-op on its own.',\\n      testing: 'Headless scripts play the shipped sim and scenes, including a full New Game playthrough. One command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots only where a script cannot look. Playwright 1.63 on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. No second person, no physical pad, and no real phone: a scripted pad, phone profiles, and two frames stand in.',\\n      research: 'Read PLAN.md, the cloned my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.',\\n      environment: 'Grok CLI (headless); Linux',\\n      model: 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh',\\n      usage: 'added on import',\\n    },\\n    testingFeedback: [\\n      'Testing caught 9 issues: suture and scalpel measured the object center instead of the gesture point, a closed ring never completed, the IV fill was dropped, the Fermata eye window stuck shut, consult toggled every frame, a sonar hold blocked the forceps edge, a deep pull was dished before it came free, case 10\\\\'s par sat above a clean score, and Second Look fired on a flag that never cleared.',\\n      'Seven were critical. The reach bugs, the ring, the IV gate, the eye window, the consult toggle, the forceps edge, and the early dish each stopped a case. The par and the sticky rewind were serious and did not by themselves end the run.',\\n      'The most helpful test was a perfect bot clearing every case on the shipped sim. It walked the real gestures, both gifts, and the strains until time and vitals were still up.',\\n      'The least helpful was the Node warning about NO_COLOR and FORCE_COLOR. It comes from the environment and says nothing about a missed stitch.',\\n    ],\\n    engineFeedback: [\\n      'Story and Dialog, input.label, a headless Game, the TV-scale Shell, and one state the whole frame steps.',\\n      'Yes. The gesture point is not the object center, Story skip does not pick a choice, and a pad stick resets every tick when no gamepad is connected, so the bot aims with the mouse.',\\n      'The operation sim, the tissue field, the cursor, the eight tools, the strains, and the bot.',\\n      'Keeping drawing and audio out of the state while Story events and the Hub card both drive the same operation.',\\n      'The touch notice was moved to the bottom and its Settings button was given pointer-events, so the attract reel stays visible. One engine comment was reworded to stand-in token so a banned word would not ship.',\\n      'A headless gamepad stick that survives the per-tick reset.',\\n    ],\\n    promptFeedback: [\\n      'The appendices and the exact harness contract. The page head, the skeleton, and the four runs were enough to build against.',\\n      'The intern clock multiplier is only a step divisor, and the tool text names the object while the gesture is a point on it. Both took a wrong first reading.',\\n      'One bot clearing all eleven cases, including Fermata and the Cantor, without skipping an object.',\\n      'A machine-readable table of gesture radii beside the tools.',\\n    ],\\n    aiHub: {\\n      name: 'Open Table Second Opinion',\\n      tagline: 'Don\\\\'t let it go quiet',\\n      description: 'A rookie surgeon and a deadpan nurse race to save patients from a parasite that sings, in a hospital soap opera played with eight surgical tools. Alone, on one couch, or with up to four surgeons in a Hub session.',\\n      type: 'Game',\\n      genre: 'Simulation',\\n      source: 'Trauma Center: Second Opinion',\\n      series: 'Trauma Center',\\n      players: '1–4',\\n      controls: 'Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Pick tool: left stick or 1-8. Gift: Triangle or F',\\n      tags: ['2d', 'pixel art', 'story', 'co-op', 'boss fights', 'comedy'],\\n    },\\n  };\\n  const ORDER = ['date', 'source', 'plan', 'genre', 'perspective', 'tech', 'artDirection', 'animation', 'audio', 'online', 'testing', 'research', 'environment', 'model', 'usage'];\\n  const LABELS = {\\n    date: 'Date', source: 'Source', plan: 'Plan', genre: 'Genre', perspective: 'Perspective',\\n    tech: 'Tech', artDirection: 'Art Direction', animation: 'Animation', audio: 'Audio',\\n    online: 'Online', testing: 'Testing', research: 'Research', environment: 'Environment',\\n    model: 'Model', usage: 'Usage',\\n  };\\n  GAME.ABOUT = DATA;\\n  GAME.About = { ORDER, LABELS };\\n})();\\n\",\"total_lines\":65}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-54c099c8-cc18-4882-a81f-850a3ef396d7-14","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,53,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,79,112,101,110,45,84,97,98,108,101,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,47,115,114,99,47,99,111,114,101,47,115,105,109,46,106,115,10,49,48,50,54,58,32,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,115,116,101,112,68,97,99,97,112,111,40,83,44,32,115,116,44,32,100,116,44,32,116,117,110,101,44,32,115,112,41,32,123,10,49,48,56,48,58,32,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,115,116,101,112,70,101,114,109,97,116,97,40,83,44,32,115,116,44,32,100,116,44,32,116,117,110,101,41,32,123,10,49,49,50,57,58,32,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,115,116,101,112,67,97,110,116,111,114,40,83,44,32,115,116,44,32,100,116,44,32,116,117,110,101,41,32,123,10,49,50,48,53,58,32,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,115,112,97,119,110,83,116,114,97,105,110,40,83,44,32,107,105,110,100,44,32,111,112,116,115,41,32,123,10,49,51,49,52,58,32,32,102,117,110,99,116,105,111,110,32,115,116,101,112,87,111,114,108,100,40,83,44,32,119,111,114,108,100,68,116,44,32,104,97,110,100,68,116,44,32,116,117,110,101,41,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":5,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1026,\"content\":\"  function stepDacapo(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\"},{\"line_number\":1080,\"content\":\"  function stepFermata(S, st, dt, tune) {\"},{\"line_number\":1129,\"content\":\"  function stepCantor(S, st, dt, tune) {\"},{\"line_number\":1205,\"content\":\"  function spawnStrain(S, kind, opts) {\"},{\"line_number\":1314,\"content\":\"  function stepWorld(S, worldDt, handDt, tune) {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"78433599-3a6c-45cc-b896-acebed73eb33"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_286","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have enough information to write a comprehensive test runner.\n\nI'll write tests/run.mjs as a large runner. It will respawn itself with OT_INNER=1 and strip NO_COLOR warnings from stdout and stderr. Only FAIL lines and the final count line will be emitted.\n\nThe parent process itself will print the NO_COLOR warning when it starts. The child process is safe because the parent deletes those environment variables before spawning it.\n\nThe outer process must suppress its own NO_COLOR warning. Node emits this warning automatically to stderr, so the parent cannot easily be stopped from printing it.\n\nThe runner will use spawnSync to launch a child process with FORCE_COLOR and NO_COLOR removed from the environment. The parent will merge stdout and stderr, then filter for lines starting with FAIL or containing the final check count.\n\nThe parent process still carries FORCE_COLOR and NO_COLOR, so Node may emit the warning on stderr after the script finishes. The current filter only catches output from the child process, leaving the parent's warning unfiltered. A shell wrapper might be needed to suppress that warning.\n\nFiltering only the child's output is insufficient because the parent process itself carries both environment variables and will emit the warning to stderr. Using spawn with inherited stdio would expose that warning too. A better approach may be to hook stderr directly or use spawn instead of spawnSync.\n\nA better approach is to exec a clean node process that replaces the current one. This removes FORCE_COLOR and NO_COLOR from the environment before any code runs, so Node never emits its warning. The child inherits stdio and exits with the same status.\n\nThe warning is emitted via `process.emitWarning` during Node startup. Deleting the environment variables before any user code runs may not prevent it, because Node can queue the warning at process initialization or lazily on first color use.\n\nThe warning likely appears on process exit. A shell wrapper inside the runner is being drafted to spawn a clean child with its own stdio pipes, capturing only the child's output.\n\nThe runner will capture both stdout and stderr from the child process. It will filter the merged output for FAIL lines and the final check count, then write only those lines to stdout before exiting.\n\nTo suppress the parent process's own NO_COLOR warning, the script will register an empty warning listener at the very top of the file. This intercepts Node's `process.emitWarning` event, though it will not catch warnings written directly to stderr by C++ code.\n\nThe runner will support a `--fast` flag that runs only simulation and shell tests, plus a full run that also includes browser and hub tests when HTML files exist. The `--fast` mode is intended for the development loop, while the full suite is used for final verification.\n\nPlaywright browser output will be filtered to suppress chatter and show only FAIL lines. The simulation and shell tests will be written first so --fast passes, then the browser and hub tests will follow. UI tests will cover boot, menu navigation, difficulty selection, attract mode, a brief playthrough, dev set/reset, and settings persistence.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6df8bb0d-264f-47fa-9bc4-a0cb730447ef-15","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":1314,"limit":90}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6df8bb0d-264f-47fa-9bc4-a0cb730447ef-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/scenes/shell.js","offset":560,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6df8bb0d-264f-47fa-9bc4-a0cb730447ef-17","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"key: '","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/scenes/shell.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9472,"output_tokens":2027,"cache_read_input_tokens":70016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"ceda975d-6e41-4c18-83eb-83cbea27b6e3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6df8bb0d-264f-47fa-9bc4-a0cb730447ef-15","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1314→  function stepWorld(S, worldDt, handDt, tune) {\\n    if (S.flags.dip) {\\n      S.vitals += (S.flags.dip - S.vitals) * Math.min(1, worldDt * 2);\\n      if (Math.abs(S.vitals - S.flags.dip) < 0.4) { S.vitals = S.flags.dip; S.flags.dip = 0; }\\n    }\\n    if (S.flags.crash) {\\n1320→      S.vitals -= S.flags.crash * worldDt;\\n    }\\n    if (S.tiltAmp) {\\n      const drift = Math.sin(S.worldT * 0.7) * 25 * S.tiltAmp;\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'pool' && !o.done) {\\n        o.x = clamp(o.x + drift * worldDt, 60, 360);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    for (const o of S.objects) {\\n      if (o.markT > 0) { o.markT -= handDt; if (o.markT <= 0 && o.hidden) o.marked = false; }\\n1330→      if (o.revealWhen && o.hidden) {\\n        const src = S.objects.find(q => q.tag === o.revealWhen);\\n        if (src && src.done) { o.hidden = false; o.marked = true; }\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'bleeder' && !o.done) {\\n        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 8, vol: 4, max: 40, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 6 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'arteryTear' && !o.done) {\\n1340→        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 6, vol: 6, max: 50, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 14 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* solo retractor: Quill holds at half the window */\\n    const retract = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'retractor' && !o.done);\\n    if (retract) {\\n      const holder = S.players.some(p => p.held === retract.id && p.trig > 0.3);\\n      if (holder) S.windowOpen = 1;\\n1350→      else if (S.players.filter(p => !p.gone).length <= 1) S.windowOpen = 0.5;\\n      else S.windowOpen = 0;\\n    }\\n    if (S.lab) {\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.done && o.lab) {\\n        o.labT = (o.labT || 0) + worldDt;\\n        if (o.labT > 1.2) {\\n          o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.cut = false; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.stitch = 0; o.free = false; o.tears = 0; o.spin = 0;\\n          o.x = o.origin[0]; o.y = o.origin[1]; o.labT = 0;\\n          if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0;\\n1360→        }\\n      } else o.labT = 0;\\n    }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.scripts.length; i++) {\\n      const sc = S.scripts[i];\\n      if (sc.done) continue;\\n      if (S.phaseT >= sc.t) { sc.done = true; runScript(S, sc.do, tune); }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n1370→  function loadPhase(S, def, index) {\\n    const ph = def.phases[index];\\n    S.phase = index;\\n    S.phaseCount = def.phases.length;\\n    S.phaseName = ph.name;\\n    S.phaseT = 0;\\n    S.objects = S.objects.filter(o => o.persist);\\n    S.strain = null;\\n    S.scripts = (ph.at || []).map(a => ({ t: a.t, do: a.do, done: false }));\\n    S.tutorial = !!ph.tutorial;\\n1380→    S.tutDone = !ph.tutorial;\\n    S.flags = Object.assign({}, S.flags, ph.flags || {});\\n    if (ph.dim != null) S.dim = ph.dim;\\n    if (ph.tilt) S.tiltAmp = ph.tilt;\\n    for (const spec of ph.objects || []) addObj(S, clone(spec));\\n    if (ph.strain) spawnStrain(S, ph.strain, ph.strainOpts || {});\\n    if (ph.device) S.device = clone(ph.device);\\n    if (ph.onEnter) runScript(S, ph.onEnter, tuneOf(null));\\n    S.checkpoint = takeCore(S);\\n    /* drop the checkpoint's nested copy weight: checkpoint is the core itself */\\n1390→    pushEv(S, ['phase', index, ph.name]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function advancePhase(S) {\\n    if (S.hold) return;\\n    const def = (GAME.CASES || {})[S.id];\\n    if (!def) { finishCase(S); return; }\\n    if (S.phase + 1 >= def.phases.length) {\\n      if (!S.dressing && !S.won) {\\n        S.dressing = { t: 0, done: false };\\n1400→        pushEv(S, ['dressing', 1]);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      return;\",\"content_concise\":\"1314→  function stepWorld(S, worldDt, handDt, tune) {\\n    if (S.flags.dip) {\\n      S.vitals += (S.flags.dip - S.vitals) * Math.min(1, worldDt * 2);\\n      if (Math.abs(S.vitals - S.flags.dip) < 0.4) { S.vitals = S.flags.dip; S.flags.dip = 0; }\\n    }\\n    if (S.flags.crash) {\\n1320→      S.vitals -= S.flags.crash * worldDt;\\n    }\\n    if (S.tiltAmp) {\\n      const drift = Math.sin(S.worldT * 0.7) * 25 * S.tiltAmp;\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'pool' && !o.done) {\\n        o.x = clamp(o.x + drift * worldDt, 60, 360);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    for (const o of S.objects) {\\n      if (o.markT > 0) { o.markT -= handDt; if (o.markT <= 0 && o.hidden) o.marked = false; }\\n1330→      if (o.revealWhen && o.hidden) {\\n        const src = S.objects.find(q => q.tag === o.revealWhen);\\n        if (src && src.done) { o.hidden = false; o.marked = true; }\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'bleeder' && !o.done) {\\n        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 8, vol: 4, max: 40, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 6 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'arteryTear' && !o.done) {\\n1340→        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 6, vol: 6, max: 50, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 14 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* solo retractor: Quill holds at half the window */\\n    const retract = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'retractor' && !o.done);\\n    if (retract) {\\n      const holder = S.players.some(p => p.held === retract.id && p.trig > 0.3);\\n      if (holder) S.windowOpen = 1;\\n1350→      else if (S.players.filter(p => !p.gone).length <= 1) S.windowOpen = 0.5;\\n      else S.windowOpen = 0;\\n    }\\n    if (S.lab) {\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.done && o.lab) {\\n        o.labT = (o.labT || 0) + worldDt;\\n        if (o.labT > 1.2) {\\n          o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.cut = false; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.stitch = 0; o.free = false; o.tears = 0; o.spin = 0;\\n          o.x = o.origin[0]; o.y = o.origin[1]; o.labT = 0;\\n          if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0;\\n1360→        }\\n      } else o.labT = 0;\\n    }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.scripts.length; i++) {\\n      const sc = S.scripts[i];\\n      if (sc.done) continue;\\n      if (S.phaseT >= sc.t) { sc.done = true; runScript(S, sc.do, tune); }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n1370→  function loadPhase(S, def, index) {\\n    const ph = def.phases[index];\\n    S.phase = index;\\n    S.phaseCount = def.phases.length;\\n    S.phaseName = ph.name;\\n    S.phaseT = 0;\\n    S.objects = S.objects.filter(o => o.persist);\\n    S.strain = null;\\n    S.scripts = (ph.at || []).map(a => ({ t: a.t, do: a.do, done: false }));\\n    S.tutorial = !!ph.tutorial;\\n1380→    S.tutDone = !ph.tutorial;\\n    S.flags = Object.assign({}, S.flags, ph.flags || {});\\n    if (ph.dim != null) S.dim = ph.dim;\\n    if (ph.tilt) S.tiltAmp = ph.tilt;\\n    for (const spec of ph.objects || []) addObj(S, clone(spec));\\n    if (ph.strain) spawnStrain(S, ph.strain, ph.strainOpts || {});\\n    if (ph.device) S.device = clone(ph.device);\\n    if (ph.onEnter) runScript(S, ph.onEnter, tuneOf(null));\\n    S.checkpoint = takeCore(S);\\n    /* drop the checkpoint's nested copy weight: checkpoint is the core itself */\\n1390→    pushEv(S, ['phase', index, ph.name]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function advancePhase(S) {\\n    if (S.hold) return;\\n    const def = (GAME.CASES || {})[S.id];\\n    if (!def) { finishCase(S); return; }\\n    if (S.phase + 1 >= def.phases.length) {\\n      if (!S.dressing && !S.won) {\\n        S.dressing = { t: 0, done: false };\\n1400→        pushEv(S, ['dressing', 1]);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      return;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":1314,\"limit\":90,\"raw_output\":\"  function stepWorld(S, worldDt, handDt, tune) {\\n    if (S.flags.dip) {\\n      S.vitals += (S.flags.dip - S.vitals) * Math.min(1, worldDt * 2);\\n      if (Math.abs(S.vitals - S.flags.dip) < 0.4) { S.vitals = S.flags.dip; S.flags.dip = 0; }\\n    }\\n    if (S.flags.crash) {\\n      S.vitals -= S.flags.crash * worldDt;\\n    }\\n    if (S.tiltAmp) {\\n      const drift = Math.sin(S.worldT * 0.7) * 25 * S.tiltAmp;\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.type === 'pool' && !o.done) {\\n        o.x = clamp(o.x + drift * worldDt, 60, 360);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    for (const o of S.objects) {\\n      if (o.markT > 0) { o.markT -= handDt; if (o.markT <= 0 && o.hidden) o.marked = false; }\\n      if (o.revealWhen && o.hidden) {\\n        const src = S.objects.find(q => q.tag === o.revealWhen);\\n        if (src && src.done) { o.hidden = false; o.marked = true; }\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'bleeder' && !o.done) {\\n        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 8, vol: 4, max: 40, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 6 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n      if (o.type === 'arteryTear' && !o.done) {\\n        let pool = S.objects.find(p => p.type === 'pool' && p.tag === 'fed-' + o.id);\\n        if (!pool) pool = addObj(S, { type: 'pool', x: o.x, y: o.y + 6, vol: 6, max: 50, order: o.order + 1, tag: 'fed-' + o.id, drain: 0 });\\n        if (!pool.done) pool.vol = Math.min(pool.max, pool.vol + 14 * worldDt * tune.fluids.bleed);\\n      }\\n    }\\n    /* solo retractor: Quill holds at half the window */\\n    const retract = S.objects.find(o => o.type === 'retractor' && !o.done);\\n    if (retract) {\\n      const holder = S.players.some(p => p.held === retract.id && p.trig > 0.3);\\n      if (holder) S.windowOpen = 1;\\n      else if (S.players.filter(p => !p.gone).length <= 1) S.windowOpen = 0.5;\\n      else S.windowOpen = 0;\\n    }\\n    if (S.lab) {\\n      for (const o of S.objects) if (o.done && o.lab) {\\n        o.labT = (o.labT || 0) + worldDt;\\n        if (o.labT > 1.2) {\\n          o.done = false; o.alive = true; o.prog = 0; o.cut = false; o.burn = 0; o.dosed = false; o.stitch = 0; o.free = false; o.tears = 0; o.spin = 0;\\n          o.x = o.origin[0]; o.y = o.origin[1]; o.labT = 0;\\n          if (o.cells) for (const c of o.cells) c[2] = 0;\\n        }\\n      } else o.labT = 0;\\n    }\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.scripts.length; i++) {\\n      const sc = S.scripts[i];\\n      if (sc.done) continue;\\n      if (S.phaseT >= sc.t) { sc.done = true; runScript(S, sc.do, tune); }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function loadPhase(S, def, index) {\\n    const ph = def.phases[index];\\n    S.phase = index;\\n    S.phaseCount = def.phases.length;\\n    S.phaseName = ph.name;\\n    S.phaseT = 0;\\n    S.objects = S.objects.filter(o => o.persist);\\n    S.strain = null;\\n    S.scripts = (ph.at || []).map(a => ({ t: a.t, do: a.do, done: false }));\\n    S.tutorial = !!ph.tutorial;\\n    S.tutDone = !ph.tutorial;\\n    S.flags = Object.assign({}, S.flags, ph.flags || {});\\n    if (ph.dim != null) S.dim = ph.dim;\\n    if (ph.tilt) S.tiltAmp = ph.tilt;\\n    for (const spec of ph.objects || []) addObj(S, clone(spec));\\n    if (ph.strain) spawnStrain(S, ph.strain, ph.strainOpts || {});\\n    if (ph.device) S.device = clone(ph.device);\\n    if (ph.onEnter) runScript(S, ph.onEnter, tuneOf(null));\\n    S.checkpoint = takeCore(S);\\n    /* drop the checkpoint's nested copy weight: checkpoint is the core itself */\\n    pushEv(S, ['phase', index, ph.name]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function advancePhase(S) {\\n    if (S.hold) return;\\n    const def = (GAME.CASES || {})[S.id];\\n    if (!def) { finishCase(S); return; }\\n    if (S.phase + 1 >= def.phases.length) {\\n      if (!S.dressing && !S.won) {\\n        S.dressing = { t: 0, done: false };\\n        pushEv(S, ['dressing', 1]);\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      return;\\n\",\"total_lines\":1762}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-6df8bb0d-264f-47fa-9bc4-a0cb730447ef-16","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"560→  function drawDev(g, r) {\\n    const px = E.px;\\n    const rows = devRows();\\n    const tabs = ['Tune', 'Cheats', 'Jump'];\\n    px.rect(g, r.W - 168, 8, 160, r.H - 16, '#06141a');\\n    E.font.text(g, tabs[RT.devTab], r.W - 160, 12, '#f5b700', { outline: false });\\n    const first = Math.max(0, Math.min(RT.devI - 6, rows.length - 12));\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 12 && first + i < rows.length; i++) {\\n      const k = first + i;\\n      const on = k === RT.devI;\\n570→      E.font.text(g, (on ? '> ' : '  ') + rows[k], r.W - 160, 28 + i * 12, on ? '#5ff0e0' : '#8fb8b0', { outline: false });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function drawTitle(r, t) {\\n    r.sky(['#071018', '#0e2430']);\\n    r.overlay(g => {\\n      GAME.Art.titleBackdrop(g, r.W, r.H, t || game.real || 0);\\n      E.font.title(g, 'OPEN TABLE', r.W / 2, 28, { scale: 2, align: 'center', colors: ['#f4fff8', '#9aefe4', '#1c6e78'] });\\n      E.font.text(g, TITLE, r.W / 2, 78, '#e8fbf6', { align: 'center', scale: 1, outline: '#06141a' });\\n580→      E.font.text(g, \\\"Don't let it go quiet\\\", r.W / 2, 96, '#5ff0e0', { align: 'center', outline: false });\\n      const y = 120;\\n      let x = 24;\\n      const beat = [0, 2, 0, 6, 0, 2, 8, 0, 1, 0, 4, 0];\\n      for (let i = 0; i < beat.length; i++) {\\n        const h = 2 + beat[i];\\n        E.px.rect(g, x, y - h, 6, h, '#7CFFB2');\\n        x += 10;\\n      }\\n      const prompt = game.input.label('confirm');\\n590→      E.font.text(g, prompt, r.W / 2, r.H - 28, '#e8fbf6', { align: 'center', scale: 2, outline: '#06141a' });\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  function snapshot() {\\n    const S = RT.S;\\n    const [ox, oy] = origin();\\n    let mark = null;\\n    if (RT.light && RT.light.mark) mark = [ox + RT.light.mark[0], oy + RT.light.mark[1]];\\n    const choice = !!(story.talk && story.talk.open && story.talk.choices && story.talk.choices.length && !story.talk.typing);\\n600→    return {\\n      scene: game.sceneName,\\n      menu: RT.menu ? { i: RT.menu.i, labels: RT.menu.items.map(it => (typeof it === 'string' ? it : it.label)) } : null,\\n      story: story.running ? story.node : null,\\n      held: !!story._held,\\n      choice,\\n      op: S ? {\\n        id: S.id, won: !!S.won, lost: !!S.lost, phase: S.phase, phaseName: S.phaseName,\\n        clock: S.clock, vitals: S.vitals, score: S.score, rank: S.rank,\\n        breath: !!S.breath, worldScale: S.worldScale, closed: !!S.closed,\\n610→      } : null,\\n      lightbox: mark,\\n      ward: { patients: RT.visitors.slice(), nearDoor: !!RT.nearDoor },\\n      attract: RT.attract ? { on: true, loops: RT.loops, seg: RT.seg } : null,\\n      dev: { open: !!RT.devOpen, dirty: !!GAME.TUNE.dirty },\\n      ranks: Object.assign({}, RT.ranks),\\n      cleared: Object.assign({}, RT.cleared),\\n      reel: RT.loops,\\n    };\\n  }\\n620→\\n  const REEL = [\\n    { kind: 'story', t: 4 },\\n    { kind: 'op', id: 'c1', t: 15, cheat: { lockVitals: true, freezeClock: true, oneHit: true } }