},{\"line_number\":104,\"content\":\"    { key: 'voices', label: 'Voices', type: 'slider', group: 'Sound', value: 0.9, min: 0, max: 1, step: 0.05, apply: (g, v) => { g.audio.voiceVolume = v; if (g.audio.applyVolume) g.audio.applyVolume(); } },\"},{\"line_number\":105,\"content\":\"    { key: 'difficulty', label: 'Difficulty', type: 'select', value: 'resident', options: [['intern', 'Intern'], ['resident', 'Resident'], ['attending', 'Attending']], apply: (g, v) => { RT.diff = v; } },\"},{\"line_number\":106,\"content\":\"    { key: 'assist', label: 'Surgical assist', type: 'slider', value: 0.6, min: 0, max: 1.4, step: 0.05, apply: (g, v) => { PREFS.assist = v; } },\"},{\"line_number\":107,\"content\":\"    { key: 'cursorSpeed', label: 'Cursor speed', type: 'slider', value: 330, min: 80, max: 500, step: 10, apply: (g, v) => { PREFS.cursor = v; } },\"},{\"line_number\":108,\"content\":\"    { key: 'swapSticks', label: 'Swap sticks', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { PREFS.swap = !!v; } },\"},{\"line_number\":109,\"content\":\"    { key: 'sustain', label: 'Sustained tools', type: 'select', value: 'hold', options: [['hold', 'Hold'], ['toggle', 'Toggle']], apply: (g, v) => { PREFS.sustain = v; } },\"},{\"line_number\":110,\"content\":\"    { key: 'hints', label: 'Hints', type: 'toggle', value: true, apply: (g, v) => { PREFS.hints = !!v; } },\"},{\"line_number\":111,\"content\":\"    { key: 'blood', label: 'Blood color', type: 'select', value: 'red', options: [['red', 'Red'], ['rose', 'Rose'], ['ink', 'Ink']], apply: (g, v) => { PREFS.blood = v; } },\"},{\"line_number\":112,\"content\":\"    { key: 'textSpeed', label: 'Text speed', type: 'slider', value: 1, min: 0.5, max: 3, step: 0.25, apply: (g, v) => { PREFS.text = v; } },\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"4ed7b3f5-7293-49b5-a298-100be8de2d03"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_287","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have a solid plan. I will write the test file.\n\nThe dacapo test marks one lobe done. It verifies that stepDacapo sets the dead flag and count to 10.\n\nI will step the simulation forward by 10.2 seconds to trigger revival and vitals reduction. I plan to use a cheat lockVitals flag to isolate the -8 direct vitals drop from drain effects. I also need to verify that dead objects stop draining during phase checks.\n\nI refined the dacapo test. After marking one lobe done, I will set the strain count to 0.05 and step forward by 0.2 seconds. This should trigger revival immediately while vitals drop by exactly 8. I am also beginning to draft a cantor rewind test.\n\nThe cantor rewind test spawns a cantor strain with move 3 and cycleT 20. It fills the ring buffer by stepping for about 0.6 seconds. It records the steady value before rewinding. After the winding completes, it checks that steady remains unchanged because keepSteady is true.\n\nI realized forceRewind restores the strain from the ring buffer, which may predate the move 3 and cycleT 20 changes. I will record a core hash before mutating an object position, then step forward to trigger rewind. The test will verify either that the rewound flag is set or that the object state matches its earlier snapshot.\n\nI refined the cantor rewind test. I will step 0.5 seconds to fill the ring buffer, then add a marker shard and record steady. After setting move to 3 and cycleT to 20, I will step 3.2 seconds. The marker object should be gone because forceRewind restores the oldest ring entry. The steady value should remain close to its state at rewind time rather than reverting to an older snapshot.\n\nThe cantor rewind test will assert that steady increases during the 3.2 second step loop, confirming forceRewind preserves the later value rather than reverting to an older ring snapshot. It will also verify the marker object is removed and the rewound flag is set.\n\nI will also test fermata. Clearing the domes and stepping briefly should open the eye.\n\nI will run the bot against all 11 test cases. Each case uses seed 3 and difficulty 'resident'. I will check that the bot wins, keeps vitals above 40, and leaves at least 30% of its starting clock. The c11 case already meets this threshold. I am now drafting tests for rounds n=1, n=2, and n=4.\n\nI will run the shell playthrough as a long test. I am also adding a determinism check: forcing art draws to true and false should produce identical simulation hashes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c74d2eef-bf95-493f-b258-185383d20bce-18","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ORDER|id: 'c|roundsCase|LIGHT","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/data/content.js","head_limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c74d2eef-bf95-493f-b258-185383d20bce-19","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/bot/bot.js","offset":240,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5634,"output_tokens":1984,"cache_read_input_tokens":79488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"f0ff611f-adf1-4a7d-8a2c-4993c1e6031c"}
