{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_307","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"game.settings is accessible via the Shell getter.\n\nThe Game class constructor confirms `this.settings` is a Settings instance. I will patch the syringe and write a comprehensive test file. Test files live in tests/ rather than src/, so regex patterns can be constructed there without literal matches appearing in source code.\n\nThe test file can contain the banned words directly. The rule only applies to shipped source and bundled HTML, not tests outside the bundle.\n\nBot playthroughs should finish in a few seconds to twenty seconds. I will set maxT to 500 for safety. Loses will be reported with id, reason, vitals, clock, and phase. Shell playthrough guard iterations are sufficient.\n\nThe shell playthrough guard is set to 120 iterations. The New Game flow test will cover title confirmation, menu navigation, difficulty selection, and the skip-story path. Resident difficulty was chosen because it matches the bot's tuned balance. A `press` helper function is being drafted to tap inputs and advance the game state.\n\nThe `press` helper is now defined. A new `enterScene` helper advances the game twice. The test script disables fade time and story skips. It injects a debug driver that feeds bot state into the device at 1/45 step rate. The playthrough sequence starts from the title screen, confirms the menu, selects New Game, checks the Intern difficulty label, moves down to Resident, and confirms the story.\n\nA 200-iteration guard will pump the game state. The loop snapshots the shell and routes by scene: it confirms story choices, advances charts with lightbox navigation, and steps through other scenes.\n\nThe playthrough loop now handles results, ward, credits, menu, and difficulty scenes by pressing confirm. It advances the guard and tracks visited scenes. Afterward it checks the title screen, all ranks are S, and no errors remain.\n\nA potential issue was spotted: after winning from story, results leads to ward, which sets nearDoor. The next loop may need an extra advance before pressing confirm to enter the ward scene.\n\nThe `press` helper taps the button before advancing twice. This means the confirm input is consumed by the current scene's update, then the first advance enters the next scene, and the second advance runs that scene's update. The one-frame press should not leak into the following scene.\n\nThe playthrough loop checks the scene name at the start of each iteration, so transitions to ward or results are handled cleanly on the following cycle. When the story is skipped, advance(0.25) processes multiple non-choice lines and deferred scene changes within a single step.\n\nThe test sequence will run attract mode before the playthrough, since the game boots on the title screen and attract confirms return to it. The dev UI test should be placed after the playthrough or explicitly return to the title screen first.\n\nTests will be grouped with try/catch so a later failure does not hide earlier results. The sequence is source hygiene, then unit sim tests, then shell boot, attract, lightbox, dev UI, settings, about, and finally the playthrough. Bot sim tests are slow and may time out. A hash-based determinism check without full clears will be added, along with a grep for Math.random. No window.open, fetch, or alert calls should appear in source code.\n\nAudio and shell code are confirmed safe from fetch calls. The test file will be written now, alongside a syringe patch. createRaw objects default to hold true so phaseClear halts cleanly without calling finishCase; this prevents an immediate loss when code blue begins after vitals drop. A diffClock test will verify steady clock increases with no objects present, tutorial off, and no cheat.\n\nIntern difficulty clock drops 1/1.3 per second. Attending drops 1.25. Vitals drain 0.7 for intern and 1.3 for attending over one second from a starting value of 80. Tutorial is disabled. A second-look test will restore the original tuning via cloneTune.\n\nThe second-look test creates a raw simulation object with Sokolova as the active doctor and a shard at 180, 120. It steps the scene forward to record the ring state, then clones the core state into `past`. The player is moved to 40, the shard is relocated to 300, and the clock and steady values are altered before calling `secondLook` against the original tuning.\n\nThe second-look test asserts the player stays at x=40 and the shard returns to its original position. It checks that the clock is near the saved value and that steady drops by 45 points after restoring the prior core state.\n\nThe second-look test must set steady to 80 before the call because the can-check runs before restoreCore. After restoreCore applies the ring snapshot and subtracts 45, steady becomes roughly zero. The test asserts that objects match the saved ring core and the clock matches the ring clock rather than the altered value.\n\nThe second-look test must not step the simulation after mutating state, because that would advance the ring's recorded entries past the pick target. The pick target is worldT minus six seconds, so with a four-second snapshot all entries remain valid and the first ring entry is selected. The clock should match the saved ring value rather than the altered one. Ghosts must also be present.\n\nA long-breath test is being drafted for the Vale gift. It creates a raw simulation with steady at 40 and steps the scene to trigger the breath effect. The test asserts that breathing activates and worldScale drops to 0.25. The cursor remains at full speed during the effect. The player position is frozen while the tuning is cloned.\n\nThe long-breath test compares cursor movement with and without the effect. It runs 60 cursor updates while aiming right and asserts the difference is within one pixel. It also verifies that the clock drops slower during breathing.\n\nThe long-breath clock drop is bounded between 0.15 and 0.4. The gift toggle does not interrupt the effect because the first step already sets the previous state, so the second step with gift false leaves the breath active. The retractor window test will be implemented carefully.\n\nA solo retractor test places a retractor and mass at 180, 140 and 220, 140. It steps the scene with trigger zero and asserts windowOpen equals 0.5. A two-player test without hold checks that windowOpen stays zero.\n\nThe two-player retractor test now steps the scene with forceps triggers on the retractor and a second trigger, then asserts windowOpen equals 1. This verifies the window gates canTouch so the second player can cut the mass once the window is open. A separate test checks that with windowOpen at zero, the scalpel stroke stays null.\n\nA da capo test is being drafted. It creates a raw simulation with vitals locked at 80 and spawns the da capo strain. The lobe is marked done, then stepped to verify the strain count becomes ten. The count is then reduced to 0.02 to check the remaining vitals.\n\nThe da capo test asserts the strain repeats once and vitals drop by at least 7.5 points despite the lock, while the lobe remains alive but no longer done. A cantor test is being drafted with vitals at 90, steady at 60, and a 0.6-second ring of 12 steps.\n\nThe cantor test adds a marker shard at 50, 50 and steps the scene for roughly 3.2 seconds. It asserts the marker is removed and steady increases by at least one point from its pre-step value. The steady rises during the step but nears the end of the cycle it is rewound to an earlier value and then restored.\n\nThe cantor test assumes keepSteady is true. Without it, the rewind would restore an early steady near 60 and the value would drop back down. With keepSteady, the steady stays elevated at roughly 61.9 instead of falling to about 60.\n\nThe cantor test asserts steady exceeds its pre-step value by more than half. This proves keepSteady is active, because without it the restored steady would fall to roughly 60.15 and stay below the starting 60.3. The marker shard disappearing confirms the ring restore occurred. The restored strain also rewinds at least one step, since move was set to three after the ring was recorded.\n\nA fermata eye test spawns the strain, clears its domes, steps the scene, and asserts the eye opens. A rank-letter test checks that 1000/1000 yields 'S', 800/1000 yields 'A', and 600/1000 yields 'B'.\n\nRank-letter thresholds are now fully mapped: 950–1000 yields S, 949–800 yields A, 600–799 yields B, 400–599 yields C, and below 400 yields D. A retry test marks a case lost and calls retryPhase; it asserts the rank cap becomes B and the lost flag clears. The code-blue peak test will use a careful loop with hit logging.\n\nAn attending doctor has no code-blue peak. The syringe air-bubble test holds the trigger for 0.95 seconds, releases, and asserts iv and sloppy grades. The fill rate is dt divided by 0.55, so the bubble reaches full capacity after 0.55 seconds and must stay held for an extra 0.3 seconds to trigger the over penalty.\n\nThe syringe test holds the trigger at 40, 40 for 0.95 seconds and releases to confirm iv and sloppy grades. A second test fills the syringe away from a reed at 200, 120 while the window is closed, then releases on the reed to verify no early injection occurs.\n\nA reed-injection test moves the syringe to the reed while still holding, then releases to confirm a laceration and slip increase. If canTouch blocks the cut, the test fails and the patch should fix it.\n\nA cautery lock test holds the trigger for 2.2 seconds at an empty spot. The lock rises to 1.2 after two seconds, then decrements to about 1.0 over the remaining half-second. It also checks for slips.\n\nA scalpel slip test places a cut object and guides the stroke manually, since cut is not auto-guided. The guide moves from [160, 120] to [160, 140] over 0.2 seconds to trigger a slip. Suction and sonar tests are straightforward.\n\nBot tests will reset GAME.TUNE at the start to avoid side effects. Art.force is disabled during bot runs because Bot.play does not draw. Sim unit tests that call Dev.set must also reset TUNE before running. The syringe patch is ready and the test file is being written.\n\nA warning handler will suppress color-related Node.js warnings before the test suite runs. The test file will be large and written with the Write tool.\n\nThe parent warning handler may be too late if Node emits the warning before user code runs. A better approach is to use execFileSync with a cleaned environment, or pass a specific --disable-warning flag to Node. The exact warning code is unknown.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3862548b-20c0-49a4-bcd1-fddfebc4710b-47","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","old_string":"      const bubble = p.over >= 0.3;\n      const tgt = nearest(S, p, 10, o => canTouch(S, o) && (o.type === 'clot' || o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'syringe')));","new_string":"      const bubble = p.over >= 0.3;\n      /* A closed reed or voice is still a target: the needle finds it and the tissue splits. */\n      const tgt = nearest(S, p, 10, o => {\n        if (!o || o.done || !o.alive || covered(S, o)) return false;\n        if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return true;\n        return canTouch(S, o) && (o.type === 'clot' || (o.type === 'lobe' && o.mode === 'syringe'));\n      });"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3862548b-20c0-49a4-bcd1-fddfebc4710b-48","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^## |^### |^- \\[ \\]","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2251,"output_tokens":6733,"cache_read_input_tokens":121344,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"ff6dcf1d-e8f4-4bf5-aee5-71d2fb61b2ce"}
