3,34,125,10,49,48,54,32,99,104,101,99,107,115,44,32,56,32,102,97,105,108,101,100,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\nEXIT:1\\nFAIL a tear leaves a laceration\\nFAIL Second Look restores the field: x 300 clock 199.89999999999998\\nFAIL c6 clears: vitals vit 0 clk 259/280 undefined ph 1\\nFAIL new game reaches difficulty: casefiles\\nFAIL intern is first: {\\\"i\\\":2,\\\"labels\\\":[\\\"Glasshouse\\\",\\\"Low Brass\\\",\\\"Crane Nine\\\",\\\"The Whistling Man\\\",\\\"Slur\\\",\\\"Bedside Manner\\\",\\\"Force Nine\\\",\\\"From the Top\\\",\\\"Dead Man's Rhythm\\\",\\\"Eloquent Cortex\\\",\\\"Last Note\\\"]}\\nFAIL one down is resident\\nFAIL a new game returns to the title: attract guard 160\\nFAIL every case ranks S: {\\\"c4\\\":\\\"S\\\"}\\n106 checks, 8 failed\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916 && node tests/run.mjs --fast > /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/tests.log 2>&1; echo EXIT:$?; cat /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/tests.log\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Run fast tests from the dev folder\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/terminal/call-ee9580e9-499a-4515-b307-d06b76509c7c-54.log\",\"total_bytes\":547}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"4f2068e3-8978-4c90-a76d-0d4fb7eb1d50"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_313","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Eight failures were found. I am beginning to analyze them.\n\nThe first failure is a missing laceration from the snap/tear code. I am checking whether the forceps actually gripped the shard and if the tear conditions were met.\n\nThe laceration should exist if the shard is held. The grip may not have registered because canTouch only checks for reed or voice objects with a window.\n\nThe shard is reachable and the forceps tool is set correctly. The first step may already trigger a tear, which would prevent the second step from adding the laceration.\n\nThe first step's instant distance of 492 exceeds the 120 limit. The shard tears immediately on that same frame. The second step cannot add another laceration because the tear cooldown is still active. The test therefore sees one laceration before and one after, so the check fails.\n\nThe laceration test should count objects before any step, not after the first.\n\nThe second failure shows the shard stayed at x=300 while the clock read 199.9 instead of 5. The core restore likely reverted the shard position, suggesting the ring entry was captured after the move.\n\nThe second failure is now clearer. The ring's oldest entry should hold the shard at x=180, but the restored state shows x=300. This suggests the live object was mutated after the ring core was cloned, or the restore logic failed to apply the stored position.\n\nThe second failure is caused by a stale object reference. The test variable `shard` still points to the old object after restore, so the restored state appears unchanged. The clock reading 199.9 confirms the core was properly restored.\n\nThe c6 failure shows vitals at zero and phase at one, indicating a vitals loss. This contradicts the earlier summary that c6 scored 4789 with vitals at 99, suggesting a seed or difficulty difference.\n\nThe c6 failure persists despite a clean TUNE. The test order places bots after determinism resets, so the tune should be default. This suggests c6 was always a tight score and the earlier summary reflected an older balance.\n\nI am now investigating why c6 lost despite its earlier high score. The bot's syringe logic might be injecting a closed reed into the heart case, or the IV logic could be interfering. I will read c6's content to verify.\n\nA new game failure also appeared: the difficulty reached casefiles because the menu index was not reset after the About screen. The menu enter() function does create a fresh menu at index zero.\n\nThe menu index failure is now traced to the developer test. After closing the dev screen with cancel, the game remains on the op screen rather than returning to title. Pressing confirm from there does not enter a fresh menu, so the index stays at casefiles.\n\nThe menu index was 1 when the second confirm pressed. The title screen likely suppressed the confirm input, or the attract idle timer blocked it.\n\nThe menu index failure is now traced to mouse hover. After the developer test closes, the cursor may still be hovering over a menu item, which shifts the focus to that item instead of starting at index zero.\n\nThe chart test left the mouse at a position that hovered over Case Files. The menu update selects that row, so the next confirm pressed Case Files instead of New Game. I will move the pointer to a corner before confirming to clear that hover.\n\nThe menu update order needs checking. If hover runs after key input, pressing up repeatedly could be overwritten by the leftover cursor position. Feeding a move to a corner like (2, 2) should clear the hover and lock the index at zero. The same fix applies to the difficulty menu.\n\nThe menu index failure is now fully understood. The developer test leaves the cursor hovering over Case Files, so the next confirm selects that item instead of New Game. The playthrough then proceeds through Case Files, which is an idle screen, and advances for 32 seconds until attract mode triggers.\n\nThe c4 rank of S is unexplained. The playthrough never started that case file, so the score must have come from a prior partial run or an unexpected loop behavior.\n\nThe casefiles scene is not handled by the playthrough loop, so it does not confirm. The resident check failure may have thrown an exception because the menu object was null.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c406e4d9-4bae-4676-96f3-963cc3868dbb-55","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/scenes/shell.js","offset":880,"limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c406e4d9-4bae-4676-96f3-963cc3868dbb-56","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/data/content.js","offset":136,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":580,"output_tokens":2896,"cache_read_input_tokens":146176,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"d3b3050e-bd8c-4715-8900-83e42a4d8924"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c406e4d9-4bae-4676-96f3-963cc3868dbb-55","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"880→        }, () => go('menu'));\\n        RT.menu.i = 0;\\n      },\\n      update() { if (RT.menu) RT.menu.update(); },\\n      draw(r) {\\n        r.sky(['#071018', '#102028']);\\n        r.overlay(g => {\\n          GAME.Art.stage(g, 'office', r.W, r.H, game.real);\\n          E.font.text(g, 'DIFFICULTY', r.W / 2, 16, '#5ff0e0', { align: 'center', scale: 2, outline: '#06141a' });\\n        });\\n890→        if (RT.menu) RT.menu.draw(r);\\n      },\\n    },\\n    casefiles: {\\n      view: 'side', camera: CAM,\\n      enter() {\\n        const items = GAME.ORDER.map(id => {\\n          const def = GAME.CASES[id];\\n          const rank = RT.ranks[id] ? '  ' + RT.ranks[id] : '';\\n          return (def.name || id) + rank;\\n900→        });\\n        RT.menu = makeMenu(items, (i) => {\\n          RT.fileCase = GAME.ORDER[i];\\n          RT.pending = 'file';\\n          RT.fromStory = false;\\n          go('difficulty');\\n        }, () => go('menu'));\\n      },\\n      update() { if (RT.menu) RT.menu.update(); },\\n      draw(r) {\\n910→        r.sky(['#071018', '#102028']);\\n        r.overlay(g => E.font.text(g, 'CASE FILES', r.W / 2, 12, '#5ff0e0', { align: 'center', scale: 2, outline: '#06141a' }));\\n        if (RT.menu) RT.menu.draw(r);\\n      },\\n    },\\n    lobby: {\\n      view: 'side', camera: CAM,\\n      enter() {\\n        RT.menu = makeMenu(['1 surgeon', '2 surgeons', '3 surgeons', '4 surgeons'], (i) => {\\n          RT.lobbyN = i + 1;\\n920→          beginCase('ferry', { players: RT.lobbyN, fromStory: false, mode: 'rounds' });\\n          go('op');\\n        }, () => go('menu'));\\n      },\\n      update() { if (RT.menu) RT.menu.update(); },\\n      draw(r) {\\n        r.sky(['#071018', '#102028']);\\n        r.overlay(g => {\\n          E.font.text