{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_318","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bot is stuck on \"prime\" and creating lacerations.\n\nThe dump point lands on adjacent reeds because the 5 reeds form a circle of radius 28. Releasing the syringe there hits a neighbor with window false, causing lacerations. This matches the climbing slips and lacerations. The recent syringe change caused this.\n\nPreviously, releasing near a closed reed was a harmless IV. Now it causes lacerations and slips. The bot must dump away from all reeds. Reverting the sim change and adjusting the test is one option.\n\nThe sim change will stay. The bot's dump point will move to a safe corner far from the reeds, such as (48, 188). This avoids lacerating closed reeds while keeping the correct product behavior.\n\nThe 22-unit side offset was meant to clear the target reed's inject radius, but it is too small to avoid neighboring reeds. The bot will move its wait position to (46, 188), a fixed safe point already used for IV.\n\nThe safe point is far enough from the reeds to avoid lacerations. Releasing there heals the bot as an IV, which helps tremolo. However, at 0.97 fill the bot dumps at the safe point and wastes the dose as an IV. The window lasts only 0.3 seconds while refilling takes 0.55 seconds.\n\nThe bot charges at the side while the window is closed. It doses immediately if fill reaches 0.9 or higher when the window opens. The dump at 0.97 fill only happens while the window is still closed.\n\nOnly the release position needs to be clear. The charge position can remain at the side while the trigger stays held. When the window opens and fill is below 0.9, the bot moves to the reed with the trigger still held.\n\nThe dump coordinates will be set to (46, 188). A new issue was found: when fill is between 0.94 and 0.97, the charging flag is false and the trigger becomes zero, which could release the syringe at the side point.\n\nThe trigger drops to zero when fill sits between 0.94 and 0.97 while charging is inactive, causing a release at the side point that lacerates a neighboring reed. The fix is to park the syringe at the safe corner (46, 188) whenever the window is closed, whether holding charge or releasing. This prevents any release near reeds during the closed window.\n\nThe charging flag is now defined as fill below 0.94, so the trigger stays held at the safe park while charging. Releases only happen at the park when the dose is full. When the window opens with sufficient fill, the bot doses directly on the reed.\n\nThe step order confirms the syringe sees the previous frame's window state, so the timing is consistent. The next step is to patch bot.js and fix the laceration test expectations.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7ae46d99-03c7-4e60-ae13-223c01bb216c-62","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"pointer|rowAt|hover","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":757,"output_tokens":1874,"cache_read_input_tokens":161152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"47c6a793-36c8-4a6f-868e-667c2c937ca9"}
