5,101,114,118,101,114,38,97,117,116,111,61,49,96,46,32,80,97,115,115,32,109,101,97,110,115,32,96,119,105,110,100,111,119,46,95,95,104,117,98,67,104,101,99,107,46,112,97,115,115,32,61,61,61,32,116,114,117,101,96,46,32,84,104,101,110,32,111,112,101,110,32,116,104,101,32,112,97,103,101,32,111,117,116,115,105,100,101,32,97,32,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,46,10,49,48,50,53,58,124,32,77,48,32,124,32,84,105,116,108,101,32,112,105,99,107,101,100,46,32,70,111,108,100,101,114,115,44,32,118,101,110,100,111,114,44,32,109,97,110,105,102,101,115,116,44,32,98,117,110,100,108,101,114,44,32,100,101,118,32,112,97,103,101,44,32,116,101,115,116,32,114,117,110,110,101,114,44,32,72,117,98,32,99,108,105,101,110,116,32,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,112,97,103,101,32,124,32,69,109,112,116,121,32,103,97,109,101,32,98,117,105,108,100,115,44,32,114,117,110,115,44,32,111,110,101,32,116,101,115,116,32,112,97,115,115,101,115,44,32,104,97,114,110,101,115,115,32,114,117,110,110,101,114,32,119,111,114,107,115,32,111,110,32,65,112,112,101,110,100,105,120,32,68,32,124,10,49,50,51,54,58,35,35,32,65,112,112,101,110,100,105,120,32,68,58,32,72,117,98,32,115,107,101,108,101,116,111,110,44,32,112,97,103,101,32,104,101,97,100,32,97,110,100,32,104,97,114,110,101,115,115,32,114,117,110,110,101,114,10,49,50,52,50,58,60,115,99,114,105,112,116,62,47,42,32,118,101,110,100,111,114,47,104,117,98,47,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,46,106,115,44,32,112,97,115,116,101,100,32,117,110,109,111,100,105,102,105,101,100,32,42,47,60,47,115,99,114,105,112,116,62,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":13,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"- Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\"},{\"line_number\":110,\"content\":\"   (mkdir -p vendor/hub && cd vendor/hub && for f in README.md session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js examples/arena.html; do curl -fsSL --create-dirs -o \\\"$f\\\" \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f\\\"; done)\"},{\"line_number\":121,\"content\":\"10. **Menus at TV size.** The pause and settings menus are the engine's HTML, too small for 10 feet by default. `new E.Shell(game, { tv: true, theme })`, made before `game.start`, scales them for a TV: at 1080p a row is 94 px tall, six pause rows fit, and with Save and Load added the last of eight rows falls below the screen, where moving the focus scrolls to it, as it does on the long Settings screen. Canvas menus: `new E.Menu(game, items, { scale: 2, rows: 6 })` (`rows` scrolls; hover and click still work; `menu.rowAt(i)` gives a row's box, for tests). Reduce density too: the page head in Appendix D carries CSS that shows a Settings row's help only on the focused row. Keep its `html` prefix: the engine injects its own CSS at runtime, and the same specificity could lose to it.\"},{\"line_number\":123,\"content\":\"12. **The Hub works on this engine.** The skeleton in Appendix D passed all four harness scenarios (14 or 15 checks each) and still runs standalone. The options that matter in a session are `live: true`, `autoPause: false`, `corner: false`, `menu.quit: false`.\"},{\"line_number\":641,\"content\":\"Follow the protocol page and Appendix D. Exact behavior:\"},{\"line_number\":642,\"content\":\"- `session.js`, unmodified, is the first script in `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`. Tags: `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` 1-4, `hub:session-mode` shared-world, `hub:session-minutes` 5, a goal of at most 60 characters, controls of at most 80.\"},{\"line_number\":908,\"content\":\"vendor/hub/                      session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, the arena example\"},{\"line_number\":924,\"content\":\"tests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\"},{\"line_number\":929,\"content\":\"Every source file is wrapped, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, G = (window.GAME ||= {}); ... })();`, and shares things through `G`; a bare top-level `const E` in two scripts would be a redeclaration error. Wrap the Appendix code the same way. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\"},{\"line_number\":1010,\"content\":\"- **Hub harness, all four runs (Appendix D's runner):** `players=2&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Pass means `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Then open the page outside a session.\"},{\"line_number\":1025,\"content\":\"| M0 | Title picked. Folders, vendor, manifest, bundler, dev page, test runner, Hub client in the page | Empty game builds, runs, one test passes, harness runner works on Appendix D |\"},{\"line_number\":1236,\"content\":\"## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\"},{\"line_number\":1242,\"content\":\"<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-59d95b11-2662-46d7-b705-a05957e758d6-71","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\">\\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n10→<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\" role=\\\"status\\\" style=\\\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\\\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\\\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\\\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.89.1</span><span style=\\\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\\\"><span style=\\\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\\\"></span></span><span style=\\\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\\\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\\n<canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas>\\n<script src=\\\"../my-3d2dge.js\\\"></script>\\n<script src=\\\"game.js\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\">\\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n10→<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\" role=\\\"status\\\" style=\\\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\\\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\\\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\\\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.89.1</span><span style=\\\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\\\"><span style=\\\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\\\"></span></span><span style=\\\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\\\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\\n<canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas>\\n<script src=\\\"../my-3d2dge.js\\\"></script>\\n<script src=\\\"game.js\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/game/index.html\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\">\\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\" role=\\\"status\\\" style=\\\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\\\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\\\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\\\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.89.1</span><span style=\\\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\\\"><span style=\\\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\\\"></span></span><span style=\\\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\\\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\\n<canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas>\\n<script src=\\\"../my-3d2dge.js\\\"></script>\\n<script src=\\\"game.js\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"total_lines\":15}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"a4a5896b-a559-41f9-87dc-09c1fa85d556"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_324","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f64e631d-124e-40fd-be27-e97ea3dee789-72","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md","offset":1236,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f64e631d-124e-40fd-be27-e97ea3dee789-73","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md","offset":880,"limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1770,"output_tokens":136,"cache_read_input_tokens":169472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"afdcdf3a-7311-405d-91aa-ac47d81b608d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f64e631d-124e-40fd-be27-e97ea3dee789-72","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1236→## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\\n\\n**Page head.** Order matters.\\n\\n1240→```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>…</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body><!-- E.bootSplash's markup here --><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>/* engine */</script><script>/* game */</script></body></html>\\n```\\n1250→\\n**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\\n\\n```js\\n// Hub skeleton: shared world on my-3D2dge. The host's copy runs the world; other copies mirror it and send their own hands.\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst game = window.G = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  input: { ...base, useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] }, menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\\n1260→const NAME = 'SKELETON', W0 = 426, H0 = 240, DOTS = 12;\\nlet info = null, phase = 'wait', card = null, over = false, sent = 0, heardSeq = 0, S = { v: 70, dots: [], p: {} }, mine = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0 }, rng = null;\\nconst place = () => ({ x: 40 + rng() * 340, y: 40 + rng() * 160 });\\nfunction hostInit() { rng = HUB.rng('deal'); S.dots = Array.from({ length: DOTS }, (_, id) => ({ id, ...place(), alive: 1 })); for (const q of info.players) S.p[q.id] = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0, score: 0, gone: false }; }\\nfunction finish(won) { if (over) return; over = true; if (HUB.server !== true && info.me != null && S.p[info.me]) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  const live = info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).sort((a, b) => S.p[b.id].score - S.p[a.id].score), standings = [];\\n  for (const q of live) { const last = standings[standings.length - 1]; if (last && S.p[last[0]].score === S.p[q.id].score) last.push(q.id); else standings.push([q.id]); }\\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(info.players.map(q => [q.id, S.p[q.id].score]));\\n  HUB.send({ t: 'over', v: S.v }); HUB.finish({ standings, scores, won, awards: live.length ? [{ id: live[0].id, title: 'Steadiest Hand', detail: scores[live[0].id] + ' clean actions' }] : [] }); }\\nasync function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n1270→  if (!info) { phase = 'solo'; return; }\\n  HUB.on('card', c => { card = c; });\\n  HUB.on('start', () => { phase = 'count'; });\\n  HUB.on('message', (d, from) => { if (info.isHost) { const p = S.p[from]; if (d.t === 'i' && p && d.n > (p.n || 0)) { p.n = d.n; p.x = d.x; p.y = d.y; p.t = d.t2; } } else if (from === info.host) { if (d.t === 's' && d.n > heardSeq) { heardSeq = d.n; S.v = d.v; S.dots = d.o.map(([id, x, y]) => ({ id, x, y, alive: 1 })); for (const [id, x, y, t, sc] of d.p) { const q = S.p[id] || (S.p[id] = {}); if (id !== info.me) { q.x = x; q.y = y; q.t = t; } q.score = sc; } } if (d.t === 'over') over = true; } });\\n  HUB.on('leave', ({ id }) => { if (S.p[id]) S.p[id].gone = true; });\\n  HUB.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) finish(false); });\\n  HUB.on('end', () => { phase = 'over'; game.audio.music(null); game.audio.mute(true); });\\n  if (info.isHost) hostInit();\\n  HUB.ready(); }\\nfunction step(dt) { const I = game.input, m = I.move(), a = I.padAim, ptr = I.pointer(); let dx = (a ? a[0] : 0) + m[0], dy = (a ? a[1] : 0) + m[1]; mine.x = E.clamp(mine.x + dx * 300 * dt, 0, W0); mine.y = E.clamp(mine.y + dy * 300 * dt, 0, H0); if (ptr && I.lastDevice === 'mouse') { mine.x = ptr[0]; mine.y = ptr[1]; } mine.t = I.value('useTool'); }\\n1280→let snapN = 0, inN = 0, acc = 0;\\nfunction hostStep(dt) { S.v = Math.max(0, S.v - .05 * dt); if (info.me != null && S.p[info.me] && !info.server) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  for (const id in S.p) { const p = S.p[id]; if (p.gone || !p.t) continue; for (const d of S.dots) if (d.alive && Math.hypot(d.x - p.x, d.y - p.y) < 12) { d.alive = 0; p.score++; } } S.dots = S.dots.filter(d => d.alive); if (!S.dots.length) finish(true); }\\ngame.start({ scene: 'hub', scenes: { hub: { pausable: true, camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false },\\n  update(dt) { const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n    if (!info && !inSession) return;\\n    if (phase === 'wait' && info) { if (I.pressed('confirm')) HUB.answer('ready'); if (I.pressed('more')) HUB.answer('more'); const c = I.clicked(); if (c) HUB.answer(c[1] > game.H * .7 ? 'more' : 'ready'); }\\n    if (phase === 'count' && HUB.time() >= 0) phase = 'play';\\n    if (phase === 'play' && !over) { step(dt); if (info.isHost) hostStep(dt); acc += dt; if (acc >= 1 / 12) { acc = 0; if (info.isHost) HUB.send({ t: 's', n: ++snapN, v: Math.round(S.v), o: S.dots.map(d => [d.id, d.x | 0, d.y | 0]), p: info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).map(q => { const p = S.p[q.id]; return [q.id, p.x | 0, p.y | 0, p.t > .25 ? 1 : 0, p.score | 0]; }) }, { reliable: false }); else HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++inN, x: mine.x | 0, y: mine.y | 0, t2: mine.t > .25 ? 1 : 0 }, { to: info.host, reliable: false }); } } },\\n  draw(r) { if (info && info.server) return; r.sky(['#143a36', '#14504a']); r.overlay(g => { E.font.text(g, NAME + ' ' + phase + (card && card.left != null ? ' ' + Math.ceil(card.left / 1000) : ''), 8, 8, '#fff', { outline: false }); for (const d of S.dots) px.disc(g, d.x, d.y, 4, '#5ff0e0'); if (info) for (const q of info.players) { const p = q.id === info.me ? mine : S.p[q.id]; if (p && !(S.p[q.id] || {}).gone) { px.disc(g, p.x, p.y, 5, q.color); E.font.text(g, q.name.slice(0, 12), p.x + 7, p.y - 4, q.color, { outline: false }); } } }); } } } });\\n1290→window.__hubProbe = () => ({ phase, over, dots: S.dots.length, v: S.v, t: HUB.active ? HUB.time() : 0 });\\nconnect();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n**Harness runner.** The folder needs the game (as `game.html`) and copies of `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. It uses an OS-picked port, checks the frame's title is your game (replace the print with a test), and stops only its own server, by handle.\\n\\n```python\\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n1300→folder = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1])\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=folder, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True)\\ntry:\\n    line = srv.stdout.readline(); port = int(re.search(r'port (\\\\d+)', line).group(1))\\n    base = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/'\\n    RUNS = ['players=2&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1', 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1']\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        b = p.chromium.launch(args=['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\\n        for q in RUNS:\\n            pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); pg.goto(base + 'harness.html?game=game.html&' + q)\\n1310→            try: pg.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=90000)\\n            except Exception as e: print('TIMEOUT', q)\\n            r = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const h = window.__hubCheck; return h ? { pass: h.pass, failed: h.checks.filter(c => !c.pass).map(c => c.name + ': ' + c.detail), n: h.checks.length } : null }\\\")\\n            title = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const f = document.querySelector('iframe'); try { return f && f.contentDocument && f.contentDocument.title } catch (e) { return 'x' } }\\\")\\n            print(q, json.dumps(r)[:700], 'title:', title); pg.close()\\n        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\\n        b.close()\\nfinally:\\n    srv.terminate(); srv.wait(timeout=5)\\n```\\n1320→\\n## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\\n\\n**A DualSense in the standard mapping, for Playwright's `add_init_script`.** Set `__pad.axes[0..3]` (left x, left y, right x, right y), `__pad.buttons[i].value` and `.pressed`: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 12 to 15 D-pad, and bump `__pad.timestamp`.\\n\\n```js\\n(() => { const axes = [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons = Array.from({ length: 18 }, () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\\n  const pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes, buttons,\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); }, reset() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); } } };\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n1330→```\\n\\n**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\\n\\n```js\\nd.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:48px 24px 24px;text-align:center;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(5,3,12,.92) 45%);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\\n// and on the button, add pointer-events:auto to its inline style\\n```\\n\\nNote it in your Engine Feedback.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1236→## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\\n\\n**Page head.** Order matters.\\n\\n1240→```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>…</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body><!-- E.bootSplash's markup here --><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>/* engine */</script><script>/* game */</script></body></html>\\n```\\n1250→\\n**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\\n\\n```js\\n// Hub skeleton: shared world on my-3D2dge. The host's copy runs the world; other copies mirror it and send their own hands.\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst game = window.G = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  input: { ...base, useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] }, menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\\n1260→const NAME = 'SKELETON', W0 = 426, H0 = 240, DOTS = 12;\\nlet info = null, phase = 'wait', card = null, over = false, sent = 0, heardSeq = 0, S = { v: 70, dots: [], p: {} }, mine = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0 }, rng = null;\\nconst place = () => ({ x: 40 + rng() * 340, y: 40 + rng() * 160 });\\nfunction hostInit() { rng = HUB.rng('deal'); S.dots = Array.from({ length: DOTS }, (_, id) => ({ id, ...place(), alive: 1 })); for (const q of info.players) S.p[q.id] = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0, score: 0, gone: false }; }\\nfunction finish(won) { if (over) return; over = true; if (HUB.server !== true && info.me != null && S.p[info.me]) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  const live = info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).sort((a, b) => S.p[b.id].score - S.p[a.id].score), standings = [];\\n  for (const q of live) { const last = standings[standings.length - 1]; if (last && S.p[last[0]].score === S.p[q.id].score) last.push(q.id); else standings.push([q.id]); }\\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(info.players.map(q => [q.id, S.p[q.id].score]));\\n  HUB.send({ t: 'over', v: S.v }); HUB.finish({ standings, scores, won, awards: live.length ? [{ id: live[0].id, title: 'Steadiest Hand', detail: scores[live[0].id] + ' clean actions' }] : [] }); }\\nasync function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n1270→  if (!info) { phase = 'solo'; return; }\\n  HUB.on('card', c => { card = c; });\\n  HUB.on('start', () => { phase = 'count'; });\\n  HUB.on('message', (d, from) => { if (info.isHost) { const p = S.p[from]; if (d.t === 'i' && p && d.n > (p.n || 0)) { p.n = d.n; p.x = d.x; p.y = d.y; p.t = d.t2; } } else if (from === info.host) { if (d.t === 's' && d.n > heardSeq) { heardSeq = d.n; S.v = d.v; S.dots = d.o.map(([id, x, y]) => ({ id, x, y, alive: 1 })); for (const [id, x, y, t, sc] of d.p) { const q = S.p[id] || (S.p[id] = {}); if (id !== info.me) { q.x = x; q.y = y; q.t = t; } q.score = sc; } } if (d.t === 'over') over = true; } });\\n  HUB.on('leave', ({ id }) => { if (S.p[id]) S.p[id].gone = true; });\\n  HUB.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) finish(false); });\\n  HUB.on('end', () => { phase = 'over'; game.audio.music(null); game.audio.mute(true); });\\n  if (info.isHost) hostInit();\\n  HUB.ready(); }\\nfunction step(dt) { const I = game.input, m = I.move(), a = I.padAim, ptr = I.pointer(); let dx = (a ? a[0] : 0) + m[0], dy = (a ? a[1] : 0) + m[1]; mine.x = E.clamp(mine.x + dx * 300 * dt, 0, W0); mine.y = E.clamp(mine.y + dy * 300 * dt, 0, H0); if (ptr && I.lastDevice === 'mouse') { mine.x = ptr[0]; mine.y = ptr[1]; } mine.t = I.value('useTool'); }\\n1280→let snapN = 0, inN = 0, acc = 0;\\nfunction hostStep(dt) { S.v = Math.max(0, S.v - .05 * dt); if (info.me != null && S.p[info.me] && !info.server) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  for (const id in S.p) { const p = S.p[id]; if (p.gone || !p.t) continue; for (const d of S.dots) if (d.alive && Math.hypot(d.x - p.x, d.y - p.y) < 12) { d.alive = 0; p.score++; } } S.dots = S.dots.filter(d => d.alive); if (!S.dots.length) finish(true); }\\ngame.start({ scene: 'hub', scenes: { hub: { pausable: true, camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false },\\n  update(dt) { const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n    if (!info && !inSession) return;\\n    if (phase === 'wait' && info) { if (I.pressed('confirm')) HUB.answer('ready'); if (I.pressed('more')) HUB.answer('more'); const c = I.clicked(); if (c) HUB.answer(c[1] > game.H * .7 ? 'more' : 'ready'); }\\n    if (phase === 'count' && HUB.time() >= 0) phase = 'play';\\n    if (phase === 'play' && !over) { step(dt); if (info.isHost) hostStep(dt); acc += dt; if (acc >= 1 / 12) { acc = 0; if (info.isHost) HUB.send({ t: 's', n: ++snapN, v: Math.round(S.v), o: S.dots.map(d => [d.id, d.x | 0, d.y | 0]), p: info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).map(q => { const p = S.p[q.id]; return [q.id, p.x | 0, p.y | 0, p.t > .25 ? 1 : 0, p.score | 0]; }) }, { reliable: false }); else HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++inN, x: mine.x | 0, y: mine.y | 0, t2: mine.t > .25 ? 1 : 0 }, { to: info.host, reliable: false }); } } },\\n  draw(r) { if (info && info.server) return; r.sky(['#143a36', '#14504a']); r.overlay(g => { E.font.text(g, NAME + ' ' + phase + (card && card.left != null ? ' ' + Math.ceil(card.left / 1000) : ''), 8, 8, '#fff', { outline: false }); for (const d of S.dots) px.disc(g, d.x, d.y, 4, '#5ff0e0'); if (info) for (const q of info.players) { const p = q.id === info.me ? mine : S.p[q.id]; if (p && !(S.p[q.id] || {}).gone) { px.disc(g, p.x, p.y, 5, q.color); E.font.text(g, q.name.slice(0, 12), p.x + 7, p.y - 4, q.color, { outline: false }); } } }); } } } });\\n1290→window.__hubProbe = () => ({ phase, over, dots: S.dots.length, v: S.v, t: HUB.active ? HUB.time() : 0 });\\nconnect();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n**Harness runner.** The folder needs the game (as `game.html`) and copies of `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. It uses an OS-picked port, checks the frame's title is your game (replace the print with a test), and stops only its own server, by handle.\\n\\n```python\\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\n1300→folder = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1])\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=folder, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True)\\ntry:\\n    line = srv.stdout.readline(); port = int(re.search(r'port (\\\\d+)', line).group(1))\\n    base = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/'\\n    RUNS = ['players=2&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1', 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1']\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        b = p.chromium.launch(args=['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\\n        for q in RUNS:\\n            pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); pg.goto(base + 'harness.html?game=game.html&' + q)\\n1310→            try: pg.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=90000)\\n            except Exception as e: print('TIMEOUT', q)\\n            r = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const h = window.__hubCheck; return h ? { pass: h.pass, failed: h.checks.filter(c => !c.pass).map(c => c.name + ': ' + c.detail), n: h.checks.length } : null }\\\")\\n            title = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const f = document.querySelector('iframe'); try { return f && f.contentDocument && f.contentDocument.title } catch (e) { return 'x' } }\\\")\\n            print(q, json.dumps(r)[:700], 'title:', title); pg.close()\\n        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\\n        b.close()\\nfinally:\\n    srv.terminate(); srv.wait(timeout=5)\\n```\\n1320→\\n## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\\n\\n**A DualSense in the standard mapping, for Playwright's `add_init_script`.** Set `__pad.axes[0..3]` (left x, left y, right x, right y), `__pad.buttons[i].value` and `.pressed`: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 12 to 15 D-pad, and bump `__pad.timestamp`.\\n\\n```js\\n(() => { const axes = [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons = Array.from({ length: 18 }, () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\\n  const pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes, buttons,\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); }, reset() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); } } };\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n1330→```\\n\\n**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\\n\\n```js\\nd.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:48px 24px 24px;text-align:center;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(5,3,12,.92) 45%);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\\n// and on the button, add pointer-events:auto to its inline style\\n```\\n\\nNote it in your Engine Feedback.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1236,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"## Appendix D: Hub skeleton, page head and harness runner\\n\\n**Page head.** Order matters.\\n\\n```html\\n<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, pasted unmodified */</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>…</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body><!-- E.bootSplash's markup here --><canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>/* engine */</script><script>/* game */</script></body></html>\\n```\\n\\n**Skeleton.** A complete shared-world game on the engine. It passed all four harness runs and runs standalone. Replace the dots with the real sim, keeping its structure: connect, the event handlers, the host's step, the 12/s snapshot and the mirror. `HUB.send` for a real event batch is reliable by default.\\n\\n```js\\n// Hub skeleton: shared world on my-3D2dge. The host's copy runs the world; other copies mirror it and send their own hands.\\n(() => {\\nconst E = My3D2dge, HUB = window.AIHub, inSession = !!(HUB && HUB.active), { px } = E;\\nconst { attack, dash, skill, jump, ...base } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\\nconst game = window.G = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: [426, 240], expand: true, view: 'overhead', touch: 'never', live: inSession, autoPause: !inSession, corner: !inSession,\\n  input: { ...base, useTool: ['Pad7', 'Pad0', 'Mouse0', 'Space'], more: ['Pad3', 'KeyM'] }, menu: { quit: inSession ? false : 'title', settings: [{ key: 'music', value: .1 }, { key: 'glyphs', value: 'playstation', options: [['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['xbox', 'Xbox']] }] } });\\nconst NAME = 'SKELETON', W0 = 426, H0 = 240, DOTS = 12;\\nlet info = null, phase = 'wait', card = null, over = false, sent = 0, heardSeq = 0, S = { v: 70, dots: [], p: {} }, mine = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0 }, rng = null;\\nconst place = () => ({ x: 40 + rng() * 340, y: 40 + rng() * 160 });\\nfunction hostInit() { rng = HUB.rng('deal'); S.dots = Array.from({ length: DOTS }, (_, id) => ({ id, ...place(), alive: 1 })); for (const q of info.players) S.p[q.id] = { x: 200, y: 120, t: 0, score: 0, gone: false }; }\\nfunction finish(won) { if (over) return; over = true; if (HUB.server !== true && info.me != null && S.p[info.me]) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  const live = info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).sort((a, b) => S.p[b.id].score - S.p[a.id].score), standings = [];\\n  for (const q of live) { const last = standings[standings.length - 1]; if (last && S.p[last[0]].score === S.p[q.id].score) last.push(q.id); else standings.push([q.id]); }\\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(info.players.map(q => [q.id, S.p[q.id].score]));\\n  HUB.send({ t: 'over', v: S.v }); HUB.finish({ standings, scores, won, awards: live.length ? [{ id: live[0].id, title: 'Steadiest Hand', detail: scores[live[0].id] + ' clean actions' }] : [] }); }\\nasync function connect() { info = await HUB.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n  if (!info) { phase = 'solo'; return; }\\n  HUB.on('card', c => { card = c; });\\n  HUB.on('start', () => { phase = 'count'; });\\n  HUB.on('message', (d, from) => { if (info.isHost) { const p = S.p[from]; if (d.t === 'i' && p && d.n > (p.n || 0)) { p.n = d.n; p.x = d.x; p.y = d.y; p.t = d.t2; } } else if (from === info.host) { if (d.t === 's' && d.n > heardSeq) { heardSeq = d.n; S.v = d.v; S.dots = d.o.map(([id, x, y]) => ({ id, x, y, alive: 1 })); for (const [id, x, y, t, sc] of d.p) { const q = S.p[id] || (S.p[id] = {}); if (id !== info.me) { q.x = x; q.y = y; q.t = t; } q.score = sc; } } if (d.t === 'over') over = true; } });\\n  HUB.on('leave', ({ id }) => { if (S.p[id]) S.p[id].gone = true; });\\n  HUB.on('time-up', () => { if (info.isHost) finish(false); });\\n  HUB.on('end', () => { phase = 'over'; game.audio.music(null); game.audio.mute(true); });\\n  if (info.isHost) hostInit();\\n  HUB.ready(); }\\nfunction step(dt) { const I = game.input, m = I.move(), a = I.padAim, ptr = I.pointer(); let dx = (a ? a[0] : 0) + m[0], dy = (a ? a[1] : 0) + m[1]; mine.x = E.clamp(mine.x + dx * 300 * dt, 0, W0); mine.y = E.clamp(mine.y + dy * 300 * dt, 0, H0); if (ptr && I.lastDevice === 'mouse') { mine.x = ptr[0]; mine.y = ptr[1]; } mine.t = I.value('useTool'); }\\nlet snapN = 0, inN = 0, acc = 0;\\nfunction hostStep(dt) { S.v = Math.max(0, S.v - .05 * dt); if (info.me != null && S.p[info.me] && !info.server) Object.assign(S.p[info.me], mine, { score: S.p[info.me].score });\\n  for (const id in S.p) { const p = S.p[id]; if (p.gone || !p.t) continue; for (const d of S.dots) if (d.alive && Math.hypot(d.x - p.x, d.y - p.y) < 12) { d.alive = 0; p.score++; } } S.dots = S.dots.filter(d => d.alive); if (!S.dots.length) finish(true); }\\ngame.start({ scene: 'hub', scenes: { hub: { pausable: true, camera: { zoom: false, wheel: false },\\n  update(dt) { const I = game.input; game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n    if (!info && !inSession) return;\\n    if (phase === 'wait' && info) { if (I.pressed('confirm')) HUB.answer('ready'); if (I.pressed('more')) HUB.answer('more'); const c = I.clicked(); if (c) HUB.answer(c[1] > game.H * .7 ? 'more' : 'ready'); }\\n    if (phase === 'count' && HUB.time() >= 0) phase = 'play';\\n    if (phase === 'play' && !over) { step(dt); if (info.isHost) hostStep(dt); acc += dt; if (acc >= 1 / 12) { acc = 0; if (info.isHost) HUB.send({ t: 's', n: ++snapN, v: Math.round(S.v), o: S.dots.map(d => [d.id, d.x | 0, d.y | 0]), p: info.players.filter(q => !S.p[q.id].gone).map(q => { const p = S.p[q.id]; return [q.id, p.x | 0, p.y | 0, p.t > .25 ? 1 : 0, p.score | 0]; }) }, { reliable: false }); else HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++inN, x: mine.x | 0, y: mine.y | 0, t2: mine.t > .25 ? 1 : 0 }, { to: info.host, reliable: false }); } } },\\n  draw(r) { if (info && info.server) return; r.sky(['#143a36', '#14504a']); r.overlay(g => { E.font.text(g, NAME + ' ' + phase + (card && card.left != null ? ' ' + Math.ceil(card.left / 1000) : ''), 8, 8, '#fff', { outline: false }); for (const d of S.dots) px.disc(g, d.x, d.y, 4, '#5ff0e0'); if (info) for (const q of info.players) { const p = q.id === info.me ? mine : S.p[q.id]; if (p && !(S.p[q.id] || {}).gone) { px.disc(g, p.x, p.y, 5, q.color); E.font.text(g, q.name.slice(0, 12), p.x + 7, p.y - 4, q.color, { outline: false }); } } }); } } } });\\nwindow.__hubProbe = () => ({ phase, over, dots: S.dots.length, v: S.v, t: HUB.active ? HUB.time() : 0 });\\nconnect();\\n})();\\n```\\n\\n**Harness runner.** The folder needs the game (as `game.html`) and copies of `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. It uses an OS-picked port, checks the frame's title is your game (replace the print with a test), and stops only its own server, by handle.\\n\\n```python\\nimport json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time\\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\\nfolder = os.path.abspath(sys.argv[1])\\nsrv = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, '-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], cwd=folder, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, text=True)\\ntry:\\n    line = srv.stdout.readline(); port = int(re.search(r'port (\\\\d+)', line).group(1))\\n    base = f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/'\\n    RUNS = ['players=2&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1', 'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave&auto=1', 'players=2&scenario=server&auto=1']\\n    with sync_playwright() as p:\\n        b = p.chromium.launch(args=['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'])\\n        for q in RUNS:\\n            pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); pg.goto(base + 'harness.html?game=game.html&' + q)\\n            try: pg.wait_for_function(\\\"() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'\\\", timeout=90000)\\n            except Exception as e: print('TIMEOUT', q)\\n            r = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const h = window.__hubCheck; return h ? { pass: h.pass, failed: h.checks.filter(c => !c.pass).map(c => c.name + ': ' + c.detail), n: h.checks.length } : null }\\\")\\n            title = pg.evaluate(\\\"() => { const f = document.querySelector('iframe'); try { return f && f.contentDocument && f.contentDocument.title } catch (e) { return 'x' } }\\\")\\n            print(q, json.dumps(r)[:700], 'title:', title); pg.close()\\n        pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width': 1280, 'height': 720}); errs = []; pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e))); pg.goto(base + 'game.html'); pg.wait_for_timeout(1200); print('standalone', pg.evaluate(\\\"() => ({ active: AIHub.active, probe: window.__hubProbe() })\\\"), errs[:3]); pg.close()\\n        b.close()\\nfinally:\\n    srv.terminate(); srv.wait(timeout=5)\\n```\\n\\n## Appendix E: gamepad stub and touch-notice patch\\n\\n**A DualSense in the standard mapping, for Playwright's `add_init_script`.** Set `__pad.axes[0..3]` (left x, left y, right x, right y), `__pad.buttons[i].value` and `.pressed`: 0 ✕, 1 ○, 2 □, 3 △, 4 L1, 5 R1, 6 L2, 7 R2, 8 Create, 9 Options, 12 to 15 D-pad, and bump `__pad.timestamp`.\\n\\n```js\\n(() => { const axes = [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons = Array.from({ length: 18 }, () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 }));\\n  const pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD Vendor: 054c Product: 0ce6)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 0, axes, buttons,\\n    vibrationActuator: { playEffect() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); }, reset() { return Promise.resolve('complete'); } } };\\n  window.__pad = pad; navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null]; })();\\n```\\n\\n**Touch notice.** In your copy of the engine, `Game.prototype._needSync` sets the notice's `style.cssText` to a full-screen dark layer. Change that one string, so the reel shows above and the notice sits at the bottom. *Verified* on an iPhone profile: the notice sits in the lower half, the canvas above it is clear, and a tap on Settings opens the settings:\\n\\n```js\\nd.style.cssText = 'position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:20;display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:center;padding:48px 24px 24px;text-align:center;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(transparent,rgba(5,3,12,.92) 45%);color:#f4f0ff;font:600 17px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif';\\n// and on the button, add pointer-events:auto to its inline style\\n```\\n\\nNote it in your Engine Feedback.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1339}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f64e631d-124e-40fd-be27-e97ea3dee789-73","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"880→\\n### Music\\n\\nWritten in code in the engine's song notation, with named layers (`on: false`, `audio.layer`), `audio.tempo` and crossfades. Default slider **10%** (fact 4). Because that's quiet, keep it simple, melodic and bass-forward, and never let it carry information.\\n\\n| Track | Character |\\n|---|---|\\n| Title | Slow, rain-soaked, the four-note hospital motif on a soft lead over a held pad |\\n| Ward | Gentle, hopeful, night-shift jazz piano feel |\\n| Story tension | Low pulse, minor |\\n890→| Operation | 128 bpm drive, layers added by phase, tempo rising as vitals fall |\\n| Emergency | Faster, percussion layer, enters on crashes |\\n| HUSH boss | The motif inverted, minor, with a choir pad |\\n| Final | All of it, then dropped entirely for Development and the Last Note |\\n| Case closed, patient lost | Stings via `audio.sting` |\\n\\nThe whole score shares one motif. Long Breath: thin to bass only, half tempo, low-pass.\\n\\nMix defaults: Volume .7 (the engine's), Music .1, Effects 1, Voices .9.\\n\\n900→---\\n\\n## 19. Code architecture\\n\\n### 19.1 Layout (relative to the dev folder)\\n\\n```\\nvendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/   engine, docs, tools (read-only unless you patch the engine; note every patch)\\nvendor/hub/                      session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, the arena example\\nsrc/config.js                    GAME_TITLE, VERSION, TUNING defaults, hub tag strings\\n910→src/core/   state.js rng.js op.js tools.js objects.js strains/*.js score.js   (the sim: no draw, audio or DOM)\\nsrc/data/   cases/*.js sites.js cast.js story/*.js barks.js songs.js         (content as data)\\nsrc/art/    tissue.js sites.js bust.js instruments.js icons.js strains.js stages/*.js props.js glyphs.js\\nsrc/audio/  sfx.js babble.js choir.js music.js\\nsrc/ui/     hud.js wheel.js results.js menus.js casefiles.js about.js dev.js attract.js card.js\\nsrc/scenes/ title.js menu.js story.js chart.js op.js lost.js results.js ward.js lobby.js credits.js hubround.js\\nsrc/net/    hub.js local.js\\nsrc/bot/    autosurgeon.js\\nsrc/main.js\\nsrc/manifest.json                load order, shared by the dev page, the tests and the bundler\\n920→src/about-data.json              written last\\ntools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\\ntools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\\nindex.dev.html                   loads the sources one by one, for working\\ntests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\\nnotes/feedback.md                your running log\\nCONTENT.md                       one page: how to add a case, a strain, a site, a character, a story node\\n```\\n\\nEvery source file is wrapped, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, G = (window.GAME ||= {}); ... })();`, and shares things through `G`; a bare top-level `const E` in two scripts would be a redeclaration error. Wrap the Appendix code the same way. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\\n930→\\n### 19.2 The sim is plain data\\n\\n**All op state lives in one JSON-safe object, `S`.** No classes, closures or canvases in it; registries hold behavior, keyed by `o.type`. Its RNG is an integer in `S`, and the sim never touches `Math.random` or the clock. This one rule gives you, for free:\\n- Second Look's rewind (`structuredClone` every .1 s).\\n- Phase checkpoints.\\n- Network snapshots (a subset of `S`).\\n- Deterministic tests, `game.stateHash`, and the attract reel.\\n\\n```js\",\"content_concise\":\"880→\\n### Music\\n\\nWritten in code in the engine's song notation, with named layers (`on: false`, `audio.layer`), `audio.tempo` and crossfades. Default slider **10%** (fact 4). Because that's quiet, keep it simple, melodic and bass-forward, and never let it carry information.\\n\\n| Track | Character |\\n|---|---|\\n| Title | Slow, rain-soaked, the four-note hospital motif on a soft lead over a held pad |\\n| Ward | Gentle, hopeful, night-shift jazz piano feel |\\n| Story tension | Low pulse, minor |\\n890→| Operation | 128 bpm drive, layers added by phase, tempo rising as vitals fall |\\n| Emergency | Faster, percussion layer, enters on crashes |\\n| HUSH boss | The motif inverted, minor, with a choir pad |\\n| Final | All of it, then dropped entirely for Development and the Last Note |\\n| Case closed, patient lost | Stings via `audio.sting` |\\n\\nThe whole score shares one motif. Long Breath: thin to bass only, half tempo, low-pass.\\n\\nMix defaults: Volume .7 (the engine's), Music .1, Effects 1, Voices .9.\\n\\n900→---\\n\\n## 19. Code architecture\\n\\n### 19.1 Layout (relative to the dev folder)\\n\\n```\\nvendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/   engine, docs, tools (read-only unless you patch the engine; note every patch)\\nvendor/hub/                      session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, the arena example\\nsrc/config.js                    GAME_TITLE, VERSION, TUNING defaults, hub tag strings\\n910→src/core/   state.js rng.js op.js tools.js objects.js strains/*.js score.js   (the sim: no draw, audio or DOM)\\nsrc/data/   cases/*.js sites.js cast.js story/*.js barks.js songs.js         (content as data)\\nsrc/art/    tissue.js sites.js bust.js instruments.js icons.js strains.js stages/*.js props.js glyphs.js\\nsrc/audio/  sfx.js babble.js choir.js music.js\\nsrc/ui/     hud.js wheel.js results.js menus.js casefiles.js about.js dev.js attract.js card.js\\nsrc/scenes/ title.js menu.js story.js chart.js op.js lost.js results.js ward.js lobby.js credits.js hubround.js\\nsrc/net/    hub.js local.js\\nsrc/bot/    autosurgeon.js\\nsrc/main.js\\nsrc/manifest.json                load order, shared by the dev page, the tests and the bundler\\n920→src/about-data.json              written last\\ntools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\\ntools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\\nindex.dev.html                   loads the sources one by one, for working\\ntests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\\nnotes/feedback.md                your running log\\nCONTENT.md                       one page: how to add a case, a strain, a site, a character, a story node\\n```\\n\\nEvery source file is wrapped, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, G = (window.GAME ||= {}); ... })();`, and shares things through `G`; a bare top-level `const E` in two scripts would be a redeclaration error. Wrap the Appendix code the same way. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\\n930→\\n### 19.2 The sim is plain data\\n\\n**All op state lives in one JSON-safe object, `S`.** No classes, closures or canvases in it; registries hold behavior, keyed by `o.type`. Its RNG is an integer in `S`, and the sim never touches `Math.random` or the clock. This one rule gives you, for free:\\n- Second Look's rewind (`structuredClone` every .1 s).\\n- Phase checkpoints.\\n- Network snapshots (a subset of `S`).\\n- Deterministic tests, `game.stateHash`, and the attract reel.\\n\\n```js\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":880,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"\\n### Music\\n\\nWritten in code in the engine's song notation, with named layers (`on: false`, `audio.layer`), `audio.tempo` and crossfades. Default slider **10%** (fact 4). Because that's quiet, keep it simple, melodic and bass-forward, and never let it carry information.\\n\\n| Track | Character |\\n|---|---|\\n| Title | Slow, rain-soaked, the four-note hospital motif on a soft lead over a held pad |\\n| Ward | Gentle, hopeful, night-shift jazz piano feel |\\n| Story tension | Low pulse, minor |\\n| Operation | 128 bpm drive, layers added by phase, tempo rising as vitals fall |\\n| Emergency | Faster, percussion layer, enters on crashes |\\n| HUSH boss | The motif inverted, minor, with a choir pad |\\n| Final | All of it, then dropped entirely for Development and the Last Note |\\n| Case closed, patient lost | Stings via `audio.sting` |\\n\\nThe whole score shares one motif. Long Breath: thin to bass only, half tempo, low-pass.\\n\\nMix defaults: Volume .7 (the engine's), Music .1, Effects 1, Voices .9.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 19. Code architecture\\n\\n### 19.1 Layout (relative to the dev folder)\\n\\n```\\nvendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/   engine, docs, tools (read-only unless you patch the engine; note every patch)\\nvendor/hub/                      session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, the arena example\\nsrc/config.js                    GAME_TITLE, VERSION, TUNING defaults, hub tag strings\\nsrc/core/   state.js rng.js op.js tools.js objects.js strains/*.js score.js   (the sim: no draw, audio or DOM)\\nsrc/data/   cases/*.js sites.js cast.js story/*.js barks.js songs.js         (content as data)\\nsrc/art/    tissue.js sites.js bust.js instruments.js icons.js strains.js stages/*.js props.js glyphs.js\\nsrc/audio/  sfx.js babble.js choir.js music.js\\nsrc/ui/     hud.js wheel.js results.js menus.js casefiles.js about.js dev.js attract.js card.js\\nsrc/scenes/ title.js menu.js story.js chart.js op.js lost.js results.js ward.js lobby.js credits.js hubround.js\\nsrc/net/    hub.js local.js\\nsrc/bot/    autosurgeon.js\\nsrc/main.js\\nsrc/manifest.json                load order, shared by the dev page, the tests and the bundler\\nsrc/about-data.json              written last\\ntools/build.mjs                  bundles into the HTML file TASK.md names and writes the exit interview\\ntools/balance.mjs                bot runs for tuning, not part of the tests\\nindex.dev.html                   loads the sources one by one, for working\\ntests/run.mjs                    the one test command; it runs tests/hub.py (Appendix D's runner) for the Hub part\\nnotes/feedback.md                your running log\\nCONTENT.md                       one page: how to add a case, a strain, a site, a character, a story node\\n```\\n\\nEvery source file is wrapped, `(() => { const E = My3D2dge, G = (window.GAME ||= {}); ... })();`, and shares things through `G`; a bare top-level `const E` in two scripts would be a redeclaration error. Wrap the Appendix code the same way. `tools/build.mjs` concatenates per the manifest. In the page, escape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\\\/script` (engine and game). `session.js` is pasted verbatim.\\n\\n### 19.2 The sim is plain data\\n\\n**All op state lives in one JSON-safe object, `S`.** No classes, closures or canvases in it; registries hold behavior, keyed by `o.type`. Its RNG is an integer in `S`, and the sim never touches `Math.random` or the clock. This one rule gives you, for free:\\n- Second Look's rewind (`structuredClone` every .1 s).\\n- Phase checkpoints.\\n- Network snapshots (a subset of `S`).\\n- Deterministic tests, `game.stateHash`, and the attract reel.\\n\\n```js\\n\",\"total_lines\":1339}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"58f65252-a0c3-45f9-8316-2bef9115f4b0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_325","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plan indicates that tests/run.mjs runs tests/hub.py.\n\nThe hub test serves from the work root. The harness is at vendor/hub/harness.html inside the DEV folder. This path mismatch needs fixing.\n\nThe test code incorrectly references `vendor/hub/harness.html` from the work root. The server should instead serve the harness from the dev folder.\n\nThe plan requires game.html, harness.html, bridge.js, and round.js to be in the same folder. The dev folder is a sibling of the work root. The test should serve from the dev folder and copy game.html there.\n\nThe test can serve from the work root. The harness at `/NAME/vendor/hub/harness.html` can fetch the game via an absolute path like `/NAME.html`. A relative `game=game.html` would resolve incorrectly to `/NAME/vendor/hub/game.html`.\n\nThe test path will be fixed to `/<devName>/vendor/hub/harness.html` so the work-root server can reach the harness. The game HTML inlines session.js, so the iframe needs no separate file. The builder will add hub metas to the HTML head. The goal text is 52 characters, under the 60-character limit.\n\nThe howto text is about 72 characters, under the 80-character limit. The builder will emit exit-interview.json from its data to prevent drift. Harness files and a game.html copy will be placed in the dev folder so either layout works. The root HTML will contain the full engine and all source code.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b4f6fe45-4e83-4938-840c-e7b1b93d6619-74","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"bootSplash|e3-boot","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":15}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b4f6fe45-4e83-4938-840c-e7b1b93d6619-75","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"</script","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/hub/session.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5036,"output_tokens":1210,"cache_read_input_tokens":171136,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"c2b7fb38-69de-44f7-8239-278d9b0d92ef"}
