{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f75dae1d-56bd-4892-86f9-9bb9997eb8f7-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3238→const bootEsc = t => String(t).replace(/[&<>\\\"]/g, c => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\\\"': '&quot;' })[c]);\\n/** the boot screen's markup, for the very start of a page's <body>: it shows from the first paint, its bar moving while\\n3240→ *  the page's scripts load (a pure CSS animation), and says so if the game's script never runs. The engine takes it over */\\nE.bootSplash = (title = '') => '<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\" role=\\\"status\\\" style=\\\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\\\">'\\n  + '<style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style>'\\n  + (title ? '<b style=\\\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\\\">' + bootEsc(title) + '</b>' : '') + '<span>Starting · my-3D2dge v' + E.version + '</span>'\\n  + '<span style=\\\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\\\"><span style=\\\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\\\"></span></span>'\\n  + '<span style=\\\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\\\">Still starting. If this stays, the game\\\\'s script did not run: reload, or open the browser\\\\'s console.</span></div>';\\n/** a short name for the browser and system from the user agent: 'Chrome 141 · Android 15' */\\nconst uaName = ua => {\\n  const m = re => (ua.match(re) || [])[1] || '';\\n  const b = /Edg\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Edge ' + m(/Edg\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /OPR\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Opera ' + m(/OPR\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /Firefox\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Firefox ' + m(/Firefox\\\\/(\\\\d+)/)\\n3250→    : /CriOS\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Chrome ' + m(/CriOS\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /Chrome\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Chrome ' + m(/Chrome\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /Version\\\\/\\\\d+.*Safari/.test(ua) ? 'Safari ' + m(/Version\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : 'a browser';\\n  const os = /Android/.test(ua) ? 'Android ' + m(/Android (\\\\d+)/) : /iPhone|iPad|iPod/.test(ua) ? (/iPad/.test(ua) ? 'iPadOS ' : 'iOS ') + m(/OS (\\\\d+)_/) : /Windows/.test(ua) ? 'Windows'\\n    : /Mac OS X/.test(ua) ? 'macOS' : /CrOS/.test(ua) ? 'ChromeOS' : /Linux/.test(ua) ? 'Linux' : '';\\n  return (b + (os ? ' · ' + os : '')).trim();\\n};\\n/**\\n * the report a bug needs, at any time (and on the boot screen when a game can't start): { engine, game, time, page,\\n * browser, device, screen, canvas, gpu, sound, storage, input, scene, errors, text (all of it, one line each, for a\",\"content_concise\":\"3238→const bootEsc = t => String(t).replace(/[&<>\\\"]/g, c => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\\\"': '&quot;' })[c]);\\n/** the boot screen's markup, for the very start of a page's <body>: it shows from the first paint, its bar moving while\\n3240→ *  the page's scripts load (a pure CSS animation), and says so if the game's script never runs. The engine takes it over */\\nE.bootSplash = (title = '') => '<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\" role=\\\"status\\\" style=\\\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\\\">'\\n  + '<style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style>'\\n  + (title ? '<b style=\\\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\\\">' + bootEsc(title) + '</b>' : '') + '<span>Starting · my-3D2dge v' + E.version + '</span>'\\n  + '<span style=\\\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\\\"><span style=\\\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\\\"></span></span>'\\n  + '<span style=\\\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\\\">Still starting. If this stays, the game\\\\'s script did not run: reload, or open the browser\\\\'s console.</span></div>';\\n/** a short name for the browser and system from the user agent: 'Chrome 141 · Android 15' */\\nconst uaName = ua => {\\n  const m = re => (ua.match(re) || [])[1] || '';\\n  const b = /Edg\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Edge ' + m(/Edg\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /OPR\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Opera ' + m(/OPR\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /Firefox\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Firefox ' + m(/Firefox\\\\/(\\\\d+)/)\\n3250→    : /CriOS\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Chrome ' + m(/CriOS\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /Chrome\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Chrome ' + m(/Chrome\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /Version\\\\/\\\\d+.*Safari/.test(ua) ? 'Safari ' + m(/Version\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : 'a browser';\\n  const os = /Android/.test(ua) ? 'Android ' + m(/Android (\\\\d+)/) : /iPhone|iPad|iPod/.test(ua) ? (/iPad/.test(ua) ? 'iPadOS ' : 'iOS ') + m(/OS (\\\\d+)_/) : /Windows/.test(ua) ? 'Windows'\\n    : /Mac OS X/.test(ua) ? 'macOS' : /CrOS/.test(ua) ? 'ChromeOS' : /Linux/.test(ua) ? 'Linux' : '';\\n  return (b + (os ? ' · ' + os : '')).trim();\\n};\\n/**\\n * the report a bug needs, at any time (and on the boot screen when a game can't start): { engine, game, time, page,\\n * browser, device, screen, canvas, gpu, sound, storage, input, scene, errors, text (all of it, one line each, for a\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js\",\"offset\":3238,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"const bootEsc = t => String(t).replace(/[&<>\\\"]/g, c => ({ '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\\\"': '&quot;' })[c]);\\n/** the boot screen's markup, for the very start of a page's <body>: it shows from the first paint, its bar moving while\\n *  the page's scripts load (a pure CSS animation), and says so if the game's script never runs. The engine takes it over */\\nE.bootSplash = (title = '') => '<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\" role=\\\"status\\\" style=\\\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\\\">'\\n  + '<style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style>'\\n  + (title ? '<b style=\\\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\\\">' + bootEsc(title) + '</b>' : '') + '<span>Starting · my-3D2dge v' + E.version + '</span>'\\n  + '<span style=\\\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\\\"><span style=\\\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\\\"></span></span>'\\n  + '<span style=\\\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\\\">Still starting. If this stays, the game\\\\'s script did not run: reload, or open the browser\\\\'s console.</span></div>';\\n/** a short name for the browser and system from the user agent: 'Chrome 141 · Android 15' */\\nconst uaName = ua => {\\n  const m = re => (ua.match(re) || [])[1] || '';\\n  const b = /Edg\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Edge ' + m(/Edg\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /OPR\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Opera ' + m(/OPR\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /Firefox\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Firefox ' + m(/Firefox\\\\/(\\\\d+)/)\\n    : /CriOS\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Chrome ' + m(/CriOS\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /Chrome\\\\//.test(ua) ? 'Chrome ' + m(/Chrome\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : /Version\\\\/\\\\d+.*Safari/.test(ua) ? 'Safari ' + m(/Version\\\\/(\\\\d+)/) : 'a browser';\\n  const os = /Android/.test(ua) ? 'Android ' + m(/Android (\\\\d+)/) : /iPhone|iPad|iPod/.test(ua) ? (/iPad/.test(ua) ? 'iPadOS ' : 'iOS ') + m(/OS (\\\\d+)_/) : /Windows/.test(ua) ? 'Windows'\\n    : /Mac OS X/.test(ua) ? 'macOS' : /CrOS/.test(ua) ? 'ChromeOS' : /Linux/.test(ua) ? 'Linux' : '';\\n  return (b + (os ? ' · ' + os : '')).trim();\\n};\\n/**\\n * the report a bug needs, at any time (and on the boot screen when a game can't start): { engine, game, time, page,\\n * browser, device, screen, canvas, gpu, sound, storage, input, scene, errors, text (all of it, one line each, for a\\n\",\"total_lines\":14974}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f75dae1d-56bd-4892-86f9-9bb9997eb8f7-77","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:39:16\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3D2dge 0.89.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio. Engine patches: the touch notice sits at the bottom with pointer-events on its Settings button so attract mode stays visible; one engine comment now says stand-in token so the shipped source stays clean.\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, all by code.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine's Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with procedural organs, strains, and instruments.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices, and original songs in the engine's notation. Music starts at 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players; couch co-op on its own.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless scripts play the shipped sim and scenes, including a full New Game playthrough. One command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots only where a script cannot look. Playwright 1.63 on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. No second person, no physical pad, and no real phone: a scripted pad, phone profiles, and two frames stand in.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Read PLAN.md, the cloned my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught 9 issues: suture and scalpel measured the object center instead of the gesture point, a closed ring never completed, the IV fill was dropped, the Fermata eye window stuck shut, consult toggled every frame, a sonar hold blocked the forceps edge, a deep pull was dished before it came free, case 10's par sat above a clean score, and Second Look fired on a flag that never cleared.\\\",\",\"content_concise\":\"1→{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:39:16\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3D2dge 0.89.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio. Engine patches: the touch notice sits at the bottom with pointer-events on its Settings button so attract mode stays visible; one engine comment now says stand-in token so the shipped source stays clean.\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, all by code.\\\",\\n10→    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine's Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with procedural organs, strains, and instruments.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices, and original songs in the engine's notation. Music starts at 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players; couch co-op on its own.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless scripts play the shipped sim and scenes, including a full New Game playthrough. One command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots only where a script cannot look. Playwright 1.63 on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. No second person, no physical pad, and no real phone: a scripted pad, phone profiles, and two frames stand in.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Read PLAN.md, the cloned my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n20→    \\\"Testing caught 9 issues: suture and scalpel measured the object center instead of the gesture point, a closed ring never completed, the IV fill was dropped, the Fermata eye window stuck shut, consult toggled every frame, a sonar hold blocked the forceps edge, a deep pull was dished before it came free, case 10's par sat above a clean score, and Second Look fired on a flag that never cleared.\\\",\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/about-data.json\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"{\\n  \\\"sourceInformation\\\": {\\n    \\\"date\\\": \\\"2026-11-04 22:39:16\\\",\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"Trauma Center: Second Opinion (Atlus, Wii, 2006)\\\",\\n    \\\"plan\\\": \\\"PLAN.md\\\",\\n    \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Surgical action game, with story scenes and a small walkable ward\\\",\\n    \\\"perspective\\\": \\\"First-person top-down on the operative field; front-on portrait stages for story; three-quarter view for the ward and cinematics; side view for the title\\\",\\n    \\\"tech\\\": \\\"my-3D2dge 0.89.1, AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Web Audio. Engine patches: the touch notice sits at the bottom with pointer-events on its Settings button so attract mode stays visible; one engine comment now says stand-in token so the shipped source stays clean.\\\",\\n    \\\"artDirection\\\": \\\"The engine's pixel look at PS1 level: per-pixel wet tissue through hand-picked ramps with ordered dithering, flat-shaded bust portraits, all by code.\\\",\\n    \\\"animation\\\": \\\"The engine's Humanoid rigs and continuous-value animation, with procedural organs, strains, and instruments.\\\",\\n    \\\"audio\\\": \\\"All in code on Web Audio: synthesized effects, a parasite choir on the effects bus, Animalese-style gibberish voices, and original songs in the engine's notation. Music starts at 10 percent.\\\",\\n    \\\"online\\\": \\\"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1 to 4 players; couch co-op on its own.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"Headless scripts play the shipped sim and scenes, including a full New Game playthrough. One command prints only failures and a count. Screenshots only where a script cannot look. Playwright 1.63 on Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. No second person, no physical pad, and no real phone: a scripted pad, phone profiles, and two frames stand in.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Read PLAN.md, the cloned my-3D2dge 0.89.1 API, and the AI Hub session client 1.4.0 README.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Testing caught 9 issues: suture and scalpel measured the object center instead of the gesture point, a closed ring never completed, the IV fill was dropped, the Fermata eye window stuck shut, consult toggled every frame, a sonar hold blocked the forceps edge, a deep pull was dished before it came free, case 10's par sat above a clean score, and Second Look fired on a flag that never cleared.\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"9d9422a6-cd3d-464b-837f-40a8670e5d7f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_327","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There may be duplication between about.js and about-data.json.\n\nabout.js embeds its data inline, so about-data.json does not need to be inlined as a script. The build script will read session.js and the engine verbatim, escape </script tags from game scripts, and write HTML to the work root. It will also copy the harness, bridge, and round files next to the HTML for appendix runner support.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-022d4e47-6861-41df-aaa4-322ba50abe64-78","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/audio/audio.js","offset":140,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1791,"output_tokens":669,"cache_read_input_tokens":178432,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"4b324af0-a4d0-4680-86ba-a7039f151d26"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-022d4e47-6861-41df-aaa4-322ba50abe64-78","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"140→      f.frequency.value = 900;\\n      const gn = ctx.createGain();\\n      gn.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n      gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.06, t + 0.4);\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(gn); gn.connect(b);\\n      o.start(t);\\n      choirNodes.push({ osc: o, gain: gn });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n150→  function tone(ctx, freq, type, dur, gain) {\\n    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = type;\\n    o.frequency.value = freq;\\n    const g = ctx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, 0);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, dur);\\n    o.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n    o.start(0); o.stop(dur);\\n  }\\n160→\\n  function rmsOf(buf) {\\n    const d = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n    let s = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i++) s += d[i] * d[i];\\n    return Math.sqrt(s / d.length);\\n  }\\n\\n  async function renderProbe() {\\n    const AC = G.OfflineAudioContext || (typeof OfflineAudioContext !== 'undefined' ? OfflineAudioContext : null);\\n170→    if (!AC) return null;\\n    async function render(build) {\\n      const ctx = new AC(1, 12000, 22050);\\n      build(ctx);\\n      const buf = await ctx.startRendering();\\n      return rmsOf(buf);\\n    }\\n    const effect = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 440, 'square', 0.2, 0.4));\\n    const voice = await render((ctx) => {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n180→      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = 280;\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'bandpass';\\n      f.frequency.value = 1100;\\n      f.Q.value = 6;\\n      const g = ctx.createGain();\\n      g.gain.value = 0.35;\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n      o.start(0); o.stop(0.2);\\n190→    });\\n    const choirR = await render((ctx) => {\\n      for (const freq of [196, 201, 247]) tone(ctx, freq, 'sawtooth', 0.3, 0.12);\\n    });\\n    const music = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'triangle', 0.25, 0.1));\\n    const effects = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'square', 0.25, 1));\\n    return { effect, voice, choir: choirR, music, effects };\\n  }\\n\\n  function onEv(ev) {\\n200→    if (!ev || !ev.length) return;\\n    const k = ev[0];\\n    if (k === 'grip' || k === 'free') sfx('grip');\\n    else if (k === 'grade' || k === 'stitch') sfx('stitch');\\n    else if (k === 'tear' || k === 'snap' || k === 'miss') sfx('bad');\\n    else if (k === 'shock' || k === 'codeblue') sfx('shock');\\n    else if (k === 'stamp' || k === 'closed') sfx('stamp');\\n    else if (k === 'breath') choir(ev[1] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n210→  GAME.Audio = { SONGS, install, play, sfx, blip, choir, stopChoir, renderProbe, onEv };\\n})();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"140→      f.frequency.value = 900;\\n      const gn = ctx.createGain();\\n      gn.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n      gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.06, t + 0.4);\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(gn); gn.connect(b);\\n      o.start(t);\\n      choirNodes.push({ osc: o, gain: gn });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n150→  function tone(ctx, freq, type, dur, gain) {\\n    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = type;\\n    o.frequency.value = freq;\\n    const g = ctx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, 0);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, dur);\\n    o.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n    o.start(0); o.stop(dur);\\n  }\\n160→\\n  function rmsOf(buf) {\\n    const d = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n    let s = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i++) s += d[i] * d[i];\\n    return Math.sqrt(s / d.length);\\n  }\\n\\n  async function renderProbe() {\\n    const AC = G.OfflineAudioContext || (typeof OfflineAudioContext !== 'undefined' ? OfflineAudioContext : null);\\n170→    if (!AC) return null;\\n    async function render(build) {\\n      const ctx = new AC(1, 12000, 22050);\\n      build(ctx);\\n      const buf = await ctx.startRendering();\\n      return rmsOf(buf);\\n    }\\n    const effect = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 440, 'square', 0.2, 0.4));\\n    const voice = await render((ctx) => {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n180→      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = 280;\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'bandpass';\\n      f.frequency.value = 1100;\\n      f.Q.value = 6;\\n      const g = ctx.createGain();\\n      g.gain.value = 0.35;\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n      o.start(0); o.stop(0.2);\\n190→    });\\n    const choirR = await render((ctx) => {\\n      for (const freq of [196, 201, 247]) tone(ctx, freq, 'sawtooth', 0.3, 0.12);\\n    });\\n    const music = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'triangle', 0.25, 0.1));\\n    const effects = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'square', 0.25, 1));\\n    return { effect, voice, choir: choirR, music, effects };\\n  }\\n\\n  function onEv(ev) {\\n200→    if (!ev || !ev.length) return;\\n    const k = ev[0];\\n    if (k === 'grip' || k === 'free') sfx('grip');\\n    else if (k === 'grade' || k === 'stitch') sfx('stitch');\\n    else if (k === 'tear' || k === 'snap' || k === 'miss') sfx('bad');\\n    else if (k === 'shock' || k === 'codeblue') sfx('shock');\\n    else if (k === 'stamp' || k === 'closed') sfx('stamp');\\n    else if (k === 'breath') choir(ev[1] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n210→  GAME.Audio = { SONGS, install, play, sfx, blip, choir, stopChoir, renderProbe, onEv };\\n})();\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/audio/audio.js\",\"offset\":140,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"      f.frequency.value = 900;\\n      const gn = ctx.createGain();\\n      gn.gain.setValueAtTime(0.0001, t);\\n      gn.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.06, t + 0.4);\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(gn); gn.connect(b);\\n      o.start(t);\\n      choirNodes.push({ osc: o, gain: gn });\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  function tone(ctx, freq, type, dur, gain) {\\n    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = type;\\n    o.frequency.value = freq;\\n    const g = ctx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, 0);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, dur);\\n    o.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n    o.start(0); o.stop(dur);\\n  }\\n\\n  function rmsOf(buf) {\\n    const d = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n    let s = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i++) s += d[i] * d[i];\\n    return Math.sqrt(s / d.length);\\n  }\\n\\n  async function renderProbe() {\\n    const AC = G.OfflineAudioContext || (typeof OfflineAudioContext !== 'undefined' ? OfflineAudioContext : null);\\n    if (!AC) return null;\\n    async function render(build) {\\n      const ctx = new AC(1, 12000, 22050);\\n      build(ctx);\\n      const buf = await ctx.startRendering();\\n      return rmsOf(buf);\\n    }\\n    const effect = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 440, 'square', 0.2, 0.4));\\n    const voice = await render((ctx) => {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = 280;\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'bandpass';\\n      f.frequency.value = 1100;\\n      f.Q.value = 6;\\n      const g = ctx.createGain();\\n      g.gain.value = 0.35;\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n      o.start(0); o.stop(0.2);\\n    });\\n    const choirR = await render((ctx) => {\\n      for (const freq of [196, 201, 247]) tone(ctx, freq, 'sawtooth', 0.3, 0.12);\\n    });\\n    const music = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'triangle', 0.25, 0.1));\\n    const effects = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'square', 0.25, 1));\\n    return { effect, voice, choir: choirR, music, effects };\\n  }\\n\\n  function onEv(ev) {\\n    if (!ev || !ev.length) return;\\n    const k = ev[0];\\n    if (k === 'grip' || k === 'free') sfx('grip');\\n    else if (k === 'grade' || k === 'stitch') sfx('stitch');\\n    else if (k === 'tear' || k === 'snap' || k === 'miss') sfx('bad');\\n    else if (k === 'shock' || k === 'codeblue') sfx('shock');\\n    else if (k === 'stamp' || k === 'closed') sfx('stamp');\\n    else if (k === 'breath') choir(ev[1] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n  GAME.Audio = { SONGS, install, play, sfx, blip, choir, stopChoir, renderProbe, onEv };\\n})();\\n\",\"total_lines\":211}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"27ff2ae5-7c8e-4ed6-a195-2ca5b48b2126"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_328","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Music gain is 0.1. Effects gain is 1. Both use the same frequency.\n\nRMS music should be about 0.1 of effects, checked at 35%.\nEach tone() connects its oscillators directly to the destination.\nAn audio check will be added to launchOnce or runLive.\nEvidence shots are still needed even if browser tests pass.\nA Playwright-driven shot function is too heavy.\n\nA lightweight Playwright screenshot helper will capture operative sites after the main browser checks. Sites include forearm, abdomen, flank, heart, brain, implant, mediastinum, and ship. The helper runs a page evaluation before capturing at 1920x1080.\n\nEvidence shots will be wrapped in try blocks so failures do not block the suite. The shot pass will open Chromium at 1920x1080 and capture operative sites by beginning a case for each site, advancing to the operator screen, and taking a screenshot. Portraits will be captured after skipping the story. Strain frames will come from cases that include them. The tool wheel will be shown via the operator HUD. A long breath shot will set S.breath before capturing.\n\nEach operative site maps to a specific case ID. Strain cases include c3 staccato, c5 legato, c6 tremolo, c8 dacapo, c9 fermata, and c11 cantor. The hub path in tests needs correction. For the client stroke test, the host is frames[0], so the first cell applies the injected reliable message; at zero latency, eight seconds into the round should be in the play phase.\n\nThe eight-second injection risks landing after the round ends. The conformance runner may have already exited when that delay expires. The stroke test should run during active play instead of after. A separate non-auto page or an earlier injection would be safer.\n\nA simpler stroke test is planned. The harness will run with two players, auto mode enabled, and a twenty-second play duration. The client will poll the hub probe to confirm the round is in the playing phase before injecting the stroke.\n\nThe stroke test will use a dedicated page with a fifteen-second play duration. It will poll the host probe until the phase is 'play', then inject the stroke via evaluate while the round is active.\n\nThe client injects the stroke into the host at player index 1. The host handler updates RT.S.players and stores H.hands immediately, so the position is set before the next step overwrites it.\n\nThe stroke test will pause three hundred milliseconds after injecting the stroke before probing the host. This allows the hub network to deliver the message before the next animation frame overwrites the position.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a1e0c8f5-df04-402a-807b-824e811cd1aa-79","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"t === 'i'|H\\.hands","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/scenes/shell.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1668,"output_tokens":1505,"cache_read_input_tokens":180096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"0d24031c-2efd-4ba4-abb3-381e1e1582ce"}
