{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a6ec7dba-579b-464e-b2f7-1b55c2ec9d64-81","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"320→      move[1] += pan[1] / Math.max(8, Math.hypot(pan[0], pan[1]));\\n    }\\n    return {\\n      digit, mouse, aim, move, keys, nudge,\\n      fine: I.down('fine'),\\n      trig,\\n      gift: I.down('gift'),\\n      consult: I.down('consult'),\\n      cancel: I.down('cancel'),\\n    };\\n330→  }\\n\\n  function drive(S, dt, opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    const inputs = [];\\n    const n = S.players.length;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n      const p = S.players[i];\\n      if (p.gone) { inputs.push({ tool: p.tool, trig: 0 }); continue; }\\n      let dev;\\n340→      if (opts.remote && opts.remote[i]) {\\n        dev = opts.remote[i];\\n      } else if (i === 0 && game.debug && game.debug.driver && !RT.attract) {\\n        dev = game.debug.driver(S, dt) || GAME.Bot.device(S, 0, dt);\\n      } else if (i === 0 && RT.auto && !RT.attract) {\\n        dev = GAME.Bot.device(S, 0, dt);\\n      } else if (i === 0 && !opts.bots && !RT.attract) {\\n        dev = readLocal(p);\\n      } else {\\n        dev = GAME.Bot.device(S, i, dt);\\n350→      }\\n      GAME.Wheel.update(p, dev, dt);\\n      const tune = playTune();\\n      if (dev.mouse) GAME.Cursor.update(p, { mouse: dev.mouse, fine: dev.fine }, S, dt, tune);\\n      else GAME.Cursor.update(p, { aim: dev.aim, keys: dev.keys, nudge: dev.nudge, fine: dev.fine }, S, dt, tune);\\n      const row = {\\n        tool: p.tool,\\n        trig: dev.trig || 0,\\n        fine: !!dev.fine,\\n        gift: !!dev.gift,\\n360→        consult: !!dev.consult,\\n        cancel: !!dev.cancel,\\n        mouse: !!dev.mouse,\\n      };\\n      if (dev.x != null) { row.x = dev.x; row.y = dev.y; }\\n      inputs.push(row);\\n    }\\n    try { GAME.Op.step(S, inputs, dt, playTune()); }\\n    catch (e) { game.fail('op', e); }\\n    if (S.ev) for (const ev of S.ev) { try { GAME.Audio.onEv(ev); } catch (err) { /* quiet */ } }\\n370→    return S;\\n  }\\n\\n  function fieldOf(S) {\\n    const key = (S.site || 'abdomen') + ':' + (S.seed || 1) + ':' + game.W + 'x' + game.H;\",\"content_concise\":\"320→      move[1] += pan[1] / Math.max(8, Math.hypot(pan[0], pan[1]));\\n    }\\n    return {\\n      digit, mouse, aim, move, keys, nudge,\\n      fine: I.down('fine'),\\n      trig,\\n      gift: I.down('gift'),\\n      consult: I.down('consult'),\\n      cancel: I.down('cancel'),\\n    };\\n330→  }\\n\\n  function drive(S, dt, opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    const inputs = [];\\n    const n = S.players.length;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n      const p = S.players[i];\\n      if (p.gone) { inputs.push({ tool: p.tool, trig: 0 }); continue; }\\n      let dev;\\n340→      if (opts.remote && opts.remote[i]) {\\n        dev = opts.remote[i];\\n      } else if (i === 0 && game.debug && game.debug.driver && !RT.attract) {\\n        dev = game.debug.driver(S, dt) || GAME.Bot.device(S, 0, dt);\\n      } else if (i === 0 && RT.auto && !RT.attract) {\\n        dev = GAME.Bot.device(S, 0, dt);\\n      } else if (i === 0 && !opts.bots && !RT.attract) {\\n        dev = readLocal(p);\\n      } else {\\n        dev = GAME.Bot.device(S, i, dt);\\n350→      }\\n      GAME.Wheel.update(p, dev, dt);\\n      const tune = playTune();\\n      if (dev.mouse) GAME.Cursor.update(p, { mouse: dev.mouse, fine: dev.fine }, S, dt, tune);\\n      else GAME.Cursor.update(p, { aim: dev.aim, keys: dev.keys, nudge: dev.nudge, fine: dev.fine }, S, dt, tune);\\n      const row = {\\n        tool: p.tool,\\n        trig: dev.trig || 0,\\n        fine: !!dev.fine,\\n        gift: !!dev.gift,\\n360→        consult: !!dev.consult,\\n        cancel: !!dev.cancel,\\n        mouse: !!dev.mouse,\\n      };\\n      if (dev.x != null) { row.x = dev.x; row.y = dev.y; }\\n      inputs.push(row);\\n    }\\n    try { GAME.Op.step(S, inputs, dt, playTune()); }\\n    catch (e) { game.fail('op', e); }\\n    if (S.ev) for (const ev of S.ev) { try { GAME.Audio.onEv(ev); } catch (err) { /* quiet */ } }\\n370→    return S;\\n  }\\n\\n  function fieldOf(S) {\\n    const key = (S.site || 'abdomen') + ':' + (S.seed || 1) + ':' + game.W + 'x' + game.H;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/scenes/shell.js\",\"offset\":320,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"      move[1] += pan[1] / Math.max(8, Math.hypot(pan[0], pan[1]));\\n    }\\n    return {\\n      digit, mouse, aim, move, keys, nudge,\\n      fine: I.down('fine'),\\n      trig,\\n      gift: I.down('gift'),\\n      consult: I.down('consult'),\\n      cancel: I.down('cancel'),\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  function drive(S, dt, opts) {\\n    opts = opts || {};\\n    const inputs = [];\\n    const n = S.players.length;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {\\n      const p = S.players[i];\\n      if (p.gone) { inputs.push({ tool: p.tool, trig: 0 }); continue; }\\n      let dev;\\n      if (opts.remote && opts.remote[i]) {\\n        dev = opts.remote[i];\\n      } else if (i === 0 && game.debug && game.debug.driver && !RT.attract) {\\n        dev = game.debug.driver(S, dt) || GAME.Bot.device(S, 0, dt);\\n      } else if (i === 0 && RT.auto && !RT.attract) {\\n        dev = GAME.Bot.device(S, 0, dt);\\n      } else if (i === 0 && !opts.bots && !RT.attract) {\\n        dev = readLocal(p);\\n      } else {\\n        dev = GAME.Bot.device(S, i, dt);\\n      }\\n      GAME.Wheel.update(p, dev, dt);\\n      const tune = playTune();\\n      if (dev.mouse) GAME.Cursor.update(p, { mouse: dev.mouse, fine: dev.fine }, S, dt, tune);\\n      else GAME.Cursor.update(p, { aim: dev.aim, keys: dev.keys, nudge: dev.nudge, fine: dev.fine }, S, dt, tune);\\n      const row = {\\n        tool: p.tool,\\n        trig: dev.trig || 0,\\n        fine: !!dev.fine,\\n        gift: !!dev.gift,\\n        consult: !!dev.consult,\\n        cancel: !!dev.cancel,\\n        mouse: !!dev.mouse,\\n      };\\n      if (dev.x != null) { row.x = dev.x; row.y = dev.y; }\\n      inputs.push(row);\\n    }\\n    try { GAME.Op.step(S, inputs, dt, playTune()); }\\n    catch (e) { game.fail('op', e); }\\n    if (S.ev) for (const ev of S.ev) { try { GAME.Audio.onEv(ev); } catch (err) { /* quiet */ } }\\n    return S;\\n  }\\n\\n  function fieldOf(S) {\\n    const key = (S.site || 'abdomen') + ':' + (S.seed || 1) + ':' + game.W + 'x' + game.H;\\n\",\"total_lines\":1395}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"d907f1ce-62fd-4233-a3d7-3ff2dcc6168b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_331","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The step function sets position directly from x and y inputs. This prevents cursor drift when aim is [0,0].\n\nThe builder, content, feedback, progress, and hub audio and shot tests still need writing. The goal character count for hub meta must be copied exactly from the appendix. The regex that extracts the Python HTTP server port from stderr may fail because the message lacks a colon before the port number.\n\nThe Python HTTP server regex will be updated to match both `port 8000` and `:8000` formats. Only one or two browsers should run at a time under earlyoom.\n\nThe full test suite will run for about six minutes. The sequence is launches, thirty-second browser tests, glyphs, touch, shots, and hub. Each browser closes before the next page opens. A fifteen-minute timeout should be set.\n\nHub tests will run before shots so that shots still complete if the hub page runs out of memory. Audio will be injected into the first launch page before it closes. The build.mjs script still needs to be written. The HTML may be several megabytes, which is acceptable. An escape function will sanitize engine and game code for script injection, though session.js itself requires no escaping.\n\nThe builder will write exit-interview.json by evaluating about.js. It may also copy harness files to the dev folder root.\n\nA dev index page is unnecessary because the hand-in bundle already contains everything. The remaining files to write are CONTENT.md, notes/feedback.md, and PROGRESS.md.\n\nThe stroke test waits eight seconds before injecting input, which may occur after the round ends. That section will be rewritten. The Python server regex will also be fixed. The engine confirms game.shell exists at line 3950.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7f04da4d-ffcc-431f-8a1d-4ea34f4b5304-82","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Controller or keyboard required|Settings","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":15}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1009,"output_tokens":1194,"cache_read_input_tokens":184448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"27b6e5c4-fd3d-4ab6-b46f-36f4a963ca95"}
