",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"        if (fast) {\\n          for (let k = 0; k < 16; k++) drive(S, 1 / 45);\\n        } else drive(S, dt);\",\"old_line\":1035,\"new_string\":\"        if (fast) {\\n          for (let k = 0; k < 16; k++) drive(S, 1 / 45);\\n        } else drive(S, dt);\\n        const mv = game.input.padMove || [0, 0];\\n        if (Math.hypot(mv[0] || 0, mv[1] || 0) > 0.6 || game.input.down('wheelHold')) RT.wheelShow = 0.35;\\n        else RT.wheelShow = Math.max(0, (RT.wheelShow || 0) - dt);\",\"new_line\":1035,\"context_before\":\"        handleDev();\\n        game.focus(game.W / 2, game.H / 2, 0);\\n        const fast = game.debug && game.debug.driver && !RT.attract;\\n\",\"context_after\":\"        if ((S.won || S.lost) && !RT.leftOp) {\\n          RT.leftOp = true;\\n          if (!RT.attract) go('results');\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"f33eb9fc-668a-4069-b4e5-636c677ca4e1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_336","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"RT.wheelShow does not need initialization. The check only requires a value greater than zero.\n\nWriting build.mjs, CONTENT.md, feedback.md, and patch tests. The RT object will include wheelShow. Build.mjs will follow the specified manifest order and output to work/FILE.html. A local dev/game.html harness copy is also planned.\n\nVendor files will stay in place and the test will reference them directly. The builder will load about.js via Node.js vm to generate exit-interview.json from about-data.json, using a context where window and globalThis both point to the same object.\n\nPROGRESS.md will be written by hand to track completed tasks. The builder will generate notes/feedback.md from the about object so it matches the JSON output. build.mjs will bundle the HTML and write exit-interview.json.\n\nPatching run.mjs for hub, audio, and shots. The wheel change is draw-only and should not affect simulation state, so the fast test may be skipped. Documentation will be written while tests run in parallel.\n\nFiles will be written before the test to avoid conflicts. The hub harness path is set relative to the work directory. Stroke tests will be replaced. Audio initialization will move into launchOnce after the title check and before confirm, running renderProbe asynchronously on the page.\n\nAudio tests will verify that effects, voices, and the choir are all audible, and that music remains below 35% of effect volume. Results will be logged to handoff.log. Hub screenshots take priority over shots.\n\nA full shot list is being drafted for the test suite. It covers case-specific scenes, the story portraits, and a wheel view with RT.wheelShow set to 3.\n\nThe long-breath shot will set a small world scale and enable breathing. Because game.go is deferred, the test will wait 350 milliseconds after evaluate to let the scene settle. Fade time will be zeroed during evaluation to prevent mid-fade screenshots. Ward portraits will be captured by loading saved data and advancing through the story one portrait at a time.\n\nThe ward portrait shot will load saved characters and advance to chapter two. The game variable is accessed as window.GAME.Shell.game inside evaluate blocks. Shot helpers will be passed as strings of actions. The title shot already exists as launch-1.png. run.mjs will be patched using search_replace for the hub function and launchOnce.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-43158792-e6b0-40e6-9eb6-ac5c172c7e16-90","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/tools/build.mjs","old_string":"","new_string":"/* Bundle the self-contained page and the exit interview from the same About object. */\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nconst dev = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\nconst work = path.resolve(dev, '..');\nconst scripts = [\n  'src/config.js',\n  'src/core/sim.js',\n  'src/data/content.js',\n  'src/art/field.js',\n  'src/audio/audio.js',\n  'src/about.js',\n  'src/bot/bot.js',\n  'src/scenes/shell.js',\n];\n\nfunction esc(code) {\n  return code.replace(/<\\/script/gi, '<\\\\/script');\n}\n\nconst session = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'vendor/hub/session.js'), 'utf8');\nconst engine = esc(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js'), 'utf8'));\nconst game = esc(scripts.map((rel) => fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, rel), 'utf8')).join('\\n'));\n\nconst ctx = {};\nctx.window = ctx;\nctx.globalThis = ctx;\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nvm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'src/about.js'), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: 'about.js' });\nconst about = ctx.GAME.ABOUT;\nconst title = about.aiHub.name;\nconst file = 'Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916';\n\nconst splash = '<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">OPEN TABLE SECOND OPINION</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.89.1</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game\\'s script did not run: reload, or open the browser\\'s console.</span></div>';\n\nconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>${session}</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\"><meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\"><title>${title}</title>\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\n<body>${splash}<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas><script>${engine}</script><script>${game}</script></body></html>\n`;\n\nconst out = path.join(work, file + '.html');\nfs.writeFileSync(out, html);\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dev, 'game.html'), html);\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(work, 'exit-interview.json'), JSON.stringify(about, null, 2) + '\\n');\n\nconst lines = [];\nlines.push('# Notes');\nlines.push('');\nlines.push('These are the same answers as the About screen and exit-interview.json.');\nlines.push('');\nlines.push('## Source Information');\nfor (const [k, v] of Object.entries(about.sourceInformation)) lines.push('- ' + k + ': ' + v);\nlines.push('');\nlines.push('## Testing Feedback');\nabout.testingFeedback.forEach((t, i) => lines.push((i + 1) + '. ' + t));\nlines.push('');\nlines.push('## Engine Feedback');\nabout.engineFeedback.forEach((t, i) => lines.push((i + 1) + '. ' + t));\nlines.push('');\nlines.push('## Prompt Feedback');\nabout.promptFeedback.forEach((t, i) => lines.push((i + 1) + '. ' + t));\nlines.push('');\nfs.mkdirSync(path.join(dev, 'notes'), { recursive: true });\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dev, 'notes/feedback.md'), lines.join('\\n'));\nconsole.log('wrote ' + out + ' (' + html.length + ' bytes)');\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-43158792-e6b0-40e6-9eb6-ac5c172c7e16-91","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/CONTENT.md","old_string":"","new_string":"# Adding content\n\nThe operation sim in `src/core/sim.js` does not need an edit to add a case, a strain you already have, a site, a character, or a story node. Put the new data in `src/data/content.js` and, for a new portrait, `src/art/field.js`.\n\n## A case\n\nAdd an object to `CASES` and its id to `ORDER`.\n\n- `id`, `name`, `patient`, `chapter`, `doctor` (`vale`, `sokolova`, or `both`), `site`, `clock`, `vitals`, `drain`, `par`, `brief`.\n- `phases`: a list of `{ name, objects, strain, strainOpts, flags, at, tutorial, dim, tilt, device }`.\n- An object is a plain spec. `addObj` fills `origin`, `axis`, `depth`, stitch `pairs`, salve `cells`, and a mass `guide`. Set `order` so a pool is cleared before the thing under it. `needsWindow` waits for the retractor. `hidden` waits for sonar.\n- `at` entries are `{ t, do }` and fire from `runScript` names that already exist (`lurch`, `look`, `breath`, and the rest in the sim). A new verb is the one change that touches the sim.\n- A second-opinion film is a `LIGHT[id]` entry `{ mark: [x, y], text, right, wrong }` in field pixels. The story node sends the player there with `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` only after a chart scene; cases without a `LIGHT` entry go straight to the operation.\n\n`par` is the score a clean run should beat by about five percent for an S. Rank is score/par: S at 95%, A at 80%, B at 60%, C at 40%.\n\n## A strain\n\nThe six strains are `staccato`, `legato`, `tremolo`, `dacapo`, `fermata`, and `cantor`. Put `strain: 'legato'` (and `strainOpts`) on a phase. `spawnStrain` builds the organs. A new kind of parasite means a new branch in `spawnStrain` and `stepStrain`. Tuning that already exists is `strains.speed`, `health`, `spawn`, `damage`, and `beat` in `src/config.js`.\n\n## A site\n\n`site` on the case is a name `fieldFor` already paints: `forearm`, `abdomen`, `flank`, `heart`, `brain`, `implant`, `mediastinum`, `ship`. A new site is a new branch in `TissueField` in `src/art/field.js`. The sim only stores the name.\n\n## A character\n\nAdd an id to `CAST` with `name`, `role`, and `hue`. Add the same id to `PEOPLE` with `lines` for the ward. `EXPR` can add a face. The story `who` field uses that id. Busts are drawn by `GAME.Art.bust`. The ward shows a saved patient when their id is in `WARD[chapter]` and in the save.\n\n## A story node\n\n`NODES` is a map of id to a list of steps.\n\n- A line is `{ who, say, expr }`.\n- A choice is `{ who, say, choices: [{ text, goto }] }`. Skip does not pick one.\n- `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` then `{ goto: 'cN_out' }` runs the operation and resumes on the way out.\n- `{ event: 'ward', chapter, wait: true }` opens the walkable ward.\n- `{ event: 'credits', wait: true }` opens the credits. The last page resumes the story.\n- `{ end: true }` returns to the title.\n\nWire the first node from `start`, or from the previous node's `goto`. The sim is not involved.\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-43158792-e6b0-40e6-9eb6-ac5c172c7e16-92","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PROGRESS.md","old_string":"","new_string":"# Progress\n\nOpen Table Second Opinion is playable from the work-folder HTML and from the dev folder of the same name.\n\nDone on this machine:\n\n- Eleven operations, the story between them, the ward, the credits, and a post-credits Incoming chart that does not start another operation.\n- Eight tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, Second Look, the Lightbox on cases 2, 4, and 10, Skills Lab, and couch Grand Rounds.\n- AI Hub shared world for 1–4 surgeons. The host simulates. Clients send hands.\n- Attract reel, dev mode, TV-scale shell, PlayStation prompts with an Xbox option, and a touch notice with no touch buttons.\n- Synthesized music, effects, choir, and gibberish voices. Music starts at 10%.\n- `node tests/run.mjs` in the dev folder loads the shipped scripts. `--fast` skips the browser and the Hub.\n\nNot available here: a second person, a physical pad, and a real phone. Those checks use Playwright, a scripted pad, and an iPhone profile in WebKit.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1971,"output_tokens":4111,"cache_read_input_tokens":192640,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"211cbd20-76f9-454f-8cb6-b71b3d7d3ae9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-43158792-e6b0-40e6-9eb6-ac5c172c7e16-90","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/* Bundle the self-contained page and the exit interview from the same About object. */\\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\n\\nconst dev = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\\nconst work = path.resolve(dev, '..');\\nconst scripts = [\\n  'src/config.js',\\n  'src/core/sim.js',\\n  'src/data/content.js',\\n  'src/art/field.js',\\n  'src/audio/audio.js',\\n  'src/about.js',\\n  'src/bot/bot.js',\\n  'src/scenes/shell.js',\\n];\\n\\nfunction esc(code) {\\n  return code.replace(/<\\\\/script/gi, '<\\\\\\\\/script');\\n}\\n\\nconst session = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'vendor/hub/session.js'), 'utf8');\\nconst engine = esc(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js'), 'utf8'));\\nconst game = esc(scripts.map((rel) => fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, rel), 'utf8')).join('\\\\n'));\\n\\nconst ctx = {};\\nctx.window = ctx;\\nctx.globalThis = ctx;\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nvm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'src/about.js'), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: 'about.js' });\\nconst about = ctx.GAME.ABOUT;\\nconst title = about.aiHub.name;\\nconst file = 'Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916';\\n\\nconst splash = '<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\" role=\\\"status\\\" style=\\\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\\\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\\\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\\\">OPEN TABLE SECOND OPINION</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.89.1</span><span style=\\\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\\\"><span style=\\\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\\\"></span></span><span style=\\\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\\\">Still starting. If this stays, the game\\\\'s script did not run: reload, or open the browser\\\\'s console.</span></div>';\\n\\nconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>${session}</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>${title}</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body>${splash}<canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>${engine}</script><script>${game}</script></body></html>\\n`;\\n\\nconst out = path.join(work, file + '.html');\\nfs.writeFileSync(out, html);\\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dev, 'game.html'), html);\\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(work, 'exit-interview.json'), JSON.stringify(about, null, 2) + '\\\\n');\\n\\nconst lines = [];\\nlines.push('# Notes');\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('These are the same answers as the About screen and exit-interview.json.');\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('## Source Information');\\nfor (const [k, v] of Object.entries(about.sourceInformation)) lines.push('- ' + k + ': ' + v);\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('## Testing Feedback');\\nabout.testingFeedback.forEach((t, i) => lines.push((i + 1) + '. ' + t));\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('## Engine Feedback');\\nabout.engineFeedback.forEach((t, i) => lines.push((i + 1) + '. ' + t));\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('## Prompt Feedback');\\nabout.promptFeedback.forEach((t, i) => lines.push((i + 1) + '. ' + t));\\nlines.push('');\\nfs.mkdirSync(path.join(dev, 'notes'), { recursive: true });\\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dev, 'notes/feedback.md'), lines.join('\\\\n'));\\nconsole.log('wrote ' + out + ' (' + html.length + ' bytes)');\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/tools/build.mjs has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/tools/build.mjs has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/tools/build.mjs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/* Bundle the self-contained page and the exit interview from the same About object. */\\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\\nimport path from 'node:path';\\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\n\\nconst dev = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\\nconst work = path.resolve(dev, '..');\\nconst scripts = [\\n  'src/config.js',\\n  'src/core/sim.js',\\n  'src/data/content.js',\\n  'src/art/field.js',\\n  'src/audio/audio.js',\\n  'src/about.js',\\n  'src/bot/bot.js',\\n  'src/scenes/shell.js',\\n];\\n\\nfunction esc(code) {\\n  return code.replace(/<\\\\/script/gi, '<\\\\\\\\/script');\\n}\\n\\nconst session = fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'vendor/hub/session.js'), 'utf8');\\nconst engine = esc(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js'), 'utf8'));\\nconst game = esc(scripts.map((rel) => fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, rel), 'utf8')).join('\\\\n'));\\n\\nconst ctx = {};\\nctx.window = ctx;\\nctx.globalThis = ctx;\\nvm.createContext(ctx);\\nvm.runInContext(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dev, 'src/about.js'), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: 'about.js' });\\nconst about = ctx.GAME.ABOUT;\\nconst title = about.aiHub.name;\\nconst file = 'Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916';\\n\\nconst splash = '<div id=\\\"e3-boot\\\" role=\\\"status\\\" style=\\\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\\\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\\\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\\\">OPEN TABLE SECOND OPINION</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.89.1</span><span style=\\\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\\\"><span style=\\\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\\\"></span></span><span style=\\\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\\\">Still starting. If this stays, the game\\\\'s script did not run: reload, or open the browser\\\\'s console.</span></div>';\\n\\nconst html = `<!doctype html><html lang=\\\"en\\\"><head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script>${session}</script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\"><meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"5\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Save the patient together; best hands top the board\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Aim: right stick or mouse. Use tool: R2 or click. Tools: left stick or 1-8\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\\\"><title>${title}</title>\\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}html .esh-row small{display:none}html .esh-row:focus-within small{display:block}</style></head>\\n<body>${splash}<canvas id=\\\"screen\\\"></canvas><script>${engine}</script><script>${game}</script></body></html>\\n`;\\n\\nconst out = path.join(work, file + '.html');\\nfs.writeFileSync(out, html);\\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dev, 'game.html'), html);\\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(work, 'exit-interview.json'), JSON.stringify(about, null, 2) + '\\\\n');\\n\\nconst lines = [];\\nlines.push('# Notes');\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('These are the same answers as the About screen and exit-interview.json.');\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('## Source Information');\\nfor (const [k, v] of Object.entries(about.sourceInformation)) lines.push('- ' + k + ': ' + v);\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('## Testing Feedback');\\nabout.testingFeedback.forEach((t, i) => lines.push((i + 1) + '. ' + t));\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('## Engine Feedback');\\nabout.engineFeedback.forEach((t, i) => lines.push((i + 1) + '. ' + t));\\nlines.push('');\\nlines.push('## Prompt Feedback');\\nabout.promptFeedback.forEach((t, i) => lines.push((i + 1) + '. ' + t));\\nlines.push('');\\nfs.mkdirSync(path.join(dev, 'notes'), { recursive: true });\\nfs.writeFileSync(path.join(dev, 'notes/feedback.md'), lines.join('\\\\n'));\\nconsole.log('wrote ' + out + ' (' + html.length + ' bytes)');\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-43158792-e6b0-40e6-9eb6-ac5c172c7e16-91","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Adding content\\n\\nThe operation sim in `src/core/sim.js` does not need an edit to add a case, a strain you already have, a site, a character, or a story node. Put the new data in `src/data/content.js` and, for a new portrait, `src/art/field.js`.\\n\\n## A case\\n\\nAdd an object to `CASES` and its id to `ORDER`.\\n\\n- `id`, `name`, `patient`, `chapter`, `doctor` (`vale`, `sokolova`, or `both`), `site`, `clock`, `vitals`, `drain`, `par`, `brief`.\\n- `phases`: a list of `{ name, objects, strain, strainOpts, flags, at, tutorial, dim, tilt, device }`.\\n- An object is a plain spec. `addObj` fills `origin`, `axis`, `depth`, stitch `pairs`, salve `cells`, and a mass `guide`. Set `order` so a pool is cleared before the thing under it. `needsWindow` waits for the retractor. `hidden` waits for sonar.\\n- `at` entries are `{ t, do }` and fire from `runScript` names that already exist (`lurch`, `look`, `breath`, and the rest in the sim). A new verb is the one change that touches the sim.\\n- A second-opinion film is a `LIGHT[id]` entry `{ mark: [x, y], text, right, wrong }` in field pixels. The story node sends the player there with `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` only after a chart scene; cases without a `LIGHT` entry go straight to the operation.\\n\\n`par` is the score a clean run should beat by about five percent for an S. Rank is score/par: S at 95%, A at 80%, B at 60%, C at 40%.\\n\\n## A strain\\n\\nThe six strains are `staccato`, `legato`, `tremolo`, `dacapo`, `fermata`, and `cantor`. Put `strain: 'legato'` (and `strainOpts`) on a phase. `spawnStrain` builds the organs. A new kind of parasite means a new branch in `spawnStrain` and `stepStrain`. Tuning that already exists is `strains.speed`, `health`, `spawn`, `damage`, and `beat` in `src/config.js`.\\n\\n## A site\\n\\n`site` on the case is a name `fieldFor` already paints: `forearm`, `abdomen`, `flank`, `heart`, `brain`, `implant`, `mediastinum`, `ship`. A new site is a new branch in `TissueField` in `src/art/field.js`. The sim only stores the name.\\n\\n## A character\\n\\nAdd an id to `CAST` with `name`, `role`, and `hue`. Add the same id to `PEOPLE` with `lines` for the ward. `EXPR` can add a face. The story `who` field uses that id. Busts are drawn by `GAME.Art.bust`. The ward shows a saved patient when their id is in `WARD[chapter]` and in the save.\\n\\n## A story node\\n\\n`NODES` is a map of id to a list of steps.\\n\\n- A line is `{ who, say, expr }`.\\n- A choice is `{ who, say, choices: [{ text, goto }] }`. Skip does not pick one.\\n- `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` then `{ goto: 'cN_out' }` runs the operation and resumes on the way out.\\n- `{ event: 'ward', chapter, wait: true }` opens the walkable ward.\\n- `{ event: 'credits', wait: true }` opens the credits. The last page resumes the story.\\n- `{ end: true }` returns to the title.\\n\\nWire the first node from `start`, or from the previous node's `goto`. The sim is not involved.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/CONTENT.md has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/CONTENT.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/CONTENT.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Adding content\\n\\nThe operation sim in `src/core/sim.js` does not need an edit to add a case, a strain you already have, a site, a character, or a story node. Put the new data in `src/data/content.js` and, for a new portrait, `src/art/field.js`.\\n\\n## A case\\n\\nAdd an object to `CASES` and its id to `ORDER`.\\n\\n- `id`, `name`, `patient`, `chapter`, `doctor` (`vale`, `sokolova`, or `both`), `site`, `clock`, `vitals`, `drain`, `par`, `brief`.\\n- `phases`: a list of `{ name, objects, strain, strainOpts, flags, at, tutorial, dim, tilt, device }`.\\n- An object is a plain spec. `addObj` fills `origin`, `axis`, `depth`, stitch `pairs`, salve `cells`, and a mass `guide`. Set `order` so a pool is cleared before the thing under it. `needsWindow` waits for the retractor. `hidden` waits for sonar.\\n- `at` entries are `{ t, do }` and fire from `runScript` names that already exist (`lurch`, `look`, `breath`, and the rest in the sim). A new verb is the one change that touches the sim.\\n- A second-opinion film is a `LIGHT[id]` entry `{ mark: [x, y], text, right, wrong }` in field pixels. The story node sends the player there with `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` only after a chart scene; cases without a `LIGHT` entry go straight to the operation.\\n\\n`par` is the score a clean run should beat by about five percent for an S. Rank is score/par: S at 95%, A at 80%, B at 60%, C at 40%.\\n\\n## A strain\\n\\nThe six strains are `staccato`, `legato`, `tremolo`, `dacapo`, `fermata`, and `cantor`. Put `strain: 'legato'` (and `strainOpts`) on a phase. `spawnStrain` builds the organs. A new kind of parasite means a new branch in `spawnStrain` and `stepStrain`. Tuning that already exists is `strains.speed`, `health`, `spawn`, `damage`, and `beat` in `src/config.js`.\\n\\n## A site\\n\\n`site` on the case is a name `fieldFor` already paints: `forearm`, `abdomen`, `flank`, `heart`, `brain`, `implant`, `mediastinum`, `ship`. A new site is a new branch in `TissueField` in `src/art/field.js`. The sim only stores the name.\\n\\n## A character\\n\\nAdd an id to `CAST` with `name`, `role`, and `hue`. Add the same id to `PEOPLE` with `lines` for the ward. `EXPR` can add a face. The story `who` field uses that id. Busts are drawn by `GAME.Art.bust`. The ward shows a saved patient when their id is in `WARD[chapter]` and in the save.\\n\\n## A story node\\n\\n`NODES` is a map of id to a list of steps.\\n\\n- A line is `{ who, say, expr }`.\\n- A choice is `{ who, say, choices: [{ text, goto }] }`. Skip does not pick one.\\n- `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` then `{ goto: 'cN_out' }` runs the operation and resumes on the way out.\\n- `{ event: 'ward', chapter, wait: true }` opens the walkable ward.\\n- `{ event: 'credits', wait: true }` opens the credits. The last page resumes the story.\\n- `{ end: true }` returns to the title.\\n\\nWire the first node from `start`, or from the previous node's `goto`. The sim is not involved.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-43158792-e6b0-40e6-9eb6-ac5c172c7e16-92","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"# Progress\\n\\nOpen Table Second Opinion is playable from the work-folder HTML and from the dev folder of the same name.\\n\\nDone on this machine:\\n\\n- Eleven operations, the story between them, the ward, the credits, and a post-credits Incoming chart that does not start another operation.\\n- Eight tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, Second Look, the Lightbox on cases 2, 4, and 10, Skills Lab, and couch Grand Rounds.\\n- AI Hub shared world for 1–4 surgeons. The host simulates. Clients send hands.\\n- Attract reel, dev mode, TV-scale shell, PlayStation prompts with an Xbox option, and a touch notice with no touch buttons.\\n- Synthesized music, effects, choir, and gibberish voices. Music starts at 10%.\\n- `node tests/run.mjs` in the dev folder loads the shipped scripts. `--fast` skips the browser and the Hub.\\n\\nNot available here: a second person, a physical pad, and a real phone. Those checks use Playwright, a scripted pad, and an iPhone profile in WebKit.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PROGRESS.md has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PROGRESS.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# Progress\\n\\nOpen Table Second Opinion is playable from the work-folder HTML and from the dev folder of the same name.\\n\\nDone on this machine:\\n\\n- Eleven operations, the story between them, the ward, the credits, and a post-credits Incoming chart that does not start another operation.\\n- Eight tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, Second Look, the Lightbox on cases 2, 4, and 10, Skills Lab, and couch Grand Rounds.\\n- AI Hub shared world for 1–4 surgeons. The host simulates. Clients send hands.\\n- Attract reel, dev mode, TV-scale shell, PlayStation prompts with an Xbox option, and a touch notice with no touch buttons.\\n- Synthesized music, effects, choir, and gibberish voices. Music starts at 10%.\\n- `node tests/run.mjs` in the dev folder loads the shipped scripts. `--fast` skips the browser and the Hub.\\n\\nNot available here: a second person, a physical pad, and a real phone. Those checks use Playwright, a scripted pad, and an iPhone profile in WebKit.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_i