{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_356","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Touch detection uses the CSS media query `(pointer: coarse) && !(any-pointer: fine)`.\n\nPlaywright iPhone emulation should set the touch pointer media query, though WebKit may ignore it. The settings screen hides the notice via `shell.screen`, and the test checks for `opened.screen === 'settings'`. Next steps are adding a launch log write and injecting a pin so strokes persist.\n\nI'll poll in the test and check audio renderProbe for exceptions. The pin will be injected via shell.js __hubInject and the client send loop. Mouse coordinates may be negative after origin subtraction, but the injected pin overrides them. I'll read about.js for exact feedback text later. The stroke test waits for the host phase to play.\n\nThe host creates the case before the client is ready, so the stroke exists when play begins. The injected pin coordinates persist because the host keeps them for 400 ms. Unreliable messages may drop, but the reliable inject should arrive and the client's player ID matches the host lookup.\n\nThe reliable inject can arrive before the host phase becomes play. The handler still writes the position and hand state, so applyHands uses it once play begins. The test waits for play to start, so this timing is safe.\n\nI will also write launch.log.\n\nThe source hygiene check only walks src, not game.html in the dev root. The bundle includes a clean engine, and about.js may not be checked for forbidden names in the fast suite.\n\nI will grep the built HTML for forbidden names after building, and I already confirmed shell.js contains no placeholder comments. The worst-case test run is roughly eight minutes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a29fc78-1f63-4b0f-b5b5-542b76f1ba83-44","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/audio/audio.js","offset":150,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a29fc78-1f63-4b0f-b5b5-542b76f1ba83-45","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/scenes/shell.js","old_string":"          H.accI += dt;\n          if (H.accI >= 1 / 15) {\n            H.accI = 0;\n            const ptr = mine.mouse || [p.x, p.y];\n            HUB.send({\n              t: 'i', n: ++H.inN,\n              x: Math.round(ptr[0]), y: Math.round(ptr[1]),\n              trig: mine.trig > 0.3 ? 1 : 0,\n              digit: mine.digit || 0,\n            }, { to: info.host, reliable: false });\n          }","new_string":"          H.accI += dt;\n          if (H.accI >= 1 / 15) {\n            H.accI = 0;\n            const ptr = mine.mouse || [p.x, p.y];\n            const pin = H.pin;\n            HUB.send({\n              t: 'i', n: ++H.inN,\n              x: pin ? pin.x : Math.round(ptr[0]),\n              y: pin ? pin.y : Math.round(ptr[1]),\n              trig: pin ? (pin.trig || 0) : (mine.trig > 0.3 ? 1 : 0),\n              digit: mine.digit || 0,\n            }, { to: info.host, reliable: false });\n          }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a29fc78-1f63-4b0f-b5b5-542b76f1ba83-46","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/scenes/shell.js","old_string":"    try {\n      HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++H.inN, x, y, trig: trig || 0, digit: 0 }, { to: H.info.host, reliable: true });\n    } catch (e) { /* not in a session */ }","new_string":"    H.pin = { x, y, trig: trig || 0 };\n    try {\n      HUB.send({ t: 'i', n: ++H.inN, x, y, trig: trig || 0, digit: 0 }, { to: H.info.host, reliable: true });\n    } catch (e) { /* not in a session */ }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a29fc78-1f63-4b0f-b5b5-542b76f1ba83-47","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/tests/run.mjs","old_string":"    await launchOnce('launch-1');\n    await launchOnce('launch-2');","new_string":"    await launchOnce('launch-1');\n    await launchOnce('launch-2');\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(scratch, 'launch.log'), browserLog.filter((l) => l.startsWith('launch-')).join('\\n') + '\\n');"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2156,"output_tokens":1640,"cache_read_input_tokens":113536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"4998dac6-b034-4fe8-84a0-27e813c4e560"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9a29fc78-1f63-4b0f-b5b5-542b76f1ba83-44","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"150→  function tone(ctx, freq, type, dur, gain) {\\n    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = type;\\n    o.frequency.value = freq;\\n    const g = ctx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, 0);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, dur);\\n    o.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n    o.start(0); o.stop(dur);\\n  }\\n160→\\n  function rmsOf(buf) {\\n    const d = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n    let s = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i++) s += d[i] * d[i];\\n    return Math.sqrt(s / d.length);\\n  }\\n\\n  async function renderProbe() {\\n    const AC = G.OfflineAudioContext || (typeof OfflineAudioContext !== 'undefined' ? OfflineAudioContext : null);\\n170→    if (!AC) return null;\\n    async function render(build) {\\n      const ctx = new AC(1, 12000, 22050);\\n      build(ctx);\\n      const buf = await ctx.startRendering();\\n      return rmsOf(buf);\\n    }\\n    const effect = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 440, 'square', 0.2, 0.4));\\n    const voice = await render((ctx) => {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n180→      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = 280;\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'bandpass';\\n      f.frequency.value = 1100;\\n      f.Q.value = 6;\\n      const g = ctx.createGain();\\n      g.gain.value = 0.35;\\n      o.connect(f); f.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n      o.start(0); o.stop(0.2);\\n190→    });\\n    const choirR = await render((ctx) => {\\n      for (const freq of [196, 201, 247]) tone(ctx, freq, 'sawtooth', 0.3, 0.12);\\n    });\\n    const music = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'triangle', 0.25, 0.1));\\n    const effects = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 330, 'square', 0.25, 1));\\n    return { effect, voice, choir: choirR, music, effects };\\n  }\\n\\n  function onEv(ev) {\\n200→    if (!ev || !ev.length) return;\\n    const k = ev[0];\\n    if (k === 'grip' || k === 'free') sfx('grip');\\n    else if (k === 'grade' || k === 'stitch') sfx('stitch');\\n    else if (k === 'tear' || k === 'snap' || k === 'miss') sfx('bad');\\n    else if (k === 'shock' || k === 'codeblue') sfx('shock');\\n    else if (k === 'stamp' || k === 'closed') sfx('stamp');\\n    else if (k === 'breath') choir(ev[1] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n210→  GAME.Audio = { SONGS, install, play, sfx, blip, choir, stopChoir, renderProbe, onEv };\\n})();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"150→  function tone(ctx, freq, type, dur, gain) {\\n    const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n    o.type = type;\\n    o.frequency.value = freq;\\n    const g = ctx.createGain();\\n    g.gain.setValueAtTime(gain, 0);\\n    g.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.0001, dur);\\n    o.connect(g); g.connect(ctx.destination);\\n    o.start(0); o.stop(dur);\\n  }\\n160→\\n  function rmsOf(buf) {\\n    const d = buf.getChannelData(0);\\n    let s = 0;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < d.length; i++) s += d[i] * d[i];\\n    return Math.sqrt(s / d.length);\\n  }\\n\\n  async function renderProbe() {\\n    const AC = G.OfflineAudioContext || (typeof OfflineAudioContext !== 'undefined' ? OfflineAudioContext : null);\\n170→    if (!AC) return null;\\n    async function render(build) {\\n      const ctx = new AC(1, 12000, 22050);\\n      build(ctx);\\n      const buf = await ctx.startRendering();\\n      return rmsOf(buf);\\n    }\\n    const effect = await render((ctx) => tone(ctx, 440, 'square', 0.2, 0.4));\\n    const voice = await render((ctx) => {\\n      const o = ctx.createOscillator();\\n180→      o.type = 'sawtooth';\\n      o.frequency.value = 280;\\n      const f = ctx.createBiquadFilter();\\n      f.type = 'bandpass';\\n      f.frequency.value = 1100;\\n      f.Q.value = 6;\\n      const g = ctx.createGain();\\n      g.gain.value = 0.35;\\n      o.connect(f); f.connec