{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_372","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Python wheel includes playwright-core version 1.\n\nplaywright-core exports chromium, firefox, webkit, and devices. The current code imports these from the playwright package.\n\nA fallback import from playwright-core is not viable because the dev folder cannot resolve it without NODE_PATH. The verifier re-runs tests locally, so the import must work without environment variables.\n\nA symlink re-export is too fragile. Installing the full npm package locally is a better option, though it may be large. The verifier might not copy node_modules if only source files are provided.\n\nThe verifier audits committed evidence rather than rebuilding tests, but may re-run the test script locally. Installing playwright in the dev folder's node_modules fixes this import issue. A fallback using Node's module resolution API is also being considered.\n\nHardcoding absolute paths to the local node_modules is fragile for a verifier running elsewhere. Installing playwright into the dev folder's node_modules is more portable, though it may require network access.\n\nSymlinking the existing playwright and playwright-core packages into the dev folder's node_modules is now being considered. This would resolve the import without installing a new copy. The hygiene walk skips node_modules, so this symlink would not affect the bundle.\n\nnpm install is preferred over symlinks for a self-contained setup. The monitor process will be killed since the test has already failed.\n\nThe monitor will be killed if it is still running. The import will be simplified to just 'playwright'. Cached browser revisions in ~/.cache/ms-playwright must match the expected versions before launching. The runner filters NO_COLOR warnings. Node_modules is not a git task.\n\nnpm install will use --ignore-scripts to prevent Playwright's postinstall script from downloading browsers. The existing cache will be used instead. Both playwright and playwright-core will be installed without scripts.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8dbb5d3d-bdd3-4311-9cb0-933beb203895-75","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='/home/micha/.local/lib/python3.14/site-packages/playwright/driver/package/browsers.json'\nb=json.load(open(p))\nfor x in b.get('browsers', b if isinstance(b, list) else []):\n    if isinstance(x, dict):\n        print(x.get('name'), x.get('revision'), x.get('installByDefault'))\nPY\nls ~/.cache/ms-playwright","description":"Match cached browser revisions to Playwright 1.63"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8dbb5d3d-bdd3-4311-9cb0-933beb203895-76","name":"kill_command_or_subagent","input":{"task_id":"2ffca321-f75f-4927-8ef7-b9645ba7ecd9"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":980,"output_tokens":1485,"cache_read_input_tokens":137984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"cb079e7c-ae61-490c-97d2-202917b28d2e"}
