{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_374","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Chromium launched. Checking whether npm install --no-save created a package.json.\n\nnpm install added 2 packages. node_modules exists. Checking if --no-save created a package.json. A test package.json would help the verifier. I will not expand scope.\n\nnode_modules is present so the current run works. Leaving it in the work folder is acceptable even though it may be large. I will check for an unexpected package.json or lockfile, then restart the full suite. I also need to verify that iPhone devices exist in this Playwright installation.\n\nThe child process spawns from the dev directory with copied environment variables. Node modules resolve correctly from the local node_modules folder. The full test suite is starting now and will run in the background for several minutes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c4f31c6a-784a-4f93-89d5-e89ff3602204-78","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916\nnode --input-type=module -e \"import { devices } from 'playwright'; const k=Object.keys(devices).filter(n=>/iPhone|iPad/.test(n)); console.log(k.join('\\n'));\"\nls -d node_modules/playwright node_modules/playwright-core package.json package-lock.json 2>&1 | head","description":"List iPhone device profiles and install files"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":425,"output_tokens":706,"cache_read_input_tokens":140544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"32e9befd-e60d-4cdb-a827-73c0247872d1"}
