{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_375","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed the iPhone 13 exists. No package.json was created.\n\nnode_modules is present. --no-save worked. Removing old tests.exit first. Memory should handle four hub iframes with a 1.5MB script. The suite will run in the background with a monitor. tests.log will capture FAIL lines for reruns. The full run order is headless checks before runLive.\n\nHeadless checks finished in about three seconds, covering 112 checks including eleven case bots and a full playthrough. The suite then failed on a playwright import at check 112. Browser tests will take roughly ninety seconds for three browsers plus hub overhead. Each hub run likely needs twenty to forty seconds, factoring in page load, play duration, countdown, and grace periods. The stroke test also plays for twenty seconds before timing out.\n\nThe stroke test runs on a separate page with a twenty-second play duration. The suite waits for the phase to reach 'play' within forty seconds, then injects the check and closes the page.\n\nThe full suite should take about four minutes. Card and countdown phases finish quickly in auto mode. The monitor will poll every fifteen seconds but only print results at the end.\n\nScreenshots will be read after the suite finishes. Firefox and WebKit may fail to launch in WSL without system dependencies, though none are missing. The Playwright bundle contains no stub files. PROGRESS.md will not be updated until results are known.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-89ba636f-af9e-4b87-b525-594c65f75409-79","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64\nSCRATCH=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer\nrm -f \"$SCRATCH/tests.exit\" \"$SCRATCH/tests.log\"\ncd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916\nnode tests/run.mjs > \"$SCRATCH/tests.log\"\necho $? > \"$SCRATCH/tests.exit\"","description":"Run the full browser and Hub test suite","block_until_ms":0}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1429,"output_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":140928,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"8b5c32a8-dbf0-4600-ae75-d7b58ec7d867"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-89ba636f-af9e-4b87-b525-594c65f75409-79","content":"{\"type\":\"BackgroundTaskStarted\",\"task_id\":\"3aa95aa5-9b65-4550-b048-6dc9661919c8\",\"task_type\":\"bash\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/terminal/call-89ba636f-af9e-4b87-b525-594c65f75409-79.log\",\"status\":\"running\",\"command\":\"export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64\\nSCRATCH=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer\\nrm -f \\\"$SCRATCH/tests.exit\\\" \\\"$SCRATCH/tests.log\\\"\\ncd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916\\nnode tests/run.mjs > \\\"$SCRATCH/tests.log\\\"\\necho $? > \\\"$SCRATCH/tests.exit\\\"\",\"summary\":\"Background task 3aa95aa5-9b65-4550-b048-6dc9661919c8 started\",\"retrieval_hint\":\"Use get_command_or_subagent_output with task_ids=[\\\"3aa95aa5-9b65-4550-b048-6dc9661919c8\\\"] when you need the output.\",\"pid\":97546}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"d997d16c-7934-4490-b2ca-398f251223ce"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_376","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Starting a monitor that only fires during tests.\n\nNo need to poll for commands while the monitor waits. I'll draft deviations, check PROGRESS.md and CONTENT.md, and review shots code for likely bugs. I'll avoid editing files the test might be loading.\n\nThe test already loaded its source files into the virtual machine. Editing shell.js now won't affect the running headless process. The browser loads the built HTML file separately.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf6e41ef-3dd1-4975-b5d4-5ce52394b5ac-80","name":"monitor","input":{"command":"SCRATCH=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer\nfor i in $(seq 1 48); do\n  if [ -f \"$SCRATCH/tests.exit\" ]; then\n    code=$(cat \"$SCRATCH/tests.exit\")\n    body=$(cat \"$SCRATCH/tests.log\" 2>/dev/null)\n    if [ \"$code\" = \"0\" ]; then echo \"DONE: $body\"; exit 0; else echo \"FAILED: exit $code\"; printf '%s\\n' \"$body\"; exit 1; fi\n  fi\n  sleep 15\ndone\necho \"FAILED: timed out waiting for the test suite\"\nexit 1","description":"Watch the full suite until it exits","timeout_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf6e41ef-3dd1-4975-b5d4-5ce52394b5ac-81","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PROGRESS.md","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf6e41ef-3dd1-4975-b5d4-5ce52394b5ac-82","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/CONTENT.md","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1359,"output_tokens":693,"cache_read_input_tokens":142336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"a7368d34-2b43-4017-9042-581f2bc5da94"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bf6e41ef-3dd1-4975-b5d4-5ce52394b5ac-80","content":"{\"type\":\"Monitor\",\"taskId\":\"600d4f0e-0ac7-4420-9af4-d62852c6aa02\",\"timeoutMs\":0,\"persistent\":true}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bf6e41ef-3dd1-4975-b5d4-5ce52394b5ac-81","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Progress\\n\\nOpen Table Second Opinion is playable from the work-folder HTML and from the dev folder of the same name.\\n\\nDone on this machine:\\n\\n- Eleven operations, the story between them, the ward, the credits, and a post-credits Incoming chart that does not start another operation.\\n- Eight tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, Second Look, the Lightbox on cases 2, 4, and 10, Skills Lab, and couch Grand Rounds.\\n- AI Hub shared world for 1–4 surgeons. The host simulates. Clients send hands.\\n10→- Attract reel, dev mode, TV-scale shell, PlayStation prompts with an Xbox option, and a touch notice with no touch buttons.\\n- Synthesized music, effects, choir, and gibberish voices. Music starts at 10%.\\n- `node tests/run.mjs` in the dev folder loads the shipped scripts. `--fast` skips the browser and the Hub.\\n\\nNot available here: a second person, a physical pad, and a real phone. Those checks use Playwright, a scripted pad, and an iPhone profile in WebKit.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Progress\\n\\nOpen Table Second Opinion is playable from the work-folder HTML and from the dev folder of the same name.\\n\\nDone on this machine:\\n\\n- Eleven operations, the story between them, the ward, the credits, and a post-credits Incoming chart that does not start another operation.\\n- Eight tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, Second Look, the Lightbox on cases 2, 4, and 10, Skills Lab, and couch Grand Rounds.\\n- AI Hub shared world for 1–4 surgeons. The host simulates. Clients send hands.\\n10→- Attract reel, dev mode, TV-scale shell, PlayStation prompts with an Xbox option, and a touch notice with no touch buttons.\\n- Synthesized music, effects, choir, and gibberish voices. Music starts at 10%.\\n- `node tests/run.mjs` in the dev folder loads the shipped scripts. `--fast` skips the browser and the Hub.\\n\\nNot available here: a second person, a physical pad, and a real phone. Those checks use Playwright, a scripted pad, and an iPhone profile in WebKit.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"# Progress\\n\\nOpen Table Second Opinion is playable from the work-folder HTML and from the dev folder of the same name.\\n\\nDone on this machine:\\n\\n- Eleven operations, the story between them, the ward, the credits, and a post-credits Incoming chart that does not start another operation.\\n- Eight tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, Second Look, the Lightbox on cases 2, 4, and 10, Skills Lab, and couch Grand Rounds.\\n- AI Hub shared world for 1–4 surgeons. The host simulates. Clients send hands.\\n- Attract reel, dev mode, TV-scale shell, PlayStation prompts with an Xbox option, and a touch notice with no touch buttons.\\n- Synthesized music, effects, choir, and gibberish voices. Music starts at 10%.\\n- `node tests/run.mjs` in the dev folder loads the shipped scripts. `--fast` skips the browser and the Hub.\\n\\nNot available here: a second person, a physical pad, and a real phone. Those checks use Playwright, a scripted pad, and an iPhone profile in WebKit.\\n\",\"total_lines\":14}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bf6e41ef-3dd1-4975-b5d4-5ce52394b5ac-82","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Adding content\\n\\nThe operation sim in `src/core/sim.js` does not need an edit to add a case, a strain you already have, a site, a character, or a story node. Put the new data in `src/data/content.js` and, for a new portrait, `src/art/field.js`.\\n\\n## A case\\n\\nAdd an object to `CASES` and its id to `ORDER`.\\n\\n- `id`, `name`, `patient`, `chapter`, `doctor` (`vale`, `sokolova`, or `both`), `site`, `clock`, `vitals`, `drain`, `par`, `brief`.\\n10→- `phases`: a list of `{ name, objects, strain, strainOpts, flags, at, tutorial, dim, tilt, device }`.\\n- An object is a plain spec. `addObj` fills `origin`, `axis`, `depth`, stitch `pairs`, salve `cells`, and a mass `guide`. Set `order` so a pool is cleared before the thing under it. `needsWindow` waits for the retractor. `hidden` waits for sonar.\\n- `at` entries are `{ t, do }` and fire from `runScript` names that already exist (`lurch`, `look`, `breath`, and the rest in the sim). A new verb is the one change that touches the sim.\\n- A second-opinion film is a `LIGHT[id]` entry `{ mark: [x, y], text, right, wrong }` in field pixels. The story node sends the player there with `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` only after a chart scene; cases without a `LIGHT` entry go straight to the operation.\\n\\n`par` is the score a clean run should beat by about five percent for an S. Rank is score/par: S at 95%, A at 80%, B at 60%, C at 40%.\\n\\n## A strain\\n\\nThe six strains are `staccato`, `legato`, `tremolo`, `dacapo`, `fermata`, and `cantor`. Put `strain: 'legato'` (and `strainOpts`) on a phase. `spawnStrain` builds the organs. A new kind of parasite means a new branch in `spawnStrain` and `stepStrain`. Tuning that already exists is `strains.speed`, `health`, `spawn`, `damage`, and `beat` in `src/config.js`.\\n20→\\n## A site\\n\\n`site` on the case is a name `fieldFor` already paints: `forearm`, `abdomen`, `flank`, `heart`, `brain`, `implant`, `mediastinum`, `ship`. A new site is a new branch in `TissueField` in `src/art/field.js`. The sim only stores the name.\\n\\n## A character\\n\\nAdd an id to `CAST` with `name`, `role`, and `hue`. Add the same id to `PEOPLE` with `lines` for the ward. `EXPR` can add a face. The story `who` field uses that id. Busts are drawn by `GAME.Art.bust`. The ward shows a saved patient when their id is in `WARD[chapter]` and in the save.\\n\\n## A story node\\n30→\\n`NODES` is a map of id to a list of steps.\\n\\n- A line is `{ who, say, expr }`.\\n- A choice is `{ who, say, choices: [{ text, goto }] }`. Skip does not pick one.\\n- `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` then `{ goto: 'cN_out' }` runs the operation and resumes on the way out.\\n- `{ event: 'ward', chapter, wait: true }` opens the walkable ward.\\n- `{ event: 'credits', wait: true }` opens the credits. The last page resumes the story.\\n- `{ end: true }` returns to the title.\\n\\n40→Wire the first node from `start`, or from the previous node's `goto`. The sim is not involved.\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Adding content\\n\\nThe operation sim in `src/core/sim.js` does not need an edit to add a case, a strain you already have, a site, a character, or a story node. Put the new data in `src/data/content.js` and, for a new portrait, `src/art/field.js`.\\n\\n## A case\\n\\nAdd an object to `CASES` and its id to `ORDER`.\\n\\n- `id`, `name`, `patient`, `chapter`, `doctor` (`vale`, `sokolova`, or `both`), `site`, `clock`, `vitals`, `drain`, `par`, `brief`.\\n10→- `phases`: a list of `{ name, objects, strain, strainOpts, flags, at, tutorial, dim, tilt, device }`.\\n- An object is a plain spec. `addObj` fills `origin`, `axis`, `depth`, stitch `pairs`, salve `cells`, and a mass `guide`. Set `order` so a pool is cleared before the thing under it. `needsWindow` waits for the retractor. `hidden` waits for sonar.\\n- `at` entries are `{ t, do }` and fire from `runScript` names that already exist (`lurch`, `look`, `breath`, and the rest in the sim). A new verb is the one change that touches the sim.\\n- A second-opinion film is a `LIGHT[id]` entry `{ mark: [x, y], text, right, wrong }` in field pixels. The story node sends the player there with `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` only after a chart scene; cases without a `LIGHT` entry go straight to the operation.\\n\\n`par` is the score a clean run should beat by about five percent for an S. Rank is score/par: S at 95%, A at 80%, B at 60%, C at 40%.\\n\\n## A strain\\n\\nThe six strains are `staccato`, `legato`, `tremolo`, `dacapo`, `fermata`, and `cantor`. Put `strain: 'legato'` (and `strainOpts`) on a phase. `spawnStrain` builds the organs. A new kind of parasite means a new branch in `spawnStrain` and `stepStrain`. Tuning that already exists is `strains.speed`, `health`, `spawn`, `damage`, and `beat` in `src/config.js`.\\n20→\\n## A site\\n\\n`site` on the case is a name `fieldFor` already paints: `forearm`, `abdomen`, `flank`, `heart`, `brain`, `implant`, `mediastinum`, `ship`. A new site is a new branch in `TissueField` in `src/art/field.js`. The sim only stores the name.\\n\\n## A character\\n\\nAdd an id to `CAST` with `name`, `role`, and `hue`. Add the same id to `PEOPLE` with `lines` for the ward. `EXPR` can add a face. The story `who` field uses that id. Busts are drawn by `GAME.Art.bust`. The ward shows a saved patient when their id is in `WARD[chapter]` and in the save.\\n\\n## A story node\\n30→\\n`NODES` is a map of id to a list of steps.\\n\\n- A line is `{ who, say, expr }`.\\n- A choice is `{ who, say, choices: [{ text, goto }] }`. Skip does not pick one.\\n- `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` then `{ goto: 'cN_out' }` runs the operation and resumes on the way out.\\n- `{ event: 'ward', chapter, wait: true }` opens the walkable ward.\\n- `{ event: 'credits', wait: true }` opens the credits. The last page resumes the story.\\n- `{ end: true }` returns to the title.\\n\\n40→Wire the first node from `start`, or from the previous node's `goto`. The sim is not involved.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/CONTENT.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"# Adding content\\n\\nThe operation sim in `src/core/sim.js` does not need an edit to add a case, a strain you already have, a site, a character, or a story node. Put the new data in `src/data/content.js` and, for a new portrait, `src/art/field.js`.\\n\\n## A case\\n\\nAdd an object to `CASES` and its id to `ORDER`.\\n\\n- `id`, `name`, `patient`, `chapter`, `doctor` (`vale`, `sokolova`, or `both`), `site`, `clock`, `vitals`, `drain`, `par`, `brief`.\\n- `phases`: a list of `{ name, objects, strain, strainOpts, flags, at, tutorial, dim, tilt, device }`.\\n- An object is a plain spec. `addObj` fills `origin`, `axis`, `depth`, stitch `pairs`, salve `cells`, and a mass `guide`. Set `order` so a pool is cleared before the thing under it. `needsWindow` waits for the retractor. `hidden` waits for sonar.\\n- `at` entries are `{ t, do }` and fire from `runScript` names that already exist (`lurch`, `look`, `breath`, and the rest in the sim). A new verb is the one change that touches the sim.\\n- A second-opinion film is a `LIGHT[id]` entry `{ mark: [x, y], text, right, wrong }` in field pixels. The story node sends the player there with `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` only after a chart scene; cases without a `LIGHT` entry go straight to the operation.\\n\\n`par` is the score a clean run should beat by about five percent for an S. Rank is score/par: S at 95%, A at 80%, B at 60%, C at 40%.\\n\\n## A strain\\n\\nThe six strains are `staccato`, `legato`, `tremolo`, `dacapo`, `fermata`, and `cantor`. Put `strain: 'legato'` (and `strainOpts`) on a phase. `spawnStrain` builds the organs. A new kind of parasite means a new branch in `spawnStrain` and `stepStrain`. Tuning that already exists is `strains.speed`, `health`, `spawn`, `damage`, and `beat` in `src/config.js`.\\n\\n## A site\\n\\n`site` on the case is a name `fieldFor` already paints: `forearm`, `abdomen`, `flank`, `heart`, `brain`, `implant`, `mediastinum`, `ship`. A new site is a new branch in `TissueField` in `src/art/field.js`. The sim only stores the name.\\n\\n## A character\\n\\nAdd an id to `CAST` with `name`, `role`, and `hue`. Add the same id to `PEOPLE` with `lines` for the ward. `EXPR` can add a face. The story `who` field uses that id. Busts are drawn by `GAME.Art.bust`. The ward shows a saved patient when their id is in `WARD[chapter]` and in the save.\\n\\n## A story node\\n\\n`NODES` is a map of id to a list of steps.\\n\\n- A line is `{ who, say, expr }`.\\n- A choice is `{ who, say, choices: [{ text, goto }] }`. Skip does not pick one.\\n- `{ event: 'op', caseId, wait: true }` then `{ goto: 'cN_out' }` runs the operation and resumes on the way out.\\n- `{ event: 'ward', chapter, wait: true }` opens the walkable ward.\\n- `{ event: 'credits', wait: true }` opens the credits. The last page resumes the story.\\n- `{ end: true }` returns to the title.\\n\\nWire the first node from `start`, or from the previous node's `goto`. The sim is not involved.\\n\",\"total_lines\":40}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"4e9560eb-32d1-419e-963b-85b036df835e"}
