{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_384","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The title screens look good and filled.\n\nThe wheel description likely refers to the tool ring around the cursor. Long breath's cold blue border matches the cold field. I'll check a couple strain shots and a site to confirm they're not blank.\n\nPortraits and ward frames are distinct. Next I will append handoff observations, update the goal plan checklist, and record deviations.\n\nPROGRESS.md will be updated to reflect the full run passed. Leftover debug scripts in scratch will be deleted. I'll verify notes/feedback.md exists, flip the checklist, and record the c10 par 2000 deviation.\n\nI will record several deviations. The engine notice patch sits at the bottom with pointer-events. The intern clock uses only a divisor. Story view uses `side` because no front view exists. The closed-reed syringe ignores the window gate. The bot charges syringe at clear park (46, 188). The tool wheel ring is drawn in the HUD. Playwright node package was missing from the module path; I installed playwright@1.63.0 with --ignore-scripts into the dev folder so tests resolve it and reuse the existing browser cache.\n\nThe tests log shows exactly 142 checks with zero failures. I will append the exit-interview and HTML observations to handoff.log, keeping tests.log clean. The music-to-effects ratio is about 0.08, well below the 0.35 threshold.\n\nI will verify game.html exists in the dev folder. I confirmed session.js is the first script. I am tracing the HTML build sizes to confirm the forbidden-name removal took effect before the test suite ran.\n\nThe HTML byte count changed between the build and the test. The first build after removing SOURCE wrote 1496455 bytes, but the later Python check reported 1496875 bytes. I am investigating why the file grew by 420 bytes.\n\nI suspect the HTML file was rewritten after the 1496455-byte build. I will check whether SOURCE is still absent and compare the current source against the file. The shell-for-pin edit occurred after that build, so it may have caused the mismatch.\n\nThe 1496513-byte build predated the SOURCE removal. The 1496455-byte build included the pin fix and no SOURCE. The full suite used that HTML and passed. The current 1496875-byte file is a later rewrite.\n\nI will stat the HTML file and check if it differs from game.html. If the file grew after the test, I will rebuild to ensure the handed-in HTML matches the source that passed.\n\nThe test finished at 01:07, so I will check the HTML file's modification time to see if it predates that run. The shell pin fix was already baked into the 1496455-byte build, and no source files were edited afterward, so the HTML should match the tested version. I will stat the file and then update the plan, progress, and handoff log.\n\nThe wheel icons cluster at the cursor offset, confirming they are the tool ring. The cold blue border is distinct from the green wheel border. I will check staccato and heart next before writing the docs.\n\nPROGRESS.md will record the 142-check run and hub/browser evidence, but omit the scratch path because that folder is deleted when the goal ends. The goal plan checklist will be flipped to completed and a Deviations section added.\n\nThe monitor process has already exited with DONE. I will append the parse observations to handoff.log, keeping tests.log as a single line. I confirmed session.js is unmodified and the HTML contains no TODO markers. I still need to check two more images and stat the HTML before writing the files.\n\nThe about screen order is confirmed in the game data. The wheel tool ring may not clearly show eight icons, but that is non-gating evidence. The deviations will be written carefully and accurately.\n\nInstalling Playwright in the dev folder is a deviation from the plan, but it is honest to record. The verifier re-runs node tests/run.mjs, so node_modules must stay or the re-run will fail. --no-save prevented package.json from being written.\n\nThe About answers from exit-interview.json will be quoted verbatim in the final message. I will also batch-check the remaining strain shots while writing files.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bf95722-934b-4e5f-8227-3861367220c4-102","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/shots/strain-staccato.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bf95722-934b-4e5f-8227-3861367220c4-103","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/shots/strain-legato.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bf95722-934b-4e5f-8227-3861367220c4-104","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/shots/site-heart.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7bf95722-934b-4e5f-8227-3861367220c4-105","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"DEV=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916\nHTML=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916.html\nstat -c '%n %s %y' \"$HTML\" \"$DEV/game.html\" \"$DEV/notes/feedback.md\"\n# confirm the handed-in page matches the dev copy and no longer has the unused source constant\ncmp -s \"$HTML\" \"$DEV/game.html\" && echo 'html copies match' || echo 'html copies differ'\ngrep -c \"const SOURCE\" \"$HTML\" || true\n# session.js byte-identical to vendor copy inside the page? just confirm first script starts with the banner\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nhtml=Path(\"/home/micha/dev