{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_405","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A critical bug was found in sim.js: Second Look ghosts are filled into state but never drawn or used. They are only set there and decremented in ghostT.\n\nThe acceptance criterion only requires filling ghost data, not drawing it. This explains why the array is populated without ever being used.\n\nThe code-correctness floor requires a handler to change state or present a feature. Ghosts are dead data because the visual replay is missing. Second Look's core purpose is a playable surgical game, so the half-second afterimage effect never reaches the player.\n\nThe verification plan requires asserting deep equality plus ghosts, but the test never checks ghosts.length or snapshot contents. The criterion's observable is the filled ghost data itself.\n\nThe code-correctness floor explicitly classifies a feature bound to no effect as a defect. Ghosts are written but never read, making them a \"wired to nothing\" placeholder. The design plan promises visual replay, yet the implementation only fills the array.\n\nReconsidering the ghost bug: the criterion only requires filling ghost data, not drawing it. The plan is a derived checklist that may clarify but cannot override the immutable contract in PLAN.md. Since STAGE.md directs building exactly what PLAN.md describes, the acceptance criteria cannot invent a drawing requirement beyond the stated words.\n\nThe goal plan's implementation approach and task checklist are design guidance, not contract. Diverging from them is never grounds to refute working code. Non-goals listed there cannot be used to reject completed features.\n\nThe goal plan's acceptance criteria are a derived checklist that may not narrow the immutable contract. OBJECTIVE requires implementing everything in PLAN.md, yet the criteria distill that full design into five items. Verifiers judge those criteria rather than a matching directory tree.\n\nThe rule against refuting for missing extensions applies to the goal plan. If PLAN.md itself requires ghost drawing, the acceptance criteria narrow the contract and that requirement still stands. The criterion passes when its evidence holds.\n\nThe verifier must not re-derive a checklist from PLAN.md. Refutations are limited to plan gaps that miss the objective's core intent or a gating criterion. The goal plan's risk list explicitly flags missing never-cut features as failures. Ghosts belong to the Second Look gift, which is a never-cut feature.\n\nThe ghost stub is a partial failure of the gift. PLAN §5.7 explicitly defines ghosts as the feature, yet the array is populated without ever being used. The criterion wording \"fills ghost data\" was likely chosen because the array is easy to assert in tests, while the visual replay remains untested presentation.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0495dff4-cbea-45be-8cd7-27e3c345c8a0-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"riff|Math\\.random|crypto\\.random|titles","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PROGRESS.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0495dff4-cbea-45be-8cd7-27e3c345c8a0-59","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Open Table|riff|random","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/notes"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0495dff4-cbea-45be-8cd7-27e3c345c8a0-60","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":840,"limit":10}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0495dff4-cbea-45be-8cd7-27e3c345c8a0-61","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"S\\.ghosts|ghosts","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916","glob":"*.{js,mjs,html}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2784,"output_tokens":2069,"cache_read_input_tokens":151936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"65f4a0d3-d24a-4f85-9707-cb7bbe0284f4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0495dff4-cbea-45be-8cd7-27e3c345c8a0-58","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0495dff4-cbea-45be-8cd7-27e3c345c8a0-59","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0495dff4-cbea-45be-8cd7-27e3c345c8a0-60","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"840→    else if (st.kind === 'cantor') stepCantor(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepStaccato(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    const beat = tune.strains.beat;\\n    for (const b of st.beads) {\\n      if (b.dead) continue;\\n      b.landIn -= dt * sp;\\n      if (!b.hopped && b.landIn < 0.5) b.hopped = true;\",\"content_concise\":\"840→    else if (st.kind === 'cantor') stepCantor(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepStaccato(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    const beat = tune.strains.beat;\\n    for (const b of st.beads) {\\n      if (b.dead) continue;\\n      b.landIn -= dt * sp;\\n      if (!b.hopped && b.landIn < 0.5) b.hopped = true;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":840,\"limit\":10,\"raw_output\":\"    else if (st.kind === 'cantor') stepCantor(S, st, worldDt, tune, sp);\\n  }\\n\\n  function stepStaccato(S, st, dt, tune, sp) {\\n    st.t += dt;\\n    const beat = tune.strains.beat;\\n    for (const b of st.beads) {\\n      if (b.dead) continue;\\n      b.landIn -= dt * sp;\\n      if (!b.hopped && b.landIn < 0.5) b.hopped = true;\\n\",\"total_lines\":1767}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0495dff4-cbea-45be-8cd7-27e3c345c8a0-61","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,52,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,