aunch, Hub, exit-interview shape, and the bot clear log were not the failure. Fix the four behaviors and assert them on the shipped sim.\\\"\\n}\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-ccef1950-85e1-4505-8073-e9663d0cb669-70","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"Second Look stores ghost samples and then ignores them, and several required dev controls do not change play. The captured suite is green because it never asserts those paths.\\n\\n- **Ghosts are a no-op.** `secondLook` (`src/core/sim.js:323-331`) fills `S.ghosts` and `ghostT`. The only later use is `ghostT -= dt` (`sim.js:1605`). `drawOp` never reads `S.ghosts`, so the six-second afterimage replay does not exist. Criterion 2 and PLAN.md §5.7 require that data to drive the look.\\n- **Hands sliders are overwritten.** `playTune` (`src/scenes/shell.js:167-171`) clones `GAME.TUNE` and then sets `hands.assist` and `hands.cursor` from Settings prefs. Dev-mode changes to those two keys never reach `updateCursor` or `step`. The test only nudges `patient.drain`, which is not clobbered.\\n- **Two strain sliders do nothing.** `tune.strains.beat` is captured in `stepStaccato` (`sim.js:845`) and never used. `strains.spawn` appears only in `DEV_KEYS` (`src/config.js:50`). Speed, health, and damage do apply; beat and spawn do not.\\n- **Clear phase cannot end a strain.** `devAct` (`shell.js:520-524`) sets every object's `done` and returns. `phaseClear` (`sim.js:1285`) returns false while `S.strain && !S.strain.done`, so Cases 4–11 stay in the phase.\\n- **Plan-required checks are missing.** `tests/run.mjs` does not assert magnet, guide-follow, the other seven wheel directions, a loose stitch, or `ghosts.length`. The cautery lock check passes on any slip. `implementer/tests.log` is `142 checks, 0 failed`, which does not cover these defects.\\n\\nLaunch, Hub, exit-interview shape, and the bot clear log were not the failure. Fix the four behaviors and assert them on the shipped sim.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/goal-classifier-08d1b960e391-1-skeptic-0.md has been created.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/goal-classifier-08d1b960e391-1-skeptic-0.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/goal-classifier-08d1b960e391-1-skeptic-0.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"Second Look stores ghost samples and then ignores them, and several required dev controls do not change play. The captured suite is green because it never asserts those paths.\\n\\n- **Ghosts are a no-op.** `secondLook` (`src/core/sim.js:323-331`) fills `S.ghosts` and `ghostT`. The only later use is `ghostT -= dt` (`sim.js:1605`). `drawOp` never reads `S.ghosts`, so the six-second afterimage replay does not exist. Criterion 2 and PLAN.md §5.7 require that data to drive the look.\\n- **Hands sliders are overwritten.** `playTune` (`src/scenes/shell.js:167-171`) clones `GAME.TUNE` and then sets `hands.assist` and `hands.cursor` from Settings prefs. Dev-mode changes to those two keys never reach `updateCursor` or `step`. The test only nudges `patient.drain`, which is not clobbered.\\n- **Two strain sliders do nothing.** `tune.strains.beat` is captured in `stepStaccato` (`sim.js:845`) and never used. `strains.spawn` appears only in `DEV_KEYS` (`src/config.js:50`). Speed, health, and damage do apply; beat and spawn do not.\\n- **Clear phase cannot end a strain.** `devAct` (`shell.js:520-524`) sets every object's `done` and returns. `phaseClear` (`sim.js:1285`) returns false while `S.strain && !S.strain.done`, so Cases 4–11 stay in the phase.\\n- **Plan-required checks are missing.** `tests/run.mjs` does not assert magnet, guide-follow, the other seven wheel directions, a loose stitch, or `ghosts.length`. The cautery lock check passes on any slip. `implementer/tests.log` is `142 checks, 0 failed`, which does not cover these defects.\\n\\nLaunch, Hub, exit-interview shape, and the bot clear log were not the failure. Fix the four behaviors and assert them on the shipped sim.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"04705244-2906-4e81-a77f-a022ccd2c998"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_411","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Refuted"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2779,"output_tokens":12,"cache_read_input_tokens":170496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"8dcce4c7-07c9-47d9-90c7-f5527236efa9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_412","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to fix the gaps flagged by the skeptic panel before claiming completion.\n\nTwo bugs need fixing. `drawOp` never paints the Second Look ghosts, so they only appear as rewinds. `playTune()` overwrites the live cursor and assist from PREFS instead of TUNE, which breaks the dev sliders.\n\nThe fix is to check TUNE.dirty before overwriting hands.cursor and hands.assist in playTune. If the dev panel changed them, use TUNE values; otherwise fall back to PREFS.\n\nThe original design intentionally overwrote hands.cursor and hands.assist from PREFS to keep settings changes from dirtying TUNE, which would block rank saves. This explains why Dev.set is ignored during play. The correct behavior must reconcile these two requirements.\n\nThe global TUNE.dirty flag means dev tuning should override PREFS for all keys once it is set. This prevents later settings changes from overriding dev values, which is acceptable.\n\nThe fix should check if TUNE values still match their documented defaults. If they do, playTune falls back to PREFS so settings sliders keep working. If dev mode changed a value, TUNE wins over PREFS. This preserves the original intent of keeping settings from dirtying TUNE while letting dev tuning override them.\n\nThe implementation is now clear. `playTune()` should only overwrite `hands.assist` and `hands.cursor` from `PREFS` when `GAME.TUNE.dirty` is false. When dev tuning has been applied, the cloned tune keeps its own values and ignores preferences.\n\nA blanket TUNE.dirty check is too coarse. It would lock in the default cursor speed even after a settings slider changes it, because any dev tuning sets the flag globally. The better approach compares each field against its documented default. If TUNE.hands.cursor or hands.assist still matches the default, playTune falls back to PREFS so settings sliders keep working. Only when a specific value was actually changed by dev mode does TUNE win over PREFS.\n\nThe dev sliders for `strains.beat` and `strains.spawn` are currently dead code. They are assigned but never read, so moving them has no effect on bead timing or spawns. These fields need to be wired into the strain simulation.\n\nI will now read the actual `playTune` implementation and its tests to confirm the exact fix.\n\nPhase marks clear objects but not `strain.done`, so the cheat cannot finish a strain phase. The cautery lock check is too weak because it triggers whenever slips are greater than zero. Missing tests cover magnet, guide-follow, all eight wheel directions, loose stitches, and non-empty Second Look ghosts. I will read the code and tests, fix these bugs, add real tests that drive shipped code, and rebuild the HTML bundle.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The skeptic panel is right: Second Look never draws its ghosts, two dev sliders do not reach the sim, and a few required checks are missing or too weak. I’ll read those paths and fix them in the shipped sim."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-851e13e5-ed4b-472a-b563-bbdc49622e5c-111","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":280,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-851e13e5-ed4b-472a-b563-bbdc49622e5c-112","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/scenes/shell.js","offset":140,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-851e13e5-ed4b-472a-b563-bbdc49622e5c-113","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/scenes/shell.js","offset":480,"limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-851e13e5-ed4b-472a-b563-bbdc49622e5c-114","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"beat|spawn|phaseClear|strain\\.done|ghosts|ghostT|cautery|loose|magnet|guide","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":132914,"output_tokens":2107,"cache_read_input_tokens":39808,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"23d359cf-b3fc-4cb6-ba57-413e51df7b2d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-851e13e5-ed4b-472a-b563-bbdc49622e5c-111","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"280→    const cursors = S.players.map(p => [round3(p.x), round3(p.y)]);\\n    const strains = strainGhost(S);\\n    S.ring.push({ t: S.worldT, core: takeCore(S), cursors, strains });\\n    const keep = S.worldT - 6.05;\\n    while (S.ring.length > 2 && S.ring[0].t < keep) S.ring.shift();\\n  }\\n  function round3(v) { return Math.round(v * 1000) / 1000; }\\n\\n  function strainGhost(S) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n290→    if (!st) return [];\\n    if (st.kind === 'legato') return (st.worms || []).map(w => [round3(w.x), round3(w.y)]);\\n    if (st.kind === 'staccato') return (st.beads || []).map(b => [round3(b.x), round3(b.y)]);\\n    if (st.kind === 'fermata' || st.kind === 'cantor') return st.eye ? [[round3(st.eye.x), round3(st.eye.y)]] : [];\\n    if (st.kind === 'tremolo') return [[round3(st.x || 213), round3(st.y || 116)]];\\n    if (st.kind === 'dacapo') return (st.lobes || []).map(L => [round3(L.x), round3(L.y)]);\\n    return [];\\n  }\\n\\n  function restoreCore(S, core, keepHands) {\\n300→    const hands = S.players.map(p => ({ id: p.id, x: p.x, y: p.y, bx: p.bx, by: p.by, color: p.color }));\\n    applyCore(S, core);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.players.length; i++) {\\n      const p = S.players[i];\\n      p.held = 0; p.stroke = null; p.fill = 0; p.over = 0; p.trig = 0; p.prevTrig = 0;\\n      if (keepHands && hands[i]) {\\n        p.x = hands[i].x; p.y = hands[i].y; p.bx = hands[i].bx; p.by = hands[i].by;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n310→\\n  function secondLook(S, tune) {\\n    if (S.mode === 'rounds') return false;\\n    if (S.gift !== 'look' && S.gift !== 'both' && S.activeDoc !== 'sokolova' && S.gift !== 'look') {\\n      if (!(S.gift === 'both' || S.activeDoc === 'sokolova' || S.gift === 'look')) return false;\\n    }\\n    const can = S.gift === 'look' || S.gift === 'both' || S.activeDoc === 'sokolova';\\n    if (!can) return false;\\n    if (S.steady < 45) return false;\\n    if (!S.ring.length) return false;\\n320→    const target = S.worldT - (tune.gift.lookSeconds || 6);\\n    let pick = S.ring[0];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.ring.length; i++) if (S.ring[i].t <= target) pick = S.ring[i];\\n    const ghosts = [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.ring.length; i++) {\\n      if (S.ring[i].t + 1e-6 < pick.t) continue;\\n      ghosts.push({ t: S.ring[i].t - pick.t, cursors: S.ring[i].cursors, strains: S.ring[i].strains });\\n    }\\n    restoreCore(S, pick.core, true);\\n    S.steady = Math.max(0, S.steady - 45);\\n330→    S.ghosts = ghosts;\\n    S.ghostT = tune.gift.lookSeconds || 6;\\n    S.breath = false;\\n    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['rewind', ghosts.length]);\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function forceRewind(S, keepSteady) {\\n    const steady = S.steady;\\n340→    const breath = S.breath;\\n    if (!S.ring.length) return false;\\n    const target = S.worldT - 6;\\n    let pick = S.ring[0];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.ring.length; i++) if (S.ring[i].t <= target) pick = S.ring[i];\\n    restoreCore(S, pick.core, true);\\n    if (keepSteady) S.steady = steady;\\n    S.breath = breath;\\n    S.worldScale = breath ? 0.25 : 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['forced', 1]);\\n350→    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  /* ---------- tools ---------- */\\n\\n  function polyDist(pts, x, y) {\\n    let best = 1e9, arcAt = 0, along = 0, total = 0;\\n    const acc = [0];\\n    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) acc.push(acc[i - 1] + hypot(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0], pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]));\\n    total = acc[acc.length - 1] || 1;\",\"content_concise\":\"280→    const cursors = S.players.map(p => [round3(p.x), round3(p.y)]);\\n    const strains = strainGhost(S);\\n    S.ring.push({ t: S.worldT, core: takeCore(S), cursors, strains });\\n    const keep = S.worldT - 6.05;\\n    while (S.ring.length > 2 && S.ring[0].t < keep) S.ring.shift();\\n  }\\n  function round3(v) { return Math.round(v * 1000) / 1000; }\\n\\n  function strainGhost(S) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n290→    if (!st) return [];\\n    if (st.kind === 'legato') return (st.worms || []).map(w => [round3(w.x), round3(w.y)]);\\n    if (st.kind === 'staccato') return (st.beads || []).map(b => [round3(b.x), round3(b.y)]);\\n    if (st.kind === 'fermata' || st.kind === 'cantor') return st.eye ? [[round3(st.eye.x), round3(st.eye.y)]] : [];\\n    if (st.kind === 'tremolo') return [[round3(st.x || 213), round3(st.y || 116)]];\\n    if (st.kind === 'dacapo') return (st.lobes || []).map(L => [round3(L.x), round3(L.y)]);\\n    return [];\\n  }\\n\\n  function restoreCore(S, core, keepHands) {\\n300→    const hands = S.players.map(p => ({ id: p.id, x: p.x, y: p.y, bx: p.bx, by: p.by, color: p.color }));\\n    applyCore(S, core);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.players.length; i++) {\\n      const p = S.players[i];\\n      p.held = 0; p.stroke = null; p.fill = 0; p.over = 0; p.trig = 0; p.prevTrig = 0;\\n      if (keepHands && hands[i]) {\\n        p.x = hands[i].x; p.y = hands[i].y; p.bx = hands[i].bx; p.by = hands[i].by;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n310→\\n  function secondLook(S, tune) {\\n    if (S.mode === 'rounds') return false;\\n    if (S.gift !== 'look' && S.gift !== 'both' && S.activeDoc !== 'sokolova' && S.gift !== 'look') {\\n      if (!(S.gift === 'both' || S.activeDoc === 'sokolova' || S.gift === 'look')) return false;\\n    }\\n    const can = S.gift === 'look' || S.gift === 'both' || S.activeDoc === 'sokolova';\\n    if (!can) return false;\\n    if (S.steady < 45) return false;\\n    if (!S.ring.length) return false;\\n320→    const target = S.worldT - (tune.gift.lookSeconds || 6);\\n    let pick = S.ring[0];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.ring.length; i++) if (S.ring[i].t <= target) pick = S.ring[i];\\n    const ghosts = [];\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.ring.length; i++) {\\n      if (S.ring[i].t + 1e-6 < pick.t) continue;\\n      ghosts