{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_416","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to implement ghost drawing in drawOp when S is active.\n\nGhosts will be drawn as faint afterimages using faded discs or crosses at their cursor and strain positions. Tests must verify that Second Look ghosts are non-empty, since the ring records every 0.1s of world time and secondLook builds ghosts from ring entries at or after pick.t.\n\nThe 0.4-second hold should produce ring entries, so ghosts ought to be non-empty. The existing test lacks a ghosts.length assertion, which I must add. If ghosts remain empty, the cause needs investigation.\n\nThe test must also verify that ghosts are actually rendered. Since drawOp is not exported, I will either export a paint function or run the shell to confirm that drawing does not throw and ghosts exist. The test should assert non-empty ghosts and that each ghost has cursors.\n\nHeadless canvas cannot verify that ghosts are actually painted. The engine's null canvas does not store pixels, so a shell test checking game.errors would be too weak to prove rendering. A real canvas or direct pixel inspection is needed.\n\nI will spy on E.px.disc during draw to verify ghosts are painted without a canvas. The test must assert non-empty ghosts and cursor arrays, and the draw bug must be fixed.\n\nI can wrap `E.px.disc` in the test to intercept ghost draws. After setting up a look with ghosts and advancing one frame with `draw:true`, I will check the intercepted color list for the ghost tint.\n\nI will use '#7ec8ff' for ghost cursors and '#c8b4ff' for strain ghosts. The shell test group already has a game instance, so I can call the scene draw directly to verify rendering without a canvas.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6863a01f-153a-4eb1-92ab-0d9eccdd1df7-127","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"this\\.scene\\s*=|scenes\\[name\\]|\\.draw\\(r\\)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6863a01f-153a-4eb1-92ab-0d9eccdd1df7-128","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":500,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6863a01f-153a-4eb1-92ab-0d9eccdd1df7-129","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/PLAN.md","offset":380,"limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3678,"output_tokens":1797,"cache_read_input_tokens":195712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"6d2d96d8-f05e-4adf-9e49-8bde677e2cf2"}
