 false,\\n      hidden: false, marked: false, markT: 0, under: 0, prog: 0, order: 0,\\n      drain: 0, grade: '', tag: '',\\n\",\"total_lines\":1767}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"70145fc0-6bfa-44cb-adc0-daf9c1894e85"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_437","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"activeDoc defaults to vale. assistOf is intern plus zero.\n\nWith assist at 0.2, pull is 54 units per second toward the target. At zero assist, pull is zero and the object stays put. Speed drops by 0.55 times assist when magnetism is below 0.95 and a target exists. The test should verify both the pull and this speed reduction.\n\nAim [0.5, 0] gives magnetism 0.5, below the 0.95 slowdown threshold but above the 0.12 pull threshold. Curved speed is about 101 units per second without assist. With assist 0.6 the speed drops to roughly 68 units per second. The test compares displacement over 0.3 seconds; the assisted path should be shorter.\n\nThe test will assert three behaviors: assist pulls the hand toward the polyp, zero assist leaves it still, and partial stick with assist travels less than without when a target is in range. For guide-follow, the scalpel stroke is started by manually setting `p.stroke` to a scalpel kind, then the object is aimed strongly perpendicular to its horizontal guide.\n\nA cut object with a horizontal guide is placed at (200, 120). The player starts there with zero speed and a scalpel stroke. With assist set to 1 and aim [0.2, 1], the across-guide velocity component is scaled by 0.2. The test will compare vertical displacement between the assisted and unassisted frames.\n\nThe along-guide velocity is unchanged by assist. The perpendicular component is scaled after the ramp, so the ratio of vertical displacement between assisted and unassisted frames should equal the assist value. A `drift` helper function is being drafted to test this.\n\nThe `drift` helper is now fully implemented. It places a cut object with a horizontal guide at (200, 120), positions the player there with zero speed and a scalpel stroke, and runs 20 frames of cursor updates with assist set to 0 and then 1 while aiming straight down. The function returns the vertical displacement from the starting Y coordinate. This produces two values for comparison.\n\nThe assertion checks that the assisted vertical drift is under 35% of the unassisted drift and positive. The scalpel target is confirmed to be the cut object because it has a guide, though with zero magnet radius the nearest-object distance may still match.\n\nFull-aim magnetism of 1 is above both the 0.12 pull threshold and the 0.95 slowdown threshold, so guide-follow still applies without interference. The eight wheel directions are mapped clockwise from north: forceps, scalpel, suture, salve, syringe, cautery, suction, and sonar.\n\nWheel index is computed from atan2(y, x), with 0 at east and clockwise because y grows downward. The tool-change threshold is 0.08 seconds, not 0.1. A test will hold each stick direction for 0.1 seconds and assert the correct tool. The first four directions are being mapped: north to forceps, northeast to scalpel, east to suture, and southeast to salve.\n\nThe remaining four wheel directions are mapped: south to syringe, southwest to cautery, west to suction, and northwest to sonar. A loop holds each direction for 0.1 seconds and asserts the correct tool. The north case is handled safely because forceps is already the default tool.\n\nStarting from a non-default tool like sonar will prove the north direction actually changes the tool, because forceps is already the default. The existing flick-wait test will be kept since it starts on forceps and northeast does not change in 50 ms. Every wheel direction will be tested from a different starting tool so each one is verified.\n\nThe wheel cooldown resets to zero after a swap, so each test needs a fresh player. A single 0.1-second update is enough to trigger the 0.08-second threshold, but the existing two-frame wait test will be kept alongside eight new direction tests held for 0.1 seconds from sonar.\n\nA loose-stitch test is being drafted: it creates a wound object with two stitches and extracts the first pair of points.\n\nThe loose-stitch test presses and releases the suture tool far from the second stitch point. Because the release is 40 units away, the stitch should remain loose and the wound state must not change. A ghost-hand test is also being added to the existing second-look scenario.\n\nThe ghost-hand test will call `game.scenes.op.draw(game.r)` directly to render ghosts without changing the active scene. This avoids disrupting the title screen and uses the shipped draw path. The renderer exists after the game starts.\n\nThe renderer may need a frame before calling scene.draw directly. Using game.advance with draw is safer because it triggers _frame. The overlay implementation is being checked to confirm this.\n\nCalling `draw()` outside `_frame` would queue overlays that never run, so the spy would miss disc calls. The cleaner approach is to perform the ghost draw check inside the shell group while the op scene is active, and add the state check in the sim group.\n\nThe ghost-hand test is being implemented inside the shell group. It temporarily replaces the renderer's `px.disc` function with a spy that records every color drawn. It injects sample ghost data into the active operation scene, advances one frame to trigger the draw call, then restores the original function and asserts that the sky-blue ghost color was painted.\n\nThe ghost-hand test will use a real secondLook on the live operation state instead of injecting ghosts manually. The shell group will run a full ring and secondLook sequence, then advance one frame to draw the resulting ghosts. This satisfies both the state assertion and the headless draw check.\n\nThe ghost-hand test now uses manual Op.step to fill the ring without the fast driver. It then rewinds the live operation into ghosts and asserts that ghosts exist with positive ghostT. A renderer spy records drawn colors during a single frame advance, confirming that sky-blue ghosts are painted.\n\nThe ghost-hand test will use a single 1/120 step so the fast driver is not active. This keeps ghostT above zero and guarantees ghosts are painted during draw.\n\nThe sky-blue ghost color #7ec8ff must be verified as unique in the source to avoid false positives from other objects.\n\nThe ghost color is being changed from #7ec8ff to #67d6ff to avoid false positives. The cautery lock test is being rewritten with clearer assertions for player lock and slip events.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-06fb74e3-6102-4854-aade-79cecec6bc57-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":40,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-06fb74e3-6102-4854-aade-79cecec6bc57-50","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"#7ec8ff|#67d6ff|#b7e4ff","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1507,"output_tokens":3994,"cache_read_input_tokens":116864,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"7e1ff911-3443-48a9-8709-10b645816c37"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-06fb74e3-6102-4854-aade-79cecec6bc57-49","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→  function objById(S, id) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) if (S.objects[i].id === id) return S.objects[i];\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  function pushEv(S, ev) { S.ev.push(ev); }\\n\\n  function slip(S, p, kind, dmg, tune) {\\n    S.slips += 1;\\n    if (p) p.slips += 1;\\n50→    S.vitals -= dmg * tune.patient.slip;\\n    S.streak = 0;\\n    S.flow = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['slip', kind, dmg, p ? p.id : -1]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function award(S, p, grade, base, tune) {\\n    const mult = grade === 'textbook' ? 1.5 : grade === 'clean' ? 1 : 0.4;\\n    const pts = base * mult * S.flow;\\n    S.score += pts;\\n60→    p.score += pts;\\n    p.actions += 1;\\n    S.techAll += 1;\\n    if (grade !== 'sloppy') S.techGood += 1;\\n    if (grade === 'textbook') { p.textbooks += 1; S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 10 * tune.gift.charge); }\\n    else if (grade === 'clean') S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 5 * tune.gift.charge);\\n    if (grade === 'sloppy') { S.streak = 0; S.flow = 1; }\\n    else {\\n      S.streak += 1;\\n      S.flow = Math.min(2, 1 + 0.05 * S.streak);\\n70→      if (S.flow > S.bestFlow) S.bestFlow = S.flow;\\n    }\\n    if (!S.tutDone) S.tutDone = true;\\n    pushEv(S, ['grade', Math.round(p.x), Math.round(p.y), grade, Math.round(pts)]);\\n    return grade;\\n  }\\n\\n  function makePlayer(i, color) {\\n    return {\\n      id: i, x: 213, y: 150, bx: 213, by: 150, tool: 'forceps', trig: 0, prevTrig: 0,\",\"content_concise\":\"40→  function objById(S, id) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) if (S.objects[i].id === id) return S.objects[i];\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  function pushEv(S, ev) { S.ev.push(ev); }\\n\\n  function slip(S, p, kind, dmg, tune) {\\n    S.slips += 1;\\n    if (p) p.slips += 1;\\n50→    S.vitals -= dmg * tune.patient.slip;\\n    S.streak = 0;\\n    S.flow = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['slip', kind, dmg, p ? p.id : -1]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function award(S, p, grade, base, tune) {\\n    const mult = grade === 'textbook' ? 1.5 : grade === 'clean' ? 1 : 0.4;\\n    const pts = base * mult * S.flow;\\n    S.score += pts;\\n60→    p.score += pts;\\n    p.actions += 1;\\n    S.techAll += 1;\\n    if (grade !== 'sloppy') S.techGood += 1;\\n    if (grade === 'textbook') { p.textbooks += 1; S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 10 * tune.gift.charge); }\\n    else if (grade === 'clean') S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 5 * tune.gift.charge);\\n    if (grade === 'sloppy') { S.streak = 0; S.flow = 1; }\\n    else {\\n      S.streak += 1;\\n      S.flow = Math.min(2, 1 + 0.05 * S.streak);\\n70→      if (S.flow > S.bestFlow) S.bestFlow = S.flow;\\n    }\\n    if (!S.tutDone) S.tutDone = true;\\n    pushEv(S, ['grade', Math.round(p.x), Math.round(p.y), grade, Math.round(pts)]);\\n    return grade;\\n  }\\n\\n  function makePlayer(i, color) {\\n    return {\\n      id: i, x: 213, y: 150, bx: 213, by: 150, tool: 'forceps', trig: 0, prevTrig: 0,\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  function objById(S, id) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) if (S.objects[i].id === id) return S.objects[i];\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  function pushEv(S, ev) { S.ev.push(ev); }\\n\\n  function slip(S, p, kind, dmg, tune) {\\n    S.slips += 1;\\n    if (p) p.slips += 1;\\n    S.vitals -= dmg * tune.patient.slip;\\n    S.streak = 0;\\n    S.flow = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['slip', kind, dmg, p ? p.id : -1]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function award(S, p, grade, base, tune) {\\n    const mult = grade === 'textbook' ? 1.5 : grade === 'clean' ? 1 : 0.4;\\n    const pts = base * mult * S.flow;\\n    S.score += pts;\\n    p.score += pts;\\n    p.actions += 1;\\n    S.techAll += 1;\\n    if (grade !== 'sloppy') S.techGood += 1;\\n    if (grade === 'textbook') { p.textbooks += 1; S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 10 * tune.gift.charge); }\\n    else if (grade === 'clean') S.steady = Math.min(100, S.steady + 5 * tune.gift.charge);\\n    if (grade === 'sloppy') { S.streak = 0; S.flow = 1; }\\n    else {\\n      S.streak += 1;\\n      S.flow = Math.min(2, 1 + 0.05 * S.streak);\\n      if (S.flow > S.bestFlow) S.bestFlow = S.flow;\\n    }\\n    if (!S.tutDone) S.tutDone = true;\\n    pushEv(S, ['grade', Math.round(p.x), Math.round(p.y), grade, Math.round(pts)]);\\n    return grade;\\n  }\\n\\n  function makePlayer(i, color) {\\n    return {\\n      id: i, x: 213, y: 150, bx: 213, by: 150, tool: 'forceps', trig: 0, prevTrig: 0,\\n\",\"total_lines\":1767}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-06fb74e3-6102-4854-aade-79cecec6bc57-50","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"46cb7f26-f71d-4058-a0b6-1875dbb05cb2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_438","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Lock requires heat >= 1. cauteryHeat is currently 0.\n\nLock countdown continues during the 2.2s hold. But the event list is cleared each step, so the lock event is missing at the end of the hold.\n\nThe test checks the final step's event list, so the lock event is missed. I'll collect events across the hold to verify it.\n\nThe test loop now accumulates events across the hold. It checks that the lock event fires and that a slip event records it. The character slip at 0.6s is also captured.\n\nHeat reaches 1 exactly at 2.0 seconds, so the lock fires precisely then. The 2.2-second hold lasts 44 steps; after the lock starts at step 40, the remaining four steps reduce the lock countdown to 1.0. Next is the playTune test.\n\nThe playTune test will be added to the shell group without breaking the new game run. Cursor speed comparisons will use the debug driver only during measurement advances, since it runs 16 substeps per update. The c1 case starts near the top edge where objects sit lower, so the cursor magnet cannot reach them and both speeds remain distinct. The Vale speed multiplier applies equally to both, preserving the ~2.4 ratio. One engine step equals roughly 0.355 seconds of cursor time under the driver.\n\nThe tuned cursor should travel at least 1.8 times the preference speed. A 0.06-second ramp leaves roughly 0.3 seconds of full-speed flight, so the faster hand covers about 144 units versus 60 for the slower one; neither reaches the far wall. For the assist override test, I will zero PREFS.assist and set TUNE.hands.assist to 1.2, then place a target near the hand while locking the driver aim to [0,0] to isolate the dev assist pull.\n\nThe assist override test will use a raw state with a manually placed polyp at (80, 40) and the player set to cautery. This avoids relying on random case objects and lets the cursor magnet pull toward a known target.\n\nThe assist override test will set the player position before entering the game so the driver does not overwrite it. The debug driver is assigned after enter, then one advance is taken to measure how far the hand is pulled toward the target. Afterward both the dev assist and the preference assist are reset to their defaults.\n\nThe assist override test asserts the tuned hand moves more than four units while the preference hand barely shifts. With both assist values at zero, playTune uses the preference value and applies no pull. The raw state is already resident, so assistOf does not add an extra bonus. The active document is correctly set to vale. Because the driver aim is locked to zero, the case object is not triggered during the advance.\n\nThe raw state keeps the phase alive because its polyp is still active. The hold flag is already true, so advancePhase exits early. The clock has 400 energy and zero drain, so it will not expire in one step. Dev.set marks dirty, but reset clears that flag afterward. Because the test helper already advances twice during enter(), positions must be set after enter() rather than before.\n\nThe pull is added directly to velocity rather than through speed, so the ramp does not affect it. A 10-unit target at distance 10 with assist 1.2 produces a pull of roughly 108 units per second. Over one engine step the hand moves about 10 units toward the target. With zero assist it barely shifts. The constant pull will overshoot and oscillate because it never stops at the target.\n\nThe assist override test asserts the tuned hand moves more than four units while the preference hand barely shifts. A zero-assist case may show a tiny float, which is acceptable.\n\nNext, a clear-phase test will be added to the shell group. It will use case c4 with seed 1 and phase 1, then reset dev flags and state before the new game begins.\n\nThe clear-phase test will open the dev menu, navigate to the cheats tab, and confirm a staccato strain. It then asserts that advancing phase completes the strain and advances to Repair. After the phase change, the active strain object is replaced by the new phase's strain.\n\nThe clear-phase test asserts that phase 2 is Repair and the strain object is null. A failed clear would leave the old strain active.\n\nThe dev menu has ten items. Seven downs from index zero lands on win. Confirming it triggers devAct(0).\n\ntoolNext consumes one tap per advance. Multiple taps are handled by advancing between each one.\n\nOne advance after the dev confirm should switch phase to 2 in the same frame. Down taps are unlikely to affect phase. Opening the dev menu while on op hides the shell. After the test I will close dev, reset cheat flags, and return to title before the playthrough. Nests are type nest and not skipped, so marking them done is required for the staccato clear.\n\nThe cheat marks all objects done, so nests do not block phaseClear. canTouch is irrelevant here; only done and alive status matter. The real bug is the single strain phase that the cheat cannot finish, and proving that phaseClear returns true after the same-frame step is sufficient. An optional extra test for the IV boost phase in case c1 may be added if time allows.\n\nThe optional IV boost test is dropped. The clear-phase cheat will set needIv to keep the patient state correct. Retractors and other objects marked dead are harmless. After the strain finishes, stepStrain exits early and phaseClear advances cleanly into Repair, which only spawns objects. The c4 case loads staccato correctly on phase 1.\n\nGhost cursors and strains are drawn after the object loop but before the breath bars, so they appear on the field beneath the hands.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4318231d-2190-45d6-b26e-07ac715ad801-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":220,"limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4318231d-2190-45d6-b26e-07ac715ad801-52","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"## Deviations|## Task checklist|## Verification","path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/goal/plan.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4697,"output_tokens":3499,"cache_read_input_tokens":118272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"6ce7e014-170e-498c-be4f-5eddcd4c6659"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4318231d-2190-45d6-b26e-07ac715ad801-51","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"220→    S.breath = false;\\n    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['lost', why]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function finishCase(S) {\\n    if (S.won || S.lost) return;\\n    S.won = true;\\n    S.closed = true;\\n    S.breath = false;\\n230→    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    const end = Math.max(0, S.clock) * 2 + Math.max(0, S.vitals) * 3;\\n    S.score += end;\\n    S.endBonus = end;\\n    S.rank = rankLetter(S.score, S.par, S.diff, S.slips, S.rankCap);\\n    pushEv(S, ['closed', S.rank, Math.round(S.score)]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function rankLetter(score, par, diff, slips, cap) {\\n    const r = par > 0 ? score / par : 0;\\n240→    let L = r >= 0.95 ? 'S' : r >= 0.8 ? 'A' : r >= 0.6 ? 'B' : r >= 0.4 ? 'C' : 'D';\\n    const order = 'DCBAS';\\n    if (cap === 'B' && order.indexOf(L) > order.indexOf('B')) L = 'B';\\n    if (diff === 'attending' && L === 'S' && !slips) return 'S+';\\n    return L;\\n  }\\n\\n  function takeCore(S) {\\n    return {\\n      rng: S.rng, clock: S.clock, vitals: S.vitals, score: S.score, slips: S.slips,\\n250→      phase: S.phase, steady: S.steady, flow: S.flow, streak: S.streak,\\n      phaseT: S.phaseT, worldT: S.worldT, flags: clone(S.flags),\\n      objects: clone(S.objects), strain: S.strain ? clone(S.strain) : null,\\n      device: S.device ? clone(S.device) : null,\\n      techGood: S.techGood, techAll: S.techAll, bestFlow: S.bestFlow,\\n      codeBlueUsed: S.codeBlueUsed, tutDone: S.tutDone, tutorial: S.tutorial,\\n      windowOpen: S.windowOpen, tiltAmp: S.tiltAmp, dim: S.dim,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n260→  function applyCore(S, core) {\\n    S.rng = core.rng; S.clock = core.clock; S.vitals = core.vitals; S.score = core.score;\\n    S.slips = core.slips; S.phase = core.phase; S.steady = core.steady; S.flow = core.flow;\\n    S.streak = core.streak; S.phaseT = core.phaseT; S.worldT = core.worldT;\\n    S.flags = clone(core.flags); S.objects = clone(core.objects);\\n    S.strain = core.strain ? clone(core.strain) : null;\\n    S.device = core.device ? clone(core.device) : null;\\n    S.techGood = core.techGood; S.techAll = core.techAll; S.bestFlow = core.bestFlow;\\n    S.codeBlueUsed = core.codeBlueUsed; S.tutDone = core.tutDone; S.tutorial = core.tutorial;\\n    S.windowOpen = core.windowOpen; S.tiltAmp = core.tiltAmp; S.dim = core.dim;\\n270→  }\\n\\n  function hashCore(core) {\\n    const s = JSON.stringify(core);\\n    let h = 2166136261;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) { h ^= s.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\\n    return h >>> 0;\\n  }\\n\\n  function pushRing(S) {\",\"content_concise\":\"220→    S.breath = false;\\n    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    pushEv(S, ['lost', why]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function finishCase(S) {\\n    if (S.won || S.lost) return;\\n    S.won = true;\\n    S.closed = true;\\n    S.breath = false;\\n230→    S.worldScale = 1;\\n    const end = Math.max(0, S.clock) * 2 + Math.max(0, S.vitals) * 3;\\n    S.score += end;\\n    S.endBonus = end;\\n    S.rank = rankLetter(S.score, S.par, S.diff, S.slips, S.rankCap);\\n    pushEv(S, ['closed', S.rank, Math.round(S.score)]);\\n  }\\n\\n  function rankLetter(score, par, diff, slips, cap) {\\n    const r = par > 0 ? score / par : 0;\\n240→    let L = r >= 0.95 ? 'S' : r >= 0.8 ? 'A' : r >= 0.6 ? 'B' : r >= 0.4 ? 'C' : 'D';\\n    const order = 'DCBAS';\\n    if (cap === 'B' && order.indexOf(L) > order.indexOf('B')) L = 'B';\\n    if (diff === 'attending' && L === 'S' && !slips) return 'S+';\\n    return L;\\n  }\\n\\n  function takeCore(S) {\\n    return {\\n      rng: S.rng, clock: S.clock, vitals: S.vitals, score: S.score, slips: S.slips,\\n250→      phase: S.phase, steady: S.steady, flow: S.flow, streak: S.streak,\\n      phaseT: S.phaseT, worldT: S.worldT, flags: clone(S.flags),\\n      objects: clone(S.objects), strain: S.strain ? clone(S.strain) 