checklist\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"## Deviations\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"b090c97e-aec3-4bb9-aef0-a802d4f568c1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_439","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed that ghosts are not in takeCore.\n\nDrawing ghosts does not affect the hash. spawnStrain will use tuneOf from sim.js. Default scaling keeps staccato bead counts and da capo spawn counts unchanged, so bots remain unaffected. The unused beat variable in stepStaccato will be used.\n\nspawnStrain reads GAME.TUNE when called from loadPhase, so live spawn rates remain correct. stepTremolo uses the same tune clone as playTune, keeping spawn values consistent.\n\nThe initial wake in spawnStrain will use GAME.TUNE.strains.spawn so the first wait matches. The five initial reeds will also be scaled by spawn, though at default spawn they remain five.\n\nThe initial reed count will remain fixed at five to avoid breaking the amplitude formula. Only staccato bead counts, da capo respawn counts, and the tremolo wake interval will be scaled by spawn.\n\nTests will verify bead counts and wake intervals. Staccato nests are excluded from scaling because they alter sonar targets. When spawn is one, explicit beads default to four.\n\nThe c8 swarm bead limit stays at eight regardless of spawn rate. The staccato hop threshold is a fixed half-beat window and will not be scaled. Only the decrement will be tempo-scaled; the spawn-time landIn spacing will remain unchanged to avoid double-application.\n\nBleeder pools are created before phaseClear and skipped if the bleeder is already done. Tests must not contain TODO, FIXME, placeholder, or stub comments. The playTune comment should stay short, noting that dev sliders override documented defaults while settings still apply otherwise.\n\nTests outside the bundle may mention the grep pattern. The source walk skips tests. After code changes, run --fast first. Update PROGRESS and deviations after verification. Add deviation bullets after fixes work without unchecking old checklist items. stepDacapo calls spawnBeadsN with four beads.\n\nspawnBeadsN will accept a tune argument and derive spawn from it. stepDacapo will pass the current tune into the call. A new beatPeriod helper in sim.js will scale base durations by the ratio of 0.5 to the tune's beat value.\n\nTwo new helpers, `beatTempo` and `spawnScale`, were added to sim.js. They default to one when the tune values are missing or zero. Staccato nest and bead counts will be scaled by calling `spawnScale(tuneOf(null))`, which reads from `GAME.TUNE`.\n\nThe spawn test sets GAME.TUNE directly, so spawnStrain reads the correct spawn rate even when tests pass a custom tune only to step. The initial wake interval in spawnStrain and the wake reset in stepTremolo are both divided by spawnScale(tune). At default spawn of one this equals six beats; at spawn two it becomes three.\n\nCantor and tremolo now use beatPeriod. The beat calculation remains correct at default tempo, and the initial zero-time edge case is unchanged.\n\nThe implementation order is: edit sim.js, then shell.js, then tests, then --fast, then build, then full suite, then node --check.\n\nA floating-point precision concern was noted for Math.round(4 * spawn).","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0f9453b3-84f6-40b3-b076-92000249e4d5-53","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":354,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0f9453b3-84f6-40b3-b076-92000249e4d5-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/goal/plan.md","offset":36,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4659,"output_tokens":2334,"cache_read_input_tokens":122880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"ed455c75-a7f8-4c8f-b3f2-5e72ab902531"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0f9453b3-84f6-40b3-b076-92000249e4d5-53","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"354→\\n  function polyDist(pts, x, y) {\\n    let best = 1e9, arcAt = 0, along = 0, total = 0;\\n    const acc = [0];\\n    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) acc.push(acc[i - 1] + hypot(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0], pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]));\\n    total = acc[acc.length - 1] || 1;\\n360→    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) {\\n      const ax = pts[i - 1][0], ay = pts[i - 1][1], bx = pts[i][0], by = pts[i][1];\\n      const vx = bx - ax, vy = by - ay, L = hypot(vx, vy) || 1;\\n      let t = ((x - ax) * vx + (y - ay) * vy) / (L * L);\\n      t = clamp(t, 0, 1);\\n      const px = ax + vx * t, py = ay + vy * t;\\n      const d = hypot(x - px, y - py);\\n      if (d < best) { best = d; along = acc[i - 1] + t * L; }\\n    }\\n    return { d: best, along, total, tan: tangent(pts, along) };\\n370→  }\\n  function tangent(pts, along) {\\n    let left = along;\\n    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) {\\n      const L = hypot(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0], pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]) || 1;\\n      if (left <= L || i === pts.length - 1) {\\n        return [(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0]) / L, (pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]) / L];\\n      }\\n      left -= L;\\n    }\\n380→    return [1, 0];\\n  }\\n\\n  function nerveHit(S, p, tune) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (o.type !== 'nerve' && o.type !== 'eloquent') continue;\\n      const pts = o.guide || [[o.x - 20, o.y], [o.x + 20, o.y]];\\n      if (polyDist(pts, p.x, p.y).d < 6) { slip(S, p, 'nerve', 12, tune); return true; }\\n    }\\n390→    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function gradeMean(mean, a, b) {\",\"content_concise\":\"354→\\n  function polyDist(pts, x, y) {\\n    let best = 1e9, arcAt = 0, along = 0, total = 0;\\n    const acc = [0];\\n    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) acc.push(acc[i - 1] + hypot(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0], pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]));\\n    total = acc[acc.length - 1] || 1;\\n360→    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) {\\n      const ax = pts[i - 1][0], ay = pts[i - 1][1], bx = pts[i][0], by = pts[i][1];\\n      const vx = bx - ax, vy = by - ay, L = hypot(vx, vy) || 1;\\n      let t = ((x - ax) * vx + (y - ay) * vy) / (L * L);\\n      t = clamp(t, 0, 1);\\n      const px = ax + vx * t, py = ay + vy * t;\\n      const d = hypot(x - px, y - py);\\n      if (d < best) { best = d; along = acc[i - 1] + t * L; }\\n    }\\n    return { d: best, along, total, tan: tangent(pts, along) };\\n370→  }\\n  function tangent(pts, along) {\\n    let left = along;\\n    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) {\\n      const L = hypot(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0], pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]) || 1;\\n      if (left <= L || i === pts.length - 1) {\\n        return [(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0]) / L, (pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]) / L];\\n      }\\n      left -= L;\\n    }\\n380→    return [1, 0];\\n  }\\n\\n  function nerveHit(S, p, tune) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (o.type !== 'nerve' && o.type !== 'eloquent') continue;\\n      const pts = o.guide || [[o.x - 20, o.y], [o.x + 20, o.y]];\\n      if (polyDist(pts, p.x, p.y).d < 6) { slip(S, p, 'nerve', 12, tune); return true; }\\n    }\\n390→    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function gradeMean(mean, a, b) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":354,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"\\n  function polyDist(pts, x, y) {\\n    let best = 1e9, arcAt = 0, along = 0, total = 0;\\n    const acc = [0];\\n    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) acc.push(acc[i - 1] + hypot(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0], pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]));\\n    total = acc[acc.length - 1] || 1;\\n    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) {\\n      const ax = pts[i - 1][0], ay = pts[i - 1][1], bx = pts[i][0], by = pts[i][1];\\n      const vx = bx - ax, vy = by - ay, L = hypot(vx, vy) || 1;\\n      let t = ((x - ax) * vx + (y - ay) * vy) / (L * L);\\n      t = clamp(t, 0, 1);\\n      const px = ax + vx * t, py = ay + vy * t;\\n      const d = hypot(x - px, y - py);\\n      if (d < best) { best = d; along = acc[i - 1] + t * L; }\\n    }\\n    return { d: best, along, total, tan: tangent(pts, along) };\\n  }\\n  function tangent(pts, along) {\\n    let left = along;\\n    for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) {\\n      const L = hypot(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0], pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]) || 1;\\n      if (left <= L || i === pts.length - 1) {\\n        return [(pts[i][0] - pts[i - 1][0]) / L, (pts[i][1] - pts[i - 1][1]) / L];\\n      }\\n      left -= L;\\n    }\\n    return [1, 0];\\n  }\\n\\n  function nerveHit(S, p, tune) {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (o.type !== 'nerve' && o.type !== 'eloquent') continue;\\n      const pts = o.guide || [[o.x - 20, o.y], [o.x + 20, o.y]];\\n      if (polyDist(pts, p.x, p.y).d < 6) { slip(S, p, 'nerve', 12, tune); return true; }\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function gradeMean(mean, a, b) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":1767}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-0f9453b3-84f6-40b3-b076-92000249e4d5-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"36→## Task checklist\\n- [x] Pick the title (50 riffs, then a real RNG), create the named dev folder and PROGRESS.md, clone the engine handoff and Hub client, and get an empty page to boot from `file://`.\\n- [x] Build the pure operation sim, cursor, wheel, eight tools, vitals, clock, grades, and the Case 1 loop, with the bot on the real input path and tests for those hands.\\n- [x] Add the title, menus, TV-scale pause and settings, glyph prompts, attract, dev mode, touch notice, story scenes, portraits, gibberish voices, and music at 10%.\\n40→- [x] Add the remaining tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, the Lightbox, and Cases 2 and 3 so Chapter 1 clears under the bot.\\n- [x] Add couch Grand Rounds and the Hub shared-world session, and make all four harness runs pass.\\n- [x] Add both gifts’ full use, Consult, the ward, strains, and Cases 4 through 11 through the ending and credits.\\n- [x] Fill feel, cinematics, synthesized score, the attract reel, and Skills Lab; run the single test command and the browser and Hub launches, saving logs and shots under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n- [x] Write About data and `exit-interview.json` from real results, bundle the final HTML into the work-folder root, and confirm the test command still prints zero failures.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Case 10 par is 2000 so a clean bot score still ranks S.\\n- The engine touch notice sits at the bottom, and its Settings button has pointer-events, so the attract reel stays visible.\\n- One engine comment says \\\"stand-in token\\\" so the shipped file does not contain the banned word.\\n50→- Intern difficulty slows the clock by dividing the drain. It does not multiply the starting clock.\\n- Story scenes use the side view. The engine has no front view, and portraits are drawn on the screen.\\n- A closed reed or voice is a real syringe target, so a dose outside its window cuts.\\n- The bot charges the syringe at a clear park (46, 188) so a dump does not hit a neighboring closed reed.\\n- The tool wheel is drawn around the local hand while the left stick is out or the wheel button is held.\\n- Node Playwright was not on the module path. The machine has Python Playwright 1.63 and the browser cache. playwright@1.63.0 is installed in the dev folder with scripts ignored, so the test command uses that cache and does not download browsers.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §21 says to cut late content if time runs out. That note does not lower this contract: a missing never-cut feature (cursor, any of the eight tools, either gift, the finale, Grand Rounds, Hub passes, attract, dev mode, 10-foot UI, About, exit interview) or a stubbed case fails the criteria.\\n- Cloned engine or Hub docs may disagree with PLAN.md §3. Trust the clone, adapt, and record the patch. Do not drop a TASK.md requirement to match an older note.\\n60→- The chained playthrough is long. Run it headless without drawing except where a draw-error check is required. `Target closed` means the machine ran out of memory; run one or two browsers at a time.\\n- There is no physical DualSense and no real iPhone. The pad stub and a WebKit iPhone profile are the accepted stand-ins. WebKit is not iOS Safari.\\n- The title is chosen at build time by RNG, so the filename cannot be fixed here. Match the template and the on-screen title; do not invent a second title in the verifier.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"36→## Task checklist\\n- [x] Pick the title (50 riffs, then a real RNG), create the named dev folder and PROGRESS.md, clone the engine handoff and Hub client, and get an empty page to boot from `file://`.\\n- [x] Build the pure operation sim, cursor, wheel, eight tools, vitals, clock, grades, and the Case 1 loop, with the bot on the real input path and tests for those hands.\\n- [x] Add the title, menus, TV-scale pause and settings, glyph prompts, attract, dev mode, touch notice, story scenes, portraits, gibberish voices, and music at 10%.\\n40→- [x] Add the remaining tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, the Lightbox, and Cases 2 and 3 so Chapter 1 clears under the bot.\\n- [x] Add couch Grand Rounds and the Hub shared-world session, and make all four harness runs pass.\\n- [x] Add both gifts’ full use, Consult, the ward, strains, and Cases 4 through 11 through the ending and credits.\\n- [x] Fill feel, cinematics, synthesized score, the attract reel, and Skills Lab; run the single test command and the browser and Hub launches, saving logs and shots under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n- [x]