{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9a9d0476-4d9c-45cb-8a43-7a1118657823-55","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"175→\\n  function inDome(S, x, y) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n    if (!st || !st.domes) return false;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < st.domes.length; i++) {\\n180→      const d = st.domes[i];\\n      if (d.t > 0 && hypot(x - d.x, y - d.y) <= d.r) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function covered(S, o) {\\n    if (!o.under) return false;\\n    const p = objById(S, o.under);\\n    return !!(p && !p.done && p.vol > 1);\\n190→  }\\n\\n  function canTouch(S, o) {\\n    if (!o || o.done || !o.alive) return false;\\n    if (covered(S, o)) return false;\\n    if (o.hidden && !o.marked) return false;\\n    if (o.needsWindow && S.windowOpen <= 0) return false;\\n    if (o.needsBoard && S.device && !S.device.shown) return false;\\n    if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return !!o.window;\\n    if (o.type === 'lobe') return !!o.open;\\n200→    if (o.type === 'eye') return !!o.open;\\n    if (o.type === 'repeat') return !!o.open;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nearest(S, p, rad, pred) {\\n    let best = null, bd = rad;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!pred(o)) continue;\\n210→      const d = hypot(o.x - p.x, o.y - p.y);\\n      if (d <= bd) { bd = d; best = o; }\\n    }\\n    return best;\\n  }\",\"content_concise\":\"175→\\n  function inDome(S, x, y) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n    if (!st || !st.domes) return false;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < st.domes.length; i++) {\\n180→      const d = st.domes[i];\\n      if (d.t > 0 && hypot(x - d.x, y - d.y) <= d.r) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function covered(S, o) {\\n    if (!o.under) return false;\\n    const p = objById(S, o.under);\\n    return !!(p && !p.done && p.vol > 1);\\n190→  }\\n\\n  function canTouch(S, o) {\\n    if (!o || o.done || !o.alive) return false;\\n    if (covered(S, o)) return false;\\n    if (o.hidden && !o.marked) return false;\\n    if (o.needsWindow && S.windowOpen <= 0) return false;\\n    if (o.needsBoard && S.device && !S.device.shown) return false;\\n    if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return !!o.window;\\n    if (o.type === 'lobe') return !!o.open;\\n200→    if (o.type === 'eye') return !!o.open;\\n    if (o.type === 'repeat') return !!o.open;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nearest(S, p, rad, pred) {\\n    let best = null, bd = rad;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!pred(o)) continue;\\n210→      const d = hypot(o.x - p.x, o.y - p.y);\\n      if (d <= bd) { bd = d; best = o; }\\n    }\\n    return best;\\n  }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js\",\"offset\":175,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"\\n  function inDome(S, x, y) {\\n    const st = S.strain;\\n    if (!st || !st.domes) return false;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < st.domes.length; i++) {\\n      const d = st.domes[i];\\n      if (d.t > 0 && hypot(x - d.x, y - d.y) <= d.r) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  function covered(S, o) {\\n    if (!o.under) return false;\\n    const p = objById(S, o.under);\\n    return !!(p && !p.done && p.vol > 1);\\n  }\\n\\n  function canTouch(S, o) {\\n    if (!o || o.done || !o.alive) return false;\\n    if (covered(S, o)) return false;\\n    if (o.hidden && !o.marked) return false;\\n    if (o.needsWindow && S.windowOpen <= 0) return false;\\n    if (o.needsBoard && S.device && !S.device.shown) return false;\\n    if (o.type === 'reed' || o.type === 'voice') return !!o.window;\\n    if (o.type === 'lobe') return !!o.open;\\n    if (o.type === 'eye') return !!o.open;\\n    if (o.type === 'repeat') return !!o.open;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  function nearest(S, p, rad, pred) {\\n    let best = null, bd = rad;\\n    for (let i = 0; i < S.objects.length; i++) {\\n      const o = S.objects[i];\\n      if (!pred(o)) continue;\\n      const d = hypot(o.x - p.x, o.y - p.y);\\n      if (d <= bd) { bd = d; best = o; }\\n    }\\n    return best;\\n  }\\n\",\"total_lines\":1767}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"ed0d0daa-4eb4-4273-8370-25dcd81d7387"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_441","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"validTarget uses p.x and p.y instead of bx and by.\n\nBoth x and bx are set in updateCursor. The magnet pull delta uses p.bx. When assist is zero, the cursor stays still.\n\nA speed drop test will verify the 0.55 factor. It compares free aim against held aim with assist set to 0 and 0.6.\n\nThe held-aim speed is checked to be below 80% of free-aim and above 10. Because the aim magnitude is 0.5, the pull block is skipped; only the slowdown applies. The expected speed ratio is roughly 0.67.\n\nThe held-aim distance of roughly 27 units exceeds the 10-unit minimum, so the speed test passes. A separate still-hand pull test will verify the magnet attraction itself.\n\nThe still-hand pull test will assert that the hand settles within one unit of the target. With assist at zero, the hand remains at its starting position.\n\nThe still-hand pull test will assert a displacement within 0.2 units. The cautery tool and default magnet value of 22 are confirmed valid for the tests. All file changes will be applied now, including batched edits to shell.js and new helpers in sim.js. The staccato flight interpolation may also need scaling.\n\nA faster landIn rate makes the bead travel faster along the path, producing the visible timing change. The beatPeriod window for tremolo will be implemented. The cantor voice window scales with beat so higher beats shorten the cycle; the default stays identical. The cantor test should remain unaffected because it holds move 3 for 3.3 seconds and skips the scaled beats. Fermata does not use beat.\n\nThe spawn test will use a try-finally block to reset GAME.Dev even if an exception occurs, preventing the next test from seeing the altered spawn value. A comparison test against hardcoded land times is considered optional.\n\nThe spawn test will reset the dev flag immediately after reading bead counts, before any assertions. If spawnStrain throws, the reset is skipped.\n\nThe ghost bead will use the color '#67d6ff'. Multiple ghosts are supported because each sample paints a disc and seen.includes prevents duplicates. The spy buffer is cleared fresh each frame to avoid stale color data. The px.disc signature is (g, cx, cy, r, c).\n\nThe engine disc wrapper forwards extra arguments to the original function. The shell test's second look does not require the game to be unpaused because go('op') handles that on entry. beginCase sets RT.S, so entering op does not recreate the state. With fadeTime set to zero, go enters immediately and updates.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4d34d5d9-33b5-423e-ade0-1c00f0e73cd1-56","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"overlay\\(fn|_overlays","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js","head_limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5238,"output_tokens":2194,"cache_read_input_tokens":131328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"268f6ff9-afbd-42e6-aa8a-7c56c32f963d"}
