{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_462","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A tap is held for the step it is pressed on. Its release occurs one step later.\n\nThe test queues a second tap during the same advance tick that releases the first. The tick processes the new press before the old release.\n\nThe press() method returns early if the code is already held. If the first tap is still held when the second tap occurs, the second press is ignored.\n\nThe second tap still gets added to _taps even though press() is ignored. During the next tick, that queued tap releases the first tap and the new one is processed.\n\nThe ignored press leaves _fresh unchanged. The next tick releases the queued tap and clears held, so pressed becomes false. The device index stays at 1. A third press succeeds because the code is no longer held.\n\nEvery other down tap is swallowed. The first tap succeeds, the second fails, and so on. The log shows four successful moves at indices 0, 2, 3, and 4.\n\nThe every-other failure theory is wrong. After the second down failed, the code was released during that tick and the ignored press still added to _tapsDue. The next tap succeeded because the code was no longer held.\n\nDown 3 succeeding contradicts the held-code theory. The accumulator might overflow and run two steps per advance call.\n\nOnly the second down tap failed. The accumulator overflow theory is being reconsidered.\n\nThe `down` key may conflict with repeat or engine menu bindings. The input map might include extra keys beyond ArrowDown and Pad12. Only one increment per pressed frame is possible because the code uses pressed state rather than repeat. Advance runs fixed time and does not account for tap release steps.\n\nThe debug script will log the step count returned by advance and the device index after each call. A swallowed tap that runs two steps would leave the index at 1, matching the log. The first successful move is explained this way. The third down still succeeding remains unexplained.\n\nThe accumulator overflow theory is confirmed. Some advance calls run two steps, releasing the button before the next tap arrives and allowing it to succeed. Other calls run only one step, so the release spills into the following advance and swallows the next tap.\n\nThe test helper advances twice after each press to clear the enter delay, but that also releases the tap on the second advance. A single advance per tap works for one move, yet consecutive taps can drop every other or swallow the next if the previous release lands in the following advance. The fix is to add an extra advance after each tap and advance so the button releases before the next tap arrives.\n\nThe test helper already performs two advances after each tap. I will switch the debug script to use `press('down')`, `press('confirm')`, and `press('toolNext')` instead of separate tap and advance calls. This ensures the button releases before the next press arrives. The second advance will not double-increment the device index because the button is already released.\n\nThe confirm button's second advance simply plays the new phase for one step, so the phase remains at Repair. Even if the first advance already consumed both the press and release, the second advance still produces exactly one increment.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ae276ddb-2399-4787-a564-d874a8dff0b3-97","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/dbg-clear.mjs","old_string":"game.advance(game.o.step);\nconsole.log('enter', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nGAME.openDev();\ngame.input.tap('toolNext');\ngame.advance(game.o.step);\nconsole.log('tab', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nfor (let n = 0; n < 7; n++) {\n  game.input.tap('down');\n  game.advance(game.o.step);\n  console.log('down', n, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n}\ngame.input.tap('confirm');\ngame.advance(game.o.step);\nconsole.log('confirm', JSON.stringify(snap()));","new_string":"const press = (action) => {\n  game.input.tap(action);\n  const a = game.advance(game.o.step);\n  const b = game.advance(game.o.step);\n  return [a, b];\n};\nconsole.log('enter', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nGAME.openDev();\nconsole.log('tab', press('toolNext'), JSON.stringify(snap()));\nfor (let n = 0; n < 7; n++) console.log('down', n, press('down'), JSON.stringify(snap()));\nconsole.log('confirm', press('confirm'), JSON.stringify(snap()));"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2107,"output_tokens":2596,"cache_read_input_tokens":175232,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"403cf921-29be-43de-940a-fa54e816db6d"}
