{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_475","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The suite appended a new audio line at line 7.\n\nThe rebuilt HTML was verified in full run 166 with zero failures. The new audio line belongs to this rebuilt page, not the previous one.\n\nPROGRESS was updated with the new game logic. Dev cursor and assist settings override preferences when they leave defaults. Beat and spawn changes affect landings and spawns. Clear phase ends a strain phase.\n\nThe scratch path was omitted from PROGRESS.\n\nTests.log is exactly one line. The debug script was deleted.\n\nBoth dev/game.html and root HTML are identical in size.\n\nNo forbidden names were added. The verify todo is marked complete.\n\nThe goal plan will receive a single ## Deviations section with one terse bullet per deviation.\n\nThe checklist items remain checked because this pass fixes already-completed work.\n\nThe final reply will lead with the game completion and fixed skeptic gaps, then include the copied About answers.\n\nThe testing feedback still shows 9 issues and 7 critical. About.js was not edited, so the published answers remain the build record. Notes/feedback.md was also rebuilt from the same object.\n\nPROGRESS will be updated to show the exact test output and the --fast flag. The deviation bullet will note that Second Look paints recorded hands and strain marks in light blue while its timer runs.\n\nThe deviation bullets are now fully drafted. Staccato beat scales bead flight and the reed and voice windows. Spawn rate scales bead counts and the Tremolo reed wait. At beat 0.5 and spawn 1 authored clocks and counts remain unchanged. Clear phase finishes the live strain including beads worms and lobes and fills a short IV order.\n\nThe debug script dbg-clear.mjs was deleted. A shell command appended the run summary to handoff.log without adding blank lines or corrupting the file. tests.log was left untouched.\n\n