{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_489","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fast test log shows 134 checks, while the full log shows 166. This discrepancy suggests the full suite may be running additional cases.\n\nThe 32 extra checks are browser and hub tail cases after line 779. The fast path includes roughly 24 new unit checks, while the full suite adds the remaining 32. Launch evidence appears after the HTML rebuild.\n\nThe handoff log claims the rebuilt page launched, but timestamps show launch occurred after rebuild. I will inspect the launch screenshot to verify the title was actually filled.\n\nThe full test path loads source in the VM and launches a separate browser for the remaining checks. The browser launch passed with zero errors. I am now checking stepTremolo to verify beat changes flare timing as claimed, though the suite passed.\n\nThe clear phase win handler sets cheatUsed before checking the key, but the test only reaches it after navigating and confirming. The suite passed. I am now checking whether other strains could fail this phase.\n\nAll strains can finish the clear phase. The ghost paint afterimage is fixed. playTune correctly overrides preferences with dev values and resets to defaults.\n\nplayTune still applies settings when both values are at defaults, and the dirty flag is not set by settings. A potential spawn bug was noted: spawn uses tuneOf(null), which reads GAME.TUNE directly rather than the tune passed to step. The live operator clones GAME.TUNE before calling playTune.\n\nThe spawn bug is harmless because playTune only overrides hands, not spawn. beat is correctly read from the cloned tune passed to step, so the dev slider affects it properly. Default identity values are tempo 1, period 1, and coda period 0.8.\n\nSpawn 1 leaves counts unchanged and sets wake to 6. The bot still clears all cases, so defaults remain sound.\n\nI will verify the inlined sim.js in the HTML matches src/core/sim.js by checking unique lines and confirming old dead code is removed.\n\nThe HTML contains no stray strains.beat assignments. The secondLook gift condition is redundant but harmless. forceRewind does not set ghosts, which is correct because the gift is Second Look. Ghosts expire via ghostT and do not need manual clearing on phase advance. drawOp ghost coordinates match the cursor sampling space.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf6ccb2a-0dfa-4f23-b0b7-e93418e36d1e-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"67d6ff","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf6ccb2a-0dfa-4f23-b0b7-e93418e36d1e-29","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/tests/run.mjs","offset":760,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf6ccb2a-0dfa-4f23-b0b7-e93418e36d1e-30","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":990,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf6ccb2a-0dfa-4f23-b0b7-e93418e36d1e-31","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function tuneOf|TUNE\\.strains|playTune\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1900,"output_tokens":1637,"cache_read_input_tokens":71936,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"483bb599-40e4-491f-a41f-da381b7fa6e