{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_490","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A subtle bug in stepTremolo spawn wake needs examination.\n\nThe stepTremolo spawn wake logic passed the test. Initial wake derives from GAME.TUNE, while respawn uses the tune argument; both see the dev slider.\n\nThe reedWait test and bead count logic are confirmed honest. The prior gaps appear genuinely fixed. A grep for 67d6ff only returned game.html, tests, and shell.js, omitting the root HTML path.\n\nThe root HTML sits in the parent work folder, so it was missed by the dev-folder grep. The earlier root search did find `#67d6ff` at line 19271. game.html and the root HTML are identical in size and timestamp, so a quick file comparison will confirm they are the same copy. The launch screenshot will be checked to satisfy the PNG review requirement.\n\nThe new launch screenshot will be read to confirm it is not blank. The plan was not weakened; deviations were added rather than criteria removed. The test count gap between 134 and 166 is explained by runLive checks, and the exact number of those checks will be tallied.\n\nThe full log shows 166 checks with zero failures, confirming no unit tests failed. The theater test drives the real input path through openDev and toolNext, then confirms the Repair phase name; it would fail if the CHEATS array order changed, but down x7 from index 0 lands on index 7.\n\nThe ghost test is honest: it spies the unique px.disc color during game.advance after secondLook, and would fail if paint were removed. The op step calls secondLook again without clearing ghosts because ghostT decrements but stays positive, so drawOp paints correctly. beginCase sets RT.S for go('op') to use.\n\nThe ghost test is confirmed sound because the drawn state and the secondLook target are the same object. The objective is not refuted. Next, the launch image will be checked and the HTML files compared for differences.\n\nA careful review of stepStaccato landIn confirms the tempo multiplier does not alter default timing. At the default beat and tempo values, the old and new formulas produce identical results for tremolo period, cantor move, coda duration, spawn count, and wake value.\n\nThe bot cleared all eleven cases at S-rank, confirming no regression in clears. The intern clock still divides by the step divisor, which is expected behavior. During clear phase, every object including lacerations is marked done before advancing, and the test confirms phase 2. The IV requirement only fills when needed, so the c4 staccato phase test passed. The objective remains unrefuted.\n\nGhost cursor handling is sound: secondLook copies ring cursors and pushRing always sets them from players, so the test requiring cursors.length is satisfied. The anti-ratchet gap is resolved because something now reads and paints. PLAN deviations explain implementation rather than weakening criteria.\n\nThe exit-interview remains valid. The root HTML test passed, confirming no external scripts. The findings array will be empty because no gaps remain. The terminal token will read `Not Refuted`. Both output files will be written. A final check of the goal plan criteria is underway.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule bars new objections unless a defect is demonstrable or a gating criterion is unmet. All gating criteria were satisfied in round one, and the refreshed evidence is current: launch, browsers, hub, handoff, and tests all carry timestamps after the rebuilt HTML. The test log and hub log share the same timestamp because the test command writes both files during runLive. Launch occurred slightly earlier in the same runLive sequence.\n\nhandoff.log is 01:40, after tests.log at 01:39:30. The child process likely wrote handoff during runLive before finish(), while the parent only captured the filtered test count afterward.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3af61d90-8e20-4b52-85bd-8ff5cb4177fb-32","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/launch-1.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3af61d90-8e20-4b52-85bd-8ff5cb4177fb-33","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cmp -s \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916.html\" \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/game.html\" && echo IDENTICAL || echo DIFFER\n# confirm inlined shell/sim match src for the four fix sites\npython3 - << 'PY'\nimport pathlib\nroot = pathlib.Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916\")\nhtml = pathlib.Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916.html\").read_text(errors=\"replace\")\nfor rel in [\"src/core/sim.js\", \"src/scenes/shell.js\"]:\n    src = (root/rel).read_text()\n    # strip the wrapper the bundle may not include: compare a distinctive interior slice\n    start = src.find(\"function strainBeat\") if \"sim.js\" in rel else src.find(\"function playTune\")\n    chunk = src[start:start+500]\n    print(rel, \"CHUNK_IN_HTML\" if chunk in html else \"CHUNK_MISSING\", \"len\", len(src), \"src_in_html\", src in html)\nPY","description":"Confirm bundle matches current sim and shell"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3802,"output_tokens":2490,"cache_read_input_tokens":73728,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"47b8d909-9f78-400b-a9cf-69e3