{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_491","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The launch image shows title art substantially filling the screen.\n\nAll five prior gaps are fixed with honest tests. No regressions were found. The verdict files will be written with refuted set to false.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The shipped page matches the current sim and shell, and the prior gaps are exercised by the passing suite. I’ll record that verdict."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8d0473d6-7fb0-448b-a916-02fff6822488-34","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/goal-classifier-08d1b960e391-2-skeptic-0.md","content":"# Re-check (skeptic 0, round 2)\n\nNot refuted. Each prior gap is fixed in the current source, inlined verbatim into the hand-in HTML, and failed by an honest check if removed. `implementer/tests.log` is `166 checks, 0 failed` (exit 0), written after the rebuild.\n\n## Prior gaps\n\n- **Second Look ghosts.** `secondLook` still stores `S.ghosts` and `S.ghostT` (`src/core/sim.js:323-331`). `drawOp` now paints each recorded cursor and strain sample while `ghostT > 0` (`src/scenes/shell.js:430-439`, color `#67d6ff`, used nowhere else). `tests/run.mjs:694-718` rewinds a live c2 operation and spies `px.disc` during `game.advance`. `tests/run.mjs:394` requires a non-empty ghost with cursor samples.\n- **Dev cursor and assist.** `playTune` copies settings only while the slider is still on the documented default (`src/scenes/shell.js:167-173`). The op scene steps with that tune (`shell.js:354`, `shell.js:369`). `tests/run.mjs:636-676` drives `game.go('op')`: cursor 480 outruns a 200 preference by more than 1.8×, and assist 1.2 pulls while a reset slider with assist preference 0 stays still.\n- **Staccato beat and spawn.** `strainBeat` / `strainSpawn` (`sim.js:832-838`) scale bead `landIn` (`sim.js:855-858`), Tremolo and Cantor windows (`sim.js:1003`, `sim.js:1154`, `sim.js:1185`), bead counts (`sim.js:1228-1233`), and the Tremolo reed wait (`sim.js:1017`, `sim.js:1251`). At beat 0.5 and spawn 1 the scales are 1. `tests/run.mjs:398-444` requires a faster beat to land and flare sooner, 4 vs 8 beads, and reed waits 6 vs 3. All eleven bot clears still rank S, so the defaults did not move the case clocks.\n- **Clear phase.** Confirm on Clear phase sets `strain.done`, kills beads, finishes worms and lobes, and fills a short IV (`shell.js:533-544`). `phaseClear` treats that as clear (`sim.js:1299-1313`). `tests/run.mjs:682-691` opens the dev panel on c4 Staccato, moves to that cheat, and expects phase 2 Repair.\n- **Verification step 1.** Magnet, guide-follow, all eight wheel directions, a loose stitch, and a cautery lock that requires `lock > 0`, a `lock` event, and a slip tagged `lock` are in `tests/run.mjs:136-204` and `tests/run.mjs:256-294`. They call `Cursor.update`, `Wheel.update`, and `Op.step`.\n\n## Bundle and launch\n\n`src/core/sim.js` and `src/scenes/shell.js` are contained in the root HTML. That file is byte-identical to `game.html` (1,498,704 bytes, rebuilt 2026-11-05 01:36:43, before the suite). Launch, browser, Hub, and handoff logs are newer than that rebuild: title buffer 480×270, Enter opens the menu, Chromium/Firefox/WebKit 30s with 0 errors, four Hub runs pass, client stroke at 111,122 on the host. `launch-1.png` shows the title art across the frame. Plan edits mark the checklist done and record these behaviors. They do not delete or weaken a criterion.\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8d0473d6-7fb0-448b-a916-02fff6822488-35","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/goal-verdict-08d1b960e391-2-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"implementer/tests.log is '166 checks, 0 failed' after the rebuild; sim.js and shell.js are inlined in the root HTML (ghost paint shell.js:430, playTune shell.js:167, strainBeat sim.js:832, clear-phase shell.js:533); launch-1.png shows the title.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"# Re-check (skeptic 0, round 2)\\n\\nNot refuted. Each prior gap is fixed in the current source, inlined verbatim into the hand-in HTML, and failed by an honest check if removed. `implementer/tests.log` is `166 checks, 0 failed` (exit 0), written after the rebuild.\\n\\n## Prior gaps\\n\\n- **Second Look ghosts.** `secondLook` still stores `S.ghosts` and `S.ghostT` (`src/core/sim.js:323-331`). `drawOp` now paints each recorded cursor and strain sample while `ghostT > 0` (`src/scenes/shell.js:430-439`, color `#67d6ff`, used nowhere else). `tests/run.mjs:694-718` rewinds a live c2 operation and spies `px.disc` during `game.advance`. `tests/run.mjs:394` requires a non-empty ghost with cursor samples.\\n- **Dev cursor and assist.** `playTune` copies settings only while the slider is still on the documented default (`src/scenes/shell.js:167-173`). The op scene steps with that tune (`shell.js:354`, `shell.js:369`). `tests/run.mjs:636-676` drives `game.go('op')`: cursor 480 outruns a 200 preference by more than 1.8×, and assist 1.2 pulls while a reset slider with assist preference 0 stays still.\\n- **Staccato beat and spawn.** `strainBeat` / `strainSpawn` (`sim.js:832-838`) scale bead `landIn` (`sim.js:855-858`), Tremolo and Cantor windows (`sim.js:1003`, `sim.js:1154`, `sim.js:1185`), bead counts (`sim.js:1228-1233`), and the Tremolo reed wait (`sim.js:1017`, `sim.js:1251`). At beat 0.5 and spawn 1 the scales are 1. `tests/run.mjs:398-444` requires a faster beat to land and flare sooner, 4 vs 8 beads, and reed waits 6 vs 3. All eleven bot clears still rank S, so the defaults did not move the case clocks.\\n- **Clear phase.** Confirm on Clear phase sets `strain.done`, kills beads, finishes worms and lobes, and fills a short IV (`shell.js:533-544`). `phaseClear` treats that as clear (`sim.js:1299-1313`). `tests/run.mjs:682-691` opens the dev panel on c4 Staccato, moves to that cheat, and expects phase 2 Repair.\\n- **Verification step 1.** Magnet, guide-follow, all eight wheel directions, a loose stitch, and a cautery lock that requires `lock > 0`, a `lock` event, and a slip tagged `lock` are in `tests/run.mjs:136-204` and `tests/run.mjs:256-294`. They call `Cursor.update`, `Wheel.update`, and `Op.step`.\\n\\n## Bundle and launch\\n\\n`src/core/sim.js` and `src/scenes/shell.js` are contained in the root HTML. That file is byte-identical to `game.html` (1,498,704 bytes, rebuilt 2026-11-05 01:36:43, before the suite). Launch, browser, Hub, and handoff logs are newer than that rebuild: title buffer 480×270, Enter opens the menu, Chromium/Firefox/WebKit 30s with 0 errors, four Hub runs pass, client stroke at 111,122 on the host. `launch-1.png` shows the title art across the frame. Plan edits mark the checklist done and record these behaviors. They do not delete or weaken a criterion.\\n\"\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3776,"output_tokens":2208,"cache_read_input_tokens":77440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"35587ad6-de30-40c0-9a3c-c06c7a6624a1"}
