1,32,111,98,115,101,114,118,97,116,105,111,110,115,32,116,111,32,96,123,83,67,82,65,84,67,72,125,47,116,101,115,116,115,46,108,111,103,96,32,111,114,32,96,123,83,67,82,65,84,67,72,125,47,104,97,110,100,111,102,102,46,108,111,103,96,46,10,50,48,58,35,35,32,78,111,110,45,103,111,97,108,115,10,50,55,58,35,35,32,65,115,115,117,109,101,100,32,115,99,111,112,101,10,51,51,58,35,35,32,73,109,112,108,101,109,101,110,116,97,116,105,111,110,32,97,112,112,114,111,97,99,104,10,51,54,58,35,35,32,84,97,115,107,32,99,104,101,99,107,108,105,115,116,10,52,54,58,35,35,32,68,101,118,105,97,116,105,111,110,115,10,54,49,58,35,35,32,82,105,115,107,115,32,47,32,67,111,110,116,114,97,100,105,99,116,105,111,110,115,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":13,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9%2Fwork/01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"## Goal kind\"},{\"line_number\":6,\"content\":\"## Acceptance criteria\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":14,\"content\":\"1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one test command PLAN.md §20 names (`node tests/run.mjs`). It must load the shipped sim and scenes (not a reimplementation or a mock of them) and assert criteria 2, 3, and 4: every tool’s success and mistake, cursor full-stick / fine / magnet / guide-follow, all eight wheel directions, vitals and clock math, Code Blue window, phase-checkpoint restore, grades and rank, each strain’s success and listed failure branch, Long Breath’s 0.25 world-time factor with hand speed unchanged, Second Look deep-equality plus ghosts, determinism with and without drawing, content-id resolution, per-case bot clears, the chained New Game → credits playthrough, attract idle and consumed exit, dev-slider live change and reset, and Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots including the retractor alone and with two. Capture stdout to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log`. Pass only if the log contains a one-line count, zero failures, and no other chatter. Re-run after any change to code those tes [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"2. gating: Launch the real root HTML from `file://` with Playwright 1.63 (Chromium, `--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`) at 1920×1080, twice in a row. Each run must have zero page errors, a drawing buffer of 480×270 (PLAN.md §3 screen-size rule, not a stale default), and a substantially filled frame (title art and the chosen title, not a blank or a few pixels). A confirm/start input must change what is on screen (menu follows the title). Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must show the same success. Then load the same file for 30 seconds in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit with zero page errors; with the Appendix E pad stub, confirm a PlayStation R2 prompt, an Xbox prompt after the Settings glyph option, and a keyboard/mouse prompt after those devices; on an iPhone-profile touch page, confirm the required notice and Settings control, no touch buttons, and that a Settings tap opens settings. Capture `{SCRATCH}/browsers.lo [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":16,\"content\":\"3. gating: Run the four Hub harness URLs in PLAN.md §20 (2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter, and loss; host-leave; server), plus a no-session open of the same page. Serve only this game on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port, confirm the framed document title is this game, and stop only that server by its PID. Pass means each run has `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, and the standalone open is not in a session and still reaches the title. With two same-origin harness frames, a client stroke must show up on the host’s state. Capture `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"4. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json` and confirm criterion 1’s shape, non-empty answers, and `usage`. Confirm the HTML inlines the game (no external script or audio URLs), contains no `TODO` / `FIXME` / `placeholder` / `stub`, and does not use the §1 forbidden names outside the allowed source-title spots. Confirm an `OfflineAudioContext` or `AnalyserNode` render of an effect, one voice, and the choir is not silent, and that at default settings the music bus is well below effects. Append these observations to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log` or `{SCRATCH}/handoff.log`.\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"## Non-goals\"},{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"## Assumed scope\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"## Implementation approach\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"## Deviations\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"## Risks / Contradictions\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-dc0fca70-2597-49a3-8da1-99f9ac18020e-2","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,57,50,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,52,45,50,50,51,57,49,54,95,95,120,52,56,56,101,98,57,47,119,111,114,107,47,79,112,101,110,45,84,97,98,108,101,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,45,79,112,105,110,105,111,110,45,84,114,97,117,109,97,45,67,101,110,116,101,114,45,83,101,99,111,110,100,