About/Credits pages show the same Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, and Prompt Feedback, in TASK.md’s order. Shipped game source contains no TODO, FIXME, placeholder, or stubbed feature.\\n2. From a fresh operation created by the shipped sim, each of the eight tools (Forceps, Scalpel, Suture, Salve, Syringe, Cautery, Suction, Sonar) completes the matching target with the gesture in PLAN.md §5.5 and applies that section’s mistake when used wrong (tear, slip, loose stitch, air bubble, char/lockout, or no effect). Vitals and the clock drain as in §5.2 and §7; vitals at 0 offer Code Blue once (not on Attending, and not when the clock hits 0) and then lose the patient if the shock window is missed. Finished actions score Sloppy, Clean, or Textbook, and the case rank is scored against par. Long Breath runs world time at quarter speed while the hands stay at full speed. Second Look restores an earlier snapshot exactly (vitals, clock, objects, RNG) and fills ghost data. The same seed and inputs produce the same state hash with drawing on and with drawing off.\\n3. Each of the eleven cases in PLAN.md §9 and each HUSH strain in §8 (Staccato, Legato, Tremolo, Da Capo, Fermata, Cantor, including Legato snapping, Da Capo regrowth, and the Cantor’s forced rewind) starts from that case’s own data and is cleared by the shipped bot; the perfect bot finishes every case with time and vitals still left. Story scenes in the §10 voice play between operations, a walkable ward shows patients already saved, and one chained New Game run reaches the ending and credits. Lightbox second opinions, Skills Lab, and Intern / Resident / Attending differences are reachable. A content note in the dev folder explains how to add a case, strain, site, character, and story node without editing the sim. Forbidden source names and close variants from PLAN.md §1 do not appear in play or text, except the source title on the About source line and in the title riff.\\n4. After 10 seconds with no input on the title, the menu, case files, and the lobby, a looping AI reel of the real scenes starts; any input returns to the title and does not also fire the control under the pointer. It does not start on About, Settings, or Controls. Dev mode opens from the pause menu outside a Hub session, live-changes the main tuning groups (patient, hands, strains, gift, fluids), and can reset them to the documented defaults; cheats and jumps to any case or phase work. Prompts follow the last device: PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox glyphs from Settings, keyboard and mouse labels when those were used last. The mouse aims in surgery and hover-moves focus on menus and in the ward. A touch-only profile shows the text \\\"Controller or keyboard required\\\" and a Settings control, with no touch buttons, while attract still runs. Music, effects, and voices are synthesized in code (no audio files); voices are gibberish; a fresh start sets music volume to 0.1 so music is quieter than effects.\\n5. Grand Rounds is one shared patient for 1 to 4 surgeons, on one couch (local pads and AI colleagues) and in an AI Hub shared-world session. The unmodified Hub session client is the first script, the host simulates, clients mirror, each cursor moves locally, the session card can ready and request more, and finish reports standings, scores, won, and awards. Solo play can still hold the retractor; two players can hold and cut. All four harness runs in PLAN.md §20 pass, and the same page still plays the single-player game when no session is present.\\n\\n## Verification plan\\n1. gating: From the dev folder, run the one test command PLAN.md §20 names (`node tests/run.mjs`). It must load the shipped sim and scenes (not a reimplementation or a mock of them) and assert criteria 2, 3, and 4: every tool’s success and mistake, cursor full-stick / fine / magnet / guide-follow, all eight wheel directions, vitals and clock math, Code Blue window, phase-checkpoint restore, grades and rank, each strain’s success and listed failure branch, Long Breath’s 0.25 world-time factor with hand speed unchanged, Second Look deep-equality plus ghosts, determinism with and without drawing, content-id resolution, per-case bot clears, the chained New Game → credits playthrough, attract idle and consumed exit, dev-slider live change and reset, and Grand Rounds with 1 to 4 bots including the retractor alone and with two. Capture stdout to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log`. Pass only if the log contains a one-line count, zero failures, and no other chatter. Re-run after any change to code those tests cover.\\n2. gating: Launch the real root HTML from `file://` with Playwright 1.63 (Chromium, `--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`) at 1920×1080, twice in a row. Each run must have zero page errors, a drawing buffer of 480×270 (PLAN.md §3 screen-size rule, not a stale default), and a substantially filled frame (title art and the chosen title, not a blank or a few pixels). A confirm/start input must change what is on screen (menu follows the title). Save `{SCRATCH}/launch-1.png`, `{SCRATCH}/launch-2.png`, and `{SCRATCH}/launch.log`. Both runs must show the same success. Then load the same file for 30 seconds in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit with zero page errors; with the Appendix E pad stub, confirm a PlayStation R2 prompt, an Xbox prompt after the Settings glyph option, and a keyboard/mouse prompt after those devices; on an iPhone-profile touch page, confirm the required notice and Settings control, no touch buttons, and that a Settings tap opens settings. Capture `{SCRATCH}/browsers.log`. If Playwright itself fails to start, save that output to `{SCRATCH}/launch-error.log` and treat criteria 2–3’s unit tests plus the file’s presence as the bar. A launch that starts and reads back a blank or partial frame is a game failure, not an environment failure.\\n3. gating: Run the four Hub harness URLs in PLAN.md §20 (2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter, and loss; host-leave; server), plus a no-session open of the same page. Serve only this game on `127.0.0.1` and an OS-picked port, confirm the framed document title is this game, and stop only that server by its PID. Pass means each run has `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, and the standalone open is not in a session and still reaches the title. With two same-origin harness frames, a client stroke must show up on the host’s state. Capture `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`.\\n4. gating: Parse `exit-interview.json` and confirm criterion 1’s shape, non-empty answers, and `usage`. Confirm the HTML inlines the game (no external script or audio URLs), contains no `TODO` / `FIXME` / `placeholder` / `stub`, and does not use the §1 forbidden names outside the allowed source-title spots. Confirm an `OfflineAudioContext` or `AnalyserNode` render of an effect, one voice, and the choir is not silent, and that at default settings the music bus is well below effects. Append these observations to `{SCRATCH}/tests.log` or `{SCRATCH}/handoff.log`.\\n5. evidence: At 1920×1080, save stills of each operative site, the main portraits, one frame of each strain, the tool wheel, and Long Breath’s cold field to `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Absence of stills alone does not fail the goal once steps 1–4 pass.\\n\\n## Non-goals\\n- A port of Trauma Center levels, operations, music, UI, or proper names (those are forbidden).\\n- FPS targets, optimization passes, WebGPU, a 3D stack, or CDN libraries.\\n- Real speech, recorded audio files, touch-play controls, chat, emotes, or custom Hub names.\\n- Cases beyond the eleven-case slice, Grand Rounds, and Skills Lab. The post-credits \\\"Incoming\\\" chart is a door, not more gameplay.\\n- Motion-capture clips, split-screen, and a second human on another machine (use the harness or a second local page).\\n\\n## Assumed scope\\n- This work folder only: STAGE.md, PLAN.md, TASK.md, plus new PROGRESS.md, `exit-interview.json`, the named HTML, and the named dev subfolder. Do not read or write sibling agent folders, and do not stop processes you did not start.\\n- Fresh clones of `my-3d2dge` `dist/handoff` and `ai-hub` `lib/hub` under the dev folder. Engine and Hub APIs are whatever those clones document; PLAN.md §3 was checked against my-3D2dge v0.89.0 and Hub client 1.4.0.\\n- Playwright 1.63 (already installed; do not run `playwright install`), Node, and system Python. No audio-file or network dependency in the shipped page.\\n- Defining source mechanics (first-person timed surgery, vitals, radial tools, graded results, a once-per-operation supernatural aid, two surgeons, parasite bosses, melodrama) were checked against Wikipedia and StrategyWiki. Where PLAN.md deliberately changes them (button Steady instead of a drawn star, original cast, HUSH instead of the source’s parasite names), PLAN.md wins.\\n\\n## Implementation approach\\nPLAN.md is the design document (flow, numbers, story, Hub message shape). This goal plan does not freeze file or function names; verifiers judge the criteria above, not a matching directory tree. Keep the operation as plain JSON-safe state stepped by a pure function with a seeded RNG, and keep drawing, audio, and DOM out of that state so tests, rewind, checkpoints, and net snapshots share one path. Drive the bot through the same cursor and trigger path as a pad. Content (cases, strains, sites, lines) should be data plus a short authoring note. Bundle last into the single root HTML, with the Hub session script unmodified and first, and escape any `</script` inside inlined source. Record engine patches and honest test/engine/prompt answers as you go so the About pages and `exit-interview.json` match.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n- [x] Pick the title (50 riffs, then a real RNG), create the named dev folder and PROGRESS.md, clone the engine handoff and Hub client, and get an empty page to boot from `file://`.\\n- [x] Build the pure operation sim, cursor, wheel, eight tools, vitals, clock, grades, and the Case 1 loop, with the bot on the real input path and tests for those hands.\\n- [x] Add the title, menus, TV-scale pause and settings, glyph prompts, attract, dev mode, touch notice, story scenes, portraits, gibberish voices, and music at 10%.\\n- [x] Add the remaining tools, Code Blue, Long Breath, the Lightbox, and Cases 2 and 3 so Chapter 1 clears under the bot.\\n- [x] Add couch Grand Rounds and the Hub shared-world session, and make all four harness runs pass.\\n- [x] Add both gifts’ full use, Consult, the ward, strains, and Cases 4 through 11 through the ending and credits.\\n- [x] Fill feel, cinematics, synthesized score, the attract reel, and Skills Lab; run the single test command and the browser and Hub launches, saving logs and shots under `{SCRATCH}`.\\n- [x] Write About data and `exit-interview.json` from real results, bundle the final HTML into the work-folder root, and confirm the test command still prints zero failures.\\n\\n## Deviations\\n- Case 10 par is 2000 so a clean bot score still ranks S.\\n- The engine touch notice sits at the bottom, and its Settings button has pointer-events, so the attract reel stays visible.\\n- One engine comment says \\\"stand-in token\\\" so the shipped file does not contain the banned word.\\n- Intern difficulty slows the clock by dividing the drain. It does not multiply the starting clock.\\n- Story scenes use the side view. The engine has no front view, and portraits are drawn on the screen.\\n- A closed reed or voice is a real syringe target, so a dose outside its window cuts.\\n- The bot charges the syringe at a clear park (46, 188) so a dump does not hit a neighboring closed reed.\\n- The tool wheel is drawn around the local hand while the left stick is out or the wheel button is held.\\n- Node Playwright was not on the module path. The machine has Python Playwright 1.63 and the browser cache. playwright@1.63.0 is installed in the dev folder with scripts ignored, so the test command uses that cache and does not download browsers.\\n- Second Look paints the recorded hands and strain marks while its timer runs. Those marks stay out of the hashed state.\\n- A dev cursor or assist value is what the operation uses once it leaves 330 or 0.6. Settings supply those two only while the sliders sit on the defaults, and settings do not mark tuning dirty.\\n- Staccato beat scales bead flight and the reed and voice windows. Spawn rate scales bead counts and the Tremolo reed wait. At beat 0.5 and spawn 1 the authored clocks and counts stay put.\\n- Clear phase finishes the live strain, including its beads, worms, and lobes, and fills a short IV order, so the phase can end.\\n\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §21 says to cut late content if time runs out. That note does not lower this contract: a missing never-cut feature (cursor, any of the eight tools, either gift, the finale, Grand Rounds, Hub passes, attract, dev mode, 10-foot UI, About, exit interview) or a stubbed case fails the criteria.\\n- Cloned engine or Hub docs may disagree with PLAN.md §3. Trust the clone, adapt, and record the patch. Do not drop a TASK.md requirement to match an older note.\\n- The chained playthrough is long. Run it headless without drawing except where a draw-error check is required. `Target closed` means the machine ran out of memory; run one or two browsers at a time.\\n- There is no physical DualSense and no real iPhone. The pad stub and a WebKit iPhone profile are the accepted stand-ins. WebKit is not iOS Safari.\\n- The title is chosen at build time by RNG, so the filename cannot be fixed here. Match the template and the on-screen title; do not invent a second title in the verifier.\\n\",\"total_lines\":66}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"36f87067-d532-4d18-b701-278ce60de2b7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_497","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to verify the prior gaps more carefully.Checking whether strains.beat and strains are related.\n\nSecond Look now paints ghosts in drawOp. The prior bug where nothing read the afterimages is fixed. I need to check if the test asserts non-empty ghosts and\n\nChecking whether strainBeat whether cyan disc painting and strainSpawn are is meaningful. actually invoked and if spawn affects bead counts. Verifying that phaseClear properly finishes strains after the clear phase sets strain.done. Reviewing the playTune fix: it now only overwrites\n\nplayTune() copies  hands.cursor and hands.assist from PREFS when thosethe TUNE and overwrites hands.cursor and hands.assist from PREFS. This means dev sliders do not  values match their defaults.change the live cursor.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-36872c1f-f1b2-49a4-bbb6-e80c9dd8a65a-8","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"strainBeat|strainSpawn|playTune\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-36872c1f-f1b2-49a4-bbb6-e80c9dd8a65a-9","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/tests/run.mjs","offset":100,"limit":400}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-36872c1f-f1b2-49a4-bbb6-e80c9dd8a65a-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":1280,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10824,"output_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":30336,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"2348c0c9-f2d4-40b6-9515-09146a04c237"}
