{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_503","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nChecking whether the draw path actually reaches ghost painting. The spy on Epx.disc only works if E.px is the same object used inside the overlay callback.\n\nThe test should be on the op scene before secondLook, so fade or scene issues are unlikely.\n\nSpying on the cyan color constant tests the real draw path rather than an implementation detail.\n\nChecking whether the cyan color is used elsewhere to avoid false positives. The test correctly validates both ghost storage and rendering. A potential real bug remains: ghosts might be included in state hashing or core logic, though the deviation says they stay out of hashed state.The fast test log shows 134 checks, while the full test log shows 166.\n\nCriterion 2 is satisfied because ghosts are part of the gift state, not the drawing process. The implementer's test log shows zero failures across 166 checks, confirming the ghost rendering check passed. I still need to verify that the test was not skipped and actually executed this assertion.\n\nThe zero-failure log confirms the ghost draw path painted cyan discs, so the prior bug is fixed. Now examining the playTune cursor\n\nI should verify whether and assist logic: if tests load the bundled a hand setting differs HTML or source modules. from its default, playTune The check count discrepancy preserves that value is likely just skipped instead of overriding groups. I am now examining it with PREFS. each fix for real bugs that tests might miss. The first fix involves Second Look ghosts painted by drawOp using cursor and strain marks from the ring.\n\nThe speedOf test passed through the real game loop. A null cursor resets to 330, then playTune applies PREFS.cursor\n\nGhost coordinates  of 200. One frame ofuse field coordinates aim movement produces consistent with object tunedCursor above 360, satisfying the threshold. drawing. The ghost timer decrements by  Dev.set runs beforereal dt, not world dt. the op scene step calls I need to verify whether playTune. The zero-failure the state hash includes ghosts, since they  log confirms the numbersare excluded from the worked. Now examining hashed state. pullOf for assist.\n\nThe test monkeypatches px.disc and advances\n\nThe pullOf assist  the game. The operationtest is suspicious.  scene draws ghosts It creates a raw simulation,through overlay calls. sets RT.S to that state, then calls game.go('op'). beginCase likely sets RT.S, so mutating ghostCase If go('op') overwrites RT.S with a fresh operation, should affect RT.S. the hand being measured belongs to the old raw simulation rather than the one the op scene steps. The next step is to verify whether go('op') preserves an existing RT.S or replaces it.\n\nThe secondLook test passed, confirming ghosts are drawn when the state is mutated. The playTune fix correctly falls back to preferences when cursor or assist values match tuning defaults. A floating point issue remains a potential concern.\n\nThe pullOf test passed, so the hand clearly moved. This means go('op') either preserved the raw simulation state or something else displaced it. The speedOf test also relies on beginCase returning a state that go('op') keeps. I need to read the shell op scene and beginCase code to confirm how RT.S is handled.\n\nThe playTune cursor and assist logic is\n\nDev slider resets  confirmed fixed. Slidersuse exact defaults,  now override PREFS when they differ fromso returning to 330  the default, while triggers the PREFS fallback.PREFS still wins if  Settings do not markthe slider is at its default value. The  dirty. The strains.beattests cover both cases, fix scales staccato and Dev.set correctly drain, tremolo flare updates GAME.TUNE.hands.cursor. Now examining strains.beat periods, and cantor and strains.spawn. voice windows.\n\nbeat and spawn are wired into staccato tempo, tremolo period, cantor voice windows, and bead spawning. The bead-landing test is honest: it passes T.strains.beat directly","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-193dc325-8abb-450d-88b9-d9e76eae2da0-20","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/src/core/sim.js","offset":960,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-193dc325-8abb-450d-88b9-d9e76eae2da0-21","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function press|function step\\(|function hold\\(|loadGame|createContext|vm\\.|file://","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261104-223916/tests/run.mjs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-193dc325-8abb-450d-88b9-d9e76eae2da0-22","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/tests.exit"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-193dc325-8abb-450d-88b9-d9e76eae2da0-23","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/launch.log","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4654,"output_tokens":1207,"cache_read_input_tokens":59264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"c4db6c9b-2015-45a8-b39e-b36b36593bb7"}
