{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_507","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" the navigation logic to confirm the cheat itself triggered the transition.\n\nThe anti-ratchet rule limits refutation to demonstrable shipped defects or unmet gating criteria. I am now hunting for real bugs, starting with whether the bundled HTML is stale.The launch image appears substantially filled with the title.\n\nThe rebuilt HTML bundle is the final artifact. If the test suite loads that shipped page, a stale build would mean the fixes never reached the user. The suite printed 166 checks with zero failures, but I must verify whether the tests import source modules directly or load the bundled HTML. A stale root file would explain why the fixes appear to pass yet remain unshipped.\n\nThe ghost positions\n\nThe tests.log is exactly may be wrong. The prior one line with zero  bug left S.ghosts andfailures, matching the gating criteria. I  ghostT unread, so drawOpstill need to verify never painted afterimages. whether this log reflects The fix paints discs the post-fix build by checking timestamps at cursor and strain against source files positions from ring or grepping the bundled samples after the rewind HTML for the ghost-paint point. and playTune logic. Prior rounds apparently accepted these launch checks as valid.\n\nThe ghost positions\n\nI will check launch.log trace the hands' path for failures without during the rewind.  re-running the suite.They paint as a static I am also inspecting cloud of dots for six the cautery lock implementation seconds rather than to ensure its test  animating in real time.is not tautological, and verifying whether clear-phase could fail on strains that regenerate objects.\n\nThe static ghost cloud may not satisfy the acceptance criteria. PLAN.md should clarify whether ghosts must be animated or if a static fill suffices.\n\nThe speedOf test advances the hand by one step after setting the cursor, so the 0.06-second exponential ramp in playTune() should have applied. I am now checking whether the op scene's step function actually invokes playTune(), and whether phase 1 is staccato and phase\n\nThe static ghost cloud 2 is Repair. satisfies the acceptance criterion of filling ghost data. Determinism is preserved because tests passed. The step wrapper omits the tune argument, but Op.step falls back to GAME.TUNE internally.\n\nThe speedOf test passed because the tuned hand moved faster than the pref hand. The pullOf test passed because a non-default assist value triggered magnet pull while the default value did not. I am now checking whether game.go('op') replaces the simulation state, since the test observed movement.\n\nThe Clear phase test passed, so the phase likely advances correctly. The test sequence may be wrong about which menu item it targets, since toolNext switches tabs and the devTab index is unclear.\n\nThe ghost-draw test confirmed the live renderer uses the current pixel reference, so mutating Epx.disc during\n\nThe Clear phase test the test is safe. The targets the correct second-look ghost test menu item. The dev  only verifies that confirm action does ghosts are non-empty;not advance the phase itself; it only sets flags. Phase advancement occurs during Op.step when phaseClear is true. it does not require them to match the cursor's final position.\n\nI need to verify whether press advances the frame and steps the operation after dev input, or if the test assertion is simply wrong. The captured tests.log might be stale or fabricated. I will run the relevant test groups directly to confirm.\n\nThe log references","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-544643db-819e-420d-b1e6-9fc88be7da7b-19","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function tuneOf|TUNING\\s*=|cursor:\\s*330|assist:\\s*0\\.6|beat:\\s*0\\.5|spawn:\\s*1","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/work/Open-Table-Second-Opinion-Traum