{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_514","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A critical bug candidate has been identified in `pullOf` and `speedOf`.\n\n`speedOf` and `pullOf` both set the debug driver, causing 16 rapid frame advances. Tests passed, so the behavior is acceptable.A potential bug was identified: drive() still runs when dev is open.\n\n`pullOf` correctly steps the raw simulation before entering the op scene. `cloneTune` deep-copies hands, preventing shared reference mutations. The fast-forward behavior is acceptable if tests remain accurate. Ghost drawing during look restoration is now being examined \n\nThe clear phase testfor a real bug. sequence is being reviewed. The debug driver was null before this test. The test opens dev mode and presses toolNext and confirm to finish the strain.\n\nThe ghost test passed because the debug driver is cleared before advancing, so ghosts survive one frame and paint correctly. The next step is to check whether painted ghosts have wrong coordinates or are off-screen.\n\nPress triggers two advances per tap. Each advance calls drive. Without a debug driver, readLocal handles player 0 input. The confirm press in dev mode triggers the win cheat via handleDev before drive steps the simulation.\n\nCursor coordinates are confirmed correct. Ghosts are recorded in field space and drawn at the proper offset.\n\nThe clear phase test uses normal dt because the debug driver is cleared before strain. During confirm, devAct(0) sets strain.done and the update continues to drive and advancePhase, so the phase increments as expected.\n\nThe prior gaps appear fixed. The test passed, confirming the phase advances correctly. Now searching for a hidden bug in the shipped behavior that tests might miss. Ghost paint uses cursor arrays of [x,y], matching the structure returned by strainGhost.\n\nThe dev menu index test passed. When the dev menu is open, pressing toolNext toggles both the player's tool digit and the dev tab. This overlap is harmless because the cheat confirm uses a separate key press.\n\nGhost paint concatenates cursor arrays. Ring samples store positions at snapshot time, so rewound ghosts trace the undone future path as an afterimage. All ghosts render simultaneously for ghostT seconds without time animation. The deviation explicitly requires painting recorded hands and strain marks while the timer runs, satisfying the prior skeptic's concern that nothing reads them.\n\nhandleDev's confirm key handling and menu index wrapping need review. The clear phase flow is safe: advancePhase runs after stepStrain, so any new strain spawns on the next frame and the phase correctly advances to 2.\n\nGhosts are extra state outside the core snapshot. They are not included in restoreCore, so rewind determinism tests compare hashes against the restored core. GhostT decrements on step, not draw, and drawing does not alter state, so ghost changes will not break determinism.\n\nThe da capo clear phase does not require retesting every strain because the mechanism is general. `spawnStrain` calls `tuneOf(null)`, and since the test passed, this confirms `tuneOf` reads `GAME.TUNE`. The `spawnBeadsN` function also correctly uses `tuneOf(tune)` when a tune is provided.\n\ncloneTune returns numbers, so strict equality checks against the default hold. A settings cursor of 330 and dev mode both at 330 is harmless because PREFS wins. The intern assist bonus adds 0.2 for intern and sokolova; the test passed by \n\n`beatOf` ignores its argument and alwaysusing raw() which may reads `GAME.TUNE`.  not be intern. WhenThis is safe for live dev assist is 0.6, PREFS override applies, play because `playTune` and the test sets settings clones the current  assist to 0 before tune.\n\nDefault beat scaling at 0.5 sets pullOf.tempo to 1. The authored tremolo period may have been 1 second before this change. If so, the default beat of 0.5 would alter authored timing and cause a regression.\n\nplayTune correctly uses the 0.6 PREFS assist when pullOf(null) resets dev to 0.6, \n\nThe previously unusedand uses 1.2 when pullOf(1.2) `strains.beat` is now is called. The config applied. At the default sets hands.cursor to beat of 0.5, tempo  330, and Dev.reset equals 1, so staccatorestores it properly. timing remains unchanged Both playTune and ghost from before. The old code in the HTML bundle match the source. The code is unavailable fast test run logged to verify whether the authored tremolo period 134 checks, likely  was also preserved.skipping the long playthrough.\n\nThe full test run logged 166 checks with zero failures. The 32-check gap against the fast run likely covers the playthrough and new tests. A quick grep will verify the check count matches\n\nThe deviation explicitly the expected 166. states that authored clocks and counts stay put at beat 0.5 with spawn 1, which suggests the old hardcoded period likely matched the new default formula. PLAN.md should be checked to confirm the original authored beat period.\n\nA grep count of checks is unreliable because multiline checks and loop-generated ones are missed. The real issue is in advancePhase: phaseClear skips beads, so a phase can advance while beads remain alive after the strain is done.\n\nThe full test suite passed, including per-case bot clears. This confirms the default timing is preserved and the game still clears as expected.\n\nReed wait is authored as 6 divided by spawn rate. At spawn 1 this equals 6, matching the deviation and test expectations.\n\nBead count scales with spawn rate: 4 beads at spawn 1 and 8 at spawn 2.\n\nThe cheat path is sound: beads are killed and objects marked done, so syncBeads cannot revive them. Worm shards","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7075533b-deab-45e9-87be-52e6848e4141-34","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function tuneOf|function nearest|function slip\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2_