{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_523","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"game.html also contains the ghost paint at the same line number as the root HTML.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1a6b5473-3e85-4f21-b9c6-7ed099d83524-42","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/goal-verdict-08d1b960e391-2-1.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"tests.log is `166 checks, 0 failed` (exit 0); shell.js:430 paints #67d6ff ghosts, playTune keeps a non-default cursor/assist (shell.js:171), strainBeat/strainSpawn scale flight and counts (sim.js:832), Clear phase sets strain.done (shell.js:537); the same lines are in the root HTML; run.mjs asserts magnet, guide-follow, eight wheel sectors, a loose stitch, a real cautery lock event, and drawn ghosts.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"## Not refuted\\n\\nEach prior gap is fixed in the shipped source and in the root HTML bundle. `tests/run.mjs` loads those scripts (not a mock) and the captured run is `166 checks, 0 failed`.\\n\\n- Second Look: `drawOp` paints recorded cursor and strain marks while `ghostT > 0` (`shell.js:430`). The suite rewinds a live operation and counts `#67d6ff` discs from the real `px.disc` path. That color is used only for those marks.\\n- Dev cursor and assist: `playTune` copies settings only while the slider is still 330 or 0.6 (`shell.js:171`). A later `Dev.set` is what `drive` passes into `Op.step`. The suite measures a 480 cursor against a 200 preference and a 1.2 assist against assist 0.\\n- Beat and spawn: `strainBeat` scales Staccato flight and the Tremolo reed period; `strainSpawn` scales bead counts and the reed wait (`sim.js:832`, `sim.js:1017`, `sim.js:1228`). Tests observe an earlier landing, an earlier flare, 4 vs 8 beads, and waits of 6 vs 3.\\n- Clear phase: the cheat sets `strain.done`, kills beads, worms, and lobes, and fills a short IV (`shell.js:533`). The next `drive` calls `phaseClear`. On case 4 the suite moves the dev menu to Clear phase and the live phase becomes Repair.\\n- The old cautery check is no longer `slips > 0`. It now requires `lock > 0`, a `lock` event, and a `slip` whose reason is `lock` (`stepCautery` at `sim.js:753`).\\n\\nGating captures still match the plan: title frames are 480×270 and filled, Enter reaches the menu, three engines stay quiet, Hub harness runs pass, and a client stroke at 111,122 is on the host. `exit-interview.json` has the required shape and `usage`. Plan edits only mark the checklist done and record these behaviors; they do not drop a criterion.\\n\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1a6b5473-3e85-4f21-b9c6-7ed099d83524-43","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/goal-classifier-08d1b960e391-2-skeptic-1.md","content":"## Not refuted\n\nEach prior gap is fixed in the shipped source and in the root HTML bundle. `tests/run.mjs` loads those scripts (not a mock) and the captured run is `166 checks, 0 failed`.\n\n- Second Look: `drawOp` paints recorded cursor and strain marks while `ghostT > 0` (`shell.js:430`). The suite rewinds a live operation and counts `#67d6ff` discs from the real `px.disc` path. That color is used only for those marks.\n- Dev cursor and assist: `playTune` copies settings only while the slider is still 330 or 0.6 (`shell.js:171`). A later `Dev.set` is what `drive` passes into `Op.step`. The suite measures a 480 cursor against a 200 preference and a 1.2 assist against assist 0.\n- Beat and spawn: `strainBeat` scales Staccato flight and the Tremolo reed period; `strainSpawn` scales bead counts and the reed wait (`sim.js:832`, `sim.js:1017`, `sim.js:1228`). Tests observe an earlier landing, an earlier flare, 4 vs 8 beads, and waits of 6 vs 3.\n- Clear phase: the cheat sets `strain.done`, kills beads, worms, and lobes, and fills a short IV (`shell.js:533`). The next `drive` calls `phaseClear`. On case 4 the suite moves the dev menu to Clear phase and the live phase becomes Repair.\n- The old cautery check is no longer `slips > 0`. It now requires `lock > 0`, a `lock` event, and a `slip` whose reason is `lock` (`stepCautery` at `sim.js:753`).\n\nGating captures still match the plan: title frames are 480×270 and filled, Enter reaches the menu, three engines stay quiet, Hub harness runs pass, and a client stroke at 111,122 is on the host. `exit-interview.json` has the required shape and `usage`. Plan edits only mark the checklist done and record these behaviors; they do not drop a criterion.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3489,"output_tokens":1364,"cache_read_input_tokens":86016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"37e3f2b4-1131-4da4-998c-ce1d28e693ef"}
