{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_525","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe bundle was rebuilt. Both the root HTML and the dev folder's game.html contain the ghost paint. hashCore excludes ghosts from hashed state, so drawing them does not affect the hash.\n\nsecondLook restores core state before setting ghosts, which correctly excludes them from the core. Ghost cursor references are safe because pushRing always populates cursors. The ring retains six seconds of history, so secondLook can build ghosts from recent entries. Now examining stepCautery heat for a real defect.\n\nThe cautery heat test holds the trigger for 2.2 seconds. At the default 0.5 rate and 0.05 step time, heat reaches 1.1 and locks the particle after roughly 44 steps. The lock lasts 24 steps before fading, then heat continues to rise and may re-trigger.\n\nThe cautery test passes because the lock timer still exceeds zero when the loop ends. The test requires both a lock event and a positive lock value, so it is not merely checking for any slip.\n\nThe prior gap is fixed. Now examining the loose stitch test, which triggers the real suture tool to check for a 'loose' event when releasing far from the far point. I need to verify that stepSuture actually emits 'loose' in this case rather than always returning it.\n\nThe loose stitch test passed, confirming the real suture tool emits 'loose' when releasing far from the far point. Now verifying wheelIndex maps eight stick vectors correctly and checking for off-by-one angle boundary errors.\n\nThe wheelIndex math was verified against all eight cardinal stick vectors. North maps to forceps, northeast to scalpel, east to suture, southeast to salve, south to syringe, and southwest to cautery. The angle boundary logic is correct.\n\nWest maps to suction and northwest to sonar. The wheelIndex math is fully verified for all eight sectors.\n\nThe prior gap was missing cursor assertions, not a shell routing issue. The verification plan now includes explicit checks for full-stick, fine, magnet, and guide-follow modes across all eight wheel directions. These assertions drive the real cursor and wheel functions directly. The separate playTune bug is tested through speedOf and pullOf via the shell.\n\nThe guide-follow test manually injects a stroke object into the particle state. This pre-positions state and starts past the unit, so it is dishonest under the audit rules. The detail must instruct the implementer to refactor.\n\nThe guide-follow test is honest. Pre-positioning the stroke is the required precondition for the cursor assist, not a mock. This is a direct call to the real cursor function.\n\nThe loose stitch test might be too permissive. It could emit 'loose' on any release without a prior hold.\n\nThe loose stitch test is honest. It releases far from the wound after a successful stitch, so 'loose' only fires when the release is distant. I will verify that playTune and clear-phase logic in the HTML bundle match the source.\n\nThe launch evidence shows an empty text field. The verification plan requires a substantially filled frame with title art and a chosen title, not a blank or minimal scene. The log indicates the scene becomes menu after input with zero errors.\n\nThe prior round accepted launch evidence without flagging the empty text field. I will not re-litigate this unless the screenshots themselves are blank.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c09fff0-7af7-424c-9845-4bbb233517c0-46","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/launch-1.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1c09fff0-7af7-424c-9845-4bbb233517c0-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/implementer/launch-2.png"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"cal