{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_531","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Evidence is newer than the source and HTML.\n\nAll timestamps confirm the evidence predates the code changes. The prior gaps are fixed. I will mark this as Not Refuted.\n\nThe launch screenshot shows the title screen. The log confirms the scene advances to menu after confirm. Both requirements are satisfied.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The five prior gaps are fixed in the shipped sim, shell, tests, and rebuilt page. I’ll record that verdict."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef938529-31f8-4db1-bc90-ec1cbb1c2c85-58","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/goal-verdict-08d1b960e391-2-2.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": false,\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"evidence\": \"tests.log is one line '166 checks, 0 failed' (exit 0) after the shell/sim edits; drawOp paints #67d6ff ghosts, playTune keeps a non-default cursor/assist, strainBeat/strainSpawn scale beads and reed waits, and Clear phase sets strain.done so c4 advances to Repair.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"Not refuted. All five prior gaps are fixed in the shipped code, covered by honest checks in `tests/run.mjs`, and the captured `tests.log` is a single line `166 checks, 0 failed` with exit 0, newer than `sim.js`, `shell.js`, `tests/run.mjs`, and the root HTML.\\n\\n- Second Look: `secondLook` still fills `S.ghosts` and `S.ghostT` (`src/core/sim.js:330`), and `drawOp` paints those cursor and strain marks while `ghostT > 0` (`src/scenes/shell.js:430`). The suite asserts a non-empty ghost list and that a real frame calls `px.disc` with `#67d6ff` (that color is used only there). The same paint is in the root HTML.\\n- Dev cursor and assist: `playTune` copies settings only while the slider is still the documented default 330 / 0.6 (`src/scenes/shell.js:167`). `cloneTune` copies `hands`, so the preference write does not stick the slider. Checks drive the op scene and show a 480 cursor outruns the preference and a 1.2 assist pulls when the preference is 0.\\n- Strain sliders: `strainBeat` scales Staccato landing and the Tremolo/Cantor windows; `strainSpawn` scales bead and nest counts and the Tremolo reed wait (`src/core/sim.js:832`). At beat 0.5 and spawn 1 the scales are 1. Checks: beat 1 lands and flares inside a window where 0.5 does not; spawn 2 yields 8 beads and a 3s reed wait versus 4 and 6.\\n- Clear phase: the cheat sets `strain.done`, kills beads/worms/lobes, and fills a short IV (`src/scenes/shell.js:533`). `phaseClear` then returns true. The dev menu on c4 phase 1 (Staccato) advances to phase 2 Repair.\\n- Required assertions are present and drive the shipped cursor, wheel, suture, and cautery: magnet pull versus assist 0, guide-follow lateral hold, all eight wheel sectors, a loose stitch that does not increment `stitch`, and a cautery lock that requires `players[0].lock > 0` plus a `lock` event (not merely `slips > 0`).\\n\\nLaunch, browser, Hub, and handoff logs are newer than the rebuilt HTML. Both launch frames are a filled 480×270 title, and the log records the menu after confirm. No new demonstrable defect in the shipped behavior.\"\n}"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ef938529-31f8-4db1-bc90-ec1cbb1c2c85-59","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223916__x488eb9/tmp/grok-goal-08d1b960e391/goal-classifier-08d1b960e391-2-skeptic-2.md","content":"Not refuted. All five prior gaps are fixed in the shipped code, covered by honest checks in `tests/run.mjs`, and the captured `tests.log` is a single line `166 checks, 0 failed` with exit 0, newer than `sim.js`, `shell.js`, `tests/run.mjs`, and the root HTML.\n\n- Second Look: `secondLook` still fills `S.ghosts` and `S.ghostT` (`src/core/sim.js:330`), and `drawOp` paints those cursor and strain marks while `ghostT > 0` (`src/scenes/shell.js:430`). The suite asserts a non-empty ghost list and that a real frame calls `px.disc` with `#67d6ff` (that color is used only there). The same paint is in the root HTML.\n- Dev cursor and assist: `playTune` copies settings only while the slider is still the documented default 330 / 0.6 (`src/scenes/shell.js:167`). `cloneTune` copies `hands`, so the preference write does not stick the slider. Checks drive the op scene and show a 480 cursor outruns the preference and a 1.2 assist pulls when the preference is 0.\n- Strain sliders: `strainBeat` scales Staccato landing and the Tremolo/Cantor windows; `strainSpawn` scales bead and nest counts and the Tremolo reed wait (`src/core/sim.js:832`). At beat 0.5 and spawn 1 the scales are 1. Checks: beat 1 lands and flares inside a window where 0.5 does not; spawn 2 yields 8 beads and a 3s reed wait versus 4 and 6.\n- Clear phase: the cheat sets `strain.done`, kills beads/worms/lobes, and fills a short IV (`src/scenes/shell.js:533`). `phaseClear` then returns true. The dev menu on c4 phase 1 (Staccato) advances to phase 2 Repair.\n- Required assertions are present and drive the shipped cursor, wheel, suture, and cautery: magnet pull versus assist 0, guide-follow lateral hold, all eight wheel sectors, a loose stitch that does not increment `stitch`, and a cautery lock that requires `players[0].lock > 0` plus a `lock` event (not merely `slips > 0`).\n\nLaunch, browser, Hub, and handoff logs are newer than the rebuilt HTML. Both launch frames are a filled 480×270 title, and the log records the menu after confirm. No new demonstrable defect in the shipped behavior.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1016,"output_tokens":2163,"cache_read_input_tokens":107776,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aa37-f7cf-7001-9198-38ad04ed0f5e","uuid":"ae12cf19-4278-4aec-b119-c105a620178d"}
